window.AKK_AN_INNOCENT_GIRL_SEEKING_A_HUSBAND_WAS_DECEIVED_AND_MARRIED_A_CHILDLESS_OFFICER_CRYING_WITH_EMOTION_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_AN_INNOCENT_GIRL_SEEKING_A_HUSBAND_WAS_DECEIVED_AND_MARRIED_A_CHILDLESS_OFFICER_CRYING_WITH_EMOTION_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":201,"title":"Chapter 201: Someone was beaten to death","paragraphs":["Meanwhile, Qiao Lanshu chased Liu Weihong for two whole streets. It didn't take long for Liu Weihong to find herself completely out of breath.","After all, even though Niuwa was young, he was quite heavy.","Weighing over thirty pounds, picking him up occasionally didn't feel like much, and for a man, it wasn't heavy at all.","But for a woman, running while carrying a child of that weight was no easy task.","Previously on the train, Qin Yuanzheng was able to easily rescue Niuwa because the woman carrying the fast-asleep child couldn't run fast, so she ruthlessly abandoned him.","Now it was Liu Weihong's turn. Her arms ached and she panted heavily from running with Niuwa in her arms. The main issue was that Niuwa was awake and had been kicking and punching her the entire way.","Liu Weihong's face was scratched all over by Niuwa. She shifted her grip on him and said viciously, You damn brat, you had better settle down right now, or else when we get back, I will beat you to death!","Liu Weihong's eyes were fierce, and her face was gloomy as she glared at Niuwa threateningly.","Niuwa was just a little boy after all. Terrified by her fierce glare, he shrank his neck and started crying again, tears welling up in his eyes.","Niuwa truly had not run away on his own this time.","He had been playing in the courtyard. Auntie Shi had locked the courtyard gate and was inside the house coaxing An'an to sleep.","She figured that at most, Niuwa would just make a mess in the vegetable garden. No matter what, he couldn't run outside.","Who knew that after Liu Weihong was harshly scolded by Zheng Weigong, she would also be sent out to look for the child.","That day, she happened to pass by Qiao Lanshu's small courtyard and heard Niuwa's voice inside. Feeling that the child's voice sounded familiar, she peeked through the crack in the door and spotted Niuwa at a glance.","Then, she took out a handful of candies and crouched by the dog hole to coax Niuwa out.","Niuwa was greedy for snacks. Seeing those delicious treats, he couldn't resist the temptation and crawled into the dog hole again.","Once again, he got stuck in the hole, but Liu Weihong told him to suck in his stomach and yanked him out.","When Niuwa got stuck in the dog hole, he regretted it and tried to back up into the courtyard, but Liu Weihong was too fast and swiftly pulled him out.","His little belly was rubbed red. Fortunately, the skin wasn't broken, but it still hurt a lot. Niuwa opened his mouth and started crying, and as soon as he cried, Auntie Shi came out.","Liu Weihong then picked up Niuwa and started running wildly.","Seeing that she was about to reach home, Liu Weihong held Niuwa tightly. She had just stopped to catch her breath when she turned around and saw Qiao Lanshu catching up.","Liu Weihong: ????","Liu Weihong was stunned and muttered in bewilderment, Why is it her? What a lingering bitch!","Liu Weihong hated Qiao Lanshu to the bone.","It was all because of Qiao Lanshu that her father and brother were caught and sent to labor camps. Her family was now ruined, and her own bright future was gone.","She even had to shamelessly cling to Zheng Weigong, acting as his free nanny.","All of this was because of Qiao Lanshu.","Liu Weihong glared at Qiao Lanshu with venomous eyes. Seeing Qiao Lanshu catching up, she didn't even have time to argue and just continued running with Niuwa in her arms.","Niuwa also saw Qiao Lanshu and cried out to her, Sister, Sister, save me!","He used to call her Auntie, but now he was calling her Sister.","Hearing this from afar, Qiao Lanshu felt both softhearted and angry.","She didn't know how Niuwa was taken away by Liu Weihong, but that was no longer important.","The important thing was, why did Liu Weihong snatch Niuwa?","Liu Weihong ran all the way to Zheng Weigong's door and took out her keys to open it.","Zheng Weigong hadn't been coming back much these past few days; he was also secretly searching for the child outside.","Liu Weihong knew she had misunderstood Zheng Weigong. If she couldn't bring the child back this time, Zheng Weigong would definitely dump her.","Fortunately, she had found him!","Liu Weihong took out her key and opened the door, then hurriedly ran into the courtyard. Before she could close the door, Qiao Lanshu rushed up and pushed it open forcefully.","Liu Weihong was already exhausted. The push made her fall to the ground, and she dropped Niuwa onto the ground as well.","Niuwa was hurt from the fall and sat there crying.","Qiao Lanshu rushed in, pointed at Liu Weihong, and scolded, Liu Weihong! I never expected you to be a human trafficker! Daring to snatch a child in broad daylight, aren't you afraid of being taken out and shot?","Liu Weihong scrambled up from the ground and said angrily, What human trafficker? You are the human trafficker! This child belongs to my family. I am bringing him home, why are you chasing me relentlessly?","Qiao Lanshu sneered, Bah, how do you have the nerve to say that? Your family's child? If you call his name, do you think he will answer you? Let go of him!","Qiao Lanshu pushed Liu Weihong away forcefully and ran over to pick Niuwa up. However, Liu Weihong lunged at her and grabbed Qiao Lanshu's hair.","Growing up and living through two lifetimes, Qiao Lanshu had never fought with anyone like this before.","Therefore, she inevitably fell at a disadvantage, and her movements in grappling with Liu Weihong were somewhat unpracticed.","Liu Weihong viciously clawed at Qiao Lanshu's face; she had long despised Qiao Lanshu's pretty face.","She was determined to scratch up Qiao Lanshu's face today and ruin her looks!","Knowing she couldn't win the fight, Qiao Lanshu naturally knew to dodge. She kept stepping back, using both hands to protect her face, and dodged around the courtyard.","Liu Weihong chased after Qiao Lanshu, shoving her with a smug look on her face. Aren't you usually so good at pretending? Why are you fighting me like a shrew now? Why aren't you acting like a delicate young lady anymore? Hmm? You know there are no men around to look at you, so you stopped pretending, right?","Being chased and hit, Qiao Lanshu heard Liu Weihong spouting nasty words but ignored her.","She looked at Niuwa, who was sitting in the courtyard crying, and shouted, Niuwa, hurry and go home!","Hearing her words, Niuwa immediately got up from the ground and was about to run out the door.","Liu Weihong suddenly lunged over. Where do you think you are going? Stop right there, you little brat!","So Qiao Lanshu lunged forward as well, and the two tangled in a fight again.","Niuwa was so frightened that he bawled loudly; it was too terrifying.","Right at that moment, Zhong Mei, who had chased them to the vicinity, heard Niuwa's crying and hurried over.","The courtyard door wasn't closed. As soon as Zhong Mei walked in, she saw Qiao Lanshu protecting her face with her hands while Liu Weihong grabbed her hair and beat her.","Zhong Mei's brows immediately shot up in anger. Wielding a carrying pole, she rushed over. You bastard, how dare you bully Lanshu! I will beat you to death!","With that, the carrying pole in her hands swung toward Liu Weihong's back.","Never hit the head when fighting—this was a lesson Zhong Mei had learned from her previous two fights with men.","She used the carrying pole to strike Liu Weihong's back and buttocks, landing solid blows every time with all her might.","Liu Weihong screamed miserably under the beating. Unable to focus on hitting Qiao Lanshu anymore, she dodged and shrieked, Who are you? What are you doing barging into my house?","Zhong Mei didn't waste her breath on her; she simply kept raining blows on Liu Weihong with the carrying pole.","Qiao Lanshu was finally rescued.","Her clothes were disheveled, and her hair had been pulled into a messy tangle. Seeing Zhong Mei approaching, she quickly dodged to the side.","Qiao Lanshu had been protecting her face the whole time, so her arms and neck were covered in red scratch marks left by Liu Weihong.","Her eyes were red from the pain. Damn it! It was her first time getting into a fight, and she had been pinned down and beaten by this detestable woman. Qiao Lanshu was so angry with herself she was about to cry.","Qiao Lanshu went over and hugged the terrified, crying Niuwa in her arms, continuously comforting him, There, there, do not cry, everything is fine now.","While coaxing Niuwa, she watched Zhong Mei chase after Liu Weihong, beating her with a carrying pole.","Liu Weihong howled under the blows, screaming and cursing as she scurried around the courtyard in a highly comical manner.","Qiao Lanshu suspected that she herself had looked just as comical when she was being chased and beaten moments ago.","Suddenly, something unexpected happened. Liu Weihong, while dodging the carrying pole, tripped over something. She fell heavily to the ground with a loud thud, her forehead coincidentally smashing right into a rock.","In an instant, Liu Weihong sat up dizzily, blood streaming all over her head and face.","Zhong Mei, who had been following closely with the pole, was stunned by this sudden turn of events.","Was she cursed to always bust her enemies' heads open?","She had only been in three fights in total, and all three times the opponent ended up with a busted head.","Would she be sent to the labor camp again this time?","Zhong Mei's face turned slightly pale, and she looked at Qiao Lanshu helplessly.","Qiao Lanshu's heart skipped a beat as well, sensing that things had taken a terrible turn.","Just then, the commotion in their courtyard attracted the curiosity of the neighbors.","Someone had already come to the door, calling out to Liu Weihong, Weihong, what is going on with you all? What happened?","With a clatter, the carrying pole dropped from Zhong Mei's hands to the ground, her face completely drained of color from nervousness.","She was not afraid of fighting, and she felt no guilt at all about chasing and beating Liu Weihong just now.","But seeing Liu Weihong's face covered in blood, she was truly scared.","Qiao Lanshu glanced at Zhong Mei, then toward the door. From her angle, she could see a crowd gathering outside.","Those people would probably come inside in a moment.","This would not do!","Qiao Lanshu and Niuwa were the original victims, but with Liu Weihong injured like this, Qiao Lanshu would lose the moral high ground no matter how right she was!","Seeing Zhong Mei almost scared silly, Qiao Lanshu could not help but feel bad for her.","The old Zhong Mei feared nothing in heaven or on earth, but after a stint in the labor camp, she had become much more cautious and timid.","Qiao Lanshu suddenly set Niuwa down on the ground and told him, Sit still, do not run around.","Then, Qiao Lanshu rushed over to Liu Weihong, who was still clutching her forehead and screaming, swiped some blood from Liu Weihong's face, and haphazardly smeared it across her own face and forehead.","Liu Weihong: ???","Still dizzy, Liu Weihong glared at Qiao Lanshu and asked furiously, What are you doing? What on earth are you doing?","She continued to shriek, You two murderers! You will not get away today. I will make you pay the price!","As soon as she said this, the neighbors outside happened to walk in and heard every word.","Right at that moment, Qiao Lanshu suddenly closed her eyes, collapsed to the ground, and lay motionless as if she had fainted.","Liu Weihong wiped the blood from the corner of her eye with her sleeve, her eyes widening in shock as she screamed, What are you doing, Qiao Lanshu? Are you trying to get yourself killed?","Watching Qiao Lanshu, Zhong Mei did not react at first.","But soon, seeing the neighbors entering the courtyard, she immediately threw herself toward Qiao Lanshu. Glaring at Liu Weihong with red eyes, she cried and scolded, How could you be like this? Not only did you snatch our child right off the street, but now you want to murder us? You want us to pay the price—does that mean paying with our lives? Do not think we are afraid of you just because you have powerful backing!","Liu Weihong: ...","Dizzy and seeing stars, Liu Weihong stared at Zhong Mei in utter disbelief at her words. She was so furious that her eyes rolled back, and she nearly fainted right there on the ground.","The neighbors were equally shocked to see this scene upon entering.","No one dared to touch Qiao Lanshu; they just gathered around and asked, What exactly is going on here?","Liu Weihong was about to speak, but Zhong Mei beat her to it, yelling at the top of her lungs, Comrades, help! She has committed murder! Please help take my sister to the hospital! And the child, our child is still crying!","Only then did the crowd notice the child sitting on the ground by the courtyard entrance, his eyes swollen from crying.","While the chaotic argument was going on, Guan Wenjun arrived with people from the Revolutionary Committee and the Public Security Bureau.","The reason they arrived so quickly was that Auntie Shi had asked a neighbor to help call the police.","Afterward, Auntie Shi was still worried about Qiao Lanshu and Niuwa, and she feared that Zhong Mei, armed with a carrying pole, might actually get into a serious fight.","So, after mulling it over, she grabbed a baby carrier, strapped An'an to her back, and ran all the way toward the mining district's military base.","However, the mining district base was quite far away in the suburbs. If she ran all the way there, who knew how long it would take?","So, Auntie Shi had a flash of inspiration and ran to the Revolutionary Committee to find Guan Wenjun instead.","Guan Wenjun had just eaten dinner at Qiao Lanshu's house the night before. Now that Qiao Lanshu was in trouble, asking him for help was not too much to ask, right?","Fortunately, Guan Wenjun was a loyal friend. Upon hearing Auntie Shi's story, he immediately gathered his men and headed out.","Dragon City was not very big, and according to Auntie Shi, the woman running away with the child could not have gone far.","So Guan Wenjun led his men to search the alleys around Qin Yuanzheng's new home. They quickly found the house with a noisy crowd gathered at the entrance—Liu Weihong's house, or rather, Zheng Weigong's house.","Zheng Weigong was not home at the moment, but he would surely receive the news soon and rush back.","Guan Wenjun had not been wasting his time all these years; he knew Zheng Weigong was a tough nut to crack. He had to establish the nature of the incident and rescue Qiao Lanshu and the child before Zheng Weigong returned.","If he could not handle Zheng Weigong afterward, he could conveniently leave it to Qin Yuanzheng to deal with.","While Zhong Mei was arguing with Liu Weihong in the courtyard, someone shouted, The Revolutionary Committee is here! The Revolutionary Committee is here!","Shh, keep your voice down. If they mistake us for accomplices, we are doomed.","These people were still very afraid of the Revolutionary Committee.","Hearing that the Revolutionary Committee had arrived, they all backed away to the doorway, not even daring to step into the courtyard, just to clear themselves of any suspicion.","Guan Wenjun was dressed in a white shirt and black trousers, with a pistol tucked into his waistband and sunglasses resting on the bridge of his nose.","He would have looked like a dashing and handsome rogue, but the gauze wrapped around his forehead significantly diminished his suave aura.","The Revolutionary Committee members rushed in first to disperse the crowd, and then Guan Wenjun strolled in with his hands in his pockets.","Running a hand through his hair, Guan Wenjun stood in the courtyard, looked around, and asked, Someone reported child trafficking here? What exactly is going on?","Seeing Guan Wenjun, Zhong Mei's heart trembled, but she could not care about that right now. She quickly cried out, Comrade, this person committed murder! She knocked my sister unconscious!","Liu Weihong clutched her forehead, seeing stars from sheer fury. \"Who? Who exactly killed someone? Stop slandering me, she's just faking it!\"","When Guan Wenjun saw Zhong Mei, he froze for a split second. Then, his eyes fell upon Qiao Lanshu, whose face was covered in blood, lying completely motionless in Zhong Mei's arms.","Guan Wenjun was so horrified that his legs gave way, nearly dropping him to his knees.","He swallowed hard, his voice trembling as he asked, \"Is... is Qiao Lanshu dead?\"","This was the young wife Qin Yuanzheng had finally married after years of bachelorhood. He doted on her like a precious treasure, and she had only just given birth to their child. If she had really been beaten to death, what on earth would Qin Yuanzheng do?","Guan Wenjun didn't even dare to imagine."]},{"number":202,"title":"Chapter 202: Seeking Justice","paragraphs":["Watching the people from the Revolutionary Committee surround the courtyard, Liu Weihong belatedly realized that she was about to get the short end of the stick once again.","This Qiao Lanshu was truly too sinister. She had long known that Qiao Lanshu was difficult to deal with and had many scheming tricks up her sleeve. She had never been a match for Qiao Lanshu before, and even her younger brother had suffered at Qiao Lanshu's hands.","And now, as luck would have it, she had run into Qiao Lanshu again.","Liu Weihong tried to force herself to calm down, but it was impossible right now. Her head was incredibly dizzy and aching. The wound on her forehead throbbed with pain, and warm blood was still slowly trickling down. The cut was definitely not shallow; she needed to see a doctor immediately.","Sitting on the ground, her head spinning, she hadn't even opened her mouth to defend herself.","Then she heard Director Guan of the Revolutionary Committee ask her in a mixture of panic and anger, Was it you? Did you beat Comrade Xiao Qiao to death with a carrying pole?","Liu Weihong: ...","Liu Weihong was so angry she almost passed out. She said resentfully, I already told you I didn't! No, I didn't, I didn't!","On the verge of a breakdown and incredibly dizzy, Liu Weihong quickly steadied herself and said to Guan Wenjun, Director Guan, do you know whose house this is? This is Zheng Weigong's house! I am his family. A group of you just barge in here like this and slander me. I am not talking to you right now. I will wait until my Zheng Weigong comes back before saying anything.","Liu Weihong had also learned to be smart, knowing that trouble comes from the mouth.","Just paying lip service, not only could she not out-talk them, but she also really didn't have the energy for it right now.","Guan Wenjun, of course, knew this was Zheng Weigong's house. He said coldly, A life for a life! Even if Zheng Weigong were here, he would still have to come with me!","Liu Weihong: ...","At this time, Qiao Lanshu, lying in Zhong Mei's arms and listening to them talk, suddenly became a bit anxious.","She was faking it, and she couldn't let this drag on any longer.","Delaying would be disadvantageous for them. She needed to get to the hospital immediately; once in the hospital, everything would be easier to handle.","Since that Zheng Weigong could become the section chief of the supply department, he must be very smart.","Someone had definitely gone to find Zheng Weigong by now, and he would probably be back very soon.","Feeling anxious, Qiao Lanshu tugged at Zhong Mei's clothes. Zhong Mei immediately lowered her head and held Qiao Lanshu's head tightly.","Qiao Lanshu whispered something in her ear, and Zhong Mei quickly called out to Guan Wenjun, no longer afraid that he might recognize her.","Zhong Mei: Director Guan! Xiao Qiao was just knocked unconscious by her. We need to hurry and send her to the hospital right now. We can't delay any longer! And Niuwa, this child was forcibly taken by this woman and is terrified now. Look at him, he has cried his voice hoarse. We can't let him stay here either.","Hearing this, Guan Wenjun hurriedly said, I know, I know. I've already sent someone to call a doctor... No, that's too slow. I will personally drive you to the hospital.","Saying that, he arranged for two other people and said, You two take her to the hospital and keep a close eye on her! After she gets out of the hospital, bring her to the Revolutionary Committee for questioning. Even if Zheng Weigong comes demanding her release, ignore him! If he dares to make a scene, tell him to go ask Qin Yuanzheng for her!","The people from the Revolutionary Committee immediately nodded in agreement and went to take Liu Weihong to see a doctor.","Guan Wenjun came over, picked up Qiao Lanshu, and hurriedly ran out the door.","Zhong Mei picked up Niuwa, who had stopped crying, and ran out right behind Guan Wenjun.","Niuwa had probably seen Qiao Lanshu faint and understood the severity of the situation. After crying alone in the corner, he surprisingly hadn't run away.","Qiao Lanshu had told him not to move around, and he indeed hadn't moved.","After getting into the car, Zhong Mei held Niuwa in her arms, pinched his cheek, and whispered, You little kid, you've finally been obedient and well-behaved for once. Good thing you didn't run around this time, otherwise I really wouldn't have had the time to chase after you.","Niuwa looked at Qiao Lanshu beside him, whose eyes were closed as if she were deeply unconscious, and whispered, Is the pretty sister dead?","He surprisingly wasn't calling her Auntie anymore, but changed it to pretty sister.","Zhong Mei found this amusing.","She glanced at Qiao Lanshu, knowing she was faking it, but she couldn't explain it to Niuwa.","Because Guan Wenjun was still driving in the front, and she absolutely couldn't let him know about this.","So she lowered her voice and whispered in Niuwa's ear, Don't worry, the pretty sister is fine. She's just too tired and fell asleep. She'll be fine once she wakes up.","Niuwa understood. The little child actually let out a very mature sigh of relief: Not dead? That's wonderful.","Zhong Mei looked at him, wondering in her heart why a child as young as Niuwa would constantly talk about death.","Did he even know what death meant?","Guan Wenjun drove very fast. In less than ten minutes, he arrived at the military region hospital, then hurriedly had someone bring out a stretcher to carry Qiao Lanshu inside.","Zhong Mei also carried Niuwa and followed them in.","Guan Wenjun anxiously asked the subordinate behind him, Did you send someone to the mining area troops to call for him? Is Qin Yuanzheng here yet?","The subordinate quickly replied, We sent someone a long time ago. Looking at the time, he should be arriving right about now.","Sure enough, just as they finished speaking, they saw several soldiers in military uniforms walking through the main entrance of the hospital.","The man leading the group was tall and had a cold, deep expression; it was none other than Qin Yuanzheng. Behind him followed four or five others also in uniform, including his adjutant, his orderly, and his chief of staff.","It wasn't clear what the group had been doing just now, but upon hearing the news, they had rushed over in a hurry.","They looked so aggressive that Guan Wenjun even shrank his neck under Qin Yuanzheng's glare.","Qin Yuanzheng walked over and asked, Where is my wife?","Guan Wenjun pointed to the inside of the ward: She was just sent in for an examination. We don't know the situation yet.","Qin Yuanzheng's face was dark. Outwardly, he remained calm as he asked again, Your people just came to pass a message, saying Xiao Qiao was beaten to death? Is that true?","Guan Wenjun had also initially thought Qiao Lanshu was beaten to death, but when he carried her into the car, he realized she wasn't dead. Her pulse was perfectly fine.","Qiao Lanshu had simply passed out.","At this moment, he quickly explained, No, she's not dead. They were talking nonsense. Xiao Qiao just fainted.","Qin Yuanzheng's gloomy and tense expression relaxed a little.","He turned his head to look at Zhong Mei. Zhong Mei was still holding Niuwa in her arms. Niuwa's eyes were swollen from crying. When he looked at Qin Yuanzheng, he also shrank his neck, lowered his head with a guilty conscience, and twiddled his thumbs, not daring to make a sound.","Qin Yuanzheng then asked Zhong Mei, What exactly is going on here? Tell me.","Zhong Mei was intimidated by the imposing aura of Qin Yuanzheng and his group of soldiers, thinking to herself that military officers really were majestic.","Just look at their physiques, look at their presence!","Guan Wenjun glanced at Zhong Mei a couple of times and called out to her, a bit frustrated, Hey, are you struck dumb? Brigade Commander Qin is asking you a question.","Zhong Mei shot Guan Wenjun a look, then, with her back to him, explained to Qin Yuanzheng what had happened.","The more Qin Yuanzheng listened, the worse his expression became. \"Zheng Weigong's family member running into my house to snatch a child. What a fine thing to do.\"","Guan Wenjun glanced at the back of Zhong Mei's head. He silently walked over to Qin Yuanzheng's side, facing Zhong Mei directly, and then said, \"Why would Zheng Weigong's family member want to snatch this child? Could it be that this child is actually Zheng Weigong's illegitimate son?\"","Qin Yuanzheng said bluntly, \"Impossible!\"","There was no way this child was Zheng Weigong's illegitimate son.","Qin Yuanzheng sneered. \"They ran to my house, snatched a child from my home, and injured my wife. I will not let this matter go easily; I will personally investigate this case.\"","As it happened, he was also planning to investigate Zheng Weigong to find out exactly why he wanted to snatch this child.","Guan Wenjun said, \"His family member is also injured and is getting bandaged up in the hospital right now. After she's done, I'll send her to the police station. Then you and Li Jianlin can handle this matter together. I'm staying out of it.\"","Guan Wenjun was busy finalizing his own work arrangements and truly didn't want to meddle in these affairs anymore.","Before long, the doctor emerged from Qiao Lanshu's ward.","Qin Yuanzheng and the others immediately went forward to meet him.","Although Qin Yuanzheng's face was calm, his eyes still revealed his worry. He asked nervously, \"Doctor, how is my wife?\"","The doctor remained silent for a few seconds before saying, \"She should be fine. The blood on her face belongs to someone else. I just examined her, and she has no obvious external injuries, let alone any bleeding.\"","Qin Yuanzheng's face darkened, and his voice grew a bit colder. \"Then why did my wife faint? Could it be internal injuries?\"","Frightened by Qin Yuanzheng's imposing aura, the doctor fell silent for another few seconds. In truth, he felt that the patient didn't look like she had fainted; instead, it seemed more like she had fallen asleep...","But he didn't dare to say that. Besides, when it came to head injuries, it was hard to say for sure.","He chose his words carefully, \"This is still uncertain at the moment. We have to wait until the patient wakes up and ask her. Please don't worry. The patient is not in danger. Why don't we wait for her to wake up first?\"","Qin Yuanzheng naturally listened to the doctor, so he nodded.","After the doctor left, Qin Yuanzheng asked his subordinates to go back first. He wanted to stay behind at the hospital.","Immediately after, he asked Zhong Mei in a cold, deep voice, \"You said that when you rushed over, Zheng Weigong's family member was grabbing Xiao Qiao by the hair and hitting her?\"","Zhong Mei nodded, adding embellishments to the story. \"Yes! You know it too, Lanshu just has too soft of a personality. She never fights. Being dragged by the hair by that woman, she couldn't run away, and she couldn't fight back either. That woman was so ruthless, scratching and hitting Lanshu's face and head. Niuwa was terrified and cried until his voice went hoarse.\"","The more Qin Yuanzheng listened, the uglier his expression became.","Standing to the side, Guan Wenjun heard this and frowned as well, saying, \"Poor Comrade Xiao Qiao. She probably hasn't been beaten like this since she was a child. Lao Qin, you absolutely cannot settle this matter! Unless you let Xiao Qiao grab the other party's hair and hit her back!\"","Qin Yuanzheng was furious, and at the same time, his heart ached.","His little wife was young and had a soft temperament. She normally wouldn't even argue with anyone, and she never even raised her voice when speaking to others.","How could such a gentle girl know how to fight?","Encountering such a fierce shrew this time, Xiao Qiao must have suffered a lot.","With a chest full of fierce hostility and nowhere to vent it, Qin Yuanzheng just stood there with a dark expression, not saying a word.","However, the aura he exuded frightened Zhong Mei into silently taking two steps back.","Niuwa was excessively quiet as well; looking at Qin Yuanzheng's face, he didn't even dare to whimper.","Guan Wenjun looked at Zhong Mei and suddenly asked, \"What about you? Are you injured?\"","Zhong Mei looked at him with a strange expression, seemingly a little surprised. \"You're asking me?\"","Guan Wenjun nodded, his expression a bit unnatural. \"Didn't you also go fight? Are you hurt? Do you want to see a doctor and get a checkup?\"","Zhong Mei immediately shook her head. \"No need, I'm fine.\"","When it came to fighting, ordinary people were no match for her.","It was just Qiao Lanshu who had suffered a loss. Although she had pretended to faint, in the beginning, she had indeed been grabbed by the hair and beaten by Liu Weihong.","At this moment, the nurse came out and said they could go in to accompany the patient.","Qin Yuanzheng took large strides into the ward.","At first, Qiao Lanshu was pretending to have fainted, but later she actually fell asleep.","After all, she had been running and chasing for a good part of the day, and then being chased and hit for another half a day; it was quite tiring. However, she only slept for a short while.","By now, she was already awake.","After the nurse went out, she opened her eyes and saw Qin Yuanzheng.","She smiled. \"Brother Zheng, you're here?\"","Qin Yuanzheng's expression was very ugly and cold. He walked over quickly without saying a word, first cupping Qiao Lanshu's face to look left and right.","Then, he went to look at Qiao Lanshu's hands. He reached his fingers into Qiao Lanshu's hair, pressing around everywhere, and asked in a low voice, \"Does it hurt anywhere?\"","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. \"No, it doesn't hurt. Brother Zheng, I'm fine.\"","Qin Yuanzheng withdrew his hands and looked at the side of Qiao Lanshu's face and neck again.","At this time, he saw several scratched nail marks on Qiao Lanshu's neck.","As well as red slap marks.","Qiao Lanshu's skin was naturally fair and tender. Normally, if Qin Yuanzheng used just a little bit of force, it would leave marks.","He cherished Qiao Lanshu dearly and wanted to pamper her well.","Pampering her delicate white skin and flesh, he couldn't bear to let her get hurt. Even if she just got a mosquito bite normally, Qin Yuanzheng would feel uncomfortable for a long time.","Now look at this, someone had scratched several nail marks into his wife's neck.","A few of the nail marks had even broken the skin, leaving bloody streaks across her fair skin, which was extremely glaring to the eyes.","The hostility in Qin Yuanzheng's eyes instantly became uncontainable.","His voice turned gloomy, yet he still kept it very low, afraid of frightening Qiao Lanshu. He asked softly, \"Does it hurt?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"It hurts.\"","Actually, when Qiao Lanshu was being grabbed and beaten by Liu Weihong, she was indeed quite panicked.","Normally, if she had been alone, avoiding this kind of thing would have been a breeze.","But at that time, because she had to look after Niuwa, she couldn't run away by herself and could only fight with Liu Weihong.","However, she really wasn't good at fighting, and that Liu Weihong was taller and bigger than her, so she truly didn't have the upper hand.","Qiao Lanshu reflected on it for a moment and said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Next time I encounter this kind of thing, I will grab a stick first. I absolutely cannot chase after them empty-handed like this again. It's too much of a disadvantage.\"","Those nail marks on her neck were considered superficial injuries, and the nurse had already disinfected them and applied medicine just now.","The nurse didn't take it seriously, thinking it was a minor matter.","But Qin Yuanzheng's heart ached terribly.","He said in a deep voice, \"Don't worry. I will definitely get justice for you in this matter.\"","He would not let Zheng Weigong off easily. Compensation was secondary; he wanted to send Liu Weihong to a labor camp.","If he couldn't even seek justice for his own wife, then what kind of man was he?"]},{"number":203,"title":"Chapter 203: Just a Nanny","paragraphs":["Liu Weihong was also at the hospital having her wounds bandaged.","She was genuinely injured. She had been running so fast that she tripped in her haste, hitting her forehead on a rock, which caused the wound to bleed non-stop.","Now, after a few stitches, the bleeding had finally stopped. The doctor applied medicine, wrapped it in gauze, and told her to rest for a few days.","Liu Weihong had been incredibly dizzy earlier, but she was finally starting to recover.","Seeing the Revolutionary Committee members guarding the door, she knew they still intended to take her away for interrogation!","She couldn't help but feel a surge of panic, knowing that Zheng Weigong definitely wouldn't help her.","They hadn't even gotten their marriage certificate yet. She had taken the risk to find the child and sneak him back just to keep Zheng Weigong from being angry with her, while also proving her usefulness.","Now that she had messed everything up, Zheng Weigong would likely distance himself from her as quickly as possible. Why would he ever bother to help her?","Just as her thoughts were running wild, Zheng Weigong finally rushed over in a hurry.","He didn't come alone; he brought his secretary and the Women's Federation Director, Zheng Wenhui, with him.","Zheng Wenhui had also brought people along. She had rushed over after receiving the news, and her target, of course, was Niuwa.","The child had gone missing under her watch, so now that he was found, she naturally had every reason to come and make arrangements for him.","Therefore, Zheng Wenhui didn't enter Liu Weihong's ward; she went straight to find Niuwa.","Zheng Weigong told his secretary to guard the door while he walked into the ward, casually shutting the door behind him.","Looking at his stern, unsmiling face, Liu Weihong's heart trembled. She knew he was angry, and she felt a bit scared.","Zheng Weigong walked in slowly. He stood by the bed and stared at her. Before he could even speak, Liu Weihong nervously explained, Weigong, they framed me this time! They were the ones chasing me with a carrying pole and beating me. Look, I'm injured!","Zheng Weigong stared at her and asked in a deep voice, When I was on my way here, I heard that Qin Yuanzheng's family member was almost beaten to death by you? She is currently unconscious in the hospital.","Liu Weihong: ...","Liu Weihong was so angry that she started feeling dizzy again. She said indignantly, I already told you, I didn't hit them! She is faking it! She deliberately pretended to faint to set me up. Why don't you believe me either? You don't know how cunning that Qiao Lanshu is; she is too scheming!","Zheng Weigong's gaze on Liu Weihong was very gloomy. At this moment, he felt a deep disgust for her in his heart.","He had only approached Liu Weihong in the first place because her father was valuable.","He even regretted not dumping her sooner, which had led to her causing him so much trouble now.","Zheng Weigong sat down on a chair and said, Right now, it is not a matter of whether you say she is faking it or not. She can just as easily turn around and say you are slandering her and refusing to admit you hurt her. In these situations, words are empty without proof. Were there any witnesses at the scene?","Liu Weihong: ...","Liu Weihong muttered, At the time, at the time there were only the two of them, and a child...","Zheng Weigong sneered, So there are no witnesses?","A three- or four-year-old child could be questioned, but the words of a child that age could not be used as testimony.","It wasn't that Zheng Weigong didn't believe Liu Weihong, but even if he did, what use was it?","Liu Weihong was destined to suffer in silence this time.","Ultimately, Qin Yuanzheng's family member was smart enough to use this trick to turn the tables.","If he had such a smart wife, his life might have been much smoother.","Zheng Weigong was furious inside, but on the surface, he still spoke to Liu Weihong in a gentle tone.","Because he had already decided to dump her. Since they wouldn't need to see each other in the future, he could naturally afford to speak nicely.","He said, I am going to visit Qin Yuanzheng's family member in a bit. I heard Qin Yuanzheng dotes on his wife. He definitely won't let this matter go easily. And since you went into their home to steal a child, this isn't just a dispute anymore; it is a crime. I can only try my best to smooth things over for you, but I might not be able to protect you.","Saying this, he added, But don't worry. For the sake of our affection over the past few years, I will do my best to arrange things and find a labor camp that is a bit closer.","Hearing these words, Liu Weihong was completely shocked. Beyond the shock came anger, as well as sheer panic.","Enduring her dizziness, she sat up and glared fiercely at Zheng Weigong. What do you mean by that? How can you take their side and indiscriminately send me to a labor camp?","As she spoke, Liu Weihong suddenly became agitated, her voice turning shrill. Didn't I do all this for you? I did it to help you get that child back!","Zheng Weigong's face darkened. He stared gloomily at Liu Weihong and sneered, You wanted to get the child back, so you went next door to the military compound, to the new house Qin Yuanzheng just moved into, and stole the child? Are you sure you were helping me, and not ruining me?","As he said this, his face was full of hostility.","Originally, he and Zheng Wenhui could have quietly brought the child back, but Liu Weihong insisted on running to the Revolutionary Committee to report him, making the matter known to everyone.","And now she had run to a military officer's home to steal a child.","It was only because Qin Yuanzheng had just moved into his new home and no guards had been assigned there yet. Otherwise, with Liu Weihong's behavior, she might have been shot dead on the spot.","Qiao Lanshu's injury was of secondary importance now. Letting Qin Yuanzheng and the others know that Zheng Weigong cared about this child—that was the biggest problem!","Zheng Weigong stared at Liu Weihong, his voice cold and heavy as he warned her, As things stand, if you obediently go to the labor camp, I can still look at our past affection and help you a bit. But if you make a fuss and start talking nonsense at the Revolutionary Committee or the public security bureau, you had better watch your back.","Liu Weihong looked at Zheng Weigong in disbelief, momentarily too intimidated by him to speak.","Since she had been with Zheng Weigong, she actually didn't know much about his affairs.","But even so, he was still threatening her!","Before she could utter a sarcastic remark, Zheng Weigong stood up and walked out.","He told his secretary to communicate with the Revolutionary Committee members and pull some strings for Liu Weihong.","Meanwhile, he headed toward Qiao Lanshu's ward.","There was a guard stationed at the door of Qiao Lanshu's ward.","He arrived at the door, and soon, the guard called Qin Yuanzheng out.","Zheng Weigong smiled politely and said, Brigade Commander Qin, regarding this incident, I apologize on behalf of Liu Weihong. It is all a misunderstanding. She mistakenly thought that the child was my illegitimate son, which is why she did such a thing.","Qin Yuanzheng's expression was cold. Section Chief Zheng, Liu Weihong is your family member, isn't she? Your family member injured mine, and that is not something a simple apology can resolve.","Unexpectedly, Zheng Weigong actually replied, Liu Weihong is not my family member. She is merely my family's nanny.","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","Zheng Weigong spoke up again. \"Still, since the nanny caused trouble, I must take responsibility for her actions. Brigade Commander Qin, how would you like to resolve this? Just name your compensation. As long as it is within my power, I absolutely won't refuse.\"","Since Zheng Weigong had made his stance so accommodating, it was hard for Qin Yuanzheng to keep pressing the issue.","However, when it came to Liu Weihong's identity, he was utterly shocked that Zheng Weigong had outright dismissed her as a mere nanny.","That was truly...","For a moment, Qin Yuanzheng was completely stunned into silence."]},{"number":204,"title":"Chapter 204: If You're Going to Play Sick, See It Through","paragraphs":["Zheng Weigong kept a very low profile, putting on a show of fully cooperating no matter how Qin Yuanzheng intended to pursue the matter.","Meanwhile, Liu Weihong was also taken away by the people from the Public Security Bureau to be interrogated about her stealing the child.","Qin Yuanzheng originally thought that Zheng Weigong would at least speak up for Liu Weihong and try to protect her.","After all, Liu Weihong kept claiming to be Zheng Weigong's family member, and the two of them did live together.","As it turned out, Zheng Weigong showed absolutely no affection.","Such cold-blooded ruthlessness was truly rare.","No wonder he wasn't afraid of being reported for improper relations with women, living with Liu Weihong for so long without a marriage certificate.","It turned out he just treated her as a nanny.","After Zheng Weigong left, Qin Yuanzheng went back to check on Qiao Lanshu again, and finally went to meet Guan Wenjun with a dark expression.","Zhong Mei was holding the child, waiting outside with Guan Wenjun. When Qin Yuanzheng came over, he happened to see Zheng Wenhui, the director of the Women's Federation, asking Zhong Mei for the child.","Wearing a Dacron shirt and leather shoes, along with glasses, Zheng Wenhui smiled with an intellectual and gentle demeanor. She was followed by two clerks from the Women's Federation office, and all three were trying to persuade Zhong Mei.","Zheng Wenhui smiled and said, \"It's so wonderful that you helped find this child! A few days ago, when Brigade Commander Qin sent the child to the Women's Federation, I originally wanted to take him home to settle him in. But unexpectedly, on the way home, the child ran away. For the past few days, our Women's Federation has been cooperating with the Public Security Bureau to find him, but we had no luck.\"","Sighing, Zheng Wenhui continued, \"Fortunately, you helped find him. Our Women's Federation has already specially arranged for someone to take care of this child. Today, we will take him back first, and then fully cooperate with the Public Security Bureau to find his family.\"","Hearing Zheng Wenhui say this, Zhong Mei hesitantly glanced at Guan Wenjun.","To Zhong Mei, these government officials were powerful and influential. Since the director of the Women's Federation had spoken, she didn't know what to say.","But this child was brought home and raised by Qiao Lanshu. Even if he really had to be sent to the Women's Federation, it should be Qiao Lanshu who sent him. Zhong Mei would not make a decision on Qiao Lanshu's behalf.","Being stared at by Zhong Mei's eager eyes, Guan Wenjun felt a bit smug.","With his hands in his pockets, he stood in front of Zhong Mei, looked at Zheng Wenhui, and said, \"You guys already lost the child once. If we hand him over to you again and you lose him, what then? Next time, you might not have such good luck to find him.\"","Zheng Wenhui looked at Guan Wenjun, feeling a bit impatient with him in her heart. \"Director Guan, taking care of abducted children is the job of our Women's Federation. Your Revolutionary Committee shouldn't be meddling in this kind of thing, right?\"","Besides, the current Revolutionary Committee was not the same as before. Who knows, it might be abolished one day.","When that time comes, this Guan Wenjun would definitely be like a rat crossing the street, chased and beaten by everyone.","What did he have to be arrogant about now?","Zheng Wenhui kept chattering on, but her main point was that she must take the child back.","Guan Wenjun mocked her, \"Director Zheng, you are in such a desperate hurry that it makes people think you are the human trafficker.\"","Zheng Wenhui: \"...\"","Zheng Wenhui's face turned livid with anger, but there was nothing she could do about Guan Wenjun.","Guan Wenjun retorted against Zheng Wenhui and then left with Zhong Mei and Niuwa.","Left with no choice, Zheng Wenhui could only leave the hospital, wondering if she should go talk to Qin Yuanzheng.","After all, it was Qin Yuanzheng who had sent the child to the Women's Federation last time. If she went to him again, perhaps he would agree.","Just as she was preparing to go find Qin Yuanzheng, her brother Zheng Weigong came out of the hospital.","Seeing Zheng Wenhui standing at the hospital entrance, Zheng Weigong knew she had failed to bring the child back.","This was quite normal. As things stood, neither the Public Security Bureau nor Qin Yuanzheng would hand the child over to Zheng Wenhui again.","From a distance, Zheng Weigong gave Zheng Wenhui a look, and the siblings left the hospital with their people.","After getting in the car, Zheng Wenhui said in frustration, \"Brother, it seems we can't send this child away.\"","Zheng Weigong's face darkened. Staring at the fleeting street scenes outside the window, a fierce look flashed in his eyes. \"Even if this child is brought back, we can't send him away anymore. Do you think you can lose the child a second time after already losing him once?\"","Zheng Wenhui whispered, \"Then what should we do? If Han Wenlin really comes to take up his post and recognizes us, what then?\"","Back then, it was Han Wenlin who had personally executed their parents.","Because the siblings had their household registrations placed in a relative's home from birth, they had not been tracked down.","They had traveled thousands of miles to settle in Longcheng, finally managed to secure high positions, and successfully hid their identities for so long.","What if they were found out?","After all, Zheng Weigong looked very much like their father, and as he grew older, the resemblance only increased. Once Han Wenlin saw him, he would definitely recognize him.","If an investigation was launched then, their situation would become extremely dangerous.","With a guilty conscience, the siblings thought about striking first to deal with Han Wenlin.","Zheng Weigong whispered, \"We just need to get rid of Han Wenlin. Forget about the child's matter.\"","Zheng Wenhui was startled by these words. \"Brother, Han Wenlin is a soldier who transferred to the Public Security Bureau. I'm afraid it won't be that easy...\"","Zheng Weigong replied, \"I will arrange it. This must be done.\"","Their subordinates had already been exposed. Si Zhemao and Guan Wenjun had investigated over there for months and finally gave up without digging deeper.","If Han Wenlin arrived now and aimed at them, what would they do?","...","In the hospital, Zhong Mei held Niuwa and went to see Qiao Lanshu.","Guan Wenjun also followed behind them. Shortly after, Qin Yuanzheng came out and called out to Guan Wenjun.","Guan Wenjun looked at Zhong Mei, then at Qin Yuanzheng. His feet felt glued to the ground, refusing to walk over. He asked from a distance, \"Lao Qin, what are you calling me for?\"","Qin Yuanzheng stood at the main entrance of the hospital, frowning at Guan Wenjun. \"There's a mission.\"","Guan Wenjun muttered, \"I'm still on vacation, what mission requires me to go...\"","As he was muttering, Zhong Mei turned her head and glanced at him.","Guan Wenjun's heart skipped a beat, and he wanted to keep following Zhong Mei forward.","Zhong Mei was filled with trepidation, wondering why this man kept secretly glancing at her and following her everywhere. Did he recognize her and was afraid she would run away, so he followed so closely?","Zhong Mei nervously peeked at him. Sensing that Guan Wenjun was turning his head to look over, she retracted her gaze in a flash, then lowered her head and hurriedly ran into Qiao Lanshu's ward carrying Niuwa.","Guan Wenjun stood in the corridor at the doorway, reaching out to stroke his chin, feeling overjoyed inwardly.","Don't think he didn't notice that Zhong Mei was secretly looking at him!","She definitely had feelings for him, otherwise why would she keep sneaking glances at him?","Just as Guan Wenjun's mind was wandering, Qin Yuanzheng strode over and glared at him with a dark face. \"Let's go, there's a mission, we need your Revolutionary Committee's help.\"","Guan Wenjun was somewhat dissatisfied. \"Why is there another mission? Are you going to leave your injured wife behind and go on a mission again?\"","Qin Yuanzheng led Guan Wenjun outside, saying as they walked, \"Didn't you say before that you wanted to go to the Longcheng City Public Security Bureau?\"","At the mention of this, Guan Wenjun became a little irritable. \"Didn't Commander Li say it was a no-go? That position is already taken.\"","Thinking about it still made Guan Wenjun feel awful.","There was originally a vacancy at the Public Security Bureau that he could have stepped right into.","As it turned out, the position had already been internally secured for some transferred military officer, leaving his employment prospects up in the air once again.","Qin Yuanzheng lowered his voice. \"The Public Security Bureau is out, but what do you think about the Supply Section?\"","Guan Wenjun paused in his tracks, looking at Qin Yuanzheng in shock. Then, he immediately slung an arm around Qin Yuanzheng's neck and asked in a hushed voice, \"Lao Qin, do you have some inside information again? Is there a vacancy in the Supply Section? How come I haven't heard about it?\"","He paused for a moment and then asked, \"Is Zheng Weigong being transferred?\"","Qin Yuanzheng brushed Guan Wenjun's arm away, opened the car door, and got into the driver's seat.","Guan Wenjun hurried to get into the passenger seat.","He urged anxiously, \"Hurry up and tell me! What do you mean by leaving me hanging like this?\"","As Qin Yuanzheng drove, he explained, \"My men found out some news. They say Han Wenlin's son went missing a month ago.\"","After rescuing Niuwa previously, Qin Yuanzheng had not only notified the Public Security Bureau, the Women's Federation, and the Revolutionary Committee, but he had also asked his people in the military to help ask around and see if anyone had lost a child.","At first, he had misjudged the situation, thinking the child was lost around the Longcheng area, so he had people follow the train routes and ask around the cities along the way, but to no avail.","Later, Qin Yuanzheng expanded the search radius, having people contact comrades and friends in major cities to ask if anyone locally had lost a child, verifying Niuwa's information against each case.","By doing this, they actually managed to collect a lot of information on missing children.","One of them matched Niuwa.","Guan Wenjun asked in surprise, \"So you're saying this kid is very likely Han Wenlin's son?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. \"Because of his missing child, Han Wenlin has already postponed his appointment for a month. According to his original work schedule, he should have reported to the Longcheng City Public Security Bureau last month, and Deputy Chief Li Jianlin should have gone to serve as the chief of the Wenxing County Public Security Bureau last month as well.\"","Listening to all this, Guan Wenjun was still a bit confused. \"Then what does this have to do with Zheng Weigong? Why would he be transferred, and can I really go to the Supply Section?\"","Guan Wenjun's mind was entirely consumed by his own job prospects; he hadn't thought that deeply about it at all.","Qin Yuanzheng shot him a glance and sneered, \"Guan Wenjun, with a brain like yours, you still want to be the chief of the Public Security Bureau?\"","Guan Wenjun was speechless.","Qin Yuanzheng continued, \"Let me tell you, Zheng Weigong cares a lot about this child. When the child went missing earlier and some people were quietly searching for him, I knew something was off. Right when Xiao Qiao was sent to the hospital, I had someone look into the backgrounds of Zheng Weigong and his sister. They aren't from Longcheng; they are from Jincheng, a thousand miles away. And Han Wenlin is also from Jincheng.\"","Hearing this, Guan Wenjun finally began to understand.","He said in a low voice, \"You suspect that Zheng Weigong has a grudge against Han Wenlin, so he deliberately abducted his child?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded; that was exactly what he suspected.","Guan Wenjun said in disbelief, \"Misfortune shouldn't extend to family. Are there really people who would sell their enemy's child for a personal vendetta? Zheng Weigong is actually that kind of person?\"","Qin Yuanzheng didn't say anything.","But in this world, what kind of people didn't exist?","Qin Yuanzheng had seen no shortage of cases where people took their grievances out on children. One should never underestimate the malice of certain people.","Because of this, ever since Qin Yuanzheng had a wife and child, he had become much more cautious in his dealings than before. Even Commander Li said he wasn't as sharp and aggressive as he used to be.","He had previously decided to live as a bachelor for the rest of his life. Without a wife or children, he naturally acted recklessly, full of sharp edges.","But now, how could things be compared to the past?","Qin Yuanzheng said coldly, \"Because of the child, Han Wenlin had already planned to give up taking up his post in Longcheng. However, I've already had someone contact him to come to Longcheng as soon as possible to identify the child first. To prevent anyone from interfering, you will take some men to Jincheng today and escort Han Wenlin here.\"","Guan Wenjun was speechless again.","Guan Wenjun had finally managed to sort through all the convoluted details in his head, only to hear this. He immediately said, \"Lao Qin, I'm still on leave! I just got back not long ago, can't you send someone else?\"","Qin Yuanzheng parked the car at the main entrance of the Revolutionary Committee. Hearing this, he immediately sneered. He looked at Guan Wenjun and asked, \"Then should the vacancy in the Supply Section be given to someone else too?\"","Guan Wenjun was at a loss for words.","He said, lacking confidence, \"These are all just your speculations. What if you guessed wrong and this has nothing to do with Zheng Weigong? Then the vacancy you mentioned definitely wouldn't exist, and wouldn't I have made a trip for nothing? Besides, they might not necessarily target Han Wenlin, right? He's a military officer, could he really be ambushed by these people?\"","Guan Wenjun was thinking about Zhong Mei in his heart. He still wanted to test the waters with her attitude; if it worked out, he might reluctantly try dating her.","So he didn't want to leave Longcheng right now.","But meeting Qin Yuanzheng's stern gaze, his heart still skipped a beat.","Qin Yuanzheng said with a cold face, \"Rambling on so much, are you going or not?\"","If it weren't for his friendship with Guan Wenjun, Qin Yuanzheng really wouldn't bother to help him out.","Back when they were teenagers, Guan Wenjun had also served in the military.","They had known each other for over a decade. Although they had had their differences in the past, their former camaraderie was still there.","But if Guan Wenjun continued to be so useless like mud that couldn't stick to a wall, Qin Yuanzheng would just wash his hands of him.","Guan Wenjun shuddered and immediately said, \"I'll go, of course I'll go! But you can't just make me do the work without letting me complain a bit, right? I'm still on leave, you know.\"","He had emphasized three times that he was still on leave.","Qin Yuanzheng couldn't be bothered to entertain him, only saying, \"Do it quickly. Get your work arranged within an hour, and then head straight to Jincheng to find Han Wenlin. Drive there and don't alert anyone. I'll arrange for some men to go with you. I'll write the application and report, you don't need to worry about it.\"","There were still some highly skilled young men in Qin Yuanzheng's unit, and this was a good opportunity for them to go out and gain some experience.","Guan Wenjun was still grumbling under his breath, but he quickly got out of the car and headed back into the Revolutionary Committee to sort out his work.","Qin Yuanzheng returned to the mining area unit and drafted three men to accompany Guan Wenjun to Jincheng.","Then, he ordered his men to continue investigating the backgrounds and past resumes of Zheng Weigong and his sister.","After keeping busy until late afternoon when the sky was turning dark, he finally drove back home first to check on Auntie Shi and An'an.","Then, he drove Auntie Shi and An'an to the hospital to deliver food to Qiao Lanshu and Zhong Mei.","Qiao Lanshu had been lying in the hospital for a day, feeling so restless and itchy all over that she couldn't stay in bed.","Zhong Mei lowered her voice and said, \"Since you are faking it, you need to make it look convincing. Stop shifting around so much, or you will give the game away.\"","Qiao Lanshu watched Niuwa running back and forth across the room and let out a heavy sigh. \"What happened to Liu Weihong? Has she been sentenced yet?\"","\"Not yet,\" Zhong Mei replied. \"You have to keep pretending to be sick. We can drop the act once she is officially sent off to the labor camp.\""]},{"number":205,"title":"Chapter 205: The child's family has arrived","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu's pretending to faint this time was entirely a choice made out of sheer anxiety and panic.","She had no choice. The last time Zhong Mei was in Yangcheng, she had smashed her blind date's head, which resulted in her being sent to a labor camp.","This time, they had gotten into a dispute and a physical fight with Liu Weihong, and Liu Weihong had accidentally cracked her own head. Who knew how the authorities would judge this?","Not only was Zhong Mei scared, but Qiao Lanshu was also worried.","So she simply fainted. Fortunately, although her method wasn't exactly moral, it was somewhat effective.","Lying in the hospital bed, she murmured to Zhong Mei, discussing their plan: \"Liu Weihong definitely won't accept this lying down. If they come to the doctor asking for my medical report, we need to keep our stories straight and say I have a concussion.\"","Zhong Mei poured a cup of warm water and, while feeding it to Niuwa, whispered, \"A concussion? What are the symptoms of a concussion?\"","Since ancient times, ailments of the brain have always been the hardest to explain.","Qiao Lanshu knew this as well, which was why she suggested it to Zhong Mei.","She said, \"We'll firmly insist that Liu Weihong knocked me out. She won't be able to argue her way out of it since she has no witnesses. We'll say she hit me with a carrying pole and knocked me unconscious. Even though there are no external injuries, I'm now suffering from severe dizziness, nausea, and when I shake my head, I can hear water sloshing. Wouldn't you say that's a concussion?\"","Zhong Mei was speechless.","Hearing this, Zhong Mei couldn't help but chuckle and nod. \"I think it could work, but they might not even come to ask. You have no idea what it was like earlier. When your man came over with those military officers, he looked so fierce. Just those military uniforms alone were intimidating enough. I don't think Liu Weihong will be able to cause any more trouble.\"","Zhong Mei also figured that Guan Wenjun from the Revolutionary Committee was Qiao Lanshu's friend, and Li Jianlin, the deputy director of the Public Security Bureau, had a pretty good relationship with Qin Yuanzheng.","Furthermore, Qin Yuanzheng himself was a high-ranking officer in the military.","Given all this, the opposing side likely wouldn't be able to stir up any fuss over this incident.","Of course, Zhong Mei's assumptions were slightly off the mark.","The reason this matter was resolved so quickly wasn't because Qin Yuanzheng was high-ranking and untouchable.","It was because Zheng Weigong had other things to attend to and had abandoned Liu Weihong.","Liu Weihong was now entirely on her own, with no backing and no family to help her. She didn't even have a workplace unit.","Under these circumstances, her fate was easy to imagine.","The plan Qiao Lanshu and Zhong Mei had spent so long discussing ended up being completely unnecessary.","As it was getting dark, Qin Yuanzheng arrived holding An'an, accompanied by Auntie Shi carrying an insulated lunch box, to visit Qiao Lanshu in the hospital.","As soon as Qin Yuanzheng walked in, he said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Hurry up and eat. After you finish, we'll go home together.\"","Qiao Lanshu was silent.","Qiao Lanshu peeked outside the door. Auntie Shi had already closed it and asked her, \"What are you looking at? There's no one else.\"","Qiao Lanshu finally breathed a sigh of relief. She immediately sat up in bed, full of energy, and looked at Qin Yuanzheng with bright eyes. \"Brother Zheng, we can go home?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded and placed An'an into Qiao Lanshu's arms. \"Of course we can go back. Look how much An'an missed you. Do you really want to stay in the hospital?\"","Staying in the hospital was so uncomfortable.","As soon as Qin Yuanzheng realized Qiao Lanshu was faking her fainting spell, he wanted to take her home.","However, Qin Yuanzheng still had to stay at the mining district military base for the next couple of days. Although Zhong Mei had found a suitable house, it hadn't been cleaned yet, and they hadn't bought furniture or other necessities.","Originally, she was supposed to go shopping with Qiao Lanshu today, but then this incident happened. Helplessly, they had to delay things for another two days.","Qiao Lanshu held An'an in her arms. An'an still couldn't sit up steadily, but she already knew how to roll around.","Upon seeing her mother, An'an broke into a wide smile, waving her arms and kicking her legs in Qiao Lanshu's embrace.","Qin Yuanzheng smiled and said, \"See, An'an missed you so much.\"","Qiao Lanshu beamed as she held An'an. She squeezed An'an's little feet and laughed, \"These short little legs sure have a lot of strength.\"","Qin Yuanzheng turned around and saw Niuwa lying on the bed, staring intently at An'an. He picked Niuwa up with one hand.","Caught off guard, Niuwa was left dangling in mid-air, struggling in vain as he shouted at the top of his lungs, \"Let me go! Let me go!\"","After being tied up by Liu Weihong, Niuwa had been much more well-behaved today. He hadn't run around or yelled and screamed anymore.","Who knows if he was just scared.","After all, when they were fighting in the courtyard that afternoon, Niuwa had been crying the whole time.","He was only a four-year-old child, and given his tumultuous past, it was truly pitiful.","Qiao Lanshu quickly said, \"Be careful, don't dislocate the child's arm. Give him to me.\"","Saying this, Qiao Lanshu held An'an with one arm and reached out with her other hand to grab Niuwa from Qin Yuanzheng's grasp.","Hearing Qiao Lanshu's words, Qin Yuanzheng placed Niuwa back on the bed. Niuwa immediately scrambled on all fours to hide behind Qiao Lanshu, glaring at Qin Yuanzheng from his safe spot.","Qin Yuanzheng let out a chuckle and said, \"This kid's got a pretty fierce glare.\"","He leaned in and asked Niuwa, \"Niuwa, do you know who Han Wenlin is?\"","Niuwa's eyes lit up. He proudly puffed out his chest and declared loudly, \"Han Weh-win is my daddy!\"","Qin Yuanzheng fell silent.","Hearing him say this, the heavy stone in Qin Yuanzheng's heart finally dropped.","Qiao Lanshu asked in surprise, \"Brother Zheng, did you find Niuwa's family?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. \"It looks like Niuwa's father is indeed Han Wenlin.\"","Qiao Lanshu asked, \"Han Wenlin? Who is that?\"","Niuwa, leaning against Qiao Lanshu, hurriedly interjected, \"My daddy! My daddy, Han Weh-win, is in the People's Liberation Army!\"","Hearing this, Auntie Shi couldn't help but laugh and said, \"Niuwa used to always say his name was Haye. I was wondering what kind of surname that was. So it turns out his surname is Han?\"","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head, somewhat exasperated. \"If his pronunciation had been just a little clearer, it wouldn't have taken us this long to find Han Wenlin.\"","When Niuwa spoke, some words were quite clear, but others were completely slurred.","Qiao Lanshu reached out and gave Niuwa an affectionate squeeze. \"Regardless, it's wonderful that we've found his family. After all, the child is still so young.\"","The four of them, along with the two children, had a simple dinner together in the hospital room. Afterwards, Qin Yuanzheng drove them back to the small courtyard.","Once they were all settled in, Qin Yuanzheng drove straight back to the mining district military base. Since he had nothing else to do, he decided to just work overtime and handle some official business.","Meanwhile, the verdict for Liu Weihong came down very quickly. Zheng Weigong completely washed his hands of her affairs, leaving her with no one to help her. For the crimes of stealing a child and injuring a military family member, she was sentenced to three years in a labor camp.","Fortunately for her, she wasn't sent to a remote and harsh location thousands of kilometers away, but rather to a farm a few hundred kilometers away to reclaim wasteland.","Not even leaving the province was already considered a good outcome. However, Liu Weihong was still dissatisfied. She cried and caused a scene at the police station for a whole day and night, yet Zheng Weigong never came to see her.","When Liu Weihong was sent to a labor camp, Qiao Lanshu was in the courtyard watching Niuwa play in the mud.","Auntie Shi sat next to her, holding An'an and soaking up the sun, while Zhong Mei had already left for work.","When Qiao Lanshu heard the news, she sighed and said to Auntie Shi, \"When Liu Weihong was a supervisor at the food factory, she was so proud. That Zheng Weigong bought her a coat, leather shoes, a watch... I thought they were seriously dating, but it turns out Zheng Weigong is that kind of person.\"","Liu Weihong was actually just a bit vain. There was nothing wrong with her dating Zheng Weigong, but she probably never expected him to be such a cold and ruthless man.","Auntie Shi held An'an, gently patting his back to coax him to sleep, and whispered, \"That Zheng Weigong is the section chief of the supply department, right? Is a director in the supply department really that rich? Things like watches and coats don't come cheap.\"","Qiao Lanshu also lowered her voice. \"I found it strange too. Brother Zheng was a regimental commander at the time, but even with his benefits and salary, he would have had to save up for months to buy those things for me. Yet Liu Weihong had just started dating Zheng Weigong, and he bought them for her right away. He was extremely generous.\"","Thinking about it now, where exactly did Zheng Weigong get his money?","It was still a planned economy; people not only lacked money, but they also lacked ration coupons.","Could it be that the section chief of the supply department had exceptionally good perks?","Hearing this, Auntie Shi sighed again and whispered, \"Xiao Qiao, you don't know, but these officials have many ways to make money.\"","Auntie Shi had been worrying lately about her son's employment.","She said, \"My second son is out of work, isn't he? He came to me a few days ago and said they are building a railway down south and are looking for workers. He knows someone who can get him in, but it will cost five hundred yuan.\"","Qiao Lanshu looked at Auntie Shi in surprise. \"Five hundred yuan? Just to go build a railway on a construction site?\"","She paused for a moment before adding, \"That's hard labor. It shouldn't be that difficult to get into, right?\"","Besides, five hundred yuan was way too expensive!","At that time, the monthly salary of a regular worker was only about thirty-five to forty yuan.","Five hundred yuan was more than a year's wages for an official factory worker.","Auntie Shi sighed once more. She had been sighing a lot these past two days. After all, five hundred yuan was no small sum. Her son asked her for it, and she couldn't just refuse, but she couldn't come up with that much money all at once either, so she told him to wait.","However, her son was unwilling to wait and was currently throwing a tantrum about it.","Auntie Shi sighed and said, \"It is a bit expensive, but the contact said they could help get him a job as a supervisor. A supervisor is different from an ordinary worker. I heard they get to sit in an office and manage people. He wouldn't have to carry bricks himself, so it shouldn't be tiring.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Speaking of this, Auntie Shi continued, \"This five hundred yuan isn't just for the middleman. Most of it has to go to the personnel department or the labor bureau. Tell me, why is Zheng Weigong from the supply department so rich? All he has to do is open his mouth and ask. For these people, isn't getting money the easiest thing in the world?\"","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu still advised, \"Buying a job for five hundred yuan is something you should be very careful about. It's a pity I don't know anyone at the labor bureau, otherwise I could help you ask around.\"","As for that railway construction site, the military units overseeing it weren't under Qin Yuanzheng's jurisdiction. Qin Yuanzheng managed the mining area. One was in the north and the other in the south, so he might not have any say in the matter anyway.","Auntie Shi knew this as well, which was why she felt embarrassed to bring it up with her employers.","It was only because the conversation naturally led there that she mentioned it to Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu still felt that paying five hundred yuan for a job was far too risky.","She advised Auntie Shi, \"Auntie, don't rush into this job thing. Five hundred yuan is not a small amount, after all. You need to be cautious. Even though jobs are hard to find these days, getting a temporary position isn't that difficult. Don't be too hasty.\"","Auntie Shi smiled helplessly and said no more.","She had originally thought the same way, but her son refused to work as a temp.","He said being a temp was humiliating and made him lose face in front of his friends with regular jobs. Plus, it would make it harder to find a girlfriend.","Anyway, he had his heart set on that railway site and insisted on spending five hundred yuan to buy the supervisor job.","Thinking of this, Auntie Shi sighed silently.","They stayed quietly at home for two days. Qiao Lanshu hardly went out, staying in with Auntie Shi to watch the two children.","On the third day, Qin Yuanzheng hurried back. As soon as he entered the courtyard gate, he saw Qiao Lanshu and immediately asked, \"Where is Niuwa?\"","Qiao Lanshu quickly replied, \"He's eating in the kitchen. What's wrong?\"","Qin Yuanzheng immediately strode toward the kitchen, saying over his shoulder, \"Han Wenlin has arrived. I'm taking Niuwa to see him.\"","Niuwa was currently in the kitchen, holding a peeled peach and munching on it.","It was the perfect season for peaches. Even fresh peaches required ration coupons. Qin Yuanzheng had bought some and brought them all back for Qiao Lanshu to eat.","Qiao Lanshu and Auntie Shi made some canned peaches together and kept half a box to eat themselves.","Niuwa had a great appetite and loved to eat everything. He had already devoured two large peaches that morning.","Qin Yuanzheng walked in and saw Niuwa's face covered in peach juice. He couldn't help but say, \"Look at your face, you look like a little messy cat.\"","Saying that, he casually grabbed a towel, wiped Niuwa's face clean, and then picked him up to leave.","Seeing this, Auntie Shi couldn't help but say, \"Chief, that's...\"","That was a dishcloth! How could he use it to wipe the child's face?","But before Auntie Shi could finish her sentence, Qin Yuanzheng had already finished wiping Niuwa's face and carried him away.","Auntie Shi looked at the towel and hurriedly took it to wash it clean.","Niuwa was still holding the peach and chewing on it. Qiao Lanshu followed Qin Yuanzheng and asked, \"Han Wenlin is here? Why didn't he come here with you? Where are you going to meet him?\"","Holding Niuwa with one arm and taking Qiao Lanshu's hand with the other, Qin Yuanzheng said, \"Han Wenlin was chased and attacked on the road. He got shot in the arm and is currently at the military hospital. Come with me. It's good timing since Niuwa listens to you.\"","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu immediately asked with concern, \"He got shot? Does he have enemies?\"","So Niuwa was abducted and sold because of Han Wenlin's enemies after all?","Qiao Lanshu whispered, \"In that case, should we hold off on sending Niuwa back for now?\"","What if he gets targeted by Han Wenlin's enemies again?","Niuwa was still so young; he was completely innocent.","Qin Yuanzheng's face was very serious. He said, \"He does have enemies, and they have significant backing. The three subordinates I sent over almost failed to protect him. Guan Wenjun was also injured; his arm is fractured, and he's in the hospital too.\"","Han Wenlin was a transferred military officer and had good combat skills himself. Along with Guan Wenjun and three other soldiers, the five of them were driving in one car from Jincheng toward Longcheng.","But they were ambushed on the road.","Guan Wenjun had sped all the way back, but the car ended up flipping over. That was exactly how he had broken his arm.","Fortunately, they had made it back in one piece.","The first thing they did upon arriving in Longcheng was to report to the military district so that troops could be dispatched.","Han Wenlin, on the other hand, was completely innocent. He was utterly clueless when questioned and had absolutely no idea who he had offended.","He had also always believed that his son had simply wandered off and gotten lost. He had suffered and blamed himself for a long time, regretting that he had been too busy with work to focus on his child.","Holding Niuwa in her arms, Qiao Lanshu got into the car and said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"So, shall we go see Han Wenlin first, and then visit Guan Wenjun?\"","As he drove, Qin Yuanzheng replied, \"There is no need to visit Guan Wenjun. Let him suffer on his own.\"","Guan Wenjun's injury was purely due to his lack of physical training; otherwise, a simple car flip wouldn't have resulted in a broken bone.","If Qin Yuanzheng had been in his shoes, he wouldn't have been injured at all.","No wonder the higher-ups hadn't assigned Guan Wenjun to the police department—he really wasn't cut out for it."]},{"number":206,"title":"Chapter 206: Even if you gave this child away, no one would want him.","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng's expression was very serious. He said, \"He does have enemies, and they have quite the background. The three subordinates I sent over barely managed to protect him. Guan Wenjun was also injured; he broke his arm and is currently hospitalized.\"","Han Wenlin was a transferred military officer and had good combat skills himself. Guan Wenjun and the three other soldiers, making it five people in total including Han Wenlin, drove a single car from Jincheng towards Longcheng.","However, they were ambushed on the road.","Guan Wenjun sped all the way back, but the car eventually flipped over. That was how Guan Wenjun fractured his arm.","Fortunately, they managed to make it back safely.","The first thing they did upon arriving in Longcheng was report to the military region, which then dispatched troops to take action.","Han Wenlin was completely innocent in all this; he was completely clueless and had absolutely no idea who he had offended.","He had also always believed that his son had simply wandered off and gotten lost. He had suffered and blamed himself for a long time, cursing himself for being too busy with work and not paying enough attention to his child.","Qiao Lanshu got into the car holding Niuwa and asked Qin Yuanzheng, \"Then should we go see Han Wenlin first, and then visit Guan Wenjun?\"","As Qin Yuanzheng drove, he replied, \"There's no need to see Guan Wenjun. Let him suffer on his own.\"","Guan Wenjun was purely slacking on his training; otherwise, he wouldn't have broken his arm just from a flipped car.","If it had been Qin Yuanzheng in that situation, he wouldn't have gotten hurt at all.","No wonder the higher-ups didn't let Guan Wenjun transfer to the Public Security Bureau; he really wasn't suited for it.","...","Qin Yuanzheng brought Qiao Lanshu and Niuwa to the military hospital.","Upon arriving, they headed straight up to the third floor to the private ward where Han Wenlin was staying.","Inside the ward, Han Wenlin was lying on the bed, with Deputy Bureau Chief Li Jianlin of the Public Security Bureau standing beside him.","Guards stood at the door, all holding guns, securing the entrance tightly.","When Qin Yuanzheng approached, the two guards saluted him and then opened the ward door.","Qin Yuanzheng then led Qiao Lanshu inside.","Qiao Lanshu was still holding Niuwa in her arms. Niuwa seemed to know that he was here to meet his father, craning his little neck to peek inside.","Seeing Qin Yuanzheng arrive, Deputy Bureau Chief Li Jianlin quickly stood up to greet him, a worried look on his face. \"Oh, Brigade Commander Qin, you're finally here. Comrade Han couldn't wait any longer; he asked me several times to take him to your house. If I hadn't been afraid we'd miss you on the way, I would have taken him out the door by now.\"","Hearing the commotion, Han Wenlin immediately sat up straight in bed. His arm had recently suffered a gunshot wound and was now bandaged up. The rest of his body only had minor injuries that didn't affect his mobility.","After all, as a recently transferred military officer, his physical fitness was excellent.","Han Wenlin was a typical northern man: tall and burly, with rugged features and dark skin.","He was actually only around thirty, but with his stubble and haggard face, he looked more like he was in his forties.","Upon seeing Qin Yuanzheng, he quickly got out of bed and hurried over. \"Brigade Commander Qin, you're finally here.\"","If they hadn't arrived soon, he really wouldn't have been able to sit still.","Lying in the hospital all day unable to do anything had made him incredibly anxious.","Han Wenlin had also been a regimental-level officer in the military, but because he and Qin Yuanzheng were not in the same military region or branch, they hadn't known each other before this.","Han Wenlin had applied for a transfer because his wife had passed away.","He didn't want to leave his child in the countryside indefinitely. His elderly mother had poor eyesight and lacked the energy, so he feared she wouldn't be able to take good care of his child.","He had been a soldier for over ten years and had never been able to take care of his family. Taking advantage of the country's current troop reduction plan, he submitted his transfer application so he could return to a stable job, care for his mother, and raise his child.","But his fears came true. He had only left his child in the countryside for about half a year when he received an urgent telegram from the village chief back home, saying the child had gone missing. The whole village had helped search for half a month, but to no avail.","Han Wenlin hurried back and mobilized all his connections and authority, searching for over a month, but still couldn't find him.","Han Wenlin was physically and mentally exhausted.","Qin Yuanzheng looked at him. The two exchanged military salutes, and then Qin Yuanzheng asked, \"Comrade Han, I heard you suffered a gunshot wound. How is your injury? Are you feeling any better?\"","Han Wenlin didn't answer Qin Yuanzheng's question.","Because all his attention was focused on Niuwa. He hadn't seen him in a while, and his child had grown so much.","When he had sent Niuwa to the countryside, Niuwa was only a little over three years old.","Now, Niuwa was fair and chubby, and his clothes were clean and neat.","He looked like he had grown taller and gained some weight.","But looking at Niuwa's eyes and brows, it was clear that Niuwa looked a lot like him. He was definitely his biological son.","Han Wenlin's eyes instantly turned red. He bypassed Qin Yuanzheng and reached out to hug Niuwa. \"Son, do you still remember Daddy?\"","Niuwa stared at Han Wenlin with a somewhat complicated expression.","It was the kind of look that showed he recognized who Han Wenlin was, yet felt that Han Wenlin was a stranger, while also being a little afraid of him.","Aside from that, Qiao Lanshu also felt he was a bit shy.","Niuwa hugged Qiao Lanshu's arm tightly and buried his face in her embrace, occasionally popping his head out to sneak little glances at Han Wenlin.","But he simply wouldn't let Han Wenlin hold him. When Han Wenlin reached out, he even shrank back.","Seeing his son's expression, Han Wenlin couldn't hold back his tears.","He didn't force a hug on Niuwa, but silently withdrew his hand and wiped his tears with his sleeve.","Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng exchanged a glance. Since the two of them were now parents themselves, they could deeply understand Han Wenlin's feelings.","Having been silent for a long time, Li Jianlin couldn't help but ask, \"Comrade Han, so are you certain this Niuwa is your long-lost child?\"","A man does not shed tears lightly; Han Wenlin had already forced his tears back.","Looking at his son, Han Ye, who sneaked glances at him from time to time, his heart was filled with emotion.","At this very moment, a heavy weight was finally lifted from his heart, and he finally felt he could face going to his late wife's grave to burn paper offerings.","After all, from the moment he found out his son was missing until now, he hadn't even dared to look at a photo of his wife.","He nodded and said, \"Yes, he's my son. I was too busy before and rarely went home, so the child isn't familiar with me. Even if he recognizes me now, he probably won't be willing to leave with me.\"","His elderly mother was still in the countryside and had fallen ill several times out of worry.","The child did recognize the old lady, but it was thousands of miles away, and he wasn't prepared to put the child through such a long journey.","He decided he might as well settle down right here, take up his post at the Public Security Bureau, and then hire a nanny to take care of Niuwa, or simply send Niuwa to a nearby kindergarten for cadres' children.","As for his elderly mother back home, he naturally planned to bring her to Longcheng as well.","However, the old lady was advanced in years, and she wasn't very willing to leave her homeland to live in Longcheng.","With his family matters unresolved and enemies hiding in the shadows, Han Wenlin really had too much on his plate to handle everything.","But fortunately, at least his child had been found, and that was lucky enough.","Hearing this, Qin Yuanzheng said to Han Wenlin, This child will definitely achieve great things in the future. It really wasn't easy getting him back.","Deputy Director Li Jianlin quickly chimed in, That's for sure! Not just anyone has the luck to be rescued by Brigade Commander Qin.","Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu rarely went out, let alone took the train.","It just so happened that day they were heading to the labor camp to find Zhong Mei, and it also happened that Qin Yuanzheng had bought Qiao Lanshu a pack of instant noodles.","At the time, Niuwa was purely hungry and drawn over by the aroma of the noodles.","Otherwise, with them staying in the soft sleeper carriage and Niuwa with the human traffickers in the hard sleeper carriage, once the traffickers drugged Niuwa and he slept the whole way...","By now, who knows which remote corner of the country Han Ye would have been trafficked to.","Qiao Lanshu coaxed Niuwa, saying, Good Niuwa, good boy, go call your daddy. This is your daddy.","Niuwa pursed his lips and smiled a little shyly. He looked at Han Wenlin but still didn't say anything.","Han Wenlin wasn't in a hurry. He smiled and said, Niuwa? Is that the name you gave him?","Qin Yuanzheng replied, No, the police chief of the neighboring city gave it to him. He said the boy is like a calf, stubborn, hard to manage, and loves to run around.","Han Wenlin knew his child loved to run. Back in the village, he was always jumping up and down, very tough and mischievous.","Han Wenlin looked at Qiao Lanshu and added, Brigade Commander Qin, this must be your wife, right?","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. Whenever his wife was mentioned, a trace of a smile couldn't help but appear on his face. Thanks to my wife, otherwise, your child might not have been found.","The first time was on the train, and the second time was when he was taken by Liu Weihong. Both rescues were to Qiao Lanshu's credit.","While on the road, Han Wenlin had already heard about these events from Guan Wenjun and the others.","As the saying goes, great kindness cannot be fully thanked with words, because no matter how many times one says thank you, it cannot offset such a massive favor.","Han Wenlin looked solemnly at Qin Yuanzheng and said, If you ever need anything from me in the future, just ask. I absolutely won't decline.","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. What are your plans now?","Han Wenlin said, Settle into my new job, work, and find a kindergarten for the kid.","Li Jianlin couldn't help but interject, Comrade Han, do you have any leads on the people who were trying to kill you this time? Do you know who they are?","Han Wenlin nodded, his expression turning somewhat grave. I have suspects, but no evidence at the moment.","Li Jianlin couldn't resist asking, Who are they? Could it be your former enemies?","Han Wenlin used to be in the military and had carried out quite a few missions.","Having enemies was perfectly normal.","The fear was not knowing who the enemy was, getting hit from behind and not being able to find the culprit.","Han Wenlin and Qin Yuanzheng exchanged a glance, and Qin Yuanzheng spoke in a deep voice, Is it Zheng Weigong?","Before coming here, Han Wenlin certainly wouldn't have thought of Zheng Weigong and his sister.","But while on the road, he must have learned about Zheng Weigong and the others from Guan Wenjun.","So Han Wenlin should also know a few things.","Sure enough, Han Wenlin nodded, his brows tightly furrowed. It should be.","However, things hadn't been fully investigated yet, and without evidence, there was nowhere to start.","The three men sat to the side and talked for a while. Then, Qiao Lanshu sat down next to Qin Yuanzheng and put Niuwa down.","After all, Niuwa, oh no, he had to be called Han Ye now, wasn't exactly light. Qiao Lanshu had held him for a long time, and her arms were getting sore.","Niuwa was very mischievous and couldn't sit still for a moment.","However, he still recognized Han Wenlin. He was his father, after all.","He wandered around the room a few times, then sneakily approached Han Wenlin and looked up at him.","Han Wenlin reached out and rubbed his head, his eyes still a bit red.","Niuwa looked at Han Wenlin and grinned. Daddy.","Han Wenlin quickly responded, a look of pleasant surprise in his eyes.","He reached out and picked Niuwa up. Niuwa didn't hide this time, happily climbing up and down on Han Wenlin.","Qin Yuanzheng whispered to Qiao Lanshu, We finally sent this Niuwa away. If he stayed at our house any longer, Auntie Shi's vegetable garden would be completely torn up by him.","Qiao Lanshu covered her mouth and chuckled, whispering, What if An'an is like this in the future?","Every time she looked at Niuwa, Qiao Lanshu would think of An'an, wondering if An'an would be just as mischievous later on.","Qin Yuanzheng clearly thought of this too. He sighed and said, It would be great if it were a baby girl. A baby girl would definitely be as pretty and well-behaved as you.","His Comrade Xiao Qiao was gentle, well-behaved, pretty, and smart. Their son should inherit at least some of that, right?","The couple whispered to each other as if no one else was around.","At this moment, Niuwa suddenly climbed down from Han Wenlin and ran over to Qiao Lanshu.","Niuwa looked at Qiao Lanshu with eager eyes and said, Auntie Qiao, I don't have a mommy anymore. Can you be my mommy?","Qin Yuanzheng: ???","Han Wenlin: !!!","Li Jianlin was completely dumbfounded hearing this.","This little brat, how did his little brain even come up with that? He really was something else.","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu actually laughed. She hugged Niuwa and said, I'm sorry, Niuwa, Auntie can't be your mommy.","Niuwa hugged Qiao Lanshu tightly and said, Then what should we do? My daddy said he's going to take me home. I asked him to take you home with us too, but he shook his head.","Qin Yuanzheng: ???","Qin Yuanzheng shot Han Wenlin a glance, making Han Wenlin feel incredibly awkward.","Han Wenlin quickly stood up, not even daring to look at Qiao Lanshu, and hurriedly explained, Children say the darnedest things! Xiao Ye just likes your wife too much and said he wanted to live with her.","Qin Yuanzheng understood what he meant. Lately, Niuwa had indeed been very clingy with Qiao Lanshu.","He also listened to her very well.","The child probably really wanted a mother. After all, he was only four years old, and yearning for a mother's love was just instinct.","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said to Niuwa, Niuwa, you have to be good. Auntie needs to live with Uncle Qin, so I can't go back with you.","Hearing this, Niuwa looked at Han Wenlin. Then, he decisively declared, Then I don't want Daddy! I don't want Daddy, I want Auntie Qiao.","As he spoke, he even glanced at Qin Yuanzheng and reluctantly called out, Daddy.","Qin Yuanzheng said with a look of disdain, Don't just call people that. Your dad is right here.","Saying that, he pointed at Han Wenlin.","What a joke. He was already annoyed enough by this mischievous kid on a normal day, and now he wanted him to be his dad?","He wouldn't even want him if he were given away for free!"]},{"number":207,"title":"Chapter 207: You Are My Mother","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng was quite annoyed by Niuwa, but the boy was simply too clingy to Qiao Lanshu.","There was nothing he could do; you couldn't reason with a four-year-old child.","All the boy knew was that Qiao Lanshu spoke to him gently, looked at him with tender eyes, gave him delicious food every day, and bathed him.","It was a pity. He had originally wanted to sleep next to Auntie Qiao, but Auntie Shi wouldn't allow it.","Sigh, how wonderful would it be if the pretty and gentle Auntie Qiao were his mother?","At this thought, Niuwa sneaked another glance at Han Wenlin and muttered, I don't know him. I don't want to go home with him.","Everyone was speechless.","Han Wenlin felt deeply guilty toward the child, so he wasn't angry at all; instead, his heart just ached.","Holding Niuwa, Qiao Lanshu also felt a bit awkward.","Niuwa continued to protest, Auntie Qiao, I don't know him. I don't want to go with him. I want to go home with you.","Qiao Lanshu cast a helpless look at Qin Yuanzheng. Seeing Niuwa clinging to Qiao Lanshu for dear life, Qin Yuanzheng's eyes practically shot fire.","It had been so long since he could properly hold his wife, yet this stubborn little brat pestered her every single day. Even An'an wasn't this clingy!","Qin Yuanzheng turned to Han Wenlin. It's getting late, and I need to take my wife home. You should just take the child with you now.","He meant Niuwa, of course. It was best to have Han Wenlin take this little brat away quickly so he wouldn't have to look at him and feel annoyed.","Han Wenlin could see it too. His son adored Qiao Lanshu so much, which meant she must have taken excellent care of him recently.","Now, just to stay with her, the boy was even refusing to acknowledge his own biological father.","Qin Yuanzheng gave Han Wenlin a rather exasperated look. Even Deputy Police Chief Li Jianlin, who was standing nearby, chimed in, Comrade Han, it looks like you'll need to spend a lot more time with your son from now on. Just look at him, the child doesn't even recognize you.","Han Wenlin remained silent.","Smiling bitterly, Han Wenlin nodded. Of course I know. I'll spend much more time with him from now on.","However, none of them knew yet that although the police department currently seemed like a relaxed place with few staff and light workloads...","...it would soon become a crucial department with real authority. Tasks would pile up one after another, and in the future, they would only get busier, the work would become harder to execute, and the pressure would mount.","This was exactly why the higher-ups had specifically transferred Han Wenlin to be the Chief of Police.","Both Guan Wenjun and Deputy Chief Li Jianlin were slightly lacking when it came to tactical finesse and boldness.","The future Chief of Police needed to be someone capable of accomplishing great things.","But right now, Han Wenlin was still hoping for a relaxed job so he could spend more time with his son. I will spend more time with him and properly cultivate our father-son bond.","Qin Yuanzheng walked over. He grabbed Niuwa, who was clinging to Qiao Lanshu with all four limbs like a koala, pried him out of her arms, and effortlessly plopped him into Han Wenlin's embrace with one hand. There's no time like the present. You can start cultivating that father-son bond right now. It's getting late, so we'll be heading back.","Holding Niuwa with one arm, Han Wenlin nodded.","He wanted to say something else, but Qin Yuanzheng had already grabbed Qiao Lanshu's hand and hurried out the door. They walked so fast it was as if they were terrified someone might latch onto them.","Han Wenlin was speechless.","Niuwa struggled in Han Wenlin's arms, punching and kicking his biological father while crying at the top of his lungs, I want to go home with my Auntie Qiao! Let me go! Let me go!","Despite being such a large man, Han Wenlin was actually forced to stumble backward a few steps by his son's kicks.","But he still didn't let go. He simply comforted the boy, saying, Alright, alright, I know you like Auntie Qiao. Just come home with me first. Once we're settled in, I'll take you to see your Auntie Qiao, okay?","Niuwa asked tearfully, Then can Auntie come home with us?","Han Wenlin fell silent.","Recalling Qin Yuanzheng's displeased glare from earlier, Han Wenlin thought to himself that let alone having Qiao Lanshu come home with them, if the two of them so much as dared to look at her one more time, Qin Yuanzheng would probably resort to violence.","Watching Niuwa throw such a massive tantrum, Li Jianlin finally understood why the boy was named Niuwa, which meant calf.","He asked Han Wenlin, Comrade Han, do you need to stay in the hospital for the next few days? What did the doctor say?","Han Wenlin shook his head. There's no need to be hospitalized. I just need to come in regularly every day to change my dressings.","Hearing this, Deputy Chief Li breathed a sigh of relief. After all, they couldn't exactly have Han Wenlin living in the hospital with a child, could they?","Han Wenlin wasn't a local. He had just arrived and hadn't even completed his onboarding procedures yet. Now that he was injured, he definitely needed to rest and recuperate for a few days.","Deputy Chief Li looked at the still-crying Niuwa and felt a massive headache coming on. He quickly asked, Then where will you be staying for the next few days? Have you not applied for housing yet? I'll head back to the bureau later and submit an application for you. Your situation is special, so I'll push them to have the logistics department arrange a house for you as soon as possible. But where are you staying in the meantime?","Han Wenlin set the crying Niuwa down and said, I'll just stay at the guesthouse.","Han Wenlin had just survived an assassination attempt, making him a key protection target. The military had dispatched guards, and the police department had also assigned personnel to shadow him.","However, since he had already reported for duty in Longcheng, the people targeting him from the shadows probably wouldn't dare to make a move so easily.","Still, until the danger was completely neutralized, it really wasn't appropriate for an injured Han Wenlin to be dragging a four-year-old child around.","Feeling conflicted, Deputy Chief Li said, In that case, it's not very appropriate for the child to stay with you. How about...","As Deputy Chief Li spoke, he suddenly realized why Qin Yuanzheng had run away so fast earlier!","Qin Yuanzheng must have also realized that Han Wenlin was currently in no condition to look after a child. To accommodate Han Wenlin, the higher-ups would likely consider placing the child in temporary foster care with another family.","That was why Qin Yuanzheng had fled so quickly!","Damn it! As the Deputy Chief of the Police Department, Li Jianlin couldn't just run away!","What was he supposed to do now? He looked at Niuwa, who was rolling on the floor, crying and screaming for Qiao Lanshu to be his mother, and a wave of panic washed over him.","He definitely didn't want to drag this stubborn little calf back to his own home.","Just then, Niuwa, who had been rolling on the floor, suddenly scrambled up and angrily bolted for the door.","Han Wenlin's eyebrow twitched. He quickly took two strides forward and grabbed Niuwa by the back of his collar with his uninjured hand.","Suspended in mid-air, Niuwa flailed his limbs wildly and shouted at the top of his lungs, Let me go! Let me go!","Han Wenlin carried him back, set him down on the hospital bed, and said sternly, You were just kidnapped! Why haven't you learned your lesson? You're just a little kid. Where do you think you're going to run off to? What if you go outside and get snatched by someone again?","Hearing this, Niuwa remained defiant. He hopped off the bed and made another dash for the door.","He moved so fast that Han Wenlin was caught off guard for a second before he hurriedly gave chase and hauled Niuwa back once more.","Although Niuwa was very smart and quick on his feet, no matter how capable he was, he was still just a four-year-old child.","How could he possibly be a match for Han Wenlin?","But Niuwa was not only physically tough, his personality was also incredibly stubborn. He didn't get discouraged. Whenever Han Wenlin dragged him back, he would think of another way to run outside, and when dragged back again, he would run again.","Han Wenlin could only haul him back time and time again. After three times, Han Wenlin simply stood guard at the main door and refused to leave.","Niuwa, like a little calf, charged straight at his stomach.","Han Wenlin dodged and then hauled him back once more.","Watching from the sidelines, Deputy Chief Li became even more convinced that they couldn't temporarily adopt Niuwa.","He felt that such a mischievous child was better left for Qin Yuanzheng to deal with.","After half an hour, Niuwa was exhausted, lying on the hospital bed panting for breath to rest. Han Wenlin squatted by the main door guarding it and asked him, \"Are you still going to run?\"","Niuwa said pitifully, \"I'm just taking a break. I'll run again in a bit.\"","Han Wenlin: \"...\"","Han Wenlin stood up, sighed, and said, \"Then drink some water first.\"","Saying so, he took out his enamel mug and poured half a cup of warm water for Niuwa.","One of his arms had a gunshot wound, so he could only hold the cup with his other arm.","As a result, just as he brought the water over, he saw Niuwa, who had been lying on the bed, suddenly jump up, dive between his legs like a monkey, and dash past him.","Han Wenlin: \"!!!\"","Han Wenlin and Deputy Chief Li were both startled. The two quickly turned to chase after him, only to see Niuwa standing on his tiptoes, reaching out for the door handle.","However, because he was too short, he simply couldn't reach it.","The two men exchanged a glance, and Deputy Chief Li almost burst out laughing.","He said to Han Wenlin, \"Comrade Han, this son of yours is something else. He will definitely be a talent in the future.\"","Han Wenlin was caught between laughter and tears. He sighed and said, \"He's already hard to manage now, let alone in the future.\"","Han Wenlin was already starting to worry about the child's future education.","This Niuwa was clearly someone who refused to be disciplined. He had no idea what to do in the future.","Deputy Chief Li walked over, picked up Niuwa who was crying out of frustration because he couldn't reach the handle, and comforted him, \"Alright Niuwa, don't cry. Uncle knows you want to go find Auntie Qiao, right? Don't worry, Uncle will take you there right now.\"","Han Wenlin said somewhat hesitantly, \"Deputy Chief Li, maybe we should forget it. I can just take the child to the guesthouse.\"","Han Wenlin didn't want to trouble Qin Yuanzheng, because it was obvious that Qin Yuanzheng didn't want Niuwa pestering his wife.","That look in his eyes was simply too easy to read.","Deputy Chief Li quickly said, \"It's better to go to them. Besides Comrade Xiao Qiao, no one can handle this child of yours.\"","In any case, Deputy Chief Li didn't want to manage him.","Deputy Chief Li added, \"Comrade Han, you are still being hunted down right now. It's better not to take the child with you for now.\"","Even if Han Wenlin wanted to take care of the child himself, the higher-ups wouldn't allow it.","When the time came, the responsibility of taking care of this child might just fall onto Deputy Chief Li's head.","Therefore, under Deputy Chief Li's persuasion and Niuwa's crying, Han Wenlin and Deputy Chief Li drove the car and sent the child to Qin Yuanzheng's small courtyard.","As soon as he got out of the car, Niuwa familiarly strutted with his chest held high, beginning to patrol his vegetable garden in the yard.","He proudly strolled a few rounds in the vegetable garden, then ran to the backyard, crossed his arms over his chest, and went to check on his various little underlings.","The little sheep was doing well, the little chicks were doing well, and oh right, the little dog was doing well too.","This little dog was recently brought back from the mining area by Qin Yuanzheng.","It was only a few months old. Niuwa had only spent one day with the little dog and almost never made it back.","At this moment, Niuwa was squatting in the backyard holding the little dog, whispering secrets to it.","Meanwhile, in the front yard, Qin Yuanzheng was holding An'an, standing at the doorway with Qiao Lanshu, looking at Han Wenlin and Deputy Chief Li;","Qin Yuanzheng's expression was not very pleasant: \"Why did you send the child back again?\"","Han Wenlin rubbed his nose, feeling a bit awkward.","Deputy Chief Li spoke up first: \"Brigade Commander Qin, you also know that Comrade Han has just encountered an assassination attempt. It might not be safe right now. Moreover, he doesn't have a house yet and can only stay in the guesthouse. It wouldn't be appropriate for the child to stay in the guesthouse with him, right?\"","Qin Yuanzheng said very coldly and ruthlessly, \"What's inappropriate about staying in the guesthouse? There's a bed to sleep in, food to eat, and security guards. There's nothing to feel wronged about, right?\"","Qin Yuanzheng's face darkened: \"Is it that the people from your Public Security Bureau are ostracizing the newly arrived Comrade Han and refusing to help him take care of the child?\"","Having this label of ostracism pinned on them made the problem extremely serious.","Deputy Chief Li quickly said, \"No, no, nothing of the sort! Brigade Commander Qin, we've known each other for so long, am I that kind of person?\"","Qin Yuanzheng said expressionlessly, \"Who knows? Hard to say.\"","Deputy Chief Li: \"...\"","At this time, Han Wenlin walked over somewhat embarrassedly. He said to Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng:","\"You two, this is truly a presumptuous request, but I have no other choice. You also know my situation, so I won't explain much. After you left this afternoon, the child kept crying and making a fuss, wanting to come find Comrade Xiao Qiao. I tried to stop him at first, but the child is too stubborn... I figured that even if I entrusted the child to someone else, he would probably run away, so...\"","At this point, Han Wenlin was genuinely feeling quite embarrassed.","Qin Yuanzheng's expression was not very good, but Qiao Lanshu's face showed some emotion.","Han Wenlin then said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, I want to ask for your help to take care of the child for a few more days. Once my matters are resolved and my house is allocated, I will take the child back.\"","As for the child's food expenses, he would definitely provide enough. It was just that at this moment, he was too embarrassed to mention it, afraid of being scolded by Qin Yuanzheng.","Qin Yuanzheng frowned slightly, feeling somewhat dissatisfied with the people from the Public Security Bureau.","Qiao Lanshu, however, said, \"Of course it's fine. It's not a bother. Comrade Han, you can rest assured and leave the child here. The child eats well and plays well here, and we don't have to worry too much.\"","Qin Yuanzheng thought to himself that although they didn't have to worry much, the child was too clingy with Qiao Lanshu. Not only did Qiao Lanshu have to take care of An'an, but she also had to deal with Niuwa clinging to her.","As a husband, he had to avoid the children just to hug his wife, and often couldn't find the opportunity.","Zhong Mei had lived here for a long time, and with Niuwa here too, Qin Yuanzheng was feeling extremely frustrated during this period.","With no place to vent his pent-up frustration, he had been irritable these past few days.","Han Wenlin was very grateful to Qiao Lanshu. He said, \"Then I will leave the child here. Thank you so much, Comrade Xiao Qiao. I will definitely repay your kindness in the future.\"","Qiao Lanshu quickly exchanged a few polite words with him. Han Wenlin didn't sit down for tea and soon left with Deputy Chief Li.","Before leaving, Han Wenlin wanted to go see Niuwa and give him a few words of instruction.","However, he searched both the front and back yards but couldn't find Niuwa anywhere.","Only after he left did Qiao Lanshu find Niuwa in the doghouse in the backyard.","Niuwa asked slyly, \"Mom, has that man left yet?\"","He was hiding from Han Wenlin, afraid that Han Wenlin would drag him back again.","Qiao Lanshu gave him a helpless look and said, \"You need to call me Auntie, not Mom.\"","Niuwa said a bit pitifully, \"But in my heart, you are my mom.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu sighed, not having the heart to say anything more. She picked Niuwa up and said, \"Go take a bath, and then get some sleep.\"","It seemed best to let Niuwa stay with them for a while. After all, raising one more child wouldn't cost them that much extra food anyway."]},{"number":208,"title":"Chapter 208: The butler can go home and live now","paragraphs":["After Han Wenlin returned, he completed his onboarding and became the chief of the Longcheng City Public Security Bureau.","However, before they could even begin their investigation, they discovered that the siblings, Zheng Weigong and Zheng Wenhui, had unexpectedly left Longcheng.","The siblings claimed they were returning to their hometown to visit relatives, having submitted leave applications and reports.","But a deeper investigation revealed that the siblings had no relatives left in their hometown.","Qin Yuanzheng had previously sent someone to investigate Zheng Weigong and Zheng Wenhui's past experiences, family backgrounds, and other records, and quickly found the problem.","Qin Yuanzheng brought the documents to Han Wenlin. Still nursing his injuries, Han Wenlin read through the files at the police station and finally understood. \"So they are actually Zheng Yan's nephew and niece...\"","In reality, Zheng Weigong was Zheng Yan's biological son. Back then, Zheng Yan was involved in illicit activities and feared exposure, so when registering his newborn son, he put him under his cousin's household register.","However, at this point, whether he was a biological son or not no longer mattered.","Zheng Weigong knew he was outmatched. After his failed assassination attempt on Han Wenlin, he fled with his sister.","Han Wenlin said in frustration, \"We were still a step too late and let them get away.\"","It should be known that catching a criminal in this day and age was incredibly difficult.","If criminals ran far enough or smuggled themselves into other countries, they were practically beyond the reach of the law.","The Public Security Bureau truly had no way to deal with them.","Both Qin Yuanzheng and Li Jianlin were in Han Wenlin's office. Li Jianlin also took the documents to read and asked, \"This Zheng Yan, what was the reason he was executed by firing squad?\"","Han Wenlin was in charge of the execution back then. He had a good memory and still remembered Zheng Yan.","He said, \"Zheng Yan was a spy. Because of him, we suffered heavy losses. He and his wife were executed together. At the time, he didn't have any children with him, but the forensic doctor mentioned that his wife had given birth before, as she had stretch marks on her abdomen. However, their capital crimes had nothing to do with their child. We had people monitoring his relatives, so we didn't specifically go looking for that child.\"","Looking at it now, even though the Zheng siblings had grown up and achieved some success.","Their hearts were still aligned with their father.","They had likely followed in their father's footsteps.","If that was the case, they absolutely could not let the siblings go.","Han Wenlin said with a serious expression, \"Leave this case to me. We have always kept an eye on their relatives. The moment the Zheng siblings return, our people will know immediately.\"","Qin Yuanzheng reminded Han Wenlin, \"When investigating, you need to pay extra attention to one thing: the siblings might not just be involved in espionage; they could also be involved in trafficking women and children.\"","If that was true, then simply keeping a closer eye on human trafficking cases might lead them right to the siblings.","Han Wenlin nodded and said gratefully, \"Comrade Qin, thank you so much for this.\"","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head. \"You're welcome. This case won't be easy to investigate, and the work might not go smoothly. Be careful.\"","Having already been hunted down once, Qin Yuanzheng didn't want Han Wenlin to face a second assassination attempt.","More importantly, Han Wenlin couldn't die. If he died, Niuwa would truly end up staying at his house forever.","Han Wenlin's wife's family actually had quite an impressive background as well.","Han Wenlin was at least a military officer, and his father-in-law was the deputy commander of another military region.","Once Niuwa's uncle arrived, perhaps they wouldn't need to trouble Qin Yuanzheng anymore.","However, Han Wenlin didn't mention this because he wasn't sure when the uncle would arrive. It could wait until he actually got there.","And so, before the gunshot wound on his arm had even healed, Han Wenlin hurriedly went back to investigating the case and hunting down the Zheng siblings.","Meanwhile, the position of the Supply Section Chief had opened up, as well as the position of the Women's Federation Director.","Lying in his hospital bed, Guan Wenjun grew incredibly anxious upon hearing this news!","He looked at his subordinates sitting nearby and said, \"Why have only you guys come to see me these past two days? Did someone else come over but you chased them away?\"","The subordinates felt very wronged. \"How is that possible, Director? Are we such unreasonable people?\"","Guan Wenjun looked at them suspiciously and said ruthlessly, \"Aren't you? Take a look at yourselves in the mirror. Do you think you're good people?\"","Subordinates: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun's arm was fractured, and he had several bruises and scrapes elsewhere on his body.","After all, the situation had been critical. When they were besieged by the enemy, he had slammed on the gas pedal and sped wildly along the mountain roads.","They barely managed to escape, but due to a moment of carelessness, the car veered off the road, plunged into the mountains, and ultimately flipped over.","Han Wenlin and the other three soldiers were agile. As soon as they noticed something was wrong, the four of them jumped out of the vehicle.","Only Guan Wenjun, who was in the driver's seat steering the car, couldn't jump out in time and rolled with the vehicle.","Fortunately, it was just a broken arm and he was still alive. Otherwise, this trip would have been a massive loss for him.","Guan Wenjun sat up in bed. His arm was still in a sling across his chest, and the bandages on his forehead hadn't been removed yet.","He anxiously got out of the hospital bed and told his subordinates, \"Let's go. We're heading back to the Revolutionary Committee.\"","A subordinate said, \"Director, there's nothing going on lately anyway. Why don't you stay in the hospital for a few more days?\"","Not only was the Revolutionary Committee idle recently, but the department was also very likely to be abolished.","Of course, this was just a rumor. None of them knew exactly what the specific policies would be.","Guan Wenjun only knew that the Revolutionary Committee wasn't a long-term solution. If he wanted stability, he still needed to find a department and secure a solid position for himself.","So now, after hearing about the vacancy in the Supply Section, he became anxious.","Wearing his hospital gown, he strode outside, saying as he walked, \"Forget about it. If we delay any longer, the vacancy will be gone, and my arm will have broken for nothing. Hurry up, back to the office.\"","As he spoke, he led his men to the door of the ward. The moment the door opened, he saw Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng standing outside.","Qin Yuanzheng was holding canned goods and apples, clearly here to visit him, the patient.","When Guan Wenjun saw Qiao Lanshu, his eyes lit up. His gaze then swept behind her and to her sides before he asked, \"Is it just the two of you?\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, \"Yes, An'an is sleeping, so it wasn't convenient to bring him out.\"","Qiao Lanshu thought Guan Wenjun wanted to see An'an.","But in reality, the person Guan Wenjun wanted to see wasn't that little child at all.","Guan Wenjun said guiltily, \"Oh, oh, my godson sure can sleep. His godfather breaks an arm, and he doesn't even come to check on me.\"","Qin Yuanzheng originally hadn't wanted to come, but Qiao Lanshu had said it would be inappropriate not to. After all, they were quite familiar with Guan Wenjun, and outside of work, they could be considered friends.","Furthermore, on the day Niuwa was taken away by Liu Weihong, Guan Wenjun had been a tremendous help.","Qin Yuanzheng looked at him. \"Are you getting ready to be discharged?\"","Guan Wenjuan nodded, then quickly shook his head. He grabbed Qin Yuanzheng and lowered his voice, \"You came at the right time. I have something to ask you.\"","With that, he brought both Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu into the room. Then, Guan Wenjuan asked in a low voice, \"Lao Qin, I heard Zheng Weigong ran away? There's a vacancy in the Supply Section, right? Do you think I can do it?\"","Qin Yuanzheng put down the apples in his hand and then said, \"I'm not from the provincial personnel department. How would I know?\"","Guan Wenjuan clicked his tongue, stared at Qin Yuanzheng, and pointed to his own arm. \"My arm is like this. You can't let me get injured for nothing, right? This time I escorted Han Wenlin for you!\"","If Qin Yuanzheng hadn't asked him to go, he wouldn't have bothered.","Wasn't it because Qin Yuanzheng said there would be a vacancy in the Supply Section, dangling it like a carrot in front of a donkey like him?","Otherwise, why would he go to such great lengths!","Listening to the two of them discuss this work matter, Qiao Lanshu felt that Guan Wenjuan was actually quite smart.","Having been reborn, she knew when the revolution would end and when the college entrance examination would resume.","But Guan Wenjuan, without knowing any of this, had also started maneuvering for his own job.","It seemed that Guan Wenjuan was quite far-sighted.","It was just a pity that in his previous life, his maneuvering wasn't successful, and his job wasn't secured.","In the end, when the Revolutionary Committee was abolished, someone took revenge on him, breaking one of his legs. To avoid his enemies, he even fled to the south.","Looking at it now, Qiao Lanshu had no idea where Guan Wenjuan's enemies came from, but the Revolutionary Committee was never a likable department to begin with. She guessed that over the years, Guan Wenjuan had done his fair share of confiscating people's properties.","Guan Wenjuan was still saying, \"You guys say I'm not suitable for the public security bureau. I admit it. I'm really not as capable as Han Wenlin, alright? But if you still don't let me go to the Supply Section, I'm going to make a fuss!\"","Qin Yuanzheng could only say, \"Go ask around at the Organization Department. This matter can probably be done.\"","When Guan Wenjuan assisted them in catching spies in the mountains before, he had already made a contribution, and the higher-ups were already arranging a job for him.","Now that there happened to be a vacancy, and a good job at that, if Guan Wenjuan made some effort to pull strings, it would probably work out.","With those words, Guan Wenjuan breathed a sigh of relief. He said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Lao Qin, with you saying that, I can rest assured.\"","As he spoke, he looked at Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu was sitting close to Qin Yuanzheng. The couple held hands, sticking closely together in a sweet, mushy way that made one's teeth ache.","Guan Wenjuan had also been thinking about getting married lately. He also wanted to live the wonderful life of having a wife, children, a warm bed, and hot meals waiting for him when he came home from work every day.","He leaned in towards Qiao Lanshu and whispered, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, don't you have a friend? Why didn't she come?\"","Qiao Lanshu was a bit baffled. She looked at Guan Wenjuan and said, \"You mean Zhong Mei? She's at work. Besides, she doesn't know you. It wouldn't be appropriate for me to invite her here, right?\"","Guan Wenjuan: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng raised his eyebrows, turned to look at Guan Wenjuan, and looked him up and down.","Guan Wenjuan coughed and said somewhat embarrassedly, \"Oh, she's at work? I just saw that she was always with you, so I asked casually.\"","Saying that, he added, \"I don't mean anything else. Please don't overthink it.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Guan Wenjuan's guilty conscience was so obvious!","Sure enough, after a short while, Guan Wenjuan suddenly leaned over again and asked her in a low voice, \"Didn't she just arrive in Longcheng not long ago? She found a job so quickly? Where does she work?\"","Qiao Lanshu was a bit vigilant, thinking to herself, could Guan Wenjuan have recognized that Zhong Mei was the one who hit him?","So Guan Wenjuan was asking this now because he wanted to take revenge on Zhong Mei?","Qiao Lanshu looked at him with slight wariness. \"Why are you asking this, Director Guan? Are you paying close attention to Zhong Mei?\"","Guan Wenjuan, feeling guilty, almost jumped up. His ears turned red, and he said very awkwardly, \"Why would I pay attention to her for no reason? Can't you see how busy I am with work lately? I'm focusing on my job. Why would I pay attention to your friend?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu probed, \"I thought you and Zhong Mei had some bad blood, which is why you were paying so much attention to her.\"","Guan Wenjuan scratched his head and tried hard to explain, \"No, no, nothing like that. I don't know her at all, so how could we have bad blood? I really just asked casually just now. Don't overthink it, it's quite embarrassing.\"","Looking at Guan Wenjuan's expression, Qiao Lanshu knew that Guan Wenjuan really hadn't recognized Zhong Mei.","Perhaps he really was just asking casually.","Qin Yuanzheng and Guan Wenjuan talked a bit more about work, then told him to rest well and recover from his injuries before leaving the hospital with Qiao Lanshu.","Qin Yuanzheng thought about the way Guan Wenjuan talked about Zhong Mei. As a man, he knew that Guan Wenjuan was probably attracted to Zhong Mei.","As for what it was about Zhong Mei that attracted him, that was unknown.","But this was fine too. If Zhong Mei could start a relationship with Guan Wenjuan, it would only benefit Zhong Mei, with no downsides.","Qin Yuanzheng held Qiao Lanshu's hand tightly and asked her gently, \"Has Zhong Mei found a place yet? When is she moving out?\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, \"She found one. It's in a shared courtyard near the food factory. There are already two families living in the courtyard, and the neighbors are quite easy to get along with. Zhong Mei rented two rooms, one with a heated brick bed and the other with a stove. The rental procedures have been completed. She's been taking time to go over and clean up these past few days, and I also went with her to buy some furniture. She said she'll move in after work today.\"","Zhong Mei was also very anxious to move out.","After all, because she was staying there, Qin Yuanzheng couldn't live at home. He had to come back for lunch every day to see his wife and child, and then go out again after dinner at night. Zhong Mei felt very guilty about it.","Zhong Mei had always been most afraid of causing trouble for others. Having troubled Qiao Lanshu for so long during this period, she already felt quite bad.","Qiao Lanshu said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"I advanced half a year's rent for Zhong Mei. She just started working, is tight on money, and has no family to support her. As her friend, I want to help her as much as I can.\"","Qin Yuanzheng rubbed Qiao Lanshu's head and said softly, \"You did the right thing. You don't have to tell me about these things. I gave you the money, so you can spend it however you want.\"","He handed over all his monthly salary to his wife, keeping almost no money in his own pockets.","A man earned money to support his wife and children. He just brought the money home and didn't care how Qiao Lanshu spent it.","Qiao Lanshu smiled and nodded. \"I know you don't mind, but I just wanted to tell you.\"","Qin Yuanzheng led Qiao Lanshu into the car. He paused for a moment and suddenly said, \"So tonight, I can sleep at home?\"","Qiao Lanshu gave him a playful glare. \"That's right. Did you just realize that?\"","Qin Yuanzheng felt a bit excited. Having not slept at home for so long, he was really dying of frustration.","He cupped Qiao Lanshu's face, gave her a loud, heavy kiss, and then murmured, \"Then I definitely have to take a good bath tonight.\"","Meeting his burning gaze, Qiao Lanshu blushed and shot him another coy glare.","That look sent a tingling jolt right through Qin Yuanzheng. He murmured, \"I am still waiting for you to take the lead. I have dreamed about it so many times.\"","Finally, he was going to experience it for real."]},{"number":209,"title":"Chapter 209: Finally Holding My Sweet and Soft Wife","paragraphs":["By the time Zhong Mei got off work today, she had already tidied up her rented house.","Her childhood dream had always been to have a room of her own.","In the past, she thought this dream would come true after she got married.","But later she realized that even after marriage, she would have to share a bed with her husband, serve him, and then serve her children. When her children grew up, she might even have to serve her grandchildren.","If she followed in her mother's footsteps, she might never have a space that truly belonged to her for her entire life.","Until now. Having rented this house, she looked at the clean and bright room after her tidying, touched the smooth surface of the kang bed, and a smile appeared on her face.","Both rooms had been cleaned up, the windows wiped spotless, and new newspapers pasted up.","The kang had also been sorted out, covered with kraft paper, and padded with a thin mattress.","The mattress and quilts were all prepared by Qiao Lanshu. Naturally, Qiao Lanshu had also helped her pay the rent.","She had already taken a notebook and recorded every single expense. Once she saved up some money in the future, she would slowly pay it back.","She hadn't bought tables and chairs yet, but those things weren't too important.","Having a kang, a stove, quilts, and a mattress was already enough.","She planned to go out tomorrow to buy some oil, salt, soy sauce, vinegar, rice, and flour.","She and Qiao Lanshu had already met the two families living next door. They knew each other now and got along quite well.","As it was getting dark, Zhong Mei lit an oil lamp, made the bed on the kang, and then took a steamed bun out of her bag to eat.","This was her dinner for today. She was frugal and didn't want to spend extra money on groceries, so she decided to just eat a steamed bun.","At this time, Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng came over together.","Qin Yuanzheng drove the car, following Qiao Lanshu's directions, and arrived there.","He took a look at the gate of the courtyard and said to Qiao Lanshu, This shared courtyard isn't bad. The people living in this area are all workers from the food factory and the textile factory. It's safe and stable.","Qiao Lanshu got out of the car and replied, Of course. Zhong Mei and I looked for a long time. I rented this place precisely because it's safe and close to the food factory.","Zhong Mei only rented two small rooms, which would only cost one yuan in rent elsewhere.","But the rent here was one yuan and fifty cents, which actually wasn't cheap.","That was because the location was good, and the neighbors all had proper jobs, were stable, and didn't cause trouble.","Seeing this environment, Qin Yuanzheng also felt a bit relieved.","Qiao Lanshu had married far away from home to come here. With no relatives or friends, she must have been very lonely.","Now that she had Zhong Mei, Zhong Mei could be considered Qiao Lanshu's only family from her maiden home. Therefore, no matter what, Qin Yuanzheng had to help out and get Zhong Mei settled in.","Qin Yuanzheng walked around the area before going to the car to fetch things.","Qiao Lanshu had gone to the supply and marketing cooperative to buy a small table and two small chairs. Since these things were relatively expensive, she bought them for Zhong Mei.","Zhong Mei had no money right now and was even stingy about buying a broom. Qiao Lanshu felt sorry for her.","Qiao Lanshu also brought over a pound of dried noodles, two pounds of millet, and a box of sweet potatoes. She was afraid Zhong Mei would be too reluctant to buy groceries and end up going hungry.","She was already malnourished. Now that she had moved out to live on her own, had a job, and was earning a salary, she couldn't afford to go hungry anymore.","Qiao Lanshu carried the noodles and millet, holding a stool as she went inside.","Qin Yuanzheng placed the sweet potatoes and the other chair on the table, carrying the table with both hands as he followed Qiao Lanshu inside.","It was dusk now, and the other two families were already cooking in their rooms.","When the old lady next door saw Qiao Lanshu, she greeted her, Xiao Qiao, are you here to see Xiao Mei?","Qiao Lanshu smiled and nodded. Yes, Auntie Wang. She moved in today, so I brought her some things.","The old lady looked at the noodles and millet in her hands and smiled, saying, Oh my, you are such a loyal friend. Many biological sisters wouldn't even do as much as you.","Qiao Lanshu wore a smile on her face, looking like a well-behaved young wife, which was exactly the type that aunties liked the most.","This old lady really liked Qiao Lanshu.","The old lady pulled Qiao Lanshu aside to chat for a bit. When she saw Qin Yuanzheng, she kept praising Qiao Lanshu for marrying so well.","Hearing Qiao Lanshu's voice, Zhong Mei hurriedly ran out.","She was still holding the half-eaten multigrain steamed bun in her hand.","She was pleasantly surprised that Qiao Lanshu had come. Lanshu! You guys are here?","Qiao Lanshu smiled and nodded. Didn't you move in today? I was worried you wouldn't have time to buy food, so I brought some over for you first.","Actually, she wasn't worried that Zhong Mei didn't have time; she was mainly worried that Zhong Mei would be too reluctant to spend money.","After all, Zhong Mei was very poor right now. After coming out of the labor camp, she was penniless.","Qiao Lanshu had lent her ten yuan before, but she guessed Zhong Mei was too stingy to spend it.","Qiao Lanshu glanced at her room and scolded her gently, Why didn't you turn on the light? It's pitch black, you can't see anything.","Zhong Mei took the things from Qiao Lanshu's hands. Seeing Qin Yuanzheng carrying the table and chairs, she kept thanking him profusely.","The three of them went inside, and Zhong Mei quickly pulled the switch for the dim little lightbulb. She smiled and said, I'm used to lighting an oil lamp at home. Since it's just me anyway, an oil lamp works just fine.","Qiao Lanshu disagreed, saying, You don't need to be that frugal with electricity. It's just you and a small lightbulb; how much could it possibly cost?","Zhong Mei said embarrassedly, I know. I'm not that frugal. Look, I even had a steamed bun today.","Qiao Lanshu looked at her helplessly. How is one steamed bun enough? You should go buy some eggs. You need to eat at least some eggs to get proper nutrition.","Besides, eggs weren't considered expensive; ordinary families could afford them.","Qin Yuanzheng carried the square table inside and placed it by the edge of the kang.","The two chairs with backrests were placed by the table.","Apart from the kang, the room had originally been completely empty, with nothing in it.","Now that there was a table and chairs, it finally looked like a proper room. At the very least, there was a place to put cups, bowls, and chopsticks.","Zhong Mei affectionately stroked the solid wood table and chairs, feeling deeply moved. She asked Qiao Lanshu in a low voice, This table and these chairs weren't cheap, were they?","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, They weren't too expensive. I bought them fresh from the supply and marketing cooperative. Just consider it my future wedding gift to you. When you get married later on, I won't give you another gift, okay?","Zhong Mei was so moved she wanted to cry.","Tables and chairs were quite expensive in this day and age.","A small square table cost forty to fifty yuan, and a single chair cost ten yuan.","That was why people nowadays demanded three turning things and one sounding thing for marriage, and then demanded thirty-six legs, seventy-two legs...","Even the furniture that had to be custom-made after marriage was very expensive.","Zhong Mei pulled Qiao Lanshu into a corner, glanced at Qin Yuanzheng who was standing at the door and hadn't come inside, and asked her in a low voice, Xiao Qiao, you bought such expensive things without even discussing it with me... Brigade Commander Qin won't have an issue with you over this, will he?","Qiao Lanshu also turned her head and glanced at Qin Yuanzheng outside the door.","Outside the door, Qin Yuanzheng was chatting with the old lady next door. With his back to the house, he wore a crisp military uniform that accentuated his tall, straight figure. Even from the side, his facial features were strikingly sharp and handsome.","Although he was a bit older, a man of his age was at the peak of his maturity and steadiness. The more she looked at him, the more charismatic he seemed.","Qiao Lanshu felt herself falling more and more in love with him.","Zhong Mei, who was currently worrying about her friend, was left speechless.","Zhong Mei reached out to cover Qiao Lanshu's eyes and whispered, \"Alright, stop staring. Look at you, acting like a lovestruck teenager. Are you really that obsessed with him?\"","Qiao Lanshu blushed, lowered her head with a smile, and said, \"I just really like him. He's a good person and treats me so well.\"","As she spoke, she reached out to hold Zhong Mei's hand and whispered, \"Don't worry, I bought all these things with my own money. I've saved all of Brother Zheng's money and haven't touched it. Besides, Brother Zheng told me I could spend his money however I want and that I never need to explain myself to him.\"","Hearing this, Zhong Mei finally felt relieved.","At the same time, she felt a twinge of envy.","She said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Seeing you live so well, I'm actually quite jealous. I feel like I'll probably never find a man who treats me this well in my entire life.\"","Qiao Lanshu comforted her, \"Everyone has their own destiny. Even if you don't find someone as good as Brother Zheng, it doesn't matter. You have a stronger personality than I do. If your future husband disobeys you, you can just forcefully suppress him. You definitely have more ways to deal with men than I do.\"","Hearing this, Zhong Mei smiled and said, \"You're right. If my future man dares to disobey me, I'll just beat him up. I bet he wouldn't dare say a word.\"","The two friends chatted in the room for a while longer before Qiao Lanshu got ready to leave.","After all, it was getting dark, and she and Qin Yuanzheng hadn't eaten yet. Auntie Shi was going to cook at home, so Qiao Lanshu needed to go back to watch over An'an.","Not to mention, they also had Niuwa at home, and he was a little troublemaker who could turn the house upside down.","After leaving Zhong Mei's house, Qin Yuanzheng drove and said, \"I chatted with those two neighbors and found them to be pretty decent people. We can definitely get along with them.\"","Getting Qin Yuanzheng's approval made Qiao Lanshu even happier. \"Really? That's exactly what I thought at the time. I felt they were easy to get along with, so I had Zhong Mei settle on this place.\"","Looking at Qiao Lanshu's smug little expression, Qin Yuanzheng couldn't help but smile and said, \"My wife is so smart.\"","Saying that, he reached out and rubbed Qiao Lanshu's hair. \"That's my wife for you.\"","By the time the couple returned home, it was already dark.","Auntie Shi had already steamed Chinese cabbage buns, cooked millet porridge, and stir-fried some sour and spicy shredded potatoes.","Seeing the couple return, Auntie Shi brought the food out.","There was a basin of buns, a full seventeen or eighteen of them, a large plate of stir-fried shredded potatoes, and she served four bowls of millet porridge.","Qiao Lanshu went to check on An'an first.","An'an had already finished his milk and was asleep on the kang bed.","An'an was already over five months old, almost half a year, and he still slept a lot.","Every day after drinking milk and basking in the sun, he would quickly fall asleep, sleeping for sixteen or seventeen hours a day.","Niuwa, on the other hand, didn't treat himself like an outsider at all. Seeing Qin Yuanzheng sit down, he also came over and reached out to grab a bun to eat.","Auntie Shi smiled and said, \"Oh my, don't rush, eat slowly.\"","Niuwa happily munched on the bun and said to Auntie Shi, \"Grandma Shi's buns are super delicious! I want to eat a hundred of them!\"","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head helplessly but didn't scold him.","Auntie Shi said to Qiao Lanshu, \"This child loves big buns the most. If we don't keep an eye on him, he can eat four big buns at once! Xiao Qiao, watch him in a bit. Let him eat at most two buns and one bowl of porridge. He can't eat any more, or his stomach will hurt in the middle of the night and he won't be able to sleep.\"","Auntie Shi had experience raising children, so what she said went.","Qiao Lanshu quickly agreed.","But after eating two buns, Niuwa still clamored for more.","Qiao Lanshu was soft-hearted. Just as she was debating whether to let him eat another half, Qin Yuanzheng took all the buns away. \"Auntie Shi said two at most.\"","Niuwa didn't dare to make a fuss with Qin Yuanzheng. After all, Qin Yuanzheng looked fierce, and he was afraid of him.","In the end, he could only aggrievedly finish his porridge and eat some shredded potatoes before returning to the room with Auntie Shi, his little belly bulging.","After Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng took their showers and returned to their room, Qiao Lanshu said, \"Brother Zheng, why didn't you let Niuwa eat a little more just now? I'm worried he isn't full.\"","Qin Yuanzheng closed the bedroom door and even slid the bolt shut.","He whispered, \"Didn't you hear what Auntie Shi said? If he eats too much, he won't be able to sleep well tonight, and I don't want him ruining my good time.\"","Saying that, he took off all his clothes, hanging them on an iron nail on the wall, leaving only his shorts on. He walked over, suddenly scooped Qiao Lanshu into his arms, took a deep breath against her chest, and said, \"We've been sleeping in separate rooms for so long, I'm dying of frustration.\"","That evening, Qin Yuanzheng had accompanied Qiao Lanshu to see Zhong Mei, waited for Niuwa and Auntie Shi to go to sleep, and only then washed himself clean before finally holding his fragrant and soft little wife.","He stripped off Qiao Lanshu's clothes as well, breathing in the scent of her neck and chest.","His wife smelled so sweet. No matter how much he breathed her in, he couldn't get enough; instead, the fire within him burned even more vigorously.","He sat on the edge of the kang with Qiao Lanshu in his arms, letting her sit on his lap. He held her waist and pressed the back of her head to kiss her.","After kissing her for a while, his hands started wandering, and he whispered, \"Wife, have you lost some weight recently?\"","When she had just finished her postpartum confinement, his wife had noticeably gained some weight, and she felt different to the touch.","Now, a month later, how had she gotten thinner again?","Qiao Lanshu leaned against his chest, the corners of her eyes slightly red, and whispered, \"Auntie Shi said that breastfeeding makes you lose weight. After giving birth and nursing the baby, the weight gradually comes off.\"","She wasn't actually that thin now, and because she was nursing, her cup size had gone up two sizes, which Qin Yuanzheng obviously loved.","He simply couldn't keep his hands off her.","As Qiao Lanshu whimpered softly, Qin Yuanzheng even reminded her, \"Keep your voice down, don't wake An'an up. The baby shouldn't see this.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Blushing, Qiao Lanshu whispered to him, \"You're clearly the one messing around...\"","He was so strong and deliberately tormented her; if she didn't make a sound, he would only escalate things.","And then he had the nerve to tell her to keep her voice down so as not to wake the baby.","This man really had a hundred different tricks up his sleeve.","But Qiao Lanshu simply couldn't resist this side of Qin Yuanzheng.","Qiao Lanshu whispered, \"Do you want me to take the lead...\"","Qin Yuanzheng held her tightly without letting go, only saying, \"You can take the lead the second time. For now, let me have my way with you just once...\"","He was dying of frustration and needed to go hard.","Otherwise, he wouldn't be satisfied, and his whole body would ache with unfulfilled desire."]},{"number":210,"title":"Chapter 210: Want a Second Child","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu could indeed feel that Qin Yuanzheng was holding back quite fiercely this time.","Like an old house catching fire, crackling and blazing.","He had repeatedly said before that his young wife was still tender in age, her body delicate, and that she needed to be carefully protected in every way.","Yet once they were on the kang, engaging in this act, he no longer remembered his wife's fragility, nor did he think of being gentle.","He had been sitting at the edge of the kang, holding Qiao Lanshu, who sat on his lap, tightly trapped by his thick arms, unable to move at all.","Qin Yuanzheng was strong, and Qiao Lanshu had grown used to it—in these matters, she had to go along with him.","Qin Yuanzheng grew bolder, asking in a low voice, \"Did it go all the way in?\"","Qiao Lanshu blushed, resting her head on his shoulder, silently nodding.","She didn't dare make a sound, afraid of waking the sleeping An'an.","An'an was still so young; once he fell asleep, he knew nothing.","If he knew his parents were doing such things beside him, he might be scared into tears.","Qin Yuanzheng's breathing grew rapid, his voice low and hoarse as his hands gripped Qiao Lanshu's waist... as if still not satisfied...","Qiao Lanshu bit her lip and pushed against him.","Qin Yuanzheng tightened his hold on her waist, whispering, \"It hasn't reached deep enough... why won't you let me...?\"","Qiao Lanshu's voice came out raspy: \"I never said no...\"","Sweat beaded on Qin Yuanzheng's forehead, his excitement palpable. He patted Qiao Lanshu's waist, coaxing her in a husky tone, \"Wife, don't be nervous...\"","They were too close; how could they continue like this?","Qin Yuanzheng still felt it wasn't deep enough.","This position didn't satisfy him.","So he stood up, and Qiao Lanshu let out a soft cry, quickly wrapping her arms around his neck.","Qin Yuanzheng carried her, pacing a couple of steps around the room.","His arms were thick, muscles solid, bulging as he held his wife—veins standing out along his biceps.","Qiao Lanshu was petite; even though she had filled out after childbirth, having been very thin before, she still looked small in Qin Yuanzheng's eyes.","His frame was nearly twice her size; his burly arms, each as thick as her thigh, held her easily.","Thus held, with Qin Yuanzheng's strength as he walked, Qiao Lanshu's eyes reddened, and she curled up in his arms, choked up, begging, \"Stop walking, please stop walking, okay?\"","Qin Yuanzheng paid no attention. He smiled, tightening his grip slightly, and said softly, \"Don't rush, let me walk a little longer...\"","Qiao Lanshu angrily beat his shoulder.","Qin Yuanzheng loved his young wife, her tiny figure pressed against him. Every time he had his way with her, she could only huddle in his arms, burying her face and crying.","He was so large and sturdy that he could cover her completely. When he was harsh with her, she was trapped with no escape, nowhere to hide.","Another half hour passed, and when Qin Yuanzheng noticed Qiao Lanshu was trembling slightly, he carried her back onto the kang, slipped a pillow under her waist, and said, \"This feels better.\"","Having been abstinent for so long, he needed to indulge himself. So, for the next while, Qin Yuanzheng spoke little, focusing solely on teasing and toying with his young wife.","Qiao Lanshu covered her mouth, forcing herself not to make a sound.","She wanted to tell Qin Yuanzheng to stop being so excessive, but he wouldn't let her get a word out.","After what felt like an eternity, Qin Yuanzheng suddenly looked down and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"The quilt is soaked. Why didn't you use that waterproof sheepskin?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng leaned in, kissed her, and murmured, \"Wife, are you dazed? Come back to me.\"","Qiao Lanshu still said nothing, only looking at him with tear-filled eyes.","Seeing her so stunned from the pleasure, Qin Yuanzheng couldn't help but chuckle. He pulled her into his arms, kissed her ear, and said, \"Already worn out? Didn't you say it would be your turn to move in a bit?\"","Though his words were gentle, his movements didn't stop.","Qiao Lanshu couldn't speak; she closed her eyes, on the verge of fainting.","Seeing her like this, Qin Yuanzheng knew he wouldn't get to have Qiao Lanshu take the lead tonight.","Never mind; he would do the work several more times, and then let her take over tomorrow.","After all, there was always time.","...","After such a long period of restraint, Qin Yuanzheng finally had his fill tonight.","Niuwa didn't come to disturb them, and An'an slept soundly.","Qin Yuanzheng carried his wife from one end of the kang to the other, then to the floor, onto the table, and finally onto a chair.","It was worth noting that between husband and wife, these matters offered a great deal of variety, with many pleasures to explore.","The couple always enjoyed themselves a lot.","Of course, Qiao Lanshu enjoyed the first hour; the hour after that left her too exhausted to continue the exploration.","Eventually, Qin Yuanzheng simply lay back on the kang, letting Qiao Lanshu...","Qiao Lanshu leaned against his chest, hearing him whisper, \"I'll do the work; you can rest awhile.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Tears streamed down her face. She felt this wasn't right—she simply couldn't rest.","And in this position...","How could that work?","Yet Qin Yuanzheng was thoroughly content. He reached out to soothe her back, murmuring, \"Wife, you're so warm.\"","Now he was gentle again, knowing how to position her.","He kissed her ear and whispered, \"You're making me hot too... Wife, do we have more of those?\"","As he spoke, he held Qiao Lanshu and reached for the drawer beside the kang.","Qiao Lanshu closed her eyes, voice weak: \"Didn't you just take three?\"","Qin Yuanzheng hugged her, kissed her, then suddenly confessed, \"Used them all up. Any left?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","After a long pause, she said, \"I think there were only three left; they're gone.\"","Qin Yuanzheng paused, frowning. \"Gone? What do we do now?\"","He could barely hold back, having already held out for so long.","This made him afraid to continue.","Qiao Lanshu hugged him, saying softly, \"It's fine... just do it without.\"","Qin Yuanzheng refused: \"No. What if you get pregnant again?\"","Childbirth was so arduous.","He didn't want Qiao Lanshu to suffer.","But Qiao Lanshu grew more proactive. She embraced Qin Yuanzheng and kissed him: \"It's perfect. While An'an is still small, let's have another quickly. That way, An'an will have a companion.\"","She had long thought it through—she wanted two children.","They should have them close together.","Raising two children at once meant only one stretch of parenthood, saving trouble.","If she waited until An'an was seven or eight to have a second, she would have to go through the baby stage all over again—how exhausting.","Besides, Auntie Shi was wonderful. With her help, raising two children shouldn't be hard. After all, Qiao Lanshu didn't plan to work for the next couple of years, so she could stay home and care for the kids.","By the time she got into college, the child would already be two or three years old. Then she could go to school, Qin Yuanzheng would be working, and the kid would just be old enough for kindergarten.","Qiao Lanshu had already planned it all out, but she just hadn't discussed it with Qin Yuanzheng yet.","After all, she couldn't explain how the college entrance exams would be reinstated next year.","Right now, Qin Yuanzheng was genuinely torn.","His rough, calloused hand suddenly pressed down on Qiao Lanshu's restless waist, lifting her up lightly. He said nervously, \"Wife, what did you just say? You want to have a second child?\"","Qiao Lanshu, held up by his hands, twisted deliberately like a seductive enchantress and whispered, \"Yeah, I want a daughter. Don't you want a daughter?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng said in a low voice, \"I do, but... there's no rush, is there?\"","An'an was only half a year old, and besides, he hadn't had enough time alone with his wife yet...","Forget it, that time alone was already gone. The moment An'an arrived, his couple time vanished.","He did want a daughter.","These days, who didn't want both a son and a daughter?","But he had originally thought they'd wait a few years, until An'an was a bit older, before having another.","Qiao Lanshu twisted and rubbed against him, stirring up his temper.","She whispered, \"Actually, there's no guarantee I'll get pregnant. Getting pregnant with An'an might have just been luck. Ge, don't worry—you might not be able to do it.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"???\"","Furious, he pressed her back down on the head of the bed...","He tormented Qiao Lanshu until she was limp and wilted.","Then he said in a deep voice, \"Don't you know if your man's capable or not? You're purposely provoking me, aren't you?\"","As he spoke, he kept going...","Saying to her, \"Wife, I think you're really asking for it sometimes. Are you behaving now?\"","Qiao Lanshu almost cried.","She was genuinely obedient now, not daring to say anything else.","The two of them messed around, all sticky and sweet, until the middle of the night. In the end, Qiao Lanshu even fell asleep before it was over.","Only then did Qin Yuanzheng feel satisfied.","Deep in the night, he quietly got up, fetched some hot water, and used a warm towel to wipe Qiao Lanshu down. He cleaned himself off, too, then put his clothes back on and climbed back onto the kang.","He carried An'an over to the corner, covering him with a small quilt.","Then he pulled Qiao Lanshu into his arms and lay down beside her.","What was the point of holding the son? Holding his wife was far more comfortable.","Soft and fragrant, it was really satisfying to hold her.","...","The next morning, Qin Yuanzheng got up early again, full of energy.","When he got up, An'an happened to wake up too. The sky was just barely lighting up.","An'an was only about half a year old and had gone to bed early the night before, so he woke up early today.","The baby was hungry and wanted milk powder, so Qin Yuanzheng prepared a bottle and fed it to him.","After drinking, An'an was still a bit drowsy, so Qin Yuanzheng placed him in Qiao Lanshu's arms, watching the mother and son cuddled together under the covers.","His heart softened at the sight.","He kissed Qiao Lanshu on the cheek, then reached out and pinched An'an's little face. He changed into his military uniform and left for work.","Qin Yuanzheng had good stamina and boundless energy. After every intimate night, he was always lively and spirited.","Qiao Lanshu, on the other hand, was exhausted, with aches all over her body, and slept until well past nine in the morning.","An'an was fully awake now, but he loved the smell of his mom, so he lay on her chest, refusing to get up.","By almost six months old, An'an could not only roll over but also sit up.","Seeing Qiao Lanshu still asleep, he rolled around on her face, back and forth.","Sometimes his little foot would end up in her mouth; other times, he'd kick her in the eye.","Finally, he plopped down and sat directly on her face.","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu reached out, pulled An'an away, held him in her arms, and lightly smacked his little feet twice, scolding him, \"You little rascal! You're so young, and already you're bullying Mommy.\"","It seemed a daughter would be better—definitely more gentle, good, pretty, and cute...","Thinking this, she said to An'an, \"Mommy's going to give you a little sister. What do you think?\"","An'an lifted his foot and stuck it into his own mouth.","Chewing on his foot, he stared at Qiao Lanshu, occasionally grinning at her with drool running down his chin.","Qiao Lanshu couldn't help but laugh. She quickly grabbed a bib, put it around An'an's neck, and wiped the drool from his mouth.","An'an loved chewing on his feet the most right now.","He would hug one foot, then the other, taking turns gnawing on them.","He chewed away with a satisfied, happy expression.","Qiao Lanshu fetched a towel, pulled out one foot, wiped it clean, and then—whoosh—An'an snatched up the other foot and started chewing it again.","The kid might be young, but he was quick.","Before Qiao Lanshu could react, he was already at it again.","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Helpless, she wiped his other foot clean too, changed his diaper, and then, since the weather was a bit warm, put him in split-crotch pants. She carried him out to the yard to soak up some sun.","In the yard, Niuwa was already running around everywhere.","He loved this courtyard. Every day, he'd head to the backyard to feed the chickens, ducks, and sheep, and then to the front garden to water the vegetable seedlings.","He could now tell which were vegetables and which were weeds, so when he had nothing else to do, he'd help Auntie Shi pull weeds.","Seeing Qiao Lanshu come out, Auntie Shi said with a smile, \"This Niuwa is going to be a hardworking young man, no doubt. Look how quickly and neatly he works.\"","Holding a ladle, he watered the vegetable garden, one plant at a time—really carefully.","Qiao Lanshu said with a smile, \"That works out nicely. He can be your little assistant, Auntie Shi.\"","Auntie Shi replied cheerfully, \"Hardworking habits start young. Don't worry, I'll train him well, and he'll help you out in the future.\"","After all, since Niuwa refused to go home, he had to work while he was here.","Qiao Lanshu carried An'an over and played with Niuwa in the vegetable garden.","Niuwa was four years older than An'an, and he didn't mind that the baby was so young; he was happy to play with him.","With Niuwa keeping him company, both Qiao Lanshu and Auntie Shi had an easier time.","...","Around midday, Guan Wenjuan suddenly showed up at the door.","Qiao Lanshu was a bit surprised to see him. She looked at him standing outside and asked, \"Director Guan, why are you here at this time? Aren't you at work?\"","Guan Wenjuan grinned, delighted, and said, \"My job issue is settled! The appointment will be announced tomorrow, and I'll report to the Supply Section on Monday.\"","Zheng Weigong had already fled—no one knew where he'd gone.","And with the vacancy he left behind, Guan Wenjuan, through all kinds of maneuvering, had actually managed to fill it.","He'd accomplished two meritorious deeds recently and had done well, and with support from the military side, he'd smoothly landed the job.","The moment he got the position, he felt an urge to drop by Qin Yuanzheng's place for a visit.","He couldn't really explain why, but he just had to come."]},{"number":211,"title":"Chapter 211: Finding a Match for Zhong Mei","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu looked at his cheerful expression and also smiled as she congratulated him. \"Congratulations, Director Guan! So you'll be working in the Supply Department now? Are you the head of the Supply Department?\"","Guan Wenjun smiled and nodded.","He used to be the director of the Provincial Revolutionary Committee, so being able to go to the Municipal Supply Department as the section chief was a decent outcome.","After all, not many people from the Revolutionary Committee even had the chance for such a transfer.","Moreover, most of the Revolutionary Committee members had offended quite a few people, so they were vulnerable to retaliation.","In terms of job transfers, there were many obstacles, and it wasn't easy to pull strings.","Guan Wenjun walked into the courtyard, casually glanced around, and said offhandedly, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, don't you have a friend? Did she go back to Yangcheng?\"","Qiao Lanshu was holding An An as she walked over. Hearing his question, she replied casually, \"No, Zhong Mei went to work at the food factory.\"","Auntie Shi was weeding in the vegetable garden with Niuwa. When she heard this, she looked up and gave Guan Wenjun a glance.","The fact that Guan Wenjun asked about Zhong Mei as soon as he arrived was indeed a bit odd.","Auntie Shi’s heart stirred, and she couldn't help but size up Guan Wenjun again.","Guan Wenjun continued, feigning nonchalance, \"Her household registration isn't here, right? Can she work at the food factory? Is she a temporary worker?\"","Qiao Lanshu also thought Guan Wenjun was acting strangely today. She shot him a puzzled look and said, \"Yes, she's from out of town, so she can only work as a temporary worker.\"","At this point, Auntie Shi suddenly chimed in, \"That's not hard to fix. Let Zhong Mei find a man here and get married. Then her household registration can be transferred over!\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded thoughtfully. \"True, I have been busy helping her with work these past few days. Now that things have settled down, I plan to look around and introduce her to some prospects — preferably someone with an urban hukou and a steady job. But I’m not sure if I can find someone suitable.\"","When it came to Zhong Mei’s marriage, Qiao Lanshu suddenly felt a bit melancholy.","Given Zhong Mei’s circumstances, it would be hard enough to find someone with an urban hukou, let alone someone with a job.","Actually, Zhong Mei wasn't bad-looking. She was clever, hardworking, and efficient.","Finding a partner wouldn’t be difficult, but her options were indeed limited.","After all, she was from another province, with her family too far away. Many men were reluctant to marry a bride from elsewhere, afraid she might run off someday.","Additionally, her household registration was under the labor reform camp, making it a rural registration.","She had no savings, no family backing, and no registered job.","The men in the city, especially those with stable jobs, tended to be picky. They usually looked for someone in a similar situation.","Often both parties had work, and both came from decent families.","Zhong Mei really had few advantages.","Even Qiao Lanshu felt lucky to have married Qin Yuanzheng.","But whether Zhong Mei would have that kind of luck was hard to say.","Thinking about this, Qiao Lanshu sighed faintly.","Auntie Shi continued tidying the vegetable garden. \"Ah, finding a match isn’t that hard. I’d say we introduce Zhong Mei to a man with an urban hukou first—whether or not he has a job is secondary. Solve the household registration problem first. That way, Zhong Mei might even get a permanent position at the food factory later!\"","At the food factory, the family workers and temporary workers who performed well all had a chance to become permanent staff.","At this point, Auntie Shi didn’t bring up her own sons. Instead, after a moment’s thought, she said, \"I know quite a few sisters who have unmarried sons at home. I’ll introduce a few to you another day—promise I’ll pick out some good ones.\"","The household registrations would definitely be urban, but whether these boys had jobs was uncertain.","Even if they did have jobs, they might just be temporary workers.","Back then, finding a job was tough, and buying one could cost hundreds or even thousands.","Qiao Lanshu knew Auntie Shi was speaking the truth. Auntie Shi herself had two sons in their late teens, so she knew the current state of matchmaking.","Qiao Lanshu thought for a moment and said, \"There’s no hurry on this. I’ll go ask Hóngméi (Zhong Mei) another day to see what she thinks.\"","Then she smiled. \"Zhong Mei might not even want to get married. I can tell she doesn’t seem to care much about it.\"","The two of them were so absorbed in their conversation that they almost forgot Guan Wenjun was still there.","Guan Wenjun stood by, listening to their talk. His expression looked strange.","Qiao Lanshu turned and saw him. She quickly said, \"Director Guan, why don’t you come in for a cup of tea? My dad just sent me some pre-Qingming tea last month. Brother Zheng said it tastes great. Want to try some?\"","Guan Wenjun hesitated, a bit tempted. He took a couple of steps toward the house, but then suddenly changed his mind and turned back.","\"Forget it, forget it. I’ll have the tea another day. Old Qin isn’t around, so I won’t stay. Besides, I’ve got things to do. I’ll head out now.\"","With that, he said his goodbyes and left without even entering the house.","After he was gone, Auntie Shi made Niuwa wash his hands and give him something to drink, handing him a cornmeal bun to eat.","Then, taking a broom, she started sweeping the yard and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Xiao Qiao, do you think Director Guan might have a thing for Zhong Mei?\"","Qiao Lanshu was holding An An while leaning back in a lounge chair in the yard. She didn’t seem too surprised by the remark—after all, Guan Wenjun’s behavior earlier was far too obvious.","She hesitated and said, \"I agree that Director Guan seemed off. This isn’t the first time he’s asked me about Zhong Mei.\"","Pausing, she sat up straighter and added, \"But they might not even know each other. Could it be that they met the time Niuwa was taken away? Maybe something happened between them that I don’t know about?\"","She was referring to the time Liu Weihong took Niuwa away and she and Zhong Mei chased after him.","That day, Guan Wenjun was the first to arrive at the scene with his people.","At that time, Qiao Lanshu had pretended to faint, and when Guan Wenjun arrived, it was Zhong Mei he had spoken to. So that must have been when they first got acquainted.","After all, Guan Wenjun had never recognized Zhong Mei.","He didn’t know that she was the girl who had beaten him up during that ’speculation and profiteering’ incident.","Thinking this over, Qiao Lanshu found it amusing how foolish Guan Wenjun could be—just a change of hairstyle on Hóngméi, and he completely failed to recognize her.","If he had recognized her, would his feelings for her still be the same?","Qiao Lanshu wondered to herself and then said to Auntie Shi, \"I don’t think they’re suitable. Director Guan plays quite a role—he’s about to be head of the Supply Department, which is no small rank. Plus, I hear his family background is really well off. Both his parents are officials, a scholarly family by the looks of it. They’d probably look down on Zhong Mei. Better to avoid trouble and find someone more down to earth for her.\"","Zhong Mei had a very assertive personality. Probably because she never had someone to rely on growing up, she came across as strong and decisive, and she refused to tolerate any mistreatment whatsoever.","If she ended up with Guan Wenjun, considering his status and family background, would Zhong Mei have to curry favor with his entire family and constantly live under their scrutiny?","Qiao Lanshu thought that wouldn’t be good.","Auntie Shi, however, saw things more clearly. While sweeping the yard, she said to Qiao Lanshu, “Fate is a mysterious thing. Who knows, Zhong Mei might just meet her own destined match, and when that happens, we won’t have to worry anymore.”","Zhong Mei was actually quite pretty: she had an oval face, cherry-like lips, and very lively eyes when she smiled.","But her skin was tanned from the sun, and she didn’t pay much attention to her appearance. The clothes she wore were old and covered in patches.","Because of malnutrition, her hair was somewhat yellow and coarse, and her figure was thin and wiry.","Yet she had good bone structure. With some proper care, she would definitely turn into a beauty.","A girl this attractive, even with modest circumstances, would have plenty of men eyeing her.","After all, let’s face it, men mostly care about looks.","Auntie Shi paused for a moment, then added, “These days, finding a wife isn’t easy. There are so many men who can’t get married. Don’t worry; pretty soon, suitors will be knocking on Zhong Mei’s door.”","Auntie Shi, with her life experience, was right. Only a few days after she said that, something started brewing with Zhong Mei.","...","That day, Qiao Lanshu was carrying her vegetable basket on her way to buy groceries, so she stopped by the food factory gate to wait for Zhong Mei.","Since Zhong Mei had moved out to rent a place a couple of days ago, Qiao Lanshu was concerned about her and wanted to check in.","Then, Qiao Lanshu saw that after work, when Zhong Mei reached the factory gate, a young male worker was walking beside her.","This man was an employee at the food factory, a regular staff member.","Qiao Lanshu recognized him—he was from the bread workshop, responsible for kneading dough. She had seen him once or twice when she used to go there to buy cheap bread.","The worker was tall and thin, with a very ordinary face—the kind of face you’d lose in a crowd.","But having an ordinary appearance wasn’t necessarily a flaw; after all, most people were average.","When a woman chooses a husband, aside from personal circumstances, the most important thing is his character.","If his character isn’t good, nothing else matters.","Qiao Lanshu didn’t know what this worker’s character was like, since she wasn’t familiar with him.","But seeing him follow Zhong Mei, laughing and chatting with her, it didn’t look right.","Qiao Lanshu rubbed her chin and thought to herself, Could Auntie Shi’s prediction be coming true?","Had someone already set their sights on Zhong Mei?","Zhong Mei worked as a temporary worker in the pickled vegetable workshop, which was thanks to Qiao Lanshu’s recommendation. She had arranged it so that Wang Xue and Deng Weijun, who were both in the same workshop, could look after Zhong Mei.","The pickled vegetable workshop was far from the bread workshop. It was rare for workers to visit neighboring workshops during work hours.","How did that man even notice Zhong Mei, especially since she hadn’t been working there long?","While Qiao Lanshu was deep in thought, Zhong Mei caught sight of her standing across from the factory.","Her eyes lit up, and a smile spread across her usually expressionless face.","She immediately said goodbye to the man, ignoring whatever else he said, and ran straight toward Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu noticed the man lingering at the factory gate, his eyes fixed on Zhong Mei.","After she ran off, he didn’t follow.","At least he had the sense to stay put.","Zhong Mei was thrilled to see Qiao Lanshu. “Lanshu, did you come to find me?”","Qiao Lanshu smiled and nodded, linking her arm with Zhong Mei’s. “Of course I did. I’m going grocery shopping, and you have to come with me.”","Zhong Mei nodded happily. “No problem at all.”","She then pulled a handful of sunflower seeds from her coat pocket and pressed them into Qiao Lanshu’s hand. “Here, these are from Deng Weijun. I’ve been busy all day and barely ate any.”","Deng Weijun used to love giving Qiao Lanshu snacks.","Now that she was gone, he was giving them to Zhong Mei instead.","Qiao Lanshu couldn’t help but laugh. “Weijun’s a good guy, isn’t he? I asked him to look out for you, since you’re new and I was worried you might have trouble fitting in.”","That was something Zhong Mei was grateful to Qiao Lanshu for.","Not only had she found Zhong Mei a job, but she had also arranged for someone to take care of her.","The two walked arm in arm for a while, then Qiao Lanshu looked back. Lowering her voice, she leaned close to Zhong Mei’s ear and asked, “By the way, that man who was talking to you—he’s Lai Hongmao from the bread workshop, right? Are you two close?”","Zhong Mei glanced back. They had walked quite far, and Lai Hongmao was already gone—no sign of him at the factory.","She turned back to Qiao Lanshu and said, “I’ve only been working there a short time; I’m not close with anyone. Yesterday, Wang Xue mentioned that the bread workshop had a new batch of products, but some quality control wasn’t good, so they were selling defective ones at a discount. I went to buy two, and that’s when I met Lai Hongmao. He’s quite helpful and seems like a nice person.”","Zhong Mei lowered her voice even further and added, “He just told me that people in his workshop can buy bread at a really cheap price—normal bread, not the defective kind. He asked if I wanted to buy some, and said he could help me get it.”","Qiao Lanshu understood immediately after hearing that.","This Lai Hongmao was interested in Zhong Mei.","She lowered her voice and warned, “You should be careful. He’s probably got his eye on you.”","Zhong Mei: “...”","Zhong Mei hesitated. “That can’t be, right? We just met.”","Though Zhong Mei and Lai Hongmao had only just met, he had likely already found out all about her situation.","Qiao Lanshu asked her, “And what about you? What do you think of Lai Hongmao? I know he’s a regular employee at the factory, with a stable job, good benefits, and can even apply for housing. As a potential match, his conditions are decent.”","Then she added, “Sure, he’s not much to look at, and we don’t know his background, so we should ask around.”","Zhong Mei: “...”","Zhong Mei hadn’t thought about it that way, but now that Qiao Lanshu mentioned it, she started to consider it.","Qiao Lanshu whispered, “What do you think of him?”","Zhong Mei shook her head. “I don’t know. I think all men are the same—nothing special. As long as his character is decent, that’s all that matters.”","After all, she wasn’t in a position to be picky.","Qiao Lanshu said, “Then I’ll find someone to ask about him tomorrow and see what they know.”"]},{"number":212,"title":"Chapter 212: Director Guan, what a coincidence","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu and Zhong Mei went to the supply and marketing cooperative together to buy groceries.","As the weather was getting warmer now, the variety of vegetables and fruits had increased somewhat.","She bought a radish, a cabbage, and a few potatoes. When she saw some fresh fennel, even though she didn’t know how to cook it, she bought some anyway.","Zhong Mei asked, “What are you going to do with this fennel? Stir-fry it or make soup?”","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, “I should chop it up and make dumplings. I saw Brother Zheng eat it in the cafeteria before; he seemed to really like it. I’ll take it home and have Auntie Shi make dumplings.”","When Zhong Mei heard this, she deliberately teased her, saying, “You know, ever since you got married, all you talk about is your dear Brigade Commander Qin. There’s no room for anyone else in your eyes.”","Qiao Lanshu carefully placed the fennel into her basket, shot a glare at Zhong Mei, and retorted, “Nonsense. Aren’t you still in my eyes?”","Zhong Mei was just joking, of course. She knew well enough that Qiao Lanshu cared about her.","Zhong Mei also bought some radishes, planning to make radish soup at home.","Since there was no meat available at the moment, they bought some eggs instead. Qiao Lanshu spotted fresh goat’s milk and bought two catties of it.","After all, the family goat had almost run out of milk by now.","And although An’an was only a few months old and could drink formula, fresh goat’s milk would surely be better.","Of course, Qiao Lanshu didn’t skimp on Niuwa’s share either.","When Han Wenlin went to the countryside to hunt down Zheng Weigong and his sister, he had left two hundred yuan and fifty catties of grain coupons for Qin Yuanzheng, which was intended as Niuwa’s living expenses.","Before long, Qiao Lanshu’s basket was packed full, while Zhong Mei’s basket only held a few eggs and a radish.","Since she lived alone, she didn’t buy much.","After leaving the supply cooperative, Zhong Mei hesitated for a moment, then still asked Qiao Lanshu, “Lanshu, you’ve been married for a year now. Have you thought about when you’ll go back to Yangcheng to visit your family?”","Qiao Lanshu sighed and spoke softly:","“I really want to go back and see my dad. I originally planned to return this summer, but I accidentally got pregnant with An’an, and now An’an is still so small—she can’t handle long, tiring journeys. Besides, the climate between Yangcheng and Longcheng is completely different, so I’m worried the baby wouldn’t adapt. Brother Zheng and I discussed it and decided it’s better to postpone for another two years, at least until the child is older before going back...”","As she spoke, Qiao Lanshu added, “I wrote to my dad about this, and he told me not to rush home, that everything is fine there, and not to worry. It’s just that my younger brother often mentions me, saying he wants to come to Longcheng to see me. But he’s still young, only five or six years old, and my dad isn’t comfortable letting him travel so far.”","The trains were very slow in those days, and transportation was inconvenient.","Yangcheng and Longcheng were two thousand kilometers apart, so it wasn’t easy for her family to meet.","Qiao Lanshu really missed her father, but now that she had An’an, she had to consider the child’s needs as well.","This was why, under normal circumstances, it was better for girls not to marry too far away.","Before marriage, it didn’t seem like a big deal, but after marriage and having children, going home became incredibly difficult.","Zhong Mei was silent, lost in thought.","Qiao Lanshu asked, “Are you thinking of going back?”","Zhong Mei immediately shook her head: “No way. Why would I want to go back? I don’t ever want to return.”","Qiao Lanshu said, “That’s true. Given your family situation, if you went back, you’d probably be tied up and sent off to some man’s house again.”","Zhong Mei nodded and said quietly, “I’m just worried about my two younger sisters. After I left, it’s probably their turn. But luckily, they’re still young. In a couple of years, I’ll find a way to go back and bring them to Longcheng.”","Zhong Mei’s family had three daughters, so the girls were considered worthless—just a waste of food at home.","Her father often said that he was unlucky to be raising daughters for someone else’s family.","After all, daughters would eventually marry into another family, so from birth, they were seen as belonging to someone else.","Growing up, they had a hard life. Their parents would beat and scold them, calling them \"money-losers.\"","Zhong Mei managed to escape on her own, but she had to find a way to rescue her two younger sisters as well.","After buying their groceries, the two women went home separately.","The next morning, Qiao Lanshu followed Zhong Mei to the food factory again.","Zhong Mei was a temporary worker and couldn’t afford to slack off or be late, so she hurried off to work in the pickle workshop.","Qiao Lanshu went straight to find the security guard uncle at the food factory.","The guard uncle was quite familiar with Qiao Lanshu. Seeing her arrive, he was pleasantly surprised: “Comrade Xiao Qiao! Long time no see. Where have you been working lately?”","Qiao Lanshu smiled and handed the guard a pack of tea leaves, saying, “I’m at home taking care of the baby, no job. Uncle, this is some pre-Qingming tea sent from my hometown in Yangcheng. Have a taste.”","The guard uncle happily took the tea. He opened the paper wrapping, sniffed it, and gave a thumbs-up: “This tea smells wonderful!”","He then put the tea into his drawer and asked Qiao Lanshu, “So, what’s the matter? Spill it.”","Qiao Lanshu stood by the door of the guardhouse, lowered her voice, and said to the guard uncle, “Uncle, you’ve worked at the food factory for many years. I want to ask you about someone.”","The guard uncle asked, “Who are you looking into?”","Qiao Lanshu glanced around, saw no one passing by, and then said, “It’s Lai Hongmao from the bread workshop. Do you know him?”","The guard uncle immediately replied, “Of course I do; let me tell you, there’s no one in the whole food factory I don’t know. That young man, Lai Hongmao—I know him. He’s worked in the food factory for about three or four years, a regular employee, a local from Longcheng, in the bread workshop.”","The guard uncle then looked at Qiao Lanshu and asked, “Why are you asking about him? Did he get into some trouble?”","Qiao Lanshu chuckled and said, “No trouble, uncle. Anyway, can you help me find out about his family background? It’s useful to me.”","The guard uncle didn’t ask further and nodded, agreeing to look into Lai Hongmao.","...","Prompted by Qiao Lanshu’s reminder, Zhong Mei also began to pay attention to Lai Hongmao.","Lai Hongmao was indeed quite attentive to her. The bread workshop and the pickle workshop were far apart, yet Zhong Mei would somehow “run into” him outside the workshop.","At lunch in the cafeteria, Lai Hongmao would “coincidentally” line up right behind Zhong Mei and greet her: “What a coincidence, Comrade Zhong Mei. We meet again.”","Zhong Mei: “...”","Such obviously staged encounters left Zhong Mei with no choice but to wonder.","Zhong Mei smiled and nodded but said nothing.","Lai Hongmao added, “By the way, I still have some bread subsidy tickets for this month. Do you want to buy some bread? You can use my tickets.”","He then added, “No charge.”","Wang Xue stood together with Zhong Mei and, upon hearing those words, immediately said, “Oh my, Comrade Lai Hongmao, so you’re such a warm-hearted person, huh? Zhong Mei doesn’t want the bread coupons, but I do! I just love bread. Can you give your coupons to me?”","Lai Hongmao: “...”","Lai Hongmao looked a bit awkward: “Ah... well...”","Wang Xue watched his embarrassed expression, smiled, and said, “Oh, all right, all right, I know I’m thick-skinned. I’m not some young, pretty unmarried girl, so I’m certainly not worthy of these bread coupons, am I?”","Lai Hongmao: “...”","He was both embarrassed and a little irritated by her words. Frowning at Wang Xue, he said, “Comrade Wang Xue, you shouldn’t joke like that.”","How awkward could this be?","Though he did have feelings for Zhong Mei, having Wang Xue say it out loud made him lose face.","Wang Xue then lightly tapped her own mouth and said, “Oh, sorry, I’m someone who speaks bluntly. Don’t mind me.”","With that, she grabbed Zhong Mei and headed off to get their meal.","Lai Hongmao’s face darkened. Wang Xue’s interruption had ruined his mood.","After Wang Xue and Zhong Mei got their food, Wang Xue whispered to her, “This Lai Hongmao guy is definitely interested in you, but you need to think carefully.”","Zhong Mei asked quietly, “What do you mean?”","Wang Xue replied, “Xiao Qiao joined later and left early, so she doesn’t know some things. This Lai Hongmao has pursued other female colleagues before and even went on blind dates with two of them—neither worked out. With his background, if he can’t even get a match through blind dates, I suspect there’s something wrong with him.”","Wang Xue’s point was that Zhong Mei should first find out about Lai Hongmao’s character and not fall for him naively.","Zhong Mei nodded. “Okay, I understand. Thanks, Sister Xue.”","Wang Xue waved her hand dismissively, telling her not to be so polite.","Wang Xue had been entrusted by Qiao Lanshu to keep an eye on Zhong Mei, so she treated her like one of her own.","When work ended in the afternoon, Lai Hongmao came looking for Zhong Mei again.","He walked beside her, pushing a heavy-duty bicycle, and said with a smile, “Zhong Mei, where do you live? Do you want me to give you a ride?”","As he spoke, he patted the back seat of his bike. “See, I can ride you home on this.”","Bicycles weren’t cheap back then—at least two hundred yuan apiece.","And even if you had the money, you needed a bicycle coupon to buy one, which wasn’t easy to get.","Lai Hongmao hadn’t brought his bike to work before, but today he had.","Maybe it was just for show.","Zhong Mei glanced at his bicycle and asked, “Comrade Lai, is this your own bike?”","Lai Hongmao nodded with some pride. “Of course it is. I bought it myself—cost me one hundred and eighty yuan. Not cheap.”","Zhong Mei felt a bit envious. She really wanted a bicycle too. Once she saved up enough money, she was definitely going to buy one!","Lai Hongmao got on his bike and said to her, “Come on, Comrade Zhong Mei, let me take you home.”","His eagerness was hard to miss, and many workers at the food factory saw it.","By tomorrow, probably everyone in the factory would know Lai Hongmao was pursuing Zhong Mei.","Zhong Mei shook her head and declined: “No need, Comrade Lai. I live very close—just a few steps away.”","Lai Hongmao: “...”","Seeing that she really didn’t want to ride his bike, he got off and walked it alongside her, saying, “Then I’ll walk you home instead.”","Zhong Mei actually wanted to ask Lai Hongmao what his intentions were—whether he truly wanted to start a relationship.","So she let him walk beside her as they crossed the street and headed into an alley.","Before she could figure out how to phrase her question, she spotted a familiar man walking toward them.","Her heart skipped a beat as she recognized him, and she instinctively lowered her head, speeding up to slip away.","Guan Wenjun watched Zhong Mei bow her head, pretending not to know him, and felt a knot of frustration in his chest.","Sure, everyone was terrified of the Revolutionary Committee, but he wasn’t working there anymore!","Besides, hadn’t they had a pretty good talk last time?","Why was she running away?","Guan Wenjun was a little annoyed.","He stood by the roadside as Lai Hongmao glanced at him briefly before looking away.","Lai Hongmao kept pace with Zhong Mei and said, “Comrade Zhong Mei, do you live around here? It really is close to our factory. By the way, how many people are in your family? Would it be convenient for me to visit?”","Guan Wenjun frowned, staring at Lai Hongmao. He had an ordinary face, an ordinary man.","Could it be that Zhong Mei actually liked this type?","Guan Wenjun couldn’t help but call out, “Zhong Mei?”","Hearing his voice, Zhong Mei froze in panic.","She turned her head slightly, pretending she’d just noticed him, and forced a fake smile. “Oh? Isn’t this Director Guan? Ha, what a coincidence! Where are you heading?”","Guan Wenjun: “...”","Did no one ever tell her that her smile was really fake?","Instead of answering, he asked, “Are you off work?”","Zhong Mei nodded and instinctively took a step closer to Lai Hongmao, as if trying to hide behind him.","Guan Wenjun’s expression darkened further. “And this is? Your friend?”","He pointed at Lai Hongmao and asked Zhong Mei.","Zhong Mei exchanged a glance with Lai Hongmao, but before she could speak, Lai Hongmao answered first: “Zhong Mei and I are just colleagues—nothing more.”","That was the right thing to say, since in those days, any hint of improper male-female relations could lead to serious consequences.","Lai Hongmao could tell that Guan Wenjun was no ordinary person, so he chose his words carefully. At the same time, he wondered: did Zhong Mei have some special relationship with this Director Guan? Why was Guan looking at him with such obvious hostility?","Guan Wenjun looked at Lai Hongmao, then stepped forward. “What a coincidence—I live around here too. I’ll walk with you.”","With that, he came to Zhong Mei’s other side and walked alongside her.","Zhong Mei: “...”","She instinctively stiffened her back, not knowing where to put her arms.","Could Guan Wenjun really live nearby?","Oh no—how unlucky was she?","If he recognized her, she’d be done for.","Lai Hongmao also felt the atmosphere was strange.","He pushed his bike, staying on Zhong Mei’s other side, but when he tried to talk to her, she answered perfunctorily.","Ever since this Director Guan showed up, Zhong Mei seemed distracted, her attention no longer on him.","What did this mean?","What was the relationship between Zhong Mei and this Director Guan?"]},{"number":213,"title":"Chapter 213: Rogue","paragraphs":["Zhong Mei had originally planned to have a proper talk with Lai Hongmao.","After all, she wasn't one to drag things out—if something needed to be said, she wanted it settled quickly.","Though she found Lai Hongmao’s appearance ordinary and his personality just so-so, at least his circumstances were decent. He had a stable job, a bicycle, and more importantly, a household registration in Longcheng.","She just didn’t know much else about him—how many people were in his family, how many brothers he had, and what kind of partner he was looking for.","Had he been approaching her these past couple of days because he wanted to pursue a relationship?","But with Guan Wenjun around, she couldn’t bring up these topics.","The three of them walked into the alley until they reached the entrance of her compound. Seeing that Guan Wenjun and Lai Hongmao showed no sign of leaving, Zhong Mei stopped at the gate and said to them, “I’m home. Take your time leaving—I’ll head inside now.”","With that, she waved at them and turned to enter the courtyard.","Lai Hongmao quickly pushed his bicycle forward and called after her, “Hey, Zhong Mei, wait a moment.”","Zhong Mei paused and looked back. “Something else?”","Lai Hongmao smiled and asked, “You live here?”","Zhong Mei nodded.","“Alright, I’ll be off then,” he said with a grin.","He mounted his bicycle, glanced at Guan Wenjun, and soon rode away.","Guan Wenjun stood there alone, suddenly feeling like a fool for walking all this way.","What was he even doing, tagging along while Zhong Mei and Lai Hongmao were obviously courting?","Not able to figure it out, he frowned darkly and stalked off with a heavy expression.","...","As for what was happening with Zhong Mei, Qiao Lanshu had no idea. Zhong Mei hadn’t come to tell her, and Guan Wenjun hadn’t visited in a while.","Zhong Mei’s marriage prospects were still pending, so while Qiao Lanshu helped her look into matches, she also kept up with her studies. She had nearly reviewed all her high school textbooks.","Qin Yuanzheng had been less busy with work lately, coming home quite early every day.","With time on his hands and little An’an still too young to understand anything, he spent every night dragging Qiao Lanshu into “exercise.”","Qiao Lanshu was truly worn out by his stamina. After two straight weeks of this, she couldn’t take it anymore. One night, she flat-out refused him, saying, “Are you a bull or what? Even if you want to plow the fields, you have to see how the soil is doing! Plowing day after day, you’ll ruin the land.”","Her voice was soft, carrying a Yangcheng accent that sounded gentle and sweet. Qin Yuanzheng loved it more and more. In the dim light of the oil lamp, he put An’an in a corner, then happily scooped Qiao Lanshu into his arms. “Ruined? Let me check,” he murmured, pressing her down onto the bed.","She let out a low yelp and scrambled to stop his hands. “Oh, don’t, don’t—stop!”","Holding her off with one hand, he pulled her pants down in one swift motion. “You said it was ruined, so I’m just checking.”","She laughed and squirmed, dodging him. “It’s not ruined, okay? Just leave me alone!”","Gripping her slender calf, his rough palm rubbing along it, he pinned her down and kissed her cheek. “No, I’m still worried. Let me check properly.”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","She was ticklish, and his touch made her giggle uncontrollably as she tried to escape, backing up to the edge of the bed. Trapped, he held her down and started his “inspection.”","And this inspection wasn’t a proper one at all—he used both hands and mouth.","By the time he was done, Qiao Lanshu couldn’t even laugh anymore.","But Qin Yuanzheng explained with a straight face, “I just checked—it was a little damaged—so I gave it some soothing care. Feeling better now?”","Qiao Lanshu was at a loss for words. She swore she’d never make a careless remark again.","He added, “Since I’ve fixed it, how about we continue tonight? I really liked the position you used last time—want to do that again?”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","With lighter work obligations, Qin Yuanzheng came home early each day. They’d finish dinner quickly, and then he’d pull her back to the room, endlessly energetic.","He demanded “three rounds of plowing” every day.","Privately, he was scheming. Last time, she had coaxed him into losing control and he’d gone all the way inside. Now he worried she might get pregnant again.","If she did become pregnant, there would be abstinence in both the first and last trimesters.","So he had to feast while he could, fill himself up now before the hardship ahead.","With that thought, even after they’d already lain down for the night, he suddenly rolled over and woke Qiao Lanshu, who was nearly asleep from exhaustion.","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","She was utterly helpless.","That man was such a bull!","...","Qin Yuanzheng had kept this up for two months, probably because he’d been holding back for too long.","He wanted to make up for lost time.","But it was Qiao Lanshu who suffered, worn out by him.","Luckily, his work soon picked up again, cutting down the frequency and giving her a chance to recover.","One morning, Auntie Shi saw Qiao Lanshu up early and exclaimed in surprise, “Oh, Xiao Qiao, you’re awake early today!”","Qiao Lanshu flushed with embarrassment. “Yeah, I woke up early today,” she said awkwardly.","It helped that Qin Yuanzheng hadn’t kept her up too long the night before, so she could get to sleep earlier.","Auntie Shi chuckled knowingly. Having been around for so long, she understood perfectly that it was because of Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu’s close relationship.","As a married woman herself, she caught on easily.","She actually envied this young couple—their affection was truly something.","Auntie Shi then said, “I still have some red dates and angelica root at home. I’ll stew a chicken soup for you. Tomorrow is Mid-Autumn Festival, and the Commander said we can slaughter a chicken.”","Mentioning the festival reminded Qiao Lanshu that she hadn’t visited Zhong Mei in a long time.","Mainly, over the past two months, Qin Yuanzheng had been so clingy at night that she got little sleep and was always drowsy during the day.","Between taking care of the baby, studying, and napping, she hadn’t had time to go out.","But Zhong Mei hadn’t come over either.","Qiao Lanshu decided it was time to check on her.","Auntie Shi added, “By the way, Xiao Qiao, when I was shopping for groceries yesterday, I heard the neighbors saying that the kindergarten in the military compound has opened. Has the Commander mentioned it? Maybe we should send Niuwa there?”","Niuwa was already four and far too mischievous—running wild in the yard every day.","It might be better to send him to kindergarten.","Besides, it doesn’t cost anything.","Qiao Lanshu had just heard about this matter and immediately said, \"Sure, this is doable. Director Han hasn't come back yet. I'll take charge of this. I'll go to the kindergarten tomorrow and fill out an enrollment form.\"","As she said that, Qiao Lanshu handed An'an to Auntie Shi, changed into a different set of clothes, and said to Auntie Shi, \"Auntie Shi, I'm going out. I'll go to the kindergarten and then visit Zhong Mei.\"","Auntie Shi nodded and said, \"Okay, go ahead. I'll take care of the house.\"","After Qiao Lanshu went out, she went to look for Zhong Mei.","At this time, Zhong Mei was not in the food factory.","The food factory had an early half - day off. Together with the Mid - Autumn Festival tomorrow, they had a one - and - a - half - day holiday.","So Zhong Mei got off work early, and Lai Hongmao still pushed his bicycle and followed her.","Over the past two months, the two of them had become quite familiar with each other.","Lai Hongmao chatted with Zhong Mei and said to her, \"Comrade Zhong Mei, can I visit your home today?\"","He had proposed to visit Zhong Mei's home several times, but each time he was rejected by Zhong Mei.","Zhong Mei shook her head with a smile and refused, \"Of course not. It's not appropriate.\"","Lai Hongmao then asked, \"Why isn't it appropriate?\"","Hearing his question, Zhong Mei felt a little unhappy.","She directly said, \"Because there's only me at home, so it's not appropriate.\"","In fact, after getting along for this period of time, Zhong Mei already thought that Lai Hongmao was not suitable.","Lai Hongmao was always getting close to her and sending her home, but he never made their relationship clear. She didn't know what he really meant.","Zhong Mei had also tried to ask him a few times, but Lai Hongmao simply ignored her hints.","In this way, Zhong Mei knew that Lai Hongmao didn't really want to be in a relationship.","The smile on Lai Hongmao's face faded a bit. He said, \"How could it be inappropriate? You live in a compound. There are other people living there. We're not really alone. Zhong Mei, it's okay. You're just too concerned about these things. I don't mind.\"","Zhong Mei: \"...\"","As they were talking, they had reached the alley entrance. Not far into the alley was the compound where Zhong Mei lived.","Although Zhong Mei had already rejected him, he still followed her.","Seeing that he still said nothing and was about to follow her here, Zhong Mei was immediately a bit unhappy. Just then, Qiao Lanshu came. She hadn't found Zhong Mei in the food factory.","After learning that the food factory was on holiday, she went to wait for Zhong Mei at the entrance of the compound where she lived. Sure enough, she waited for her. \"Zhong Mei, so you're on holiday today?\"","When Zhong Mei saw Qiao Lanshu, her eyes lit up. She quickly ran over and said, \"Lanshu, you came to see me?\"","She explained to Qiao Lanshu, \"I originally planned to visit you this afternoon. I've been very busy at work before. I didn't dare to go out at night, so I haven't been able to visit you.\"","Qiao Lanshu hadn't come to see her for two months, but she wasn't worried. After all, Qiao Lanshu had married an officer and was a military dependant. Now there were guards at the entrance of the yard.","Qiao Lanshu glanced at Lai Hongmao. Lai Hongmao knew Qiao Lanshu. He nodded with a smile and said, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, long time no see.\"","Qiao Lanshu also nodded politely. Then she asked Zhong Mei, \"Zhong Mei, what's going on here?\"","Did Zhong Mei and Lai Hongmao get together during this time?","Zhong Mei shook her head at her and gave her a meaningful look.","After all, they were good friends. Qiao Lanshu almost immediately understood what Zhong Mei meant.","She was a bit surprised. After two months, Lai Hongmao still hadn't expressed his feelings to Zhong Mei?","He was really too dilatory.","What on earth was this Lai Hongmao thinking?","Zhong Mei didn't fall out with Lai Hongmao. Presumably, she was thinking that they both worked in the food factory and she was still a temporary worker. She couldn't afford to make any mistakes at work.","So she didn't dare to offend people casually.","But Qiao Lanshu didn't have to consider so much.","She took Zhong Mei's hand and turned to look at Lai Hongmao. She directly asked him, \"Comrade Lai Hongmao, do you always send Zhong Mei home these days because you want to be in a relationship with her?\"","Lai Hongmao didn't expect Qiao Lanshu to ask so directly.","He was stunned for a moment and then said awkwardly, \"Well, um... you can put it that way.\"","Qiao Lanshu's face darkened. She looked at him and asked, \"What do you mean by 'you can put it that way'? What does your words mean?\"","Zhong Mei's face also turned cold. She looked at Lai Hongmao with a cold look in her eyes and had already imagined smashing Lai Hongmao's head a dozen times in her heart.","But thinking of her previous labor - reform experience, she took a deep breath and suppressed the anger in her heart.","Lai Hongmao leaned against his bicycle and said to Qiao Lanshu with a smile, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, to be honest, I really like Zhong Mei. I do want to be in a relationship with her. But, you know, such things have to go through both parents before they can be confirmed. Don't we young people have to listen to our parents? I can't make the decision on my own, and neither can Zhong Mei. We can only get in touch with each other privately first. We'll talk about these things after we get more familiar.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"???\"","Hearing this, Zhong Mei couldn't help rolling her eyes. She sneered and said, \"Oh, really? Then I'm really sorry. I'm an orphan and I don't have parents.\"","Hearing this, Lai Hongmao looked a bit surprised.","However, he quickly smiled again and said, \"Zhong Mei, it doesn't matter. I don't mind that you're an orphan, and I don't mind that you don't have a proper job. Well, how about we be in a relationship first? We can meet my parents later when we think it's appropriate. After all, you can't tell in just one or two days about a relationship...\"","With a \"pop\" sound, Qiao Lanshu directly slapped Lai Hongmao.","Lai Hongmao: \"???\"","Lai Hongmao was completely stunned. He didn't even know why Qiao Lanshu suddenly attacked him. He pointed at Qiao Lanshu with his finger, and his face was gloomy. \"Comrade Qiao Lanshu! I was talking nicely. Why did you hit me?\"","Lai Hongmao was very angry, but he didn't dare to fight back. After all, he knew Qiao Lanshu's identity.","Qiao Lanshu was so angry that her face turned red. She sneered and scolded him, \"What do you mean by 'be in a relationship first'? A relationship without the intention of getting married is just playing around! You say nothing and just want to be in a relationship first. Then, later, are you going to...\"","She originally wanted to say, \"Kiss first, sleep together first. After sleeping together, when you don't want to be responsible, are you going to say it's not suitable and break up, so you don't have to meet the parents and get married?\"","Qiao Lanshu thought that Lai Hongmao was simply coveting Zhong Mei's beauty.","But he looked down on Zhong Mei's conditions and didn't want to be responsible for her!","Qiao Lanshu pointed at him and shouted, \"Scoundrel!\"","Zhong Mei also stared at Lai Hongmao gloomily. She walked over and kicked his bicycle, scolding him, \"Get out!\""]},{"number":214,"title":"Chapter 214: Let Me Set You Up with Someone","paragraphs":["Lai Hongmao really found Qiao Lanshu and Zhong Mei to be completely baffling.","He had been getting close to Zhong Mei for over two months, but the opportunities to walk her home were actually quite rare.","A while back, the food factory was very busy—after all, the Mid-Autumn Festival was approaching, and orders had surged. Workers in both the pickled vegetable section and the bread section had been putting in overtime, busy making mooncakes, sweet cakes, and all sorts of pickled vegetables and fermented delicacies.","Lai Hongmao was responsible for kneading dough in the bread section. From morning till night, he was swamped, never leaving work on time.","Now that things had finally wound down these past two days, he hurried over to find Zhong Mei.","And what did he get? A slap from Qiao Lanshu.","Lai Hongmao’s face darkened. He leaned his bicycle against the wall, his eyes fixed on Zhong Mei as he said, “Zhong Mei, come over here for a moment. I need to talk to you.”","Then, glancing at Qiao Lanshu, he added, “It’s private. Not convenient for others to be present.”","Qiao Lanshu shot him a cold glare and snapped, “What are you so guilty about? What dirty business do you need to whisper in private?”","Lai Hongmao’s face flushed crimson with anger. If he hadn’t been afraid of offending Qiao Lanshu—who was, after all, the sister-in-law of Director Yang—he would have lost his temper on the spot.","Zhong Mei knew Qiao Lanshu was genuinely furious.","Zhong Mei couldn’t afford to have a full-blown falling-out with Lai Hongmao, but Qiao Lanshu had no such concerns, so she decided to step in for Zhong Mei’s sake.","Zhong Mei placed a hand on Qiao Lanshu’s arm and said quietly, “Let me go make things clear to him, so he stops bugging me from now on.”","Even though she hadn’t met with Lai Hongmao many times, the colleagues at the factory all knew he was pursuing her. Sometimes, when they ran into each other, people would even tease and joke about it.","Zhong Mei had finally settled down—she had a job, she had rented a place—and she didn’t want to court any trouble.","So she followed Lai Hongmao to the side and said to him, “Comrade Lai Hongmao, what do you want to say?”","Lai Hongmao looked at her, still unwilling to give up. He said, “Comrade Zhong Mei, I really want to be in a relationship with you. I haven’t made things clear before now because I hadn’t talked to my family yet—I was afraid they might not approve. I didn’t mean anything else. Comrade Qiao Lanshu has misunderstood me.”","No matter how he explained, Zhong Mei’s opinion of Lai Hongmao had already soured.","A grown man like him, and he still had to get his family’s permission to date someone.","If she agreed to go along with him now, and someday he said his family didn’t approve, wouldn’t he just dump her?","Her reputation would be ruined!","Zhong Mei’s face turned stern. She said, “Then I’m sorry, but I have no intention of finding a partner. You should look elsewhere.”","With that, she turned and walked away.","Lai Hongmao followed after her, calling out, “Zhong Mei! You’d better think this through! You’ve got a rural household registration, you’re only a temporary worker. Without solving that registration problem, you don’t even have a hope of becoming a permanent employee. If you go with me, at least I can help you solve the household issue!”","Zhong Mei sneered, looking back at him: “If I date you, can you really solve my household registration? And what if your family doesn’t agree? Would you secretly go and register our marriage with me?”","Lai Hongmao was taken aback, and his voice wavered: “If we really start dating, my family might come around.”","Empty words, all empty words.","If Zhong Mei couldn’t see through that, she hadn’t survived all these years for nothing.","She said coldly, “Let’s drop this whole thing. Don’t bother me again, or I’ll have no choice but to report you to the Revolutionary Committee.”","After saying that, she ran off.","Lai Hongmao stood there, still unwilling to let go.","He sneered to himself, “With your lousy circumstances, I’d like to see what kind of man you end up with.”","Then he pushed his bicycle away angrily.","Qiao Lanshu and Zhong Mei stood at the entrance of the compound, watching as he pedaled off into the distance, before finally going back inside.","The compound gate was locked at night, so it was fairly safe. Besides Zhong Mei, two other families lived there, so she wasn’t worried about Lai Hongmao coming to harass her.","Qiao Lanshu was still fuming. She said to Zhong Mei, “A-Mei, don’t worry. I’ll definitely help you find a good match. Auntie Shi said she can introduce some people. Even if the work isn’t ideal, at least the household issue can be solved. Once that’s taken care of, finding a good job will be much easier. Don’t rush; let’s take it slowly.”","Qiao Lanshu was afraid that Zhong Mei, out of desperation, might end up marrying some awful man.","That would only bring more trouble down the road.","As she spoke, Qiao Lanshu was already mentally running through a list of eligible young men she knew.","Qin Yuanzheng’s military unit had plenty of single soldiers.","But ordinary soldiers weren’t stationed there permanently; they’d have to leave eventually.","As for officers with a bit of rank, they had a lot of choices and might not be interested in Zhong Mei.","Zhong Mei’s main problem was that she had been sent to a labor reeducation camp, and her household registration was still stuck there. That put her at a serious disadvantage.","Zhong Mei smiled and said, “I understand all that. I’ll be careful.”","To her, men were all the same—it didn’t really matter which one she married. Her goal was simple: solve her household registration and job problems.","In those days, if the household issue was settled, finding work was much easier. And once she had a job, she could apply for housing.","Then her life would finally have some real hope.","The two of them stood at the compound gate, cursing Lai Hongmao for a while. But since others in the compound might overhear, they decided not to air their grievances further.","So they walked outside again. It was still early, and they headed to the supply cooperative to buy groceries.","Tomorrow was the Mid-Autumn Festival, and the cooperative would have mutton and pork available, along with some locally grown grapes and mooncakes.","Qiao Lanshu said to Zhong Mei, “If that Lai Hongmao bothers you again, go find Sister Xue. She’s a longtime employee at the factory, knows a lot of people, and can help you out.”","Zhong Mei wasn’t really afraid of Lai Hongmao. She was just worried that as a newly hired temporary worker, stirring up trouble so soon might get her fired.","The two walked along the alley, still chatting about Lai Hongmao, when Qiao Lanshu suddenly spotted Guan Wenjun again.","She paused, glancing suspiciously at Guan Wenjun and then at the surroundings. What was he doing here?","Zhong Mei saw him too. She leaned close to Qiao Lanshu and whispered, “This Director Guan—it seems like he lives around here. I’ve run into him several times before.”","Zhong Mei even patted her chest in relief. “Luckily, he hasn’t recognized me. Every time I see him, my heart is in my throat.”","But that incident was quite a while ago, and Zhong Mei wasn’t as worried anymore.","She figured Guan Wenjun had probably forgotten all about it.","When Qiao Lanshu heard this, she was puzzled: “Who told you Director Guan lives around here? He doesn’t seem to live in this area.”","Qiao Lanshu knew that Guan Wenjun had always lived in the unit's housing.","He'd probably moved into the Supply Department dormitory by now, since he'd gone there.","No matter what, there's no way he'd live here. This whole area was filled with courtyard compounds, mostly housing workers from the food factory and the textile mill.","Besides, it was far from both the Revolutionary Committee and the Supply Department. Even if Guan Wenjun didn't stay in the dormitory and wanted to rent a place, given his personality, he wouldn't choose to rent in a compound like this, would he?","As Qiao Lanshu reasoned this out, Zhong Mei grew flustered: \"Huh? But I've run into him several times around here lately. Could it be...\"","Zhong Mei lowered her voice and whispered, \"Has he recognized me?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu looked at Guan Wenjun and murmured quietly, \"Don't you think Chief Guan seems a little off?\"","Then, remembering what Auntie Shi had said earlier, a possibility struck her. \"Could it be that Chief Guan has taken a liking to you?\"","Zhong Mei: \"...\"","Zhong Mei's expression shifted to panic: \"Lanshu, have you lost your mind over my marriage prospects? How is that even possible?\"","Qiao Lanshu grew thoughtful, the more she thought about it, the more reasonable it seemed: \"Come to think of it, why didn't I ever ask Chief Guan about this before? He can be a bit scatterbrained sometimes, but he's still a capable worker. Besides, not only is he single, he also has a thing for southern girls.\"","She lowered her voice again: \"Southern girls are hard to come by around here. It's all northern girls. In the whole of Dragon City, we're probably the only two from the south. It makes sense for him to be interested in you.\"","Zhong Mei was stunned. She was silent for a moment before asking, \"Why does he like southern girls? Is there a special reason? Is his mother from the south?\"","Qiao Lanshu thought of something and couldn't help but laugh: \"I don't know. I just get the feeling he does.\"","After all, the first time they met, Guan Wenjun had flirted with her.","Back then, Qin Yuanzheng was so furious he'd kicked him straight out the door.","Every time they met after that, Guan Wenjun would make some small talk with her. Qiao Lanshu thought that if he really liked her type, then Zhong Mei would be a good match too.","She figured there was no harm in asking. They were all familiar enough that she wasn't worried about making him angry.","Guan Wenjun had spotted Zhong Mei and Qiao Lanshu just as he reached the mouth of the alley.","Lai Hongmao, who usually walked Zhong Mei home, wasn't around. That was strange—today, he hadn't followed her?","Guan Wenjun didn't want to admit he had feelings for Zhong Mei. He felt that someone in his position, with his impressive stature, should be pursued by women, not the other way around.","But lately, whenever he had free time, he couldn't help coming by this area to \"run into\" Zhong Mei.","During several of those encounters, he'd seen Lai Hongmao.","Guan Wenjun had even started to think Zhong Mei and Lai Hongmao were together.","So he became more and more conflicted. The more conflicted he got, the more aloof he acted, and the more Lai Hongmao irritated him.","Qiao Lanshu and Zhong Mei stood to the side, both staring intently at Guan Wenjun.","Guan Wenjun thought their gazes were odd, which suddenly made him feel a lot of pressure.","Qiao Lanshu smiled warmly and waved at him: \"Oh, Chief Guan, what a coincidence to run into you here.\"","Guan Wenjun felt like her smile wasn't entirely innocent, but he glanced at Zhong Mei and awkwardly walked over: \"Yeah, what a coincidence.\"","He was flustered. He remembered telling Zhong Mei he lived nearby.","But Qiao Lanshu definitely knew he didn't live here...","How was he supposed to explain that later...","Qiao Lanshu shot Zhong Mei a meaningful look, then walked up to Guan Wenjun and spoke in a low voice: \"Chief Guan, since we've met today, there's something I've been meaning to ask you. Come with me for a moment.\"","Curious, Guan Wenjun followed her without thinking: \"What's so mysterious?\"","As he walked, he kept turning back to look at Zhong Mei. When he caught her staring back, he quickly averted his gaze, his ears burning red as he followed Qiao Lanshu.","Zhong Mei: \"...\"","Before, every time Zhong Mei ran into Guan Wenjun, she'd been nervous and scared, so she'd never paid close attention to his expressions.","Now, with Qiao Lanshu's prompting, she observed him more closely and noticed that from just now until this moment, she'd caught him stealing glances at her three times.","And there he went again—another quick look back at her.","When he saw she was still watching him, he awkwardly looked away again.","Zhong Mei: \"...\"","A feeling of disbelief washed over her.","No way. Was Guan Wenjun really interested in her?","What did he see in her?","Was he just in the habit of playing benefactor, and decided to throw some charity her way too?","If she were dating Lai Hongmao, she could at least negotiate some terms.","But dating Guan Wenjun would mean she'd be marrying way above her station. There'd be no room for bargaining. As long as he'd marry her, she'd take anything.","Thinking like that, Zhong Mei suddenly saw Guan Wenjun as a perfect catch.","A section chief in the Supply Department—that was no small rank.","The housing he'd be allocated must be spacious and nice.","Plus, his salary and benefits were definitely generous. She'd never have to worry about money again.","And more importantly, her children wouldn't have to suffer hunger and hardship like she did. They'd have a completely different life.","Zhong Mei's gaze toward Guan Wenjun shifted.","She had to try to snag this golden bachelor, even if she had to use a little cunning.","Qiao Lanshu pulled Guan Wenjun aside and asked softly, \"Chief Guan, how old are you this year?\"","Guan Wenjun and Qin Yuanzheng had met while in the military, meaning Guan Wenjun had served before joining the Revolutionary Committee. He was probably around the same age as Qin Yuanzheng.","Guan Wenjun answered casually, \"I'm 29. I'll be 30 by the end of the year. Why do you ask?\"","As he spoke, he kept turning his head to look at Zhong Mei.","Qiao Lanshu noticed his gaze and found it rather amusing.","She decided to cut straight to the chase: \"Chief Guan, you're this age and still not married. Haven't you ever thought about finding a partner?\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","He felt a little embarrassed being asked that. Turning to face her, he replied, \"You're a married woman—why are you asking me that? What, are you trying to set me up?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded, looking at him: \"That's right. I want to introduce someone to you. Interested in meeting her?\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Finally, it clicked.","Qiao Lanshu had no relatives here and hardly any friends.","Who could she possibly introduce him to?","It was as clear as day.","Guan Wenjun's ears flushed bright red, and he stammered awkwardly, \"This, this... who exactly are you introducing to me?\"","As he said it, he turned and stole another furtive glance at Zhong Mei."]},{"number":215,"title":"Chapter 215: Director Guan Is Looking for a Partner","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu was originally testing Guan Wenjun, but after just a few exchanges, Guan Wenjun’s little glances kept darting toward Zhong Mei several times.","Well, that clearly showed he had some interest in Zhong Mei.","Qiao Lanshu had never seen Guan Wenjun sneak such furtive looks at any girl before.","Qiao Lanshu said bluntly, “Hey, do you see my friend Zhong Mei? I want to set someone up for her. Do you want to meet Zhong Mei?”","Guan Wenjun coughed a couple of times. He shoved his hands in his pockets and said quite primly, “This doesn’t seem quite right, does it? I need to think it over.”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","One look at Guan Wenjun like this, and Qiao Lanshu knew he was putting on airs again.","But she could understand it—after all, with Guan Wenjun’s qualifications, what kind of girl couldn’t he find?","If he wanted to, he could even chase after a female college student from a cadre family.","Never mind. Qiao Lanshu sighed and said, “You’re right; you two really aren’t a good match. Zhong Mei’s situation is a bit complicated... By the way, Director Guan, you’ve been in Dragon City for so long—do you happen to know any young men around? Could you introduce one to Zhong Mei?”","Guan Wenjun’s eyes widened. He stared at Qiao Lanshu, disbelief written all over his face.","Come on, when setting someone up with a match, was it this casual?","Shouldn’t there be back-and-forth refusals, at least two or three rounds?","After all, this was about matchmaking—he felt shy about it too, you know.","Guan Wenjun stood there, glaring at Qiao Lanshu, and said nothing for a long while.","Mostly because he didn’t know what to say.","Just then, Zhong Mei walked over. She stood beside Qiao Lanshu and said, “Xiao Qiao, let me speak with Director Guan for a bit.”","Qiao Lanshu nodded, not intending to step away. She stayed right beside Zhong Mei, waiting for her to speak.","Guan Wenjun was also waiting for Zhong Mei to speak.","But Zhong Mei stood there, only fixing her eyes on Guan Wenjun without saying a word.","Guan Wenjun glanced at Zhong Mei once, then again.","He noticed that Zhong Mei was just staring straight at him. Her big, pitch-black eyes were riveted on him, and he had no idea what she meant by it.","Stared at until his skin crawled, Guan Wenjun fumbled nervously, not knowing what to do with his hands.","Zhong Mei stared at Guan Wenjun for a good long while, watching him turn red from ears to cheeks, and then she suddenly burst out laughing. She exchanged a glance with Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu also covered her mouth and laughed.","Director Guan was just too innocent—look, his face was redder than a monkey’s rear end.","Qiao Lanshu and Zhong Mei were both laughing heartily, which made Guan Wenjun even more awkward.","But they were both very pretty. Qiao Lanshu had fair skin and dimples when she smiled, looking very cute; Zhong Mei wasn’t as fair-skinned, but she had almond-shaped eyes, an oval face with a pointed chin, and a little canine tooth when she smiled—very beautiful.","Seeing these two gorgeous girls laughing uncontrollably, being a man, Guan Wenjun couldn’t bring himself to get angry.","He looked at Qiao Lanshu, then at Zhong Mei, feeling like a monkey in a zoo.","He scratched his head and asked, “What are you laughing at?”","As he spoke, he stole another glance at Zhong Mei and asked, “So, what did you want to say to me?”","Zhong Mei looked at him with a smile and said directly, “I’m the straightforward type. I don’t like beating around the bush. Director Guan, I’ll just come out and say it: I think you’re a good man, and I’d like to be with you. Will you go out with me?”","Qiao Lanshu covered her mouth, staring at Zhong Mei in shock.","Guan Wenjun was even more dumbfounded. He stood there staring at Zhong Mei, unable to speak for a long while.","Both of them were stunned by Zhong Mei’s bold bluntness.","This girl, she didn’t have any reserve at all!","Qiao Lanshu had been the one to pursue Qin Yuanzheng actively, but even she hadn’t dared to be this direct.","What if Guan Wenjun turned her down outright?","Wouldn’t that leave no room for turning back?","Qiao Lanshu blinked her eyes and turned to look at Guan Wenjun.","And there he was, red-faced and stammering, “This, this, we don’t really know each other yet...”","Even though he did think Zhong Mei was pretty good, to decide so hastily whether to start dating—wasn’t that a bit too rash?","He seemed to think of something and said, “Aren’t you dating Lai Hongmao?”","He looked at Zhong Mei: “Did you two break up?”","The smile on Zhong Mei’s face faded slightly, and she said, “Lai Hongmao? That man has moral flaws. I thought he was unsuitable, so I told him never to come looking for me again.”","When Guan Wenjun heard this, his heart lifted a little. He said a bit guiltily, “Then you can rest assured, my moral character definitely has no flaws.”","Zhong Mei smiled and said with sincere expression,","“I know. I heard from Lanshu that you regularly support orphans, bought lots of winter clothes and shoes for the orphanage, helped fix their leaky roof, and repaired their smoky heating bed. You’re a kind and good person.","Director Guan, your wonderful virtue really moved me. But I have no education, no job—I’m afraid I don’t deserve such a good person as you. Director Guan, what do you think of me? Can you give me a chance to get to know you?”","After she said this, Qiao Lanshu was completely stunned.","She covered her mouth, turned around, and stared at Zhong Mei in disbelief.","Zhong Mei had entered society early. Qiao Lanshu had gone through junior and senior high school, but Zhong Mei hadn’t even finished elementary school before she went out to work.","She took care of her younger siblings, did housework, washed clothes, cooked, and went out every day for odd jobs to help support her family.","She was very good at reading people.","She probably said all this because she thought Guan Wenjun was a good prospect and was ready to go for it.","Still, this was the first time Qiao Lanshu had heard Zhong Mei compliment a man like this. For some reason, she felt like laughing.","She bit her lip, covered her mouth, and lowered her head, not daring to look at the smug little expression on Guan Wenjun’s face. She was afraid she’d burst out laughing.","Zhong Mei, seeing how red Guan Wenjun’s face was, shyly added a few more words: “Director Guan, you’re such a good man, so warm-hearted, and your abilities are excellent. I heard you were recently transferred to the Supply Department? That’s really impressive! It must be because you’re exceptionally capable that you got this opportunity, right?”","Zhong Mei then added, “I wonder if such an outstanding man like you could give me the chance to get to know each other and see?”","Guan Wenjun, completely swept away by Zhong Mei’s barrage of praise, was so dizzy he almost forgot his own name—let alone who he was.","The corners of his mouth involuntarily curled up. He covered his mouth, coughed, and said a bit bashfully, “Oh, it’s nothing, nothing. I’m not that great actually.”","As he spoke, he unconsciously stepped forward two steps, and Zhong Mei immediately followed.","She walked beside him, speaking with ease, “Director Guan, we’ve met a few times now, so let me formally introduce myself. My name is Zhong Mei. I’m nineteen this year, the same age as Lanshu. She’s my childhood friend and old classmate. Our hometown is both in Yangcheng.”","\"However, her conditions are better than mine. Her father is a department store manager, while my parents are just temporary workers without formal jobs. I also have two younger sisters and a younger brother at home, and my household registration is still at the labor camp...\"","As she spoke, Zhong Mei's eyes reddened, and she lowered her head as if about to cry. She asked Guan Wenjun, \"Director Guan, would you look down on me for having been in a labor camp? I can really explain this matter, but if you don't want to hear it, then I won't say anything. After all, when Lai Hongmao found out about my labor camp history, he refused to listen to my explanation...\"","Lai Hongmao actually had no idea about this; Zhong Mei deliberately said it because Guan Wenjun cared about his reputation and considered himself a righteous man. He surely wouldn't judge someone with prejudice, and certainly wouldn't want to be outdone by a \"bad person\" like Lai Hongmao.","Sure enough, Guan Wenjun immediately said, \"Comrade Zhong Mei, you are a very proactive and hardworking female comrade. I heard Old Qin mention your labor camp situation. You must have been a victim too. It's not your fault.\"","Zhong Mei immediately lifted her head, her eyes sparkling as she looked at him. \"So, you mean you don't mind this?\"","Guan Wenjun nodded with a serious expression. \"Of course, how could I mind? I already told you, it's not your fault.\"","Zhong Mei then gazed at Guan Wenjun with an admiring look, sincerely praising him, \"Director Guan, you are truly a good person.\"","Guan Wenjun coughed, adjusted his collar, and felt quite pleased with himself.","The two walked side by side through the alley. Zhong Mei asked again, \"Then, Director Guan, can we, you know, start dating?\"","Looking at Zhong Mei's admiring yet expectant eyes, he instinctively replied, \"Alright, let's give it a try.\"","As soon as he said it, Guan Wenjun regretted it inside. Oh dear, why did he agree so quickly?","He had originally planned to take things slowly, learn about her character and temperament first, and then start dating when he felt it was suitable.","But under Zhong Mei's flattering words, he gradually lost track of himself and nodded in agreement.","Something was off, really off.","He felt his ears were too soft; that wouldn't do.","While Guan Wenjun was still pondering this, Zhong Mei suddenly reached out and looped her arm through his.","Guan Wenjun: \"!!!\"","Guan Wenjun instantly tensed up, feeling as if all the blood in his body had congealed in his arm.","He stood rigidly, staring at Zhong Mei in panic.","Zhong Mei: \"...\"","Zhong Mei quietly withdrew her hand, then looked at Guan Wenjun with a bit of embarrassment. \"Director Guan, didn't you agree to date? I've seen other couples holding hands.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun felt things were moving too fast, so fast he was getting nervous.","After all, he had no experience dating, had never held a young woman's hand before, and suddenly being linked arm-in-arm startled him.","Looking at Zhong Mei, he thought his reaction earlier was a bit poor and embarrassing.","He coughed, pretending to be calm, and said, \"Of, of course we can hold hands. Do you want to now?\"","With that, he stared at Zhong Mei's face, then shifted his gaze to her hand.","He was tempted to reach out and take her hand.","But he felt he needed to be reserved and not too eager, to avoid making a fool of himself.","Zhong Mei studied his expression, amused inside, while feigning shyness on her face. She lowered her head and said, \"Director Guan, I promised Lan Shu I'd go with her to the supply cooperative to buy things for the Mid-Autumn Festival, so I need to go now.\"","Guan Wenjun was taken aback, feeling a bit disappointed. He nodded. \"Ah, I see. Well, alright then.\"","Zhong Mei smiled and asked, \"So tomorrow, for the Mid-Autumn Festival, will Director Guan come to find me?\"","Guan Wenjun's ears reddened again. Tomorrow was the Mid-Autumn Festival. If he came to see her, just the two of them alone... that would be a date, right?","What could people do on dates?","Oh my, just thinking about it made him a bit embarrassed.","Guan Wenjun said very reservedly, \"I'll see how my schedule is.\"","Zhong Mei smiled again. \"That's wonderful, Director Guan. I hope you'll have time tomorrow, so we can see each other again.\"","Hearing those words – 'I hope you'll have time' – tsk, it was clear Zhong Mei really liked him.","Zhong Mei turned and walked away, glancing back every few steps as if reluctant to part from him.","Guan Wenjun wanted to follow them to the supply cooperative, but didn't want to seem too eager, as that would hurt his pride.","Still, after standing there for a while, he ended up chasing after her. He pulled a stack of ten-yuan notes from his pocket and handed them to Zhong Mei, saying, \"Here, buy more food to nourish yourself. You're too thin.\"","Zhong Mei was somewhat surprised.","This time, it wasn't an act; she was genuinely taken aback.","Everyone had always asked her for money; it was the first time someone had handed her money.","Zhong Mei stared blankly at Guan Wenjun, momentarily forgetting to say sweet words to flatter him.","Guan Wenjun, however, looked a bit awkward. He stuffed his hands in his pockets, coughed, and said to Zhong Mei, \"What are you standing there for? Go ahead and shop at the supply cooperative with Comrade Xiao Qiao.\"","With that, he ran a hand through his hair, assuming a cool pose, and turned around, walking off stylishly.","Zhong Mei watched his retreating figure, then looked down at the money in her hand, stunned for a long time.","Qiao Lanshu had been standing at the end of the alley, watching them talk.","When she saw Guan Wenjun leave, she quickly ran over. \"Zhong Mei, what are you spacing out for?\"","Zhong Mei seemed a bit dazed as she looked at Qiao Lanshu. \"Director Guan agreed to date me.\"","Qiao Lanshu was shocked, her mouth slowly falling open. \"Ah? He agreed so quickly? Are you serious?\"","So Guan Wenjun was that easy to win over?","Qiao Lanshu was truly surprised.","Zhong Mei then handed the money to Qiao Lanshu to show her. \"He also gave me money, saying I should buy more things to nourish myself.\"","Zhong Mei added, puzzled, \"Why did he suddenly give me money?\"","Qiao Lanshu fell silent for a moment. Then she took the money, counted it carefully – seven ten-yuan notes in total, along with a one-jin candy voucher, half a jin of meat vouchers, and five jin of food vouchers.","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu said softly, \"Could he have given you all the Mid-Autumn Festival subsidies he just received?\"","A few days ago, Qin Yuanzheng had also brought home Qiao Lanshu's Mid-Autumn subsidies, which included food and candy vouchers.","But Qin Yuanzheng's subsidies were more generous – three jin of meat vouchers, plus non-staple food and fruit vouchers.","Of course, it was also possible that Guan Wenjun had only brought what he had on him.","But the fact that he willingly gave Zhong Mei so much already showed he was quite generous.","He was far better than that Lai Hongmao, who only blabbered without doing a thing.","Qiao Lanshu stuffed all the money and vouchers into Zhong Mei's coat pocket, smiling as she said, \"This is a good thing. It proves Director Guan is serious about dating you. Ah Mei, Director Guan is a decent person. You should make the most of this opportunity.\"","Zhong Mei certainly knew she had to seize the opportunity.","But just now, she had deliberately gone along with him, trying to cheer him up, without much sincerity behind her actions.","Now, looking at such an earnest Guan Wenjuan, Zhong Mei instead began to feel a pang of guilt.","On top of that, she had injured Guan Wenjuan earlier and never apologized for it. She felt she had done him wrong."]},{"number":216,"title":"Chapter 216: My partner really admires me","paragraphs":["Zhong Mei took Guan Wenjun's money, and though she felt a bit guilty, she had no intention of letting go of a wealthy catch like Guan Wenjun.","She set aside her conscience for now—her priority was to secure the man, get the marriage certificate, and resolve her household registration issue.","This man was so capable and held such a high status that she could whisper sweet nothings in his ear and coax him into sorting out her job as well.","By then, even if he grew to despise and detest her, she wouldn't care.","Life wasn't just about a household registration or a job?","Men were actually lower on the list.","Zhong Mei thought this way, and the rare flicker of conscience vanished again.","She had a goal and knew what she wanted—that was enough.","Besides, once they were married, she could give Guan Wenjun a son, and no matter how much he regretted it later, it wouldn't matter.","He wouldn't dare divorce her, would he?","These days, cadres couldn't easily get divorced; a divorce would tarnish their character and cast a shadow over their future.","With that thought, Zhong Mei tucked Guan Wenjun's money into her pocket and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Let's go to the supply and marketing cooperative. I want to buy some meat and liquor and treat Director Guan to a meal tomorrow.\"","Qiao Lanshu found it amusing and kept covering her mouth as she laughed.","Zhong Mei, embarrassed by her laughter, glared at her and said, \"Stop laughing, you're making me feel guilty.\"","Qiao Lanshu barely held back her laughter. She linked her arm with Zhong Mei's, and they walked while chatting in low voices.","She asked softly, \"Have you made up your mind? Are you really going to date Director Guan?\"","Zhong Mei nodded. \"Of course, he's already agreed.\"","Though she had charmed him into saying yes with a few sweet words, and once he calmed down and thought it over, he'd probably regret it.","But since he'd agreed, he couldn't back out now.","So she planned to strike while the iron was hot and go all out.","Qiao Lanshu added, \"Think it over carefully. Director Guan might look young, but he's 29, ten years older than you.\"","Even though Qiao Lanshu felt that her own older man was pretty great—older men knew how to be caring and how to tease.","But compared to Qin Yuanzheng, Guan Wenjun wasn't as outstanding.","Zhong Mei didn't mind at all. \"It's only ten years, not a big deal. He can give me what I want, and that's enough.\"","She paused and then said, \"Besides, if I found someone my age, they probably wouldn't even have a job. What could I expect from them?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded, agreeing with Zhong Mei. \"You're right, you've thought it through more thoroughly. I never considered any of that.\"","Back when she pursued Qin Yuanzheng, it was purely because of her past-life experience, not for any practical motives.","Zhong Mei had gone out into society early and experienced the ups and downs of human relationships; she knew how to choose to make a good life for herself.","Qiao Lanshu patted Zhong Mei's arm and encouraged her. \"Go for it! Get Director Guan locked in soon! A cadre his age who isn't married is really rare. It's probably because Director Guan was in the Revolutionary Committee that it was hard for him to find a match.\"","After all, in the past few years, the Revolutionary Committee might have been formidable, but it was also a place everyone feared.","People in the committee might not be dared to be provoked publicly, but behind their backs, countless people cursed them.","Now that Guan Wenjun had moved to the Supply Department, it was a proper good unit. After the reforms and opening up, he wouldn't be implicated.","With his work and life stable, it made sense that Guan Wenjun was looking for a partner.","Zhong Mei smiled and whispered, \"Don't worry. Tomorrow, I'll show him what I'm capable of!\"","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu felt a bit regretful. \"So you won't be coming to my place for dinner? Niwa was just talking about you the other day, saying he hadn't seen you in a while.\"","Zhong Mei thought of Niwa and laughed. \"That little rascal, as energetic as an ox, running around everywhere. Didn't you say you'd send him to kindergarten? Did you?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"I've already signed him up. He'll start after the Mid-Autumn Festival. Director Han is still out of town, and I don't know when he'll be back. Sigh, with a dad like that and no mother, I don't know when this kid will be taken back home.\"","Qiao Lanshu secretly wondered if she might end up raising this child permanently.","Wouldn't that be a huge win for her?","Getting a grown son for nothing, and with a bureau chief dad to boot—a solid backer.","...","Tomorrow is the Mid-Autumn Festival, so tonight, Qiao Lanshu brought Zhong Mei over for dinner.","Because Zhong Mei had her 'date' with Guan Wenjun tomorrow, she said she needed to prepare properly to make sure she'd reel in Director Guan.","So she couldn't come tomorrow.","Tonight was her only chance to gather.","Yang Wenyan and Deng Xiaozhen, the couple, also came over for dinner.","Deng Xiaozhen was nearly six months pregnant, with a prominent belly. In previous years, she always had Qin Yuanzheng over for the meal.","But this year, she didn't plan to host. Besides, for the Mid-Autumn Festival, she and her husband were going back to her parents' home with Deng Weijun and his wife to celebrate.","So they came a day early for the meal.","Since becoming pregnant, Deng Xiaozhen hadn't returned to her in-laws' place.","Yang Wenyan was wholly focused on the arrival of their child and was completely obedient to Deng Xiaozhen.","When his mother wrote to ask him to come home for the festival, he refused.","Shi Sao set up two tables in the courtyard, and together with Qiao Lanshu, Zhong Mei, and Deng Xiaozhen, they started making dumplings stuffed with cabbage and pork.","Qiao Lanshu saw Qin Yuanzheng picking vegetables in the yard. She walked over and whispered in his ear, \"Didn't I ask you to invite Director Guan for dinner? Did you?\"","Qin Yuanzheng plucked the greens, tossing them into a basket, and nodded. \"I already called him. He should be here soon.\"","Qin Yuanzheng glanced at Qiao Lanshu and asked in a low voice, \"What's up? Why did you suddenly think of inviting him to dinner?\"","Because Guan Wenjun used to stare at Qiao Lanshu, Qin Yuanzheng was always wary of him.","Whenever Qiao Lanshu mentioned Guan Wenjun, Qin Yuanzheng would subtly probe with extra questions, fearing that his young wife might change her mind and run off with another man.","Qiao Lanshu leaned close to Qin Yuanzheng and lowered her voice. \"Zheng Ge, let me tell you something, but you probably won't believe it.\"","Qiao Lanshu couldn't help but laugh. Qin Yuanzheng looked at her smiling face and almost reached out to pinch her cheek.","But his hands were dirty from picking vegetables, so he held back.","Qiao Lanshu leaned against him, wrapping her arms around his, and whispered in his ear, \"Director Guan—he's dating Zhong Mei!\"","Qin Yuanzheng was silent for a moment, truly taken aback.","He asked quietly, \"Really? They're already together?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded and told Qin Yuanzheng everything that had happened that afternoon.","After hearing it, Qin Yuanzheng smiled and said, \"Director Guan really should get married. He's getting on in years.\"","Guan Wenjun wasn't from Longcheng either; his parents lived elsewhere, and as a transferred cadre, the three of them were scattered across different places.","His family never worried about his marriage. His parents didn't even necessarily know where he was and what he was doing.","Guan Wenjun had been used to freedom since childhood. After breaking up with his first girlfriend, he never thought about getting married.","But perhaps due to his advancing age, he began to yearn for a wife and a son.","After all, even Qin Yuanzheng, who suffered from infertility, had a son. How could he not?","Qin Yuanzheng could probably guess some of Guan Wenjun's thoughts.","He glanced at Zhong Mei. Zhong Mei was making dumplings with Sister Shi and the others. Niu Wa was running around in the yard, and An An was sitting on a chair between Sister Shi and Zhong Mei, kneading a piece of dumpling wrapper for fun.","Qin Yuanzheng lowered his voice and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Your friend is quite capable. Director Guan is no match for her.\"","Qiao Lanshu just smiled and said,","\"That's exactly what it should be. Zhong Mei is already in a disadvantaged position. If she can't keep him in check, then it's better not to continue the relationship. Director Guan is generally a good person, but sometimes he can be a bit muddle - headed. It's the best that Zhong Mei can keep him in line.\"","Qin Yuanzheng didn't comment.","He squatted on the ground, holding a basket in one hand and gently putting his arm around Qiao Lanshu's waist with the other. He whispered, \"What about me? What do you think of me?\"","Qiao Lanshu gave him a reproachful look and said, \"Of course, you're the best.\"","Qin Yuanzheng whispered again, \"Can you keep me in check?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu suspected that Qin Yuanzheng was being a hooligan. She glared at him and turned to leave.","Qin Yuanzheng quickly chased after her and said with a smile in her ear, \"You can keep me in check. I just like being under your control.\"","Qiao Lanshu was so annoyed that she reached out and hit him. \"Get out of here. You're so annoying.\"","There were so many people in the yard, and he was saying such things.","Qiao Lanshu was really afraid of being heard. How embarrassing that would be!","Qiao Lanshu turned around and hurriedly ran to where Sister Shi and the others were.","Qin Yuanzheng watched her back and happily carried the vegetable basket into the kitchen.","Qiao Lanshu came back to help make dumplings. Deng Xiaozhen joked with her, \"Oh, you're the only one who dares to hit Brigade Commander Qin, Xiao Qiao.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was top - notch in martial arts in the army, and considering his rank, there were probably few people who could hit him.","Hearing Deng Xiaozhen's words, Qiao Lanshu blushed shyly. She didn't know what to say and just said, \"Oh, cousin - in - law, stop teasing me. You've hit the factory director plenty of times too.\"","While the women were chatting and laughing, Guan Wenjun finally arrived.","...","Since he had a heart - to - heart talk with Zhong Mei at noon.","Guan Wenjun had been thinking about dating Zhong Mei all the time.","It was like a dream. He walked with his head held high and looked extremely pleased with himself at the unit.","After all, he was no longer a bachelor. He also had a girlfriend.","Before long, he would be able to live a happy life with a wife and children.","He no longer had to envy Qin Yuanzheng.","When a passing colleague saw him, he politely said, \"Oh, Section Chief Guan, why are you so happy? Is there any good news?\"","Guan Wenjun immediately stopped and said proudly, \"What? Even you know I have a girlfriend? The news spreads really fast.\"","Colleague: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun stood there, smoothed his hair with his hand, put one hand in his pocket, frowned, and said,","\"Well, it's okay. Her conditions are average, but she's a nice girl. The most important thing is that she admires me very much. She's very sincere when we get along. I thought, well, I might as well give her a chance. After all, it's normal for her to admire a man as good as me.\"","Colleague: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun said with a smile, \"By the way, do you have a girlfriend?\"","Colleague: \"...\"","The colleague shook his head. \"No...\"","Guan Wenjun clicked his tongue and said to him, \"No girlfriend? Forget it. I can't explain it to you.\"","With that, Guan Wenjun turned around and left.","He left the colleague standing there, looking utterly confused and thinking that this new Section Chief Guan was a bit crazy.","However, thanks to him, the news that Guan Wenjun had a girlfriend spread throughout the Supply Section in just one afternoon.","Even the Revolutionary Committee, his old unit, heard about it.","Many people were quite disappointed that the older single man Guan Wenjun had a girlfriend.","Some people came to quietly inquire if the news was true.","After Guan Wenjun was transferred to the Supply Section as the section chief, he suddenly became very popular.","Many people who had no grudges against him were inquiring about his marriage, hoping to marry their daughters to him.","It was just that Zhong Mei took the initiative. She made her move not long after Guan Wenjun was transferred to the Supply Section.","Otherwise, if it was delayed for a few more months, the people who came to propose marriage to Guan Wenjun would probably have crowded the Supply Section's office.","By then, Guan Wenjun would probably have been grinning from ear to ear.","...","Guan Wenjun came to Qin Yuanzheng's house for dinner, of course, not empty - handed.","He bought a pound of fruit candies, a pound of biscuits, two bottles of canned yellow peaches, and a bag of apples.","When he came, he guessed that Zhong Mei would probably be there too.","So, he went back to his dormitory to take a shower, change his clothes, and even greased his hair to make it shiny. He looked quite flashy.","Fortunately, he had fair skin and was tall and handsome. He could carry off any flashy look.","As soon as he entered the door, he saw the women sitting around the table on the steps, making dumplings.","He scanned the area with his eyes and saw Zhong Mei sitting there.","Zhong Mei was still wearing the same clothes as in the daytime and looked no different from the daytime.","Guan Wenjun felt a bit regretful. He regretted going home to change his clothes and dress up!","It made him look so eager!","However, his regret didn't last long because Zhong Mei also saw him.","Then, Zhong Mei, who had been expressionless, immediately broke into a surprised smile.","Under the dim light, her eyes seemed to be shining, and her smile was so sweet.","She put down the dumpling in her hand and took a few steps towards him in surprise. Then, as if she had realized something inappropriate, she stopped in her tracks and didn't dare to walk towards him anymore.","She stood in the yard, smiling shyly at him, and said softly, \"Director Guan, you're here. Was work tiring today? You've worked so hard. Come and sit down and have a rest.\"","With that, she came over to take the things from Guan Wenjun's hands and whispered in a voice that only the two of them could hear, \"I made dumplings for you...\"","As she said that, she looked up at Guan Wenjun, gave him a coy smile, and then carried the things and quickly walked into the house.","Guan Wenjun was left standing there with a red face and ears, sweating all over with a hot feeling.","He thought to himself, look, how much she liked him!","She even made dumplings for him specially!"]},{"number":217,"title":"Chapter 217: How did you know I want a child","paragraphs":["Guan Wenjun watched as Zhong Mei entered the room. He stood there for a moment, dazed, and then followed her inside.","But his gaze still couldn’t help drifting toward her from time to time.","These subtle glances between the two did not escape the notice of Sister Shi and Deng Xiaozhen, who took it all in.","Sister Shi’s face showed no surprise, as if she had long expected this. She said in a low voice, “Looks like we’ll be toasting at their wedding before long. Did you see Director Guan’s expression just now? He’s completely smitten with Zhong Mei.”","Deng Xiaozhen was equally stunned. She stared at Guan Wenjun’s back and whispered, “Wait—when did Comrade Zhong Mei and Director Guan start seeing each other? Those two... those two...”","She paused for quite a while, unable to continue.","The shock was too great for her.","She had heard about Zhong Mei’s background, but she never imagined Zhong Mei would end up with Guan Wenjun.","She had originally thought a man like Guan Wenjun would have very high standards, be extremely picky.","Probably not even look twice at a girl from an ordinary family.","And yet...","Deng Xiaozhen shook her head with a sigh and said, “This really is ‘fate brings people together across a thousand miles.’ Destiny, pure destiny—just like Xiao Qiao and Yuanzheng.”","Qin Yuanzheng had been single for nearly thirty years, never marrying, until he married Qiao Lanshu, a woman from the south.","And now Guan Wenjun, after all these years as a bachelor, had also found himself a southern girl.","Among all the people in Dragon City, these two might be the only girls from Guangzhou, and both had found older men.","The thought struck Deng Xiaozhen as rather amusing.","Qiao Lanshu took a towel and wiped the drool from An’an’s chin. She listened to their chatter, a smile on her face, but she didn’t say a word about Zhong Mei and Guan Wenjun.","Sister Shi continued, “It seems Zhong Mei is fortunate. If she marries Director Guan, she won’t have to worry about the rest of her life.”","That would certainly be better than marrying one of those young men who, despite having urban household registrations, had no jobs.","As she spoke, Sister Shi felt a hint of envy.","Her own marriage had been far from ideal—otherwise, she wouldn’t have had to work as a nanny all these years.","Her daughter was already fourteen or fifteen, almost old enough to start looking for a match.","Sister Shi had long been hoping to find a good son-in-law for her daughter—at least someone with a steady job, so her daughter would have a secure future.","But a good son-in-law was hard to come by these days.","Thinking about this, Sister Shi shook her head again and let out a sigh.","Just then, the dumplings were ready. Sister Shi picked up the tray and said, “I’ll go to the kitchen and cook these.”","Qiao Lanshu nodded: “Alright, I’ll clean up here.”","With that, she turned to Deng Xiaozhen and said, “Cousin-in-law, could you keep an eye on An’an? I’ll tidy up the table.”","There were too many people eating dinner tonight, and the house couldn’t hold them all.","So they had to move the meal outside to the courtyard.","They pushed two tables together—there would be enough room soon.","Deng Xiaozhen nodded and sat down with An’an to rest.","An’an couldn’t walk yet; he could only sit or crawl.","Now that he was placed in a chair with a backrest, he could only sit and play. Without an adult picking him up, he couldn’t get down.","But An’an was a restless child by nature, full of energy and never willing to sleep.","His hands and feet were constantly moving; even when sitting on a chair, his hands kept playing with toys, and his little short legs kicked here and bumped there without a moment’s rest.","His big, dark, shiny eyes stared unblinkingly at Niuwa, who was running around the yard with the chickens and dogs.","Every now and then, he babbled a few sounds, his face full of longing to join Niuwa.","Niuwa came over carrying the puppy, stopped in front of An’an, and said to the dog, “Come on, get familiar with my little brother’s scent. From now on, he’s your owner too, got it?”","The puppy, only a few months old, sniffed around An’an, wagging its tail quickly.","Afraid that the dog might pounce on An’an, Deng Xiaozhen picked him up and sat him on her lap. She asked An’an, “Do you like puppies, An’an?”","As she spoke, she pointed at the dog: “Pup-py. Do you like it?”","An’an imitated her tone and said something like “puppy,” but his speech was unclear, so it came out as “eee-ya.”","Niuwa tucked the puppy under his arm, leaned in with a smile, and said, “Oh wow, An’an, you’re talking!”","Deng Xiaozhen looked at Niuwa and asked with a smile, “Niuwa, do you miss your daddy?”","Niuwa answered casually, “Daddy? Isn’t my daddy right here?”","With that, he reached out and pointed at Qin Yuanzheng, who was squatting in the yard washing vegetables, and called out, “Daddy.”","Deng Xiaozhen: “...”","Qin Yuanzheng had grown numb to this lately.","At first, when Niuwa called him “Daddy,” he didn’t want to bother with the boy.","But Qiao Lanshu told him that the child was still young, had no mother, and his father was too busy working to look after him. So Qin Yuanzheng shouldn’t be so harsh with the kid; it wouldn’t hurt to be his honorary dad.","Since Qin Yuanzheng always listened to Qiao Lanshu, he stopped objecting and silently accepted Niuwa as his honorary son.","Han Wenlin was probably on his way back soon; his housing application had been approved, and then they could send Niuwa home.","Looking at Niuwa, Qin Yuanzheng had to admit—after raising him for so long, he’d grown fond of the boy.","He said, “Niuwa.”","Niuwa immediately stood up straight: “Yes, sir!”","Qin Yuanzheng: “Come over and help wash the vegetables.”","Niuwa instantly replied, “Roger that!”","Then Niuwa put the puppy down on the ground, ran over to Qin Yuanzheng, and started washing vegetables alongside him.","Lately, Niuwa had been following Sister Shi, helping her with chores every day and learning quite a bit.","He could weed the vegetable patch, pick and wash vegetables, wash dishes and cups—though sometimes he didn’t clean them thoroughly, so Sister Shi had to check and rinse them again behind his back.","Niuwa, however, thought he was doing a great job, so he worked with boundless enthusiasm every day.","With Sister Shi’s praise, he got completely hooked on doing housework.","While washing vegetables, Niuwa said to Qin Yuanzheng, “Daddy, once my little brother learns to walk, I’ll bring him along to wash vegetables too. I bet he’ll do a great job as well.”","The four-year-old boy sounded pretty mature for his age.","Qin Yuanzheng found it amusing and said, “Alright, if you can teach your little brother to do chores, I’ll definitely reward you.”","Right now, Niuwa’s biggest idol was Qin Yuanzheng. It couldn’t be helped—Qin Yuanzheng always wore a sharp military uniform, looking incredibly handsome.","His presence was also commanding.","Seeing Qin Yuanzheng like this every day, how could Niuwa not worship him?","Qin Yuanzheng said he would reward him, which made him even more excited. He shouted loudly, 'Don't worry, Chief, I will definitely teach my little brother well.'","Qin Yuanzheng chuckled and gave his round head a pat.","He found himself liking this kid, Niuwa, more and more.","Deng Xiaozhen watched this scene, then touched her own belly, thinking to herself, if only she could have a son too.","Looking at Qiao Lanshu, who was tidying the table nearby, she asked, 'Xiao Qiao, what's the situation with this Niuwa now? Is he really staying at your place and not leaving?'","Qiao Lanshu, holding a rag, wiped the table clean and then moved to wipe the stools. Hearing Deng Xiaozhen's question, she said, 'Director Han went on a mission, and no one knows when he'll be back, so he's temporarily left Niuwa here.'","Then Qiao Lanshu sighed, 'Niuwa is a kid who's particular about people. If you put him in someone else's home, he'll run off. But now that he's used to living here, he doesn't run around anymore. He's well-behaved, and that's just fine.'","Deng Xiaozhen roughly knew Niuwa's situation.","While bouncing An An and playing with him, she said, 'It shouldn't be long. At most a few months, and Director Han will definitely be back.'","Qiao Lanshu thought the same and nodded.","After a while, Deng Xiaozhen smiled and said, 'Actually, taking him as a godson isn't bad. After all, he's the son of the Public Security Bureau chief. Later, he can play with An An—it's a good thing.'","If it were Deng Xiaozhen, she would definitely be willing to take him as a godson.","Too bad she didn't have that luck.","Qiao Lanshu hadn't really thought about taking Niuwa as a godson.","But if it came to it, it wouldn't be a big deal. She didn't see it as an issue, so she dropped the topic.","...","Meanwhile, Guan Wenjun, who had followed Zhong Mei into the house, came out again.","There were too many women in the kitchen, so he felt awkward going in. After thinking it over, he turned back.","Seeing Qin Yuanzheng and Niuwa talking, he immediately went over and said to Niuwa, 'Niuwa, do you still remember Uncle?'","Niuwa was squatting there washing vegetables. Hearing this, he looked up at Guan Wenjun and nodded, 'I remember. You're Uncle Guan Wenjun.'","Guan Wenjun smiled and quickly said, 'Since you remember me, then come on, call me \"Dad\" for a listen?'","Niuwa: '...'","Niuwa gave him a glance with a hint of disdain.","He shook his head seriously and said, 'No way. I already have a dad.'","Then Niuwa scooted closer to Qin Yuanzheng.","Guan Wenjun, a bit unwilling to give up, said, 'You already call him \"Dad,\" so isn't it okay to call me \"Dad\" once? You have plenty of dads anyway—what's one more?'","Then he pulled out two White Rabbit candies from his pocket, held them out, and tempted Niuwa, 'Come on, call me \"Dad\" once, and I'll give you these candies.'","Niuwa stared at the two candies and swallowed his saliva.","Without hesitating long, Niuwa reached out and took the candies from his hand.","Guan Wenjun glared at Niuwa: 'Call me \"Dad\"! Call me!'","Niuwa peeled one candy and put it in his mouth, then looked at Guan Wenjun as if helpless, after which he stared at Qin Yuanzheng and yelled loudly, 'Dad!'","Qin Yuanzheng: '...'","Guan Wenjun: '...'","Qin Yuanzheng felt his ears ringing. This kid Niuwa really had a loud voice.","Guan Wenjun felt something was off. He pointed at the boy and asked, \"You little brat, who are you calling?\"","The boy said matter-of-factly, \"I'm calling my dad. Isn't that what you told me to do?\"","Guan Wenjun stood up abruptly and made a move to grab him. \"You little rascal, are you messing with me?\"","The boy jumped up and ran straight toward Qiao Lanshu.","Guan Wenjun was fuming inside. He then pointed at Qin Yuanzheng and said, \"Look, look—a perfectly good kid, and you've already ruined him! I think this boy might as well take me as his dad; at least I wouldn't teach him wrong.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless. He said to Guan Wenjun, \"Chief Guan, what's going on with you lately? Going around trying to claim sons everywhere? If you're so eager to be a father, go have one of your own.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","In the past, hearing this would have set Guan Wenjun off, and he'd have argued with Qin Yuanzheng for a while.","But now, instead of getting angry, he looked a little embarrassed. \"What are you talking about? How did you know I'm planning to have a child?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng was left speechless. He gave Guan Wenjun a look and said, \"You're not even married yet—you don't even have a spouse—and you're already talking about having a child? How? Planning to take those kids from the orphanage home as god sons?\"","Guan Wenjun snorted and looked at Qin Yuanzheng smugly. \"What do you know? Let me tell you, I already have a partner now, got it?\"","He wasn't the same man he used to be!","Qin Yuanzheng thought Guan Wenjun's smug expression deserved a punch.","So what if he had a partner?","Did he have to flaunt it everywhere?","...","...","Guan Wenjun might be young and accomplished, but he was easy to coax and quick to act on impulse.","This time, when he started dating Zhong Mei, apart from actually having some interest in her, it was largely because Zhong Mei had managed to flatter him, and he agreed to the relationship on a whim. If he had followed his own judgment, he probably would have taken a few more months to think it over.","Earlier, when there was a spark between Zhong Mei and Lai Hongmao, although it made him a bit uneasy, he wasn't in a hurry.","After all, he always felt he wouldn't lack options when it came to partners, and Zhong Mei's circumstances were indeed a bit lacking.","But now that he had agreed to date Zhong Mei, his mind was fully on her, and he didn't consider other women anymore.","He was actually quite looking forward to married life.","After all, he had been eating at the cafeteria, dining out, or mooching off colleagues for years, and that wasn't ideal anymore.","He felt he needed a woman to cook for him and keep his home—that was what real life should be.","Zhong Mei and Sister Shi were in the kitchen, boiling dumplings and cooking dishes.","From time to time, Zhong Mei would peek through the window to watch Guan Wenjun standing in the yard, eavesdropping on his conversation with Qin Yuanzheng.","Sister Shi poured cold water into the pot and asked Zhong Mei, \"Amei, are you really dating Director Guan?\"","Zhong Mei came back from the window, threw some firewood into the stove, and nodded with a smile. \"Yes, but it's just started. Who knows how it'll turn out?\"","Sister Shi had lived through hard times herself, and she actually admired Zhong Mei.","She had once thought about introducing Zhong Mei to her own son, but after seeing how strong-willed, independent, and opinionated Zhong Mei was—likely not someone who would settle for her son—she dropped the idea.","She said to Zhong Mei, \"Although there's quite a gap in your social status, you two actually match well in personality.\"","Sister Shi lowered her voice and said, \"With Director Guan, you have to flatter him, pamper him. Once you make him happy, he'll give you anything.\"","Sister Shi then added in a hushed tone, \"I'll say something a bit harsh... These young officials really care about face. Since you're already dating him, why not find a chance to make things official? You know, seal the deal. With someone like Director Guan, he'd definitely agree to get the marriage certificate right away.\""]},{"number":218,"title":"Chapter 218: Can Have Three","paragraphs":["The reason Auntie Shi said this was entirely out of concern for Zhong Mei.","She was afraid that Guan Wenjun might have high standards, only being interested in Zhong Mei's looks, just casually dating her without any intention of marrying her.","Having worked as a nanny for so many years, Auntie Shi had seen plenty of such situations.","Some girls who came from the countryside to the city to stay with relatives, or some young maids, were easily tricked by city men and ended up being taken advantage of.","They assumed the men would take responsibility for them, but in reality, the men looked down on them, finding them lacking in education, worldliness, and family background, all because they came from rural areas.","They worried that marrying such women would bring ridicule and lower their own status.","Thus, after having their fun, they would simply send those young women back to the countryside.","The gap between Zhong Mei and Guan Wenjun was immense—no different from that between a cadre and a nanny.","If Guan Wenjun and Zhong Mei got together later, even if he refused to take responsibility, what could Zhong Mei do about it?","Wasn't it just like that former Supply Section Chief, the one named Zheng or something, who was with Liu Weihong for over two years, only to abandon her when trouble came, claiming she was just his nanny?","And even if Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng could help, it would be useless. Could they tie Guan Wenjun down and force him to get married?","After all, he was still a Section Chief!","Zhong Mei listened to Auntie Shi’s words and felt a shock inside.","Not because Auntie Shi was teaching her such low-class tricks, but because she was shocked to realize that Auntie Shi’s thoughts were exactly the same as her own.","She had originally planned that tomorrow, for the Mid-Autumn Festival, she would have dinner with Guan Wenjun in her rented room, coax him into being happy, and then seduce him into bed.","Guan Wenjun had just taken up his post in the Supply Section—it was a hard-earned position, and as a Section Chief, his rank was not low.","Once she got him into bed, she was sure he wouldn't dare to shirk responsibility!","Zhong Mei’s goal was marriage and a household registration; she only wanted to use Guan Wenjun, without giving much thought to what might happen later.","She stared at the flames in the stove, remained silent for a long while, and then said, “Auntie Shi, you’re right. I’ll think it over.”","Auntie Shi watched the water in the pot boil, but the dumplings weren’t done yet, so she ladled in another bowl of cold water.","Then she said to Zhong Mei, “But this plan has its drawbacks too.”","She paused before continuing, “I’m afraid that after you get married, he might settle scores, accusing you of being frivolous, of lacking self-respect, of seducing him into bed before you were wed...","Anyway, men are all the same like dogs. It clearly takes two hands to clap, yet they can’t control their own impulses. They still blame women, saying the women led them on, called them wanton and unfaithful... You need to think carefully. I suspect that Director Guan’s temperament is exactly the type to hold a grudge later.”","Guan Wenjun was easy to fool—easily led around by the women he liked, making him lose his head.","But once he calmed down and reflected on things, he would regret his rashness.","Before, Qiao Lanshu had coaxed him into funding an orphanage and supporting five children.","Later, Qiao Lanshu had sweet-talked him into taking her along on a work trip to a countryside forest farm.","After each instance, he regretted it, but there was no cure for regret, and the next time he saw Qiao Lanshu, he’d fall for the same tricks again.","Now, he had taken a liking to Zhong Mei, finding her beautiful and to his taste, so when Zhong Mei sweet-talked him, he got dizzy-headed again.","But after they got married and he sobered up, he might start a fight with Zhong Mei.","Listening to Auntie Shi say all this more and more impressed Zhong Mei with her wisdom.","No wonder people said that having an elder in the family is like having a treasure.","If she had had a mother like this to guide her growing up, her life might not have turned out this way.","Auntie Shi was quite talkative, and she spoke without a filter. Only at this point did she realize that Zhong Mei was still an unmarried young woman, and she shouldn’t be saying such things.","She let out an awkward laugh, quickly changing the subject, saying, “Oh dear, the dumplings are done. Let me scoop them out. Everyone must be hungry—let’s get ready to eat.”","Upon hearing this, Zhong Mei quickly got up, grabbed a basin, and went to help.","The dumplings were divided into two basins. Zhong Mei carried one basin out first and set it on the table by the courtyard.","Guan Wenjun, who had been playing with Niuwa in the yard, spotted Zhong Mei and hurried over. Glancing at the steaming dumplings, he whispered to Zhong Mei, “Did you make these dumplings?”","Zhong Mei looked at him, seeming a bit shy as she lowered her head. “Auntie Shi made the filling; I only helped wrap some.”","Guan Wenjun looked at her, feeling as if she were shy about it.","And indeed, being in a relationship was different from not being in one.","Before they started dating, Zhong Mei would run away as soon as she saw him, like a mouse seeing a cat.","He couldn’t even steal a few glances at her.","Now that they were together, Zhong Mei blushed and acted shy every time she looked at him.","Guan Wenjun felt a warm glow inside. He leaned in closer, lowering his voice to say to Zhong Mei, “You’re shameless, saying you made dumplings for me. They’re clearly made by all of you. In this whole big basin, which ones did you make for me?”","Zhong Mei’s cheeks turned slightly red, and she looked a bit embarrassed.","She raised her head, glanced around, and then said to Guan Wenjun, “Tomorrow is Mid-Autumn Festival. Come to my place, and I’ll make them for you alone.”","With that, she gave him a meaningful look and quickly walked away.","Guan Wenjun: “...”","Watching Zhong Mei’s shy retreating figure, Guan Wenjun stood with his arms crossed, savoring the thought. She had invited him over, and promising to make dumplings just for him tomorrow—wasn’t that an invitation for a date?","Guan Wenjun was overjoyed, his lips spreading into a grin he couldn’t close.","Once all the food was ready, everyone gathered around the table to eat.","They intentionally left the seat next to Guan Wenjun empty, letting Zhong Mei sit beside him.","Zhong Mei seemed very shy, eating with her head down and saying little.","However, she deliberately moved her leg, using her knee to brush against Guan Wenjun’s.","Guan Wenjun was in the middle of talking to Qin Yuanzheng when he sensed something unusual. His expression froze, he had a dumpling dangling from his mouth, but he instinctively turned to look at Zhong Mei.","Zhong Mei acted as if nothing was amiss, just eating quietly with her head down, occasionally chatting with Qiao Lanshu beside her.","Guan Wenjun: “...”","He felt both nervous and oddly thrilled.","His whole body involuntarily tensed up. He lost interest in what anyone else was saying, his attention completely fixed on his leg.","But Zhong Mei seemed to have been unintentional—her knee pressed against his leg for just a few seconds, then pulled back as she reached for food.","Guan Wenjun subtly brought his hand down to rub the spot on his leg that Zhong Mei’s knee had just touched.","It felt completely numb.","Just as he was starting to relax, it wasn’t long before Zhong Mei’s leg leaned against him again.","Guan Wenjun: “!!!”","With a large group of people, they ate, chatted, and admired the moon together, the meal stretching on for over an hour.","During this, Zhong Mei’s leg occasionally brushed against Guan Wenjun, stirring up his thoughts and leaving him restless and distracted.","But it only happened three times. After the third time, Zhong Mei seemed to finally notice something was off, so she gave him an apologetic glance and quietly moved her leg back.","Guan Wenjun’s heart was in turmoil.","Wait, what did Zhong Mei mean by this?","They were already dating, so wasn’t it normal for their legs to touch while eating?","Why was she moving so far away?","Did she not want him to touch her?","His mind began to race, worrying about what he would do if Zhong Mei didn’t want physical contact.","Of course, kissing and hugging were essential in a relationship. If she wouldn’t let him kiss or hold her, what kind of relationship was that?","Tomorrow, when he was alone with her, he would have to ask what she was thinking.","He was nearly thirty years old—Qin Yuanzheng already had a child, while he was still inexperienced. They were all adults. Wasn’t dating about eventually getting married and having kids? If Zhong Mei wouldn’t let him touch her, he might as well break up!","Just those few times Zhong Mei had brushed her leg against him had thrown Guan Wenjun into a chaotic state. He sat there with a stern face, eating his dumplings and occasionally glancing at her, his eyes full of complicated emotions.","Zhong Mei knew roughly what he was thinking.","But it didn’t matter. His thoughts weren’t important.","She pretended to be shy, deliberately avoiding his gaze and not meeting his eyes, so she wouldn’t have to explain or talk to him.","Instead, she only chatted with Qiao Lanshu beside her.","She helped Qiao Lanshu take care of An’an.","Niuwa sat next to Auntie Shi, under her supervision.","Qiao Lanshu held An’an while Zhong Mei assisted with looking after him.","Zhong Mei asked Qiao Lanshu, “Is An’an six or seven months old now? Can he start eating solid food?”","At the moment, An’an was still being fed goat’s milk and formula. Qiao Lanshu had little breast milk, so she had stopped breastfeeding when An’an was half a year old.","Qiao Lanshu brought over a small bowl of rice paste and said, “Auntie Shi ground some stir-fried rice into powder and then poured boiling water over it. This is safe for An’an to eat.”","An’an was now over seven months old and could start eating solid food.","Sometimes Auntie Shi would cook some rice porridge for him, and other times she’d make this rice powder paste.","An’an currently ate two solid meals, two servings of goat’s milk, and two servings of formula each day.","He ate six times in total, which kept him nice and plump. As he grew, he began to look more and more like Qiao Lanshu—fair-skinned, clean, and exceptionally cute.","Qiao Lanshu held An’an, while Zhong Mei held the small bowl of rice paste and fed him with a tiny spoon. Her voice was gentle, and her movements were delicate.","Guan Wenjun kept stealing glances from the side, thinking to himself: It seems Zhong Mei really likes kids and is good at taking care of them. Once they got married, they could have three.","Guan Wenjun enjoyed his meal immensely.","After eating, the seven adults and two children sat in the courtyard, looking at the moon, drinking tea, and snacking on pastries.","Qiao Lanshu brought out some pre-Qingming tea sent from Guangzhou and brewed it for Yang Wenyi and his wife, as well as for Zhong Mei and Guan Wenjun.","After tidying up, Auntie Shi noticed that An’an was getting sleepy, so she said, “I’ll take the two children to bed first. Xiao Qiao, you all can keep drinking tea.”","Qiao Lanshu nodded. “Alright. Thank you, Auntie Shi.”","Auntie Shi smiled and said, “I can’t really keep up with you young folks’ conversations anyway. Might as well take the kids to sleep.”","With that, she led the children back to the room.","Guan Wenjun glanced at Zhong Mei, who was sitting quietly drinking tea, then suddenly turned to Qin Yuanzheng, who was sitting beside him. “How long have you had Auntie Shi? An’an is almost a year old now. Is she going to leave soon?”","Qin Yuanzheng shot him a look and asked, “Why do you ask?”","Guan Wenjun took another peek at Zhong Mei and noticed she happened to be stealing a glance at him too.","Finally, after an entire evening, Zhong Mei was looking at him.","Guan Wenjun immediately straightened his back, cleared his throat, and said to Qin Yuanzheng, “I’m just asking casually. If I ever get married and have kids, you know, I’d need to hire a nanny myself.”","Qin Yuanzheng was truly exasperated.","He was about to say something when Deng Xiaozhen chimed in faster.","She laughed and said, “Director Guan, then you’ll be disappointed. Even if Auntie Shi leaves this house, it’d be my turn first. Look at me—I’m about to give birth. No matter how eager you are, you can’t be more eager than me, right?”","Yang Wenyi also added, “Ah, we’d like to hire Auntie Shi too, but Yuanzheng and Xiao Qiao won’t let her go. Director Guan, it looks like we’ll have to look elsewhere.”","They all needed nannies, since both husband and wife worked, and their parents weren’t available to help.","But finding a good nanny wasn’t easy. Yang Wenyi had been asking around for two months already.","Guan Wenjun felt a bit awkward. He wasn’t even married yet, yet here he was worrying about hiring a nanny, just like a pregnant woman.","He cleared his throat again, somewhat embarrassed, and said, “I was just asking casually. It’s not like I actually need one.”","Throughout the evening, Qiao Lanshu noticed that Guan Wenjun’s gaze was practically glued to Zhong Mei.","She knew then that Zhong Mei had him completely under control.","She felt happy for Zhong Mei.","When everyone was leaving, Qiao Lanshu said to Guan Wenjun, “Director Guan, would you mind taking A-Mei home? It’s getting late, and it’s dangerous for a girl to walk alone in the dark. Since you have a car, it would be a big help if you could drive her home. Thank you.”","Guan Wenjun had been thinking the same thing, but he still looked at Zhong Mei, wanting her to ask him herself.","Zhong Mei understood perfectly well.","She spoke softly, “It’s really dark outside, and I’m scared alone. Could... could you trouble yourself to take me home?”","Guan Wenjun was pleased. He nodded with satisfaction and said, “Alright, I’ll take you home.”","With that, he put his hands in his pockets and walked out the door first.","Zhong Mei waved goodbye to Qiao Lanshu and followed him outside.","Once out the door, Guan Wenjun deliberately waited for her to catch up. When she did, he said, “Let’s go. My car is parked over there.”","Then he paused, adding in a meaningful tone, “Speaking of which, didn’t that Lai Hongmao ride you home on his bicycle before?”","Zhong Mei hadn’t actually ridden with Lai Hongmao.","But since Guan Wenjun brought it up, she just nodded silently.","Sure enough, Guan Wenjun snorted and said, “It’s mid-autumn now. It’s so cold at night. What’s the point of riding a bicycle? From now on, you ride in my car. I’ll drive you.”","In the dark, Zhong Mei covered her mouth and secretly smiled.","She found Guan Wenjun quite amusing.","Still, she really did prefer riding in a car."]},{"number":219,"title":"Chapter 219: Guan Wenjun, You Money-Losing Wretch","paragraphs":["After everyone had left, the yard grew quiet.","Qiao Lanshu cleaned up the teapot, teacups, and plates of snacks, while Qin Yuanzheng moved the tables and chairs back into the house.","Auntie Shi had already taken the two children to bed.","Now, only Qiao Lanshu and her husband Qin Yuanzheng remained in the yard.","Qiao Lanshu washed the teacups, dried them, and wiped her hands with a towel, saying to Qin Yuanzheng, “I think Guan Wenjun and Zhong Mei are getting along well. Maybe they’ll get married soon.”","Qin Yuanzheng couldn’t care less about others. He walked over, wrapped his arms around his petite wife, leaned down, and kissed her cheek. In a low voice, he asked, “Did you take a bath today?”","Qiao Lanshu smiled at him. “Yes, I did.”","Qin Yuanzheng immediately scooped her up and headed inside. “Then let’s go to bed.”","Qiao Lanshu whispered, “You’ve been at it so many times lately. Aren’t you exhausted? Can’t you hold back a little?”","Qin Yuanzheng murmured back, “I’ll hold back. Just twice tonight.”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","Even though Qiao Lanshu was young and could endure the activity, Qin Yuanzheng had an endless amount of energy.","Sometimes, she was genuinely a bit afraid of him.","After all, the older man was not only brimming with vigor but also took his time, lasting a long time each round.","He even had some peculiar cravings, like kissing and nibbling all over...","Qiao Lanshu often found herself drifting off to sleep halfway through.","Lately, though, Qin Yuanzheng had stopped using protection during their marital intimacy.","After not using it a few times, he had completely let loose. Qiao Lanshu wondered silently, with how frequent things had been lately, whether she might end up pregnant with a second child.","Qiao Lanshu was laid on the bed by Qin Yuanzheng, and then he pressed down on her.","Qin Yuanzheng was large and heavy, and Qiao Lanshu couldn’t push him off. She said softly, “Zheng-ge, how long has it been since last time? Do you think I might be pregnant with our second child already?”","Qin Yuanzheng: “...”","He muttered, “That can’t be, can it? Is it that soon?”","He hadn’t had his fill yet, not even close.","If it happened that fast, wouldn’t he have to go without again?","Qin Yuanzheng looked seriously at Qiao Lanshu’s belly, then rubbed his rough palm over it, saying with a straight face, “I’ve checked. You’re not pregnant.”","With that, he leaned back down to kiss Qiao Lanshu’s face.","He thought his little wife smelled sweet and felt soft, and her scent made his whole body ache with desire.","He peppered messy kisses all over Qiao Lanshu’s face and neck.","Qiao Lanshu felt like Qin Yuanzheng was like some kind of big dog, sticking to her relentlessly, and she couldn’t push him away.","She let out a couple of soft whines, reached up to push his face aside, and looked at him with watery eyes. “What kind of check was that? You...”","Qin Yuanzheng didn’t stop. “It shouldn’t be that fast. Don’t worry.”","And with that, he sped up, as if afraid he’d miss out tonight.","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","Qiao Lanshu was utterly helpless.","It seemed that the older man had been restrained for too long before, so now he was making up for lost time.","Qiao Lanshu was also worried about getting pregnant again, so these days she went along with Qin Yuanzheng’s antics.","Even if it meant several rounds a night, she didn’t complain.","Thinking that once she did conceive again, the older man would have to go without, she softened. She hugged Qin Yuanzheng and said, “Alright, just be gentle...”","Qin Yuanzheng rasped, \"You know me, I can't be gentle.\"","He was actually always holding back his strength.","But his young wife was too delicate, always whimpering and whining, either telling him to slow down or to ease up, and he felt he wasn't using any force at all.","No help for it—his wife was fragile, so what else could he do?","Qin Yuanzheng was big and muscular, almost twice the size of Qiao Lanshu.","He even teased Qiao Lanshu, saying, \"Look at your thighs—they're not even as thick as my arms.\"","As he spoke, his rough, massive palm gripped Qiao Lanshu's waist, pressing slightly as he murmured, \"Your waist isn't as thick as my arm either.\"","Before, Qiao Lanshu's waist had indeed been thinner than his arm—slim, with little flesh, just a slender curve.","But after giving birth, she had filled out a bit, her belly gaining some soft, plump flesh.","Still, because Qiao Lanshu had been mindful about doing postnatal exercises, her waist remained slender, though it had become more curvaceous.","During her breastfeeding period, not only had her chest become fuller, but the rest of her body had turned softer too.","Qin Yuanzheng absolutely loved it.","Qiao Lanshu seemed to have ripened from an unripe fruit into a fully matured cherry.","Even her scent carried a sweet, fruity fragrance, luring Qin Yuanzheng to nuzzle and taste her, like a large dog in spring.","Qiao Lanshu, a little annoyed, lifted her leg to kick him, her eyes red as she glared, saying, \"Stop pinching my legs—it hurts.\"","This old man—did he even realize how strong he was?","And he kept comparing her to himself, teasing her about how small she was everywhere.","How could she possibly compete with someone like Qin Yuanzheng, who trained regularly?","Besides, Qin Yuanzheng was naturally built big.","Qin Yuanzheng took her kicks without moving an inch.","He casually caught her ankle, his voice slightly hoarse. \"You're upset? Then kick me a few more times?\"","With that, he lifted Qiao Lanshu's foot to his shoulder and said, \"Kick right here, let off some steam, huh?\"","But even as he said that, he didn't stop his playful teasing of Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu's cheek was pressed into the pillow, her tears soaking the fabric.","She really wanted to give him a few hard kicks.","But she realized that even if she kicked him, she'd be the one getting tired, and it wouldn't hurt him at all—so the urge faded.","This man was tough-skinned, built like a rock, with arms thicker than her thighs—what could she do?","She had no choice but to let him have his way.","...","On the other side, Guan Wenjun walked Zhong Mei back to the small alley.","His car couldn't drive in, so he parked it by the roadside and followed Zhong Mei into the alley.","Guan Wenjun was still quite restrained. They walked side by side in the pitch-black alley, neither speaking for a long time.","He kept glancing at Zhong Mei from time to time, before breaking the silence. \"This alley is way too dark at night.\"","Zhong Mei nodded. \"Yeah, but this is actually my first time walking it in the dark. I usually come straight home from work and never go out at night.\"","Although household registration and management were strict in these times, kidnappers still existed.","And in the city, there were plenty of unemployed loafers, drifters, and hoodlums who liked to wander at night, harassing young women and wives.","Zhong Mei lived here alone and rarely dared to go out after dark.","After eight or nine in the evening, the compound’s main gate would be locked. Once she returned to her room and locked her own door, it felt perfectly safe.","Guan Wenjun said, \"The city is indeed not that safe. For a young woman like you, it’s best not to walk alone at night.\"","As Zhong Mei’s boyfriend now, Guan Wenjun felt entitled to ask, \"How many families live in that compound of yours? Are they easy to get along with?\"","Zhong Mei nodded. \"They’re easy to get along with. Besides me, there’s a young couple, and a family of five.\"","Guan Wenjun nodded again, and by then, they had already reached the entrance of the compound.","The gate wasn’t locked yet. A dim bulb hung by the door, casting a faint, sickly light.","He felt a bit of disdain for the place. Though the surroundings weren’t terrible, they couldn’t compare to the staff dormitory where he lived.","A rush of impulse made him say to Zhong Mei, \"Once we’re married, I’ll apply for housing. Then you won’t have to live in a place like this.\"","The alley was pitch-black, without even a single streetlamp, making it impossible to walk at night without stumbling.","Come to think of it, he could buy a flashlight for Zhong Mei.","He figured she’d need one.","Hearing him mention marriage lifted Zhong Mei’s spirits.","Since Guan Wenjun had brought it up, she felt more confident.","It seemed that if she just coaxed him a bit more, they might even get their marriage certificate within the month.","Guan Wenjun walked her to the compound’s entrance. Under the dim light, Zhong Mei pushed the door open, then stood by the threshold, looking up at him with an expression that said she had something to say but hesitated.","Guan Wenjun also felt that this might be the moment to say something.","In the dim light, Zhong Mei’s features seemed softer, gentler.","They exchanged a silent gaze for a moment. Just as Guan Wenjun was wondering whether he should reach for her hand or perhaps give her a hug, Zhong Mei suddenly took a step back. Glancing at him shyly, she said, \"It’s getting late, Director Guan. Take care on the road.\"","Guan Wenjun froze.","His arm, which he had just started to lift, awkwardly moved to rub his nose instead. He nodded and said, \"Oh, alright. You take care too.\"","At this, Zhong Mei let out a light laugh. Then, under his embarrassed gaze, she closed the compound door.","Guan Wenjun stood there for a few seconds in silence before lightly slapping his own cheek.","He had misspoken again. She was already home, and he’d told her to take care. He’d been too busy staring at her, speaking without thinking.","he’d embarrassed himself once more.","As he walked out of the alley, he muttered to himself, how strange—why did Zhong Mei look so familiar?","Could it truly be fate? A bond from a past life?","Back in her room, Zhong Mei first went to the kitchen to heat water for a bath. After washing up, she hung her clothes to dry in the courtyard.","Once that was done, she began tidying her room.","As she cleaned, she thought of Guan Wenjun’s expression when they parted.","She couldn’t help but smile, remembering the look of hopeful shyness on his face, the arm he had raised, and his flustered embarrassment when she bid him farewell.","Guan Wenjun was even more innocent than she had expected.","This would make things much easier.","There was no need to actually coax him into sleeping together; just giving him a little sweetness would probably make him lost.","Zhong Mei thought this as she took out her keys again, unlocked the drawer, and pulled out a notebook. Tucked inside were some \"Big Unity\" bills as well as five-yuan and two-yuan notes.","She took out a \"Big Unity\" bill, planning to go to the Supply and Marketing Cooperative early the next day to buy groceries, come back to make dumplings for Guan Wenjun, and also buy a bottle of liquor to get him to drink.","After all, drinking makes things easier.","...","The next morning, it was Mid-Autumn Festival.","All the factories were on holiday.","The streets were bustling with activity. Most households had big red lanterns hung at their doors.","Workers had subsidies, and the Supply and Marketing Cooperative had stocked meat like mutton, pork, chicken, and fish, as well as fresh fruits like pomegranates, pears, and persimmons.","Meat was usually unavailable, though fruit was sometimes in stock.","So the meat counter had a long line stretching out.","Zhong Mei came alone—she had told Qiao Lanshu that she would be meeting Guan Wenjun today and wouldn’t be visiting her.","She arrived early, waited in line for over half an hour, and used the money and meat coupons Guan Wenjun had given her to finally buy half a chicken.","She then bought some red dates and angelica root, planning to go back and stew a chicken soup.","Seeing the fresh apples and bright red pomegranates, she stood there hesitating for two minutes.","She kind of wanted to buy a pomegranate to try.","She had never tasted the big red pomegranates from the north and wondered what they were like.","But after hesitating for a long time, she still couldn’t bring herself to buy them.","Fruits were probably as expensive as meat, so she’d better save the money.","She was still thinking about saving up to bring her two younger sisters out of Yangcheng by the end of the year.","Carrying the half chicken and the dried goods she’d bought, she thought it over and then bought some pork and celery, planning to make celery and pork dumplings when she got home.","Last night, she had specifically asked Auntie Shi for advice on how to season dumpling filling and had memorized the recipe. Today was a good chance to put it into practice.","After buying the groceries, Zhong Mei hurried back to prepare.","At home, Guan Wenjun couldn’t sit still either.","Thinking about visiting Zhong Mei's place for dinner today, he was both excited and nervous.","He changed into new clothes: a Dacron shirt, black trousers, and black leather shoes.","After spending ages preening in front of the mirror, he headed to the department store for a couple of rounds and bought a flashlight for Zhong Mei.","Then he remembered it was already Mid-Autumn, with the weather gradually turning cold. Zhong Mei, a girl from the south, probably couldn’t handle the chill here.","So he bought a black cashmere scarf for women.","He also thought about getting a women’s coat, a pair of cashmere boots, and such—since Zhong Mei looked thin, her clothes were old and flimsy, and she probably hadn’t started preparing winter clothes yet.","Winter came fast here, turning cold after Mid-Autumn, with frost and snow starting by late autumn.","He was afraid Zhong Mei wouldn’t have enough clothes and would end up freezing.","Guan Wenjun never kept track of his spending.","To put it in a way that might invite envy, the guy had never been short of money since childhood.","He was generous with his cash, and buying these things for Zhong Mei didn’t bother him at all.","But then he thought again: they had just started seeing each other, barely counting as their second day.","If he came on too strong, like some desperate fool, what would Zhong Mei think of him?","What if people found out he had money and deliberately played hard to get, treating him like an easy target and asking him for this and that?","The moment that image popped into his head, he immediately put the coat down.","Never mind. A flashlight and a scarf should be enough.","Thinking this, Guan Wenjun grabbed the two items, got into his car, and rushed off toward Zhong Mei’s home.","On the way, he saw someone selling bright red fruit from a pole in an alley. He stood at the entrance of the alley for a few seconds, torn.","His rational mind told him to stop spending money on women—enough already!","But his legs wouldn’t obey.","By the time he came to his senses, he had already bought a bag of apples, a bag of bright red pomegranates, and another bag of walnuts.","Weighed down by these heavy purchases, Guan Wenjun’s face darkened as he silently scolded himself: You useless, money-losing fool!"]},{"number":220,"title":"Chapter 220: A Lone Man and a Single Woman Alone in a Room","paragraphs":["The Mid-Autumn Festival is a time for family reunions.","Many people go home to celebrate the holiday with their families.","For comrades like Guan Wenjun and Zhong Mei, who were from other places, they could only spend it alone.","In previous years, Guan Wenjun would simply have a meal with his comrades from the Revolutionary Committee and eat some mooncakes, and that counted as celebrating the festival.","This year, instead of seeking out those brothers, he brought a bunch of things to celebrate the holiday with Zhong Mei, his heart feeling somewhat nervous.","Still, amid the nervousness, there was also a bit of happiness.","After all, he finally had a significant other. This year, he could celebrate the Mid-Autumn Festival with her, instead of fooling around with his buddies.","The gate of the compound was not closed. Guan Wenjun walked in and glanced around the yard.","The room Zhong Mei rented was near the compound’s entrance, visible as soon as he stepped in.","The family with a few members lived at the far end, requiring a walk across the entire compound to reach them, so the distance was actually a bit far. In the middle of the yard was a well, with a jujube tree beside it.","A young couple lived in the middle room, and their door was also open. The man was carrying a bucket to fetch water from the well.","When he saw Guan Wenjun, he nodded in a friendly manner.","Guan Wenjun nodded back, looking serious, and carried his things to Zhong Mei's door.","Zhong Mei was making dumplings in the kitchen. Most of the dumplings were already prepared, and the water in the pot had been boiling for a while.","She put the dumplings into the pot to cook, then checked on the chicken soup stewing in another small pot.","When Guan Wenjun reached the door, she heard the noise. Turning her head, her eyes lit up, and she also felt a bit shy: \"Director Guan, you're here?\"","Guan Wenjun cleared his throat and nodded somewhat awkwardly: \"You're cooking?\"","Zhong Mei smiled and nodded. She dried her hands on her apron, then stepped out quickly to take the things Guan Wenjun was carrying. She said in surprise, \"Director Guan, why did you buy so much? That's too extravagant!\"","Guan Wenjun also felt it was extravagant.","But since he had bought it, Zhong Mei had to accept it.","He thrust everything into Zhong Mei’s hands and said, \"I saw these on the way and just grabbed a few things. I don’t know what you like, so take a look first.\"","Guan Wenjun had bought quite a lot. Zhong Mei hurriedly took them and set them down in the kitchen area.","The room was small; Zhong Mei usually cooked and boiled water here, and ate here as well.","Near the door, she had placed a small table, but it had just been used for wrapping dumplings and hadn't been cleared yet, so there was no place to put things.","After a moment's hesitation, Zhong Mei set everything on the floor.","Guan Wenjun glanced around the kitchen, a hint of disdain in his eyes.","The house was old and very small. When Zhong Mei moved in, she clearly hadn't hired anyone to fix it up. The windows were a bit broken and wouldn't close tightly.","The door was also shabby.","He asked her, \"You cook here—which room do you sleep in?\"","Zhong Mei was squatting on the floor, sorting through the items. Hearing his question, she pointed next door: \"That room over there. I rented these two rooms.\"","The layout here was the same as that of the young couple across the way—two rooms, a smaller kitchen and a larger bedroom.","The floor was packed dirt, and the walls were made of mud bricks mixed with straw.","The roof looked fine, but she wasn’t sure if it leaked when it rained.","After looking around outside, Guan Wenjun didn't stand on ceremony and went straight into the room.","Zhong Mei cast a glance at him from behind but let him go. After all, her room had long been tidied up, and there was nothing to hide.","Besides, now that Guan Wenjun was dating her, he was her boyfriend—it was fine for him to enter her room.","Guan Wenjun stepped inside and looked around. The room was tidy and clean.","Against one wall was a large kang covered with soft bedding, with a neatly folded quilt stacked against the wall.","Beside the kang stood a small square table and two small chairs.","Against the wall sat two wooden cabinets, likely used for storing clothes.","Other than that, there was nothing else.","At first glance, everything was clean and empty, but the walls were bare earth, not even covered with newspaper.","He went to check the window—it was in good condition, closing tightly with the latch locked, impossible to open from outside.","Guan Wenjun walked over and sat down on the edge of the kang. Then he caught a faint scent of soap, the same smell as the clothes Zhong Mei wore.","Thinking that this was a young woman’s private room, he felt a little embarrassed.","So he stood up again and slowly wandered back to the kitchen.","Zhong Mei had already taken a basket and put away the apples and pomegranates Guan Wenjun had bought. Seeing the red apples and pomegranates, she couldn’t hide the joy in her eyes.","Just as she had been craving them, Guan Wenjun had bought them—maybe it was fate.","She counted: five apples and five pomegranates, along with a bag of walnuts, which she had never tried either.","She also set the walnuts in the basket and placed it on the table, then took out the flashlight and the cashmere scarf Guan Wenjun had bought.","She first looked at the scarf, caressing it lovingly, then turned to the flashlight.","She frowned slightly. These things were all very expensive.","The fruit went without saying, but the scarf was made of fine fabric—a single scarf probably cost around ten yuan, plus cloth coupons.","The flashlight, she had seen before at the department store, cost five yuan apiece and needed industrial coupons.","Just these two items alone would come to fifteen yuan.","And then there was the fruit...","Zhong Mei stood there hesitating. Just then, Guan Wenjun returned. He cleared his throat and looked at her expression, asking, \"What's wrong? Don't you like these? Is it the flashlight or the scarf you don't like?\"","Zhong Mei liked them both, of course.","She said a little uncertainly, \"Director Guan, weren’t these things expensive? Why are you spending so much...\"","As a temporary worker at a food factory, her monthly salary was only ten yuan now.","Even with subsidies, it was just twelve yuan.","She couldn’t afford such items.","She hesitated about whether to accept them.","She said, \"Director Guan, why don’t you return these things—especially this scarf. It’s too expensive, no need for it.\"","Hearing this, Guan Wenjun was a bit displeased.","He was willing to be the one spending money on her, and yet Zhong Mei wasn’t happy about it?","He sat down on the kitchen chair and said, \"Since we’re dating, of course I should buy you something. Don’t say any more—just accept it as I tell you.\"","That was just Guan Wenjun’s nature: he liked being pampered, obeyed, and listened to.","He thought Zhong Mei had a good personality—gentle, submissive, and fond of him. He figured that after marriage, she would be the clingy type.","He was very satisfied with Zhong Mei and never imagined she would be disobedient.","Of course, at this moment, Zhong Mei was also willing to go along with him.","She immediately nodded and said, \"Alright, then I’ll accept them.\"","With that, she gazed at Guan Wenjun with affectionate eyes and said, \"Thank you, Director Guan. You’re so good to me.\"","Guan Wenjun looked rather pleased with himself. \"Don't worry, as long as you behave yourself, I'll treat you even better in the future.\"","Zhong Mei thought to herself that she had never been one to associate with the word \"obedient\" since she was a child, but for the sake of these gifts, she would play along for a while.","She took everything into the adjacent bedroom, leaving only two apples and a pomegranate out, and locked the rest in the wooden cabinet.","Then, she hurried over to scoop out the dumplings.","Zhong Mei said, \"The dumplings are ready. This is my first time making the filling—pork with celery. I'm not sure if you'll like it.\"","Guan Wenjun stood beside her, watching the plump, round dumplings bob on the surface of the water, rolling with the boiling broth.","He said, \"No matter how bad dumplings are, they can't be that bad. I'm sure I'll love them.\"","As he spoke, the two of them glanced at each other without meaning to, then both shyly looked away.","Guan Wenjun tilted his head to look at the sky, while Zhong Mei hung her head and continued scooping out the dumplings.","The dumplings were done, and the chicken soup was ready too.","She cleared the small table in the kitchen, placed the dumplings on it, and brought over two bowls of chicken soup—giving Guan Wenjun's bowl a generous portion of chicken meat.","Her own bowl had very little chicken.","Guan Wenjun noticed this, and his heart swelled with joy. He thought to himself that Zhong Mei must really like him to save all the meat for him.","Zhong Mei also took two cucumbers from the vegetable basket. These cucumbers were given to her by Qiao Lanshu, because Shi Sao had planted a lot of vegetables in the yard, enough for her whole family. Since Zhong Mei rarely visited, Qiao Lanshu picked some for her.","Zhong Mei smashed the cucumbers, added vinegar and sesame oil to mix them, and lunch was ready.","The two sat facing each other. Zhong Mei said a little sheepishly, \"The meal is simple, Director Guan, I hope you don't mind.\"","It was only at this moment that Zhong Mei realized she had forgotten to buy mooncakes.","She wondered if Guan Wenjun would be upset.","Luckily, Guan Wenjun was too nervous himself, his mind completely occupied by Zhong Mei sitting nearby to think about much else.","He picked up his chopsticks, started eating the dumplings, and sipped the soup. To his surprise, Zhong Mei's cooking was quite good—the chicken soup was sweet and fragrant, and the dumplings were tasty, though a bit bland. Guan Wenjun added salt to his bowl twice, which stunned Zhong Mei.","She thought the seasoning was just right for her, but Guan Wenjun really liked his food salty!","Zhong Mei pondered for a moment, then suddenly brought out a bottle of liquor. She took two cups and poured a drink for each of them.","Guan Wenjun was startled. He looked at her and asked, \"You like to drink?\"","Zhong Mei replied with some embarrassment, \"No, it's just that today is Mid-Autumn Festival, and it's our first time... I thought we should have a toast...\"","Seeing Zhong Mei looking so shy, Guan Wenjun immediately put down his chopsticks, took the cup, and said, \"Right, we really should have a toast.\"","With that, Guan Wenjun clinked his cup against Zhong Mei's and downed it in one gulp.","The liquor was strong and fiery. Guan Wenjun was used to drinking, so he didn't change expression. Zhong Mei refilled his cup.","After three cups in a row, Guan Wenjun said, \"Alright, stop pouring. I can't drink anymore. Any more and I'll get drunk.\"","But Zhong Mei poured him another cup anyway. \"I haven't congratulated you on your transfer to the Supply Department yet. I wanted to earlier, Director Guan. You're really impressive.\"","Guan Wenjun was feeling the effects of the alcohol, and her praise made him lightheaded again. He tilted his head back and drank it down.","After four cups, Guan Wenjun was clearly getting dizzy.","Zhong Mei set down her own half-finished cup, urged Guan Wenjun to eat some more dumplings, and then asked with concern, \"Director Guan, are you tired? Maybe you should go next door and rest for a while?\"","Guan Wenjun stared straight at Zhong Mei. He said in a low voice, \"Zhong Mei, I always feel like you look really familiar.\"","Zhong Mei: \"...\"","Zhong Mei's heart suddenly tightened, and she looked at him nervously.","Guan Wenjun was a bit dizzy now, so he didn't notice her expression.","He suddenly grabbed Zhong Mei's hand, squeezed it softly, leaned in, and said, reeking of alcohol, \"Zhong Mei, tell me, have we met somewhere before?\"","Zhong Mei: \"...\"","His words made her heart race.","Zhong Mei swallowed nervously, not knowing what to say. She replied tensely, \"R-really? Maybe I just have a very ordinary face, looks like everyone else?\"","Guan Wenjun looked at her face, then at her eyes, and shook his head. \"You're very pretty. Not ordinary at all.\"","Guan Wenjun was also a man who cared about appearances. If Zhong Mei had been plain-looking, he probably wouldn't have taken any notice.","Besides, Qin Yuanzheng had married such a beautiful wife—he couldn't just settle for someone plain, could he?","He definitely wanted to find someone attractive, too.","Zhong Mei was a bit embarrassed by his compliment.","But now wasn't the time to dwell on that. She needed to speed things up.","She had to prevent Guan Wenjun from suddenly remembering how they first met. If that happened, forget about getting married—they might not even be able to date.","Zhong Mei quickly went to help him up. She said gently, \"Director Guan, I think you might be a little drunk. It's better to go rest next door.\"","Guan Wenjun's mind was still clear, but the alcohol had gone to his head.","He felt a bit dizzy, which normally would pass after resting.","As Zhong Mei came to support him, she held his arm, and the softness of her chest inadvertently brushed against his elbow.","Guan Wenjun's body instantly stiffened, and a wave of heat surged downward from the alcohol.","Guan Wenjun: \"!!!\"","Guan Wenjun shut his mouth tightly and walked stiffly, following Zhong Mei to the next room.","Zhong Mei helped him to sit on the kang. \"Director Guan, sit here and rest for a bit. I'll get you some water.\"","With that, Zhong Mei turned and went back out. She quickly cut up two apples, put the leftover dumplings in the pot to keep warm, then carried a plate of apples in one hand and a teapot in the other as she left the kitchen. She locked the kitchen door before returning to the room.","Guan Wenjun was still sitting rigidly on the kang, and when Zhong Mei came in, he awkwardly crossed his legs, as if trying to hide something.","After all, he was a twenty-eight- or twenty-nine-year-old virgin who had suddenly experienced such close contact with a woman. Guan Wenjun was having a hard time handling it.","He watched Zhong Mei enter the room and then close the door with her foot.","Once the door was shut, the room became an enclosed space.","They were alone, man and woman, in a room with nothing but a large kang big enough for three or four people to lie down on.","This, this...","Guan Wenjun watched Zhong Mei approach him. Sitting on the kang, his gaze happened to land on her chest.","He had never paid so much attention to a female comrade's figure before.","He noticed that Zhong Mei was very slim—her arms and legs were slender. Oh, and when she tied on that apron, her waist was tiny, too.","But she had curves in the right places, her chest looking quite full.","Guan Wenjun thought about the soft touch he had felt on his arm earlier, so soft that it felt like...","He thought for two seconds. Oh, just like a steaming white steamed bun fresh from the pot...","Zhong Mei glanced at Guan Wenjun. His face was flushed from the alcohol—his pale skin had turned red, along with his ears and neck. He sat upright, his gaze following her intently.","Zhong Mei felt a bit shy under his stare. She placed the apple and teapot on the table by the heated brick bed and said to Guan Wenjun, “Director Guan, how about some tea or an apple?”","As she spoke, she took down the two ceramic cups covering the spout and poured two cups of tea.","Guan Wenjun looked at Zhong Mei’s slender yet slightly rough hands, nodded silently, and took the cup, drinking a few sips of tea.","The tea was warm, and after finishing the cup, an even greater heat stirred inside him.","What was he to do? He felt as if he’d been bewitched today, unable to stop himself from wanting to do something to Zhong Mei.","What Guan Wenjun didn’t know was that Zhong Mei had deliberately dressed in thin, figure-hugging clothes to see him.","Despite the chill in the air, she wore layers that were thin, intentionally tailored at the waist, and with added padding in her undergarments for the chest. She knew what men liked.","The outfit she had on today made her breasts look full and her waist slender, accentuating her figure perfectly.","Guan Wenjun already harbored some feelings for her. Now, tipsy and flushed with heat, seeing her dressed like this, if he could keep his hands to himself, Zhong Mei would start to wonder if something was wrong with him.","Just then, Zhong Mei took off her apron, leaving only a thin, short-sleeved top. Guan Wenjun’s gaze fell on her, and his heartbeat suddenly quickened.","At that moment, Zhong Mei leaned toward him and said softly, “Director Guan, why are you sweating so much? Is it too hot? Why don’t you take off your jacket?”","As she spoke, Zhong Mei took out a handkerchief, wiped the sweat from his forehead, and then moved to help him remove his jacket.","Guan Wenjun: “!!!”"]},{"number":221,"title":"Chapter 221: He is acting like a hooligan.","paragraphs":["Guan Wenjun really did feel very hot.","He figured it was from drinking too much.","He regretted having had alcohol just now—what if he lost his composure?","Zhong Mei thoughtfully helped him take off his jacket and hung it on the nail behind the door.","Then she came back, sat down on a chair by the table, glanced at him shyly, and picked up her teacup to drink.","Guan Wenjun looked at the tightly closed windows and door, then at Zhong Mei sitting beside him, as if she had something to say but held back.","At that moment, he felt the air in the room was thick and tense.","He tugged at his shirt collar, a little guiltily, and glanced at Zhong Mei again.","She really was quite pretty. Every time he looked at her, he found her more pleasing to the eye.","It’s just that this young woman was too shy, and she wasn’t very old either. Since they were already in a relationship, he, as the man, had to take the lead.","Otherwise, if they kept being so polite and reserved, when would their relationship ever progress?","Zhong Mei sipped her tea slowly, then picked up a piece of apple with a toothpick and handed it to Guan Wenjun. “Director Guan, have an apple.”","Guan Wenjun took the apple, ate it in one bite, and looked at her, saying, “Given how close we are now, calling me ‘Director Guan’ feels too formal.”","Besides, he was no longer the director of the Revolutionary Committee; his current position was head of the Supply Section.","When Zhong Mei heard this, she asked a little bashfully, “Then... what should I call you?”","Guan Wenjun cleared his throat, his eyes wandering, and said, “You can call me Jun Ge.”","Zhong Mei was silent for a moment.","Looking at the slightly expectant expression in his eyes, she said, “Alright, Jun Ge.”","Guan Wenjun felt pleased inside. He couldn’t help but smile briefly, then, thinking he should appear more steady, he stopped smiling and nodded. “Good. Keep calling me that from now on.”","Zhong Mei thought to herself that Guan Wenjun was actually quite easy to read.","He was clearly someone who had grown up in a well-off family, cherished by his parents.","He seemed sharp and capable at work, even fierce when handling business, but deep down, he was pretty straightforward.","He was completely different from Qin Yuanzheng, Qiao Lanshu’s husband.","Qin Yuanzheng’s mind was unfathomable, but Zhong Mei found Guan Wenjun easy to understand.","As they talked, silence fell between them again.","Zhong Mei didn’t speak, and Guan Wenjun kept quiet too.","Guan Wenjun felt the atmosphere growing more and more awkward. Even after taking off his coat, he was still sweating all over.","He fixed his gaze on Zhong Mei. She ate two pieces of apple, then, sensing his stare, lifted her head to meet his eyes for a moment before bowing her head again, seemingly shy.","Guan Wenjun thought to himself, Well, it looks like he still had to make the first move.","He patted the kang beside him and said, “Zhong Mei, come sit over here.”","Without asking why, she got up and sat down next to him.","Feeling her presence, he caught the faint scent of soap from her.","He reached out and took her hand. She froze and instinctively tried to pull back.","Guan Wenjun, who had been a bit embarrassed himself, frowned at her reaction. He tightened his grip and held her hand firmly. Looking at her with a serious expression, he asked, “Why are you pulling away?”","Zhong Mei lowered her head, feeling too shy to meet his eyes, and didn’t say a word.","Guan Wenjun said again, “We’re already in a relationship now, so it’s normal for us to hold hands, hug, and even kiss, got it?”","When he said “kiss,” Guan Wenjun felt a bit embarrassed himself.","But clearly, in their relationship, he was the one taking the lead, not Zhong Mei.","If they waited for Zhong Mei to make the first move, that would take forever.","So, thinking this way, Guan Wenjun put on his chauvinistic boldness, reached over, and wrapped an arm around Zhong Mei’s shoulder. He swallowed hard and said in a low voice, “Can I kiss you?”","Zhong Mei was a little nervous too—she had never been this intimate with any man before.","But looking at Guan Wenjun’s handsome, fair face, she thought he was indeed pretty good.","This was probably the best catch she could hope for right now.","He was tall, handsome, had a decent job and family background, and, most importantly, his character was acceptable.","With that in mind, Zhong Mei blushed and nodded.","Guan Wenjun leaned in and kissed her immediately.","For the first time, he was shy, so he just kissed her cheek.","The girl’s skin was clean, smooth, and soft.","Fueled by courage from the alcohol, Guan Wenjun got carried away. He held Zhong Mei and kissed her, and as things heated up, he pressed her down onto the kang (traditional heated bed).","Zhong Mei was slender. Guan Wenjun touched her for a while and said in a low voice, “You’re too skinny. You’ll need to eat more and gain some weight.”","Before Zhong Mei could say anything, he leaned in again to kiss her.","Guan Wenjun was also inexperienced—this was his first time. All he knew was rubbing lips together, and he hugged Zhong Mei tightly, fumbling around excitedly for a long time.","After more than ten minutes, it was clear that Guan Wenjun was getting more and more worked up, almost losing control.","Zhong Mei quickly pushed him away. She scrambled to stand in the corner of the room, blushing furiously as she looked at Guan Wenjun, one hand still clutching the front of her clothes. Red-faced and flustered, she said, “Guan Zhu... Brother Jun, we’re not married yet...”","Guan Wenjun: “...”","Guan Wenjun had been right in the heat of the moment when Zhong Mei suddenly shoved him off. Now, his body was burning with desire, only to be cut off abruptly.","He glanced at Zhong Mei, then looked down at himself, and belatedly realized he had gotten a bit carried—he had almost lost control.","They had just started dating, and Zhong Mei was clearly frightened. Guan Wenjun immediately felt like a real jerk.","He quickly stood up, adjusting his pants, his expression extremely awkward.","Looking at Zhong Mei’s face, he asked nervously, “Are you... are you okay? I just now...”","He paused, his expression embarrassed, and added, “I didn’t mean to do that. I really just wanted to kiss you, honestly.”","He honestly had only meant to kiss her, but who would have thought he couldn’t stop himself?","If Zhong Mei hadn’t pushed him away, by now, he might have even taken off her clothes.","Judging by her wrinkled, rumpled outfit and her swollen lips, it was clear how excited and forceful he had been.","Zhong Mei kept her head down, not daring to look at him. She said softly, “It’s... it’s okay. But we haven’t gotten our marriage certificate yet, so we shouldn’t do things like this in the future. I’m not that kind of easy woman.”","Guan Wenjun quickly replied, “I know, I know. I know you’re not easy. Just now, I was the one being too forward.”","He nervously explained himself for a while, and then noticed Zhong Mei’s gaze drifting toward his lower body.","Guan Wenjun: “!!!”","Guan Wenjun quickly said, “The food was really good today. Anyway, I, uh, I have something at work, so I’ll head out now. I’ll come see you again tomorrow.”","With that, Guan Wenjun hurriedly opened the door and ran off.","You could almost call it a frantic escape.","Zhong Mei chased to the doorway, but Guan Wenjun was already out of sight;","he had run far away.","So Zhong Mei went back inside, closed the door, picked up her apple, and continued eating.","The apple was crisp, sweet, and fragrant.","Even at her age, this was the first time she had ever eaten an apple.","Even in the apple-producing regions of the north, apples weren’t cheap.","On her own, Zhong Mei would never have been willing to spend money on fruit like that.","But now, just the second day into dating Guan Wenjun, he had already bought her apples and even a big red pomegranate.","It sure was nice to be with someone who had money.","Zhong Mei thought about that, then reflected on Guan Wenjun from just moments ago.","She knew that Guan Wenjun was like any ordinary man: once things got steamy with a woman, he would inevitably want to do the deed—no normal man could resist it.","But she absolutely could not sleep with Guan Wenjun before marriage.","She was planning to marry him and have a stable life together.","If she fooled around with him before the wedding, then once Guan Wenjun calmed down later, he would surely see through her.","She was already on unequal footing with Guan Wenjun in terms of her background, so she had to be especially careful in this regard.","Zhong Mei mused to herself that, after this episode, her relationship with Guan Wenjun should probably be secure, right?","If it wasn’t, then she could just kiss him a few more times.","Still, as she bit into the apple, Zhong Mei let out a soft “tsk” and touched her lips, muttering under her breath, “He’s really like a dog.”","Biting hurt so much.","She looked up at the door again and suddenly noticed that Guan Wenjun had forgotten his jacket.","Perfect—she could return it to him tomorrow.","...","Unlike Zhong Mei’s calmness, after Guan Wenjun fled the crowded courtyard, he ran all the way back to his own dormitory.","He hadn’t taken the car today, since Zhong Mei’s courtyard wasn’t far from the supply department’s dormitory—about a half-hour walk.","This time, he ran the whole way back.","After returning home, Guan Wenjun, panting heavily, locked the door tight. He didn’t even acknowledge the people who greeted him along the way.","Leaning against the door, his heart still hammered wildly.","He looked down, then unbuckled his belt...","Never mind, never mind—at a time like this, with lust burning in his head, he’d better take care of the problem first and then figure out what to do.","He replayed their first contact with Zhong Mei in his mind...","It was his first kiss with a woman. Zhong Mei’s lips were so soft, and the way she looked at him was so gentle. She was very thin, with a slender waist that he could seemingly hold with one hand.","Oh, and though she was slender, she had a good figure—at least everything that should be fleshy was fleshy.","At that moment, he had genuinely felt it, and it reminded him of steaming-hot white buns...","He’d almost completely lost control right then.","Thinking of this, Guan Wenjun suddenly froze, and he double-checked in disbelief.","Then he cursed under his breath: “Damn... barely a minute...”","Guess he really was getting older, and it was time to find a woman to marry.","...","The day after Mid-Autumn Festival was still a holiday, so no one was at work.","After what happened yesterday, Zhong Mei figured that Guan Wenjun would definitely come looking for her again.","After all, a man with unfulfilled desires basically has no self-control.","But Zhong Mei thought that playing hard to get would be more suitable for Guan Wenjun.","So the next morning, she packed two apples and two big red pomegranates in a vegetable basket and went to look for Qiao Lanshu.","By the time she arrived, it was already nine in the morning.","But Sister Shi told her, “Xiao Qiao hasn’t gotten up yet. Since you’re here, you can keep an eye on the two kids while I make breakfast.”","Zhong Mei was astonished: “It’s this late already, why hasn’t Qiao Lanshu gotten up yet?”","That didn’t make sense—she usually woke up pretty early, didn’t she?","Sister Shi covered her mouth with a laugh and said, “Well, these past few days, our Commander Qin hasn’t gone to work either. Since the couple is both home for once, they’ve been getting up late.”","Zhong Mei: “...”","Even though she wasn’t married yet, Zhong Mei understood.","She blushed slightly and said to Sister Shi with a smile, “Sister, I brought some apples and pomegranates. You can take them to the kitchen.”","As soon as Sister Shi saw them, she quickly remarked, “Oh my, these fruits aren’t cheap, are they?”","Zhong Mei replied, “They’re not too expensive. They’re for the kids.”","Sister Shi didn’t refuse, since the gifts were actually meant for Qiao Lanshu. She was just the nanny, so she’d mention it to Qiao Lanshu when she was up.","She took the fruits and said with a smile, “Have you had breakfast yet? I bought some soy milk and I’m about to make some egg pancakes. Want to join us for a bite?”","Zhong Mei smiled and said, “Sure, thanks, Sister Shi.”","In the yard, Niuwa was watering the vegetable patch, while An’an sat on the porch where a sheet had been spread out, holding a baby bottle and drinking milk.","Zhong Mei went over, picked up An’an, and started playing with the child.","Inside the house, Qiao Lanshu heard Zhong Mei’s voice through the window. She quickly nudged Qin Yuanzheng, who was lying on top of her, and whispered, “Zhong Mei is here. Let me get up.”","Qin Yuanzheng, finally having two days off, was reluctant to let his wife go.","He kissed Qiao Lanshu’s neck, and she kept dodging, “Oh, you haven’t shaved again.”","Qin Yuanzheng wouldn’t let her avoid him. He pressed her down and kissed her from her neck to her face, and then from her face to her ear.","Her earlobes were soft and plump, and he liked them a lot, so he gave them extra attention.","Qiao Lanshu couldn’t help but whisper, “Stop fooling around—it’s already nine...”","Qin Yuanzheng murmured, “They all understand. What are you afraid of?”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","That was exactly why she was embarrassed: because they all understood.","But Qin Yuanzheng wouldn’t give in. He said softly, “I’m already ready. Just ten minutes...”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","She kicked him with her foot. “Don’t try to trick me. There’s no way it’ll be over in ten minutes.”","So Qin Yuanzheng grabbed her knee. “Then let me have a little morning meal.”","He hadn’t had it in a long time. Every night these past few days, he’d wanted it, but Qiao Lanshu wouldn’t let him.","He really craved it.","And since Qiao Lanshu couldn’t make a sound or cause a commotion right now, he might as well take his breakfast.","Before Qiao Lanshu could stop him, he had his way.","Qiao Lanshu’s eyes turned red as she kicked him. “You—you didn’t even shave again!”","But Qin Yuanzheng was too busy to pay her any mind. It was early morning, his stomach was growling, and he had to hurry up and eat his breakfast.","He always liked something soupy and watery in the morning...","Qiao Lanshu was truly terrified of Qin Yuanzheng’s mouth.","Not only was his stubble prickly and uncomfortable, but even the kiss was hard to bear.","Qiao Lanshu kept retreating backward until she reached the head of the bed, with nowhere left to go.","But the person in front of her kept pressing forward.","She covered her mouth, enduring it with great difficulty.","The couple stayed in the room until around ten o'clock, when Qin Yuanzheng finally emerged from the room dressed in his military uniform and cap, wearing an expression of stern seriousness.","Seeing his intimidating demeanor, Zhong Mei, holding An'an in her arms, straightened up: \"Brigadier Qin, are you heading to work?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded with an air of formality: \"Yes, I have a meeting at the headquarters. Make yourself at home.\"","With that, Qin Yuanzheng, his face set in severity, walked out of the main door and carefully closed the door behind him.","Zhong Mei watched Qin Yuanzheng's retreating figure, thinking to herself: Lanshu's husband is so rigid, so strict, and looks so fierce.","He definitely wouldn't be unable to control his desires like Guan Wenjun."]},{"number":222,"title":"Chapter 222: Going to Kindergarten","paragraphs":["After Qin Yuanzheng left, Qiao Lanshu lay limp on the kang, resting for quite a while.","She could hear the voices of Zhong Mei and An'an coming from outside the house, along with the sound of Niuwa chasing the dog around the yard.","She also heard Sister Shi running into the vegetable garden, shouting at Niuwa for trampling her seedlings again.","Qiao Lanshu picked up the watch on the bedside table and saw that it was already ten o'clock in the morning.","It was already this late!","Qiao Lanshu reached back and rubbed her lower back, feeling soreness in her waist and legs, utterly exhausted.","It was all Qin Yuanzheng's fault. He really was... really...","Qiao Lanshu buried her face in the quilt, closed her eyes for a moment longer, then got up to change her clothes.","By the time Qiao Lanshu had dressed, washed up, and stepped into the yard, Niuwa, who had been arguing with Sister Shi just moments before, immediately rushed over at the sight of her. He hugged Qiao Lanshu's thigh and started wailing loudly. The puppy that Qin Yuanzheng had brought back from the mining site followed Niuwa, barking furiously.","Zhong Mei and Sister Shi were both stunned.","That little rascal—he was turning the tables and blaming others!","Qiao Lanshu nearly stumbled when Niuwa, strong as a little calf, threw himself at her.","She quickly crouched down, hugging Niuwa, and asked, \"What's wrong? What's wrong? Has my Niuwa been wronged?\"","Niuwa sobbed loudly while showing Qiao Lanshu his bright red bottom.","Qiao Lanshu held back a smile, rubbed it gently for him, then looked up at Sister Shi.","Sister Shi, while tidying her seedlings in the garden, said angrily, \"This little brat—I asked him to help water the vegetables this morning, but instead, he started playing with the water. He soaked his own clothes, and on top of that, he flooded my seedlings. Look, this whole patch has turned into a puddle.\"","What made it even more infuriating was that Niuwa, knowing wet clothes could make him catch a cold, had stripped them off and tossed them into the vegetable garden, covering them in dirt.","Zhong Mei, holding An'an in the corridor, had actually tried to tell Niuwa to stop when she saw him playing water fights with the dog, but Niuwa didn't react at all.","She couldn't tell if he genuinely hadn't heard her or was intentionally ignoring her.","So Zhong Mei had called Sister Shi over.","Then Sister Shi had grabbed Niuwa and slapped him a few times on the bottom.","Strictly speaking, Sister Shi was the housekeeper. Whether the children in the family were adopted or biological, she wasn't supposed to hit them.","But this time, she truly couldn't hold back.","So after explaining, she apologized to Qiao Lanshu. \"Xiao Qiao, I'm really sorry. I just couldn't help it. That boy Niuwa is too mischievous. Look what he's done to my garden!\"","If it were her own child, Sister Shi would have used a broomstick. A few slaps would have been the least of it.","Qiao Lanshu sighed and looked at Niuwa. He was staring back at her with pitiful eyes, waiting for her to scold Sister Shi.","Qiao Lanshu shot him a glare and said to Sister Shi, \"Kids are naughty; it's right to discipline them. If Niuwa acts up again, sister, just spank him as you see fit! When Director Han gets back, I'll explain it to him.\"","Niuwa: \"!!!\"","Niuwa's eyes went wide instantly, as if the sky had fallen.","He started wailing again, clinging to Qiao Lanshu and playing the sympathy card. \"Mommy, you don't love me anymore. Mommy, you can't let other people hit me, because hitting hurts a lot, and if it hurts a lot, I'll be sad, and if I'm sad, I won't be happy...\"","Everyone: \"...\"","Zhong Mei couldn’t help but laugh when she heard this: \"A four-year-old boy who can express himself so well—he’s definitely got the makings of a good student.\"","Zhong Mei had taken care of several younger siblings before, and none of them had been able to talk this much at the age of four.","Niuwa really knew how to play on people’s sympathy. He’d figured out that if he cried and then acted pitiful with a few well-chosen words, Qiao Lanshu would inevitably scold him.","The last time he refused to leave with Han Wenlin, he’d used the same trick.","It worked every single time.","Sure enough, Qiao Lanshu picked him up and said, \"Alright, stop crying. Go apologize to Sister Shi, then take a bath and change your clothes. Go on.\"","And so Niuwa stopped crying, happily went to apologize to Sister Shi, picked up his clothes—which were covered in mud—put them in the basin, and took them under the tap to wash them himself.","Zhong Mei carried An’an over and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Niuwa is a decent kid. He’s a bit mischievous, but I think he’s actually quite sensible. He probably understands everything in his own way. He’s a clever child.\"","Qiao Lanshu watched An’an playing with the rocking horse and said softly, \"I hope An’an will be well-behaved when he grows up. I don’t want him causing trouble every other day.\"","If Niuwa caused trouble, it could be blamed on Han Wenlin. But if An’an started getting into trouble, it would be up to her and Qin Yuanzheng to handle it.","Qiao Lanshu picked An’an up, kissed him several times, then suddenly remembered something and looked at Zhong Mei. \"Didn’t you say you were supposed to be spending these two days dating Director Guan and building your feelings? Why are you here today? You’ll be back at work tomorrow, right? You only had today left—why didn’t you seize the chance?\"","At this, Zhong Mei’s face flushed slightly.","She looked a little embarrassed, lowered her voice, and said, \"I met him yesterday. I made him dumplings, and we had lunch together. And then...\"","She paused here, looking a bit awkward.","Qiao Lanshu led Zhong Mei into the house. Once they were seated inside, Zhong Mei lowered her voice and whispered in Qiao Lanshu’s ear, telling her everything that had happened the day before.","After hearing it all, Qiao Lanshu’s expression was quite colorful.","She looked at Zhong Mei, who looked back at her, equally embarrassed.","Qiao Lanshu couldn’t help but laugh. She said in a low voice, \"From what you’re saying, I think Director Guan is already hooked. But A-Mei, you’ve got to remember—with men, you can’t fill them up too quickly...\"","Just then, she thought of Qin Yuanzheng...","Forget it. Men could never be filled up.","A bit embarrassed, she rephrased it differently: \"What I mean is, don’t satisfy them too soon. At least wait until you get the marriage certificate before doing that kind of thing... You know what I’m saying, right?\"","In truth, Zhong Mei had originally planned that if Guan Wenjun wasn’t interested in her, she would use some tricks—like getting him drunk and sleeping with him.","But yesterday, she suddenly changed her mind.","She felt that Guan Wenjun was different with her, and if he truly liked her, she definitely wanted to treasure that kind of feeling.","She’d take it slow with him, go out properly for a while, then get married and live a steady life together afterward.","Precisely because she wanted to live a good life with him, to spend decades together, she couldn’t rush into things and just steam the rice before it was fully cooked.","She listened to Qiao Lanshu’s words, nodded, and said, “That’s what I think now too. So, he’ll probably come looking for me today. I want to let him cool off for a while and not see him until tomorrow.”","When Qiao Lanshu heard this, she smiled again.","She knew that Zhong Mei had always been very resourceful and good at reading people, and she was much more thoughtful and clever in handling matters than she was.","So, she had nothing more to remind Zhong Mei about and instead teased her, saying, “Well then, it looks like I should start preparing your wedding gifts now?”","Zhong Mei quickly stopped her, saying, “Please don’t. The little square table and chair you bought me before—you already said they were an early wedding gift. When I get married, you absolutely must not give me anything else.”","Her rent for the past six months had been paid by Qiao Lanshu, and she still hadn’t repaid her.","She owed Qiao Lanshu too much already and couldn’t trouble her any further.","Zhong Mei stayed with Qiao Lanshu in the room, sharing some heartfelt words. After lunch, she followed Qiao Lanshu to the supply cooperative to buy things.","Around four o’clock in the afternoon, she said goodbye to Qiao Lanshu and carried her vegetable basket home.","Qiao Lanshu saw her off at the alley entrance before returning home herself.","The next day, work and school would resume as usual.","Qiao Lanshu had previously enrolled Niuwa in a kindergarten run by the military, where all the children were from military families.","At first, Niuwa hadn’t wanted to go. To coax him into it, Qiao Lanshu not only made him a beautiful new outfit but also sewed him a small backpack. The backpack was made of yellow and blue fabric, with very nice colors.","Moreover, Sister Shi had embroidered a chubby little white cow on the backpack and even stitched his full name, “Han Ye,” onto it.","When Niuwa saw the backpack, he joyfully put it on and refused to take it off even when sleeping. Before bed, he kept murmuring about wanting to go to school.","When Qin Yuanzheng returned home that evening and learned that Niuwa was starting kindergarten the next day, he said to Qiao Lanshu, “I pass by the kindergarten on my way to work. From now on, I’ll take him there. What time do they get out in the afternoon?”","Qiao Lanshu was sitting on a chair in front of her desk. On one side of the desk, five or six textbooks were neatly stacked, and beside them sat a ceramic pen holder with a few pens.","On the other side lay a sewing basket. She was currently holding one of Qin Yuanzheng’s undershirts, mending it.","Although Qin Yuanzheng was not short of money, he was very frugal in daily life.","Several of his army-green undershirts had holes in them, but he still kept wearing them.","The same went for his socks. Qiao Lanshu had noticed that some of his socks also had holes today, and he hadn’t even mentioned it.","So she had gone through his clothes and taken out all the torn ones to patch up.","When Qin Yuanzheng saw this, he came over and said, “Aren’t you not good at sewing? Leave the clothes for Sister Shi to mend.”","Qiao Lanshu was sewing his undershirt under the lamp, smiling as she said, “I learned a bit from Sister Ling before, and later from Sister Shi. Now I can patch up your clothes just fine.”","But she still couldn’t make clothes or quilts.","Those were really too difficult. Even the backpack she had made for Niuwa today was the simplest kind: she sewed the fabric into a circle, then stitched a drawstring around the edge, so pulling the string turned it into a pouch.","That was the easiest to make and could hold a lot of things. Niuwa really liked it.","She had even learned simple mending, since it was relatively much easier.","Qin Yuanzheng walked over to look at the clothes she was stitching. Sure enough, the stitches were very fine, using thread of the same color. If one didn't look closely, it was hard to notice.","He immediately planted a kiss on Qiao Lanshu's cheek and said in a low voice, \"My wife is really amazing. The clothes she mends are so beautiful. I can guarantee no one can sew better than you.\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled at his praise. She looked up at Qin Yuanzheng and said with a laugh, \"Brigade Commander Qin, are you speaking against your conscience now?\"","Qin Yuanzheng replied seriously, \"Not at all. I always tell the truth. My wife is truly impressive.\"","With that, he stepped forward, reached out, grabbed Qiao Lanshu by the waist, lifted her up, and sat down on a chair, placing her on his lap. Holding her close, he took a deep breath and said, \"Alright, keep sewing, my capable little wife.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","She glanced at the time; it was already past eight in the evening. Qin Yuanzheng must have been quite tired today, so they should rest early.","Thinking this, she stayed seated on his lap and said, \"Almost done. When I finish this piece, we'll go to sleep.\"","Qin Yuanzheng adjusted her sitting position, making her sit facing away from him, straddling his lap. His hands then began to wander.","One arm wrapped around her waist, rubbing her belly.","The other hand moved upward...","Qiao Lanshu, flustered by his antics, quickly put away her needle and thread, folded the clothes, and placed them on the table. She turned to look at him. \"Alright, stop fooling around. Let's talk about something serious.\"","Qin Yuanzheng didn't stop his movements. He kissed her ear a few times and asked in a low voice, \"What serious matter?\"","Then he added, \"By the way, the pants I'm wearing now are also torn. You can mend them for me tomorrow.\"","He had just finished his bath and, as soon as he entered the room and closed the door, he had taken off his clothes.","Now he was only wearing a tight black pair of shorts.","As he said this, he slightly arched his hips, toward Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu blushed and lightly slapped him there, saying, \"You're being naughty again.\"","Qin Yuanzheng grunted, as if in punishment, and squeezed her with both hands.","Qiao Lanshu quickly arched her back to avoid it, pleading, \"Ah, ah, don't!\"","Qin Yuanzheng bit her earlobe gently and asked in a low voice, \"Will you still hit me?\"","Qiao Lanshu hurriedly replied, \"I won't. I definitely won't in the future.\"","In truth, this wasn't the first time she had done it. Sometimes she deliberately teased Qin Yuanzheng; other times she truly found him too rough in that regard and, scared by his intensity, would lightly slap him to vent her frustration.","She never used much force, so it probably didn't hurt much.","Qin Yuanzheng was just finding excuses to tease her.","While sliding her pant leg down from her ankle, he asked, \"What serious matter?\"","Qiao Lanshu, completely limp in his arms, said in a soft voice, \"It's about Niuwa going to kindergarten. The kindergarten picks up kids at five every afternoon. You definitely won't make it in time, so I'll go pick him up.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded, focusing on his own actions, without further comment.","Actually, this kind of kindergarten could watch the kids until late, no problem.","After all, it was a kindergarten run by the military, so it could be trusted. Besides, many officer families didn’t necessarily have time to pick up their children—they usually sent an orderly to do it.","Qin Yuanzheng said, “If you don’t want to go, I’ll have the orderly do it.”","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. “It’s fine. I have nothing to do anyway...”","Besides, it would be nice to get out and walk a bit every day.","After a moment, Qiao Lanshu suddenly lowered her voice and said, “Your, your hands are even rougher!”","Qin Yuanzheng murmured in a low voice, “We’ve been training a lot recently, pressing down on the gun...”","The couple didn’t say much more. Qin Yuanzheng scooped Qiao Lanshu up in his arms and strode toward the heated brick bed.","Qiao Lanshu was still thinking about Niuwa. “I hope he doesn’t get into fights at kindergarten. I hope he behaves.”","Qin Yuanzheng said nothing—he was busy having his late-night snack."]},{"number":223,"title":"Chapter 223: Guan Wenjun wants to get one step closer.","paragraphs":["The next day, Qin Yuanzheng took Niuwa, who was dressed in new clothes and carrying a new schoolbag, to the kindergarten gate early.","Niuwa stood curiously at the kindergarten entrance, looking at the guard and the kind-faced female staff, his expression a bit hesitant.","Was this school? Would he really be studying here starting today?","Qin Yuanzheng got out of the car, led Niuwa to the kindergarten gate, and chatted briefly with several women responsible for receiving the children.","Then he bent down, looked Niuwa in the eyes, and warned him in a low voice, “Comrade Han Ye, behave in the kindergarten, eat well, listen to the teachers, and don’t run off. If you run out and get snatched by human traffickers again, I won’t come to rescue you. Got it?”","Niuwa immediately puffed out his chest and said, “I know, Dad. I absolutely won’t run around. You can rest assured.”","Qin Yuanzheng had grown numb to this title of “Dad” by now.","Well, if Han Wenlin had no objections, why should he?","This godson was officially acknowledged.","With that thought, he reached out and ruffled Niuwa’s hair again, saying, “Be good. Auntie Qiao will pick you up this afternoon.”","Hearing that Qiao Lanshu would be coming, Niuwa immediately brightened: “Great! I’ll definitely be good!”","Niuwa now really liked his new mother, Qiao Lanshu, and he also liked Sister Shi, because she always made him plenty of buns and big white steamed buns.","Besides, Qiao Lanshu gave him fruit every day, and there was the puppy he loved in the courtyard, as well as his little brother.","He loved his new home now, so he no longer planned to run away.","Qin Yuanzheng had also noticed that over the past two months, Niuwa had been very well-behaved. Even with the yard gate wide open, he never went out, only playing inside.","He had indeed become much more sensible, which Qin Yuanzheng found very reassuring.","So he confidently handed Niuwa over to the female staff at the kindergarten and drove off to the military base.","By the way, it had been some time since Qin Yuanzheng got promoted to brigade commander. His work at the mining area was just about finished, and he probably would be facing a job transfer soon.","He estimated that he would still be transferred within the same military district and wouldn’t have to go to another place.","But nothing was settled yet, so he hadn’t mentioned it to Qiao Lanshu.","After waking up, Qiao Lanshu ate breakfast and then stayed in the room to read and review her studies.","She had actually already gone through the textbooks for middle school and high school once. She had also asked Qin Yuanzheng to borrow many books for her, and she had nearly finished those as well.","Checking the time, the resumption of the college entrance examination was less than a year away. To be safe, she had also found some old exam papers from previous years and worked on several sets every day.","During lunch, Sister Shi suddenly said to Qiao Lanshu, “Xiao Qiao, after lunch, once An’an falls asleep for his nap, I’d like to go home for a visit. It’ll probably take me two or three hours. Would that be all right?”","Sister Shi’s family also lived in Dragon City—her husband and her two sons and one daughter were all at home.","Qin Yuanzheng had long checked on her family situation. They were originally from a village in the Dragon City suburbs, but after her husband found work, the whole family moved into the city.","At first, life for Sister Shi’s family had been very hard because her husband didn’t earn much and the three children were still young.","They lived in the same kind of cramped compound that Zhong Mei now rented, with a family of five squeezed into one room.","Every month, their grain had to be carefully rationed, and they lived on wild vegetable soup. The children were so malnourished they looked gaunt and sallow.","It was only when the children grew older and Sister Shi went out to work as a nanny that the family’s life slowly improved.","Sister Shi was very dedicated. Whether taking care of the baby or cooking and doing housework, she was thorough and attentive.","Qiao Lanshu really liked her and was naturally happy to make things convenient for her.","She nodded and said, “Of course, Sister. Has something happened at home? Do you need any help?”","Sister Shi shook her head helplessly and said, “It’s not a big deal, really. It’s about my eldest son’s job situation. I have to go back and see about it this time.”","Qiao Lanshu remembered Sister Shi mentioning before that her son was planning to spend five hundred yuan to buy a job.","Could you really buy a job with five hundred yuan?","Qiao Lanshu didn’t understand all those intricacies, but she didn’t ask further and simply agreed: “That’s fine, Sister. Go ahead. If there’s something at home, you can come back tomorrow morning instead. I can take care of the baby tonight.”","Sister Shi quickly said, “Oh, no, no need! I’ll be sure to come back before dinner to make the meal for you and the children.”","Qin Yuanzheng was generous, Qiao Lanshu had a good personality, An’an was well-behaved, and Niuwa went to kindergarten. Sister Shi was very satisfied with this employer.","Having worked as a nanny for so many years, she had seen all kinds of employers.","Some families had elderly people and several children—the elderly were hard to deal with, and the kids were a handful. That kind of work was truly exhausting.","Sister Shi cherished this job, so she was afraid of making Qiao Lanshu unhappy.","She absolutely had to come back in time to make dinner tonight.","After all, Qiao Lanshu wasn’t very good at cooking—especially northern-style dishes. But Commander Qin loved noodles, steamed buns, and the like. If she didn’t come back to cook, what if Commander Qin wasn’t satisfied with the meal and blamed her in his heart?","Thinking like this, Sister Shi changed her clothes, said goodbye to Qiao Lanshu, and hurried out the door.","At home alone, Qiao Lanshu coaxed An’an to sleep for his nap, then took out some of Qin Yuanzheng’s undergarments to mend.","Some of Qin Yuanzheng’s underwear had holes in them. Qiao Lanshu thought to herself that since they got married, Qin Yuanzheng had hardly bought any new clothes.","His bedding and sheets were all issued by the military, and so were his clothes and shoes.","Even his undershirts and underwear were provided by the military, since these young men traveled far from home to serve. Most of them were unmarried and had no family nearby to do their mending.","So the military took care of everything.","Even Qin Yuanzheng’s socks were issued by the army.","But even so, Qin Yuanzheng still wore out his clothes quickly. Qiao Lanshu checked and found that most of these things had holes.","She neatly folded the good clothes and put them in one drawer, then gathered the rest—the torn undershirts, underwear, and socks—into a laundry basket. Whenever she had free time, she would take them out to sew.","Qin Yuanzheng’s underwear was very large, with the fabric loose and sagging in the middle—clearly showing his ample endowments in that area.","When washing his clothes, Qiao Lanshu had never looked closely.","Now that she examined them carefully, her face turned red.","She covered An’an with a small blanket, sat down at her desk, and continued mending the clothes.","She also needed to prepare winter clothes for An’an, since he was already over seven months old. Babies at this age grew quickly, changing week by week.","The winter clothes she had made for him last year were already too small.","Qiao Lanshu took out those clothes, and also pulled out two old military overcoats of Qin Yuanzheng’s. She folded them all neatly and set them aside, planning to take them over to Huang Erling when she had the chance, so that Huang Erling could take them apart and make two padded winter jackets and a small cotton quilt for An’an.","Qiao Lanshu had been busy at home until five in the afternoon, but Sister Shi still hadn’t returned.","Qin Yuanzheng hadn’t gotten off work either.","So Qiao Lanshu changed into her outdoor clothes. It was autumn, the wind was strong outside, and the afternoon had turned a bit chilly. She put on a jacket made from an old military uniform, wrapped An’an in a thin blanket, picked him up, and headed out the door.","There were guards outside their courtyard as well—after all, she was the wife of Battalion Commander Qin, which came with some conveniences. Qiao Lanshu went straight to the guard and asked him to drive her to the kindergarten to pick up the child.","The guard immediately said, “Sister-in-law, it’s inconvenient for you to go with the child. We can just pick him up and bring him back.”","Qiao Lanshu thought for a moment and still insisted, “I’ll go too. I promised Niuwa I’d pick him up.”","After all, when she had coaxed Niuwa into going to kindergarten, she had agreed that when he got out of school, she would be the first to pick him up.","So the guard drove the car, taking Qiao Lanshu and An’an to the military district kindergarten.","Although this kindergarten was called a military district kindergarten, it wasn’t actually located in the military district.","It was in a two-story building behind the command headquarters.","At this time, the kindergarten gate was already open. The children were playing in the yard, guards stood at the entrance, and parents lined up one by one to pick up their kids.","Qiao Lanshu got out of the car, handed An’an to the guard, and walked to the kindergarten entrance. The female staff member there recognized Qiao Lanshu.","After all, she was the well-known wife of Battalion Commander Qin and the guardian of Han Wenlin’s kidnapped son—it was hard not to know her.","The female staff member at the entrance smiled and said, “Comrade Qiao, you’re right on time. The kids were just brought out.”","Qiao Lanshu asked nervously, “Comrade, how was my Niuwa today? Did he behave well?”","Had he gotten into fights with other kids, torn apart the classroom, or tried to climb walls or crawl through dog holes to escape?","For the first time sending a child to kindergarten, Qiao Lanshu—even though her biological child wasn’t yet a year old—already understood the worries of a mother.","The female staff member laughed and said, “Niuwa? He did great. He was very obedient and hardworking, especially at mealtime. He was really enthusiastic—ate two white-flour buns, a bowl of millet porridge, and a plate of stir-fried cabbage.”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","Right, he sure could eat. Since he had such an appetite, his mood must have been good.","It seemed Niuwa had a good first day at school and hadn’t caused any trouble.","Qiao Lanshu finally felt relieved.","The kindergarten’s meals were pretty good too—they fed the kids white flour. A little guy like Niuwa could still pack away two buns.","While they were chatting, Niuwa came running out cheerfully with his backpack.","From a distance, he shouted, “Mom!”","Even though he was adopted, hearing him call out “Mom” made Qiao Lanshu’s heart soften.","Qiao Lanshu picked up Niuwa and asked him, “How was kindergarten today? Are you coming back tomorrow?”","The children in this kindergarten ranged widely in age.","Some were as young as one, others as old as six.","The one-year-olds had just learned to walk and didn’t understand anything—they were brought here to be looked after by unfamiliar aunties.","Even though the female staff didn’t dare take any risks, Qiao Lanshu still felt sorry for those kids.","Niuwa, though it was his first day, didn’t seem to have any separation anxiety. Probably, he had long been used to being apart from others.","He said excitedly, “It was fun, really fun. Mom, I want to come again tomorrow.”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","Well, it seemed the only one with separation anxiety was her. She had worried all day for nothing.","Niuwa was taken by Qiao Lanshu into the car. He sat An’an on his lap.","Niuwa started playing with An’an.","Niuwa leaned close to An’an, looked up at Qiao Lanshu, and asked, “Mom, why doesn’t An’an go to kindergarten?”","Qiao Lanshu explained, “Because An’an is still young. He has to be around three before he can go.”","But then Qiao Lanshu thought, next year she would be taking the college entrance exam. If she passed, she’d need to report to school in September next year.","By then, An’an would be about two, so she’d have to ask Sister Shi to help take care of him.","Of course, if Sister Shi wasn’t available, then two-year-old An’an would have to go to kindergarten too.","Niuwa asked again, “Then can my Little Yellow go to kindergarten too?”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. “No, dogs can’t go to kindergarten.”","Niuwa looked disappointed. “Why not? Why can I go but Little Yellow can’t?”","Qiao Lanshu patiently explained, “Because kids are afraid of dogs. Dogs can bite people, so they can’t go to kindergarten.”","Hearing this, Niuwa immediately defended his dog. “Little Yellow is very well-behaved. He doesn’t bite.”","Qiao Lanshu mercilessly refused him. “Still no.”","Then, after a pause, she added, “Chickens can’t go either, ducks can’t go, and neither can the big sheep or the little sheep.”","Niuwa: “...”","Niuwa’s excitement was dampened.","He sighed like a little adult and said, “Alright, Mom, I understand.”","But he didn’t have any friends in kindergarten, and no one to play with.","He really missed An’an, and he also missed Little Yellow. What could he do?","Niuwa put An’an on his lap, kissed his chubby cheek, and whispered, “An’an, would you like to go to kindergarten with big brother?”","An’an, holding a wooden toy tank, grinned at Niuwa, drool running down his chin.","Niuwa sighed again and wiped An’an’s drool with his sleeve.","He was a big brother with a younger brother to take care of now; he had to be responsible!","...","Qiao Lanshu’s day had been calm and fulfilling.","As for Zhong Mei, her day had been pretty interesting too.","She had deliberately not stayed home yesterday and had gone to visit Qiao Lanshu instead.","And just as she had predicted, Guan Wenjun had indeed come to the compound looking for her yesterday.","He had come early in the morning, but naturally, he found no one.","After returning from Zhong Mei’s home on Mid-Autumn Festival, Guan Wenjun had spent the whole day thinking about her. His mind replayed their time together like a movie, scene after scene.","And that mental movie would zoom in and slow down.","In his mind, all he could replay was Zhong Mei’s shy face, her slender waist, and her shy eyes when he held her and kissed her.","He had thought about Zhong Mei all day. That night, on the kang, he tossed and turned restlessly—his body and heart both in turmoil.","As a result, he didn’t fall asleep until very late. And when he did, he dreamed of Zhong Mei again!"]},{"number":224,"title":"Chapter 224: Let's Go Get Our Marriage Certificate","paragraphs":["Guan Wenjun had no idea whether Zhong Mei was playing hard to get with him.","He thought he had been too forward and scared Zhong Mei off, which was why she had deliberately avoided him yesterday.","Because of this, Guan Wenjun went back home and regretted it for quite a while.","He wondered if he had come on too strong and scared the young woman away.","But regardless, since things had already reached this point, he had to take responsibility for Zhong Mei.","So, after thinking it through, Guan Wenjun came straight to the food factory at noon today to wait for her.","The elderly security guard at the factory gate recognized Guan Wenjun, but he still didn't let him in. He said, \"Comrade Guan, wait here at the gate for a moment. I'll go inside and call her out for you.\"","Guan Wenjun was very anxious and said impatiently, \"We're old acquaintances. Why can't you just let me in? I used to be able to walk right in before.\"","The security guard wasn't intimidated and spoke frankly, \"Comrade Guan, you're a section chief now, and before that, you were a committee director, but we have to follow procedure. Let me go find Zhong Mei first and ask her. It won't take long.\"","Guan Wenjun was left speechless.","He used to be the director of the provincial revolutionary committee, so naturally, he could go anywhere—who would dare to mess with the revolutionary committee back then?","But now that he was assigned to the Supply Section, things were different. If he wanted to enter these factories now, he needed a Supply Section pass. Without official paperwork, they wouldn't let him in.","Guan Wenjun was incredibly frustrated but had no choice but to wait at the gate.","The security guard went to the cafeteria and found Zhong Mei.","Zhong Mei was eating alone in the cafeteria.","The cafeteria food was always very plain. Today, they had wild vegetable lump soup, coarse grain steamed buns, and pickled radish.","The portions weren't large, just enough for Zhong Mei to feel about eighty percent full.","Still, she was quite satisfied—at least this was the subsidy provided by the food factory for its workers.","She knew that in some factories, employees had to pay for their meals in the cafeteria. For example, each person had a fixed monthly ration of grain, but the grain wasn't distributed to the workers directly—it was allocated to the cafeteria. The workers ate all three meals there. If someone arrived late and the food was gone, they would go hungry because there was no grain at home.","Take the meal Zhong Mei was eating now. Many of the female workers in the food factory couldn't eat their entire portion themselves.","They would pack their lunch in their lunch boxes to take home and share with their children.","If they had many children, the portions would be even smaller when divided. The lump soup would need extra water to stretch it out, and by the time it was shared among the children, there would be barely any richness left.","This was an era of planned economy, where grain was precious, and everyone was struggling to get by.","Zhong Mei herself had grown up constantly hungry. She had almost never eaten a full meal in her childhood.","Coming to Longcheng and joining the food factory had been the best days she'd had in years.","Zhong Mei put one steamed bun into her pocket, planning to take it home for dinner.","Then she ate the remaining bun, finished the soup and pickled radish, and got up to wash her dishes.","Just then, the security guard came over to her and said, \"Zhong Mei, there's someone at the gate looking for you. It's Section Chief Guan from the Supply Section. Do you want to go see him?\"","Qiao Lanshu had previously asked the security guard to look out for Zhong Mei.","Qiao Lanshu had also given the guard gifts like cigarettes, tea, apples, and persimmons. The guard remembered that well.","So he added, \"If you don't want to see him, you don't have to go out. Don't worry, I'll send him away for you.\"","Sure, he was a section chief. But so what? back then, Director Guan could be unreasonable, but Section Chief Guan can't just throw his weight around.","Zhong Mei wasn't surprised at all when she heard this.","In fact, she felt Guan Wenjun's delay was a bit late. She had expected him to come find her either yesterday afternoon or in the evening.","Zhong Mei quickly washed her bowl and said with a smile to the guard, \"Thank you, Uncle. I'll go out and see him now.\"","The guard nodded. \"All right. If you need any help, just call me.\"","Zhong Mei smiled, repeated her thanks a few times, and headed out.","Meanwhile, Guan Wenjun was getting restless waiting outside the factory gate.","His mind was in turmoil. It had been two days since the afternoon before last, and he still hadn't seen Zhong Mei. How could he not be anxious?","Besides, the braised pork knuckle and potato braised noodles he had packed in his lunch box would taste terrible if they got cold.","Guan Wenjun paced back and forth holding the lunch box. Finally, after ten minutes, he spotted Zhong Mei jogging toward him from a distance.","The moment he saw her, he immediately stood up straight.","And when he saw that she was running over, the tension on his face melted away. The corners of his mouth turned up slightly, and his eyes were now fixed entirely on her.","Zhong Mei jogged up to the gate and said breathlessly, \"Jun Ge, why did you come at this hour?\"","That casual \"Jun Ge\" struck a chord deep in Guan Wenjun's heart.","Well, it seemed like Zhong Mei wasn't angry.","Guan Wenjun was secretly delighted.","The security guard opened the gate, and Zhong Mei stepped out of the factory. They walked together to a shaded spot under a tree across from the factory gate, where they could talk without being easily seen.","Guan Wenjun stared at Zhong Mei for a long moment before asking awkwardly, \"Have... have you eaten?\"","Zhong Mei nodded. \"Yes, I've just finished. And you, Jun Ge?\"","He nodded in return. \"Yeah, I've eaten too.\"","Saying that, he handed her two lunch boxes. \"The food in your factory cafeteria can't be very good, right? Here, I bought this meal for you. Take it and eat it while it's still hot. You're so thin, you need to eat more and put on some weight.\"","Zhong Mei took the lunch boxes a bit shyly and looked at Guan Wenjun without saying a word, just gazing at him with affectionate eyes.","Her stare made him even more nervous. He hesitated for a long time before finally saying, \"About the day before yesterday... I was out of line. You're not mad, are you?\"","Before their kiss the day before yesterday, Guan Wenjun had said things like holding hands, hugging, and kissing were all normal between a couple.","But now, only two days later, he was apologizing.","Zhong Mei found it a little amusing but didn't dare to laugh. She shook her head. \"I'm not mad...\"","She trailed off, still watching him, waiting to see what else he would say.","Then she heard him suddenly declare, \"Zhong Mei, I promise I'll take responsibility for you.\"","He took her hand and said solemnly, \"Zhong Mei, let's get married.\"","Zhong Mei was stunned.","For once, a look of confusion appeared on her face.","She gazed at Guan Wenjun, then at her hand in his.","As soon as Guan Wenjun had spoken those words, he felt a huge sense of relief. He added enthusiastically, nodding to himself, \"Yes, let's get married. Let's go get the marriage certificate now. Then tomorrow, we can move in together.\"","Then they would be a legally married couple, and he could kiss her and do whatever he wanted whenever he wanted.","He still wanted three kids. How could they have three kids if they didn't get married?","He had already pinned Zhong Mei down and kissed her, so he absolutely had to take responsibility for her. Since he was going to take responsibility anyway, why not do it now? Get the marriage certificate earlier, and he could sooner enjoy the privileges of a husband.","Yes, that was it.","Guan Wenjun said this, then looked at Zhong Mei and repeated, \"Zhong Mei, let's get married!\"","Zhong Mei: \"...\"","She was silent for a long time. This truly caught her off guard.","Her conscience rare stirred, and she hesitated as she asked Guan Wenjun, \"Don't you want to... think it over?\""]},{"number":225,"title":"Chapter 225: Getting Married with Certificate","paragraphs":["Zhong Mei looked at Guan Wenjun and said softly, “Getting married is a very serious matter. It’s a lifelong commitment. You’d better think it over. Besides, doesn’t your family even know you’re seeing someone?”","What Zhong Mei said was true, but hearing it made Guan Wenjun feel anxious.","He tightened his grip on Zhong Mei’s hand slightly and stared at her, asking, “Zhong Mei, are you having second thoughts?”","Zhong Mei: “???”","She looked at him with some surprise. “Second thoughts about what? No, I’m not.”","Guan Wenjun’s expression darkened. Frowning, he asked again, “Then has Lai Hongmao come looking for you again?”","Zhong Mei felt a bit speechless. She couldn’t help but laugh and said, “Why are you bringing up Lai Hongmao again? What does he have to do with any of this?”","Guan Wenjun looked at her, his tone tinged with frustration. “Then why won’t you agree to marry me? After what we’ve done...”","He paused briefly, as if a little embarrassed.","Clearing his throat, he added, “Anyway, I have to take responsibility for you. Don’t you want to take responsibility for me?”","Zhong Mei: “...”","Guan Wenjun pressed on, “It’s too late for you to back out now. You have to take responsibility for me. We’ve already kissed. If we don’t get married, no other woman will want me.”","Zhong Mei: “...”","Her right hand was being squeezed so tightly by him that it hurt a little.","She tucked a strand of hair behind her ear and looked at Guan Wenjun with a rather strange expression. Lowering her voice, she said, “If you went on blind dates, plenty of women would be willing to marry you, wouldn’t they?”","After all, Guan Wenjun had such good looks and a great job, earning a decent amount every month.","Guan Wenjun, unaware of her thoughts, persisted stubbornly, “What kind of joke is that? I’ve already swallowed your saliva. Do you think any other woman would want me now?”","Zhong Mei quickly made a shushing gesture, her face reddening. “Keep your voice down! What if someone hears you?”","Listen to him! What was he even saying?","Swallowing her saliva—was that something to brag about? And why did he have to say it so loudly...","Even Zhong Mei, who had seen her share of things, couldn’t help blushing and feeling hot in the ears.","Guan Wenjun squinted at Zhong Mei and lowered his voice, “Zhong Mei, you’ve swallowed my saliva too. Don’t even think about marrying another man. No man would want you either.”","Zhong Mei: “...”","Guan Wenjun paused briefly, then added with a cold laugh, “And forget about Lai Hongmao. If he found out you swallowed my saliva... Hmm, why are you covering my mouth?”","The hand she had pressed over his mouth was also pulled down and held in his grasp.","Zhong Mei was completely exasperated.","Even with her thick skin, she couldn’t bear to hear him keep talking about swallowing saliva.","She lowered her voice and said, “Stop talking about that... and stop mentioning Lai Hongmao. There’s really nothing between us anymore.”","Ever since that day when Lai Hongmao was slapped by Qiao Lanshu and Zhong Mei kicked his bicycle, he had stormed off in a rage.","Still, he had caused trouble for Zhong Mei afterward.","Feeling humiliated—unable to retaliate against Qiao Lanshu for the slap—he decided to take it out on Zhong Mei instead.","Thinking it would be too cowardly to let the loss of face slide, he came to the factory to bother Zhong Mei. But Wang Xue, Deng Weijun, and others worked in the same workshop as Zhong Mei and helped drive Lai Hongmao away with their scolding.","Zhong Mei knew Lai Hongmao wouldn’t let things rest. She suspected he was already plotting something, like reporting her to get her fired.","That was also why she had decided to playfully entice Guan Wenjun—she wanted to marry him as soon as possible.","Judging by how things were going, Guan Wenjun seemed even more eager than she was.","Guan Wenjun stared at Zhong Mei and urged her, “What are you thinking about now? Make up your mind quickly. You need to understand: you can only marry me, because you’ve swallowed my...—”","“Stop it!”","Zhong Mei covered his mouth again and said helplessly, “I get it. You don’t have to keep repeating it over and over.”","Guan Wenjun gazed at her intently. “So, do you agree to marry me?”","At this point, Zhong Mei was more than ready to say yes immediately.","Still, she wanted to explain a few things to him.","Lowering her voice, she said, “Brother Jun, we haven’t known each other long, so you might not know much about my family situation. I can’t go back to my family anymore, and I won’t contact my parents in the future.”","Guan Wenjun nodded. “So you’ve cut ties with them?”","Zhong Mei nodded. “You could say that. But I still have two younger sisters and one younger brother. My brother is young and my parents dote on him, so he’s not my concern. My main worry is my sisters. In the future, I might need to help support them.”","She didn’t dare mention bringing them to Dragon City.","To be honest, if not utterly desperate, she wouldn’t even think of taking them there.","For one thing, Dragon City was too far from home, with a completely different climate and customs. She herself wasn’t fully used to it.","For another, she still hoped her sisters could continue their education and remain in Yangcheng.","But she would definitely help them financially—there was no doubt about that.","She was afraid Guang Wenjun might object or look down on her for it.","But before getting married, she had to tell him this, to avoid arguments over it later.","After all, for the first few years of marriage, she would still rely on him.","Unexpectedly, Guan Wenjun didn’t seem bothered at all.","He said casually, “What’s the big deal? Helping your own sisters is only right. Besides, I’ve been sponsoring five kids from an orphanage—fixed monthly expense of fifty yuan. I’ve been doing it for a year now, and I’ll keep it up until they come of age. When the time comes, don’t fight with me about it, understand?”","Guan Wenjun hadn’t done many good deeds before, but he hadn’t done much bad either.","Sponsoring orphanage children was a genuinely good thing. Fifty yuan a month was no small sum.","Now that he was a section chief, his monthly salary was around one hundred and eighty yuan, plus various allowances.","He couldn’t spend it all on himself alone, so he felt he could keep sponsoring the children.","Zhong Mei had long known about his sponsorship.","After all, Qiao Lanshu had talked him into doing it. Qiao Lanshu had already told Zhong Mei about it.","Having endured hardship herself, Zhong Mei felt sympathy for poor children.","She nodded. “Don’t worry, I definitely won’t fight with you about it.”","Guan Wenjun immediately said, “Then it’s settled. Go back to the factory now and get a letter of introduction. I’ll come find you at four in the afternoon, and we’ll go get our marriage certificate.”","Zhong Mei: “...”","At this point, Zhong Mei had no more objections.","After all, Guan Wenjun was the one rushing to marry her. Later, if he regretted it, there would be no taking it back.","Zhong Mei nodded and smiled. “Alright, I’ll go now.”","Seeing Zhong Mei's enthusiastic demeanor, Guan Wenjun finally managed to regain his smugness.","He suddenly stepped forward, hugged Zhong Mei, patted her head, and said with a smile, \"Don't worry, marrying me—I'll treat you well. I promise you won't regret it.\"","Zhong Mei thought to herself, Just make sure you won't regret it; I definitely won't.","Figuring the time was about right, Guan Wenjun urged Zhong Mei to head back.","He himself was in a rush, eager to get back to the Supply Department to get the letter of introduction.","He couldn't wait to get the marriage certificate and take Zhong Mei home.","A man in his late twenties, who had finally found a suitable partner, no longer wanted to hold back.","As Zhong Mei was about to turn and head back to the food factory, Guan Wenjun suddenly grabbed her arm: \"Hold on.\"","He leaned in close and said in a low voice, \"Let's have a kiss before you go.\"","With that, he planted a kiss on her cheek, giving her a satisfied wave before jogging off with a grin.","Zhong Mei: \"...\"","She wiped the saliva off her face, then couldn't help but laugh.","Truth be told, Guan Wenjun was quite an amusing man.","Still, the letter of introduction didn't come through that quickly.","Zhong Mei's was fast enough—since she was a temporary worker with a low rank, her letter only needed to be issued internally at the food factory and then stamped.","But Guan Wenjun was different. As the head of the Supply Department, he had to submit documents and get approval from higher-ups before the marriage letter could be stamped.","It wasn't as strict as reporting to the military department, but the process still took two days.","Once the letter finally came through with the official seal, Guan Wenjun drove early in the morning to take Zhong Mei for the marriage certificate.","After they got the certificate—a large, award-like document—he finally felt at ease.","At his age, it hadn't been easy to find a wife he truly desired.","Now, Zhong Mei was finally his wife.","Guan Wenjun said cheerfully, \"Come on, I'll help you move your things. Today we're moving you to my place.\"","Guan Wenjun was currently living in the Supply Department's dormitory area.","As a single man, he lived in a large communal room, though he had it all to himself.","After marriage, he could apply for an apartment, similar to the ones Qin Yuanzheng had lived in before.","But the apartment wouldn't be ready just yet.","When Zhong Mei heard this, she said, \"The dormitory area is pretty crowded, isn't it? How about you move in with me first?\"","Zhong Mei added, \"That way, when your apartment is approved, we can move together. What do you think?\"","Guan Wenjun recalled the large compound where Zhong Mei rented a room. The neighbors were simple—three households dispersed in three different directions with a big courtyard between them, not too close together.","Her small room was shabby but tidy and clean. Recalling what had happened in that room the other day, he didn't hesitate long before nodding: \"Fine! We'll move today.\"","They acted quickly—quickly decided to date, quickly decided to get married, and now quickly moved in together.","Guan Wenjun was even more impatient than Zhong Mei.","That very day, he packed his belongings and clothes, carried them over, and bought some candy and cookies. He took Zhong Mei to visit the other two households in the compound, handing out the wedding sweets to introduce themselves and ask for their goodwill.","The elderly woman living in the innermost household was genuinely happy for Zhong Mei and even gave them a basket of vegetables.","Another household, a young couple, gifted them some eggs. The three households got along well and otherwise kept to themselves.","When they returned, Zhong Mei looked at the leftover cookies and candy and asked Guan Wenjun, \"When should we give the sweets to Lanshu? She doesn't know about our marriage yet.\"","Guan Wenjun gazed at Zhong Mei's blushing face and her slender figure, feeling parched with desire.","He was restless.","After days of craving marriage so he could openly share intimate moments with Zhong Mei, all that hustling had finally paid off—and now she wanted to go to Qin Yuanzheng's house?","Guan Wenjun led Zhong Mei back to her small room, his expression serious: \"Zhong Mei, you don't know this, but Qin Yuanzheng once stole a girlfriend from me. There's bad blood between us.\"","Zhong Mei: \"...\"","She folded a newspaper into a square pouch, poured the candy and cookies inside, wrapped it up, and said, \"So what does that have to do with me and Lanshu?\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","She continued, \"From now on, you just don't go over there. I'll go—I want to see Lanshu.\"","That shut him up. He glanced at the sky and said, \"Look, the sun is about to set. Why don't we go another day?\"","Zhong Mei stood up to check the weather outside.","She didn't have a watch, and of course, her home didn't have a clock.","She hadn't bargained with Guan Wenjun over a bride price or the \"three rounds and a sound\" (bicycle, watch, sewing machine, radio).","Not that she didn't care—she was also anxious to get the marriage certificate and worried that if she made too many demands, Guan Wenjun would have to spend time buying things, delaying the process.","Better to get the certificate first and ask for the rest later.","If he dared to refuse, she had ways and means.","So she sighed, \"I can't tell the time just by looking at the sky. I don't even have a watch.\"","Guan Wenjun quickly said, \"Right, watch. Don't worry, I'll get the ticket soon and buy you one! The Shanghai-brand women's watch, eighteen yuan a piece, sold at the department store.\"","As he spoke, he took out his own watch: \"Look at mine.\"","He checked it—it was four in the afternoon. Was that still too early?","He quickly adjusted the dial to 5:40.","Then he handed the watch to Zhong Mei: \"See? It's almost six. Maybe we shouldn't go. They're probably having dinner now, and it'd be awkward to drop in for a meal.\"","Zhong Mei, though clever, hadn't expected this little trick from Guan Wenjun.","So, after looking at the watch, she genuinely thought it was nearly six.","She glanced back outside and muttered, \"Almost six, and the sun is still this harsh?\"","Guan Wenjun walked over and shut the window.","The window was covered with newspaper, so once closed along with the door, the room grew dim.","He put his hand on Zhong Mei's shoulder and whispered, \"That's because this is the north. The timing is different here compared to the south, don't you know?\"","He said seriously, \"In the south, it's already dark by six, but in the north at six, the sun is still blazing. Here, it doesn't get dark until eight. You'll get used to it.\"","With that, he began helping her take off her coat. \"Now, it's time for our wedding night.\"","It has already been a day since we got our marriage certificate, and we’ve openly acknowledged our relationship in front of the neighbors in the courtyard.","If we don’t consummate the marriage soon, he’s going to start making a fuss."]},{"number":226,"title":"Chapter 226: There's no time, let's get on the kang first.","paragraphs":["Guan Wenjun and Zhong Mei still weren't all that familiar with each other.","But they had known each other for a few months now.","Even though they had only been dating for a few days.","Still, they had already kissed, held hands, and even gotten their marriage certificate.","Guan Wenjun immediately pulled Zhong Mei onto the kang and said to her, \"It's getting late, let's get on the kang first.\"","He was about to die of impatience.","To ensure they could properly bond as husband and wife and strengthen their relationship, Guan Wenjun had taken three days of marriage leave, and Zhong Mei had naturally done the same.","What's marriage leave for?","Isn't it meant to make it convenient for couples to get down to business?","Now, facing the impatient Guan Wenjun, Zhong Mei was getting nervous too.","After all, it was her first time, and she was still just a nineteen-year-old girl.","Seeing her shyness, Guan Wenjun realized he would have to take the lead in this marriage.","If he didn't take the initiative, Zhong Mei probably never would in her lifetime.","Guan Wenjun held Zhong Mei's hand and said, \"Don't dawdle, it'll be dark soon.\"","Zhong Mei blushed and scolded him, \"Why are you in such a hurry? Isn't it better to wait until it's dark to get down to business?\"","Guan Wenjun clicked his tongue and looked at her. \"No, we northerners have to do it before dark, or else it's bad luck.\"","Zhong Mei: \"...\"","Zhong Mei was very suspicious of his words.","But she didn't know the northern customs, so she couldn't argue with him.","Guan Wenjun pulled Zhong Mei onto the kang and quickly stripped off his clothes. When he was down to his undershirt, he saw her moving slowly, so he leaned over, pressed her down, and kissed her.","There was nothing else he could do—his wife was too shy, and he had to guide her.","Even though it was his first time too.","This was their second kiss, and both of them were a bit embarrassed.","But the first time is awkward, the second time familiar. When Guan Wenjun's desire flared up, his shyness was pushed aside.","Who would understand that he, at his age, was finally about to lose his virginity?","They kissed on the kang for a long time, and Guan Wenjun stripped off all his clothes. Without a second word, he was ready to get to the main event.","Neither of them had experience, and Zhong Mei actually had no idea what to do.","Guan Wenjun tried multiple times but couldn't get it in... and started to panic.","Panicking, he tried a few more times, and then Zhong Mei sensed something was wrong. She looked up at him.","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","His face flushed deep red. He stared at Zhong Mei, his cheeks burning, and the two of them looked at each other in silence for a long time.","Guan Wenjun stammered an explanation: \"I, I don't think it was that quick. Actually, if you count it, it's been about ten minutes...\"","Before it had really even started, he was already finished—this was a utter disgrace!","He struggled to salvage his image in front of Zhong Mei. \"I was just a little too excited. Give it another try, and I'll definitely do it right!\"","Zhong Mei quickly comforted him, saying, \"It's okay, Brother Jun. Actually, it's nice that you can be quick. I kind of like it that way.\"","Guan Wenjun almost bristled with anger. He said, \"What do you mean you like it quick? Well, sorry, but I can't go fast.\"","Zhong Mei: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun was furious at himself too. This thing really was no good!","It made him lose face in front of his wife.","Severely damaging his majestic image in her eyes!","So Guan Wenjun mustered a fresh resolve and tried again. Luckily, this time he finally held steady and succeeded.","But things weren't going smoothly. After all, it was their first time, and both of them were flustered.","Zhong Mei had been cooperating with him the whole time, since they were already married—husband and wife in the eyes of the law.","Zhong Mei's own family background was troubled, so she had always longed to start a family of her own.","But only at this moment did she realize that building a family also meant enduring things like this.","Because it really hurt.","She gritted her teeth and said to Guan Wenjun, \"Are you... almost done?\"","She couldn't take it much longer.","Guan Wenjun looked at her helplessly and said in a low voice, \"What are you thinking? We haven't even started yet. Just hold on a little longer.\"","They hadn't even really begun, and Zhong Mei was already desperate for it to end.","No way!","Guan Wenjun muttered, \"Don't underestimate me. That last time was a real accident. This time, I'll show you what a real man is!\"","As he spoke, he... entered...","Zhong Mei: \"...\"","Zhong Mei gasped sharply. On instinct, she grabbed a pillow and slammed it against Guan Wenjun's head with all her strength—twice.","Her eyes reddening, she said, \"It hurts!\"","Caught off guard, Guan Wenjun was stunned by the blows.","He snatch the pillow from Zhong Mei's hands and froze, staring at her in shock.","Ever since he became the director of the Provincial Revolutionary Committee, he had barely been hit by anyone.","The last time had been in that alley, when he was trying to buy something from the black market and ran into a woman selling wild grass as wild vegetables.","That woman had done exactly the same thing—hitting him on the head with a basket.","He stared intently at Zhong Mei, and she stared back at him with red-rimmed eyes.","Fortunately, while Guan Wenjun stayed still and talked to her, she felt a bit better—at least the pain subsided.","That kind of pain was truly unbearable.","After a long pause, Guan Wenjun suddenly asked, \"Zhong Mei, have we met before?\"","Zhong Mei: \"...\"","She hesitated, looking at him, and asked, \"Why do you suddenly ask that?\"","Didn't he realize that, under these circumstances, in this position, in this particular moment, such a question ruined the mood?","Guan Wenjun suddenly leaned down, bringing his face close to hers. He looked her over carefully.","\"I remember now. You were the one who broke my head, weren't you? It was you!\"","He then reached out, pinched her cheek, and tilted her chin left and right for a better look.","\"That's right—it was you! And you even cut your hair short!\"","Zhong Mei felt a little guilty. At the same time, her body was uncomfortable, aching with pain.","Because even at a time like this, Guan Wenjun still refused to... pull out.","And on top of that, while talking about all this, his intensity didn't let up—in fact, he grew even harder.","Zhong Mei: \"...\"","She felt utterly helpless.","Guan Wenjun felt as if the sky was falling. The 'enemy' he had been searching for so long had actually been brought home as his wife!","Now she was his legal wife!","Once he recognized Zhong Mei, everything from the past became clear!","When he visited Qiao Lanshu's house, Zhong Mei would hide in her room and refuse to come out.","Whenever he ran into Zhong Mei, she would turn around and flee.","Several times he saw Zhong Mei secretly watching him from the shadows, and he always thought it was because he was too handsome and charming, that Zhong Mei had a secret crush on him.","Guan Wenjun closed his eyes in frustration, pinched Zhong Mei’s chin, and said through gritted teeth, “If you hadn’t kept sneaking glances at me, always sizing me up behind my back, I wouldn’t have misunderstood. If I hadn’t misunderstood, I wouldn’t have noticed you. If I hadn’t noticed you, we wouldn’t have started dating, let alone gotten married!”","Guan Wenjun stared at her, his warm breath brushing against her ear, making her sensitive ear flush faintly red.","He fixed his gaze on Zhong Mei, grinding his teeth. “Zhong Mei, you’ve kept this from me for so long. Has everything between us all this time just been a...”","“I’m sorry.”","Zhong Mei cut him off, her eyes red as she looked at him pleadingly. She cried, “I’m sorry, husband.”","Guan Wenjun’s whole body trembled, goosebumps rising. He let go of Zhong Mei’s hand, leaned back slightly, and stared at her. “What did you just call me?”","Zhong Mei blinked, and a tear rolled down her cheek. She whispered, “Husband. After marriage, don’t you call each other ‘husband’ and ‘wife’ around here?”","Guan Wenjun: “...”","Guan Wenjun was stunned. He savored the word “husband,” feeling a strange tingling sensation all over his body. It was weird...","It made his whole body feel strange, and certain parts even more...","He stared intently at Zhong Mei’s face and said, “Say it again.”","Zhong Mei blinked and quickly called out, “Husband; I’m sorry, I really didn’t mean to...”","Guan Wenjun pointed at her. “Don’t tell me you didn’t recognize me either! You must have recognized me long ago, known I was the one whose head you broke, but you deliberately kept it from me, sneaking around to watch my reaction for fun, right?”","Zhong Mei felt a bit uncomfortable, but at least the pain had eased, and she breathed a small sigh of relief.","She had thought that once Guan Wenjun recognized her, he would immediately... leave, or even demand a divorce.","But now...","He seemed even more worked up?","Zhong Mei frowned first, her eyes red as she looked at Guan Wenjun.","Guan Wenjun trembled, glanced down briefly, and quickly explained, “I, I didn’t move. I just accidentally...”","Zhong Mei took his hand and said softly, “I’m sorry. I did recognize you a long time ago, but I didn’t mean to hide it from you.”","She continued quietly, “I, I just thought you were really great. I couldn’t help wanting to look at you, to get close to you, but I was afraid you’d despise me or hate me...”","Guan Wenjun: “...”","By now, Guan Wenjun was no longer angry. In fact, he began to wonder if he was being too petty—making Zhong Mei cry over such a small matter.","Just then, Zhong Mei slowly shifted her body, trying to push Guan Wenjun away and sit up. She sobbed, “I’m sorry for only telling you this now. Maybe we should just get divorced? Even though I’ve been really happy getting to spend these days with you, if it bothers you, it’s better to part ways.”","Guan Wenjun was stunned, and the words slipped out before he could think: “Divorce just like that? That’s a bit much...”","As he spoke, Zhong Mei had already pushed him away and was starting to sit up.","Seeing that he was about to be ‘returned’...","Guan Wenjun: “!!!”","Guan Wenjun’s face darkened as he pulled Zhong Mei back, saying:","\"I never said I wanted a divorce, so why are you crying? You haven't finished what you started, and you think you can run off? Since you split my head open, now I'll give you a taste of the same, and we'll call it even. Even if it hurts later, you have to take it, you hear me?\"","Zhong Mei just kept covering her eyes and crying, ignoring him.","Guan Wenjun's mood was complicated, extremely complicated.","On one hand, he was angry at Zhong Mei for deceiving him, for hiding it from him for so long.","But on the other hand, he heard her say she cared about him, liked him, and she even called him \"husband.\"","It sent shivers through his whole body.","Over this period, he had really grown fond of Zhong Mei.","Since things had come this far, of course they had to continue. How could they possibly get divorced?","So, Guan Wenjun, with an air of menace, started again...","He had been worried about Zhong Mei feeling uncomfortable before, but now he didn't care, just focused on...","Guan Wenjun had little experience and didn't know much, so he relied entirely on instinct.","At first, Zhong Mei felt uncomfortable, but slowly, her sensations began to... stir...","Guan Wenjun leaned in to look at her and said, \"Call me husband, why stop? You were shouting pretty loud just now, weren't you?\"","Zhong Mei covered her face, feeling like Guan Wenjun was acting like a rascal.","Though, to be fair, he had never been a particularly proper person.","Guan Wenjun gave her backside a slap and growled, \"Call me!\"","Zhong Mei gritted her teeth. Fine, fine, she was in the wrong this time, and she had barely managed to fool him into calming down.","She couldn't let it all fall apart now.","So Zhong Mei did as he asked and called him.","Then, Guan Wenjun, as if he had taken some kind of drug, became completely...","...","From around four in the afternoon until past eight in the evening.","Guan Wenjun finally gave Zhong Mei a real taste of what it meant to be with a true man.","And Zhong Mei truly believed now that last time was an accident.","Because he was anything but quick, he was very enduring.","The sun had already set, and outside it was pitch black.","Guan Wenjun got off the kang, went to the room, and turned on the light.","Zhong Mei lay on the kang, drenched in sweat, her whole body weak and limp. In a low voice, she said to him, \"Don't turn on the light, it costs electricity. Just light the oil lamp.\"","She gestured to the small oil lamp on the table by the kang.","Guan Wenjun was naked, and after flipping the light switch, he strutted back over, hugged Zhong Mei, and said, \"Electricity isn't that expensive. I'll pay for it. Don't be so frugal.\"","Then he kissed her again and said, \"One more round?\"","Zhong Mei was shocked, wanting nothing more than to kick him off the kang.","She shook her head and said, \"No, I'm tired. I'm hungry...\"","Guan Wenjun didn't listen; he pressed on with her again...","Zhong Mei was fuming inside, but she was too exhausted to argue with him.","On top of that, Guan Wenjun kept bringing up that she had split his head open, acting as if he had suffered a grave injustice.","Zhong Mei couldn't argue with him about that because she was indeed in the wrong.","So she was held and tossed around by Guan Wenjun again and again.","By around ten at night, Zhong Mei was completely worn out, and only then did Guan Wenjun stop.","Guan Wenjun lay beside her, smugly saying, \"Alright, wife, I forgive you. From now on, let's live well together, have a few kids, and life will be complete.\"","Zhong Mei really didn't want to deal with him anymore.","She said, \"I'm hungry, and I want water.\"","Guan Wenjun immediately said, \"I'm hungry too, wife. Do you have anything to eat here?\"","Zhong Mei: \"...\"","Zhong Mei was this close to rolling her eyes. She shot him a glare and said, \"Go to the next room, start a fire, and cook some porridge. Neither of us has had dinner yet.\"","Guan Wenjun lay still on the kang, hesitating. \"But, wife, I don't know how to cook. I've never cooked in my life. How about you make something for me?\"","Zhong Mei: \"...\"","Her hand groped around by the head of the kang.","Guan Wenjun kept rambling, \"I'm really hungry. Oh, and water—there's no water in this room, wife. How about you go boil some water for me—\"","A loud thud rang out. Zhong Mei grabbed the rolling pin she kept by the head of the kang for self-defense and slammed it hard against the edge of the kang, pointing at Guan Wenjun. \"Are you going to cook the porridge, or not?\"","If she weren't so exhausted, she would have kicked him off the kang right now.","He was really pushing his luck!","Guan Wenjun was so startled he rolled off the kang, stammering in panic, \"Wait, wife, don't get upset! I'm just saying I don't know how to cook—I never said I wouldn't do it! Why are you so furious...\"","Muttering to himself, he pulled on his pants and, under Zhong Mei's fierce gaze, skulked off to the kitchen next door to light the fire and start cooking, looking utterly pathetic.","While kindling the fire, it slowly dawned on him: Huh, wait a minute—wasn't his wife supposed to be the gentle, devoted, and virtuous type? Why was she so fierce just now?","Could it be that his performance in bed was so bad he'd ticked her off?"]},{"number":227,"title":"Chapter 227: His character is quite decent.","paragraphs":["Guan Wenjun really didn’t know how to cook.","Still, he could manage to light a fire and boil water.","Zhong Mei was hardworking and capable, keeping the kitchen neat, tidy, and spotless.","Guan Wenjun saw that the pot was clean, so he poured two ladles of water into it, then rummaged around everywhere without finding any rice, flour, or oil.","So he went back to the bedroom and asked Zhong Mei, “Wife, where’s our millet? Didn’t you say you wanted millet porridge?”","When Zhong Mei heard him say “our,” she felt some of her anger subside.","This man—despite having many flaws—had a good character, and that was rare and valuable.","A man’s character mattered most; even if feelings faded, a person of good character would still act with conscience.","Zhong Mei lay in bed, turned her head to look at him, and gestured with her chin toward the wooden cabinet against the wall. “It’s in that cabinet. The key is here,” she said, then pulled a key from under her pillow and handed it to him. “Use this to open it.”","The only thing locked in Zhong Mei’s room was that wooden cabinet.","She usually locked both doors of her rooms when she went to work at the factory.","But she had lived through hard times and knew how precious food was, so she never kept it in the kitchen. Instead, she stored it in the cabinet, locked up tight to ensure it wouldn’t be stolen.","Zhong Mei looked tired in the bedcovers.","He couldn’t help thinking back to the taste of their intimate moments earlier.","So he eagerly climbed back onto the kang, pressed kisses on Zhong Mei through the quilt, and then hesitated for a moment before saying, “Wife, how about one more round?”","That’s how newly initiated men were—never satisfied.","But Zhong Mei wasn’t about to indulge him. She smacked his arm and scolded him, “Stop dawdling and go make me something to eat!”","Guan Wenjun: “...”","He frowned and rubbed his arm. His skin was fair, and where Zhong Mei slapped him, a red handprint appeared.","He made a pitiful face and said, “Wife, don’t be so rough. Why do you keep hitting me? It hurts.”","Zhong Mei: “...”","She quietly pulled her hand back and said to Guan Wenjun, “Who told you to be disobedient? I told you to cook the porridge. If I wait for you to make a meal, I’ll starve to death here.”","Guan Wenjun then coaxed her, “Wife, just lie here patiently. Your man will go make you something to eat right now.”","Zhong Mei closed her eyes and nodded.","Guan Wenjun stared at her for a long time, the more he looked, the cuter he found his wife.","She wasn’t any worse than Qin Yuanzheng’s wife, in his opinion.","He took the key, went to unlock the cabinet, and asked, “Wife, why do you lock up the food? Did someone try to steal around here?”","Zhong Mei lay in bed, eyes closed, exhausted, and replied, “Just to be safe. Who knows when a thief might show up? Food is precious. If it gets stolen, I’ll have nothing to eat.”","Guan Wenjun thought she was exaggerating.","But he didn’t argue with her right then.","When he opened the lock, he saw two big red pomegranates, two large apples, and a bag of walnuts in a basket inside—things he had bought for Zhong Mei a few days earlier.","He hadn’t expected her to be so frugal that she hadn’t even finished them yet.","Fortunately, apples and pomegranates could keep well for a week or more without going bad.","He took out the apples and pomegranates and placed them on the table by the kang. “These fruits need to be eaten soon, or they’ll spoil,” he said.","Then he grabbed an apple, took a big crunching bite, and exclaimed, “Mm, really sweet.”","Zhong Mei glanced at him but didn’t respond, going back to sleep.","Guan Wenjun was genuinely hungry. After eating half an apple, he found millet and sweet potatoes in the cabinet, carried them to the adjacent room, and began making sweet potato millet porridge.","He really didn’t know how to cook. The water in the pot was already hot. First, he added firewood to the stove, then scooped half a bowl of millet.","Without washing it, he poured it straight into the pot.","Then he grabbed a sweet potato, inspected it left and right, finally washed it, sliced it into chunks, and threw those in too.","Then he put the lid on and waited for the porridge to cook.","As for kneading dough for steamed buns, making noodles, or stir-frying—he had no clue how to do any of that.","Having some sweet potato porridge wasn’t bad. If worse came to worst, he could go to a state-run restaurant to buy meals or bring back food from the cafeteria for Zhong Mei tomorrow.","It was only then that Guan Wenjun once again realized the value of having a maid.","If he had someone like Auntie Shi, he wouldn’t need to worry about cooking at all.","Come to think of it, should he try to poach Auntie Shi from Qin Yuanzheng?","It might be worth it to take her away entirely. Without someone to cook, the household wouldn’t work.","...","The Auntie Shi that Guan Wenjun was thinking about had also run into trouble these past few days.","The trouble came from her own family.","She had taken leave and gone home, and her husband and son immediately asked her for money.","They wanted five hundred yuan at once.","Auntie Shi hesitated. “Asking for five hundred yuan at once is no small sum. If we take it all out, we’ll have nothing left.”","She had worked all these years, not daring to spend a single penny frivolously, saving up everything.","That money was meant for her sons’ marriages and building houses.","If she gave it all away now to buy her son a job...","Well, if it truly secured a legitimate job, that might be acceptable.","The question was whether the connection was reliable.","Auntie Shi’s husband puffed on his cigarette and said, “Our second son is almost nineteen. He can’t just loaf around at home forever. He needs to find a job, or how will he ever find a wife?”","Her husband was a worker with urban residency. They had three children, and the eldest had responded to the government’s call to go to the countryside.","Now the second son was nineteen, and still unemployed.","He refused to take temporary work, thinking it would make him lose face and make it harder to marry a city girl.","So for some time, he had been pestering them to spend money to buy a job.","The second son added, “Mom, I told you before to ask your employer if they could give me a quota and place me at the mining area. But you wouldn’t! Now I’m asking you for money, and you won’t give it! Are you even my real mother?”","Auntie Shi: “...”","She felt helpless at his words.","But he was still her son, and she was soft-hearted. After hesitating for a moment, she asked, “Did that man say what kind of job five hundred yuan would buy? What unit is it in? Did you ask clearly?”","The second son immediately replied, “I asked. They said the neighboring city is building an airport and has been recruiting workers for a while. Most positions are filled, but if I pay, I can buy a foreman’s job. I’ll sit in an office all day and supervise workers, Mom!","This is a golden opportunity—once in a lifetime. After all, this provincial capital hasn’t built an airport in centuries!”","Auntie Shi was shocked. She asked her husband, “The neighboring city? You mean Wencheng? They’re building an airport there? Why isn’t Longcheng building one?”","Auntie Shi's husband had always been working on construction sites, and he had heard some rumors as well, so he said:","\"I heard six months ago that an airport was going to be built, and our engineering corps would be in charge. But I don't know which regiment will be sent. Still, buying a job should be legitimate. An airport is huge, and it'll need a lot of workers.\"","Hearing her husband say this, and being pestered endlessly by her son,","Auntie Shi finally gave in. She dug out all the family's savings and scraped together five hundred yuan for her son.","Her son took the money and went off to purchase the job.","Auntie Shi didn't stay home long. She told them to send her a message once the job was secured.","Then, before dark, she hurried back to the small courtyard where Qiao Lanshu lived.","She still had to rush to cook dinner for Qiao Lanshu's family."]},{"number":228,"title":"Chapter 228: Expecting a Second Child","paragraphs":["When evening came, the family finished dinner. Qin Yuanzheng took Niuwa to the courtyard to practice boxing.","Qiao Lanshu carried An’an back into the house to rest.","Sister Shi followed them inside and said, “Xiao Qiao, I want to ask you about something.”","Qiao Lanshu placed An’an on the kang, letting him crawl around and play.","An’an was now over eight months old. His legs were strong, and he could stand for short periods, but not for long, so Qiao Lanshu let him crawl on the kang every day.","She sat on the edge of the kang with Sister Shi, watching An’an crawl to keep him from falling off.","As Qiao Lanshu folded and organized the clothes of the family of three, she asked, “Sister Shi, what did you want to ask about?”","Sister Shi played with An’an while speaking in a low voice: “I heard that in Wencheng, the city next to us, they’re going to build an airport. Is that true?”","Qiao Lanshu paused in her folding and thought for a moment.","She hadn’t worked for over half a year, and she didn’t have much contact with the outside world.","But these days, she listened to the radio at home every day, so she knew a lot of news.","She knew that Wencheng already had an airport. After the reform and opening up, when the country transitioned from a planned economy to a market economy, cities would develop rapidly.","Back then, Wencheng—right next to Longcheng—would merge into this province, and Wencheng’s airport would become the province’s first.","At that time, anyone returning to Longcheng would have to fly to Wencheng and then transfer by car.","But for now, the reform and opening up hadn’t happened yet. An airport...","Qiao Lanshu thought it over and said quietly, “Sister Shi, do you mean a helicopter airport? For transporting coal and oil?”","It must be for the convenience of transporting key resources that the state was considering building a helicopter airport.","Sister Shi’s eyes lit up, and she looked at Qiao Lanshu. “So, is the airport really being built?”","Even though Sister Shi trusted her husband and son, she was still worried her son might be scammed.","After all, five hundred yuan was her savings of over a decade.","Though the salary Qin Yuanzheng paid her was quite high, that was only because he was generous.","Her previous wages weren’t high—just over thirty yuan a month—and she had to scrimp and save to raise her kids, with no way to put money aside.","Qiao Lanshu said to Sister Shi, “I’m not sure either. Why don’t I ask Brother Zheng? Wait a moment.”","Sister Shi looked at Qiao Lanshu gratefully. “Thank you, Xiao Qiao.”","Even though Sister Shi had worked as a nanny here for nearly a year, she rarely spoke with Qin Yuanzheng.","After all, Qin Yuanzheng held a high position, and his demeanor was naturally intimidating.","Plus, he was usually busy with work. When he came home, aside from eating and bathing, he spent his time cuddling with Qiao Lanshu in their room.","In the mornings and evenings, he was busy training.","Every time Sister Shi saw him punching the sandbag in the yard, she was terrified.","Now that she needed help, she didn’t dare ask Qin Yuanzheng herself, afraid he might get upset.","So she quietly came to Qiao Lanshu, since Qin Yuanzheng only ever showed a kind face to her.","Qiao Lanshu handed An’an to Sister Shi and walked out of the house.","In the courtyard, a dim yellow light bulb hung in the apple tree, casting its glow.","Qin Yuanzheng had hung a sandbag on the persimmon tree and was practicing boxing with Niuwa.","Niuwa was now over four years old, old enough to start training.","He had inherited Han Wenlin’s large build; even at his young age, his body was as sturdy as a little calf.","His boxing moves already looked practiced and sharp.","Qiao Lanshu stood by and watched for a while, then walked over. “How long have you been at it? Want to rest and have a drink of water?”","Niuwa kept punching while shouting loudly, “Mom, I’m not tired! I can keep going!”","Niuwa wore a pink little vest and yellow shorts.","These were hand-me-downs from their former good neighbor, Huang Erling.","The old clothes that Huang Erling’s daughter had outgrown fit Niuwa perfectly, without needing any alterations.","Niuwa practiced boxing with great effort; his hair was soaked with sweat, and droplets streamed down his cheeks.","Qin Yuanzheng ruffled his head and said, “I was talking to my wife, kid. Why are you answering? Keep practicing!”","Niuwa replied loudly, “Yes, Chief!”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","Qin Yuanzheng grabbed a towel to wipe the sweat from his head, walked over to Qiao Lanshu, and said, “I’m thirsty. Where’s the water?”","Qiao Lanshu shot him a playful glare and said, “Are you being too strict with the child?”","As she spoke, she walked to the table under the eaves, picked up the teapot, and poured him a large glass of water.","Qin Yuanzheng took the water and downed it in one go, then said, “Strict? He likes it himself. If I told him to stop, he’d cry.”","Qiao Lanshu was a bit surprised. She stood there watching Niuwa for a long moment.","Niuwa was indeed practicing very seriously, and he didn’t seem tired at all.","It seemed the boy had found something he truly loved—he didn’t even want to play or rest.","Qiao Lanshu sighed and said, “This kid will definitely amount to something. Director Han will probably send him into the military, right?”","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. “He’s a good prospect, full of energy. If he isn’t managed in the military, he might stir up trouble outside.”","So, to keep things simple, they’d just send him to the military. The state would raise Director Han’s son well.","The couple chatted for a while about Niuwa, then about An’an. After that, Qiao Lanshu brought up the airport in neighboring Wencheng.","When Qin Yuanzheng heard her question, he looked a bit surprised. “You know about the airport in Wencheng too?”","Qiao Lanshu asked, “So, is an airport really being built?”","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. “Yes, a helicopter airport is being built. The designers and engineers are already in place, and Zhao Jiannong has been transferred there.”","Zhao Jiannong was their former neighbor, the battalion commander of the Independent Second Battalion of the Southern Suburb Forest Farm.","Since such an important task was given to him, it seemed he was about to be promoted to deputy regimental commander.","Qin Yuanzheng wasn’t involved in this project, so he didn’t know the specifics, but the construction of the helicopter airport in Wencheng was indeed happening.","Once Qiao Lanshu had it confirmed, she didn’t ask any more questions.","Just then, Niuwa finished his boxing practice, tired. Qin Yuanzheng stood up and said, “I’ll take Niuwa to bathe. He’s been boxing every evening lately, so he goes to bed early and sleeps deeply.”","Sleeping deeply meant he wouldn’t wake up in the middle of the night and come looking for Qiao Lanshu.","Qin Yuanzheng was very pleased with that.","Once Sister Shi had confirmation from Qin Yuanzheng about the airport in Wencheng, she felt relieved.","It seemed her son’s job was secure this time.","Since Niuwa started boxing a few days ago, his boundless energy was finally spent.","His appetite shot up, and his sleep quality was excellent.","After his bath and milk, he fell asleep as soon as he hit the bed.","Qiao Lanshu came in to check on him. Sister Shi was sitting by the bed, mending Niuwa’s clothes. She said softly to Qiao Lanshu, “This little guy has been sleeping so soundly lately. He used to wake up once at night, but these past few days, he hasn’t. He sleeps all the way until dawn.”","Niuwa hadn’t wet the bed recently either. He’d pee before bed just fine, then sleep through until morning, and pee again when he woke up.","Sister Shi sighed and said, “This kid is really easy to take care of.”","When she said this, Sister Shi completely forgot the time before she started practicing boxing when Niu Wa was jumping around and making her so angry she wanted to hit him.","Qiao Lanshu came over with a smile to look at Niu Wa. Niu Wa was lying on the kang, sleeping spread out, with a small blanket covering his belly. His exposed arms and legs looked thick and strong.","Qiao Lanshu reached out and pinched Niu Wa’s leg, saying softly to Sister Shi, “This baby seems even sturdier now.”","His legs seemed thicker?","Sister Shi lowered her voice and said, “It’s better for his arms and legs to be thick; that means more strength and a bigger frame. When he grows up, he’ll be a big, strong man, just like Commander Qin—capable and tough in a fight.”","Qiao Lanshu laughed and said, “Sister, I’ll go rest too. You should get some sleep as well.”","Sister Shi nodded and saw Qiao Lanshu out.","Qiao Lanshu turned off the light in the main room and then went back to her own room.","An’an had been sleeping with her lately and was already asleep.","Qiao Lanshu also checked An’an’s arms and legs, gently pinching his little calf.","Qin Yuanzheng had just come back from his bath and seeing this, he asked, “What’s wrong?”","Qiao Lanshu whispered, “I’m checking if An’an’s arms and legs are thick and strong. Sister Shi said if they are, he’ll have more strength and grow up tall and sturdy. If his legs are too thin, he won’t have much power.”","Qiao Lanshu was mainly worried about her own small frame—she feared An’an might take after her. What if he ended up short and scrawny?","After all, her own father wasn’t very tall and was quite thin.","Qin Yuanzheng came over, pinched An’an’s arms and legs, and laughed. “Don’t worry. This little guy won’t be short. Other kids don’t stand until they’re a year old, but he’s already standing at eight months. His legs are already very strong.”","As he spoke, Qin Yuanzheng pulled Qiao Lanshu into his arms and buried his face in her chest...","He said, “It’s time for husband and wife emotional bonding. Come on, let’s not get on the kang this time, so we don’t wake An’an.”","He directly lifted Qiao Lanshu and sat down with her on a chair.","Qiao Lanshu leaned on him, whispering in his ear, “Zheng Ge, my period hasn’t come for two months.”","Qin Yuanzheng’s hand, buried under her clothes, paused. His expression turned serious as he looked at Qiao Lanshu. “Really?”","Qiao Lanshu covered her mouth and giggled, clearly very happy.","She nodded with a smile, looking at him. “Tomorrow, I’ll ask Sister Shi to accompany me to the hospital for a check-up.”","Qin Yuanzheng: “...”","Earlier, when Qiao Lanshu said she wanted another child, Qin Yuanzheng had been very hesitant.","He did like children, but he liked Qiao Lanshu more.","He didn’t want her to go through the pain and hardship again.","But Qiao Lanshu wanted it—she had long planned to have two children.","So, Qin Yuanzheng had been working very hard, several times a day, making sure the field was thoroughly irrigated.","Maybe he did have some infertility issues, but Qiao Lanshu was definitely an easy-to-conceive type.","He reached out, pressed gently on her belly, and looked at her, asking in a low voice, “How do you feel? Are you really pregnant?”","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. “No special feeling. It’s just that I haven’t had my period for two months. I don’t know what it means.”","Qiao Lanshu hoped she was pregnant. If she were, the baby would be born around May or June next year.","Then, the college entrance exams would resume in July. After that, she’d be busy studying and wouldn’t have time to have children.","Thinking this, Qiao Lanshu felt it wasn’t safe enough—she needed more irrigation.","So, she hugged Qin Yuanzheng, twisted her waist, and said to him, “Zheng Ge, don’t you want it? Why aren’t you moving?”","Qin Yuanzheng: “...”","Of course, Qin Yuanzheng wanted to, but he was also afraid his little wife might truly be pregnant.","So, after thinking for a few seconds, he said, “Alright, let’s go gently. You lie down first, and I’ll take care of it...”","Qin Yuanzheng had this on his mind.","He was very gentle that night, only once, and then deliberately stopped.","This usually lustful man suddenly became abstinent.","He pulled Qiao Lanshu and An’an both into his arms and said softly, “Tomorrow morning, I’ll go with you to the hospital. I can’t rest easy letting someone else accompany you.”","Qin Yuanzheng thought to himself, good thing he hadn’t agreed to go to Wencheng.","Originally, the higher-ups wanted him to handle the airport project in Wencheng.","He refused, citing that his child was still young, and recommended Zhao Jiannong instead.","Although that airport project was very important, there were plenty of talented officers besides him in the engineering corps. Many excellent young officers worked under him.","Commander Li, seeing how hard Qin Yuanzheng had worked over the years and that he finally had a son, considered his situation and didn’t force him to go to Wencheng.","But Commander Li also said that in a few years, when An’an was older, Qin Yuanzheng would definitely be reassigned. When that time came, he wouldn’t be able to refuse.","Thinking about this, Qin Yuanzheng couldn’t sleep until the middle of the night, finally drifting off around two or three in the morning.","Then, he had a dream. He dreamed he was still on a mission in some jungle.","In the dream, he was walking under a giant tree in the jungle.","Suddenly, he heard a swish—a huge, colorful bird flew over his head.","Then, a colorful egg fell from the tree. Qin Yuanzheng instinctively reached out and caught it.","The egg landed in his palm, and the shell cracked open. A little white bird emerged.","When Qin Yuanzheng woke up, he stared at Qiao Lanshu in his arms for a long time.","After a while, he sighed softly. “Could there really be a second child?”","Earlier, when Qiao Lanshu was pregnant with An’an, she had dreamed of a white tiger.","Now it was his turn—he had dreamed of a bird’s egg.","Qiao Lanshu seemed to be sleeping very late recently.","Qin Yuanzheng, after waking up, trained for an hour and then took Niu Wa to kindergarten.","By the time he came back, it was almost nine o’clock. An’an was already awake, playing with the blanket on the kang, then crawling onto Qiao Lanshu’s body to roll around, using her as a slide.","When Qin Yuanzheng entered the room and saw that even with all this ruckus, Qiao Lanshu still had her eyes closed and refused to get up,","He strode over, picked up An’an with one hand. An’an’s thick little legs kicked hard at his face, babbling angrily as if cursing.","Qin Yuanzheng easily pinned both legs with one hand and glared at An’an sternly. “Don’t bully Mom. If you ever roll around on her again, you’ll sleep with Sister Shi.”","Their kang was huge—almost two and a half meters wide—enough for several people.","Usually, An’an slept quietly at one corner.","But now, with Qiao Lanshu pregnant, shouldn’t this little troublemaker be separated from her? What if he crawled onto her belly in the middle of the night and started rolling around?","Qin Yuanzheng held An’an in his arms while warming up his milk, thinking maybe he should make a small bed for the boy.","Though it was possible to have An’an sleep with Sister Shi, An’an was now at an age where he recognized people. He would only sleep with Qiao Lanshu, needing her scent and to hold her arm—otherwise, he wouldn’t settle down.","Thinking this over, Qin Yuanzheng decided he needed to make a small bed for An’an. As soon as he had a free moment, he would draft the design and ask one of the carpenters at the construction site to help build it.","Just then, Qiao Lanshu finally opened her eyes. She had actually woken up much earlier when An’an stirred but had been too exhausted to get up. She yawned, got dressed, and came out of the room. Spotting Sister Shi busy in the kitchen, she walked into the courtyard.","There she saw Qin Yuanzheng holding the chubby, fair-skinned An’an in one arm while punching a sandbag with the other. He said to the child, “Come on, you give one a try for Daddy. Let me see if you’ve got any strength in those little arms.”","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","An’an was still so young—letting him punch a sandbag could easily break his arm."]},{"number":229,"title":"Chapter 229: Hunting in the Mountains","paragraphs":["In the morning, Qin Yuanzheng didn’t go to work. He drove Qiao Lanshu to the hospital.","After the examination, the doctor confirmed, “Congratulations! Comrade Qiao is pregnant again.”","The doctor looked at Qin Yuanzheng with great satisfaction.","This officer, who had once been falsely rumored to be infertile, had finally shed that label.","Married and a father within the same year, two children in three years—at this rate, four in five years wouldn’t be a problem!","The elderly doctor smiled kindly and said, “Two months along. It’s still early, so take rest and care for the pregnancy. Eat more meat and eggs—it’s good for both the mother and the baby.”","The advice was the same as before.","Having been through it once, Qin Yuanzheng was much calmer this time.","He put his arm around Qiao Lanshu as they left the hospital and whispered, “Do you think this one is a girl?”","Qiao Lanshu murmured back, “I have a feeling it is. It feels different from last time. This pregnancy has me especially sleepy.”","Pregnant women often have a sense of these things.","When she was carrying An’an, Qiao Lanshu felt it was a boy.","This time, she felt it was a girl.","And the pregnancy symptoms were different from before.","Last time, she had almost no morning sickness and carried the baby smoothly until birth.","She hadn’t felt particularly tired either.","But this time, she kept nodding off—sleeping during the day and at night, always drowsy.","When she was pregnant with An’an, she had still been working and hadn’t felt this way.","As soon as Qin Yuanzheng heard it might be a daughter, excitement lit up his face. “A daughter is wonderful! I’d love a girl.”","After having An’an, he hadn’t thought much about boys or girls.","But since taking in Niuwa, he had come to realize that boys could be exasperating—always itching for trouble.","He wrapped his arm around Qiao Lanshu’s waist and said softly, “If we have a girl who looks like you, we’re really going to have our hands full.”","Qin Yuanzheng was already worrying. “There are too many rascals around here. We’ll have to keep a sharp eye on her.”","He didn’t want some reckless kid to steal his daughter’s heart.","Thinking further, he added, “I need to keep working hard. When our daughter grows up, I’ll pick an officer from my men to be her match. With him under my watchful eye, he won’t dare to mistreat her.”","After a pause, he continued, “If it comes to it, he can marry into our family...”","Qiao Lanshu interrupted him, “Brother Zheng, she’s only two months along. Aren’t you thinking way too far ahead?”","Qin Yuanzheng opened the car door for her and helped her fasten her seatbelt, his expression serious. “How is that far ahead? Time flies, and they grow up in a blink.”","He looked at Qiao Lanshu, the young wife he had worked so hard to win.","She was only twenty, with fair skin touched with pink, big eyes, and a cherry-like mouth. When she smiled, her eyes curved sweetly, and two little dimples made her especially adorable.","Back when he was trying to find Qiao Lanshu a match, he had felt that few of his men could measure up to her.","If his future daughter wanted a partner, how would he ever choose?","As these thoughts ran through his mind, he suddenly decided a daughter might not be so good after all. Maybe a son would be better.","A son could just run around and grow up. By seventeen or eighteen, he’d be sent to the military camp, and a father’s duty would be mostly done.","As for marrying, he wouldn’t bother with that—if his son had the ability, he’d find a wife himself, just as he had.","All the way home, Qiao Lanshu kept glancing at Qin Yuanzheng. One moment he’d be smiling, the next sighing, then hoping their daughter would arrive soon.","Qiao Lanshu shook her head with a smile and touched her belly, thinking that after this baby, she’d stop. Two children were enough.","The news of Qiao Lanshu’s pregnancy was only shared with Sister Shi. Qin Yuanzheng didn’t tell anyone else, since the baby was still early along. She stayed home every day, reading when she had time, keeping an eye on An’an and Niuwa, and mostly, sleeping.","Every time Qin Yuanzheng came back, Qiao Lanshu was either just waking up or about to go to sleep.","Perplexed, he went to the kitchen to ask Sister Shi, “Sister, why is Xiao Qiao so sleepy this time?”","Sister Shi was kneading dough and chuckled. “Don’t worry, Chief. It’s normal. Young women expecting often love to sleep.”","Qin Yuanzheng frowned. “But she wasn’t this tired when she was pregnant with An’an.”","Sister Shi smiled again. “That’s a good thing! It means this pregnancy is different from the last. This one might be a girl.”","Sister Shi had two sons and a daughter herself, so she knew that pregnancies could vary. She wasn’t concerned about Qiao Lanshu’s constant sleep—as long as she ate well and rested, it was fine, especially since she didn’t have to work.","Hearing this, Qin Yuanzheng felt a bit reassured.","But he was still somewhat worried.","Fortunately, the mining area wasn’t as busy lately. He had gradually handed over his duties to two deputy regimental commanders.","He freed up his time, heading home early each day to pick up Niuwa from kindergarten and then come back to accompany his wife as she slept.","And he meant that literally—along with taking care of the kids.","Sister Shi handled the cooking, prepared nutritious meals for Qiao Lanshu, and tended the vegetable garden, keeping herself quite busy.","Qin Yuanzheng also started raising chickens and ducks near the mining area again, preparing for Qiao Lanshu’s postpartum recovery.","Worried about her nutrition, he set aside time one day, grabbed his rifle, and decided to go hunting in the mountains.","He took Staff Officer Lin, Company Commander Xiao Yang—though Xiao Yang was now a deputy battalion commander—and four guards with him.","The seven of them, armed, headed into the mountain range behind the mining area.","As they walked, Staff Officer Lin said, “Chief, what’s got you suddenly wanting to hunt? Usually, you warn us not to wander into the mountains for no reason, and now you’re going yourself. No more lecturing us from now on.”","Xiao Yang and the guards followed behind, watching the terrain and listening in.","Qin Yuanzheng was in a good mood and didn’t argue with Lin Yucheng.","He just said, “Take a look at Xiao Yang.”","Lin Yucheng turned to Xiao Yang, whose young face broke into a sheepish grin.","Lin Yucheng asked, “What about Xiao Yang?”","Xiao Yang quickly said, “Nothing’s wrong with me, Chief of Staff!”","Lin Yucheng clicked his tongue. “I was asking our chief.”","Qin Yuanzheng snorted. “Xiao Yang knows not to run his mouth.”","Lin Yucheng: “...”","Just then, one of the guards called out, “Hey, there’s a stupid roe deer over there.”","The group quickly raised their hunting rifles and circled in slowly.","Qin Yuanzheng was a sharp shooter and hit the deer with one shot.","Within an hour, they had bagged the roe deer, along with a few pheasants and rabbits.","Lin Yucheng said, “That should be enough, Chief. How about we head back?”","This haul of meat would be plenty for Qin Yuanzheng and his wife to enjoy for several days.","Thinking of this, Staff Officer Lin then asked, “Could it be that Comrade Xiao Qiao is craving meat? Is that why you came in to hunt?”","After all, the supply cooperative hadn’t had any meat recently, so no one had any to eat.","Xiao Yang, who never spoke much, immediately asked, “Really? What kind of meat does sister-in-law want to eat? Is there any in today’s haul?”","Qin Yuanzheng: “...”","Qin Yuanzheng turned to look at them, pointed a finger at them, and then said, “No, she wants to eat wild boar.”","Staff Officer Lin glanced at Xiao Yang.","Xiao Yang clutched his shotgun, his face serious: “Reporting to the colonel, last time I went into the mountains, I came across a wild boar’s nest. I can lead the way.”","Qin Yuanzheng couldn’t help but laugh in exasperation: “You bastard, why didn’t you say so earlier?”","Before Xiao Yang could speak, Lin Yucheng answered instead: “Report! Because he didn’t know his sister-in-law wanted pork.”","The guards burst into laughter.","Xiao Yang looked awkward, hesitating, and Qin Yuanzheng kicked him.","Qin Yuanzheng put on a stern face: “If we don’t bag a wild boar today, none of you are going back!”","The men immediately stood at attention: “Yes, sir!”","After half a day in the mountains, they finally managed to hunt a wild boar.","Qin Yuanzheng had it processed right at the military camp. Hearing that pig liver was good for blood, he took some of the liver and half a side of pork home.","The rest, including the roe deer and pheasants, was all sent to the mess hall to be added to everyone’s meal.","He waited until it was dark before cutting the prepared half-side of pork into several large pieces, placing them in a basket, and loading them onto the car to take home overnight.","It was now autumn, and the weather would only get colder. The pork could be salted and air-dried to last a while.","It would be enough for Qiao Lanshu to eat for over a month.","From now on, whenever there was no meat to be had, he planned to go hunting in the mountains. No matter what, he had to keep his wife and child well-fed and plump.","Qiao Lanshu and Sister Shi were stunned when they saw the basket full of pork.","Sister Shi didn’t dare ask where the meat came from. Hearing Qin Yuanzheng call out, “Sister Shi, take care of salting this meat, hang it up, and don’t let it spoil,” she quickly nodded and went into the kitchen to find coarse salt.","Qiao Lanshu looked at the meat and asked Qin Yuanzheng, “Brother Zheng, where did you get all this meat?”","While taking off his dirty clothes, revealing his sturdy muscles, Qin Yuanzheng whispered in Qiao Lanshu’s ear, “I hunted it in the mountains. What do you think? Pretty impressive, your man, huh?”","Qiao Lanshu looked at him in surprise: “Really?”","Then she gave him a thumbs-up: “Brother Zheng, you’re amazing! You actually hunted a wild boar.”","His little wife’s praise was worth more than anything.","Qin Yuanzheng added, “There’s also a roe deer, a few wild rabbits, and pheasants. Two of the pheasants were still small, so I kept them at the mining area. When your belly gets bigger, I’ll bring them back and stew them with mushrooms for you.”","Qiao Lanshu smiled and nodded: “Okay.”","Truthfully, Qiao Lanshu hadn’t been thinking about eating meat, but seeing that she’d been looking off-color lately, Qin Yuanzheng worried she wasn’t getting enough nutrition, so he had gone hunting.","Her heart moved with gratitude, and in the courtyard, she wrapped her arms around Qin Yuanzheng.","Qin Yuanzheng stretched his arms out and said, “I haven’t showered yet; I’m dirty.”","He was covered in the smell of sweat and felt uncomfortable himself.","But Qiao Lanshu didn’t mind. Leaning against his chest, she smiled and said, “I don’t care. My man is the best.”","Qin Yuanzheng’s heart burned hot. Too bad he had to abstain for now.","Qin Yuanzheng silently sighed, then went to the washroom to take a cold shower.","...","After resting at home for a few days, Qiao Lanshu thought she should go see Zhong Mei and also tell her about her pregnancy.","Besides, Zhong Mei hadn’t visited her in over half a month—far too long. Qiao Lanshu couldn’t help but wonder if something had happened to Zhong Mei.","Luckily, before she could leave, Zhong Mei showed up.","Zhong Mei came with Guan Wenjun.","After Zhong Mei had brought it up several times, Guan Wenjun finally agreed to come out with her.","In the past half-month, Guan Wenjun had just gotten a taste of what a woman was like and was pressing Zhong Mei for physical intimacy every single day.","Even at work, he would find her during lunch and take her to the car, stealing kisses in private.","At night, back home, he was like a wolf hungry for days, bothering her endlessly.","During this time, Zhong Mei used their situation to make quite a few demands of him.","For instance, she asked for a five hundred yuan betrothal gift, and also for him to buy her a bicycle and a watch.","Guan Wenjun thought those were only right—every woman married with those things—and agreed without a second thought.","By now, Zhong Mei had five hundred yuan in her hand and a watch on her arm.","The bicycle hadn’t been bought yet, as Guan Wenjun hadn’t gotten the necessary ticket.","Beyond that, Zhong Mei kept pushing Guan Wenjun to quickly sort out her household registration.","Guan Wenjun also nodded and had already asked someone to handle it these past few days.","When a man is really smitten, he’ll agree to just about anything.","Now Zhong Mei just needed the household registration settled; she had already deposited the five hundred yuan.","When Qiao Lanshu saw them come together, she assumed they were simply dating.","Looking at Zhong Mei, she asked with concern, “Ah Mei, haven’t you been resting well lately? You look so worn out.”","Zhong Mei: “...”","Zhong Mei shot Guan Wenjun a glare.","Guan Wenjun trotted over eagerly, all clingy, and asked, “Wife, were you looking for me?”","Zhong Mei: “...”","Zhong Mei sighed helplessly and said, “I want to talk with Lanshu for a bit. Go amuse yourself.”","Guan Wenjun was now very attached to Zhong Mei; every time he saw her, he wanted to hold her and get cozy on the kang.","Newlyweds—this was the most clingy time for them.","But he felt Zhong Mei wasn’t very clingy toward him, and sometimes even seemed to find him annoying.","Guan Wenjun said, “What is there that I can’t hear?”","Qiao Lanshu was getting confused watching them. She grabbed Zhong Mei’s hand and whispered in the Cantonese dialect of Yangcheng, “What’s going on between you two? Why does he call you his wife?”","Zhong Mei followed Qiao Lanshu inside and said, a little embarrassed, “Lanshu, I actually got my marriage certificate with Guan Wenjun half a month ago. It happened suddenly, and I didn’t have time to tell you.”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","Qiao Lanshu was completely stunned.","She repeated: “You got the certificate?”","Zhong Mei nodded, then said, “We’re already living together. He moved into my rented place. These past few days, I’ve had him help with getting my household registration transferred.”","Qiao Lanshu sighed in admiration: “Looks like Director Guan really likes you, or he wouldn’t have been in such a rush to marry you.”","As for liking or not, Zhong Mei didn’t know.","But she knew Guan Wenjun enjoyed her body a great deal.","Over the last half-month, it was nonstop.","Every time they were alone, he had to cuddle her, touch her here and there, and want to do the deed. He never seemed to tire of it.","Zhong Mei had only been married to him for half a month, yet she was up past midnight every night and going to work in the morning, already starting to look haggard.","Zhong Mei looked at Qiao Lanshu’s rosy cheeks and said to her, “Lanshu, your man is really something—restrained, steady, and he doesn’t wear you out. Oh, that Guan of mine—I’m going to have a serious talk with him.”","If he kept carrying on like that, even Zhong Mei wouldn’t be able to take it much longer.","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","Who said her man didn’t wear her out?","In the early days of their marriage, he’d been even more intense, plain and simple.","It just went to show that Qin Yuanzheng’s cold, stern face could really fool people."]},{"number":230,"title":"Chapter 230: No job, no baby","paragraphs":["After Qiao Lanshu and Zhong Mei entered the room, Guan Wenjun pulled over a small stool and sat outside, chatting with Auntie Shi while secretly eavesdropping on the sounds coming from inside.","Unfortunately, Qiao Lanshu and Zhong Mei were speaking in the Cantonese dialect, and he couldn’t understand a single word.","Seeing his distracted state, Auntie Shi brewed him a pot of tea and brought over a plate of sunflower seeds for him to snack on before heading off to tend the vegetable garden.","Leaning against the window, Guan Wenjun listened to the murmurs inside, but since he couldn’t understand, he scratched his head in frustration.","He stood up and paced near the door, then finally decided to press his face against the doorframe, peeking through the crack to get a better look inside.","Just then, Qin Yuanzheng came back. The moment he stepped into the room, he caught sight of a shady figure pressed against his door, spying. How could he tolerate that?","With a stern expression, he stepped forward and asked, “What are you looking at?”","As he spoke, he grabbed Guan Wenjun by the collar and with a strong pull, threw him outside the room.","Guan Wenjun stumbled, nearly falling to the ground.","Fortunately, he caught himself on the table, saving what little dignity he had left.","Stunned, Guan Wenjun looked at Qin Yuanzheng and said, “Old Qin, what’s wrong with you?”","Qin Yuanzheng frowned at him. “I haven’t even asked yet—why are you pressed up against my door? Peeping on my wife?”","Guan Wenjun was speechless.","He awkwardly stood up, straightening his clothes and nervously rubbing his hands. “Well, uh... to be honest, I’m a bit embarrassed to say...”","Qin Yuanzheng lifted his foot again.","Guan Wenjun jumped aside just in time, then quickly said, “Zhong Mei and I are married! She’s right inside your room now!”","Qin Yuanzheng slowly lowered his raised fist, staring at Guan Wenjun expressionlessly. “You’re married to Zhong Mei?”","Guan Wenjun nodded proudly. “What, you don’t believe I’m married?”","Qin Yuanzheng ignored him and turned to walk back into his room.","Just then, the door opened, and Qiao Lanshu and Zhong Mei came out holding hands. Qin Yuanzheng stopped in his tracks and didn’t move forward.","Qiao Lanshu looked at the two of them and asked, “What happened just now? Director Guan, I thought I heard you scream?”","Guan Wenjun’s face went blank.","He immediately straightened his back and put on a serious expression. “Huh? Did I? I don’t think I screamed. Old Qin just suddenly got physical with me, startled me a bit. It’s not that I can’t handle him, but since we’re good friends, there’s really no need to get rough, right, Old Qin?”","Qin Yuanzheng was utterly speechless.","He said, “What were you doing, pressed up against the door like that?”","Guan Wenjun quickly glanced at Zhong Mei’s expression and hurried to explain, “I was just standing by the door waiting for my wife. I wasn’t pressed up against it. Can you please speak properly?”","As he spoke, he frantically gave Qin Yuanzheng a pleading look.","He had just gotten married—couldn’t he at least save him some face in front of Zhong Mei?","Qin Yuanzheng couldn’t bear it any longer and turned to leave.","Guan Wenjun hurried over to Zhong Mei with a hint of grievance in his voice. \"Honey, why did you stay inside so long? Don’t you know how lonely it is for me to wait out here all by myself?\"","Qiao Lanshu looked at him with a touch of disdain. \"Director Guan, you’re a grown man. If you’re bored, why not find something to do instead of being so clingy?\"","Guan Wenjun quickly defended himself, \"Being clingy between husband and wife? That’s not clingy at all! It just means I care about my wife.\"","Qiao Lanshu was amused; she thought Guan Wenjun’s cheek was really something—completely shameless.","Turning to Zhong Mei, Qiao Lanshu said, \"I’ll go help out in the yard. You two stay and have lunch together today.\"","Zhong Mei understood immediately—Qiao Lanshu was deliberately leaving her alone with Guan Wenjun.","Zhong Mei cast a sidelong glance at Guan Wenjun and said, \"Next time I come over, I’m not bringing you along. You’re just in the way.\"","Guan Wenjun felt hurt. Grabbing Zhong Mei’s hand, he said, \"Honey, we just got married not long ago, and you’re already saying I’m a nuisance?\"","He had only been married for a little over half a month, and the taste of married life had just begun to whet his appetite. He was still eager, still craving.","Right now, he was sticking close to Zhong Mei, wanting to hold her, to hold her hand and gently squeeze it.","He was like a cat in springtime.","But to Zhong Mei, he was not only an eyesore but also a bit of a nuisance.","She whispered, \"I finally managed to have some heart-to-heart with Lanshu. Why were you eavesdropping outside the door?\"","A department head, and still so shameless.","From now on, she wouldn’t come here with him.","Zhong Mei decided that next time she came to see Qiao Lanshu, she’d come alone—no more dragging Guan Wenjun along.","Guan Wenjun squeezed her hand softly and said, \"Even if I was eavesdropping, it didn’t bother you, did it? Besides, I couldn’t understand what you were saying.\"","That last part irritated him.","Zhong Mei was speaking in dialect with Qiao Lanshu—clearly on purpose, to keep him out.","Before he could even mention it, Zhong Mei beat him to it.","He felt uncomfortable and spoke up bluntly, \"Don’t speak in dialect anymore. I don’t understand it.\"","Zhong Mei ignored him, shrugged off his hand, and went to help Qiao Lanshu wash vegetables.","Qiao Lanshu teased her, \"Why did you come over here? Look at your Section Chief Guan—the way he’s looking at you, all puppy-eyed like a little lapdog.\"","Zhong Mei was speechless.","She glanced back at Guan Wenjun and sure enough, he was standing there, looking at her with those longing eyes.","Seeing that expression, Zhong Mei knew he was in heat again.","She sighed in frustration, \"Before we got married, I never imagined he’d be like this—a man who’s like...\"","Her voice trailed off as she let out a deep sigh.","No, she thought, she really couldn’t handle this.","She needed to find something for Guan Wenjun to do; otherwise, if he kept clinging to her all day, she’d be driven crazy.","Seeing Zhong Mei ignoring him, Guan Wenjun had no choice but to approach Qin Yuanzheng.","He pulled a handful of colorful candies from his pocket and offered them, \"Old Qin, have some wedding sweets. Take some of my good luck.\"","Qin Yuanzheng glanced at the bright candies in Guan Wenjun’s hand, took them casually, and slipped them into his pocket. Then he asked, \"When did you get married?\"","Guan Wenjun said proudly, \"We got married half a month ago, and we've had our marriage certificate for eighteen days already.\"","Qin Changfeng recalled what Qiao Lanshu had told him earlier—that Zhong Mei and Guan Wenjun had started dating about half a month ago.","And they already got their marriage certificate?","Qin Yuanzheng sneered at him, \"Didn't expect you to be so eager.\"","Guan Wenjun instantly bristled and shot back, \"Heh, you're not the least bit eager. I was only away on a business trip for a few days, and when I got back, not only had you married a wife, but you’d even applied for a house! If anyone's eager, it’s definitely you.\"","Qin Yuanzheng gave him a look, feeling that Guan Wenjun was just letting off steam today.","But since Guan Wenjun had finally married and held a wedding, Qin Yuanzheng didn’t continue to tease him.","Seeing Qin Yuanzheng fall silent, Guan Wenjun once again boasted, \"The day after tomorrow at 6 p.m., at the State-Owned Restaurant, I’m inviting everyone to the wedding banquet. Make sure you bring your wife and kids along.\"","Qin Yuanzheng replied, \"Alright, don’t forget to order some stewed pork knuckles—my wife loves that.\"","Guan Wenjun magnanimously promised, \"I’ll make sure there’s plenty.\"","During the meal, Qiao Lanshu learned that Zhong Mei’s household registration hadn’t been resolved yet, and she grew a bit anxious. She asked Guan Wenjun, \"Section Chief Guan, when will Zhong Mei’s household registration be transferred over?\"","Guan Wenjun was sitting next to Zhong Mei. He wanted to help her with some food but hesitated, afraid of drawing attention and becoming the subject of jokes.","Hearing Qiao Lanshu’s question, he said, \"It’s being processed now. Should take about seven or eight days. I’ve already been pushing it along.\"","After marriage, transferring household registration became much easier.","Zhong Mei trusted that Guan Wenjun wouldn’t leave her hanging.","Qiao Lanshu then asked, \"What about work? Zhong Mei can’t keep working as a temp forever, right?\"","Temporary work paid too little, and the subsidies weren’t as good as those for regular employees.","It wasn’t easy to become a full-time employee either.","Since Guan Wenjun was a section chief and well-off, if he was willing to pull some strings, he could probably get Zhong Mei a full-time position.","Both Qiao Lanshu and Zhong Mei looked expectantly at Guan Wenjun.","Guan Wenjun casually said, \"Work isn’t urgent, right? Zhong Mei and I just got married. Her main task now is to have a few kids and stay at home to support me and raise the children...\"","With a sharp slap, Zhong Mei put down her chopsticks.","Meeting Zhong Mei’s fierce glare, Guan Wenjun shivered all over and instinctively corrected himself, \"But work is important too. Women can hold up half the sky, after all. So I’ll keep an eye out for work opportunities for her.\"","Qiao Lanshu was utterly speechless with Guan Wenjun. She couldn’t help but say a few more words:","\"Section Chief Guan, you should really discuss these things more with Zhong Mei. After all, you’re husband and wife. If she wants to work, as her husband, you should support her.","Our country supports women working and contributing to society. We can’t ignore the social contributions women make! Women are not limited to just supporting their husbands and raising children. What kind of era is this, still saying things like that? So old-fashioned.\"","Guan Wenjun was left speechless by Qiao Lanshu’s words. Especially since Qin Yuanzheng sat there with a stern face. If he dared to argue with Qiao Lanshu, Qin Yuanzheng would probably kick his ass again.","Zhong Mei also glared at him coldly, her voice sharp: \"Guan Wenjun, I’m really disappointed in you for thinking like that.\"","Guan Wenjun was at a loss for words.","He scratched his head nervously and stammered, \"Ah, I—I didn’t mean it like that...\"","Zhong Mei pressed him, \"Then what do you mean? Having a few kids, being a good wife and mother—how can you say that?\"","Guan Wenjun sighed helplessly, \"I just want kids. You can’t just refuse to have any, can you?\"","Zhong Mei was speechless. She thought about how lately, Guan Wenjun had been acting like he was possessed, always trying to drag her to bed. So that was his real intention—to have children?","Her expression immediately darkened, and she said coldly, \"Until your work is settled, I won’t have any kids for you!\"","Guan Wenjun was speechless again.","He rubbed his temples and said, \"Alright, alright, I get it. It’s just work, right? I’ll find a solution for you. Just don’t be mad, okay?\"","In his mind, Guan Wenjun was puzzled. Before they got married, he never realized Zhong Mei had such a fiery temper.","Wasn’t she gentle, shy, and quite admiring of him?","So why, now that they were married, was this sweet little white rabbit suddenly baring her fangs?","He thought Zhong Mei had been really fierce lately.","He suspected she’d been spoiled by Qiao Lanshu.","After all, Qiao Lanshu was always so tough on him.","After dinner, Guan Wenjun hurriedly took Zhong Mei out, saying, \"It’s getting late, let’s head back.\"","Afraid Zhong Mei would be unhappy and start scolding him again, he quickly added, \"Since we still have some time, let’s go browse the department store. Autumn’s here, and it’s getting cold—I’ll buy you a coat, how about that?\"","Zhong Mei had only been in Longcheng for a few months. She hadn’t even bought autumn clothes yet, let alone winter ones.","The weather was indeed getting colder, and she was planning to buy some fabric to make clothes herself.","Since Guan Wenjun offered to buy for her, of course she was happy about it.","So Zhong Mei said goodbye to Qiao Lanshu, then was hurriedly pulled out the door by Guan Wenjun.","Once outside, Guan Wenjun finally breathed a sigh of relief. He hooked his arm around Zhong Mei’s neck, pulled her close, and whispered, \"Honey, maybe we should come here less often.\"","Zhong Mei frowned, \"You can come less, but I want to come often.\"","Guan Wenjun whispered back, \"Let’s just live our own life. Why do you keep running off to other people’s homes?\"","He thought to himself that finding her a job far away would be a good idea.","If she worked farther away, she wouldn’t be dropping by Qiao Lanshu’s place all the time.","Right now, they still lived too close.","Unexpectedly, he heard Zhong Mei say, \"No way. Lanshu is pregnant. I have to visit her often. Otherwise, it’s boring for her to be stuck at home all day.\"","Guan Wenjun stopped in his tracks, his expression a mix of shock and disbelief: \"What? Comrade Xiao Qiao’s pregnant again?\"","Zhong Mei was startled by his loud voice and elbowed him, whispering, \"Why are you shouting? There are people around. Keep your voice down. Lanshu said the pregnancy is still early. She hasn’t told anyone else yet.\"","Guan Wenjun’s heart was a mess of envy, jealousy, and resentment.","He obediently lowered his voice and said, “You know, Qin Yuanzheng originally had infertility issues, right? A man who couldn’t have children finally manages to have a son. I guess we can just say he earned some good karma, and heaven rewarded him with a child.","But how old is his son? Not even a year yet, right? And now his wife is pregnant again? That means he’s about to have two kids? If this keeps up, in four years he’ll have three, in five years four, and in six years five...”","The more he spoke, the more distressed Guan Wenjun became.","He grabbed Zhong Mei’s hand and pressed it against his chest, wincing as he said, “Honey, I don’t feel well here. I’m uncomfortable.”","Zhong Mei rolled her eyes at him and coldly pulled her hand back. “What does it matter to you how many kids they have? Why are you so concerned about them?”","Guan Wenjun sneered, “What else could it be? Because Qin Yuanzheng is my mortal enemy!”","As he spoke, he grabbed Zhong Mei’s hand and hurried forward, talking as they walked, “Enough of that, honey. Let’s get back and start our own baby-making plan. We’ll work hard together and have twins for our first—then we’ll surpass Qin Yuanzheng in no time!”","Zhong Mei thought Guan Wenjun was crazy.","She said, “Find me a job, or else...”","Guan Wenjun quickly said, “I know, I know, I’ll definitely get you a good job. Then you can focus on having two... no, three kids for me!”","Zhong Mei rolled her eyes again, too tired to argue.","She wasn’t against having children herself, but she didn’t want too many—just like when she was a kid. Her parents had four kids all at once, and when she left home, her mother was pregnant again.","By now, the fifth child was probably born.","They were so poor they could barely afford food, yet they kept having kids.","No one cared for them after they were born. As the eldest, she had to be both sister and mother, raising two younger sisters and a younger brother.","Those hard times were something she didn’t even want to remember.","She would never let her own children live like that.","She shared the same idea as Qiao Lanshu—at most, two kids.","But she wouldn’t tell Guan Wenjun that. After all, he wanted three.","What if she told him and he refused to find her a job?","Men were like that sometimes—sometimes you had to coax them, sometimes you had to trick them, but you could never let them get too full of themselves, or they’d think they could conquer the world.","Guan Wenjun didn’t care about any of that anymore. Once they got home, he eagerly pulled Zhong Mei into bed. “Come on, honey, I’m a little impatient. You take off your clothes yourself.”","Zhong Mei: “...”"]},{"number":231,"title":"Chapter 231: Five Hundred Bucks Down the Drain","paragraphs":["Ever since Auntie Shi heard that an airport was being built in Wencheng, she started waiting every day for her son to send her news. But she waited and waited; over half a month passed, and still no message came from either her son or her husband.","Worried sick, Auntie Shi asked Qiao Lanshu for another two hours off. Qiao Lanshu was pregnant and often felt sleepy, so she took An'an for a nap and told Auntie Shi to just come back before dark.","Auntie Shi quickly grabbed a vegetable basket, filled it with some greens she had grown herself, and hurried home.","When she got back, her husband, son, and daughter were all there.","Seeing her come in, her son looked a bit guilty.","Auntie Shi asked, \"How did the job thing go? When are you reporting for duty?\"","Her son hung his head and said, \"The job didn't work out.\"","Auntie Shi: \"...\"","Her heart sank. She pressed further, \"And the money? That five hundred yuan—did you get it back or not?\"","Her son said impatiently, \"No! Mom, five hundred isn't enough. They said jobs are scarce now, and everyone's looking. The prices aren't what they used to be. For a foreman's job now, you need at least eight hundred. My five hundred would only get me some ordinary labor job...\"","Then, sounding annoyed, he added, \"A few days ago, they arranged for me to start, but it wasn't a good job. They made me haul bricks. It was too exhausting, I couldn't take it, so I came back.\"","Auntie Shi: \"...\"","She exchanged a look with her husband, who was smoking his pipe with a worried expression.","Clearly, the Old Man had known about all this all along, but he couldn't argue with their son, so he just let him come home and laze around.","Auntie Shi was nearly fuming. She couldn't help scolding her son:","\"I found you a temporary job before, and you turned up your nose at it—said it wasn't respectable, the pay was too low, and it made it hard to find a girlfriend. So this time, I gave you money to pull some strings for a proper job. How could you come back so easily? At least you should have gotten the money back! That was five hundred yuan!\"","Five hundred yuan—she had saved it up through all sorts of hardship. Money wasn't easy to come by. She and her husband had scrimped and saved, one person's earnings going to food and expenses, the other's to savings, just to scrape together that five hundred.","And now her son had taken that money to \"buy\" a job. They had promised him a foreman's position, but when he got to the worksite, it turned out to be manual brick-hauling. He quit after two days.","And he hadn't even asked for the money back.","Auntie Shi stared at her son, her eyes red with anger.","Her son, still stubborn, said:","\"Mom, it's all your fault for not helping me. If you'd just gone to that brigade commander and asked him to get me a job at the mining area, it would have been as easy as a word from him! He's a brigade commander! You have such a big connection and you won't use it, but you make me go pay someone else for a job. Who do I even know? They all look down on me for having no backing and give me the cold shoulder.\"","Auntie Shi was trembling with rage. \"Your mother is just a nanny! And you know he's a brigade commander—do you really think he's going to help me? I don't have that kind of face.\"","She paced around the room a few times, then asked, \"Who did you give that five hundred yuan to? Take us there right now. We'll go ask for the money back.\"","The Old Man put down his pipe and said gravely,","\"Son, we really ought to get that money back. After all, you didn't take the job, did you? Five hundred yuan—if we get it back, we can still look into other connections for you later. If we don't, then the next time there's an opportunity, your mother and I won't have the money to help.\"","The couple took turns reasoning with him, and finally their son nodded, though still reluctant. \"But I already handed over the money, and I reported for the job. Now going back to ask for a refund—where's my dignity in that? How am I supposed to hold my head up in the future?\"","Auntie Shi was so mad she wanted to smack him. \"Is your face worth five hundred yuan? Stop talking nonsense. Let's go before it gets dark and get our money back!\"","...","Qiao Lanshu woke up from her nap and found it was already four in the afternoon. An'an had woken up a little earlier and was playing on the kang by herself.","Qiao Lanshu had some water, prepared a bottle of milk for An'an, and then carried her out to the courtyard for a stroll.","It was already five o'clock, and Auntie Shi still hadn't returned. So Qiao Lanshu, holding An'an, called the guard outside the yard and went to the kindergarten to pick up Niuwa.","Qin Yuanzheng happened to be there picking up Niuwa too, so the couple brought the two kids home together.","Qin Yuanzheng asked Qiao Lanshu, \"Why did you bring An'an out? Isn't Auntie Shi home?\"","Qiao Lanshu said, \"Auntie Shi asked to go home this afternoon, but she hasn't come back yet. I'm not sure if something's come up at home.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was easygoing. Auntie Shi was a good person, thorough in her work, and he wouldn't fault her for being late.","He squeezed Qiao Lanshu's hand. \"Are you hungry? What do you want for dinner? I'll cook for you.\"","Ever since they got married, and even before they hired Auntie Shi, Qin Yuanzheng had always been the one to cook.","Before Qiao Lanshu could answer, Niuwa piped up loudly, \"I want chive flower rolls! I'll have three! And I want dough-drop soup, cucumber salad, pickled radish, and steamed egg custard.\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at him with disdain. \"That much? Can you even finish all that?\"","Niuwa nodded vigorously. \"I can! I'm so hungry. The aunties at kindergarten won't let me eat enough. I ask for seconds, but they say no. They're so mean.\"","Qin Yuanzheng snorted. \"That's because you already ate three bowls of rice. They didn't dare let you keep eating, for fear you'd burst your belly. Comrade Han Ye, listen to me: from now on, don't eat so much, or you won't be Niuwa anymore—you'll be Piggy. Do you know what a pig looks like? White and fat, and come New Year, it gets butchered for meat.\"","Niuwa: \"...\"","Niuwa swallowed nervously and hugged Qiao Lanshu's arm, whispering, \"Mom, I'm not a pig. I'm not fat at all.\"","Qiao Lanshu laughed and ruffled Niuwa's head. \"Of course, our Niuwa isn't fat at all. But still, try to control yourself a bit. Three bowls is plenty. We don't need to ask for more, alright?\"","Niuwa hesitated, then nodded.","He didn't understand. Was four bowls really that much?","But he felt like he could still eat. He was always hungry.","In fact, Qiao Lanshu had been observing Niuwa. She thought his big appetite might be natural.","Niuwa was just born liking to eat more than other kids, with a bigger appetite.","Also, it probably had a lot to do with his activity level.","Niuwa was naturally a high-energy kid. Every day he'd be racing around with the dog, jumping all over the place without ever getting tired.","And now, every evening, Qin Yuanzheng took him to practice boxing for over an hour.","With such high energy expenditure, of course he needed to eat and sleep more.","Plus, Niuwa was already half a head taller than other kids his age—he was shooting up fast.","Qiao Lanshu gently ruffled Niuwa’s hair and said to Qin Yuanzheng, “Niuwa is growing fast, so it’s only natural he eats a lot. He can have more during the day, but less at night. A bottle of milk formula before bed and another in the morning should be enough for his nutrition.”","When Qin Yuanzheng heard this, he looked at Niuwa again and let out a long sigh after a moment.","He said, “Who knows when Han Wenlin will finally catch those Zheng siblings and bring them back? This can’t go on forever. Leaving such a handful of a son with us while he’s off living it up somewhere.”","Qin Yuanzheng wasn’t really complaining about Niuwa.","He was mostly worried about Qiao Lanshu.","She had to take care of An’an, was pregnant, and already exhausted—and now she had to look after Niuwa too.","Still, Niuwa had been fairly easygoing lately and was very obedient during boxing practice, which made Qin Yuanzheng rather fond of him.","On that note, Qin Yuanzheng suddenly added, “Oh, by the way, the house Han Wenlin applied for has been approved. It’s a small, standalone courtyard in the housing authority’s residential complex. Once Han Wenlin gets back, Niuwa can move in there.”","As soon as Niuwa heard this, he said anxiously, “Ah, who is Han Wenlin? I don’t want to live with him. I want to live with my Mother Qiao!”","Qin Yuanzheng: “...”","Qiao Lanshu, holding An’an in one arm and Niuwa in the other, felt a little helpless too.","If Niuwa was acting like this, Han Wenlin must be even more miserable.","His own son would rather claim someone else as his parents than go back with him.","Putting herself in his shoes, Qiao Lanshu found it hard to accept.","The family of four returned to their small courtyard.","Auntie Shi still hadn’t come back, so Qin Yuanzheng changed his clothes, washed his hands, and started cooking.","Even though he kept saying he resented Niuwa and wanted to send him away, as soon as they were home, he went out to cut a few bunches of chives, came back to knead dough, and began steaming chive flower rolls.","Worried that Niuwa might overeat again, he deliberately made the rolls smaller—each one tiny and round, only the size of Niuwa’s fist. Qiao Lanshu couldn’t help but praise him, “Brother Zheng, you’re amazing! The flower rolls you make are so beautiful.”","Qin Yuanzheng found himself working even harder after her compliments.","He steamed the flower rolls, made drop soup, and prepared smashed cucumber salad. He skipped the pickled radish because the radishes Auntie Shi had planted were still too small to harvest.","At dinner, Qiao Lanshu turned on the electric light. Watching the darkening sky, she said worriedly, “It’s almost seven in the evening. Why isn’t Auntie Shi back yet? Nothing’s happened to her, has it?”","Qin Yuanzheng set the dishes on the table, glanced outside, and replied, “It’s fine, don’t worry. If she’s still not back by nightfall, I’ll have someone go to her house and ask.”","He had already looked into Auntie Shi’s home address, how many people were in her family, and what work they did. It wouldn’t be hard to send someone to check.","Qiao Lanshu nodded and ate with the children. After the meal, she first helped An’an freshen up and then put him to bed.","Qin Yuanzheng, on the other hand, took Niuwa to wash the dishes and mop the floor. Then he led Niuwa to the yard for training—punching the sandbag and running.","Around eight o’clock in the evening, the guard from the front gate of their compound came by to deliver a message: “Brigade Commander Qin, someone just came by to say your housekeeper had an urgent family matter tonight and can’t return. She’ll be back by noon tomorrow.”","When Qin Yuanzheng heard this, he asked, “Did the person say what happened at Auntie Shi’s home?”","The guard shook his head. “No, they only said those two lines. Commander, shall we go check on Auntie Shi’s place?”","Qin Yuanzheng was silent for a moment, then shook his head. “No need. Since she said so, there’s probably nothing serious. I’ll ask her when she returns tomorrow. You can go back now.”","The guard turned and left.","Qin Yuanzheng locked the courtyard gate and put out the fire beneath the stove where food was kept warm.","Then he took Niuwa to bathe.","With Auntie Shi gone for the night, Qin Yuanzheng would have to put Niuwa to bed himself.","Looking at the grimy boy beside him, Qin Yuanzheng sighed silently to himself."]},{"number":232,"title":"Chapter 232: Another Year Has Passed","paragraphs":["Auntie Shi's side had indeed stirred up trouble.","She and her husband, along with their son, went to demand money from the intermediary who had supposedly been helping to secure a job.","That intermediary was a young thug—only a good-for-nothing like Auntie Shi's son would have known the likes of him.","Getting money out of that sort of person was nearly impossible.","So the two sides started arguing. Auntie Shi's husband lost his temper and picked a fight with the man, only to get beaten badly in response.","In the end, the whole family was caught by the patrol team and locked up in the police station.","When Qiao Lanshu woke up the next morning, Auntie Shi was nowhere to be seen.","She stepped out of the house and spotted Qin Yuanzheng holding An'an with one arm while watering the vegetable garden in the yard with the other.","An'an had already been changed into a clean diaper and was clutching a bottle of milk to drink.","The baby loved being held by his father—his father's arms were strong and sturdy, making it very comfortable to lie there drinking milk.","Qiao Lanshu walked to the doorway and stood under the eaves, watching quietly for a while before stepping outside. She looked around and asked curiously, \"Brother Zheng, Auntie Shi isn't back yet?\"","As soon as Qin Yuanzheng saw her come out, he immediately carried An'an over and said, \"You're up? It's windy today—go inside and put on more clothes.\"","It was already late autumn, and the weather was getting colder. Qin Yuanzheng worried that Qiao Lanshu might catch a chill.","Qiao Lanshu laughed and said, \"I'm not cold. I'm wearing a cotton jacket.\"","Qin Yuanzheng held An'an with one arm and wrapped the other around Qiao Lanshu as the family of three walked back inside. He said, \"Auntie Shi’s family had some trouble. This morning, someone from the police station came by and told me that last night, her family got into a conflict with others and a fight broke out. I'll head over in a while to check on it.\"","It was Deputy Police Director Li Jianlin who had sent word.","Deputy Director Li knew Auntie Shi and was aware she worked as a nanny in Qin Yuanzheng's home.","Worried that the incident might be connected to Qin Yuanzheng, he kindly arranged for someone to deliver the message.","As for whether he went or not, that was up to Qin Yuanzheng himself. After all, a Brigadier Commander like him was hard for common folk to meet. It wasn't really necessary for him to go all the way to the police station just for a nanny—sending one of his adjutants would have been enough.","Qiao Lanshu looked a bit worried. \"Auntie Shi is a decent person. There’s no reason she’d start a fight for no cause.\"","Qin Yuanzheng thought the same, but he would have to go see the details for himself.","Auntie Shi was an excellent nanny, and Qin Yuanzheng was satisfied with her work. Besides, Qiao Lanshu was pregnant now and needed extra care.","So Qin Yuanzheng didn’t want anything to happen to Auntie Shi. This time, he was willing to go in person to ask questions and help resolve her problem.","Breakfast was also made by Qin Yuanzheng—simple pumpkin millet porridge, steamed chive rolls left over from last night, and a plate of pickled sour vegetables.","Recently, Qiao Lanshu had been feeling nauseous and had a poor appetite, so Auntie Shi had pickled some vegetables. They could be eaten raw or used to make stewed sour cabbage; either way, they were spicy, sour, and refreshing.","After finishing their meal, Qin Yuanzheng tidied up the house, had Qiao Lanshu hold An'an and rest at home, locked the door, and drove to the police station.","At the station, Auntie Shi, her husband, and their son had been detained overnight, and none of them had gotten any sleep.","The son, seeing his father's bruised and battered face from the beating, finally realized this time he had done something wrong.","He hung his head and said, \"Dad, Mom, maybe we shouldn't take this money.\"","Auntie Shi kept a cold face and said nothing.","Her husband sighed and said, \"Five hundred yuan—do you know how long it took our family to save up five hundred yuan?\"","Their son said gloomily, \"But there's nothing we can do about him. He's got connections. His cousin is the section chief of the Supply Department—he's got a lot of power. Otherwise, how could he make money by selling jobs?\"","\"I told you last night: let's forget the money and not go. But you insisted on going. Now look—you got beaten up, and then locked up in the police station. What are we going to do now? Are we going to be sent to labor reform?\"","As Auntie Shi listened, she gradually felt something was off. She turned to stare at her son and asked him, \"What did you say? His cousin is the section chief of the Supply Department? Are you sure?\"","Wasn't the Supply Department's section chief Director Guan?","Did Guan have a cousin who earned money by selling jobs?","Did Qiao Lanshu know? Did Brigade Commander Qin know?","So, when Qin Yuanzheng came to the police station in person to meet Auntie Shi, she told him the whole story in detail.","Of course, she also mentioned that the Supply Department section chief was the scammer's cousin.","Qin Yuanzheng told Auntie Shi not to worry, to stay in the police station for a couple of days, and that he would look into the matter.","Deputy Director Li overheard all this and quickly asked Qin Yuanzheng, \"Brigade Commander Qin, was this really done with Section Chief Guan's... I mean, Section Chief Guan's approval? Is he really making money this way?\"","No way—back then, Guan Wenjun took on all kinds of missions to get that job, even risking his life escorting Han Wenlin to Long City.","How long had he been in the position now? Hadn't even reached two months yet, had he?","Was he already making money by selling jobs?","Qin Yuanzheng walked to the entrance of the police station, remained silent for a couple of seconds, then said, \"It's unlikely. Section Chief Guan is newly married, and the couple is still in the honeymoon phase—he probably doesn't have time for this.\"","And during his earlier time at the Revolutionary Committee, it would have been even more impossible.","So the most likely possibility could only be the former Supply Department section chief, Zheng Weigong.","After Han Wenlin arrived safely in Long City and officially registered at the police station, Zheng Weigong fled with his sister.","The fact that Han Wenlin still hadn't caught him showed just how good they were at hiding—they had probably planned multiple escape routes long ago.","Thinking of this, Qin Yuanzheng asked Li Jianlin, \"What background does that guy who sells jobs have?\"","Li Jianlin replied, \"He's just a local street punk—loafs around all day, gets into fights, hangs out drinking and playing with a bunch of shady friends... Come to think of it, I had people look into him. He has made a lot of money selling jobs. Before this, all the jobs he arranged worked out, and no one came back to cause trouble.\"","In other words, the jobs he arranged before were reliable—expensive, sure, but they actually got people in.","But now it was different. Why?","It must be because Zheng Weigong and his sister had fled, and without their backing, he couldn't find good jobs anymore.","Qin Yuanzheng thought that since Han Wenlin had been unable to track down Zheng Weigong and his sister, maybe they could start with this guy.","Thinking of this, Qin Yuanzheng said to Li Jianlin, \"You should quickly send a telegram to Han Wenlin and ask him to come back with his men. It's very likely that Zheng Weigong hasn't escaped. He probably is still hiding in Longcheng or in the neighboring Wencheng. Let Han Wenlin start the investigation from this young man.\"","Han Wenlin had chased after the suspect based on certain clues before. However, now it seemed that Zheng Weigong might have spread false information.","Everyone had been deceived by him, and he might be hiding somewhere in the vicinity at this moment.","Qin Yuanzheng inclined to the idea that Zheng Weigong was hiding in the neighboring Wencheng.","Otherwise, this loafer wouldn't be selling jobs in Wencheng. According to the investigation, he used to sell jobs on construction sites in Longcheng. The prices were not low, ranging from 300 to 500 yuan.","After arranging this matter, Qin Yuanzheng told Li Jianlin to release Auntie Shi and her family of three.","When Auntie Shi's son saw Qin Yuanzheng, he didn't dare to say a word. He didn't even dare to look up at Qin Yuanzheng.","Because Qin Yuanzheng was staring at him with a serious look, which scared him half to death. He kept hiding behind Auntie Shi and didn't dare to show his face.","Qin Yuanzheng really had never seen such a good - for - nothing young man.","He saw that Auntie Shi and her husband had not only lost 500 yuan for this son, but also the old man, being of advanced age, had been beaten up. It was really pitiful.","Having become a parent really made a difference.","In the past, when he saw such things, he wouldn't have much empathy, but now?","He thought of his own son, An'an.","If An'an grew up to be as good - for - nothing in the future, Qiao Lanshu didn't know how much trouble she would have to take.","Auntie Shi and her husband thanked Qin Yuanzheng profusely. Auntie Shi said, \"Chief Qin, you've really gone out of your way for us. If it weren't for you, we wouldn't know what to do.\"","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head. \"Ma'am, you're welcome. After all, you're the nanny of my family. When something happens, of course I'll help. As for the 500 yuan, I'll try my best to get it back for you. But you don't have to be in a hurry. This matter won't be resolved quickly. You just wait for the news at home.\"","Since Qin Yuanzheng had said so, Auntie Shi naturally trusted him.","If Qin Yuanzheng said he could get the money back, he definitely could.","Auntie Shi's eyes were red with gratitude. \"Thank you, thank you, Chief.\"","Qin Yuanzheng glanced at Auntie Shi's son again and decided to give her a hand. He said, \"I can make a call for you at the Wencheng Airport and let your son go there for a try. But in the beginning, he'll surely have to start from the basics, like carrying bricks. Can he do it?\"","As Qin Yuanzheng spoke, he stared sternly at Auntie Shi's son.","Auntie Shi and her husband turned to look at their son.","Auntie Shi was a bit anxious. What a good opportunity this was! With Qin Yuanzheng making the call himself, there was no need to mention the future prospects.","Not to mention anything else, the people at the construction site wouldn't bully her son.","What was wrong with carrying bricks? Auntie Shi thought there was nothing wrong with it. So what if it was hard and tiring?","Who didn't have a hard and tiring job?","To her surprise, her son was still hesitating!","Because he simply didn't want to carry bricks!","If he had wanted to carry bricks, the 500 - yuan job he bought would have been a brick - carrying job. He could have just stayed and done it then, so why did he come back?","Seeing that her son didn't want to go, Auntie Shi was so angry that she reached out and hit him. She scolded him in a low voice, \"Hurry up and thank Brigade Commander Qin! He's willing to give you this face and help you out, and you're being so picky!\"","The son whispered, \"Mom, I don't want to carry bricks...\"","Auntie Shi was so angry that she hit her son several more times, this time putting all her strength into it, making a thumping sound on his back.","Qin Yuanzheng said sternly to them, \"Then it's settled. Three days later, you'll report to the construction site of Wencheng Airport.\"","Then he added a reminder, \"Since I've already made arrangements, you must go. Otherwise, I'll have you tied up and taken there.\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at Auntie Shi's son and continued, \"Don't think about slacking off. Work hard there. Do you understand?\"","Auntie Shi's son felt goose - bumps all over his body under Qin Yuanzheng's stare and instinctively nodded.","Only then did Qin Yuanzheng let him go and turned to leave.","He still had to go to the mining area. He had already wasted too much time here today.","Auntie Shi's son was on the verge of crying.","He suspected that he was being threatened. If he didn't go to the construction site to carry bricks, he thought the military people would tie him to a tractor and drive him around the site three times.","However, no matter how reluctant he was, he didn't dare not to go at this point.","He couldn't really let the military people tie him up and take him to the construction site. How embarrassing would that be?","He still had his pride.","So, on the morning of the third day, Auntie Shi's husband personally sent his son to the construction site of the Wencheng Airport project to work as a laborer carrying bricks.","The commander of the engineering corps in charge of this airport project was Zhao Jiannong.","Zhao Jiannong had received instructions from Qin Yuanzheng, so he told the supervisor to keep a close eye on Auntie Shi's son and make sure he carried bricks for two months.","If he could persevere and still wanted to stay, they would consider transferring him to another position and making him a full - time worker.","If he couldn't hold on and made a fuss to run away, he would be sent to the pig farm to take care of pigs.","Such a lazy and spineless person needed to be taught a good lesson, lest he just stayed at home all day and caused trouble for his parents.","...","Auntie Shi didn't know all these details. She only knew that Qin Yuanzheng had helped to make arrangements at the airport.","With Brigade Commander Qin's promise, her son was sure to have a bright future at the airport!","At the very least, he would definitely become a full - time worker. Auntie Shi just hoped that her son would be sensible, endure hardships, and work hard, and not mess up this great opportunity.","After Auntie Shi's matter was settled, a few days later, Han Wenlin finally returned with his men.","Then he rushed to Wencheng for an investigation. Soon, he found Zheng Weigong who was hiding in Wencheng.","Han Wenlin had some experience in dealing with spies. He was worried that Zheng Weigong was hiding in Wencheng to sabotage the construction site of the airport.","Among the surrounding cities, the most important places were the mining area under Qin Yuanzheng's management and the airport project in Wencheng under Zhao Jiannong's management.","So, Han Wenlin brought some military dogs and joined forces with Zhao Jiannong. They actually found explosives buried underground around the construction site!","And they also found Zheng Weigong hiding in a resident's house in Wencheng.","This case caused a great stir. Han Wenlin had just taken office and had made great contributions.","By the time everything was settled and the dust had settled, three months had passed, and it was already the twelfth lunar month.","The Spring Festival was approaching.","Another year had gone by.","Qiao Lanshu's belly was getting bigger and bigger, and Niuwa had grown a year older. He was as strong as a young calf.","Qiao Lanshu bought new cloth and cotton and asked Huang Erling to make new Spring Festival clothes for Niuwa and An'an.","While Niuwa was trying on new clothes in the room, Qin Yuanzheng pushed open the door, stood at the entrance, and said to him, \"Niuwa, come out quickly. Your dad is here to pick you up and go home for the Spring Festival.\"","Niuwa had just put on the new cotton-padded jacket. It was black, which was stain-resistant, and thickly stuffed with cotton. Wearing it, he looked like a little round ball.","Hearing this, his face changed. Pretending to be stupid, he asked, \"Dad? Aren't you my dad? I'm definitely going to celebrate the Spring Festival here. Right, Mother Qiao?\"","Qiao Lanshu was holding An'an in her arms and looking at Qin Yuanzheng.","Qin Yuanzheng turned around, looked at Han Wenlin standing behind him, and said, \"You've heard it, right? It's really not that I don't want to send him back. It's just that he himself doesn't want to leave.\""]},{"number":233,"title":"Chapter 233: Who are you saying is on a hunger strike The prodigy kid","paragraphs":["As the New Year was fast approaching, Han Wenlin had rushed back just in time.","He had barely taken up his new post in Longcheng when he got involved in the Zheng Weigong affair.","It was a complicated case, involving human trafficking, illegal job trading, and leaking state secrets.","If not for the current policies, the Zheng Weigong siblings would have fled abroad with their ill-gotten gains long ago.","Unable to escape, they hid in Wencheng instead.","Han Wenlin had coordinated with the local military garrison in Wencheng to capture them.","Even so, wrapping up the case took a very long time.","With the New Year looming, Han Wenlin missed his only son terribly. He worried that being away from Niuwa for so long, leaving the boy in someone else’s care, would harm his development.","He was afraid Niuwa would grow distant and resent him.","So Han Wenlin worked day and night without rest, finally managing to return home just before the Little New Year.","The day after he got back, without even tidying up his own house, he hurriedly bought gifts and went to Qin Yuanzheng’s home to pick up his son.","And what did he find? The boy was happily trying on new clothes and new shoes, calling out \"Mommy\" with warmth and affection.","It was like a happy, harmonious family.","If only the son weren’t his biological child...","Han Wenlin had been away for months, tanning darker and losing some weight.","He hadn’t even shaved, showing up looking scruffy and disheveled.","Yet Niuwa didn’t even come out to see him.","So Han Wenlin walked to the doorway, peered inside, and caught sight of Niuwa at once.","The boy had grown taller and sturdier, though he’d darkened in the sun too.","Seeing Niuwa in a new cotton-padded jacket and a handmade winter hat with earflaps, Han Wenlin threw Qiao Lanshu a grateful glance.","Then he called out, \"Comrade Han Ye, come out here for a moment.\"","Niuwa turned to look at him. A moment later, he pretended not to recognize him and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Mommy, look! There’s a wild man at the door!\"","Everyone: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu lightly smacked his bottom and whispered, \"Don’t be silly. That’s your father. He’s here to take you home for the New Year. Be good, sweetheart, and go with him...\"","Before she could finish, Niuwa burst into tears. He clung to Qiao Lanshu’s arm, sobbing, \"Mommy, are you sending me away? Don’t you want me anymore? Wahhh, I finally have a home. Don’t make me go back to wandering! Wahhh!\"","He cried harder and harder, starting with whimpers and turning into loud wails.","Then he threw himself on the ground, rolling and weeping.","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu’s heart ached.","This child, ever since she rescued him from the traffickers, had never been able to settle anywhere.","At first, he stayed at the home of a public security bureau chief in a neighboring city—only to run away multiple times in just a few days.","When Qin Yuanzheng brought him back and placed him with the director of the Women’s Federation, he ran away again.","Now, he had finally come to see this place as home and stayed put. He was obedient every day, eating, bathing, and sleeping without being reminded. He went to kindergarten without causing trouble.","He even helped Auntie Shi water the vegetables and feed the dog.","What a good child. Qiao Lanshu had grown fond of him. Seeing him cry like this tore at her heart.","She said quickly, \"I’m not sending you away. I do want you. Get up first—the ground is cold.\"","As she spoke, she set aside baby An’an, who was in her arms, and bent to help Niuwa up.","But her belly was already four months along. Worried Niuwa might accidentally bump into her, Qin Yuanzheng strode over and gestured for her to sit. \"Don’t move. Stay away from this little ox.\"","Then he grabbed Niuwa, who was still rolling on the ground, by the scruff of his neck and lifted him up with one hand.","Qin Yuanzheng put on a stern face and growled, \"Stop crying. If you keep it up, I’ll really throw you out.\"","Niuwa: \"...\"","He instantly stopped crying and stood still, obedient.","Han Wenlin set the fruit and biscuits he was carrying on the table, then crouched in front of Han Ye. \"Son, do you really not want to see me?\"","Han Ye stiffened his neck and yelled, \"I’m not your son!\"","Han Wenlin rubbed his forehead in dismay. Then he asked, \"Dad has a small courtyard now too, a brand-new house. I’ve prepared a separate room just for you. Don’t you want to come see it?\"","Niuwa shook his head. \"No. I sleep fine here, with Granny Shi and my little brother.\"","At this point, with Qiao Lanshu’s belly growing and one-year-old An’an getting bigger, it had been arranged for Auntie Shi to sleep with Niuwa and An’an.","The two boys got along well. An’an was very attached to Niuwa. At first, An’an refused to sleep without Qiao Lanshu, but Niuwa would hold and soothe him until he quietly went to sleep with his older brother.","Niuwa was four years older than An’an. Perhaps because he was the older brother, he felt a sense of responsibility. He’d taken it upon himself to teach An’an good habits and tell him to listen to their mom. He acted like a little adult. And Niuwa himself had become much more sensible, no longer as mischievous.","After all, whatever he did, An’an would imitate. Niuwa was afraid of setting a bad example to his little brother, which might ruin his dream of becoming a soldier one day.","These days, even Qin Yuanzheng had grown reluctant to let Niuwa go.","Once Niuwa left, there was no guarantee An’an would agree to sleep with Auntie Shi.","What if he cried and demanded to be with his mom?","Qin Yuanzheng turned to look at Han Wenlin, who returned the gaze with a worried expression. \"Brigade Commander Qin,\" Han Wenlin said awkwardly, \"Niuwa must have been a lot of trouble for you during this time.\"","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head. \"Not really. Niuwa’s been quite sensible. He even helps take care of his little brother. He’s a good older brother.\"","As they talked, Niuwa had shuffled little by little to hide behind Qiao Lanshu.","Han Wenlin noticed, but said nothing. After a long silence, he walked over again and spoke to Niuwa. \"Comrade Han Ye, you’ve already stayed here a long time. It’s time to stop imposing. Come home with Dad. I’ll get you a dog too, okay?\"","Niuwa hid silently behind Qiao Lanshu, pouting and saying nothing.","In short, he didn’t want to leave.","But he also knew—this wasn’t his home. He and An’an weren’t real brothers. Qiao Lanshu wasn’t his mother.","He actually understood everything. He just pretended not to, hoping that as long as he played dumb, he could keep living here.","Han Wenlin approached him again and said, \"Son, you’re five years old. You’re not a little kid anymore, right? Your Aunt Qiao is pregnant and will soon have another baby. An’an is still young. Aunt Qiao doesn’t have the energy to take care of so many children.","Be a good boy and come home with me first. If you ever miss being here, you can visit anytime. Our place isn’t far—just two streets away.\"","Niuwa still didn't say a word. An'an, noticing this beside him, handed him the little sheep plush toy he was holding, babbling in baby language that only Niuwa could understand.","Niuwa hugged An'an and cried, \"My poor little brother! From today on, you won't have a younger brother anymore. You'll be a little brother without your big brother to protect you. You're really, truly pitiful, wuwuwu.\"","Everyone was speechless.","Han Wenlin was utterly embarrassed.","He never expected his own son to be like this.","Just listen to what he said—could anyone actually come up with such a thing?","Han Wenlin rubbed his forehead again, head aching.","Finally, Han Wenlin couldn't take it anymore. He grabbed Niuwa and said, \"It's getting late. We still need to go to the department store to buy some furniture and daily necessities, so let's head out now.\"","Niuwa knew he couldn't completely leave his father, Han Wenlin.","So he made a demand: \"I'll only go back with you for the New Year. Once it's over, I'm coming back here to live.\"","Han Wenlin thought to himself, \"You really think this is your home now?\"","\"You want to come back? Don't even bother seeing if they welcome you.\"","But just then, Qin Yuanzheng suddenly spoke up. He said, \"Niuwa is right, Director Han. You're already very busy with work, and there's usually no one at home. Niuwa is just a child and can't take care of himself. After the New Year, why don't you just send Niuwa back to me?\"","He'd worked hard to straighten Niuwa out—he wasn't about to waste a free little helper.","He needed Niuwa to put An'an to sleep.","Han Wenlin said a bit apologetically, \"Wouldn't that be too much trouble for you?\"","Qin Yuanzheng replied, \"No trouble at all. Just remember to pay the living expenses.\"","Han Wenlin was left speechless.","...","After Han Wenlin took Niuwa away, the yard instantly fell quiet.","So quiet that even Qiao Lanshu and Auntie Shi found it hard to get used to.","Qiao Lanshu said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Without Niuwa here at home, it doesn't feel lively anymore.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was holding An'an, following Qiao Lanshu out for dinner. Hearing this, he said, \"That kid Niuwa is usually way too noisy. Finally, we can have a few days of peace and quiet.\"","Niuwa had a loud voice and boundless energy, shouting and carrying on all day long. He really was quite the racket.","Auntie Shi came out carrying a basin of steamed flower rolls. She sighed and said, \"I even steamed so many of these flower rolls. Why didn't Niuwa eat any before he left?\"","Then she started grumbling again: \"Oh dear, that Director Han is a bachelor, with no woman in the house. And he's so busy with work. Once Niuwa goes back, he probably won't even get to eat his beloved mantou and flower rolls anymore.\"","Han Wenlin worked as the director of the Public Security Bureau. With policies changing and many revolutionary committees being abolished, all the workload had shifted to the Public Security Bureau. Han Wenlin was so busy he didn't even have time to sleep. How was he supposed to take care of a child? Did he even have time to cook for him?","Niuwa loved eating more than anything. He especially loved white flour mantou and chive flower rolls. He also liked baozi, dumplings, and noodles. But all these things took time to make, and Han Wenlin probably didn't have it.","Auntie Shi also felt sorry for Niuwa. She said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Xiao Qiao, how about I pack a few flower rolls later and send them to the Public Security Bureau?\"","Qiao Lanshu was handing a flower roll to An'an to gnaw on. The chive flower roll was fragrant, soft, and fluffy. An'an took a bite with his two front teeth, munching happily with a big grin on his face.","Qiao Lanshu hesitated for a moment, then looked at Qin Yuanzheng beside her, and asked, \"Zheng Ge, do you think we should send some?\"","She was also worried that Niuwa wouldn't have anything to eat.","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head. \"No need to send any. These past few days, Han Wenlin is on leave. He has time to cook.\"","Han Wenlin hadn't taken a break in months. He'd saved up his vacation days, and since it was around the New Year, he took them all at once.","Auntie Shi nodded after hearing that, but she still thought about Niuwa as she looked at the big basin of chive flower rolls.","...","This was Qiao Lanshu's second New Year in Dragon City. Last year, Qin Yuanzheng had promised her they'd find a chance to go back to Yangcheng. But now she was pregnant again, so naturally, they couldn't go.","Qin Yuanzheng felt terribly sorry for Qiao Lanshu and worried she might be homesick.","So, some time ago, he wrote letters to his old comrades in southern cities, asking them to help buy a lot of things—like southern rice, New Year oranges, bananas, cured meats and sausages, dried shrimp, and dried squid.","Just before the New Year, these items arrived one after another.","Qin Yuanzheng brought everything home and unpacked them one by one for Qiao Lanshu to see.","Other stuff was fine, but the oranges and bananas were hard to ship.","The bananas had been cut from the trees while still green, carefully wrapped and mailed all the way from the south to the north. By the time Qin Yuanzheng received them, the bananas were already mostly yellow. And because the north was so cold, the bananas had frozen stiff and some turned black in spots, ruining the taste.","Oranges were even harder. Bananas could be picked while still green and ripen during transit, but oranges didn't work that way. They had to be picked ripe, then shipped. If the journey was slow, it took eight or nine days; fast, at least four or five.","This box of oranges had been sent by his comrade from the south. They were picked from the tree just before the train arrived, packed, and loaded. The train took three days to reach Dragon City.","Fortunately, Dragon City's cold weather kept the oranges from spoiling completely. They weren't super fresh, but their taste was still decent.","Qin Yuanzheng went to all this trouble just because he feared Qiao Lanshu might get homesick and because she'd recently lost her appetite and wasn't eating much.","Qiao Lanshu picked up an orange and looked at it, then looked at Qin Yuanzheng with emotion in her eyes.","Those who truly loved her would get her anything she wanted.","Without her saying a word, Qin Yuanzheng had already thought of all this. She felt she'd definitely married the right man.","As Qin Yuanzheng checked each orange one by one, he said softly, \"What's the matter? You just realized your man is amazing and love me even more?\"","Qiao Lanshu blushed and glared at him. \"An'an is right here! Don't talk nonsense.\"","Qin Yuanzheng glanced at An'an and said, \"Anyway, he can't talk yet. Even if he hears it, he probably didn't understand.\"","Qiao Lanshu grabbed a vegetable basket and put in some bananas that hadn't frozen and a few oranges. She planned to give some to Zhong Mei, who used to love oranges.","They spent two days sorting through the New Year goods. That evening, An'an absolutely refused to sleep with Auntie Shi. Qiao Lanshu had no choice but to bring him to their room, and together, the couple coaxed him to sleep.","On the third day, the twenty-eighth of the twelfth lunar month, Han Wenlin came rushing over, with Niuwa following behind him.","His eyes were red as he said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Brigade Commander Qin, I really have no choice. That boy—once he went back, he refused to eat anything. For three whole days, he wouldn't touch the food I made. I'm genuinely afraid he'll starve himself to death.\"","So Han Wenlin had hurriedly brought the child back.","Fine. No matter how much Qin Yuanzheng complained about Niuwa behind his back, he had to send him back.","He only had this one precious son, he couldn't let anything happen to him.","Both Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu's expressions were ones of shock.","Qiao Lanshu asked in surprise, \"Hasn't eaten for three days? A hunger strike? Who are you talking about? Niuwa?\""]},{"number":234,"title":"Chapter 234: Folk Remedies for Having a Son","paragraphs":["It wasn’t just Qiao Lanshu who was stunned; even Qin Yuanzheng nearly lost his composure.","Holding An’an in one arm and propping his other hand on his hip, Qin Yuanzheng looked at Han Wenlin with a complicated expression, then at Niuwa, who had just been set down and was now standing next to Han Wenlin. “Director Han, Niuwa hasn’t eaten for three days? Why are you only telling us now?”","Han Wenlin looked a little awkward. “Well, it’s not exactly that he’s on a hunger strike. He just eats very little each time, but keeps complaining that he’s hungry. He lies weakly on the bed. I figured... maybe he misses you all?”","Just then, Auntie Shi came out wearing an apron, holding two meat buns in her hands. She said with surprise, “Niuwa, you’re on a hunger strike? Not even these fragrant meat buns?”","Niuwa was leaning weakly against Han Wenlin. As soon as Auntie Shi approached, his nose twitched, and his gaze locked onto the buns in her hands. He swallowed hard and said, “Grandma Shi, I want to eat the buns! Give them to me quick.”","Auntie Shi handed him the two buns. Niuwa grabbed one in each hand and gobbled them down without lifting his head, mumbling between bites, “So good, really good—these meat buns are amazing!”","Everyone was speechless.","They all turned to look at Han Wenlin, whose expression was equally complicated.","He said, “This kid... he was using a hunger strike to threaten me, just so I’d send him back here? He wouldn’t eat the buns I made, but he has to come here for them.”","Han Wenlin was so frustrated his head ached.","Qiao Lanshu looked at Niuwa with pity and said softly, “Niuwa, slow down, don’t choke. Come on, let’s sit down and eat.”","With that, she led Niuwa over to the steps to sit.","Niuwa had already devoured both buns in a frenzy.","Then, very naturally, he reached out his hand toward Auntie Shi and called out, “Grandma Shi, I want more.”","Qin Yuanzheng called Auntie Shi “sister-in-law,” Niuwa called Qin Yuanzheng “Dad,” and then called Auntie Shi “Grandma.”","This messed up the generational titles entirely. Han Wenlin’s head ached even more as he stood nearby, staring at his son with a somber gaze, thinking, “My wife is gentle and virtuous—so who on earth did this son take after?”","Auntie Shi went to get Niuwa two more buns. After he wolfed those down too, he was still asking for more.","Auntie Shi didn’t dare give him any more. Instead, she poured him a glass of milk powder and told him to sit and drink it slowly.","Qiao Lanshu looked at Niuwa and asked, “Niuwa, after you went back with your father, why didn’t you eat? Starving yourself only hurts you, not anyone else. No matter what happens, you can’t use a hunger strike—that’s harming your own body, understand?”","Niuwa had indeed purposely starved himself a bit to make Han Wenlin suffer.","But that wasn’t the main reason.","He complained to Qiao Lanshu pitifully, “Mom, I wasn’t really on a hunger strike! I just think the food he cooks is so bad even a dog wouldn’t eat it!”","After they went back, Han Wenlin kept his promise and bought Niuwa a little mutt.","Niuwa couldn’t stomach Han Wenlin’s cooking, so he poured the food into the dog’s bowl.","And guess what?","Even the dog wouldn’t touch Han Wenlin’s cooking!","As Niuwa said this, he even gagged, shuddering in dread. “It was just that awful, truly terrible!”","Everyone was speechless again.","They all turned in unison to look at Han Wenlin.","Han Wenlin was at a loss for words.","His expression shifted uncomfortably as he said, weakly defending himself, “How could it be? I don’t think it tastes bad when I eat it.”","Despite not being much of a cook, Han Wenlin didn’t believe his food could be that terrible.","He added, “The food’s all cooked through, and I put salt and oil in it. There’s no way it could taste bad.”","He stressed, “Cooking with lard—how could that be bad? When we were kids, we didn’t even have lard, let alone pork, and we still ate whatever we had, right?”","What Han Wenlin said wasn’t entirely wrong, and both Qin Yuanzheng and Auntie Shi could see that.","But Niuwa had spent months here, being well-fed by Auntie Shi and Qiao Lanshu until he was plump and healthy. Auntie Shi’s cooking was delicious, especially her buns, steamed buns, and twisted rolls—each one soft and fluffy. Even Qiao Lanshu, who wasn’t fond of such things, could eat two in one meal.","On top of that, Qiao Lanshu often made southern-style stir-fries, braised meats, and soups, all of which tasted wonderful.","Having gotten used to their cooking, how could Niuwa go back to eating Han Wenlin’s plain, tasteless dishes—merely boiled with no flavor or texture?","And Han Wenlin was guiltily hiding a few things.","For instance, his steamed buns were not only hard and dense but also had a bit of a sour taste—he wasn’t sure why.","Or his dumplings, which had thick skins because he wasn’t good at rolling them out.","Standing there under everyone’s gaze, Han Wenlin suddenly felt awkward.","Meanwhile, his heartless son was clutching a ceramic mug, gulping down his milk with a blissful expression.","Qiao Lanshu wrapped her arm around Niuwa and said sympathetically, “Niuwa looks like he’s lost weight in just three days.”","Auntie Shi immediately chimed in, “Exactly, he has lost weight.”","Auntie Shi had noticed it herself but hadn’t wanted to say anything.","She understood her position and knew when to hold her tongue.","But Qiao Lanshu had no such reservations. She said to Han Wenlin, “Director Han, maybe it’s better to leave Niuwa here at my place for now. We can take care of him, so you don’t have to worry.”","After those three days of parenting, Han Wenlin had learned how hard it was to raise a child.","But he still felt a bit uneasy about imposing. After all, leaving his child with someone else was a real inconvenience, wasn’t it?","Plus, Qiao Lanshu was pregnant. He said a little apologetically, “To be honest, it’s not that I mind. I’m just worried he’ll cause you trouble, since you already have a child to take care of at home.”","Niuwa was eavesdropping on the adults’ conversation.","When he heard this, he turned and looked at Qiao Lanshu with pleading eyes.","Was he a burden?","He felt a little sad.","Qiao Lanshu quickly said, “No trouble at all. Niuwa is very well-behaved and capable. He’s especially good—we barely have to do anything for him. Director Han, you’re truly lucky to have such an obedient and sensible son.”","When Niuwa heard this, he perked up and said to Han Wenlin, “Having me is your lucky charm.”","Han Wenlin was at a loss for words.","He massaged his forehead again, realizing he had no idea how to handle a child, especially one like Niuwa.","Now he finally understood why his chubby, adorable son—whom he thought was so cute—was nicknamed Niuwa by others.","The name truly fit.","And so, after the adults talked it over, Niuwa was finally allowed to stay at Qiao Lanshu’s home.","Once he’d eaten and drunk his fill, he picked up An’an to play, but soon grew bored because An’an, who had just learned to walk, couldn’t run yet.","So Niuwa took off his coat, jumped and climbed all over the yard, and ran around wildly with the family dog.","Han Wenlin watched his gleefully rambunctious son, standing silently in the yard for a long, long time.","Qin Yuanzheng walked up to him and watched for a while too. Then he said, \"Don't worry. Leave the child with me. Nothing will go wrong.\"","Han Wenlin nodded silently.","Of course, he trusted Qin Yuanzheng's character. He just couldn't bear to part with Niuwa.","But he had no other choice. After all, Niuwa was raised by his wife during the toddler years and then sent to the countryside for more than half a year.","As a father, he had never been by the child's side.","Now that the child was not close to him and didn't like him, he accepted it.","He just felt guilty towards the child and very sorry for Niuwa.","Qin Yuanzheng said to him, \"Come here for a meal during the Spring Festival. If you miss Niuwa, you can come and see him at any time. Our two families live close to each other. Just come over when you're free.\"","Han Wenlin nodded. Before leaving, he suddenly took out his grain ration card from his pocket.","It was a grain ration card from the Public Security Bureau. The monthly grain ration was 30 catties, and the salary was about 100 yuan.","He gave his grain ration card directly to Qin Yuanzheng and said to him, \"This child Niuwa loves to eat and can eat a lot. Give my grain ration card to Comrade Qiao Lanshu and let her collect the grain every month for Niuwa to eat.\"","Qin Yuanzheng didn't take it and said, \"Keep it for yourself. Don't you need to eat?\"","Han Wenlin stuffed the grain ration card into his hand and said, \"I still have some stored grain at home. Don't worry. The subsidies and my salary are enough for me. I'm just one person, and I don't have a family to support.\"","Then, Han Wenlin added, \"Since Niuwa doesn't want to go home with me, I'll go to buy a train ticket and go back to my hometown to see my mother. I'll have to trouble you with the child this Spring Festival. I reckon I'll be back after the Lantern Festival.\"","Han Wenlin's hometown was in the countryside, and he wasn't a native of Longcheng. He had to take a train this time. It was a one - day - and - one - night journey by train, and then he had to transfer to a bus, a tractor, and a donkey cart...","It was not easy to go back home.","If it hadn't been for looking for Niuwa, he wouldn't have come here in such a hurry.","His old mother didn't want to leave her hometown, so he could only go back to see her when he had time. Fortunately, there were still relatives like uncles, aunts, and cousins in his hometown to take care of his mother. He just needed to send money home to his old mother every month.","Qin Yuanzheng nodded and said, \"Alright. Then have a safe journey.\"","Han Wenlin nodded, went to talk to Niuwa for a while, and then left.","Qin Yuanzheng also began to miss his family. His parents were also old. He was the only son in the family, and his father and mother had already retired. But the old people had health problems, and the north was cold and the journey was far. His parents often wrote to him, hoping that he would take his wife and children back to their hometown for a visit.","He could only wait until the two children were a bit older before taking them back.","Auntie Shi took An'an and Niuwa to take a nap.","Qin Yuanzheng went back into the house and saw Qiao Lanshu lying on the kang, listening to an ancient Chinese literature appreciation program on the radio.","He leaned over, reached out to rub her belly, and asked in a low voice, \"Why aren't you taking a nap?\"","Qiao Lanshu opened her eyes, looked at him, and whispered, \"I've been waiting for you. Has Director Han left?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded and said, \"He said he's going back to his hometown for the Spring Festival and has entrusted me to take care of Niuwa.\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, \"Director Han loves Niuwa. After all, Niuwa is his only child.\"","Qin Yuanzheng said slowly, \"Children will become more sensible as they grow up. Maybe when Niuwa is a bit older, he'll want to go back and find his father on his own.\"","Then, Qin Yuanzheng gave Qiao Lanshu Han Wenlin's grain ration card and said, \"Take it. It's Niuwa's living expenses.\"","Qiao Lanshu was speechless for a moment.","She took the grain ration card, looked at it, and couldn't help saying, \"What about Director Han himself? Why did he send the grain ration card here directly?\"","Previously, he had always given money and coupons. Now, he even sent the grain ration card.","Qin Yuanzheng said, \"He lives alone and doesn't often cook. The Public Security Bureau is going to expand its staff soon, and a canteen will be opened after the Spring Festival. Then they can eat in the canteen. After all, the subsidies from the Public Security Bureau are quite good.\"","When Qin Yuanzheng used to live alone, he hardly spent the subsidies and money from the army.","He lived in the unit and ate in the unit. He really didn't need much.","Qiao Lanshu put the grain ration card into the drawer beside the bed, stacked it with her various certificates, and then locked the drawer.","She said softly, \"Then let's keep it for now. If Director Han gets married again in the future, we'll return it to him.\"","Han Wenlin was still young, and he only had one son.","Maybe he would get married again.","But if he did, would Niuwa become even more estranged from his father?","Qin Yuanzheng pinched her chin and turned her face towards him, saying, \"Why are you thinking so much? It's time for your nap.\"","Qiao Lanshu yawned and then lay in Qin Yuanzheng's arms, saying, \"Yes. I have to take a nap while the children are asleep. I'm so tired.\"","Qin Yuanzheng lay down beside her, put his arm around Qiao Lanshu, and stroked her belly.","Her belly was already a bit prominent at more than four months. This was their second child.","Qin Yuanzheng looked at Qiao Lanshu's face and thought that this child should look like Qiao Lanshu. Only if it looked like Qiao Lanshu would it be beautiful.","After Qiao Lanshu fell asleep, Qin Yuanzheng went to tidy up the books on the desk.","Since Qiao Lanshu quit her job, she had been reading textbooks every day. Qin Yuanzheng knew that she wanted to study.","So he had once thought about whether to find someone to recommend her to a Workers', Peasants', and Soldiers' University.","But Qiao Lanshu had refused.","Since she didn't want to go to a Workers', Peasants', and Soldiers' University, but still read textbooks and did test papers every day.","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head. He didn't ask. Anyway, whatever Qiao Lanshu wanted to do, she could just do it. As her husband, he would definitely support her unconditionally.","...","During the Spring Festival, Guan Wenjun, whom they hadn't seen for a long time, came to pay New Year calls with Zhong Mei.","They also brought a lot of things.","Guan Wenjun had managed to apply for a house before the Spring Festival. He had been busy cleaning and decorating the house with Zhong Mei during this period.","So Zhong Mei hadn't come to see Qiao Lanshu for a long time.","She and Guan Wenjun had been married for a few months. Her household registration had been sorted out, but she still didn't have a proper job.","She was still working as a temporary worker in a food factory.","As soon as Guan Wenjun entered the door, he gave red envelopes to Niuwa and An'an. Then he took out another red envelope and handed it to Qiao Lanshu, saying, \"Here. This is for the second child.\"","Qiao Lanshu took the red envelope and thanked him with a smile.","Guan Wenjun said sourly, \"You're welcome. There will come a time when you'll have to return the favor.\"","Then, Guan Wenjun went to look at Zhong Mei's belly.","Since their marriage, Zhong Mei and Guan Wenjun had been getting along quite well.","Guan Wenjun was generous and was willing to hand over the money to her. He would buy whatever she wanted.","Except that sometimes Guan Wenjun's male chauvinism would get the better of him and he would say some unpleasant things. Zhong Mei thought that this husband was still okay.","It was just that his sexual needs were very strong. He would drag her into bed two or three times a day. Zhong Mei was gradually getting annoyed.","After a few months, Zhong Mei still hadn't gotten pregnant. Guan Wenjun started nagging about having a child again and said that he would take Zhong Mei to the hospital for a check - up to see if there was something wrong with her body.","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu couldn't help but say, \"It's only been a few months since they got married. Why is he in such a hurry?\"","Zhong Mei said somewhat speechlessly, \"He always loves to compare with you guys. He said that you got pregnant with An'an just a few months after your marriage, but I've been married for five months and still haven't conceived.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Zhong Mei gritted her teeth and said, \"If he keeps doing this, I'll really can't help but beat him up.\"","A few months after their marriage, Guan Wenjun gave Zhong Mei quite a lot of money. He also bought her a bicycle and a watch, and sorted out her household registration.","Guan Wenjun didn't look down on Zhong Mei because of her family background and status.","Just like how urban people normally marry their wives, he didn't miss out on anything that should be given.","So Zhong Mei was very grateful to him and always showed a lot of tolerance towards him.","However, recently, because of the matter of having a child, Zhong Mei was about to lose her patience.","Qiao Lanshu found it quite funny. She whispered, \"You were malnourished and over - tired before. You should take good care of your body now. Once your body recovers, you'll naturally get pregnant. Just go to the hospital and let the doctor take a look. It's also a good thing to get some tonics.\"","Hearing what Qiao Lanshu said, Zhong Mei finally felt less angry.","She whispered, \"I just hate that he always compares everything with Brigade Commander Qin, like getting married and having children. He keeps nagging about it from time to time. It's like he's crazy. I've told him that Brigade Commander Qin is a brigade commander, while you're just a section chief of the city supply department. Why don't you compare yourself with the brigade commander? Brigade Commander Qin has won several second - class merits. What about him? Does he have any?\"","As Qiao Lanshu listened to Zhong Mei talking, she was peeling an orange and eating it. When Zhong Mei saw it, she said again, \"Look, Brigade Commander Qin even buys his wife oranges, bananas from the south, and rice and cured meat from the south. What about him? Has he bought any? He doesn't compare in the right aspects but keeps staring at the wrong ones all day long. Do you think he has a screw loose?\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, \"Section Chief Guan is just such a person. Maybe he doesn't really think that way in his heart, but he just has a sharp tongue and likes to say a few more words. Don't pay attention to him. As time goes by, you'll gradually understand his character.\"","Zhong Mei and Guan Wenjun got married in a hurry, and they actually didn't know each other well.","Zhong Mei was now gradually getting to know Guan Wenjun's temperament. So, she was just venting her frustration to Qiao Lanshu.","She didn't really dislike Guan Wenjun.","In the yard, Guan Wenjun was also talking to Qin Yuanzheng. He said, \"Lao Qin, tell me the truth. Did you have some secret recipe to have a son right after getting married?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at him as if he were looking at an idiot and said, \"Come on, how could I have such a thing?\"","Guan Wenjun didn't believe it. \"You must have it. Before you got married, you went to the hospital several times because of infertility. Don't think I don't know.\"","Qin Yuanzheng snorted. \"I think the most urgent thing for you is not to have a child.\"","Guan Wenjun then asked, \"Then what is it?\"","Taking medicine? Conditioning the body?","Qin Yuanzheng carried An'an and walked around a couple of times, and casually said, \"You should go and get your head examined first.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\""]},{"number":235,"title":"Chapter 235: I've Given Birth to a Daughter","paragraphs":["After the Spring Festival, time flew by. In May, Qiao Lanshu gave birth to her second child.","The second child was a daughter, tiny and delicate, with fair skin and big eyes. She was just like a mini-version of Qiao Lanshu.","Since she was born in summer, the couple named her Qin Qiaoxia, and her nickname was Xiaxia.","At this time, An'an was already two years old. He could run and jump, and could also say some simple words, but he couldn't speak long sentences clearly. Whenever he tried, his words would be slurred and he would just babble.","With a new little sister in the family, Niuwa and An'an were both very curious.","When Qiao Lanshu was on maternity leave, Niuwa and An'an lay on the kang and peeked at their little sister on the bed.","Niuwa was already six years old and much more sensible. He stared at Xiaxia intently.","When An'an reached out his hand to touch Xiaxia, Niuwa slapped his hand gently and said seriously, \"An'an, you're a big brother now. Don't be so rough with your little sister.\"","An'an looked at Qiao Lanshu with a wronged expression.","Qiao Lanshu smiled and held Xiaxia in her arms. Then she stretched out Xiaxia's little hand and said, \"Come on, big brother can shake hands with little sister.\"","An'an happily leaned over and shook Xiaxia's hand.","The age gap between the two brothers was only two years.","Qiao Lanshu thought it was great to raise two children at the same time. Once they started school, she would have less to worry about.","Niuwa was standing beside them, looking longingly and urging An'an, \"Okay, okay, let big brother touch her too.\"","An'an obediently withdrew his hand and let Niuwa hold Xiaxia's hand.","Niuwa held Xiaxia's hand carefully. Staring at Xiaxia's face, he said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Mom, little sister looks so much like you. Her skin is so fair.\"","Niuwa had been tanned as dark as a black cow. The older he got, the darker his skin became. He resembled Han Wenlin in three of his facial features. Han Wenlin said that he looked more like his mother and was more handsome than him, a rough guy.","There was nothing he could do about his dark skin. After all, Niuwa practiced boxing in the yard every day and ran around outside, exposed to the sun all the time.","Even An'an, who followed Niuwa around, had gotten much darker.","Qiao Lanshu held Xiaxia in her arms and swayed gently. She said softly, \"You two big brothers have to be careful in the future. Xiaxia is still a little baby and can't play with you yet.\"","Niuwa lowered his voice and said, \"I know, Mom. I'll be very careful.\"","Looking at An'an jumping up and down on the kang with the bed sheet in his hand, Niuwa said to Qiao Lanshu again, \"Mom, you can leave An'an to me. You just take good care of little sister.\"","Niuwa was acting like a little adult.","Qiao Lanshu nodded with a smile and said, \"Okay, then I'll have to trouble you, Niuwa.\"","However, Qiao Lanshu was still a little worried in her heart.","Niuwa had become more and more mischievous recently. Or rather, he had reached the age when even chickens and dogs would dislike him.","He had become a little overlord around the neighborhood.","Most of the kids around were younger than him. Those who were one or two years older than him were not as tall, as strong, or as good at fighting as he was.","After all, he had been practicing punching sandbags with Qin Yuanzheng since he was four years old. His arms and legs were very strong, and the other kids were no match for him.","So they secretly called him the boss.","Niuwa would often hold a stick in his hand and lead a group of little followers to run around the yard.","Now An'an had also joined his group of followers.","However, An'an was like the \"younger brother of the crown prince\". Although he was the youngest, no one dared to bully him.","Qiao Lanshu was very afraid that Niuwa would cause trouble.","What she didn't know was that Niuwa had actually caused quite a few problems, but they were all minor ones. The other kids were afraid of him, and besides, Niuwa would threaten them, saying, \"My real dad is the director of the public security bureau, and my godfather is the brigade commander of the army. If you dare to tell on me, I'll beat you up every time I see you.\"","With these threats, the other kids didn't dare to go against him.","Since he didn't actively bully other kids, these things hadn't reached Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng's ears yet.","Niuwa and An'an came out of the house. He took out a dollar from his pocket and said to An'an, \"We have a new little sister. This is a big happy event. Come on, let's go to the grocery store and treat my little followers to some candies.\"","An'an didn't understand these things. All he knew was that he could have candies, so he happily followed Niuwa and ran away.","Auntie Shi came in to bring Qiao Lanshu her meal. Following the recipe given by Qiao Lanshu, she had stewed ginseng chicken soup, steamed eggs for Qiao Lanshu, and cooked fragrant white rice.","She put the food on the counter beside the kang, then took Xiaxia from Qiao Lanshu's arms and said with a smile, \"Oh, it's really great to have Niuwa. He helps take care of An'an, which saves me a lot of trouble.\"","When Qiao Lanshu was on maternity leave, Qin Yuanzheng could only take a few days off. After the vacation, he still had to go to work.","Auntie Shi had to take care of Qiao Lanshu during her maternity leave and help take care of the kids at the same time. She was really busy.","Fortunately, Niuwa was sensible. He took An'an to play every day and came home on time for meals. He was really worry-free.","All the yards in this area were surrounded by walls, and a large area was enclosed. There were guards at the gate, so there was no need to worry about the kids running out.","Auntie Shi sighed in her heart. Sure enough, it was best to marry an officer. Look at how good their life was.","Qiao Lanshu was sipping the chicken soup and said with a smile, \"Niuwa is becoming more and more sensible. He's precocious and very smart. He's also taller than kids of the same age. He looks reliable.\"","Auntie Shi looked at Xiaxia and said, \"Like father, like son. Our An'an and Xiaxia will also be very smart and capable in the future.\"","After all, they were the children of Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu looked at An'an with a gentle look in her eyes.","Xiaxia looked like Qiao Lanshu. Especially after three months, Xiaxia could roll over by herself. She was so tiny, rolling around on the kang.","She inherited Qiao Lanshu's fair skin, and her big black eyes would light up with a giggle whenever she saw someone.","She was a little girl who loved to laugh.","Although Qin Yuanzheng knew he shouldn't be partial and that both sons and daughters were equally good.","But every time he saw Xiaxia, he couldn't help but feel soft inside.","Now, every time he got home, he would wash his hands and then hold Xiaxia. Xiaxia had almost grown up in his arms.","Qiao Lanshu had also gone to the hospital for postpartum rehabilitation recently. After giving birth to her second child, she always felt pain in her lower back, so she went to see a doctor. The doctor told her to go to the hospital for rehabilitation every other day, which would be good for her recovery.","So Qin Yuanzheng would hold Xiaxia and accompany her to the hospital for rehabilitation. After they came back, he would go to make milk for Xiaxia.","When Qiao Lanshu came out of the shower, she saw that it was already six o'clock in the afternoon. She then asked Auntie Shi, \"Sister-in-law, haven't An'an and Niuwa come back yet?\"","Auntie Shi was cooking dinner in the kitchen. Hearing her question, she said with a smile, \"You've been going to the hospital a lot recently, so you don't know. These two brothers have made new friends recently. They say they want to go to play with their new friends every day.\"","Auntie Shi continued with a smile, \"It's the son of a certain regimental commander. He used to grow up in the countryside. Now that he's going to start primary school, he's been brought here. Niuwa gets along well with him, so he takes An'an to find him every day.\"","Qiao Lanshu then asked, \"Do you know which regiment commander it is? What's his surname?\"","Auntie Shi was kneading dough while saying, \"Oh, I really don't know about this. I'll go out to the yard and ask around some other day.\"","Auntie Shi had been going out less recently, so she hadn't inquired in such detail.","Qiao Lanshu didn't think much of it either. After all, it was a regiment commander, and they all lived in the same yard. It wouldn't be a bad thing to get along well.","As a result, Niuwa still didn't come home after dinner.","The guard carried An'an back and found Qin Yuanzheng, saying, \"Brigade Commander, your eldest son got into a fight with the son of Regiment Commander Zhou from the Northern Suburb Mine. Right now, he's being held down by Regiment Commander Zhou's guard, waiting for you to go over.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was holding Xiaxia and feeding her milk. When he heard this, he was a bit speechless. \"What's going on?\"","As he said that, he glanced at An'an in the guard's arms and asked him, \"Qin Qiao'an, tell me what exactly happened.\"","An'an could barely speak clearly, but he was indignant and gesturing with his hands and feet as he said, \"They beat big brother! They're so bad.\"","Qin Yuanzheng didn't quite believe it. He suspected that Niuwa had gone looking for a fight on his own initiative.","But since things had come to this, he still had to go and have a look.","Qiao Lanshu also came out. She took An'an from the guard and looked at Qin Yuanzheng. \"Shall we go and have a look together? Niuwa actually got beaten?\"","This was really strange. As far as she knew, Niuwa was the boss around here. No one could beat him, and no one dared to.","Qin Yuanzheng put Xiaxia in the cradle and said to her, \"You don't need to go. I'll go and have a look. If this stinky boy really caused trouble, I'll take him to the public security bureau and let his real father interrogate him.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Was it really necessary to send him to the public security bureau?","It was already time for dinner. As a father, this was the first time Qin Yuanzheng had been called to deal with his child's misbehavior.","He had a bit of a headache.","Currently, all the people living in this area of the yard were from the military. His place was relatively remote, while Regiment Commander Zhou lived in the central area, in a large yard where several families lived.","The regiment commander from the Northern Suburb Mine was named Zhou Anping. They were from the same military region, and Qin Yuanzheng had known him for a long time.","However, he had never seen Regiment Commander Zhou's family members or his children before.","When he arrived at the yard, he indeed saw three six - or seven - year - old boys standing there.","One of them was Niuwa, who was the tallest.","The other two boys were a bit fairer and looked somewhat similar. They were presumably Regiment Commander Zhou's children.","Two guards were standing beside them, keeping an eye on them to prevent another fight.","After all, one was from the brigade commander's family and two were from the regiment commander's family. It wouldn't be good if either side got hurt.","When Qin Yuanzheng came over, Zhou Anping happened to be coming in from the outside in his military uniform in a hurry.","As soon as they met, they greeted each other.","Zhou Anping was very tall and looked quite gentle. He spoke very politely. \"Brigade Commander Qin, why did you come here in person? I've heard about it. It's just kids making a ruckus. It's a small matter.\"","Qin Yuanzheng also said politely, \"I'm just afraid Niuwa doesn't know his own strength. You know Niuwa. He's too reckless and no one can control him.\"","Since they all lived in the same yard, Zhou Anping of course knew Niuwa.","It could be said that no officer living in this area didn't know him.","At first, when Zhou Anping learned that his son had been beaten, he was very angry.","After all, his son had been raised in the countryside, and he felt he owed his child.","He had just brought the child here to go to school, and then he was beaten. Anyone would be unable to bear it.","But later, when he heard that his two sons had been beaten by Niuwa, he wasn't as angry anymore.","Because almost every child here had been beaten by Niuwa.","All the parents had accepted it. After all, they were all from the military. If you couldn't beat someone, it meant you were not good enough. They could only train their sons hard and try to defeat Niuwa next time.","Zhou Anping looked at the three boys and joked, \"It seems that my two boys don't understand the rules here and have annoyed Big Brother Niuwa?\"","When Niuwa heard him say this, he didn't even feel embarrassed. He said, \"Just let them call me big brother from now on, and I'll protect them.\"","As he said that, he even patted his chest.","Zhou Anping and Qin Yuanzheng looked at each other. Zhou Anping smiled and said, \"Then you have to ask them if they're willing.\"","Niuwa raised his fist and said to the two boys, \"In this place, it's the fists that speak. Do you submit?\"","He had just fought against the two of them alone and had suffered a loss. He hadn't been able to defeat them.","So they didn't submit.","The older boy was fair - skinned and didn't look like someone who could fight, but he had fought quite fiercely just now. Niuwa felt he had misjudged him.","This older boy was named Zhou Dingwen. He said to Niuwa, \"You're one year younger than me. I can't call you big brother.\"","The younger boy was named Zhou Dingwu. He also said, \"You can't even beat us brothers. What kind of big brother are you?\"","Niuwa frowned, his fist tightened, and he charged forward like a young calf. \"Then let's fight again!\"","As a result, on the way, he was grabbed by Qin Yuanzheng.","Niuwa was very strong. His pounce made Qin Yuanzheng take a step back. Qin Yuanzheng said, \"Good boy, you've got some strength!\"","He held Niuwa down and said seriously, \"Did you start this fight?\"","Niuwa also had a serious look on his face and said seriously, \"This is a fight for leadership. It doesn't matter who started it.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Zhou Anping laughed. He walked up to Niuwa and said to him, \"Good boy, you're right. But fighting is wrong. We don't advocate fighting. If there's anything, we can sit down and talk. Don't start a fight easily, okay?\"","Niuwa pursed his lips. Looking at the provocative looks in the eyes of Zhou Dingwen and his brother, he stamped his foot angrily and turned around and ran away.","Qin Yuanzheng shouted at him, \"Han Ye! Come back and apologize.\"","Han Ye didn't listen to him at all and had already run out of sight.","Qin Yuanzheng had a bit of a headache. He said to Zhou Anping, \"This child is not easy to discipline. Today's incident is Niuwa's fault. Don't worry. I'll go back and educate him well.\"","Niuwa's personality had shown signs since he was three years old.","He was a bit reckless, self - centered, and didn't like to be disciplined or restricted. However, he was also smart and could draw inferences from one instance. Ordinary reasoning wouldn't work on Niuwa.","Even his real father, Han Wenlin, had tried countless times. Now, Niuwa was already six years old, and he still refused to call Han Wenlin \"dad\".","Zhou Anping nodded. \"I know. It's not a big deal among kids. However, we still need to pay attention to this child. Otherwise, send him to the army early. Don't let him wander around outside.\"","For a child like Niuwa, if he wasn't sent to the army and was allowed to roam in society, he might go astray and become a difficult person to deal with.","Of course, Qin Yuanzheng knew this. But the child was only six years old today, and the army didn't accept six - year - old child soldiers."]},{"number":236,"title":"Chapter 236: Difficult to Discipline Children","paragraphs":["After returning home, Qin Yuanzheng made Niuwa stand in a horse stance.","He pulled up a chair, sat down in front of Niuwa, and took a bite of a freshly steamed bun while asking, \"Do you know what you did wrong?\"","Niuwa had been running wild all day and had spent the afternoon fighting with the Zhou family's two kids. By now, he was both starving and parched.","Standing in his horse stance, he stared longingly at the bun in Qin Yuanzheng's hand and swallowed hard.","When Qin Yuanzheng saw that Niuwa wasn't answering, his face grew sterner. He asked again, \"Han Ye, do you know what you did wrong?\"","Niuwa said stubbornly, \"I didn't do anything wrong.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless.","He closed his eyes in frustration, tempted to bundle Niuwa up on the spot and send him back to Han Wenlin.","Pointing a finger at Niuwa, he said, \"Fine. Then you stay here in your horse stance and think it over. You'll eat when you know what you did wrong.\"","With that, Qin Yuanzheng turned and stormed back into the house.","Qiao Lanshu stood at the doorway holding their daughter, watching the scene for a while. Seeing how angry Qin Yuanzheng was, she said softly, \"Brother Zheng, the kids are still young. He's already been standing there for half an hour. How about just making him face the wall and reflect instead?\"","Auntie Shi kept glancing at Niuwa too, muttering under her breath, \"This kid hasn't eaten all afternoon. He must be starving right now. This is usually when he has dinner, and he can put away four steamed buns at a time.\"","Before, Qiao Lanshu used to limit Niuwa to two or three buns per meal and a bowl of milk powder before bed. But now that he was a bit older, she let him eat four buns per meal.","Niuwa loved to eat and ate heartily. His stomach was empty, and after watching Qin Yuanzheng munch on that bun, he couldn't stand it anymore.","His horse stance was starting to wobble.","An'an was also sitting on the doorstep, watching his older brother in the yard. He looked at the bun in his own hand, then quietly slipped it into his pocket.","But he couldn't hide such a small move from the adults.","All three of them noticed. Qiao Lanshu and Auntie Shi exchanged a glance, then looked at Qin Yuanzheng.","Pretending not to see, Qin Yuanzheng sat down, grabbed another bun, and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"What are you standing there for? Come eat, the food's getting cold.\"","So Qiao Lanshu walked over, still holding their daughter in her arms.","As Qin Yuanzheng ate, he looked at Xiaxia nestled in Qiao Lanshu's arms. At just a few months old, she was already adorable, as lovely as jade and snow.","The anger in his heart melted away in an instant.","He reached out and said, \"Let me hold our daughter. You eat.\"","He took Xiaxia, cradling her in one arm, while Auntie Shi quickly prepared a bottle of milk powder and handed it to her. Xiaxia clutched the bottle and began to drink.","Xiaxia was still too young for solid food and needed six bottles a day. An'an was only two years old, but every time he saw his baby sister drinking milk, he wanted some too.","Qin Yuanzheng didn't stop him. If An'an wanted milk, he could have it—he had plenty of money for formula.","An'an also liked steamed buns, but this time, he was eating an awful lot.","As An'an climbed onto a chair and reached for a fourth bun, Qin Yuanzheng, who had been pretending not to notice, finally couldn't hold back.","He stared at An'an. \"Qin Qiao'an, how many buns have you had?\"","He could turn a blind eye to small matters, but these boys couldn't push it too far.","Sneaking one bun to Niuwa to tide him over was one thing, but the way An'an was going, he was trying to stuff Niuwa silly!","An'an was pretty scared of Qin Yuanzheng, since even Niuwa was afraid of him.","When Qin Yuanzheng called him out, An'an froze and didn't dare move, but he still clutched the two buns in his hands without letting go.","Qin Yuanzheng was already irritated by these two little rascals. He tapped the table and said, \"Your dad's asking you a question. How many have you taken?\"","An'an silently backed away, quietly climbed down from the chair, and furtively stuffed the two buns into his pockets.","But both his pockets were already stuffed with buns, so he couldn't fit anymore.","So he just shoved the two buns straight down the collar of his shirt, then said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Daddy, your voice scared me.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was left speechless again.","He glanced at Qiao Lanshu. She held back a laugh and said in a low voice, \"You spoke too harshly. He got scared.\"","Qin Yuanzheng had no reply.","His head was buzzing with frustration. He stared at An'an in silence, about to give him another lecture, when Xiaxia, who had finished her bottle, suddenly started crying.","An'an immediately said, \"Daddy, Sister's ringing!\"","Qin Yuanzheng was dumbfounded.","He hurried to comfort Xiaxia, and when he looked up again, An'an had already scurried away on his short little legs.","Qin Yuanzheng turned to Qiao Lanshu and said, \"What's up with An'an's way of talking? Even the birds the chief keeps talk more clearly than he does.\"","Qiao Lanshu had been laughing so hard at An'an's words. Defending her child, she said, \"An'an's only two. Saying that much at two is already amazing. Look, he even knows enough to tell you not to be so harsh and that his sister needs comforting when she cries.\"","Qin Yuanzheng muttered under his breath, \"Wife, don't spoil them too much. A doting mother raises failures.\"","Qiao Lanshu paused to reflect for a second, then said, \"If I'm the gentle one and you're the strict one, doesn't that balance out perfectly?\"","She added, \"It's not like both of us have to be harsh. How scared would the kids be? They're still so young. Don't be too hard on them.\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at his wife and felt helpless.","Every time he disciplined the kids, they'd go crying to Qiao Lanshu, and then she'd come back to scold him.","As he bounced Xiaxia in his arms, he said, \"Daughters are the best. My little girl is the sweetest.\"","Judging by Qiao Lanshu, his daughter would probably grow up to be calm and obedient.","As for those two boys... forget it. Thinking about them only gave him a headache.","An'an had snuck out with the buns and found Niuwa in the yard.","Niuwa was so moved his eyes were full of tears. \"An'an, you're my real little brother. I don't know what I'd do without you!\"","Then, while Qin Yuanzheng wasn't looking, they crouched on the ground and started wolfing down the buns.","An'an had brought four buns total. He ate one himself, and Niuwa polished off three.","Niuwa was still hungry, but he didn't dare say anything.","When Qin Yuanzheng came back to the yard after eating, Niuwa quickly jumped back into his horse stance, forgetting to even wipe the crumbs off his lips.","An'an, feeling guilty too, flashed Qin Yuanzheng a sweet smile and called out, \"Daddy.\"","Qin Yuanzheng patted him lightly on the head and said, \"Go inside, take a bath, and get to bed.\"","An'an dashed back into the house without a second thought.","Now that Niuwa had a full belly and had stolen a little rest, his horse stance was perfectly steady. He even puffed out his chest and met Qin Yuanzheng's eyes with an air of righteousness.","Qin Yuanzheng stared at him for a moment, then said, \"Alright. You go wash up and get to bed too.\"","Niuwa was stunned and immediately snapped to attention. \"Really?\"","That was it? That was such a light punishment!","Qin Yuanzheng's face turned serious. \"Of course it's true. I'm not your real father; I can't control you. Tomorrow morning, I'm taking you to the police station and letting your real dad deal with you.\"","Niuwa: “???”","Niuwa’s little face scrunched up. “I’m not going,” he said.","Was he kidding? Didn’t he have his pride to think about?","The top dog of the military compound, actually having been in a police station—how could he ever show his face around here again?","As he spoke, he went back to squatting in a horse stance.","He would rather do that than go to the public security bureau.","After a moment, Niuwa lowered his voice and said, “I know I was wrong. I won’t do it again.”","Qin Yuanzheng felt a bit helpless. He really couldn’t do anything with Niuwa.","What a stubborn ox!","When he grew up, heaven knew which girl he’d end up causing trouble for.","Since Niuwa had verbally admitted his mistake, no matter what he was thinking inside... well, Qin Yuanzheng couldn’t worry about that anymore.","It was getting late, so he made Niuwa hold the horse stance for an hour, then had him practice boxing, exhausting him completely.","Qin Yuanzheng had never disciplined Niuwa this harshly before.","Niuwa really had a rough time this time.","After he finished bathing, he was so tired he couldn’t even keep his eyes open. As he walked toward the room, he said to Auntie Shi, “Grandma Shi, I’m so hungry. Could you get me some steamed buns? And make me a bowl of malted milk, please...”","“No!”","Qin Yuanzheng stood at the door, staring sternly at Niuwa. “I told you, you’re not allowed to eat anything!”","Niuwa flinched in fright, his eyes snapping wide open.","Now, whenever he saw Qin Yuanzheng, he felt his legs aching and his hands hurting.","Because Qin Yuanzheng had said he liked fighting, he’d made him punch a sandbag for two hours.","Niuwa had truly been scared straight this time.","After being scolded by Qin Yuanzheng, he didn’t dare ask for food again and trudged back to his room pitifully.","Because his training had run late, An’an had already fallen asleep on the kang before he got back.","Auntie Shi sat at the table, mending clothes for Niuwa and An’an.","Boys of this age wore out their clothes the fastest, especially pants—they always had holes at the knees.","Auntie Shi took out all their torn pants, folded scraps of cloth into two or three layers, and patched them up so they’d last a bit longer.","After Niuwa returned, Auntie Shi went outside the room to check; the lights in the main hall and the yard were already off.","Qin Yuanzheng had also gone to bed.","Auntie Shi closed the door, walked to the kang, and looked at Niuwa lying on it with his eyes shut. She whispered, “Niuwa, Grandma has some rice cakes here. Do you want to eat?”","At the mention of food, Niuwa’s eyes lit up instantly. He whispered back, “Yes, yes, yes! Grandma, I want some.”","Auntie Shi had expected as much.","She opened her wardrobe, took out a cloth bag, and pulled out two pieces of jujube and millet rice cake.","She had saved them specially for Niuwa, knowing he’d be hungry.","She handed the cakes to him, and as he wolfed them down without lifting his head, she said quietly, “Niuwa, you need to behave, you know. Listen to your Dad Qin and Mother Qiao, all right? Don’t keep picking fights.”","Niuwa gobbled the cakes but didn’t answer.","Auntie Shi knew that whenever Niuwa didn’t want to agree or didn’t accept something in his heart, he’d stay silent.","He’d learned to be clever: if he didn’t say anything, he wasn’t agreeing, and if he didn’t agree, he could still do what he wanted.","Auntie Shi pressed on. “The kids in the military compound, their fathers are all military officers. Your real dad is the police chief, but a police chief isn’t as powerful as an officer, you know. If there’s ever a real fight, your dad won’t be as strong as theirs.”","Auntie Shi never hesitated to bring up Han Wenlin—it was the truth, after all.","Niuwa didn’t mind her saying all this, since he knew himself that he wasn’t Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu’s biological child.","Still, he got a little upset at that. “The police chief is still powerful. Before Han Wenlin became chief, he was a military officer too.”","Auntie Shi corrected him. “That was before he became chief. Now he’s not an officer anymore.”","Truth be told, Auntie Shi’s words were a bit biased—the police chief was also very important, and the police and military were two different systems entirely.","But Niuwa didn’t know that, and Auntie Shi genuinely thought officers were the best.","So after finishing his rice cakes, Niuwa fell silent for a while.","Auntie Shi went on. “There are children of brigade commanders, division commanders, and even the general’s kids in the compound. Are you going to fight them too?”","He’d already fought them—and they all called him boss.","He just didn’t dare say it out loud.","After thinking it over, Niuwa said, “Then I’ll join the army when I grow up. I’ll become an officer too. Then no one will dare mess with me!”","Auntie Shi: “...”","Great. All her lecturing had been useless.","Instead, she’d just stirred up his competitive streak.","She pushed him down onto the kang and said, “Sleep.”","Then she turned off the lamp by the kang.","Niuwa snuggled close to An’an, who was warm and cozy.","In a low voice, he muttered, “I’m going to be an officer. I’m going to be a general!”","Auntie Shi: “...”","Auntie Shi: “Just go to sleep. You can be the Jade Emperor in your dreams if you want.”","...","After Qin Yuanzheng returned to the room, he saw that Xiaxia was already asleep.","Qiao Lanshu was sitting at the desk, writing a practice test.","It was only a few months until the resumption of the college entrance exam, and the news should be coming out soon.","When the time came, a lot of people would sign up, and the competition would be fierce.","Although Qiao Lanshu felt confident, she still worried about not getting into her ideal school.","So every night before bed, she finished a test paper to practice.","When Qin Yuanzheng came in, he asked, “Did Niuwa go back to rest?”","Qin Yuanzheng nodded and sat beside her, watching her paper. He said softly, “He went back to sleep. That little rascal is really hard to manage.”","Qiao Lanshu comforted him. “Boys are like that—rambunctious. If he were as well-behaved as a girl, that would be more worrying.”","Qin Yuanzheng lowered his voice. “Han Wenlin came to see me again yesterday, saying he wants to take Niuwa back. Niuwa’s about to start elementary school, and there’s a school near the police station. He wants Niuwa to go there.”","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. “Niuwa definitely won’t go.”","He hadn’t wanted to go back before, and after living here for two years, there was even less chance now.","Qin Yuanzheng sighed, troubled by the matter. He looked at Qiao Lanshu’s profile and felt that his wife was becoming more beautiful every day.","Without another word, he picked her up and said, “Let’s stop talking about them. Time for bed.”"]},{"number":237,"title":"Chapter 237: Arranged a Childhood Betrothal","paragraphs":["Niuwa getting into fights outside was one thing, but he also had to drag An'an along.","Qin Yuanzheng felt that things couldn't go on like this.","So, to prevent Niuwa from causing trouble outside and then having the parents called in again,","Qin Yuanzheng decided that as soon as school was out, he would take Niuwa to the military unit.","Qin Yuanzheng was still working in the mining area of Dragon City, which had already been nicely developed nearby.","As long as the kids didn't run around recklessly, there was no danger.","Qin Yuanzheng didn't let Qiao Lanshu pick up Niuwa from school. Instead, he would take Niuwa to kindergarten when he went to work.","After Niuwa's classes ended, a guard would bring him to the military unit. If Qin Yuanzheng had time, he would personally train Niuwa.","If he was busy, he'd hand Niuwa over to the guard, who would take the boy to punch sandbags, practice boxing, and run laps on the training field.","In short, dealing with a high-energy kid like this boiled down to one word: exercise!","Niuwa had a heavy training load, so he got hungry fast. Qin Yuanzheng paid extra to the mess hall to arrange for Niuwa to have special meals there.","Every afternoon after school, Niuwa would be dragged off to train, and two hours later, starving, he'd follow the guard to the mess hall for dinner, where he'd wolf down four steamed buns—not counting the porridge and soup.","The unit's mess hall often had meat, and Niuwa, eating meat every day, was quite happy.","When Qin Yuanzheng asked him if he still wanted to go to the mining area for training, Niuwa nodded and said yes, because he could eat all the meat he wanted!","And so, Qin Yuanzheng managed to keep Niuwa in line, while An'an and Xiaxia were still little.","Qiao Lanshu settled into reviewing her studies for a while, and soon enough, the news of the resumption of the college entrance exams spread through the radio.","The whole nation was in an uproar.","Countless young people, especially the sent-down youth, scrambled to sign up.","As soon as the news of the resumed exams broke, it was followed by the announcement that the exams would be held in winter.","The country needed talent and couldn't wait until the next July, so the exams would be held that very winter.","This left everyone with virtually no time to prepare, but those who had kept up their studies or had a solid educational background were still confident.","When Qin Yuanzheng heard this news, the first person he thought of was Qiao Lanshu.","Standing in his office, listening to the broadcast, his expression grew serious.","Over the past two years of marriage, Qiao Lanshu had been relentlessly reading books, most of them middle school and high school textbooks. And in the past six months, she had often been doing practice problems.","Had she known all along that the country was going to resume the college entrance exams?","Qin Yuanzheng paced in place a couple of times.","Since Qiao Lanshu didn't mention it, he naturally didn't ask.","After some thought, he didn't rush home impulsively. Instead, he waited until the end of the workday, took Niuwa to the mess hall for dinner, and only drove home with Niuwa after the boy had eaten until his belly was round.","As soon as they got home, they found the place buzzing with activity.","Guan Wenjun and Zhong Mei had come over, along with Wang Xue, a former colleague of Qiao Lanshu's from the food factory.","They had all come to talk to Qiao Lanshu about the resumption of the college entrance exams.","News traveled slowly in those days, so whenever something big happened, everyone passed the word around, eager to make sure no one missed it.","Zhong Mei took Qiao Lanshu's hand and said, \"Lanshu, are you planning to take the exams?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded: \"Yes. Both my parents were college graduates; I can't let them down, and I'm sure they want me to go.\"","Qiao Lanshu had always wanted to go to university, but in her previous life, she never had the chance.","Coming back to this chance, she would not miss it this time.","Zhong Mei said enviously, \"You've always had good grades, and you even finished high school—you'll definitely pass the exam.\"","Zhong Mei had only completed a few years of elementary school and hadn't had the opportunity to study in recent years. Her education level was low, so there was no way for her to take the college entrance exam.","Wang Xue also said enviously, \"I can't take it either. I didn't even finish middle school, and my child is about to start junior high now. Oh, these opportunities are better left for the younger generation.\"","Wang Xue had come specifically to find Qiao Lanshu and tell her the news about the resumption of the college entrance exam. When she heard the news herself, Qiao Lanshu was the first person who came to mind.","To be honest, when the news of the exam's resumption spread, even though it caused nationwide excitement, there were actually very few people capable of signing up for it.","In those days, even getting enough to eat was difficult, and many people couldn't afford to go to school.","This was especially true for girls, who had to start doing housework, look after their younger siblings, and then follow their parents' arrangements—marrying early to save the family food and bring in a bride price.","Wang Xue shook her head and added, \"Going to university is great. Once you graduate from university, jobs are assigned directly. It's so hard to find a job these days. Passing the college entrance exam means you've got a secure, lifelong position.\"","When Zhong Mei heard this, she became even more envious.","She had been married to Guan Wenjun for a year, and although her household registration had long been settled, a job was still nowhere in sight.","It wasn't that Guan Wenjun wasn't helping her, but decent full-time positions were genuinely hard to come by.","Guan Wenjun told her not to worry, but Zhong Mei couldn't help it.","Wang Xue asked Qiao Lanshu again, \"Lanshu, have you decided which university to apply to?\"","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. \"I haven't made up my mind yet.\"","She needed to discuss it with Qin Yuanzheng. Now that she had a family and a child, there were more factors to consider.","But she did have a preference in mind; she just had to wait until Qin Yuanzheng came back to talk it over with him.","Wang Xue didn't stay long and left soon after.","Zhong Mei and Guan Wenjun stayed for dinner.","Qiao Lanshu asked Zhong Mei, \"Is your job situation still not resolved?\"","Zhong Mei shook her head and sighed. \"Guan Wenjun says there are no good openings right now, so we'll have to wait and see later.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"That makes sense. With the college entrance exam brought back, there's no telling what other changes might come. Better to wait—maybe in the future, job positions like that won't be so desirable.\"","After all, after the reform and opening-up, people who went into business would become rich and be big bosses—who would care about a few dozen yuan salary by then?","Zhong Mei sighed again and said, \"Guan Wenjun mentioned that they're bringing electricity to the countryside these days, so a lot of meter readers will be needed. He might be able to buy a position for me later.\"","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu smiled. \"It looks like Section Chief Guan is reliable after all—he even knows about that kind of job. He's definitely been asking around for you.\"","Zhong Mei nodded, glancing at Xiaxia, who was crawling around on the heated bed, and sighed.","When she and Guan Wenjun got married, An'an still couldn't walk. Now, even Xiaxia was crawling.","Guan Wenjun had been urging her to have a child. She didn't know why, but he was desperate for a baby.","Zhong Mei had been building up her health for a year now. She was eating well and her body was better nourished, but still—why hadn't she gotten pregnant?","During dinner, Qin Yuanzheng came back with Niuwa.","Niuwa had already eaten his fill in the army canteen, but when he got home and saw the meal Auntie Shi had prepared, he could still manage a little more.","As soon as Qin Yuanzheng returned, he washed his hands and face, changed into a clean set of clothes, and came out of the room holding Xiaxia in his arms.","When Guan Wenjun saw this, he immediately latched onto him, gazing enviously at Xiaxia in Qin Yuanzheng's arms. He said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Lao Qin, come on, let me hold her. I haven't held little Xiaxia in ages.\"","With that, Guan Wenjun reached out his hands to take Xiaxia.","But Qin Yuanzheng avoided his grasp, looking at him with disdain. He said, \"You've been working all day—aren't you dirty?\"","Guan Wenjun was speechless. He said, \"I already washed my hands ages ago. See? My hands are very clean.\"","Qin Yuanzheng ignored him. \"That's still not good enough. If you want to hold a baby, go have one of your own.\"","Then he suddenly added, \"But it's a pity—you couldn't produce a daughter as adorable as this.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun was furious inside, but he had nothing to say, because Xiaxia really was too cute. Although looks have something to do with genetics, a lot of it is still innate. Good looks aren't something you can envy your way into.","Guan Wenjun said sourly, \"You're a big, rough guy, dark as coal—how did you end up with... oh, two little glutinous rice dumplings? Heaven has been way too generous with you, Lao Qin!\"","Xiaxia took after her mother in looks, while An'an took more after his father. But both children got their skin from their mother—fair as jade and snow, rosy and lovely. They were truly two beautiful children.","Qin Yuanzheng said smugly, \"Don't envy me. However much you envy me, you'll never have what I've got.\"","Guan Wenjun said stubbornly, \"My son is going to be very handsome too, you know.\"","After all, Zhong Mei was already very beautiful, and having gained a bit of weight this year, she looked even better.","Guan Wenjun felt his son's looks probably wouldn't be too shabby either. So he lowered his voice and said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Lao Qin, how about this—let's arrange a childhood betrothal first. Make your Xiaxia my future daughter-in-law, what do you think? We know each other inside out, and Zhong Mei and Xiao Qiao are good sisters. If Xiaxia comes to our house, we'll definitely treat her well. I'll dote on her like my own daughter...\"","\"Get lost.\"","Qin Yuanzheng gave him a chilly look. \"It's getting late. You'd better go home and get some sleep—you can dream about anything there.\"","Guan Wenjun said indignantly, \"What's the matter with you? What's so wrong with being my daughter-in-law? I'm at least the section chief of the Supply Division. Being married into the Guan family wouldn't be shabby for Xiaxia, would it?\"","Qin Yuanzheng snorted coldly. \"Anyway, don't even think about it.\"","He had already made up his mind: he would stay in the military for life—no retirement, no transfer to civilian work. Later, when his daughter grew up, his rank would likely go up a few more notches. By then, he'd find an officer from the military region as her husband. Just imagine—his future son-in-law wouldn't dare to disobey him.","Or he could find someone willing to marry into the family, and that would be even better—that son-in-law would be even more afraid to step out of line.","If any son-in-law dared to bully his Xiaxia, he'd personally go teach him a lesson!","As for Guan Wenjun—he'd better give up. Whether he could even father a son was still in question.","Guan Wenjun wouldn't give up and kept pestering Qin Yuanzheng with grumbles. When Zhong Mei and Qiao Lanshu saw this from inside the house, Qiao Lanshu said with a smile, \"Section Chief Guan seems to really like daughters. Look—every time he comes, he can't take his eyes off Xiaxia.\"","Zhong Mei snorted coldly and said, \"It's not that he wants a daughter. He wants Xiaxia to be his daughter-in-law!\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Zhong Mei sighed and then said, \"We don’t even have a son yet, and he’s already thinking about a daughter-in-law. I’ve never seen anyone more impatient than him.\"","Qiao Lanshu was at a loss for words as well.","She stood up and walked over, taking Xiaxia from Qin Yuanzheng’s arms.","Guan Wenjun immediately chimed in, \"Hey, Comrade Xiao Qiao, let me hold Xiaxia for a bit, let me soak up some good luck.\"","Qiao Lanshu shot him a glare and said, \"No.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun lowered his voice and asked Qin Yuanzheng, \"What’s wrong with Comrade Xiao Qiao? I didn’t offend her, did I?\"","Qin Yuanzheng had no idea either; he could only say, \"You’ve never been well-liked, didn’t you know that?\"","Guan Wenjun was used to getting brushed off here.","So he didn’t take it to heart. The couple stayed for dinner, and afterward, they left together.","As soon as they were out the door, Guan Wenjun couldn’t help himself. He wrapped an arm around Zhong Mei, reached out to touch her belly, and whispered, \"Wife, we’ve got to have a son soon, or we won’t make it in time to marry Xiaxia.\"","Zhong Mei had already grown tired of arguing with Guan Wenjun. She was silent for a moment before saying, \"Having a child depends on fate too; let’s just let it happen naturally.\"","...","That night, as they lay down to sleep, Qin Yuanzheng held Qiao Lanshu and chatted.","Qin Yuanzheng finally asked the question he’d been holding in all day: \"Wife, did you already know that the college entrance exams were going to be restored?\"","Qin Yuanzheng thought back to how Qiao Lanshu knew how to drive, and at the time, she’d said she learned it from him in a dream.","He lowered his voice and said, \"You’re not going to tell me that this was something you learned from me in a dream too, are you?\"","Nestled in his arms, Qiao Lanshu laughed and said, \"No, I found out from listening to the radio in my dream.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at her with a calm gaze. Under the dim yellow light, his young wife was smiling at him, the dimples by her lips growing more adorable the longer he looked.","Qin Yuanzheng stared at her in silence for a moment, then asked, \"What other dreams have you had? Tell me all about them.\"","Leaning against his sturdy chest, Qiao Lanshu said, \"Well, there’s not much else. In the dream, you became a division commander, you were very good to me, and we were deeply in love and very happy.\"","Qin Yuanzheng didn’t used to believe in such things, but now, looking at Qiao Lanshu’s beaming face, he felt that perhaps some things science couldn’t explain might actually be real.","Qin Yuanzheng asked with keen interest, \"And in that dream, did you get into college?\"","Qiao Lanshu’s expression faltered. She paused for a few seconds before forcing a smile and saying, \"Yes, I did.\"","Qin Yuanzheng held her tighter, his expression turning serious, and then asked, \"What about An’an and Xiaxia? How were they? What jobs did they have when they grew up? Did they get married?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","In the dream, of course, there were no children. She had married Qin Yuanzheng at thirty, and he had passed away five years later.","They had no children, and that was Qiao Lanshu’s greatest regret.","Qin Yuanzheng looked at her intently: \"What’s wrong? Did you not dream about that part?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"I only dreamed of fragments; it wasn’t like I lived a whole life from start to finish.\"","As she spoke, her voice grew heavier. \"In the dream, there was no An’an, and no Xiaxia. I didn’t dream of them.\"","Qin Yuanzheng noticed that Qiao Lanshu was in a bad mood, so he quickly said, \"It's okay, not dreaming is also a good thing. Those two children are a gift from heaven to us. They have their own unknown paths in life. If you could predict everything in your dreams, wouldn't that make you a prophet?\"","Qin Yuanzheng patted Qiao Lanshu reassuringly and then asked her, \"In your dream, which school did you get into?\"","Qiao Lanshu replied, \"I was fooling you. In my dream, I didn't take the college entrance exam at all.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu gave him a kiss and said gently, \"Brother Zheng, what do you think of me becoming a teacher in the future?\"","Qin Yuanzheng, still not fully recovered from the intimacy of her kiss, immediately nodded upon hearing this. \"That sounds great. You want to be a teacher?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded.","She had actually thought about many options—perhaps entering politics and working in a government position, or studying fashion design, or even architecture, and later going into business to become a big boss.","But after much deliberation, she felt she wanted to spend more time on the family, focusing on raising the two children.","Qin Yuanzheng was very busy in the military, often leaving home for missions.","So she couldn't be too busy herself—whether working in a government role or running a business, neither seemed suitable.","Moreover, given Qin Yuanzheng's position, their family had enough money. They already had a house and a car, and their current priority was educating the children well.","She said, \"Being a teacher is great. I'll have winter and summer breaks to spend time with the kids. My work hours will match the children's school schedule—when they get out of school, I'll be off work too. I can keep an eye on An'an and Niuwa at school. What do you think?\"","She planned to apply for a teacher's college, graduate, and then teach at a middle school, continuing on to pursue a master's degree.","In those days, getting into graduate school was extremely difficult, with fierce competition, but Qiao Lanshu wanted to give it a try.","After all, life needed some aspirations—otherwise, what was the difference between that and being a walking corpse?","And following the reform and opening up, being a teacher was quite relaxed. The profession was respected, benefits were decent, and it was a good job overall.","As Qin Yuanzheng listened to Qiao Lanshu lay out her plans, he naturally agreed. He said, \"That's great, Teacher Qiao. I support you. I'm sure you'll get in.\""]},{"number":238,"title":"Chapter 238: Got Admitted to University","paragraphs":["After Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu discussed it together, Qiao Lanshu initially settled on a school: she would apply to the Normal University in the neighboring city of Wencheng.","Wencheng was a fairly important city, being a provincial capital with promising future development.","Moreover, the Normal University in Wencheng had been established for many years and housed many highly respected senior scholars.","More importantly, Wencheng wasn't far from Longcheng. If Qin Yuanzheng's job didn't get transferred anytime soon, he wouldn't have to drive too long to commute back and forth.","Once the decision was made, Qiao Lanshu set this school as her first choice.","Time flew by. In December, Qiao Lanshu, along with thousands of young people, took the college entrance exam.","The exam results came out quickly, and Qiao Lanshu performed excellently—she achieved the highest total score in the entire province.","Before Qin Yuanzheng had even gotten off work, many people came to congratulate him: \"Commander, we heard your wife is the provincial top scorer—impressive!\"","Another comrade-in-arms said, \"Brigade Commander, this might make you a bit unworthy of Ma'am now. With her being so educated, you can't lag too far behind, right?\"","Qin Yuanzheng was in a great mood and didn't mind these remarks. He said, \"This is my fate. I'm lucky, and you guys can't be jealous of that.\"","As he spoke, he drove out of the military base and headed straight to the headquarters.","He then went directly to Commander Li's office.","Commander Li was busy and was a bit surprised to see him. \"Why are you here?\" he asked.","As soon as Qin Yuanzheng entered, he started looking around, saying, \"Commander, a provincial top scorer has come out of our military families. As the district commander, shouldn't you offer something to show your appreciation?\"","Upon hearing this, Commander Li put down his pen.","He looked astonished. \"Oh? Is that so?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. He wandered around the office for a bit, then casually opened a box on Commander Li's desk to take a look.","The box contained pastries—at a glance, there were green bean cakes, red bean cakes, and purple potato cakes, all shaped like flowers.","Qin Yuanzheng's eyes lit up, and he reached out to grab one.","Commander Li immediately slapped his hand away, annoyed. \"What do you think you're doing? Acting like a bandit? Robbing me outright!\"","Qin Yuanzheng stared at the box of pastries, reluctant to let go. \"Commander, it's just a box of pastries. Think of it as a reward for the provincial top scorer. That's the province's top scorer—how many years has it been since we've seen one around here?\"","Commander Li snorted. \"Yes, it's been many years. After all, the college entrance exam only resumed this year.\"","Qin Yuanzheng said matter-of-factly, \"So, giving the top scorer a little gift shouldn't be a problem, right?\"","Commander Li watched Qin Yuanzheng's smug behavior and slowly caught on. He looked at Qin Yuanzheng suspiciously and said, \"Judging by how cocky you are, could it be that the provincial top scorer is your wife?\"","Qin Yuanzheng coughed a couple of times, barely able to hide the gleam in his eyes. \"That's right—it's Comrade Qiao Lanshu. As a military family member, she's been proactive and diligent in her studies, taking care of her husband and children while still achieving such outstanding results. Commander, the military district should reward her as a gesture of encouragement.\"","Commander Li: \"...\"","Commander Li was thoroughly exasperated with Qin Yuanzheng.","He pointed a finger at Qin Yuanzheng, intending to scold him, but then again, the provincial top scorer was indeed exceptional.","Still, he said, \"There's no precedent for this sort of thing. Rewards should be handled by the neighborhood committee. The military isn't really supposed to get involved. However...\"","Qin Yuanzheng quickly interjected, \"However, you could give it as a personal gift from you—send a box of pastries to the excellent Comrade Qiao Lanshu as a token of encouragement.\"","With that, Qin Yuanzheng grabbed the box of pastries and turned to leave. \"On behalf of Comrade Qiao Lanshu, thank you, Commander.\"","Commander Li: \"...\"","Commander Li fumed, \"Get out! I don't want to see you for the next few days!\"","The box of pastries had only been in his office for less than two hours before Qin Yuanzheng whisked it away.","That rascal Qin Yuanzheng had clearly come to scope out his place because he couldn't find anything nice to delight his wife.","It was just like when he first got married—he'd swept through the office, taking a bunch of rice and sweet potatoes.","Commander Li paced around his office in irritation a few times, then walked to the door and asked the guard on duty, \"Have the college exam results come out? Is Qin Yuanzheng's wife really the provincial top scorer?\"","News of this had already spread throughout the military district as soon as it broke.","Now, countless people were envious of Qin Yuanzheng.","Before, when he was nearly thirty and unmarried with rumors of infertility, everyone pitied him.","But now? He had both a son and a daughter, his wife had gotten into university, and she was even the provincial top scorer—such good fortune made others green with envy.","The guard nodded. \"Yes, Commander. Reporters from Longcheng Daily have already gone to interview her.\"","Commander Li had been stuck in his office all day, so he'd heard the news a bit late.","Now that he knew, he rubbed his nearly bald head and said, \"Yuanzheng really is a lucky guy.\"","...","Qin Yuanzheng carried the box of pastries he'd taken from the commander's office and couldn't wait to drive home.","As soon as he arrived, he saw a crowd gathered at the entrance of the compound. He drove in and asked the guard, \"What's going on at the gate? Why so many people?\"","The guard quickly replied, \"Brigade Commander, they're all reporters. They want to interview our provincial top scorer.\"","Since this was a military compound, the guard couldn't let them in, so he had them wait outside while he reported inside.","Qin Yuanzheng thought for a moment. An interview could be a good thing, but he wasn't sure if Qiao Lanshu would be willing to appear publicly.","He said, \"I'll go back and ask my wife. Have them wait a little longer.\"","The guard nodded and hurried back to the gate.","When Qin Yuanzheng got home, he saw Qiao Lanshu and Auntie Shi sitting in the yard, looking at the score report.","Niuwa and An'an were playing in the yard, while Xiaxia was sleeping in a cradle.","It was a peaceful, idyllic scene.","Qin Yuanzheng stood at the door watching for a moment. Then Qiao Lanshu spotted him.","She jumped up excitedly and ran over, saying happily, \"Brother Zheng, look! I got into university!\"","Qin Yuanzheng crouched slightly, then suddenly scooped up the running Qiao Lanshu and spun her around twice. He laughed and said, \"I know—I got the news! I never thought an illiterate guy like me could marry a top scorer. My ancestors must have blessed me.\"","Of course, Qin Yuanzheng wasn't entirely illiterate—he had joined the army early and attended a military academy there. But if he hadn't enlisted, he wouldn't have gone to university, and he didn't believe he could have passed the exam.","Yet his wife was incredibly capable.","Absolutely amazing!","After spinning her around, he suddenly said, \"Sweetheart, let's go eat out today. I want to treat my friends!\"","With a wife as impressive as his, he had to tell everyone.","Qiao Lanshu nodded happily and said, \"We should. I'll invite my friends too. It's rare to get together, so let's treat everyone to the state-run restaurant.\"","Now that she'd gotten into university, Qiao Lanshu would soon be heading to Wencheng to study.","They would surely have to relocate the whole family there.","A helicopter airport was being built in Wencheng, and Zhao Jiannong and his wife Huang Erling were already over there.","Qiao Lanshu also planned to meet with Huang Erling once she arrived in Wencheng.","Ever since Huang Erling moved away, Qiao Lanshu couldn’t find anyone to help her make quilts and cotton-padded jackets anymore.","Qin Yuanzheng handed Qiao Lanshu the box of pastries and said, “By the way, this is a gift from our Commander. You’ve never had anything like it before—come on, try some.”","Qiao Lanshu looked a little surprised and said, “Is it from Commander Li? He’s too kind, even sending such beautiful pastries...”","Inside, there were five different flavors, each with five pieces, shaped like little flowers in various colors—absolutely lovely.","Qiao Lanshu put the pastries on the table, gazing at them again and again, reluctant to eat them.","Seeing her like this warmed Qin Yuanzheng’s heart. He knew Qiao Lanshu would like them.","He’d just have to ask Commander Li to part with them for now. Next time, he’d see if he could find any rare goods to send over to Commander Li, so the old man wouldn’t keep fussing.","Auntie Shi also took a look and sighed, saying, “These pastries definitely aren’t cheap. They’re beautiful, and they look delicious too.”","Niuwa perked up the moment he heard about food.","By then, he had already dashed over carrying An’an on his back: “Mom, what’s good to eat?”","He reached out, but Qiao Lanshu slapped his hand away: “You little black cat, go wash your paws first before you come eat.”","So Niuwa took An’an and ran off to wash their hands.","The whole family sat together and tasted the pastries.","After finishing the pastries and tea, Qin Yuanzheng accompanied Qiao Lanshu outside to be interviewed by reporters.","This time, the interview even involved taking Qiao Lanshu’s photo, with plans to publish it in the newspaper.","A total of three newspaper agencies interviewed Qiao Lanshu.","Then, staff members from the local street office also arrived, handing Qiao Lanshu a two-hundred-yuan bonus. They said that the top three spots at the provincial level each received money—the top scorer got two hundred, the second one hundred, and the third fifty.","This reward was meant to support their studies, as a great number of people had registered for this year’s college entrance exam.","Among them, most were sent-down youth and factory workers, and some even included those previously labeled as the “Five Black Categories”.","Although college tuition, room, and board were all covered after they were admitted, these students might not even have enough money for the train tickets to school.","Thus, this bonus was also called “travel expenses.”","But not everyone who got into college was eligible.","Only provincial top scorers like Qiao Lanshu received this. Other admitted students probably didn’t, though their local street offices, production brigades, or sent-down youth stations might offer some encouragement and support.","Qiao Lanshu took the two hundred yuan and said, “Thank you.”","The street office staff were very excited: “Comrade Xiao Qiao is really outstanding! With so many people registering for the exam this year, who would have thought the top scorer would come from right here?”","The 1977 college entrance exam was arguably one of the most competitive rounds ever. Over 5.7 million people took part, but only 270,000 were admitted—the admission rate was extremely low.","Wencheng Normal University, where Qiao Lanshu had applied, admitted only seven hundred students across its fifteen majors.","Under such circumstances, every student who got into college enjoyed a high social status and was almost guaranteed a good job in the future.","Passing the exam was nearly equivalent to passing the imperial examinations in ancient times—a future full of promise.","So, many people came to see Qiao Lanshu that day—delegates from various departments.","Qiao Lanshu felt a bit overwhelmed, so Qin Yuanzheng helped fend them off.","After three days like this, Qiao Lanshu was finally able to rest in peace.","One evening while resting, Qin Yuanzheng hugged Qiao Lanshu and let out a sigh.","Qiao Lanshu looked at him: “Why sigh? Aren’t you happy I got into college?”","Qin Yuanzheng replied, “How could I not be? I’m very happy.”","But he was thinking that Qiao Lanshu would be going to college now, and she was only twenty years old—at her most vibrant and beautiful age.","And she was so pretty.","If, on campus, she met other young, educated male classmates who shared her interests, would her heart waver?","Qin Yuanzheng was usually very confident.","Only in matters of the heart was he insecure.","What could he do? He was married to such a beautiful, young, and educated wife.","He held Qiao Lanshu tighter and said softly, “Wife, when you go to school, will you be staying in the dormitory?”","Qiao Lanshu thought for a moment and responded, “If it’s not mandatory, then I won’t. But if we haven’t moved yet, I can stay there for a while first. After you’ve found a house, we can slowly bring the kids over.”","Hearing that, Qin Yuanzheng got very uneasy.","Qiao Lanshu alone in Wencheng for her studies, sleeping away from home every night, while he stayed home with the children?","Absolutely not.","He couldn’t live without his wife.","He immediately couldn’t sleep anymore and sat up abruptly, saying, “I’ll call Zhao Jianlin and ask him to help find a house.”","Qiao Lanshu quickly pulled him back: “Oh, it’s the middle of the night! Let’s wait a couple of days. There’s no rush—we still have until March before school starts.”","But Qin Yuanzheng couldn’t sleep. After thinking it over, he added, “Or I could apply for a transfer to Wencheng. There’s a military garrison over there—I could go just in time.”","However, if he were transferred, it would be as the garrison’s regional commander. Although it was a lateral move, it meant becoming the top person in the branch, and there would be plenty of competition.","Over the past two years, he’d been busy taking care of his wife and children, neglecting to pursue such positions. Before Qiao Lanshu decided to take the college entrance exam, he had started trying again.","But he still hadn’t found an opportunity.","Qiao Lanshu saw that it was late at night, and he was still not sleeping—now even getting dressed.","She got up as well and scolded him, “It’s already past midnight, and it’s snowing outside. Where do you think you’re going?”","Qin Yuanzheng, while putting on his coat, came over and kissed her, rubbing her cheek and saying, “I’m going to the Commander’s place. You go to sleep first—don’t wait up for me.”","With that, he hurried off.","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","She muttered to herself, “Why be in such a rush?”","Honestly, staying in the dormitory for a while wouldn’t be a problem. After all, school management was fairly strict back then, and not just anyone could enter the campus.","The dormitory was quite safe.","After Qin Yuanzheng left, Qiao Lanshu couldn’t sleep either.","She got up and took out her transcript, gazing at it over and over again. The happier she got, the more she smiled.","Regrets from her past life—aside from not having children with Brother Zheng—included never being able to attend university.","She had always wanted to go to college.","Now, in this life, her dream had come true.","She placed the transcript by the desk and began writing a letter to her father far away in Yangcheng.","She told him she had been admitted to college, and that she planned to become a teacher in the future.","She also asked about the family’s situation.","At the end, she enclosed the transcript in the envelope, sealed it with wax, and affixed a stamp, planning to mail it the next day.","She had never mentioned Zhong Mei’s matter to her father, afraid that Zhong Mei’s family might track her down through him, and end up ruining her peaceful life.","Qiao Lanshu stared out the window at the swirling snowflakes, full of anticipation for her university life ahead."]},{"number":239,"title":"Chapter 239: Going to Wencheng","paragraphs":["After the New Year, when spring arrived in March, the first batch of those who had passed the university entrance exams were to report to their schools.","During this time, Qin Yuanzheng was busy applying for a transfer order, while Qiao Lanshu was preparing for the move.","Qin Yuanzheng had said that no matter whether his transfer order came through or not, once Qiao Lanshu went to report to the university, their whole family would relocate there.","After all, he couldn't bear to be apart from his wife.","One morning, Qin Yuanzheng arrived early at the headquarters building to meet his old superior, Commander Li.","In the morning, they first held a routine meeting. When the meeting ended and everyone was about to leave, Qin Yuanzheng stayed behind in the office.","Commander Li noticed he had stayed and gave him a few appraising looks. Then, without a word, he quietly put away the two oranges on the table, tucking them into a drawer.","Qin Yuanzheng: “...”","Somewhat speechless, Qin Yuanzheng said, “Commander, is this really necessary? You’re guarding against me like I’m some bandit.”","Commander Li snorted, glaring at him, and said, “Aren’t you a bandit? You’re not far off from one.”","Qin Yuanzheng couldn’t help but laugh. Then he said, “Commander, you have to believe me—I really do want to show my respect for you. It’s just that I have a wife and kids to support at home, and we’re poor, so I don’t have anything nice to offer.”","At that time, military personnel indeed didn’t earn much. Many officers who had been promoted later often made less than their subordinates.","This situation wouldn’t improve until the 1980s, when the military underwent internal adjustments, redefining ranks and salary structures, which eventually boosted soldiers’ incomes.","For now, Qin Yuanzheng’s salary was just enough to support his family, so he certainly had no spare money to give Commander Li as a tribute.","Commander Li didn’t really expect such gifts from his subordinates anyway; he was just teasing Qin Yuanzheng, who always showed up like a locust swarm, cleaning out all the good stuff.","Commander Li cast a sidelong glance at him and said, “Cut it out. Don’t come crying poverty to me. Here, I’ll give you two.”","He said this as he pulled two plump, bright red oranges from the drawer, adding, “These were sent by my son-in-law from distant Xiangcheng. They’re still fresh. Take them home for your wife to taste.”","Qin Yuanzheng smiled and said to Commander Li, “Commander, this time you’ve misunderstood me. I stayed behind not because I had my eye on your oranges.”","Even as he said that, he reached out, took the two oranges, and stuffed them into his pocket.","Commander Li glared at him and reached out to grab them back. “No? If not, give them back. Come on, hand them over.”","Qin Yuanzheng certainly wasn’t about to return them. His wife had a real weakness for those southern oranges and tangerines, which were hard to come by. Finding ready-made ones, he couldn’t bear to give them up.","He covered his pocket with one hand and pulled a packet of tea from his trouser pocket with the other, pressing it into Commander Li’s hand. “Commander, freshly pan-fried Mingqian Longjing tea, sent by my father-in-law from Yangcheng. Try it.”","Commander Li: “???”","He looked at the tea in his hand, his expression stunned as he stared at Qin Yuanzheng.","After a few moments, Commander Li placed the tea on the table, stood up, came around from behind his desk, and circled Qin Yuanzheng twice.","Qin Yuanzheng just stood there, watching as Commander Li looked him up and down from head to toe.","Qin Yuanzheng frowned. \"Commander, what exactly are you doing?\"","Commander Li walked up to him, reached out sternly, and punched him in the shoulder, asking angrily, \"Nothing for nothing. Out with it—what mistake did you make?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Commander Li was a fierce general on the battlefield in his younger days and hadn't let his martial skills rust. The punch landed hard, making Qin Yuanzheng wince.","Qin Yuanzheng rubbed his shoulder and said helplessly, \"Commander, I really just thought this Qingqian tea was good, so I specially brought a pack for you. Don't you like tea?\"","Commander Li sneered. \"In all these years, this is the first time I've ever received anything from you. You're usually so stingy—why the sudden generosity? Don't tell me you haven't done something wrong!\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","He couldn't help but reflect inwardly—was he really that stingy?","Not really, was he?","Then again, he had never actually given Commander Li anything before.","He thought to himself with a clear conscience: Giving gifts to a superior is bribery—he couldn't do that.","Qin Yuanzheng cleared his throat and said to Commander Li, \"Commander, I really haven't made any mistakes. I have a wife and a child now—how could I not be extra careful?\"","He paused, then finally stated today's purpose: \"I just wanted to ask—how far along is the application for my transfer order? Has it been approved or not?\"","Commander Li was the commander-in-chief of this military region, with authority over the forces in several surrounding cities.","The neighboring city of Wencheng, of course, fell under his jurisdiction.","As one of his veteran subordinates, Qin Yuanzheng was just applying for a transfer to Wencheng—it wasn't a big deal. Commander Li should have agreed.","Besides, there wasn't much going on at the mining area. Qin Yuanzheng had already arranged everything.","Hearing this, Commander Li let out a cold snort, returned to his desk, and sat down without speaking. He picked up the tea pack, opened it to have a look, sniffed it, and then said, \"Fetch me the thermos.\"","The guard at the door heard him and was about to enter.","Qin Yuanzheng quickly said, \"No need, let me do it.\"","With that, he personally picked up the thermos and brewed a pot of tea for Commander Li.","Commander Li glared at him, annoyed. This was his most prized subordinate, but also his biggest headache.","Before, the headache was that Qin Yuanzheng never married—he worried the man would end up alone.","Now, it was the opposite—he was too love-sick, always thinking about staying home, with none of the drive he used to have.","Commander Li snorted. \"What a waste of potential!\"","Qin Yuanzheng set down the thermos and said, \"How am I a waste?\"","Commander Li: \"Running after your wife all day long—isn't that a waste?\"","Qin Yuanzheng rubbed his nose and started playing the sympathy card. \"Commander, you know, getting a wife wasn't easy for me. Really, very not easy! On top of that, my wife is still so young. She's going to college—young, beautiful, educated, cultured. What am I? Just a rough guy who doesn't understand romance. Tell me, if I don't keep a close eye on her, what if she's lured away at school by some smooth-talking male student who knows all about romance?\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at Commander Li and asked, \"When that happens, could you find me another wife as good as her?\"","Commander Li: \"...\"","He really had enough of Qin Yuanzheng’s shamelessness. Unable to bear it any longer, he said, “Keep an eye on your own wife. If she can be stolen away that easily, that’s your fault. What’s it got to do with me?”","As if he could just conjure up another woman for him—did he look like the god of matchmaking, making wishes here?","Qin Yuanzheng sat down beside him and said, “Exactly, I plan to watch her myself. That’s why I want to go to Wencheng. Commander, just approve my transfer order. I know there’s an opening in that military district.”","It was rare for Qin Yuanzheng to speak so humbly to Commander Li.","Commander Li, having had his fill of amusement, finally pulled out the transfer order he had already signed and approved long ago. “Alright, alright, it’s been done for a while now. Take it.”","Commander Li had a sharp tongue but a soft heart. He was protective of his people and held great affection for the subordinates he had personally groomed.","As it happened, the military reform was underway, with hundreds of thousands of soldiers being transferred to civilian posts and various military districts undergoing restructuring.","Thus, Qin Yuanzheng’s application had long been approved, and the transfer order had already been issued.","However, the various military districts still needed time to handle the handover and coordination, so Qin Yuanzheng couldn’t head to Wencheng just yet.","But that wasn’t a problem. Even if the final appointment hadn’t been announced, he could still move to Wencheng in advance.","Auntie Shi’s home was in Longcheng, but she was willing to go along this time. After all, Qin Yuanzheng paid her well, and after all these years, they had built some rapport. She felt that if she left this household, she’d have to find another one, and it might not be as easygoing as Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng.","Besides, Qin Yuanzheng had even arranged work for her son.","Her son was now working on the airport project in Wencheng. He had started by hauling bricks, doing hard labor under army supervision for months, and grew as thin as a bamboo pole—but he had tough it out.","Eventually, he was transferred to logistics. Though he wasn’t a permanent employee yet, the work was much lighter, and the benefits were decent. Auntie Shi was already deeply grateful.","If she went to Wencheng with them, she could also see her son more often.","The next issue, naturally, was Niuwa.","One day, Han Wenlin took time out of his busy schedule to visit, toting some pork.","Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng received him together.","The three of them sat in the courtyard talking, while Niuwa and An’an played outside and hadn’t come back yet.","Han Wenlin was a little disappointed not to see his son.","Qin Yuanzheng said to him, “Been busy at the Public Security Bureau lately?”","Han Wenlin nodded. “Yes. The Revolutionary Committees have been dissolved, and their work is gradually being handed over to us. We’re short-staffed at the bureau. I heard the military reform is happening, and some soldiers will be transferred over. That should help.”","It was now 1978, and changes weren’t limited to the military—every major department was undergoing transformation.","The times were turbulent, policies were shifting drastically, and in the future, it wouldn’t just be the Public Security Bureau under pressure; other departments would face their own strain.","Qin Yuanzheng knew this well. After a moment of silence, he said, “My wife is going to Wencheng for university. She received her acceptance letter long ago and needs to report in March. I’ve already applied for housing, and we’ll be moving in the next few days. What’s your take on Niuwa?”","Niuwa had been staying with them. Since Han Wenlin lived nearby, he could drop by now and then, have a meal, take Niuwa to school, and pick him up afterward.","Although the father and son didn’t live together, Han Wenlin could still see Niuwa almost every day.","Now that he was moving to Wencheng, wouldn’t that mean they would barely see each other all year long?","Han Wenlin was currently the director of the Longcheng City Public Security Bureau, and his job was unlikely to change anytime soon—at least for the next three years, he would have to stay in Longcheng.","Qiao Lanshu was moving to Wencheng for college, and since her program was three years long, she might not move back to Longcheng even after graduation.","Besides, Qin Yuanzheng had also applied for a transfer, likely to work at the military district in Wencheng.","Han Wenlin was silent for a long time before letting out a deep sigh. He said, “Thank you both for helping me take care of Niuwa over the past two years.”","Niuwa had been well cared for; he had grown tall and sturdy. After training with Qin Yuanzheng, he had become quite skilled in martial arts—it was fair to say he was the toughest kid in the military compound.","Even so, Han Wenlin decided it was time to bring Niuwa back to live with him.","He said to Qin Yuanzheng, “Last year, I went back to my hometown to see my mother. When the old lady heard that Niuwa refused to come home with me, she started clamoring to come to Longcheng, saying she wanted to take care of him herself.”","The old lady still had a bond with Niuwa, though it was hard to say whether Niuwa felt the same way about his grandmother.","Han Wenlin added, “I’ll talk to Niuwa and see what he thinks.”","Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu exchanged glances. Qiao Lanshu sighed softly, feeling a little reluctant to let Niuwa go.","She said to Han Wenlin, “If Niuwa doesn’t want to leave, he can come with us to Longcheng. We don’t mind the trouble.”","Han Wenlin certainly knew that.","But to be honest, he also didn’t want to part with his son.","After all, Niuwa was still just a child.","When dusk fell, Niuwa came home with An’an. Han Wenlin called the muddy boy over and had a chat with him.","Niuwa was now seven years old and would be starting first grade this year. He was already quite sensible.","As Han Wenlin talked about these things, Niuwa said firmly at first, “I want to go with my mom. I don’t want to live with you.”","Han Wenlin had heard these words countless times and had long since grown numb to them.","He nodded and said, “But your grandmother is coming here soon. She hasn’t seen you in a long time and misses you very much. She knows Dad’s busy with work and can’t cook well, so she’s traveled a long way to come and make meals for you.”","Han Wenlin looked at Niuwa’s hesitant face and said softly, “When you were little, you loved the steamed buns your grandmother made, and the shepherd’s purse dumplings she wrapped. Do you still remember?”","Niuwa frowned, standing there with his head down, kicking at small stones.","Han Wenlin watched him without saying more, knowing that Niuwa was torn.","When Niuwa was three, he had lived with his grandmother. He was gifted for his age and already had memories from that time.","He even remembered being taken by snatchers and put onto a train—he remembered all of it.","After watching Niuwa struggle silently for a while, Han Wenlin said, “Your grandmother will be arriving soon. She’s come all this way, making a difficult journey, so please stay and keep her company, alright?”","The old lady was indeed getting old—nearly sixty. At that time, elderly folks in the countryside looked much older, worn out from a lifetime of hard labor in the fields, dealing with various aches and ailments.","Considering that their village didn’t even have a doctor, moving her to the city would allow her to see a doctor at a hospital, and he would be around to take care of her. That’s why Han Wenlin had decided to bring his aged mother to live with him.","Previously, the old mother refused to come, but after hearing about Niuwa’s situation, she felt it wasn’t right to leave her grandson in someone else’s home, so she hurriedly agreed to move over.","Niuwa said, torn with indecision, “Even though I really want to move to Wencheng with my mom and them, Grandma is very old now, and maybe she doesn’t have much time left.”","Han Wenlin: “...”","Han Wenlin coughed and corrected his son, “Your grandma still has a lot of time ahead of her.”","Niuwa sighed and said, “Forget it, I’ll stay here and keep Grandma company.”","Han Wenlin’s eyes lit up, his spirits lifting instantly.","But soon, he heard Niuwa add, “Still, later on, I want to go find Mother Qiao and my little brother, so I’ll have to go to school in Wencheng eventually.”","Han Wenlin naturally agreed and said, “Okay, I promise you.”","They could worry about the future later.","Niuwa could finish elementary school here and then go to middle school in Wencheng.","But by then, once the boy hit adolescence, who knows if he’d still want to go to Wencheng— nothing was certain."]},{"number":240,"title":"Chapter 240: Six Years Later","paragraphs":["Although Niuwa had agreed to stay with his grandmother, he was still a bit sad.","He clung to Qiao Lanshu for days, staying close to her all the time and saying every now and then, \"Mom, make sure you come pick me up in a few months. I promised to look out for my little brother when he starts kindergarten.\"","He also went to Auntie Shi and said, \"Grandma Shi, you need to remind Mom to come get me. I'm afraid she'll forget about me by then.\"","Watching such an affectionate Niuwa, Auntie Shi couldn't help but say to Qiao Lanshu, \"This child really tugs at your heartstrings. He may be mischievous usually, but he's quite sensible when it matters.\"","Qiao Lanshu was truly reluctant to let Niuwa go as well, but she and Qin Yuanzheng weren't his biological parents, after all. The child had to return to his own family.","Besides, Niuwa's grandmother was coming from far away, and such an elderly woman had it hard enough as it was.","Niuwa, as the only grandson of the Han family, really wasn't suited to be raised in someone else's home.","...","The truth was, Niuwa still preferred living with Qiao Lanshu's family.","Kids don't understand big principles. He just knew he was happy here—eating well, sleeping well, wearing nice clothes, since Qiao Lanshu and Auntie Shi often made him new outfits.","Auntie Shi knew his tastes and would think up delicious meals every day.","And here, he had a mom, a little brother, and now a little sister too.","Besides all that, he couldn't bear to leave Qiao Lanshu's dog either.","He sat in the yard every day, hugging the dog and calling it \"Big Yellow\" in such a pitiful tone, as if they were parting forever. Big Yellow was squeezed so tight its neck could barely breathe. If it struggled, Niuwa would spank it and cry, \"Ow ow ow, Big Yellow, don't run! If you run again, I'll lock you in a crate and hide you!\"","Big Yellow: \"...\"","On moving day, Han Wenlin worried Niuwa would throw a tantrum—he was still so young, and separation is cruel.","So Han Wenlin suggested taking him to the department store to buy some things for the grandmother who would be arriving soon.","Niuwa didn't really want to go at first, but when Han Wenlin mentioned there would be lots of candy and cookies at the department store, he was tempted. He reluctantly followed Han Wenlin.","Qiao Lanshu packed up Niuwa's things—his clothes, shoes, socks, towels, pillow covers, sweatbands, and everything else. She also tucked in a freshly made outfit and a pair of winter wool gloves as a farewell gift to Niuwa.","Auntie Shi, still worried he wouldn't get enough to eat and would shrink from a plump little calf into a skinny monkey, steamed a big pot of steamed buns, a batch of chive rolls, and pickled a jar of sour vegetables for him. After boxing everything up in the alley, she had the guards deliver it to Han Wenlin's home.","...","That day, Guan Wenjun also brought Zhong Mei to see them off.","Zhong Mei reluctantly held Qiao Lanshu's hand, her eyes red, and said, \"Lanshu, you have to remember to come back and see me. You're my only friend.\"","She sighed and added, \"I thought we'd live here together our whole lives. But so soon, you're moving away. I'll be all alone from now on, with no one to go shopping or do groceries with.\"","The two of them had no family here—only each other as their one true friend. Zhong Mei didn't really know many people. Her neighborhood had plenty of neighbors, but she wasn't close to them. The thought of being lonely made her sad.","Qiao Lanshu's eyes were red too. She was reluctant to leave Zhong Mei.","She said softly, \"At least Wencheng and Longcheng aren't far apart. If you miss me, come find me in Wencheng.\"","Then she added, \"And if Guan Wenjun ever bullies you, come tell me. I'll have your back.\"","Zhong Mei nodded. The two sisters held hands and talked for a long time.","Qiao Lanshu took out things she found hard to take with her and had Zhong Mei bring them back. \"These pickled vegetables were made by Auntie Shi. Didn't you say they were delicious? Since they're inconvenient for us to bring, have Guan Wenjun take them all back. And this table and these chairs—Brother Zheng had them custom-made; the wood is excellent.\"","Zhong Mei nodded. \"Thanks, Lanshu. I'll take them, then.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded, counted her belongings again, and walked around the yard and the house with Zhong Mei, feeling reluctant to leave.","In the yard, Guan Wenjun watched Qin Yuanzheng and the guards moving things. He strolled around a few times and asked, \"Old Qin, this house of yours is so nice. Will you have to give it back?\"","It would be a shame to return such a lovely little courtyard.","Unfortunately, Guan Wenjun's job wasn't within the military system, so he couldn't apply for this courtyard. These courtyards were only for officers in the army.","Qin Yuanzheng said while moving things, \"Not right away. I'll keep living here for another year.\"","His work assignment hadn't been transferred to Wencheng yet; it wasn't clear when the transfer order would come through.","Even after the order was issued, he'd need to come here often, so he'd keep this little courtyard.","As for later, he didn't know if he could buy the place.","He and Qiao Lanshu both loved this yard, and he'd hate to give it back.","Auntie Shi was busy that day too, picking the vegetables she had grown to give away.","There were too many to take, so besides bringing some home, she gave a lot to Zhong Mei and some to the neighbors too.","Once everything was packed, Qin Yuanzheng drove his wife and children to Wencheng.","...","The military compound in Wencheng also had apartment buildings, each five stories tall, similar to the building where Qin Yuanzheng lived when he first got married.","Qin Yuanzheng applied for a ground-floor unit with a small yard, at least so they could grow some vegetables and the kids could play outside.","After settling in, in early March, Qiao Lanshu reported to Wencheng Normal University and officially began her college life.","In September of that year, An'an started kindergarten.","The following spring, Qin Yuanzheng's transfer order finally came through. He was transferred to the Wencheng Military Subdistrict as commander, so he no longer had to drive back and forth between places.","By the time they had been in Wencheng for six years, Niuwa—who had been fussing for years—finally came to Wencheng to start middle school.","That year, An'an was in third grade, Xiaxia was in first grade, and Qiao Lanshu had graduated from university long ago and had been teaching Chinese at Wencheng High School for three years.","And around the time Xiaxia started kindergarten, Auntie Shi's son got a formal job at the airport, got married, and had a child. So Auntie Shi quit her job and left their home to go take care of her grandchild.","Niuwa finished elementary school in Longcheng. Over the years, he visited Qiao Lanshu every holiday.","Han Wenlin had promised him that he could go to middle school in Wencheng.","Coincidentally, Wencheng is the provincial capital, and the provincial public security bureau is located in Wencheng. Han Wenlin was transferred to be the director of the provincial public security bureau, so he also moved to Wencheng.","...","Han Ye, who had entered junior high school, was already as tall as Han Wenlin. At his age, he had already grown to over 1.8 meters. It was estimated that he would continue to grow taller. Maybe it was because he had a good diet, and he was even faintly surpassing Han Wenlin.","Han Ye was tall and strong, with well - built muscles. His facial features had fully developed, losing the baby fat and showing sharp edges. He already had the vigor of a young man.","Han Ye was studying in the junior high school where Qiao Lanshu worked. After coming out of the main entrance of the junior high school and crossing the road, there was the primary school where Qin Qiao'an and Qin Qiaoxia studied.","Han Ye currently lived with Han Wenlin and his grandma. Sometimes, he would also have the nerve to stay at Qiao Lanshu's home. There were only three rooms in Qiao Lanshu's house. Qiao Lanshu and her husband used one room. Because Qin Qiao'an and Qin Qiaoxia were timid, the two siblings shared one room, each with their own bed.","The remaining room was temporarily for Han Ye.","When Qiao Lanshu got off work late, Han Ye was responsible for picking up the younger brother and sister across the road.","On this day, after school, Han Ye came out of the school, carrying his schoolbag and getting ready to cross the road to pick up Qin Qiao'an and Qin Qiaoxia.","On the way, two male classmates saw him and mocked him, \"Yo, Nanny Han is going to pick up the kids again. Who would have thought you were so hard - working.\"","Hearing the familiar voices, Han Ye glared at them fiercely and said, \"Zhou Dingwen, are you looking for trouble again?\"","The two boys were the sons of Colonel Zhou. When they used to live in the Longcheng Military Compound, the three of them often got into fights.","Later, when they were in primary school, Han Ye was in the same school as them. For six years, there had been a lot of chaos, and Han Wenlin had been called to the school by the teachers many times.","Finally, when they entered junior high school, Han Ye thought he would never have to see these annoying brothers again in his life.","Han Wenlin also thought he wouldn't have to be called to the school anymore.","But guess what? Colonel Zhou was suddenly transferred to the Wencheng Military Sub - district and became a subordinate of Qin Yuanzheng.","Naturally, the Zhou Dingwen brothers also came to study in Wencheng and happened to be in the same school as Han Ye.","The elder brother, Zhou Dingwen, was in the second year of junior high, and the younger brother, Zhou Dingwu, was in the first year, in the same grade as Han Ye. Zhou Dingwu was even in the same class as Han Ye.","The chaotic days were about to start again.","What a fateful relationship!","Han Ye didn't want to deal with them today. He said, \"Stay away from me. I'm going to pick up my younger brother and sister. You guys who don't have sisters can just envy me. It's no use being envious.\"","Zhou Dingwu shouted, \"Who's envious? Only you think it's something to be proud of being a nanny for others.\"","Han Ye casually slung his schoolbag behind his back and said, \"You're getting angry. I hit a nerve, right? Well, getting angry won't help!\"","Then, he ignored the Zhou brothers and hurriedly went across the road to pick up his younger brother and sister.","The primary school across the road had already finished classes, and the pupils were cheering and running out of the school.","Han Ye stood under a tree by the school gate, staring intently at the children.","There were so many primary school students, chattering and running out. It was really not easy to find his younger brother and sister.","Finally, he saw Qin Qiao'an and Qin Qiaoxia holding hands and coming out.","Once upon a time, little An'an and Xiaxia had now grown up. An'an was in the third grade, and Xiaxia was in the first grade. Both siblings had fair skin and were very good - looking. However, the elder brother, An'an, looked more like Qin Yuanzheng, and his sharp eyebrows and eyes could already be seen.","Xiaxia, on the other hand, looked almost exactly like Qiao Lanshu, looking cute and gentle.","She was simply a miniature version of Qiao Lanshu.","Xiaxia was as cute as a porcelain doll. She had two little braids, and her big, bright, black eyes were full of sparkle.","She had no memories of getting along with Niuwa when she was a child. Although Niuwa came to their home during festivals, he always went to find An'an. Xiaxia was quiet. Being the youngest and a girl, she didn't like to run around. So, her relationship with Niuwa was just so - so.","Seeing them coming, Han Ye smiled and said, \"School's over? Come on, let big brother carry your schoolbags.\"","As soon as Qin Qiao'an saw him coming, he instantly jumped up with joy. He quickly ran over and stuffed his schoolbag into Han Ye's arms, excitedly saying, \"Brother, why are you the one to pick me up today? Where's Mom?\"","Han Ye took their schoolbags and said, \"Aunt Qiao has a meeting today. We don't know when it will end. Our principal is extremely long - winded. She was afraid you'd be hungry, so she asked me to come and pick you up first.\"","Han Ye was carrying three schoolbags in his hands and walking beside them. Qin Qiao'an's body hadn't fully grown yet, and Qin Qiaoxia was even shorter.","Han Ye stood among them, towering over them like a crane in a flock of chickens. There was nothing he could do; he was just too tall.","Qin Qiao'an said cheerfully, \"Mom's gone to a meeting again? What are we going to have for dinner tonight? Brother, I'm hungry.\"","Han Ye thought for a while and said, \"Let's buy some snacks to fill our stomachs first. Then we'll see what there is to eat when we get home.\"","Hearing this, Qin Qiao'an immediately jumped up with joy and said, \"Great! I want to drink soda and eat bread!\"","As he said this, he quickened his pace and ran forward. There was a convenience store in front of the school, and there were a lot of delicious things in it.","Han Ye looked down at Xiaxia. Xiaxia was silent and didn't say a word.","He playfully tugged at Xiaxia's little braid and said, \"Xia'er, why don't you greet big brother when you see me?\"","Xiaxia looked up at him. Her big, round eyes blinked, and she obediently greeted him, \"Big brother.\"","Han Ye smiled and couldn't help but tug at her braid again, saying, \"Xia'er is so good. You have to greet me every time you see me, okay?\"","Han Ye quite liked Xiaxia. However, maybe because he had played pranks on her a lot when she was a child, Xiaxia didn't really like to talk to him. Sometimes, she would even avoid him. Well, it was no wonder, since Han Ye was so mischievous with both his hands and his mouth.","Of course, Xiaxia equally ignored all boys.","This was all the result of Qin Yuanzheng's painstaking education. After all, Xiaxia was so beautiful. Qin Yuanzheng was really worried.","He was always afraid that some naughty boys outside would lead his daughter astray.","Han Ye took out one yuan from his pocket and said with a smile, \"Come on, big brother will take you to buy soda.\"","At this time, the Zhou Dingwen brothers came over. Zhou Dingwu stared at Xiaxia for a while with wide - open eyes and said, \"Han Ye, is this your sister?\"","Han Ye stood in front of Xiaxia, glared at him, and said, \"This is your grandma. Be a good boy and make way.\""]},{"number":241,"title":"Chapter 241: Fortunately, It Didn’t Turn Out Wrong","paragraphs":["The Zhou Dingwen brothers were provoked by Han Ye’s attitude.","Zhou Dingwen said helplessly, “Han Ye, do you have to go this far? Qiao’an isn’t even your real brother—are you really going to act like you’re his big brother?”","Qin Qiao’an didn’t like hearing that and shot back, “He IS my big brother! You two are so annoying, why are you always picking on him?”","Han Ye might not have the best temper, but Qin Qiao’an wasn’t much better.","After all, Qin Yuanzheng was the regional commander, and here in the military compound, every officer treated their family with respect.","Qin Qiao’an had grown up spoiled and uncontrollable.","The Zhou Dingwen brothers had known them since childhood, so they were well aware of their personalities. Now they just couldn’t be bothered to argue—it was getting late, and they all had to head home for dinner.","Besides, now that they were in Wencheng, they didn’t dare get into fistfights as easily as they had back in Longcheng.","For one thing, they were older now—in middle school—not clueless little kids anymore.","And for another, Qin Yuanzheng was way too strict. They’d gotten into one fight before, and Qin Yuanzheng had his guards drag them to the military base, where Han Ye, Zhou Dingwen, and Zhou Dingwu were forced to train all day. Eight hours later, all three of them were so exhausted they threw up, standing right outside the training ground, spitting out sour bile.","Ever since then, they’d wisely stuck to verbal insults instead of throwing punches.","The Zhou Dingwen brothers turned and walked away. “Come on, Dingwu, let’s go. Ignore them.”","Qin Qiao’an still wasn’t done yelling. “If you’ve got guts, don’t run! Let’s settle this at the back hill—whoever doesn’t show is a coward!”","The Zhou Dingwen brothers’ faces darkened, but they held back.","Han Ye covered Qin Qiao’an’s mouth and whispered, “An’an, stop it. Don’t let your mom find out.”","Qiao Lanshu had been a high school teacher for years, and all the elementary and middle school teachers here knew each other. If one of them reported this to her, what then?","Han Ye still shuddered at the memory of that last training session.","It was only because Qin Qiao’an was still young—barely past the stage of hitting sandbags—that he didn’t know how ruthless his father could be!","Han Ye then glanced at Xiaxia. “Qin Qiaoxia, what are you staring at them for? Let’s go.”","With that, he stepped in front of Xiaxia, placed his hand on her head, and pushed her along.","Qin Qiaoxia had been watching the Zhou Dingwen brothers walk away. Now, being guided by Han Ye, she finally looked back and asked, puzzled, “Brother Ye, why do you always fight with them? Uncle Zhou is really nice—he comes to our house for tea all the time.”","Xiaxia wasn’t very close to Han Ye; she hadn’t grown up with him like An’an had. She only claimed An’an as her real brother. She called Han Ye “Brother Han Ye” or “Brother Ye.”","At first, that upset Han Ye—it stung a little.","But Xiaxia was too adorable, tilting her head and looking at him with big eyes, and Han Ye just couldn’t stay mad.","Qin Qiao’an cut in, “Xia’er, don’t you know? There’s old grudges between us—ancient feuds!”","Xiaxia asked, “Brother, how old are you? How can you have old grudges? Last time Uncle Zhou came to our house for New Year’s with Zhou Dingwen, you drank plenty of the soda they brought.”","Qin Qiao’an was left speechless.","He said a bit awkwardly, \"That, that was bought by Uncle Zhou, not by Zhou Dingwen. I'm drinking something that belongs to Uncle Zhou...\"","Xiaxia sighed like a little adult.","Hearing this, Han Ye suddenly became unhappy and asked, \"That Zhou Dingwen, did he come to your house to pay New Year's visits too?\"","An'an nodded: \"Yeah, he came for the Mid-Autumn Festival this year too, and brought a lot of things.\"","Han Ye was furious: \"All those officers in the military compound, how come none of them come to pay New Year's visits? Why does Zhou Dingwen's family have to come?\"","Just now, Zhou Dingwen had asked if Xiaxia was his sister. Hah, he was clearly asking something he already knew, just trying to strike up a conversation with Xiaxia.","Thinking about this, Han Ye looked down at Xiaxia.","Xiaxia was seven years old now, with fair skin and delicate features; even at such a young age, she was already a little beauty.","She was humming a tune lightheartedly, hopping around every now and then, looking carefree.","Han Ye was in middle school now and understood many things. The two Zhou brothers—one in eighth grade, the other in seventh—weren't little kids either.","Qin Qiao'an was still talking: \"Big Brother, that's nothing really. Besides them, some other officers do come to pay New Year's visits to my dad too. After all, they're comrades-in-arms, they have good relationships. The military doesn't ban officers from visiting each other for New Year's. But I don't like them either, so when they come to our house, I don't pour them tea!\"","He had poured tea for Uncle Zhou, but not for Zhou Dingwen—he deliberately didn't.","Big Brother's enemies were his enemies!","Han Ye said with deep disappointment, \"You're wrong. You should've just not let him in the door.\"","With a pretty little sister at home, you had to keep a close watch; all the men around were nothing but wolves in sheep's clothing.","Han Ye bought a carton of soy milk each for his younger siblings, along with some dried plums, and they ate as they walked home.","Qiao Lanshu also got off work around this time. She was now a high school Chinese teacher. Over the past two years, she had been continuing her studies, preparing to take the graduate school entrance exam.","Earlier, she had been delayed in reviewing because Sister Shi had gone back home to take care of her grandson, leaving Qiao Lanshu to worry about the two children.","Now that both kids were in elementary school and Han Ye could help her pick them up and drop them off, it had eased a lot of her burden.","She didn't have to cook lunch for the kids anymore either, because Han Ye would take his younger siblings to eat at the public security bureau's cafeteria.","After all, Han Wenlin was the bureau chief. As long as he gave the word and paid a little extra, the kids could eat at the public security bureau cafeteria every day for lunch. After eating, they could even go rest and play in the chief's office.","After getting off work, Qiao Lanshu left the school with her colleagues, then rode her bike to the nearby market to buy groceries. After shopping, she went home to cook for the kids.","On the way, she ran into a colleague—a young math teacher in his twenties.","The math teacher was also on a bike and greeted her: \"What a coincidence, Teacher Qiao. Out shopping for groceries again?\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled and nodded: \"Yeah, you too are buying groceries?\"","The young Teacher Zhao nodded, pushing his bike, and naturally came up beside her to walk together: \"I got off work early today. I wanted to see if there was any fresh fish to buy.\"","Although Qiao Lanshu thought Teacher Zhao was young, in reality, he was only one year younger than her.","Qiao Lanshu was 27 this year. She had been married to Qin Yuanzheng for nine years, and her child was already in third grade.","However, she looked young for her age. She was naturally a beautiful woman, and after giving birth, she followed the doctor’s advice and did postpartum recovery exercises, so she kept her figure well. People who didn’t know the truth would see her and assume she was an unmarried young girl.","Back in college, she had many suitors, but after she started working, once people learned that she had two children, the number of pursuers dwindled.","Qiao Lanshu never discussed her family situation with others. Qin Yuanzheng was the commander of the military district, and such a status wasn’t something she could casually promote. She never told anyone about her husband. Apart from a few close relatives and friends, she had now been working for over three years, yet her office colleagues had never seen her man. Some even thought she was a widow.","But Qiao Lanshu had long since explained the situation. However, Teacher Zhao was new here—he had been working for less than three months. He didn’t know her marital status and was too embarrassed to ask, so he kept creating opportunities to run into her.","Qiao Lanshu didn’t think much of it. The two chatted for a while, then entered the market and shopped separately.","On their way back, they naturally bumped into each other again. The faculty dormitory wasn’t far from the military district dormitory. Teacher Zhao rode his bicycle alongside her for a stretch, and when they reached a fork in the road, Qiao Lanshu parted ways with him.","Teacher Zhao stopped at the intersection, staring at Qiao Lanshu’s retreating figure for a long time before finally turning around and riding home on his bicycle.","What he didn’t notice was that a car had just passed by on the roadside—someone had already seen his actions.","From a distance, Qiao Lanshu spotted the three children standing at the street corner, eating popsicles.","When Xiaxia saw her, her eyes lit up, and she ran over happily, shouting, “Mom! Mom!”","An’an also ran toward her. Qiao Lanshu’s bicycle basket was filled with groceries. She stopped with a smile, pinched Xiaxia’s rosy cheeks, and asked them, “Why are you all standing here? Go home quickly.”","Xiaxia held up her popsicle. “Brother Ye treated us to popsicles and soda.”","Han Ye quickly ran over too, glanced at the basket, and asked, “Mom, did you buy my favorite roast chicken?”","As he spoke, he reached out to rummage through the basket.","Qiao Lanshu smacked his hand and scolded him, “Roast chicken has to be bought from the restaurant. I didn’t go there today. I’ll get it for you tomorrow.”","Han Ye looked disappointed. “Ah, Aunt Qiao, don’t you love me anymore? I said yesterday that I wanted roast chicken.”","This little rascal—when he wanted to be sweet, he called her “Mom”; when he was unhappy, he called her “Aunt Qiao.”","As if he could get away with it.","Qiao Lanshu gave him a light tap and said, “If you want it so badly, buy it yourself. Don’t you have money?”","Honestly, that Han Wenlin really spoiled his son too much.","He doted on Han Ye to the point of letting him run wild.","Whatever Han Ye asked for, he got. He handed out pocket money in ten-yuan bills.","When factory workers earned only a few dozen yuan a month, Han Ye could casually pull several big banknotes from his pocket.","Luckily, Han Ye hadn’t gone astray. Over six years of elementary school, his personality had become a bit more mischievous, but he still knew to study hard, not to bully the weak, and occasionally even did some good deeds.","He was still hot-tempered, rebellious, and headstrong, though.","Xiaxia looked at Han Ye with disdain and said, “Exactly, exactly! You have your own money, so go buy it yourself.”","Han Ye tugged at her braid and glared at her. \"You little ungrateful thing. Big Brother has bought you so much to eat, and now you won't even say a word for me?\"","Xiaxia was eating the popsicle he had bought for her. She made a face at him, then turned away and ignored him.","Han Ye was so angry his teeth itched.","Qin Qiao'an walked on the other side of Qiao Lanshu. He lowered his voice and asked, \"Mom, who was that uncle who just walked you home?\"","Qiao Lanshu answered casually, \"He's a colleague of Mom's, also a high school teacher.\"","Han Ye sighed. \"Another young uncle. Looks like Uncle Qin has a lot of pressure on him.\"","Qiao Lanshu frowned and shot Han Ye a glare. \"Are you asking for a beating?\"","This kid—why did he have to talk in such a sarcastic tone? There was nothing going on between her and Teacher Zhao...","Thinking about it, Qiao Lanshu suddenly realized, belatedly, that she had been running into Teacher Zhao an awful lot lately.","She hesitated for a moment before Han Ye spoke again. \"Aunt Qiao, this is the third time I've seen him come back with you. Does he live on this street too?\"","Qiao Lanshu fell silent. She pushed her bicycle, leading the three children into the military compound. She said, \"You're still a kid, and now you're trying to boss me around? If you've got nothing to do, go water the vegetable garden for me.\"","They entered their yard, which belonged to a ground-floor house. The yard wasn't big, and the plots on either side had been converted into vegetable gardens.","But it had been two years since Auntie Shi left, and the garden hadn't been carefully tended. There weren't as many vegetables planted as before.","Qiao Lanshu didn't know how to garden. The vegetables were all planted by Qin Yuanzheng, and they were growing fairly well, enough to feed the family.","Han Ye went inside and then headed out to water the vegetable garden. It was a chore he had been doing since he was little, so he was very used to it.","Qin Qiao'an helped him by handing him things.","Xiaxia didn't like playing with her brothers. She preferred to stick close to Mom.","Qiao Lanshu was cooking in the kitchen, and Xiaxia came to help wash vegetables, tend the fire, and peel garlic.","Qiao Lanshu asked her, \"Xiaxia, how was school today?\"","Xiaxia nodded. \"Pretty good. The teacher even praised me for paying attention in class. But I wasn't too happy during labor class.\"","The school still had labor class twice a week. The labor teachers would take the students out to the fields to work—transplanting rice seedlings, planting vegetables, turning soil, and all sorts of tasks. The crops were grown on school grounds, and the harvest was distributed to the students.","Qiao Lanshu continued chopping vegetables as she asked, \"Why weren't you happy in labor class?\"","Qiao Lanshu noticed that Xiaxia was a bit too quiet. She wasn't very lively; she didn't like running or jumping around and preferred to just sit and read all day.","She also wasn't as loud and talkative as An'an and Han Ye, and she seemed to not enjoy talking much either.","It was truly strange—who did she take after with this personality?","Xiaxia sat on a small stool, resting her chin on her hands as she watched the flames in the stove. She said, \"There were bugs in the vegetable field. I got scared and started crying, and then my classmates made fun of me.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","She paused her movements, her expression turning serious. \"Is that so?\"","She asked again, \"Did you tell your brother?\"","Xiaxia shook her head. \"No.\"","She thought it was pretty embarrassing and didn't feel comfortable telling her brothers about it. Han Ye loved to tease her, bully her, and pull her braid. If she told him, he would definitely laugh at her loudly.","Her biological brother Qin Qiao'an actually had a good relationship with her, but he loved sticking with Han Ye every single day, running around everywhere. If she told Qin Qiao'an, he'd just turn around and blab to Han Ye, and then the two of them would come laugh at her together.","Xiaxia rested her chin on her hand, gazing quietly at Qiao Lanshu: \"Mom, I want some braised pork with pickled cabbage.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu kept chopping vegetables as she looked at her and said, \"Look at you, kid. Your mental toughness is impressive. I was just thinking you'd be crying about not wanting to go to school tomorrow.\"","But instead she asked for braised pork with pickled cabbage. If she was still thinking about food at a time like this, it seemed Xiaxia wasn't really taking the classmates' teasing to heart.","Xiaxia let out a sigh and said, \"I'm just scared of bugs, what's so funny about that? They're just being childish. I can't even be bothered to talk to them.\"","Qiao Lanshu had spoken to Xiaxia's homeroom teacher before, and the teacher had said the kids in class actually really liked Xiaxia. So why were they teasing her like this?","Qiao Lanshu decided to go find the teacher again tomorrow and ask about it.","Just then, Qin Yuanzheng came home.","He parked the car in the yard, walked into the courtyard with a grim face.","Han Ye caught his expression and quietly said to An'an, \"Be good later, don't make your dad angry. His face is already green.\""]},{"number":242,"title":"Chapter 242: Running Away from Home","paragraphs":["After Qin Yuanzheng returned, he went straight to the kitchen.","Ever since Sister Shi left, there had been no one to cook at home. Whoever got home first between Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu would be the one to prepare dinner.","Most of the time, it was Qiao Lanshu who bought groceries and cooked, since she got off work earlier than Qin Yuanzheng.","Qin Yuanzheng usually didn’t come back until after six, while Qiao Lanshu returned home just after five.","So, seeing Qin Yuanzheng home today, Qiao Lanshu was a bit surprised. \"You’re back? So early today?\"","Xiaxia also happily called out, \"Dad!\"","Although Han Ye and Qin Qiao'an were somewhat afraid of Qin Yuanzheng—after all, he showed no mercy when training them—Xiaxia had no such fear. Qin Yuanzheng simply couldn't bring himself to scold his daughter. Every time he saw her face, which was seventy or eighty percent similar to his wife's, he couldn't muster the sternness. Besides, Xiaxia was quiet and obedient.","He reached out and ruffled her hair, saying, \"I’ll help your mom. Go read your books.\"","Xiaxia loved reading—a trait she inherited from Qiao Lanshu. Qin Yuanzheng thought it was a good thing; better for her to grow up knowledgeable than to cause trouble like those two rascals.","Xiaxia cheerfully ran off to read.","At the time, the library had a vast collection. Qiao Lanshu worked at the school, and her internal library card allowed free borrowing, so Xiaxia often used it to check out books.","She spent her days sitting at home reading, since the school rarely assigned much homework, giving her plenty of free time.","Han Ye often wanted to take the two siblings out to play, but he could only ever bring Qin Qiao'an along, because Xiaxia always refused.","But whenever Han Ye bought snacks or toys, Xiaxia accepted them all without hesitation.","Han Ye thought his little sister was ungrateful, so he often liked to mess with her.","When Xiaxia went outside, she heard Han Ye calling from the yard, \"Xia'er, come here! I’ve got something cool to show you.\"","Curious, Xiaxia walked over, only to see Han Ye toss a twisting, pitch-black worm at her feet.","Xiaxia screamed in fright and scrambled back into the house.","Han Ye and An'an burst out laughing in the yard.","Hearing the commotion, Qin Yuanzheng turned around and came out, glaring at them.","An'an quickly explained, \"Dad, it’s just an earthworm, an earthworm!\"","Han Ye added, \"Yeah, Xiaxia used to put earthworms in your pockets when she was little, and now she’s scared of them? Hilarious!\"","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless.","From inside the house, Xiaxia shouted, \"I’m cutting ties with you! I’m not talking to you anymore!\"","Han Ye grabbed the earthworm, ran to the window beside her, and said to Xiaxia inside, \"Come on, Xia'er, look—it’s just an earthworm. I brought it to make it up to you.\"","With a slap, Xiaxia slammed the window shut.","As she grabbed a book from the shelf, she muttered, \"You two are just awful.\"","They didn’t act like brothers at all.","Not even as good as the Zhou Dingwen brothers. Although the Zhou brothers were Han Ye’s sworn enemies, they were always nice to Xiaxia. When they came over during the New Year, they didn’t say much, but they treated her politely and never scared her.","Back in the kitchen, Qin Yuanzheng helped Qiao Lanshu chop vegetables.","As she cooked, Qiao Lanshu said, \"Did Han Ye scare Xiaxia again?\"","Qin Yuanzheng replied helplessly, \"That little brat never learns. Thankfully, he hasn’t gotten into any fights lately, or I’d have to drag him to the army.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"Minor mischief is fine, as long as he doesn’t cause real trouble. And don’t be too partial to Xiaxia—you should also pay more attention to An'an.\"","In truth, Qin Yuanzheng did care—about both his son and daughter.","But when one is a mischievous troublemaker and the other a quiet, book-loving girl, wouldn’t anyone favor the latter? It was only human nature.","Qin Yuanzheng said nothing.","He stood nearby, staring at Qiao Lanshu with a wistful gaze.","Sensing his look, Qiao Lanshu raised her head. \"What’s wrong? Is there something on my face?\"","Qin Yuanzheng’s voice carried a hint of jealousy. \"Wife, am I getting old?\"","He reached out and touched his own face.","Qiao Lanshu was twenty-seven, and Qin Yuanzheng was eleven years older, now thirty-eight.","Though he had never slacked off on training over the years in the army, keeping himself as fit and strong as many younger men, his age was still apparent next to his young wife. He looked much older.","Fine lines had appeared at the corners of his eyes, and his mannerisms felt a bit old-fashioned to him. He wondered if he seemed too stiff and dull compared to the younger men outside.","Since Qiao Lanshu started college and now at work, she had always been surrounded by highly educated, quality young men in their twenties—with advanced degrees and respectable jobs. Among them, he remembered quite a few who had expressed interest in her.","Qiao Lanshu looked at him and smiled. \"What’s this? Why the sudden question?\"","Qin Yuanzheng reached out and wrapped his arms around her waist, resting his chin on her slender shoulder. In a low voice, he asked, \"That man who dropped you off today—who is he?\"","Qiao Lanshu laughed. \"Who? That’s Teacher Zhao, a new colleague.\"","Qin Yuanzheng grumbled, \"You sure have a lot of male colleagues.\"","Catching the jealousy in his tone, Qiao Lanshu comforted him. \"Of course there are many colleagues, but a husband—there’s only one.\"","She leaned in and gave him a quick kiss on the lips. \"Alright, let go of me. The pot’s heating up.\"","She found it amusing that Qin Yuanzheng, nearly forty, could still be so possessive.","Rolling up his sleeves, Qin Yuanzheng washed vegetables at the sink, his muscular arms exposed in his short sleeves. \"Starting tomorrow, I’ll drive you to and from work,\" he said.","Qiao Lanshu was at a loss for words.","As she ladled lard into the pan, she couldn’t help but say, \"Isn’t that unnecessary? The school’s close to home—I can walk back on my own. Besides, you don’t get off work until past six, right?\"","Being the commander of a military subdistrict came with a heavy workload. Though Qin Yuanzheng never spoke about military matters, it was only a few years since the Reform and Opening-Up policy had begun, and the military restructuring had just ended.","What’s more, the National Day military parade was only five months away, and as a participant, Qin Yuanzheng was extremely busy.","He naturally couldn’t pick Qiao Lanshu up from work.","Still, he had to keep an eye on his wife—she was still young, while he was already aging.","\"Don’t worry,\" he said. \"I’ll arrange for an orderly to pick you up.\"","Qiao Lanshu was rendered speechless again.","\"Really, it’s not necessary,\" she said.","As a teacher, she had to walk past many people every day coming and going, and she didn’t want the school to know her husband was an officer.","But Qin Yuanzheng wouldn’t listen. \"It’s settled,\" he said.","In short, he wasn’t about to let any other male teacher take Qiao Lanshu home.","That was how an older man acted in matters of the heart—insecure and domineering.","Qiao Lanshu thought for a moment and decided it was okay. After all, some of her colleagues also had family members who drove cars. In this day and age, driving a car wasn't that eye - catching.","Han Ye had been staying here these days. It wasn't because Han Wenlin was on a business trip again, but because the father and son had an argument, and Han Ye just naturally left home.","During the meal, Qin Yuanzheng asked him, \"Why have you come here again these days? Isn't Director Han at home recently?\"","Han Ye's grandmother still lived with them. But since the old lady was getting on in years, Han Wenlin hired a nanny to take care of the old woman at home and cook for both the old lady and the children.","Even if Han Ye went back now, the nanny would still cook his favorite dishes for him. So there was really no need for him to come all the way here just for three meals a day.","Han Ye had gobbled up two bowls of rice in one go. Now he was holding a third bowl and eating while saying, \"Han Wenlin is going on a blind date. Just thinking about having to call another woman 'Mom' makes me upset. So I might as well not go back and leave the house to him to start a new family, so that the other woman won't find me in the way.\"","Then, Han Ye looked at Qiao Lanshu pitifully and said, \"Mom, please don't drive me away. They say once there's a step - dad, there'll be a step - mom. I'll be a homeless child from now on.\"","Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng exchanged a surprised look.","Qiao Lanshu repeated, \"Director Han is going on a blind date?\"","Come to think of it, Han Wenlin was now the director of the provincial public security bureau, a quite high - ranking position. The ladies who could go on a blind date with him probably also had a good social status.","Hearing this, Xiaxia glanced at Han Ye and said to him, \"Even if you have a step - mom, your home is still your home. What are you so afraid of?\"","Xiaxia really couldn't understand. Wasn't Han Wenlin still Han Ye's father? Would this fact change just because Han Wenlin got married?","An'an swallowed the food in his mouth and then said,","\"Xia'er, you don't understand. Big Brother is afraid that Uncle Han will have a child with the newly - married woman. Then, once they have a child, who will care about Big Brother? Maybe they'll even give the house, the car, and all the money to the new child. Then Big Brother will not only be homeless but also have no money.\"","Xiaxia, at such a young age, was greatly shocked. She said in surprise, \"But Uncle Han is so old. Can he still have a child?\"","In Xiaxia's mind, only young people could have children.","How could an old person have a child?","She hadn't even seen her parents have a child.","As soon as she said this, Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu were silent for a moment.","Han Ye also frowned slightly, looking thoughtful.","It was An'an, who was about the same age as Xiaxia, who seriously talked about this topic with Xiaxia, \"Old people can also have children. Li Yiting's parents in my class are quite old. Their hair is all white...\"","\"Qin Qiao'an,\" Qin Yuanzheng said with a cold face, staring at him. \"Shut up and eat your food.\"","An'an was confused and didn't know what he had said wrong. But because he was so afraid of his father, he quickly shut up and buried his head in eating.","Qin Yuanzheng then looked seriously at his daughter and said to her, \"Xiaxia, don't mention the topic of having children in the future. You're still young. Don't say whatever comes to your mind.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was a bit annoyed. How old was his daughter? She was only in the first grade. Why was she starting to pay attention to the matter of having children?","As a father, he couldn't help but think too much. Had some male classmates said something to her at school?","Had she played the game of getting married and having children with other boys?","Xiaxia was also frightened by Qin Yuanzheng's expression and silently lowered her head to eat.","Han Ye didn't dare to say a word either. It was he who had told An'an all those things about having a step - mom, a step - dad, and losing everything once there were younger siblings.","An'an was his most loyal little brother and would stand by his side and scold Han Wenlin with him, so he had said those things.","Who knew that An'an would tell Xiaxia about having children? He knew Uncle Qin would be angry.","Under Qin Yuanzheng's intimidation, none of the three children dared to speak and they all ate their meals in silence.","Qiao Lanshu picked up a piece of fish for each of the three of them. Seeing An'an sweating profusely while eating, she picked up a piece of sparerib for him and said in a low voice, \"Eat slowly. Don't choke.\"","An'an always ate too fast and too hurriedly, gobbling his food down. He had been a worry since he was a child.","Fortunately, Xiaxia ate slowly, chewing each mouthful carefully, which made people feel at ease.","When the meal was almost over, Qiao Lanshu still couldn't help asking Han Ye, \"Who is Director Han going on a blind date with? Has he already found someone he likes, or is he just starting to look?\"","Han Wenlin had said before that since Niuwa was still young, he wouldn't get married because he was afraid that a step - mom would treat his son badly, and he was too busy with work to take care of the family.","Presumably, now that he saw Niuwa had grown up and was already in junior high school, as tall as Han Wenlin himself;","plus, after years of military training, Han Ye had well - built muscles and was good at fighting. He stood there tall and strong, with his skin tanned by the sun.","Han Wenlin knew that no one could bully his son anymore, so he started thinking about a blind date.","After all, Han Wenlin was only in his thirties. He had been a widower for eight years. He couldn't be one for decades more.","Actually, Han Ye didn't object to Han Wenlin's blind date either. He had secretly hoped that Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu would get divorced, and then his father could take advantage of the situation.","But unfortunately, so many years had passed, and as Qin Yuanzheng got older, he watched his wife even more closely.","The Han Wenlin father - son duo saw that there was no hope, so they gave up.","Han Ye silently finished his third bowl of rice, then went to get a fourth one. Then he said, \"He's just starting to look. I heard there are three female comrades. One is a primary school teacher, one is a comrade from the Organization Department, and the other one seems to be the daughter of a provincial cadre. I'm not really sure. These are all what my grandma said. My grandma is really happy.\"","After all, Han Wenlin came from a rural area. Like Qin Yuanzheng, he had fought hard in the military, been on the battlefield, and won military honors. It was not easy for him to reach his current status.","Now, his second wife would be an intellectual from a dual - income family in the provincial capital, with a presentable education, good family background, a decent job, and a respectable social status.","So Han Ye's grandma had been very happy recently and would tell everyone about it.","The happier his grandma was, the more uncomfortable Han Ye felt.","An'an comforted Han Ye, \"Brother, it's okay. If that home doesn't want you, this home does. You can move here to live from now on, just like when we were kids. We can sleep in the same bed.\"","Han Ye sighed and said, \"Anyway, I won't go back these days. It's annoying to see.\"","Qiao Lanshu comforted him, \"Your father still loves you very much. Don't worry. He will definitely consider your feelings. If you have any thoughts, just tell him. The most important thing is communication. Don't keep it all in your heart, okay?\"","But then again, the primary school teacher who was going on a blind date with Han Wenlin wouldn't be from An'an and Xiaxia's school, would she?","Qiao Lanshu knew quite a few single female teachers. She just didn't know which one it would be."]},{"number":243,"title":"Chapter 243: Classroom Tattling","paragraphs":["The next morning, while dropping the kids off at school, Qiao Lanshu took the opportunity to visit Xiaxia’s homeroom teacher, Teacher Qian.","Teacher Qian was a young woman in her twenties, strict in her teaching. Since the start of the semester, Qiao Lanshu had only met her twice.","Seeing Qiao Lanshu approach, Teacher Qian looked a bit surprised. “You’re Qin Qiaoxia’s parent, right? Is something wrong today?”","Qiao Lanshu replied politely, “Yes, there’s something.”","When Qiao Lanshu entered the teachers’ office, Teacher Qian pulled out a chair for her.","Qiao Lanshu didn’t sit. She got straight to the point. “Teacher Qian, Xiaxia mentioned that during labor class a couple of days ago, some classmates mocked her. What exactly happened? Could you tell me the details?”","It was a small matter, really. Most kids wouldn’t mention it at home, and even if they did, parents often wouldn’t pay much attention.","Back then, parents generally listened to teachers. Some teachers even disciplined children physically at school, and parents would applaud them for it.","So a parent like Qiao Lanshu, coming to question a teacher over a child being teased, was something Teacher Qian had never encountered before.","Teacher Qian felt a bit put off. No parent had ever asked her about this before, and she felt this parent was challenging her authority as a teacher.","But since Qiao Lanshu was a teacher at the local high school, Teacher Qian kept her tone polite. She gave a faint smile and said, “Teacher Qiao, children are still young. This was probably just a joke. At their age, they love to play around. Maybe they wanted to have fun with Xiaxia, but Xiaxia misunderstood them.”","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu nodded, though she didn’t fully agree. “You make a good point, Teacher Qian. That’s what I thought at first, too. But this isn’t the first time it’s happened. Xiaxia has mentioned it a couple of times at home. So I hope next time something like this occurs, you’ll step in to stop those kids. Even if they meant to play with Xiaxia, if Xiaxia herself doesn’t want to, then she shouldn’t be forced to go along with it, don’t you think?","Besides, the kids are still young—just first graders. This is exactly the time they need guidance. I believe with your direction, Teacher Qian, they can learn that forcing someone to play when they don’t want to, or mocking and humiliating others publicly, is wrong behavior.”","Teacher Qian was displeased by Qiao Lanshu’s words.","She felt that Qiao Lanshu, as a high school teacher, was looking down on her—a primary school teacher with only a vocational school diploma—and had come specifically to lecture her.","But she, too, was a teacher. She was used to being the one educating others, not being educated herself.","Her displeasure showed plainly on her face. She said flatly, “Don’t worry, Teacher Qiao. I know the kids in my class well. They’re very sensible. Next labor class, I’ll keep an eye on things and make sure they don’t bother Xiaxia.”","Qiao Lanshu noticed Teacher Qian’s expression and realized she was upset. She couldn’t help but reflect—had she, after three years of teaching, unconsciously adopted a lecturing tone when speaking?","But she was only trying, as a mother, to speak up for her child.","Leaving the primary school, Qiao Lanshu headed to the high school for work.","She had classes every morning, as she was both the homeroom teacher and a Chinese language instructor.","By the time she returned to the office, classes had already started. Near the door sat a female teacher in her thirties, who, upon seeing Qiao Lanshu, sneered, “Oh, Teacher Qiao is back, is she? It’s this late and you’re still so laid-back as a homeroom teacher? You’re the only one.”","This teacher was Wang Lanying, who had started working six or seven years before Qiao Lanshu.","She had previously competed with Qiao Lanshu for the position of sophomore homeroom teacher but lost. Ever since, she held a grudge against Qiao Lanshu.","In those days, being a high school homeroom teacher wasn’t very stressful. The students who made it to high school typically came from well-off families and had good manners; they barely needed managing.","There was no overtime or extra tutoring sessions. Homeroom teachers also received an extra subsidy of fifty yuan per month and had more opportunities for evaluations and recognition.","That Wang Lanying—a veteran teacher—was outperformed by a newcomer like Qiao Lanshu naturally rankled her.","So she constantly looked down on Qiao Lanshu, making snide remarks whenever she could.","Qiao Lanshu glanced at her and said, “I already told the director about it. Besides, I don’t have any classes in the morning.”","Wang Lanying shot Qiao Lanshu a glare and muttered, “Must be nice to have connections. Everything goes smoothly. Unlike me—I can’t even swap a class.”","Qiao Lanshu had never openly talked about her husband being a military commander—after all, a commander’s identity was sensitive and needed to be kept confidential.","So her colleagues only knew that her husband was an army officer, but not his rank.","Given Qiao Lanshu’s youth, those who knew her better guessed her husband might be a company or battalion commander. Those who didn’t know her even suspected she was divorced.","Wang Lanying’s husband worked in the education bureau, and she made no secret of it—she boasted about it everywhere, so no one dared to offend her.","Qiao Lanshu deliberately said, “Speaking of connections, isn’t your husband in the education bureau? That’s definitely a stronger backing.”","Wang Lanying snorted, knowing Qiao Lanshu was mocking her. “I can’t be bothered to argue with you,” she said, picking up a book to read.","Qiao Lanshu casually glanced at the book and noticed it was a textbook for graduate school entrance exams—the same kind that sat on her own desk.","Qiao Lanshu was at a loss for words.","Could it really be such a coincidence? Please don’t tell her that, in pursuing a graduate degree, Wang Lanying was also on the same path as her?","Their field of study was offered by only one university in the city, and competition was fierce. The program Qiao Lanshu wanted to apply to had only admitted five students last year.","She certainly hoped Wang Lanying wouldn’t end up competing for that same spot...","Meanwhile, in a first-grade classroom, Xiaxia was sitting in the front row, with classmates to her left, right, and behind her.","The girl behind her kept pushing her desk forward, crowding Xiaxia.","Xiaxia endured it for one class period, then turned around to look at her. “Li Taohua, could you pull your desk back a bit? It’s really cramped here.”","Li Taohua was tall and sturdy, with slightly dark skin. If Qiao Lanshu had been there, she would have recognized her as Wang Lanying’s daughter.","Wang Lanying hated Qiao Lanshu, and by extension, she hated Qiao Lanshu’s child too. Several times after school, she had even shouted insults at them.","So Li Taohua also hated Xiaxia.","What real hatred could children have? It was all fueled by adult grudges.","Li Taohua had never liked Xiaxia, and now, influenced by Wang Lanying, she disliked her even more.","She said to Xiaxia, “It’s my desk. You can’t tell me what to do.”","As she spoke, she pushed the table forward again. Xiaxia was naturally very thin, and her frail body was squeezed between the desks. Her deskmate whispered, \"Xiaxia, maybe you should tell the teacher.\"","This Li Taohua was always picking on Xiaxia. During their last labor class, Li Taohua had even instructed a boy to put a caterpillar on Xiaxia's head. It was really annoying.","But Li Taohua was stockier and taller than the rest of them, and they were all pretty scared of her because they couldn't win a fight with her.","Xiaxia was gentle and quiet by nature, and she didn’t want to stir up trouble. After thinking it over, she decided to endure it for ten minutes.","When the bell rang for class, Teacher Qian entered the classroom holding a textbook. After they greeted the teacher, Xiaxia raised her hand.","Teacher Qian put down the textbook and, seeing Xiaxia’s arm in the air, immediately scowled and said, \"Qin Qiaoxia, class has just started. Who are you going to tattle on now?\"","Xiaxia felt confused by her words—it sounded as if she liked complaining all the time.","But since the semester started, she had never reported anything to Teacher Qian.","Xiaxia felt a little embarrassed by Teacher Qian’s comment. Although she didn’t think she was in the wrong, she was still only a seven-year-old child.","Still, she stood up and said earnestly to Teacher Qian, \"Teacher, it’s because Li Taohua keeps pushing her desk forward, squishing me so much that I can barely sit.\"","Teacher Qian walked over and looked at their desks, indeed noticing that it was quite cramped.","The other students' desks were lined up in a row, but Li Taohua's desk stuck out, trapping Qin Qiaoxia inside.","Teacher Qian frowned slightly. However, she didn’t get angry at Li Taohua. Instead, she asked her, \"Li Taohua, are you deliberately squeezing Qin Qiaoxia with your desk?\"","Li Taohua knew that Teacher Qian wouldn’t really get mad at her, so she wasn’t flustered at all. She immediately replied, \"Reporting to the teacher, I didn’t mean to. My side is narrow too. I had to move my desk forward a bit.\"","Teacher Qian glanced at her. Li Taohua was plump and sturdy, but her spot was actually quite spacious. No one behind her would dare to crowd her.","But because she was bigger than the other students, she needed more room—there wasn’t much to be done about that.","Teacher Qian knew that Li Taohua disliked Qin Qiaoxia. During the last labor class, Li Taohua had been the one to lead the prank against Qin Qiaoxia.","At the same time, Teacher Qian was also aware that Li Taohua’s mother, Wang Lanying, was a high school teacher, and her father was a deputy section chief in a department of the Education Bureau.","Given those connections, Teacher Qian certainly wouldn’t offend them.","Teacher Qian paused for a few seconds, then said, \"Alright, move your desk back a bit. Don’t crowd the other students too much.\"","Li Taohua wasn’t scolded, and a smug grin spread across her face. She happily nodded and said, \"Okay, Teacher, I’ll move it right away.\"","Then she shifted her desk back just a tiny amount—barely anything—and sat down.","Xiaxia turned to look at Li Taohua’s desk. She frowned slightly. After sitting back down, it still felt very cramped.","Moving it or not made no difference.","But Teacher Qian didn’t criticize Li Taohua. Instead, she said sternly to Xiaxia, \"Xiaxia, classmates should be united and considerate of each other. Since you’re thin, it’s fine for you to have a bit less space. You need to make room for others and not be so petty about things, understand?\"","Xiaxia pressed her lips together. She was quite unhappy hearing those words.","Despite her quiet, obedient appearance, inside she was rebellious and resistant.","She said stubbornly, \"Why should I have to sit so cramped just because I’m thin? There are forty classmates in this class, and some are even skinnier than me. Why are their seats plenty wide? Teacher Qian, if Li Taohua is too fat, why don’t you just give her a separate seat?\"","The moment she said that, Teacher Qian’s face darkened. This was the first time a student had talked back to her, and she was furious.","She slammed the ruler on the desk and said harshly, \"Is this how you talk to your teacher? Hold out your hand!\"","Xiaxia sat there, startled by the stern tone. She started to doubt whether she had really done something wrong.","Teacher Qian glared at her: \"Hold it out!\"","Xiaxia extended her left hand, and Teacher Qian struck her palm ten times until it was red and swollen. Only then did she tell Xiaxia to sit down and start the lesson.","Seeing that Teacher Qian actually resorted to hitting, the entire class stayed silent—so quiet that you could hear a pin drop. Satisfied with how subdued the children had become, Teacher Qian felt content.","Back in those days, punishing students with slaps was common. Teacher Qian often hit hands, so after being struck, Xiaxia didn’t come to hate her teacher.","But she still felt uncomfortable sitting. With Teacher Qian enabling her, Li Taohua became even bolder. She kept pushing her desk forward during class, and sometimes even deliberately jabbed Xiaxia in the back with her pencil.","When Xiaxia turned around, Li Taohua would say, \"Oh, sorry about that. Your desk is just too close to mine. It was an accident.\"","But Xiaxia knew she was doing it on purpose.","After school at noon, her brother Qin Qiao'an came running over with his schoolbag on his back, arm-in-arm with a few classmates. He was going to pick up his sister and then find their older brother to eat together at the Public Security Bureau cafeteria.","His classmates asked him, \"Qiao'an, going to find your sister again?\"","Qiao'an said, \"Obviously. Who else would give me lunch if I didn’t find my sister?\"","Just then, Xiaxia was already standing at the school gate with her bag on. Qiao'an proudly said to his classmates, \"Look, that’s my sister. Pretty, right?\"","His classmate played along and said, \"Pretty, pretty! Our sister is gorgeous!\"","Qiao'an puffed out his chest and ran over.","He looked at Xiaxia and asked, \"Xiaxia, what’s wrong? Why do you look so grumpy?\"","Xiaxia sighed, shook her hand, and said, \"My hand hurts so much.\"","Qiao'an reached for her hand. \"What happened to your hand?\"","Then he saw Xiaxia’s red and swollen palm. He immediately got angry. \"Who hit you?\"","Xiaxia said, \"Teacher Qian did. She hit me ten times. It really hurts.\"","Luckily, it was her left hand that got hit; if it had been her right, she wouldn’t have been able to write all day.","When Qiao'an heard it was Teacher Qian, he felt a bit resigned. As they walked, he said, \"Why did Teacher Qian hit you? You’re so well-behaved.\"","Xiaxia was serious about her studies and did well, much better than her two brothers, in fact.","A good student like that normally wouldn’t get hit.","So Xiaxia explained how Li Taohua had been squeezing her with her desk.","As soon as Qin Qiao'an heard that, he was furious."]},{"number":244,"title":"Chapter 244: The Children Are Fighting","paragraphs":["Qin Qiao'an heard that his younger sister had been bullied.","He immediately set out to teach Li Taohua a lesson.","Qin Qiao'an shoved his backpack into Xiaxia's arms, a fierce look on his fair, handsome face. \"That bastard dares to bully my sister—he's completely disregarding me! Xiaxia, wait here. Your brother's going to get revenge for you.\"","With that, Qin Qiao'an turned and sprinted off, moving at lightning speed.","Xiaxia was left carrying her own backpack while hugging his in her arms, nearly buried under the load.","\"Brother, brother, wait up!\" she called after him several times, but Qin Qiao'an didn't respond. In the blink of an eye, he was already far away.","Xiaxia grew worried, afraid her brother might end up in trouble. After hesitating for just two seconds, she clutched his backpack and ran after him.","Although Qin Qiao'an wasn't the best student academically, he was well-liked, and most of the boys in his class were on good terms with him. He got along with classmates from his own grade and others too.","After rushing back to school, he grabbed three or four male classmates along the way, yelling that they were going to find Li Taohua and settle the score for his sister.","Boys in their early teens were all about loyalty and stirring up trouble. None of the kids felt scared—instead, they were excited.","At the same time, Li Taohua was with her own brother, Li Jian, a tall, sturdy fifth grader.","Qin Qiao'an wasn't intimidated. He blocked them with his group of classmates, frowning. \"Li Taohua, why did you bully my sister?\"","Qin Qiao'an, like Xiaxia, had fair skin. His features were a mix—two parts like Qiao Lanshu, five or six parts like Qin Yuanzheng—with thick eyebrows, big eyes, and a handsome face. He was very good-looking.","Li Taohua recognized him (after all, not many people were that attractive, and it left a strong impression).","\"I never said I bullied your sister! I didn't!\" Li Taohua retorted.","Qin Qiao'an was fuming. \"If it weren't for you, would my sister have been hit by Teacher Qian? Now go back to the classroom and move your desk back where it belongs. Otherwise, I'll smash it, and you'll have to stand through class!\"","Li Taohua raised her voice. \"Try it! The desks and chairs belong to the school. If you smash them, you'll have to pay—and the teacher will call your parents!\"","Qin Qiao'an was the type who feared nothing, least of all paying compensation.","He pointed at Li Taohua. \"Just watch me!\"","With that, he dashed toward the first-grade area.","But Li Taohua's brother, Li Jian, blocked his path. \"Stop right there!\"","Li Jian was a head taller than Qin Qiao'an and twice as broad.","Qin Qiao'an shoved him. \"Get out of my way!\"","Li Jian refused, and the two of them tumbled into a brawl.","Li Taohua swung her backpack at Qin Qiao'an, but one of his classmates stopped her. \"Hey, hey, hey—no fighting from you, miss. Don't make us hit you.\"","Li Taohua was pushed aside. She snorted coldly and stood by, watching. \"Just wait—my brother's going to wipe the floor with you.\"","Qin Qiao'an and Li Jian were locked in a chaotic fight. Having trained with Qin Yuanzheng since he was young, Qin Qiao'an was decently skilled.","Li Jian's only advantages were his size and strength—he had no systematic training and fought purely with brute force.","They'd been at it for several minutes when Xiaxia finally ran up, panting, still clutching both backpacks. \"Stop fighting!\" she shouted. \"Stop! The teacher's coming!\"","As soon as they heard a teacher was coming, a few of Qin Qiao'an's classmates rushed over to break up the fight: \"Stop it, stop it! The teacher's here!\"","The two were barely separated. Li Jian's face was fine, but his body was already covered in bruises, hurting like crazy. He spat angrily and said, \"Qin Qiao'an, if you ever bully my sister again, I'll beat you to death.\"","Qin Qiao'an was clever—he knew to hit where it hurt and avoid leaving marks on the face, aiming instead at tender spots that wouldn't easily show bruises.","But Li Jian didn't understand that, so Qin Qiao'an's face ended up black and blue with bruises, while his body had fewer injuries.","This made it look like Li Jian had beaten Qin Qiao'an's face to a pulp.","Xiaxia's eyes reddened with heartache, and silent tears began to fall.","Qin Qiao'an wiped his swollen cheek and glared fiercely at them: \"I'm telling you too, Li Taohua! If you dare bully Xiaxia again, you just wait—I'll come for you!\"","Li Taohua shrank back under Qin Qiao'an's fierce gaze, too scared to utter a word.","Li Taohua was the type to bully the weak and fear the strong. When faced with Qin Qiao'an, she kept her mouth shut, but seeing how meek Xiaxia was, she sneered inwardly, not caring about Xiaxia at all.","It was just around school dismissal time—everyone was heading home or going to eat, so there weren't many people left on campus.","That's why their fight hadn't been discovered.","Seeing a teacher approaching from a distance, the two groups finally split up.","A battered and bruised Qin Qiao'an walked out with a sobbing Xiaxia. Han Ye was already waiting at the school gate.","Seeing them like this, Han Ye was startled and asked with a dark expression, \"What happened? Did you get into a fight?\"","Qin Qiao'an explained what had just happened.","After listening, Han Ye sneered, \"Xiaxia, go back this afternoon and check if Li Taohua's desk has been moved back. If it hasn't, tell me, and I'll go move it for her personally.\"","Han Ye was already in middle school—if he showed up, wouldn't that be like an older kid bullying a younger one? At that point, even if they were in the right, they'd end up being wrong.","Qin Qiao'an said, \"Big Brother, no need for you to get involved. I'll personally take Xiaxia to school this afternoon.\"","Han Ye scolded him, \"You've been beaten into a mess, and you still want to go? Fine, listen to me—I'll take Xiaxia this afternoon, Qiao'an. You just go to class.\"","Since Big Brother had already decided, that settled it.","Half of Qin Qiao'an's face was swollen, and he kept wincing in pain even while eating lunch. He was truly a pitiful sight.","Seeing her brother like this, Xiaxia felt terrible inside.","She said, \"I'll go to school by myself this afternoon. Neither of you need to come. I can handle it.\"","Han Ye said sternly, \"Eat your meal. Leave this to me. I promise no one will dare bully you from now on.\"","Then he added, \"It must be because you look too gentle that everyone thinks you're easy to push around. From now on, don't be so soft—try to act a little fiercer, got it?\"","Xiaxia: \"...\"","How was she supposed to act fiercer? Xiaxia frowned.","Seeing her like that, Han Ye felt utterly helpless.","After lunch, Han Ye took Qin Qiao'an to the clinic. He applied medicine to his face and examined his body to make sure there were no wounds. Only then did he let it go.","When it was time for afternoon classes, Han Ye told Qin Qiao'an to go to his own classroom. Then, he led Xiaxia toward the first floor.","Their school building had six floors, one grade per floor.","First grade had five classes, all on the first floor.","When Xiaxia reached the classroom door, she hesitated and looked up at Han Ye. \"Brother Ye, maybe... maybe you should just go back?\"","Han Ye glared. \"I'm already here. You're not going to let me take a look?\"","Xiaxia: \"...\"","It sounded like he was visiting as a guest or something.","Han Ye walked into the classroom first, glanced around, and asked, \"Where's your seat?\"","Xiaxia led him to her desk.","Just then, Li Taohua came in and sat down at her own desk.","Han Ye went up to her and took a look, startling Li Taohua.","He pressed one hand down on Li Taohua's desk and slowly pushed it backward.","Li Taohua tried to hold it in place, but she wasn't as strong as Han Ye.","He shoved her desk far back until Li Taohua was wedged between two desks.","Li Taohua, being overweight, could barely breathe.","Han Ye smirked coldly at her. \"Now you know how it feels to get squeezed by a desk. How is it? Good?\"","Li Taohua was so scared she started crying. \"Class is about to start. Get out.\"","Han Ye told Xiaxia to sit down, then kept one hand pressed on Li Taohua's desk. \"Sorry, but I'm here today just to keep an eye on you.\"","Li Taohua hung her head, trapped between the desks, too afraid to speak.","Soon, the bell rang. Li Taohua sneaked a glance at Han Ye, hoping he would leave.","Instead, Han Ye turned and walked to the back of the classroom to stand.","Li Taohua turned around and saw Han Ye staring darkly at her with a grim expression.","She quickly looked away, glaring resentfully at Xiaxia.","Xiaxia was also worried about Han Ye, but when she caught Li Taohua's stare, she deliberately said, \"Don't you have a brother too? Tell him to come stand here, then.\"","Li Taohua: \"...\"","This Han Ye was obviously taller and stronger than Li Jian. If it came to a fight, Li Jian would definitely lose.","Li Taohua wasn't stupid. She knew her brother couldn't help her now.","So in her heart, she hated Xiaxia even more.","Why did some people have it so good?","Not only good grades and a pretty face, but also two handsome brothers.","And both of them doted on her so much.","Just then, Teacher Qian came in with a textbook and a ruler.","As soon as she entered, she felt something was off. She glanced around and locked eyes with Han Ye standing at the back.","Teacher Qian froze, confused. She put down the textbook, walked over with the ruler in hand, and looked Han Ye up and down. \"Who are you? Get out. We're about to start class.\"","Han Ye stood still. \"Sorry, teacher, but I can't leave today. And not just today—I'll be here every day from now on. I have to protect my sister. Someone's been bullying her, and since you all didn't do anything about it, I have to handle it myself.\"","Teacher Qian's face darkened. She stared at him. \"Which one is your sister? Who's been bullying her?\"","Han Ye pointed at Li Taohua. \"She almost crushed Qin Qiaoxia flat with a desk. Teacher, didn't you see that?\"","He spoke rudely. \"Teacher, if your eyesight's that bad, maybe you shouldn't be a teacher anymore. A blind person can't lead students the right way.\"","Teacher Qian was so angry she nearly fell over. She pointed at Han Ye. \"You... you're Qin Qiaoxia's brother?\"","Han Ye grinned lazily. \"Guess?\"","Teacher Qian: \"...\"","Teacher Qian was furious. Looking at the burly Han Ye, she didn't dare to confront him head-on.","She turned around and quickly left the room, then sent someone to the nearby high school to find Qiao Lanshu.","For something like this, she had no choice but to call the parent to come.","At the same time, because Han Ye had skipped class, his homeroom teacher also went to the high school to find Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu first heard about Han Ye skipping class, and then she received another notice from the elementary school asking the parents to come.","Qiao Lanshu had no choice but to go to the elementary school first. Han Ye was already grown up, so his matter wasn't as urgent.","This was Qiao Lanshu's first time being called in as a parent.","She hurried to the school and saw Teacher Qian waiting for her at the school gate.","Qiao Lanshu was a bit surprised. She jogged over and asked, \"Teacher Qian, what's wrong with Xiaxia? Why did you suddenly call me over?\"","Qiao Lanshu was worried, fearful that something had happened to her daughter.","Teacher Qian saw her and said with a stern face,","\"Teacher Qiao, since you're also a teacher, I assume you know how to educate children, right? Look at your son. He has no manners at all. Knowing full well that we were having class, he still walked into the first-grade classroom and stood there, disrupting the lesson and wasting everyone's time. This is truly unacceptable. Please discipline your child properly, give him a serious scolding, and make sure it never happens again.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu was a bit confused by what she said.","She frowned and asked, \"Teacher Qian, could you please explain clearly? What exactly happened? What did my son do?\"","At this moment, she still thought the \"son\" Teacher Qian mentioned was Qin Qiao'an.","But Teacher Qian replied, \"Your son is already in middle school, yet he came to the first grade to bully a female student. Do you think that's appropriate? No matter what, whatever happens in my class, I will handle it myself. There's no need for a middle schooler to come play judge. As his mother, you really need to educate him properly.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Oh, now she finally understood where Han Ye had disappeared to after skipping class all afternoon.","She stopped walking and said to Teacher Qian, \"Please hold on for a moment. Let me send someone to inform the child's father and ask him to come educate the child.\"","With that, Qiao Lanshu ran to the school gate and asked the security guard at the gatehouse to send a message to the public security bureau.","Teacher Qian had never met Qin Qiaoxia's father before, so she didn't think much of it at the time.","She remembered that Li Taohua's father worked in the Education Bureau, and since Li Taohua had been wronged in her class, it was very possible that Li Taohua's parents would come to question her.","So, before entering the classroom, she said to Qiao Lanshu, \"No matter how you look at it, what happened today was indeed your son's fault. A middle school boy coming to bully a first-grade female student—what kind of behavior is that? Later, you need to have your son apologize to Li Taohua. Make sure he says it nicely and doesn't scare her into crying again.\"","Qiao Lanshu listened to her the whole way and felt very displeased.","But since she still didn't know the specific situation, she didn't share her opinion prematurely.","Teacher Qian kept criticizing Han Ye, saying everything that was wrong with him.","But why would Han Ye, without any good reason, skip class and go stand in a first-grade classroom?","And what did Li Taohua have to do with all this?","Teacher Qian hadn't mentioned the cause and effect of the matter at all.","Therefore, Qiao Lanshu's expression was also unpleasant. She listened to Teacher Qian in silence, then quickened her pace until she reached the entrance of the first-grade classroom.","She stood at the door and glanced inside. In one look, she spotted the tall and burly Han Ye, standing against the wall at the back of the classroom with his hands in his pockets.","Judging by his demeanor, he really did look like someone asking for a beating."]},{"number":245,"title":"Chapter 245: Triple Tribunal","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu stood at the classroom door. Both Xiaxia and Han Ye saw her.","Guilt flickered across their faces simultaneously.","Although they knew this incident had blown up and would inevitably involve parents being called in, Han Ye had originally assumed the teacher would contact Han Wenlin. After all, Han Wenlin spoiled his son to no end—as long as Han Ye didn’t commit anything morally unforgivable, Han Wenlin would indulge him without limits.","But the problem was, why had Qiao Lanshu shown up instead?","At that moment, Han Ye still didn’t know that both he and Xiaxia had been summoned with their parents. So not only was Han Wenlin coming, but Qiao Lanshu had also arrived.","The moment Han Ye saw Qiao Lanshu, he quickly pulled his hands out of his pockets and stood up straight.","His cocky expression gradually turned serious.","Xiaxia turned around and exchanged a glance with him. Both could see the panic in each other’s eyes.","Xiaxia sighed inwardly. She had told Han Ye earlier to go back and not follow her here.","Qin Qiao’an had already gotten into a fight, and Xiaxia was on edge because of it. Yet Han Ye had still come, standing in the classroom like a stone sentry. This issue, if taken seriously, was actually quite serious.","After all, he had disrupted someone else’s class. It was lucky the security team hadn’t shown up, or Han Ye would have been hauled away.","Teacher Qian walked into the classroom as well. She stood next to Qiao Lanshu, pointed at Han Ye in the back of the room, and said:","“Teacher Qiao, this is your son, isn’t it? He’s standing here right now—how are we supposed to teach like this? Look, classmate Li Taohua has been scared to tears by him. He must apologize to Li Taohua.”","Teacher Qian had been busy lately with a performance review, and her application had already been submitted to the Education Bureau, so she was feeling anxious.","She kept insisting that Han Ye apologize to Li Taohua.","Qiao Lanshu faced Han Ye’s gaze, her expression unchanged. In front of all the children, she asked Teacher Qian:","“Teacher Qian, shouldn’t we discuss this in the office? Could another teacher take over the class first, so these students don’t miss a whole lesson?”","Hearing this, Teacher Qian suddenly realized the point.","She had completely forgotten to arrange for another teacher to take over. Handling these matters in the classroom like this was indeed inappropriate.","But being reminded by Qiao Lanshu irritated her.","Frowning, she said, “Fine. Qin Qiaoxia, and you—come with me to the office.”","Xiaxia silently stood up and walked to the classroom door with Han Ye.","Qiao Lanshu looked at them, then asked Teacher Qian: “Wasn’t there also a Li Taohua? Have her come along too.”","Teacher Qian stood there: “Teacher Qiao, this is your son’s problem. Why drag another student into this?”","By now, Qiao Lanshu was starting to get angry. She was usually easygoing and rarely lost her temper.","But Teacher Qian’s favoritism was far too obvious.","Standing on the hallway outside the classroom door, with Han Ye and Xiaxia behind her, she said:","“Teacher Qian, before we’ve clarified what happened, please stop insisting that everything is my son’s fault. Jumping to conclusions like this, without asking about the facts or the sequence of events—such eagerness to pin blame makes me seriously wonder if there’s something underhanded going on here.”","Teacher Qian frowned: “Leaving everything else aside, the fact is that a middle school student barged into a first-grade classroom, stood there, and refused to leave, disrupting our lesson—that’s undeniable, isn’t it?”","Qiao Lanshu stood her ground: “That’s just the outcome. Every outcome has a cause, doesn’t it? Why would he cut class and come to a first-grade classroom, deliberately trying to stop you from teaching? What’s the reason? Teacher Qian, I’ll say it again—please ask Li Taohua to come out too. We’ll go to the office and find out exactly what happened.","If this really is our son’s fault, I’ll make sure he apologizes—even in front of the entire school if necessary. But if it’s someone else’s fault, then that person should apologize too. As a homeroom teacher, I trust you can be fair and impartial, right?”","With that, Qiao Lanshu walked to the door and called inside: “Li Taohua, please come out.”","By this point, Li Taohua was already very scared.","She might usually bully Xiaxia without a second thought, but when it came down to it, she was just a child. She realized Teacher Qian couldn’t protect her anymore, and that this matter had blown up bigger than expected.","But then she thought again. Her mother was a high school teacher, and her father was a section chief in the Education Bureau. Many people fawned over their family.","Even Teacher Qian had come to their house with gifts during the New Year.","What did she have to be afraid of?","Li Taohua was used to arrogance. She quickly calmed down and walked slowly to the classroom door.","Teacher Qian was getting annoyed. Her original plan had been to have Qiao Lanshu take Han Ye away and then make him apologize to Li Taohua.","That would have been the end of it.","But instead, Qiao Lanshu had called Li Taohua out, as if deliberately making a big scene.","Teacher Qian looked at Qiao Lanshu: “Teacher Qiao, what exactly are you trying to do? Don’t tell me you’re going to turn this trivial little thing into a full-blown court hearing.”","Qiao Lanshu nodded: “Teacher Qian, something like this might seem small to us. But to these children, it’s a big deal! Since you called me here, then call Li Taohua’s parents over too. Let’s get to the bottom of this together.”","Teacher Qian frowned: “There’s no need for that, is there?”","Then she added, “Forget it, let’s just go to the office first.”","By now, she was already regretting having called Qiao Lanshu in.","Qiao Lanshu was proving to be far too difficult to handle.","And so, Teacher Qian led Qiao Lanshu, along with Han Ye, Qin Qiaoxia, and Li Taohua, into the office.","It was class time, so there weren’t many teachers in the office.","As soon as they entered, before Teacher Qian could speak, Qiao Lanshu took the lead and asked: “Han Ye, tell me—what exactly happened with you today?”","Her eyes were stern as she looked at him. Han Ye could count on one hand the times she had looked at him like that since he was little.","Whenever this happened, Han Ye knew that Qiao Lanshu was truly angry.","But Han Ye didn’t think he had done anything wrong. So he straightened his back and said:","“Mom, I came here today to stand up for Xiaxia. That Li Taohua keeps bullying her. She sits behind Xiaxia and pushes the desk forward to squeeze her. You have no idea—Xiaxia’s seat space is only this wide.”","Han Ye used his thumb and index finger to measure a tiny gap, exaggerating ridiculously.","But it made Qiao Lanshu understand the whole situation.","Han Ye continued: “It’s so narrow, it’s practically crushing Xiaxia into a pancake. The teacher wouldn’t do anything about it, so it was up to me, her brother, to step in.”","Teacher Qian immediately shot back: “Nonsense! I never said I wouldn’t deal with it. And it’s not nearly as bad as you claim. I checked—there’s enough space there. Xiaxia has plenty of room to sit.”","At this point, Teacher Qian still hadn’t realized that she had become more like the accused, while Qiao Lanshu had taken on the role of the judge.","Upon hearing what they said, Qiao Lanshu more or less understood the situation.","She asked Xiaxia, \"Xiaxia, was it this classmate Li Taohua who you said teased and mocked you during the labor class before?\"","Xiaxia nodded, completely calm and unfazed. \"My mom, it was her. She sits behind me and often bumps my desk with hers. She also pokes me in the back with her pencil.\"","As she spoke, she turned around to show her mother her back. Qiao Lanshu looked closely at the blue school uniform and indeed spotted several light gray pencil tip marks."]},{"number":246,"title":"Chapter 246: A fight broke out in the office","paragraphs":["After Qiao Lanshu finished examining Xiaxia’s back, her expression immediately turned serious.","This was clearly a case of bullying at school.","Of course, at the time, “school bullying” wasn’t a popular term. All Qiao Lanshu knew was that her daughter had been stabbed in the back with a pencil tip by a classmate at school. How painful must that have been?","Her precious daughter—the one she and Qin Yuanzheng couldn’t bear to scold harshly—was being treated like this at school.","How could Qiao Lanshu tolerate it?","Qiao Lanshu pulled Xiaxia aside and gently lifted the back of her collar to peek inside. Xiaxia’s back was fair and flawless, with no visible injuries.","Thank goodness.","Qiao Lanshu breathed a sigh of relief.","With a grim expression, she looked at Teacher Qian. “Teacher Qian, we need to get Li Taohua’s parents here to deal with this. I want an explanation today, and I mean it.”","Before Teacher Qian could respond, Qiao Lanshu added, “I want this resolved today. If you can’t handle it, then call in the head teacher or the principal. If that still doesn’t work, I’ll call the police and let the officers handle it. What do you think?”","Teacher Qian’s face darkened. “There’s no need to blow this out of proportion. It’s just a conflict between kids.”","She paused, then added, “Fine, I’ll have someone call Li Taohua’s parents...”","But then she hesitated, looking at Qiao Lanshu with a warning tone. “Teacher Qiao, are you sure you want to call Li Taohua’s parents? Her father is a section chief at the Education Bureau.”","Teacher Qian felt she had no choice but to say this.","Qiao Lanshu was also a teacher, and future evaluations would pass through the Education Bureau. If she knew what was good for her, she should stop now.","But upon hearing this, Qiao Lanshu’s expression grew even more stern.","She fixed her gaze on Teacher Qian and said coldly, “Teacher Qian, is this why you’ve been letting Li Taohua bully her classmates? Because her father is a section chief at the Education Bureau? Just because Qin Qiaoxia’s father doesn’t work at the Education Bureau, she deserves to be bullied?”","Seeing that Qiao Lanshu wouldn’t budge, Teacher Qian grew annoyed. “Fine, Teacher Qiao. Since that’s your attitude, I’ll call Li Taohua’s parents over. You two can sort it out yourselves.”","Clearly, Teacher Qian didn’t want to get involved anymore. To put it bluntly, she simply didn’t want to offend Li Taohua’s family, so she planned to dump the responsibility on Qiao Lanshu.","After all, however it was resolved, it would be between the parents.","Wang Lanying and Qiao Lanshu were colleagues, both high school teachers.","Wang Lanying arrived quickly, since the two schools were only separated by one street. As soon as she entered the office, she saw Li Taohua standing timidly across from Qiao Lanshu, whose face was stern.","Wang Lanying rushed over, shielding Li Taohua, and glared angrily at Qiao Lanshu. “Teacher Qiao, what’s this supposed to mean? You come to school just to bully my daughter?”","Qiao Lanshu replied grimly, “Your daughter sits behind my daughter. She keeps pressing her desk into my daughter’s back, making it hard for her to even stand up. And she’s been using a pencil tip to stab my daughter. Look for yourself—these are all the marks.”","As she spoke, Qiao Lanshu pulled at the back of Xiaxia’s school uniform to show Wang Lanying, so she wouldn’t claim it was made up.","She continued, “Li Taohua herself admitted everything. Teacher Qian was here listening too, so don’t say I’m lying.”","Wang Lanying was speechless.","Wang Lanying didn’t like Qiao Lanshu, and by extension, she didn’t like Xiaxia either.","She didn’t think her daughter had done anything wrong. Casually, she said, “So what if she poked her with a pencil a few times? What’s the big deal? Kids play around—that’s normal. Who didn’t get poked by a pen as a child?”","Wang Lanying was about to say more, but suddenly Qiao Lanshu grabbed a pen from the desk and swiftly jabbed it into Wang Lanying’s arm.","Wang Lanying let out a shriek, clutching her arm, staring at Qiao Lanshu with shock and rage. “Qiao Lanshu, have you lost your mind?”","Qiao Lanshu said nothing. She moved quickly, silently stabbing Wang Lanying’s arm several more times. After Wang Lanying pushed her away, she lunged again, jabbing randomly at Wang Lanying’s body.","Wang Lanying screamed wildly, scrambling backward to escape.","Everyone present was stunned by the sudden turn of events.","Han Ye watched the chaos unfold. Quietly, he shifted his position. When Wang Lanying stumbled back in panic, he silently stuck out his leg.","Wang Lanying shrieked again and crashed to the floor with a loud thud.","“Qiao Lanshu, stop! Are you trying to kill me?” Wang Lanying screamed.","Qiao Lanshu stabbed Wang Lanying’s arms and body maybe twenty or thirty times. She didn’t count exactly, but it was a lot.","Teacher Qian snapped out of it and pulled her back. “Teacher Qiao, calm down, calm down! Let’s talk this out peacefully.”","Teacher Qian was utterly shocked.","She never expected Qiao Lanshu to be so fierce.","Before this, Teacher Qian’s impression of Qiao Lanshu was just that of a gentle, soft-spoken, refined female teacher.","Even her daughter seemed to inherit her personality—timid, introverted, and quiet—easy to pick on.","But now...","Teacher Qian’s hair stood on end from the tension.","Qiao Lanshu still clutched the pencil tightly in her hand. The pencil tip wasn’t sharp, having been used for writing, so it was somewhat rounded.","But she had jabbed hard enough to cause real pain.","Still unsatisfied, Qiao Lanshu stood there, her face dark, and asked Wang Lanying, “Teacher Wang, what’s the big deal? I just poked you a few times with a pencil. Why are you yelling so loudly?”","Wang Lanying was in agony. Her arms, shoulders, and stomach throbbed from the jabs.","Sitting on the floor, she was so furious her eyes turned red. “You’ve gone too far! I’m reporting you! Reporting you! You’ve got no morals—you used violence on me!”","Qiao Lanshu shot back, “So poking someone with a pencil a few times is violence on you, but a minor thing when it’s my daughter? Wang Lanying, are you even human?”","She put down the pencil and said to Teacher Qian, “Teacher Qian, even Li Taohua’s mother admits that poking someone with a pencil is an act of violence. I demand that Li Taohua apologize to Qin Qiaoxia and be immediately transferred to a different class. I won’t allow them to stay in the same class.”","Wang Lanying was dizzy with rage. “If anyone’s transferring, it should be your daughter! As if my daughter wants to be in the same class as her! What a nuisance!”","Seething, Wang Lanying got up and reached for a pen, but Han Ye was quicker, snatching the pen holder away.","Wang Lanying glared at him furiously and swung her bag at him. “Who are you? Get lost!”","Han Ye dodged her attack, hiding behind Teacher Qian, and made a face at her. “Who am I? I’m your daddy!”","Wang Lanying's face was green with fury. Clutching her bag, she lashed out wildly at Han Ye. \"You bastard, you tripped me just now, didn't you? I'm going to report you, I'll have the police arrest you!\"","Han Ye dodged behind Teacher Qian, retorting, \"Turning things upside down! Trying to have your own father arrested—your grandpa wouldn't allow it.\"","Teacher Qian took the brunt of it, getting smacked several times on the head and face by Wang Lanying.","Now she was furious too. Seeing that Qiao Lanshu had no intention of intervening, she spun around and pointed at Han Ye, yelling, \"Can you stop causing trouble? Get the hell out of this office right now!\"","Han Ye shrugged his shoulders and said with a grin, \"Didn't you just call me in here? Now you're telling me to scram—so, do I still apologize or not?\"","Teacher Qian's face darkened as she pointed to the office door and roared, \"Right now, this instant, get the hell out of here!\"","Han Ye crossed his arms. \"I'm not leaving until Li Taohua formally apologizes to Qin Qiaoxia.\"","Wang Lanying had never met Han Ye before. At that moment, she demanded angrily, \"Teacher Qian, who on earth is he?\"","She had originally thought today's conflict was just between her and Qiao Lanshu.","But now, there were others involved?","Before Teacher Qian could answer, a man's voice suddenly came from the doorway of the office. He said, \"He's my son, Han Ye.\"","Everyone froze and turned to look.","Standing at the office entrance was a middle-aged man in a police uniform, his face stern as he watched them.","The people in the office wore various expressions.","They had no idea how long this police officer had been standing there.","Teacher Qian was the most visibly shaken.","She straightened her clothes, walked to the door in shock, and looked at Han Wenlin, lowering her voice to ask, \"Director Han, what brings you here?\"","Then, a delayed realization hit her as she pointed at Han Ye. \"You just said he's your...\"","Han Wenlin nodded expressionlessly. \"That's right. He's the son I told you about, the one now in middle school. His name is Han Ye.\"","Teacher Qian stood speechless."]},{"number":247,"title":"Chapter 247: Report on Qiao Lanshu's Improper Work Conduct","paragraphs":["The middle school student named Han Ye before her was the son of Director Han. So what was Qiao Lanshu, as a mother, to Han Wenlin?","Teacher Qian was stunned for a moment, her heart fluttering with unease as she felt these relationships were becoming messy.","She forced a smile and spoke: \"Director Han, you're not joking with me, are you? Didn't you say your ex-wife had already...\"","Han Wenlin walked into the office with a serious expression. He glanced at the people around him, nodded at Qiao Lanshu, and explained to Teacher Qian: \"Comrade Xiao Qiao is my son's godmother.\"","Then, he added: \"Let's set aside personal matters for now and focus on official business. Teacher Qian, what happened today? I heard my son caused trouble for you here?\"","Teacher Qian's expression shifted several times. She opened her mouth but couldn't find the words.","How was she supposed to explain this?","And Qiao Lanshu!","She kept insisting that Han Ye was her son, but why didn't she clarify he was her godson?","What a mess...","Teacher Qian's heart raced with panic. She felt that Han Wenlin's gaze toward her was cold and distant.","It was different from when they had met before.","She was a primary school teacher, only in her twenties, young and pretty, with a respectable job. Through a matchmaker, she had been set up with Han Wenlin for a date.","Although Han Wenlin was remarried and had a son, he was the director of the provincial public security bureau—not a county or city bureau—so his status was hardly ordinary.","Besides, his son was already in middle school. A stepmother wouldn't have to take care of the boy, since in just a few years, he would be entering the military. He wouldn't disrupt the life of Han Wenlin and his new wife.","Moreover, Han Wenlin was only in his thirties, tall and strong, with an impeccable character.","Teacher Qian was very satisfied with him.","After their first meeting, Han Wenlin had chosen her from among three potential matches, thinking she was suitable for further courtship.","So three days ago, they had a second meeting and even had a meal together.","It had seemed like a done deal.","But then today's incident happened.","Teacher Qian felt flustered and anxious, with a hint of regret.","She didn't know how long Han Wenlin had been standing at the door or how much he had overheard.","Had he caught everything she had said in scolding Han Ye?","Actually, it wasn't just Teacher Qian who deflated; even Wang Lanying's arrogance faded when she saw Han Wenlin.","Her husband was merely the deputy section chief of the municipal education bureau's logistics department, with no real authority over the education department, let alone adult education.","He could bluff his way through scaring a few teachers, but faced with a provincial-level official, she dared not act too arrogantly.","So, Wang Lanying jumped in before Qiao Lanshu could speak: \"This is all a misunderstanding. It was just some roughhousing among the kids during class—a trivial matter. There's no need to blow it out of proportion. The children are still young, only seven years old. What do they really understand?\"","Han Wenlin listened and roughly understood the situation: Li Taohua had been bullying Xiaxia.","But why was Han Ye here?","Han Wenlin asked Teacher Qian: \"Disrupting the class was indeed Han Ye's fault. As his father, I apologize to everyone on his behalf. I've failed in teaching my son; I'm truly sorry to all of you.\"","Teacher Qian quickly said: \"It's nothing, nothing. Actually, Han Ye just wanted to care for his sister. This can't be blamed on him...\"","Han Wenlin then said: \"In that case, should we let him go back to class?\"","What else could Teacher Qian say? She nodded in agreement.","Han Wenlin had always been fiercely protective of his own, so he immediately said to Han Ye: \"There's nothing for you here. Hurry up and get back to class.\"","Han Ye didn't want to leave just yet: \"No way. My mom and my sister are still here.\"","Han Wenlin glared at him in anger.","Qiao Lanshu quickly interjected: \"Han Ye, you go back first.\"","Han Ye was about to say something more, but Qiao Lanshu shot him a stern look: \"Be obedient.\"","Han Ye: \"...\"","Han Ye rubbed his nose and said to Han Wenlin: \"You better help them out, or I won't recognize you anymore.\"","Han Wenlin was exasperated, pointing at him: \"Get lost, now.\"","This rascal couldn't go a single day without stirring up trouble!","After Han Ye left, the few people in the office stood there in awkward silence. Teacher Qian didn't dare say a word.","With a public security bureau director standing right there, who would dare cause trouble?","Qiao Lanshu looked at Wang Lanying and said: \"Solving this matter is simple. Have Li Taohua apologize to Qin Qiaoxia, and then transfer her out of this class. She can't be in the same class as Qin Qiaoxia.\"","Wang Lanying's face darkened: \"Teacher Qiao, even with a public security bureau director here, I still have to say this: if anyone should be transferred, it should be your daughter. Why should it be my daughter?\"","Wang Lanying snorted coldly: \"An apology is fine, but you have to apologize to me too. You just stabbed me with a pen!\"","Qiao Lanshu turned to look at Teacher Qian: \"Teacher Qian, what do you think?\"","Teacher Qian: \"...\"","Han Wenlin also fixed his gaze on Teacher Qian, his expression stern.","Awkwardly, Teacher Qian said: \"Li Taohua, bullying classmates is wrong. First, apologize to Qin Qiaoxia.\"","Li Taohua stood there, glanced at Wang Lanying, and stayed silent.","Wang Lanying gave a slight nod. Li Taohua lowered her head and muttered to Qin Qiaoxia: \"I'm sorry.\"","Qin Qiaoxia glanced at Li Taohua with a hint of disdain and looked away.","Teacher Qian watched her anxiously: \"Qin Qiaoxia, Li Taohua has apologized. Don't you have anything to say?\"","Qin Qiaoxia: \"Teacher, I have nothing to say. I don't plan to forgive her, so I don't want to talk to her right now.\"","Everyone: \"...\"","Han Wenlin looked at Qin Qiaoxia with a hint of admiration, thinking to himself that she was indeed Qin Yuanzheng's daughter—strong-willed and independent.","Wang Lanying's face turned ugly. She glared resentfully at Qiao Lanshu and Qin Qiaoxia and said: \"My daughter has already apologized, Teacher Qiao. Shouldn't you apologize to me? You stabbed me just now!\"","Qiao Lanshu snorted coldly: \"I won't apologize for something I didn't do wrong. Wang Lanying, you'd better keep your daughter in check. If there's a next time, just wait.\"","Then, she said to Teacher Qian: \"Teacher Qian, let's consider this matter settled for now. I hope you arrange Li Taohua's transfer as soon as possible. If she's still in this class tomorrow, I'll have to talk to the principal.\"","Teacher Qian felt threatened.","But with Han Wenlin present, she couldn't lash out.","She only said: \"Transferring classes isn't that easy. There are procedures to follow. It's not something we can just do on a whim. But I'll submit the application; rest assured about that.\"","In the end, she still didn't agree to the transfer, just talked about submitting an application. Who knew how long that would take?","Qiao Lanshu was also a homeroom teacher and knew that transferring a student wasn't just up to the homeroom teacher.","So she accepted Teacher Qian's response.","She silently decided that if Li Taohua wasn't transferred within three days, she would go to the principal or even the education bureau.","And so, the matter was finally settled.","Han Wenlin hadn’t really been able to help much, but he felt that Teacher Qian’s character wasn’t quite up to par, so he didn’t talk much with her. Once the matter was handled, he prepared to leave.","Seeing him about to go, Teacher Qian quickly caught up.","She smoothed her hair and said with a smile, “Director Han, didn’t you mention last time that you’d be free this weekend? How about we go to the cinema?”","Han Wenlin turned to glance at her, his expression distant, and replied, “Sorry, but I’m not free this weekend.”","With that, he walked off without giving her another look.","Teacher Qian stood there, watching his retreating back, her face a mix of embarrassment and frustration. What did Han Wenlin mean by this? Was he backing out on her?","...","Qiao Lanshu walked out of the school with Xiaxia and asked her, “How about Mom gives you a few days off? You can rest at home first. Once that Li Taohua gets transferred, you can go back to school, okay?”","Xiaxia shook her head. “It’s fine, Mom. After today, that Li Taohua shouldn’t dare to bully me anymore.”","At least on the surface, Li Taohua would have to hold back a bit.","After all, Li Taohua now knew that Xiaxia had a fierce older brother in middle school and a mother who would stand up for her.","Xiaxia wasn’t the kind of person with a fragile heart. She saw everything clearly. Most of the time, she chose not to say anything simply because she couldn’t be bothered to argue with people like that.","Qiao Lanshu looked at her and said quietly, “It’s not Li Taohua I’m worried about. I’m afraid Teacher Qian might target you.”","Xiaxia lowered her voice too and said, “Mom, you can be even more at ease about that. Just now, Uncle Han told Teacher Qian to take good care of me, and she agreed.”","Qiao Lanshu could tell that the atmosphere between Han Wenlin and Teacher Qian was off, but that was because she was an adult.","Yet Xiaxia had picked up on it too. Qiao Lanshu ruffled her hair and said in astonishment, “You little girl, how come nothing gets past you?”","Xiaxia smiled triumphantly. “Of course! I’m the smartest.”","Qiao Lanshu felt a bit wistful. Xiaxia might not say much or make a fuss, but she was actually the sharpest of them all.","Still, her too-easygoing nature wasn’t great. She never fought for anything, and sometimes she couldn’t even be bothered to pursue things when she was bullied, because she didn’t care. If it didn’t really hurt her, she thought it wasn’t worth her time.","But wouldn’t that make her look like a fool or a pushover in other people’s eyes?","Qiao Lanshu sent Xiaxia back to the classroom, her heart full of worry.","This couldn’t go on. Today there was Li Taohua, tomorrow there would be a Wang Taohua or a Niu Taohua.","After thinking it over, Qiao Lanshu decided to let Xiaxia skip a grade.","Xiaxia had always been clever and done well in school. If she studied the third-grade material and took the skip-grade exam, she could end up in the same class as her big brother, Qin Qiao’an.","That way, with her brother watching over her, Qiao Lanshu could rest easy.","Having made up her mind, Qiao Lanshu went back to work. She planned to discuss the idea of Xiaxia skipping a grade with Qin Yuanzheng when he got home from work that evening.","Meanwhile, back in the classroom, Li Taohua did stop pressing her desk against Xiaxia’s, but she kept glaring at Xiaxia with venomous eyes.","Xiaxia just focused on the lesson and pretended not to notice.","Starting from the second period, Teacher Qian arrived early and moved Li Taohua to a different seat.","Another classmate was placed behind Xiaxia instead.","Teacher Qian looked at Xiaxia with a complicated expression. She still didn’t like Qin Qiaoxia, but considering Qin Qiaoxia’s connection to Han Wenlin, she suppressed her displeasure.","She said to Qin Qiaoxia, “If anything comes up in the future, come tell me, and I’ll handle it. Don’t go complaining to your brother or anything again. Making a big deal out of things is bad for everyone, got it?”","Qin Qiaoxia nodded, looking every bit the obedient student. “I understand, Teacher. I’ll be careful.”","Teacher Qian left, feeling stifled.","After Wang Lanying left the school, the spot on her arm where Qiao Lanshu had jabbed her was still throbbing.","The more she thought about it, the angrier she got. Her daughter had only stabbed the other girl a few times, but Qiao Lanshu had jabbed her dozens of times in return!","And on top of that, her daughter had apologized, but Qiao Lanshu refused to say sorry!","When she thought about it, she’d come out on the losing end and let her daughter down too.","Wang Lanying sneered inwardly.","That Qiao Lanshu usually seemed so refined, but behind the scenes, she’d hooked up with the Public Security Bureau director!","And claiming that Han Ye was just her godson—who would believe that?","Qiao Lanshu had to be having an affair with Han Wenlin. The two of them were messing around in an improper relationship, with corrupt morals and tainted character. The school should fire someone like that!","Wang Lanying remembered that Qiao Lanshu had recently been recommended by the school as an Outstanding Teacher of the Year, as well as a Five-Good Youth award.","She immediately went home and wrote a letter of complaint. Before noon, she personally took the letter to the City Education Bureau.","Her husband worked in the bureau’s logistics department and happened to oversee matters like this.","She handed the letter directly to him, explained the whole story from start to finish, and told him to handle it right away—reject all of Qiao Lanshu’s award nominations, and not only that, but also give her a disciplinary sanction!","Demote her, publicly criticize her!","Wang Lanying’s husband was a big, dark, chubby man who looked very much like their two children in appearance and build.","He looked at the complaint letter and hesitated. “Are you sure there’s something going on between them?”","Wang Lanying said firmly, “Absolutely! That Qiao Lanshu has been working here for two or three years, and I’ve never once seen her husband. He’s probably either divorced or dead. And this Director Han’s son is already in middle school and calls her ‘Mom’ nonstop. For something as trivial as this, the director himself went to school to back her up. If they’re not having an affair, I’ll cut my head off for you!”","Wang Lanying kept rambling. “I always thought Qiao Lanshu had no connections, yet she acts so recklessly at school, never showing respect to anyone. Our principal and dean are always siding with her. I used to think they had the hots for Qiao Lanshu, but it turns out she’s got a director backing her.”","“Hmph,” Wang Lanying continued. “I can’t touch a Public Security Bureau director, but I can still go after Qiao Lanshu, a teacher. You handle this quickly. If she doesn’t accept it, just follow the procedures and investigate her. Something’s bound to turn up!”","Her husband couldn’t talk her out of it, but he was still cautious.","Before rejecting all of Qiao Lanshu’s award nominations, he used his access to check her files.","Qiao Lanshu had been directly assigned to teach at the school after graduating from university.","She had an impressive academic record and work history.","The file only listed her father’s details, and under the ‘spouse’ column, it said Qin Yuanzheng, with the occupation listed as ‘military.’","So he told Wang Lanying, “See, she has a husband, and he’s a soldier.”","Wang Lanying sneered, \"That's right. Her husband is a soldier, so her moral misconduct is even more serious! While soldiers are out there protecting the country and enduring long separations from their spouses, she couldn't bear the loneliness and got involved with another man. What do you think of that? What she did is criminal. Firing her was getting off easy.\"","......"]},{"number":248,"title":"Chapter 248: Her Husband Is the Commander","paragraphs":["So, on that afternoon, all of Qiao Lanshu’s applications for various excellence awards had already made their way to the Education Bureau, but they still got sent back.","Along with them came staff members from the Education Bureau. They called them staff, but in truth, they were investigators assigned to handle this particular whistleblowing case.","If investigators had already been dispatched to conduct a probe, that meant the complaint letter had been accepted, and now the Municipal Education Bureau was pushing forward with an investigation into the matter.","For Qiao Lanshu, this was extremely troublesome. No matter how things turned out in the end, it would inevitably impact her work.","At the very least, if this dragged on for seven or eight days, she would miss the deadline for the awards. And if that happened, wouldn’t all her chances of getting an award this year be ruined?","The investigator from the Education Bureau arrived at the principal’s office and, with a relatively polite tone, said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Teacher Qiao, we’ve received a complaint regarding your personal conduct. We’ve come down today to look into it and need to ask you some questions. You must answer truthfully and cooperate with the investigation, without any concealment.\"","Qiao Lanshu stood in the office and cast a glance at the director of the school’s logistics department.","The director was also quite taken aback. He looked at Qiao Lanshu and asked, \"Teacher Qiao, what have you done recently? Why is someone accusing you of misconduct?\"","Qiao Lanshu looked somewhat bewildered as well. She said, \"I have no idea either.\"","The logistics director then asked the Education Bureau staff, \"What does the complaint letter say? Our Teacher Qiao has always been exemplary in conduct—diligent and proactive. Where exactly is this problem supposed to be?\"","The Education Bureau staff member cleared his throat and said, \"Someone reports that she has committed the crime of disrupting a military marriage. As a military family member, she is allegedly involved in an improper relationship with another man...\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu began to reflect on exactly who she might have been involved with improperly.","Could it be Teacher Zhao?","That shouldn’t be. Ever since that 'accidental' encounter with Teacher Zhao at the market, she had made things clear with him, and they hadn’t seen each other for several days now.","Besides him, who else could there be?","It seemed there was no one?","Qiao Lanshu felt a bit nervous at first. If Qin Yuanzheng found out about this, he would probably be jealous again.","She would have to spend a long time coaxing him later.","Damn it. Just who was the bastard who would make up such a malicious complaint and try to frame her?","...","As a devoted teacher, moral character was naturally of utmost importance.","Since Qiao Lanshu was a high school teacher, if she was caught engaging in messy relationships and allegedly disrupting a military marriage, these two charges piling up would make even criticism and dismissal seem lenient.","Qiao Lanshu sat upright in the office, her back straight, her face stern, without the slightest hint of panic as she defended herself: \"My husband works at the military district here in Wencheng. He usually lives with our family as well. We’ve been married for ten years, and we are very much in love. I wouldn’t, and I couldn’t, do something like that.\"","Then, she turned to the Education Bureau investigator and said, \"Comrade, the complaint is pure nonsense. I demand a thorough investigation into the person behind it. I suspect this is a deliberate slander.\"","The logistics director, of course, sided with Qiao Lanshu. He said, \"Comrades, this must be a misunderstanding. Our Teacher Qiao has been teaching at this school for three years now. We’ve all seen her character. Surely she wouldn’t do such a thing.\"","Then the director asked, \"Since someone wrote a complaint letter, did they mention who, exactly...\"","The office director paused for a moment, glanced at Qiao Lanshu, and then asked, “Does it clearly state the name of the person who was allegedly having an improper relationship with Teacher Qiao? If not, isn’t this just baseless slander? If it does, then we should summon that person here and question them on the spot—wouldn’t that be simpler?”","The official from the Education Bureau nodded and said, “It says it’s Director Han of the Provincial Public Security Bureau, Han Wenlin.”","The office director was stunned. “Ah? A bureau director?”","Was this person really that influential?","The office director hesitated and said, “Comrades, he’s a provincial bureau director—there’s no reason for him to do something like this, right?”","The two Education Bureau officials also felt it seemed unlikely.","One was a high school teacher, the other a provincial bureau director—both were in positions where reputation and face mattered greatly.","Would they really do such a thing?","But Qiao Lanshu understood in an instant—this complaint letter must have been written by Wang Lanying.","Having just dealt with the matter of her two children that morning, Wang Lanying was surely holding a grudge against her now.","Looking directly at the two Education Bureau officials, Qiao Lanshu spoke up: “Comrades, this complaint letter was submitted by Wang Lanying’s husband, wasn’t it?”","Afraid they might not know Wang Lanying, she added, “I mean the logistics department’s Section Chief Li, or Deputy Section Chief—is there such a person? He’s Wang Lanying’s husband. Wang Lanying and I have some history, and she might be targeting me because of that.”","The office director’s expression turned grim. “You mean Teacher Wang? Why would she do that?”","Those who became teachers were typically highly educated intellectuals with unimpeachable character.","But then again, Qiao Lanshu had been among the first batch of candidates after the resumption of the college entrance exams. Before her cohort of teachers joined, most of the earlier teachers had either inherited their positions from their parents or were former \"worker‐peasant‐soldier\" students who were assigned posts after graduation.","Wang Lanying was one of those \"worker‐peasant‐soldier\" university students. She had been teaching at the school for seven or eight years, and the office director knew her character best.","He didn’t immediately refute Qiao Lanshu; instead, his expression turned troubled.","The two Education Bureau officials exchanged surprised glances, and one of them nodded, saying, “The complaint was indeed submitted by Deputy Section Chief Li. However, regardless of the complainant’s identity, we still need to investigate the allegations regarding your conduct.”","In such cases of alleged moral misconduct, the accused not only had to cooperate with investigators but also had to write extensive materials to prove their innocence.","Seeing that time was getting late, Qiao Lanshu thought to herself that at least Han Ye was helping pick up the children, so she didn’t have to worry about that.","Han Ye might usually be a careless troublemaker, but when it came to taking care of his younger siblings, he was quite reliable.","Because of this complaint letter, not only did Qiao Lanshu have to stay and write a defense, but the office director also had to stay and accompany her. The principal had asked a few questions but then left to attend to other matters.","The two investigators from the Education Bureau remained on-site to take notes.","Of course, while Qiao Lanshu had investigators here, there would naturally be a separate investigation into Han Wenlin’s side.","However, the investigators sent to the Public Security Bureau weren’t from the Education Bureau—they were sent by the Organization Department.","Qiao Lanshu was cooperating with the investigators and writing a statement, but she was fuming inside. She thought to herself that once this matter was resolved, she would definitely report Wang Lanying for defamation.","As dusk fell, the office director turned on the lights and said, “Comrades, it’s getting late. How about we all head home for now and continue tomorrow?”","Qiao Lanshu had only written half of her statement. She shook her wrist, thinking she should go home and cook dinner for the kids.","But the two investigators from the Education Bureau replied, “That won’t do. We’d like to go home too, but according to the rules, the statement must be submitted today. The Bureau requires that the investigation be concluded and a disciplinary notice issued within two days at the latest.”","Qiao Lanshu sighed and had no choice but to continue writing.","Just then, someone knocked on the door. The office director opened it and was surprised to see the principal.","The principal was a slightly plump man with glasses. He had left half an hour ago.","Now he had returned, and behind him were five or six cadres from the secretariat and logistics departments, along with members from the campus security team. A whole crowd of people stood silently in the corridor outside the office.","This was a big show of force, but there was no serious meeting to hold or important policy to relay. Why had everyone suddenly come back? What major incident had occurred?","The office director stood at the door and looked at the principal. “Principal Qi, what’s going on?”","The principal walked in with a stern expression, while the others remained in the corridor, not saying a word.","After entering, Principal Qi asked, “Where is Comrade Qiao Lanshu?”","The director pointed. “She’s in the room writing her statement. Someone reported her, and she’s cooperating with the investigators.”","The director didn’t believe Qiao Lanshu could have done what she was accused of, so he wasn’t worried, but he still had to cooperate as required.","The two investigators from the Education Bureau stood up and greeted Principal Qi.","Principal Qi nodded. “Teacher Qiao’s husband has arrived. He heard about this and said he’d cooperate with the investigators as well. If you have any questions, feel free to ask him later.”","As he spoke, he coughed twice, a hint of mockery in his eyes, as if he was ready to watch someone make a fool of themselves.","The two colleagues from the Education Bureau immediately said, “Really? That’s even better. Then we can finish the investigation sooner and go home.”","The office director asked in a low voice, “Principal, Teacher Qiao’s husband is here? Isn’t he a military man? Did he have time to come?”","Didn’t military personnel have to file a report to leave the base? How had he come so quickly?","Principal Qi nodded. “He really is here. Look, there he is.”","With that, Principal Qi quickly stepped out to greet him.","The office director also hurried out.","None of them had ever met Qiao Lanshu’s husband, and they didn’t even know his exact identity. They were all men in their thirties or forties, and even if they were curious, they couldn’t just ask a young female teacher in her twenties about such a personal matter, right?","What if it caused misunderstandings?","When Qiao Lanshu heard that her husband had arrived, her hand, holding the pen, stopped. She muttered to herself, “Why is Qin Yuanzheng here?”","Hadn’t they told her that his identity was classified and he couldn’t just show up casually?","Before she could overthink it, she saw Qin Yuanzheng striding in from the corridor, clad in a crisp, imposing military uniform and cap, flanked by two guards, and surrounded by Principal Qi and the school’s security personnel.","The two investigators from the Education Bureau abruptly stood up. They exchanged a glance, both visibly startled by what they saw.","The office director was utterly dumbfounded, standing by the door, unable to speak for a long while as he stared at Qin Yuanzheng.","Qiao Lanshu quickly rose to her feet, somewhat surprised to see him: “Why are you here? Why didn’t you go home first?”","Qin Yuanzheng’s presence was so commanding that no one in the room dared to utter a word. They all stared at his insignia, mentally calculating his rank.","Only Qiao Lanshu showed no fear. Instead, she scolded him in displeasure: “You should have gone home first. The kids won’t have me there when they return, and there’s no food. That just won’t do.”","Qin Yuanzheng sighed inwardly. He had been worried sick himself when he got home and didn’t find her.","His young wife was beautiful and clever, and he knew many of the younger male teachers at the school had a fondness for her.","Qin Yuanzheng took Qiao Lanshu’s hand and said, “I heard there are allegations about your conduct—improper relationships and violations concerning marriage with a military member—so I came specifically to look into it.”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","Everyone else: “...”","One of the guards brought over a chair for Qin Yuanzheng. He sat down without hesitation, then gestured for everyone else to sit as well. He sat there like a commanding general, his gaze bearing down on them with heavy authority. He turned to the Education Bureau officials and asked, “I understand someone has reported concerns about my spouse’s conduct. May I see the complaint letter?”","The Education Bureau officials quickly nodded and handed over the letter.","As they did, they thought to themselves: Principal Qi had just urged them to ask anything they wanted.","But who would dare to interrogate an officer of his rank?","That Principal Qi was truly scheming!","Qin Yuanzheng read through the complaint letter briefly, then let out a sudden laugh. “Han Wenlin? No way,” he said.","He addressed the room: “My wife would never stoop to that. Han Wenlin is our friend; we raised his son. Our families are close. If exchanging a few words with a friend counts as an improper relationship, then I suppose none of you here have been innocent.”","Everyone: “...”","None of them dared to respond.","The two Education Bureau investigators, unnerved by Qin Yuanzheng’s stern gaze, were already breaking into cold sweat.","One of them mustered the courage to say, “Commander is right, of course. But we’re simply following standard procedures in handling public complaints. It’s almost done.”","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. He set the complaint aside and asked, “What else is needed?”","The investigator wiped the sweat from his forehead. “Just a written statement from the person in question. Once we have that, we can proceed.”","Qin Yuanzheng turned to Qiao Lanshu: “Have you finished your statement?”","Qiao Lanshu nodded. “Almost.”","She quickly wrote a brief statement and handed two full pages to the investigator.","The investigator took the materials and didn’t dare linger further. He said only that he would submit them for review, with the result to be announced within two days.","Qin Yuanzheng stood up, his tall and imposing figure drawing the eyes of everyone in the room, who found themselves looking up at him.","Qin Yuanzheng said to the investigators, “If after a thorough investigation, the contents of the complaint are found to be entirely groundless, then I must ask you to strictly investigate the complainant and impose serious consequences as a warning to others. Otherwise, if anyone can casually file false accusations and slander others, won’t society descend into chaos?”","What more could the investigators say at that point?","They could only nod repeatedly, while silently thinking to themselves: Did the person who submitted that complaint actually know that Teacher Qiao’s husband is a Commander?","If she did know, would she still have written that complaint letter?"]},{"number":249,"title":"Chapter 249: Wife, are you asking for a beating again","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu had thought that cooperating with the investigators today would mean she wouldn't be able to get home until at least eight or nine in the evening.","After all, there had been cases before where people were reported, and due to the seriousness of a teacher's identity, the investigation would take a long time and be very troublesome, whether the accusations were true or not.","But this time, as soon as Qin Yuanzheng appeared, the investigators stopped making things difficult for her.","It seemed that as the wife of the military district commander, she still enjoyed some preferential treatment.","The chauffeur drove the car, with Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu sitting in the back.","Qin Yuanzheng held Qiao Lanshu's hand and stroked it, kneading each of her fingers one by one.","But Qin Yuanzheng remained silent for a long time, so Qiao Lanshu tilted her head to look at him. \"What's wrong? Brother Zheng, are you angry?\"","Qin Yuanzheng sat there and turned to look at her. His expression was still serious with a hint of coldness.","But there was also a trace of tenderness in his eyes as he looked at Qiao Lanshu. Even though he deliberately put on a stern face, he still couldn't fool his little wife.","Qiao Lanshu couldn't help but laugh and said softly, \"Brother Zheng, are you jealous?\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at Qiao Lanshu's fair and rosy face. His wife had given birth to two children and had been married to him for nearly ten years, yet she was still a young and beautiful girl.","Her fair skin was flawless, her eyes as clear as ever, and her figure had shed the slenderness of a girl, becoming the plump and full figure of a young matron.","Only her waist remained slender. He reached out and grabbed her waist firmly, jealous, even slipping his hand into her clothes and pinching her soft waist.","Qiao Lanshu let out a low cry, and then he pressed her into his arms with one hand.","He held her tightly, looking at her with a straight face, and asked in a deep voice, \"What exactly is going on? Last time it was young Teacher Zhao, and this time it's Han Wenlin.\"","He paused, very displeased, and said, \"Why Han Wenlin? He's about the same age as me, and he doesn't look as good as me. Look at his hair—half of it is white. Could you really fall for him?\"","The work at the public security bureau was too exhausting. Over the past few years, Han Wenlin had been mentally and physically drained. Although he was only in his thirties and in his prime, white hair had already appeared.","Qin Yuanzheng felt that in terms of appearance alone, Han Wenlin was absolutely no match for him.","Qin Yuanzheng continued, \"Besides, how many years has Han Wenlin been out of the military? He hasn't kept his figure either—he doesn't even have abs anymore. If you fell for him, wouldn't you miss out on your favorite abs?\"","As he spoke, he unbuttoned his military jacket, grabbed Qiao Lanshu's hand, and pressed it against his own abs.","Qin Yuanzheng had always kept himself in excellent shape. Perhaps because his wife was so young, he had become more and more concerned about his appearance and physique in recent years.","He went to the training ground every day, even earlier than the young soldiers.","He had to maintain his body, training from his arms to his torso and legs.","A man's stamina must not decline—once it does, women won't like it anymore.","The two young chauffeurs sitting in the driver's and passenger's seats heard their commander say these things for the first time.","They were extremely shocked but dared not look back, nor could they exchange glances. They could only hold it in with great effort.","They never would have imagined that the commander they regarded as cold, stern, and rigid was actually so desperate in private.","Just to win his wife's favor, he was even selling his looks.","Qiao Lanshu was also amused by Qin Yuanzheng despite herself.","He pressed her into his arms, and she laughed so hard she was shaking all over. As he watched her laugh, even his stern expression couldn’t hold up.","He pinched Qiao Lanshu’s chin and said in a low voice, “Still laughing? You’ve got some nerve laughing?”","Qin Yuanzheng was practically fuming at Qiao Lanshu, but then he reconsidered—his wife hadn’t really done anything wrong. The real culprit was the one who had filed a baseless complaint against her after catching wind of some rumor.","Qiao Lanshu leaned against him, wrapped her arms around his neck, and murmured, “Of course I wouldn’t take a liking to Han Wenlin. I’ve already got the most handsome and outstanding man in the world. ‘Once you’ve seen the vast ocean, no other water can compare.’ Now, aside from you, I can’t see anyone else worth my attention.”","Even though she found those words a bit cheesy, Qiao Lanshu knew that Qin Yuanzheng loved hearing them.","And sure enough, after hearing that, Qin Yuanzheng could barely keep his composure.","He lowered his head, playing with Qiao Lanshu’s earlobe as he said quietly, “If this matter isn’t handled well, it could affect your future work and promotions.”","He continued softly, “Let me handle it. I’ll go to the Education Bureau myself tomorrow.”","Qiao Lanshu looked up at him. “Do we really need that? Isn’t that going a bit overboard?”","The thought of the military district commander showing up at the Education Bureau—didn’t that sound a little intimidating?","Qin Yuanzheng was still in a sour mood. “Overboard? My wife’s been reported, so it’s only natural and proper for me to follow up on it.”","Qiao Lanshu didn’t argue any further.","What she didn’t expect, though, was that not only would Qin Yuanzheng go to the Education Bureau, but the Public Security Bureau director, Han Wenlin, would go as well. But that was a story for later. For now, Qiao Lanshu still had to deal with the jealous husband at home.","When the couple got home, Han Ye had already cooked the rice, fried a plate of eggs, blanched some lettuce, washed and plated some pickled vegetables, and steamed a few sausages. The three kids were sitting together eating dinner.","Just as they were finishing up, Han Ye finally relaxed when he saw Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng walk in.","Xiaxia put down her bowl and rushed out. “Mom, you’re finally back!”","Qiao Lanshu gave Xiaxia a hug and smiled. “Your big brother made dinner for you?”","An’an came out holding his bowl, a piece of sausage still in his mouth. He said, “Big brother can’t cook. The rice is still hard in the middle, and the eggs are all burnt from too much soy sauce. Mom, why did you take so long? I’m so hungry.”","Qiao Lanshu looked at her son, her smile faltering. She frowned, reached out, and pinched An’an’s cheek, turning it left and right to examine it. “What happened to your face? Did someone hit you?”","Qin Qiao’an had fought with Li Taohua’s older brother, Li Jian, that morning, and half of his face had swollen up from the blows.","Thankfully, after an afternoon, it looked a lot better now. But one side of his face was still a little bruised, which looked alarming. Han Ye had even boiled an egg earlier to roll over his face to help with the swelling.","An’an said guiltily, “No, nothing...”","Xiaxia cut in right away, “Mom, big brother got beaten up by Li Taohua’s brother this morning. That brother is too fat and really tall too. My brother couldn’t beat him.”","Qiao Lanshu: “???”","Qin Qiao'an was unhappy the moment he heard this. He said loudly, \"Who says I can't beat him? Didn't I make him howl in pain? Sure, the injuries on my face look scary, but he had plenty of bruises too—they just don't show.\"","Qiao Lanshu asked Xiaxia a few questions and finally learned what had happened.","It turned out that before Han Ye went to school to stand up for Xiaxia, An'an had already gotten into a fight with Li Taohua and her brother.","Qiao Lanshu sighed and turned to look at Qin Yuanzheng.","Qin Yuanzheng stared at An'an's face, his expression stern.","Qin Qiao'an sensed his father's bad mood and immediately grew a little guilty.","Even Han Ye sat there nervously, not daring to move.","The two brothers, who were nothing short of arrogant outside, now seemed meek and cautious.","Qin Yuanzheng looked at his son several times before saying, \"What you did today was right. When your sister is being bullied, it's proper for her brothers to step up and help.\"","He paused and then continued, \"But you also need to be smart about it. What you did today was too reckless—injuring the enemy a thousand only to suffer eight hundred yourselves! Especially you, Qin Qiao'an. If you're going to fight, at least win! This summer, you're coming with me to the military base for training.\"","Qin Qiao'an: \"...\"","The moment he heard about military training, he immediately wilted.","He'd heard that training at a military base was incredibly grueling. Even though he was still just a kid and the guards probably wouldn't be too strict with him, it would still be exhausting. He'd rather go out and play.","Han Ye, intimidated by the atmosphere, didn't dare to make a sound. He quickly stood up, slung his schoolbag over one shoulder, and dashed to the yard, calling out, \"Mother Qiao, I have things to do at home, so I'll head back now. There's food in the pot—take your time eating.\"","With that, he vanished like a gust of wind. Given his years of training, he sure was fast.","Qin Yuanzheng had initially wanted to call Han Ye back and give him a piece of his mind, but on second thought, Han Wenlin seemed to have been pretty idle lately—idle enough to have rumors spread about him and his wife, and he'd even been going on blind dates, trying to find a girlfriend.","Let Han Ye go back. Having such a dutiful son around would give Han Wenlin something to keep him busy.","With that in mind, Qin Yuanzheng didn't stop Han Ye and let him slip out quickly.","By now, it was getting late, and the kids were hungry. Qiao Lanshu was also famished.","She said, \"Let's put everything aside for now and eat first.\"","Qiao Lanshu went to check the dishes on the table. Han Ye couldn't cook well, but considering no parents were home, it was still impressive that he managed to make a few dishes for his younger brother and sister.","However, the fried eggs had too much soy sauce. Qiao Lanshu soaked them in hot water to rinse off the soy sauce before eating them.","The blanched lettuce had turned a bit yellow—it lacked oil when blanched—but it was still edible.","Qiao Lanshu steamed the undercooked rice again, along with a few sweet potatoes, and the family finally had their dinner.","After dinner, Qin Yuanzheng took Qin Qiao'an to the yard for boxing practice.","Because Qin Qiao'an had lost his fight today, Qin Yuanzheng made him train an extra half hour, focusing on teaching him hand-to-hand combat.","Qin Yuanzheng had initially wanted to teach his daughter as well, but Xiaxia was afraid of getting tired and didn't want to learn. She only wanted to read.","Sometimes, Qin Yuanzheng worried that his daughter might turn into a bookworm.","After finishing the training and taking a shower, Qin Yuanzheng went back to the house.","Their house had three rooms. Both his son and daughter had their own rooms, but since the two children were timid, they usually slept together in one room.","When Han Ye came over, he got a room to himself.","Qin Yuanzheng wiped his hair with a towel and glanced into the room. There were two beds inside, with a table set up between them. On the table sat a small oil lamp.","The lamp gave off a faint light. An'an and Xiaxia each lay on their own beds, already asleep.","Xiaxia was covered with a quilt, sleeping in a quiet, well-behaved manner.","But An'an, exhausted from the training, had his feet still on the floor and his upper body sprawled across the blanket. He was snoring softly, fast asleep.","Qin Yuanzheng chuckled, walked over, moved An'an onto the bed, pulled the quilt over his belly, and then left the room.","Qiao Lanshu had also finished her bath. She hung up the clean clothes to dry, and when she saw Qin Yuanzheng coming over, she asked in a low voice: \"Are they both asleep?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. He took the clothes from her hands, helping to hang them, and said quietly: \"They're both asleep. Should we turn in too?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. Once the couple returned to their room, she was about to discuss with Qin Yuanzheng the idea of letting Xiaxia skip a grade.","But Qin Yuanzheng suddenly scooped her up and headed straight for the bed. He said in a low voice: \"Let's talk about other things later. First, let's deal with the matter of you disrupting a military marriage.\"","Qiao Lanshu looked surprised: \"I thought that matter was already settled?\"","Qin Yuanzheng said quietly: \"It's not that easy to settle. To make sure you don't set your eyes on any other man, I need to remind you of my capabilities.\"","He continued: \"I've been too busy lately. How long has it been since we've been intimate? Twenty-something days, right? Or a month? Have you been thinking I'm losing my touch, and that's why you've been getting so close to other men?\"","Qiao Lanshu felt that Qin Yuanzheng was talking nonsense.","She couldn't help laughing and said: \"I've never thought that...\"","Qin Yuanzheng carried her onto the bed. They were an old married couple by now—look, his wife didn't even blush at the sight of him anymore.","He looked at her and asked: \"So tell me, is a month a long time?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded honestly: \"It has been a little long.\"","Not wanting to be teased by him the whole time, she deliberately replied: \"Brother Zheng, you've never held back this long before. Why have you stopped for nearly thirty days this time? Are you telling me you've got someone else out there?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","His face darkened, and with a loud \"smack,\" he hit her on the bottom.","He said sternly: \"Nonsense. Besides you, who else could I have eyes for?\"","Qiao Lanshu covered herself, let out a few soft grumbles, and glanced at him: \"Who's to say? You're now the commander of the military subregion. There must be plenty of female comrades in your office, right? The time you spend with them every day is more than the time you spend with me. So who knows...\"","Qin Yuanzheng abruptly pinned Qiao Lanshu down on the bed. He was genuinely irritated by her and said through gritted teeth: \"It looks like you're just asking for a spanking today. Just wait—I'll see if you can still say that later.\"","With that, his big hand reached out and began pulling off her clothes.","Qiao Lanshu put up a playful resistance as she said: \"Hey, hey, hey, Chief Qin, before you finish explaining yourself, don't you dare mess around. A gentleman uses words, not hands!\"","Qin Yuanzheng pulled off her pants, placing a pillow under Qiao Lanshu's lower back. He pressed down on her legs, squinting as he said, \"Fine, I'll use my mouth and not my hands. Don't complain later when you're not satisfied.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng felt that Qiao Lanshu was being a bit too cheeky—she really needed a good lesson this time.","It had been nearly thirty days since they'd last been intimate, so it had been a while.","Before half an hour was up, Qiao Lanshu couldn't take it anymore. She said, \"Ah, Brother Zheng, maybe you could...\"","Qin Yuanzheng wiped his face, cutting her off. \"It was you who said a gentleman uses his mouth, not his hands.\"","Qiao Lanshu was on the verge of tears and started to act cute. \"I was wrong, I was wrong, okay? Besides, Brother Zheng, are you really a gentleman?\"","Hearing this, Qin Yuanzheng immediately slapped her once and said in a deep voice, \"Still teasing? Asking for another spanking?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu dared not say another word. Qin Yuanzheng had plenty of strength and ways to make her regret it—she wouldn't provoke him anymore.","But even staying silent wasn't okay.","Qin Yuanzheng gave her another spank and ordered, \"Talk!\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\""]},{"number":250,"title":"Chapter 250: Backing Up My Daughter-in-Law","paragraphs":["When Qiao Lanshu woke up in the morning, her entire lower back ached.","She hadn't felt this way in a long time.","Ever since the children had grown older, and Qin Yuanzheng was no longer young, and because both of them were busy with work, he had exercised a lot more restraint and wasn’t as rough with her as he had been in their younger days.","But last night, something must have gotten into Qin Yuanzheng. He’d set his mind on making her recognize his abilities.","As if she didn’t already know exactly what he was capable of!","She’d begged for mercy for half the night, but it was useless. He’d tossed and turned her around and “taught her a lesson” three or four times.","At the start, they’d agreed that a gentleman uses words, not fists, but he couldn’t keep that promise at all. Before the battle had even officially begun, he was already laying into her with a thorough thrashing.","Qiao Lanshu didn’t dare say another word about it, afraid that the more she complained, the more worked up he would get.","Even now, she still felt sore. She didn’t dare sit down. She quickly stood up, her face grimacing. Looks like she’d be spending the whole day on her feet. The pain had mostly faded, but it was still deeply uncomfortable.","And the more she thought about it, the more she hated that Wang Lanying.","This was all her fault!","If it hadn’t been for her writing that completely baseless letter of accusation, claiming Qiao Lanshu had improper relationships with men, she wouldn’t have been punished and tormented like this by Qin Yuanzheng.","Qiao Lanshu changed her clothes, pinning up her glossy black hair with a hairpin. Today, she was going to find Wang Lanying and settle the score properly!","Qin Yuanzheng had already finished breakfast with the children, and they were all dressed and ready.","When Qiao Lanshu came out, Xiaxia said, “Mommy, you’re late getting up today. Hurry up and eat breakfast, or we’ll be late.”","Qiao Lanshu gave Qin Yuanzheng a resentful glance. He was standing to the side in his military uniform, a sly smile lingering at the corner of his mouth.","Qiao Lanshu glared at him, walked over to sit next to Xiaxia, and lowered herself down with extreme caution.","There was still a dull, numbing ache, both front and back.","Xiaxia and An’an were both very considerate children. The siblings kept piling food onto her plate, urging her to eat quickly so they could leave.","Qiao Lanshu grabbed Xiaxia’s left hand to take a look. The swelling and redness had completely faded. Now it looked rosy and fair, and her hand had already healed.","Xiaxia smiled and said, “Mommy, my hand hasn’t hurt for a long time.”","Qiao Lanshu nodded. “That’s good.”","She had come home late last night, and Xiaxia’s hand was nearly better. She knew that teachers sometimes hit students’ palms with a ruler. She’d had it done to her when she was a child, too.","So she wasn’t particularly angry that Xiaxia had been punished that way. What bothered her was something else. She thought Teacher Qian’s punishment was unfair. The one who deserved to be hit should have been Li Taohua, not Xiaxia.","But that business with Li Taohua was already resolved, so there was no need to bring it up again. As for Teacher Qian hitting the children, Qiao Lanshu was thinking about whether she should talk to her, at the very least to make sure she never laid a hand on Xiaxia again.","Either way, she still needed to quickly arrange for Xiaxia to skip a grade.","Qiao Lanshu ate a few bites. Qin Yuanzheng swiftly cleared the dishes and then led them out the door, saying, “Let’s go. We’ll take you to school today.”","Xiaxia and An’an were usually dropped off by Qiao Lanshu, or by the guard if she was too busy.","Qin Yuanzheng rarely took them, so today the siblings were both delighted.","In the car, Qiao Lanshu told Qin Yuanzheng about the plan to let Xiaxia skip a grade. He nodded and said, “Xiaxia loves to study, and her grades are good. Skipping a grade shouldn’t be a problem. But Xiaxia, what do you think?”","Before Xiaxia could speak, An’an cut in. “This is a good thing, Xiaxia! Then you’ll be in my class, and I’d like to see who still dares to bully you!”","Xiaxia thought for a moment and then nodded. “I think so too. I don’t like Teacher Qian, and I don’t like Li Taohua.”","She had no idea whether Li Taohua would be moved to a different class, but she was pretty sure Teacher Qian wouldn’t be transferred. Teacher Qian was the homeroom teacher and Chinese teacher for the first graders. No matter which class Xiaxia switched to, she wouldn’t be able to avoid her.","But Teacher Qian didn't teach any third-grade classes. So if she skipped a grade, she wouldn’t have to take Teacher Qian’s lessons anymore. Just thinking about it made Xiaxia happy.","She turned to Qin Yuanzheng and said, “Daddy, I want to do what Mommy says. I want to skip a grade.”","Qin Yuanzheng nodded as he drove. “Alright then. Daddy will arrange it.”","He first dropped the two younger children off at their elementary school and then drove Qiao Lanshu to the high school across the street.","On the way, with the children out of earshot, Qin Yuanzheng asked, “Still sore?”","As he spoke, he reached over and pressed down on Qiao Lanshu’s lower back.","Without any hesitation, Qiao Lanshu smacked his arm and said, “You can’t hit me anymore. I still have to teach.”","Qin Yuanzheng was unflappable. “Fine. I’ll just wait until summer or winter break to punish you, then.”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","Furious, Qiao Lanshu smacked him again.","Ever since they’d had children, Qin Yuanzheng hadn’t gotten to flirt and fool around with his wife like this in a long time.","Last night had been very satisfying for him, which was why he was in such a good mood today.","He pulled the car over in front of the high school gates, leaned over, grabbed Qiao Lanshu by the waist, and planted a firm kiss on her cheek, whispering, “Why are you so angry? Weren’t you enjoying it quite a bit last night?”","Qiao Lanshu blushed and pushed him away. “We’re at the school gate. Mind your image.”","Qin Yuanzheng withdrew his hand. “Yes, ma’am, Teacher Qiao.”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","Just as Qiao Lanshu was about to get out of the car, Qin Yuanzheng added, “Don’t you worry about Xiaxia. I’ve already sent the guard to the school to talk to the teacher. You don’t need to go over there yourself. And as for the accusation letter, I’m heading to the Education Bureau right now to sort it out for you. You just go and focus on your job.”","Qin Yuanzheng felt that his wife was still too gentle and kind-hearted. She was far too easygoing.","Talking to those teachers wouldn’t do any good. They weren’t afraid of her.","These kinds of matters required him to step in.","Qiao Lanshu nodded when she heard him speak this way. She gave him a playfully cross glance. “Yes, sir, Chief Qin.”","This man, when he was being serious, was truly reliable.","It was just that when he was fooling around, he was impossible to handle.","...","The Principal's Office.","Teacher Qian knocked and entered, and immediately saw several people sitting in the inner office.","The principal and all the department heads were present. There was also a guard.","Teacher Qian was a bit confused. She walked in and asked, “Principal, you wanted to see me?”","The principal nodded. “Xiao Qian, come in. It’s nothing very serious today. A student’s parent has come to school to ask you a few questions about their child.”","Teacher Qian scanned the office. Aside from the school leaders, there was only one stranger.","That guard, who was wearing a police-style uniform.","But this guard looked very young, even younger than she was. Was he supposed to be a parent?","Hesitantly, Teacher Qian stepped inside and nodded. “Alright. Which student’s parent? What do you want to ask about?”","The guard stood up, greeted Teacher Qian politely, and then said, “Teacher Qian, I am the bodyguard assigned to Chief Qin. The Chief is very busy and couldn’t get away, so he asked me to come in his stead.”","The word “Chief” made Teacher Qian’s heart tighten. A military officer of that high a rank actually had a child in her class?","How had she never known this before?","Teacher Qian was extremely stunned. Before she could even ask, the guard spoke again, quite politely:","\"Our chief’s child, named Qin Qiaoxia, has apparently been behaving poorly these past few days and even had her palm struck during class. Our chief just wanted to ask—has the child been inattentive in class? Or has she had a conflict with other students? Once we clarify the situation, we can better cooperate with the teacher in educating the child back home.\"","Teacher Qian: \"...\"","Teacher Qian’s face changed color. She stared at the guard in shock and asked, \"What did you say? Who are you talking about?\"","...","The guard had been sent by Qin Yuanzheng. Though he claimed it was merely to inquire about the child’s performance at school, only Teacher Qian knew the truth: the chief was giving her a veiled warning.","She realized that he must have seen the marks on his daughter’s palm and was displeased, but he couldn’t come to the school himself to question her.","That’s why he deliberately sent a guard instead.","Thinking this over, Teacher Qian finally understood why Teacher Qiao Lanshu could be so arrogant, not even fearing the Education Bureau.","With a husband who was a commander in the military district, what did Qiao Lanshu have to be afraid of?","After the guard left, the principal and the dean kept Teacher Qian for a while, offering some gentle advice. The principal said, \"Teacher Qian, in the future, try to avoid striking the children. As educators, we should be patient with them.\"","The dean added, \"Yes, look at this situation—it’s gotten to the point where the chief sent someone to ask questions. Though he didn’t say it outright, he’s clearly unhappy, or he wouldn’t have dispatched his personal guard. After you go back, reflect on this. Don’t be too harsh on the children.\"","Though the leaders spoke tactfully, without directly criticizing her, Teacher Qian knew they were already dissatisfied with her.","After all, having a guard come to the school to question a teacher was unheard of, and the principal was far from pleased.","Teacher Qian’s expression was awkward. She nodded and said, \"I understand, Principal.\"","Once she stepped out of the office, her face was grim.","She had already offended Qiao Lanshu, and Qin Qiaoxia didn’t like her either. Even if she tried to be kind to Qin Qiaoxia now, what good would it do?","Moreover, because of this incident, the principal and the dean had taken issue with her.","From now on, she could forget about any evaluation-related honors. She might not even be fit to remain a homeroom teacher.","...","Meanwhile, over at the Education Bureau, the atmosphere was even more awkward.","Qin Yuanzheng had come in person to testify on behalf of his wife, to clear her name of the accusations.","And as it happened, Han Wenlin, the director of the Public Security Bureau, had also arrived early.","So, while the Education Bureau’s director and section chiefs were cordially meeting with Han Wenlin, a report came in less than ten minutes later that Qin Yuanzheng, the commander of the military sub-district, had also arrived.","Upon hearing this, the municipal Education Bureau director, Wu, jumped to his feet and asked his secretary, \"Why is a military district chief here? Has a spy infiltrated our bureau?\"","Han Wenlin, hearing that Qin Yuanzheng had arrived, immediately understood the situation.","He chuckled and said, \"Chief Qin is here for the same reason I am—regarding the accusations against Teacher Qiao. This whole mess has nearly doomed me; I’ve been wrongly labeled a third party, meddling in our Chief Qin’s marriage. I suspect Chief Qin will haul me back to the troops for an interrogation.\"","These words stunned everyone in the room.","Director Wu exclaimed in shock, \"What? Are you saying the female teacher accused this time is Chief Qin’s family member?\"","Han Wenlin nodded. \"Exactly. Even I’m scared enough to come here and vouch for her. What do you think?\"","He was exaggerating a bit. He hadn’t come because he was afraid of Qin Yuanzheng.","Rather, he simply didn’t want a good comrade like Qiao Lanshu to be slandered and have her reputation ruined.","Besides, his own filial son had given him an earful all night, berating him for being useless as a bureau director, lacking authority, and being manipulated by others.","It had made his head buzz, keeping him awake all night.","He was utterly exhausted.","The Education Bureau’s directors, deputy directors, and section chiefs all turned their gazes toward one person.","Director Wu, his face dark, stared at that person and said coldly, \"Deputy Section Chief Li, you submitted the accusation letter, and you arranged the investigation. Think about how you’re going to explain yourself.\"","By then, Deputy Section Chief Li had turned pale and was at a loss for words.","The accusation letter had been brought in by his wife, Wang Lanying.","At the time, Wang Lanying had sworn the matter was true and urged him to dispatch investigators immediately.","He had always obeyed his wife without question. Besides, she had filed accusations against others before. Even if the accusations were baseless, as long as the Education Bureau’s investigators delayed the results, the accused party would remain under suspicion, delaying or canceling their evaluations or selections.","But this time, he had stepped on a landmine.","This Qiao Lanshu turned out to be someone with serious backing—not just the provincial bureau director Han Wenlin, who came to vouch for her, but even the military district commander showing up in person.","Now, he was in deep trouble.","Deputy Section Chief Li’s face was ashen. Before he could figure out what to do, Qin Yuanzheng, accompanied by a few guards, followed the Education Bureau’s secretary into the room.","Qin Yuanzheng was quite easygoing. He said, \"Why is everyone standing? Let’s all sit down and talk.\"","They carefully seated themselves, and a few people began discussing the matter, revolving around the accusation letter.","Of course, by this point, everyone knew Teacher Qiao was clearly innocent. This was undoubtedly a planned and malicious defamation.","The Education Bureau officials were deeply embarrassed. Since they hadn’t verified the facts before deciding on the matter and sending investigators, it was a lapse in their work.","So Director Wu apologized to both Qin Yuanzheng and Han Wenlin.","Qin Yuanzheng didn’t respond directly. Instead, he suddenly asked, \"Director Wu, in this case of malicious defamation, have you found the accuser? Have you properly investigated their motives?\"","Director Wu: \"Uh, well, not yet...\"","Qin Yuanzheng frowned and said, \"A malicious accusation slandering a military family member—my family member—while also dragging in the Public Security Bureau director. I have good reason to suspect that the accuser might have some hidden, ill intentions.\"","Everyone’s heart skipped a beat. Director Wu said nervously, \"This... could there really be a spy in our bureau?\"","Everyone: \"...\"","Deputy Section Chief Li was terrified. If he were labeled a spy, his entire family would be finished.","He suddenly stood up and explained, \"No, no, Director, this was my mistake. I received the accusation letter and didn’t verify it carefully. It was an oversight on my part. I’m willing to accept punishment.\""]},{"number":251,"title":"Chapter 251: Someone Is Trying to Take My Sister Away","paragraphs":["The incident of this report had become serious due to the involvement of Qin Yuanzheng and Han Wenlin.","After Qin Yuanzheng made his stance clear, he didn’t linger too long at the Education Bureau. The bureau gave him a promise on the spot—they would investigate the report—so he left.","Han Wenlin stayed a bit longer. He said to Director Wu, \"Director Wu, I’ve heard before that malicious reports happen often. This time, you need to investigate thoroughly and impose penalties to warn the others. If you can’t handle it, you can come to me. Our Public Security Bureau has some excellent officers who are good at solving cases.\"","Director Wu looked embarrassed and replied, \"Director Han, you’re joking. This isn’t a major case; we can handle the internal investigation. Rest assured, we’ll have results within three days.\"","Han Wenlin was satisfied with that and left the Education Bureau.","Meanwhile, Wang Lanying arrived at the school in the afternoon. She had planned to enjoy seeing Qiao Lanshu being embarrassed and gossip with other colleagues about Qiao Lanshu’s behavior problems. But before she could approach Qiao Lanshu, she was called to the principal’s office.","In the principal’s office, besides the principal, there were two people from the Education Bureau.","The moment Wang Lanying saw Education Bureau officials present, her heart skipped a beat, and she had a bad feeling.","The principal looked at her sternly without saying a word. The investigator from the Education Bureau nodded at her and said, \"Hello, Teacher Wang. Was this report letter submitted by you?\"","Wang Lanying looked at that report letter—she had indeed written it and given it to her husband.","Her lips trembled as she hesitated, \"Well, I...\"","The investigator said, \"Deputy Section Chief Li has already confessed. Teacher Wang, don’t think about denying it.\"","Wang Lanying was speechless.","She tried to calm herself down and said, \"I did write it, but so what? Anyone can report things, right? I didn’t break any rules.\"","The investigator said sternly, \"Of course you can report, but you can’t do it out of disregard for facts and without evidence. That’s slander! What’s more, the person you maliciously reported is the family member of a military officer.\"","Hearing this, Wang Lanying was stunned. She said in surprise, \"The one I reported was just an ordinary teacher. How could she be an officer’s family member?\"","Now, looking at the expressions of the principal and the investigators, Wang Lanying also realized what was happening.","It turned out that although Qiao Lanshu’s husband rarely appeared in public, his status was not low.","Otherwise, Qiao Lanshu would have been the one under investigation, not Wang Lanying.","Seeing her expression, the investigators became even angrier and said, \"What, if you had known she was a military officer’s family member, wouldn’t you have dared to report her? Just because you didn’t know and thought she was an ordinary high school teacher, you went ahead and filed the report?\"","The investigator’s face darkened. \"Teacher Wang, your ideological awareness is too poor!\"","Or rather, she had bad moral character. No matter who the other party was, she shouldn’t have made false reports without any evidence.","Especially for people like them, who are teachers, educating and nurturing future pillars of the nation—they cannot have moral flaws.","Wang Lanying couldn’t help but ask, \"Is Qiao Lanshu’s husband a military officer? What rank?\"","The principal couldn’t hold back and said, \"Teacher Wang, why are you asking about that?\"","Wang Lanying replied, \"Principal, why can’t I ask? I just wrote a report letter, and now the Education Bureau is investigating me instead. I don’t accept this.\"","The investigator couldn’t take it anymore and said,","\"Teacher Wang, at this point, just calm down. You don’t accept it? What else do you want to do? Director Han from the Public Security Bureau has said they’ll assist in the investigation and even brought up past reports. Anything handled by Deputy Section Chief Li—your husband—will be reopened and reinvestigated. You’d better watch yourself.\"","Upon hearing this, Wang Lanying’s face turned white.","She panicked. \"What? Even the past reports are being looked into? This... this...\"","She had never expected that just because she disliked Qiao Lanshu and casually wrote a report, both she and her husband would end up being investigated.","She had done this kind of thing several times before, and every time it went smoothly.","Even when the reports didn’t match the facts, the reporter never faced trouble.","But this time, why did she fall into such a trap?","What Wang Lanying didn’t realize was that the era had changed. It was already the time of reform and openness, and the revolutionary committees had been abolished for years.","Although people were still used to reporting others, this trend needed to be stopped.","Over the years, the Public Security Bureau had received various reports, and some people had no choice but to come and report being maliciously slandered.","Han Wenlin had been busy lately dealing with human traffickers.","He hadn’t had time to handle such cases, but since Wang Lanying had walked right into the line of fire, it was the perfect opportunity to make an example of her and warn the public.","So, the several reports Wang Lanying had filed in the past were all pulled up for investigation. The reason she kept succeeding and being so reckless was that she had a husband who worked as a deputy section chief in the Education Bureau’s logistics department.","Therefore, this time, both husband and wife were suspended from duty for investigation. To cooperate, they had to report to the Public Security Bureau.","...","Qiao Lanshu had initially planned to confront Wang Lanying at work and have it out with her.","But Wang Lanying didn’t show up in the morning, and when she came in the afternoon, she only appeared briefly before disappearing.","On the third day of work, the principal called all staff together for a meeting and announced that Wang Lanying, for maliciously reporting a colleague out of unfair competition and being a repeat offender—over seven years having used similar means to report colleagues and friends, causing two teachers to be suspended and one staff member to be investigated under charges of defamation—had been fired from public office and would never be rehired.","In those days, there was no forced labor, and Wang Lanying’s case wasn’t serious enough for jail time. She was just dismissed from her job and barred from further employment.","Her husband, similarly, for abusing his position to cooperate with his wife in these acts, was also suspended and investigated.","After the meeting, when leaving the conference room, Qiao Lanshu was a bit surprised.","She thought, So Wang Lanying had reported so many people before?","Then it was no injustice this time.","...","On another note, when Han Wenlin was leaving work, he unexpectedly ran into Teacher Qian at the entrance of the Public Security Bureau.","Teacher Qian had been criticized at school, and she didn’t know if she could still make progress in her career.","So, she wanted to try even harder to win over Han Wenlin.","After all, they had met twice and had a meal together. Han Wenlin had had a very good impression of her.","But last time, due to a conflict between two students, when Han Wenlin left the office, he hadn’t even looked at her or spoken to her again.","She felt a bit flustered. Although she didn't want to admit it, she thought that Director Han seemed really reluctant to continue contacting her.","Teacher Qian thought about it all night by herself and decided that she had to make another attempt to meet Han Wenlin.","As soon as Han Wenlin stepped out of the door, he saw her standing beside him.","Han Wenlin paused in his steps, quite surprised. He didn't expect Teacher Qian to come here.","When Teacher Qian saw him, her eyes lit up. She quickly took two steps forward, tidied her hair, and looked at Han Wenlin. \"Director Han, are you off work?\"","Han Wenlin stopped and looked at her. \"Miss Qian, why did you come here?\"","Teacher Qian said shyly, \"Director Han, after we had dinner together last time, didn't we say that if we had time next time, we could meet and get to know each other better?\"","Han Wenlin smiled, with an apologetic look on his face. He said to Teacher Qian, \"Miss Qian, I've thought it over carefully and I think we're actually not quite suitable. You're so young and you can have more opportunities to meet other young male comrades. Let's just call it off.\"","As soon as he said this, Teacher Qian's face turned ugly. She couldn't help taking a step forward. \"Director Han, didn't we get along well before?\"","Han Wenlin was still quite polite. He said gently, \"Before, we were just at the initial stage of getting to know each other. We didn't know much about each other. But after the previous three meetings, I think we're really not suitable. And,\"","He paused for a moment and then added politely, \"My son doesn't like you.\"","This was really straightforward.","No matter how thick - skinned Teacher Qian was, she felt extremely embarrassed at this moment.","They had only met formally twice, but Han Wenlin said three meetings. So, the third meeting was the one in the school office last time because of the kids' matters.","Moreover, he said his son didn't like her. His son was Han Ye, that tall and rather arrogant boy who called Qiao Lanshu mom.","Teacher Qian's face burned with shame. How could she have the face to stay?","After saying goodbye to Han Wenlin, she quickly walked away.","There was really no possibility for her and Han Wenlin's match.","After Han Wenlin got home, surprisingly, he saw Han Ye at home.","He remembered that Han Ye had scolded him last night because of Qiao Lanshu's being reported, and his head started to buzz.","He asked, \"Why are you back?\"","Wasn't Han Ye always fond of staying at Qiao Lanshu's place?","Han Ye was lying on the sofa, reading a martial - arts novel. As soon as he heard Han Wenlin's voice, he immediately bounced up from the sofa and said, \"What? Don't you want me to come back?\"","Han Wenlin took off his shoes and entered the house. \"I didn't say that.\"","Han Ye snorted. \"I'm telling you, I'll stay at home these days and won't go anywhere.\"","Han Wenlin was really surprised this time. When his son didn't come back, he missed him so much.","But as soon as he came back, he found him so annoying that he felt like his heart disease was about to act up.","He said calmly, \"Really not going anywhere?\"","Han Ye nodded. \"I have to keep an eye on you, in case you marry a snake - hearted woman! Let me tell you, old man, next time when you go on a blind date, you'd better have someone investigate the other person's resume first. Don't find a vicious step - mother.\"","Han Wenlin: \"...\"","He picked up a water cup and took a sip of water. \"Don't worry. I won't meet Teacher Qian again.\"","Didn't he know what Han Ye was thinking?","He must be worried that he would marry Teacher Qian.","Without Han Ye's reminder, he also thought that Teacher Qian's character was not good.","Han Ye snorted. \"You'd better not meet. If you do, I'll run away from home and never come back.\"","Han Wenlin: \"...\"","Although Han Ye said he would stay at home to keep an eye on Han Wenlin, with his personality, he couldn't stay for long.","Three days later, he went to the primary school again and picked up Qin Qiao'an and Qin Qiaoxia and took them back to the military compound.","As it turned out, he had only been away for three days, and Zhou Dingwen, the person he disliked the most, had actually mixed with his younger brother and sister.","Zhou Dingwen was also in junior high school. Since his father was a regiment commander, their family also lived in the military compound.","They lived quite close to Qin Yuanzheng's family.","Regiment Commander Zhou and Qin Yuanzheng had a good relationship and often visited each other.","If it weren't for the feud between Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen since childhood, where they would either quarrel or fight whenever they met, the two brothers of Zhou Dingwen and the siblings of Qin Qiao'an should have had a very good relationship.","Well, Han Ye had only been away for three days, and they were playing together again.","Han Ye was so angry.","He threw his schoolbag on the ground and strode towards the three of them.","Here, Zhou Dingwen was holding two bottles of soda and handing them to Qin Qiao'an and Qin Qiaoxia. He said to them, \"Here, I'll treat you to soda.\"","An'an swallowed his saliva. He wanted to drink but hesitated and didn't take it. He said, \"Zhou Dingwen, you treated us to soda yesterday. Are you treating us again today?\"","This made Qin Qiao'an a bit embarrassed.","If Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen fought again next time, Qin Qiao'an would feel embarrassed to help Han Ye.","Was this Zhou Dingwen trying to win him over?","Qin Qiao'an was feeling quite sad and indignant in his heart. He couldn't betray his elder brother!","But he really wanted to drink the soda.","While he was struggling here, Xiaxia standing beside him had already reached out her hand and taken the soda.","Xiaxia smiled and said, \"Thank you, Brother Dingwen.\"","Qin Qiao'an immediately turned his head and looked at Xiaxia in surprise.","Zhou Dingwen looked at Xiaxia and smiled. \"You're welcome.\"","Zhou Dingwen only had a brother and no sister. He really liked Xiaxia.","Xiaxia was the dream sister of all boys. She had good grades, was obedient and sensible, gentle and well - behaved, and was also very beautiful.","She always smiled before speaking. When she smiled, her eyes curved and two dimples appeared. She was so adorable.","Zhou Dingwen handed the remaining bottle of soda over. \"Since Qiao'an doesn't want it, then give it to Xiaxia too.\"","Qin Qiao'an turned his head again, shocked at Zhou Dingwen.","Wasn't he supposed to win him over?","He had just said no once. Shouldn't Zhou Dingwen have said a few more words like 'It's okay, just take it and drink', 'No, no, I can't drink your soda', 'Come on, it's just a bottle of soda and it's not worth much' and go through a few rounds of pushing and then he would take the soda embarrassedly?","Zhou Dingwen didn't play by the rules!","Zhou Dingwen gave both bottles of soda to Xiaxia and then asked Xiaxia, \"Xiaxia, I rode my bike here. Do you want me to take you home?\"","Before Xiaxia could say a word, suddenly an angry roar came from behind. \"Take your mother home!\"","Then, the two bottles of soda in Xiaxia's hands were snatched by Han Ye and thrown forcefully at Zhou Dingwen!","This bastard dared to try to win over his younger brother and sister while he was away. He was asking for death!"]},{"number":252,"title":"Chapter 252: Learning","paragraphs":["Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen had never gotten along; you could say they had been at odds since childhood.","But in reality, there weren’t many real conflicts between them—strictly speaking, no major grudges either.","They just couldn’t stand each other.","Han Ye threw the two bottles of soda back, but Zhou Dingwen was quick-eyed and caught them, his expression dark. “Han Ye, what are you doing? I was just offering Xiaxia some soda, not for you. Why are you acting so hostile?”","Han Ye sneered, “Thanks, but my family’s rich—we don’t need your soda.”","With that, he grabbed Qin Qiao’an and Qin Qiaoxia each by the arm and pulled them away. “Come on, Big Brother will buy you some.”","Zhou Dingwen watched Han Ye’s retreating back with a sullen face, feeling frustrated.","But there was nothing he could do—after all, he couldn’t beat Han Ye, and Han Ye was indeed closer to the siblings Qin Qiao’an and Qin Qiaoxia.","Zhou Dingwen stuffed the sodas into his backpack and turned to leave.","Han Ye bought sodas for his younger brother and sister, then earnestly lectured Xiaxia: “That Zhou Dingwen isn’t a good person. He’s just a middle schooler, hanging around the elementary school gate for no good reason—he must have some ulterior motive! So, no free handouts from him, understand? Don’t take anything from him ever again.”","Qin Qiao’an immediately nodded, “Don’t worry, Big Brother, I didn’t take anything from him!”","Han Ye looked seriously at Xiaxia and said, “Xia’er, did you hear me?”","Xiaxia, holding the soda Han Ye had bought, nodded, “Got it.”","Although deep down, she thought Zhou Dingwen was actually a pretty decent guy.","But since both older brothers disliked each other, she decided it was best to keep her distance from him.","After this incident, Han Ye started staying over at Qiao Lanshu’s house from time to time, diligently picking up and dropping off his younger siblings every day, guarding Qin Qiao’an and Qin Qiaoxia like a hawk against Zhou Dingwen and his brother.","......","During this time, Qiao Lanshu’s application for an outstanding teacher award was approved, and she earned the opportunity to study in the capital.","This kind of chance was extremely rare. Nationwide, fewer than a hundred teachers were selected for this program—each province choosing their best young educators who had worked for over three years and held university degrees.","Clearly, this was because after the reform and opening-up, the country was eager to develop all industries, and education was no exception.","These young teachers selected for centralized training were key talents the state intended to cultivate, destined for future promotion and important roles.","Although she had to be away from home for nearly half a year, Qiao Lanshu didn’t want to miss this golden opportunity.","Qin Yuanzheng fully supported Qiao Lanshu, but since he couldn’t accompany her, his heart was heavy with worry.","He lost his appetite and had trouble sleeping.","One evening, while the whole family was eating, Qiao Lanshu teased him, “It’s still two months away. Why are you already sighing like this?”","In front of the children, Qin Yuanzheng couldn’t bring himself to say any sweet nothings. After a pause, he said, “I’ll go with you when the time comes.”","Qiao Lanshu frowned, “No need. If you go, what about the kids? Are you planning to take them with us?”","When she was about to start her studies, the school was just about to break for the holidays. Taking the children along wasn’t a bad idea, but Qiao Lanshu felt the two kids were still too young, and she worried they might get lost.","After all, they had never traveled far before, and with the current state of society being quite chaotic, cases of women and children being abducted were unfortunately common.","Qiao Lanshu said to him, “You stay home and watch the children. We’re going as a group, with a teacher leading us. Nothing will happen.”","Qin Yuanzheng remained uneasy. Looking at the three children, he said to Han Ye, “Han Ye, when the time comes, take An’an and Xiaxia to your place and take good care of them.”","Han Ye nodded immediately. “Don’t worry, Uncle Qin. I promise I’ll look after them well.”","Qin Qiao’an often stayed at Han Ye’s house, though Xiaxia rarely went over.","Although Han Wenlin was busy with work, Han Ye was fairly reliable.","But in the end, Han Ye was still just a kid who had just started middle school—not an adult—so leaving two children in his care was still worrisome.","Qin Yuanzheng thought for a moment and added, “No, it’s better to send the two of them to our cousin in Longcheng’s house to stay for a few days. After I drop you off, I’ll come back quickly. It won’t take long.”","After the reform and opening up, Yang Wenyan had refused a transfer order and stayed at the food factory, personally investing to take over its operations.","Now, he was both the factory director and the owner.","His cousin’s wife, Deng Xiaozhen, had given birth to a son a few years ago but hadn’t conceived again since. She doted on their only child.","Qiao Lanshu considered this and said, “Actually, sending them to Zhong Mei’s place would work too. Didn’t they move recently? Their house is pretty big.”","Many years had passed, and Qiao Lanshu hadn’t been to Longcheng for a long time, nor had she seen Zhong Mei in quite a while.","She added, “Our cousin runs his factory and must be very busy. They don’t have a nanny, so his wife has to juggle taking care of the kids and helping out at the factory. She must be overwhelmed. It might be better to send the kids to Zhong Mei’s place. The four children are close in age, and Zhong Mei just quit her job recently and has some free time.”","Zhong Mei had previously worked as a meter reader—a formal position arranged by Guan Wenjun.","She only worked for a couple of years before giving birth to two sons in quick succession. Since neither of them had parental support, they had to hire a nanny. Zhong Mei balanced working and caring for the children alongside the nanny.","Later, with the reform and opening up, Zhong Mei saw a business opportunity. Once the kids were a bit older, she quit her job.","She planned to open a general store to sell goods and make money. She felt that just earning a fixed salary wasn’t enough; she wanted to do business and make big money.","However, she had been unemployed for several months and hadn’t figured out how to start the business yet. The beginning was always the hardest, and she was still thinking it over.","Qin Yuanzheng agreed, “Sending them to Zhong Mei’s place works too. The four kids are about the same age and can play together.”","Han Ye listened to their discussion and couldn’t help but chime in, “Mom Qiao, if you leave the kids with me, it’ll be totally fine. No need to go through the hassle of sending them all the way to Longcheng. Really, you don’t have to worry about how I handle things.”","Qiao Lanshu shot him a sharp look and said, “It’s precisely because it’s you handling things that I don’t feel at ease.”","Han Ye: “......”","Muttering under his breath, Han Ye said, “What’s there to worry about? I’m pretty reliable when it comes to getting things done.”","Xiaxia interrupted, “You’re always getting into fights. That’s not reliable at all.”","Han Ye quickly defended himself, “Those were all started by others. I never pick fights first.”","Qin Qiao’an hurriedly said, “Dad, Mom, why don’t you just take us along? I’ve never been to the capital before, and I want to see it!”","Xiaxia, on the other hand, looked calm. She was more of a homebody and didn’t like going out much.","But Han Ye’s eyes lit up. “Take me too! I’ve never been to the capital either! I want to go!”","Qiao Lanshu: “......”","Qin Yuanzheng rubbed his chin and hesitated, “Actually, we could bring them along, right? The three kids are pretty sensible. They won’t run off. It’s just an overnight train ride, no transfers needed.”","......","......","In the days leading up to Qiao Lanshu’s trip to the capital for her studies, Qin Yuanzheng had been making all the arrangements.","Their final decision was to take the kids with them.","First, the children had never been outside the hospital before, so it would be a good chance to broaden their horizons.","Second, Qin Yuanzheng and the kids had never been apart from Qiao Lanshu for this long before.","After all, they would be separated for half a year. Not only did Qin Yuanzheng want to send her off, but the kids also wanted to see her off.","Since they were going out of the province, it was quite a long trip.","Having decided to travel as a family, Qiao Lanshu began preparing about five or six days in advance.","They packed food and water for the five of them, along with clothes and daily necessities.","Since she would be away for six months of training and study, there was a lot to prepare.","Qin Yuanzheng and the kids would also be away from home for a few days, so the chickens they raised and the vegetable garden needed someone to take care of them.","Qin Yuanzheng arranged for a security guard to come by daily to feed the chickens and water the garden. Since he wasn’t bringing a guard with him this time, and the others had no other duties besides training, this was the best solution.","Once everything was arranged, the whole family set off.","Han Ye went with them too. Tall and strong, he carried two bags and kept an eye on his younger brother and sister—very capable.","Qin Yuanzheng also carried two bags as they arrived at the train station.","They had bought sleeper tickets again. Qin Yuanzheng purchased five tickets, with one in the adjacent carriage. After settling his wife and children in one carriage, he went to check on the nearby carriage.","Qiao Lanshu and Xiaxia were assigned to the upper berths, as Han Ye had suggested. He said, “Mom, the train can be a bit chaotic. It’s safer for you ladies to sleep up top.”","Han Ye wasn’t new to long trips either. In fact, he had been rescued on a train by Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu when he was a child.","He still remembered all these things vividly, so every time he took the train or went on a trip, he remained extremely cautious, always feeling like everyone around him was out to get him.","Qiao Lanshu and Xiaxia naturally had no objections. Xiaxia grabbed two books and immediately climbed up to the upper bunk to lie down, resting against the pillow as she began reading.","Qin Qiao'an was quite curious—after all, it was his first time on a train. Sitting on the lower bunk, swinging his legs, he asked Qiao Lanshu, “Mom, can I go out and have a look? I want to see what the other carriages are like.”","Han Ye was tidying up their things as he replied, “This is the soft sleeper carriage. There’s also the hard sleeper carriage and the seat carriage. Come on, I’ll show you around.”","Qiao Lanshu climbed down from the upper bunk and took out some boiled eggs, apples, and pancakes from her bag. “Don’t wander too far. Come back soon to eat.”","Han Ye and Qin Qiao'an nodded in agreement and were about to head out.","Han Ye hesitated for a moment, then asked, “Xia’er, do you want to come with us?”","Xiaxia flipped a page without lifting her head. “No thanks. It’s just train carriages. What’s so interesting about that?”","When they first boarded, she had already seen the hard sleeper and seat carriages—they were crowded and chaotic, noisy and cramped. Many people couldn’t even get inside and were climbing through the windows. It was honestly quite scary.","Right now, Xiaxia was incredibly grateful that her father was an officer and Han Wenlin was the provincial bureau chief, so they could buy tickets for the soft sleeper carriage.","Otherwise, if she had to go out there and squeeze among all those people, she would have chosen to stay put.","Qiao Lanshu reminded Han Ye, “You two just take a quick look around and come back soon.”","Han Ye and Qin Qiao'an both nodded and went out together.","After the two brothers left, Qin Yuanzheng returned as well. His seat was in the adjacent carriage, but except for when he was resting at night, he still made sure to come back to see his wife and kids.","Otherwise, he wouldn’t feel at ease.","Qiao Lanshu had already taken out the food and handed Qin Yuanzheng a cucumber. “Sit down and have something to eat.”","Qin Yuanzheng took a bite of the cucumber and then sat down beside Qiao Lanshu.","The couple chatted casually for a while.","This trip to the capital was planned so that before Qiao Lanshu started her studies, they could take the children around to see the city—places like Tiananmen Square.","It wasn’t easy to come here, so they wanted the kids to broaden their horizons.","Qiao Lanshu said to Qin Yuanzheng, “Let’s save up over the next few years and buy a house back in Yangcheng. Then when I go back to visit my family, we’ll have a place to stay.”","In recent years, she had returned to Yangcheng twice to see her family, but both times Qin Yuanzheng had accompanied her. The kids were still young, so she hadn’t brought them along.","She had been married far from home for many years. Her younger brother had grown up and was now in high school.","At home, there was a stepmother, not her biological mother. Whenever she brought her family back, she wanted to stay longer, but it never felt quite right.","Besides, her family’s house was small and crowded.","But at that time, property couldn’t be freely bought or sold. Although she wanted to buy a house, it wasn’t possible yet.","She counted on her fingers—only about five more years until the 1990s, when buying and selling property would become unrestricted.","Over the past five years, she planned to save up as much money as possible, so that by then they could return to Yangcheng and buy a small house.","When Qin Yuanzheng heard her say this, he nodded in agreement without objection. He said, “Buying a house sounds like a good idea. In the future, we could even spend winters in Yangcheng.”","Qiao Lanshu smiled at this and replied, “Maybe someday, the transportation will improve, so it won’t take so long to get back. Besides, houses will only become more valuable over time. Buying a house is a way to save money.”","Qin Yuanzheng thought about it for a moment. He realized that since the reform and opening-up, the country’s economy was indeed picking up. Salaries were steadily rising year by year, and goods were becoming more abundant.","Perhaps his wife was right — houses would only get more expensive, so if they wanted to buy one, they had to act sooner rather than later.","He said, “By that logic, houses in the capital must be even more valuable. Do you want to buy one there? Maybe the kids will develop their careers in the capital someday, and having a place to settle down would be good.”","Qiao Lanshu gave Qin Yuanzheng a playful glare and said, “Where would we get that kind of money? Our family is dirt poor.”","Though Qin Yuanzheng was an officer, his salary was truly modest. For many years, it had been just a hundred yuan.","It wasn’t until 1985, when military ranks were reassessed and income standards clarified, that his salary was adjusted to around three hundred yuan. Fortunately, besides the salary, officers enjoyed other benefits.","For example, the government provided housing and cars, as well as education and healthcare for their children — all allocated by the state, so they didn’t have to spend extra money.","Because of this, every month when Qiao Lanshu received Qin Yuanzheng’s salary, she saved it all.","Her own salary was only about seventy yuan, which she used entirely for daily expenses. After all, raising children was quite costly.","Qiao Lanshu told Qin Yuanzheng, “We simply couldn’t save money before. Your salary was low, and it was only since last July that it increased a bit. We’ve been married for nearly ten years, and I’ve managed to save about fifteen thousand yuan. That amount isn’t nearly enough to buy a house.”"]},{"number":253,"title":"Chapter 253: Traveling by Train","paragraphs":["In the first few years after Qiao Lanshu gave birth to An'an, she didn't have a job herself. At that time, they also hired Auntie Shi as a nanny, so the expenses were quite high. They hardly saved any money during those years.","Qiao Lanshu pondered and said, \"Let's save some more. In a few years, we'll be able to buy a house in Yangcheng. As for the one here in the capital, let's talk about it later.\"","Hearing what Qiao Lanshu said, Qin Yuanzheng suddenly felt a bit uncomfortable.","He was very busy in the army and hadn't taken good care of the children these years. Sometimes when he had to carry out missions, he would be away for several days. Qiao Lanshu really had a tough time.","But now, he didn't have the money to give to Qiao Lanshu either.","Seeing his bad complexion, Qiao Lanshu comforted him, \"Come on, stop thinking about it. Our family is already doing well. There are so many poor people out there. We should be content with what we have.\"","Moreover, Qiao Lanshu just liked to live this kind of peaceful and stable small life.","It was enough for the money to be just sufficient. She had already realized her dream of going to college and had a job she loved. The children were also healthy and happy. She had no regrets in this life.","Qin Yuanzheng silently finished munching on a cucumber and then picked up an egg to peel.","Xiaxia was lying on the upper bunk and hadn't turned a page in her book for a long time.","Listening to her parents' conversation, she also felt very at ease. She thought to herself: Mom and Dad have such a good relationship. What kind of man will she marry in the future?","Will she be able to be as affectionate with her husband as her parents are with each other?","At this time, Han Ye and Qin Qiao'an, who had gone out for a stroll, came back.","Not only the two of them, but there was also a girl in her early teens following behind.","The girl had a round face and was wearing very simple clothes. Although her appearance was just average, she was still quite likable when she smiled.","Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng glanced at each other and then both looked at Han Ye.","Qin Qiao'an had already run in cheerfully, holding a pink peach in his hand. As he ate, he said, \"Mom, guess who we met?\"","Seeing Qin Qiao'an rushing over like a cannonball, Qin Yuanzheng quickly reached out to hold him back and asked him, \"Where did you get the peach?\"","Qin Qiao'an pointed at the girl behind Han Ye and said, \"She gave it to me.\"","Qin Yuanzheng wanted to teach him a lesson and tell him not to take things from others casually, but in front of outsiders, he didn't want to say anything.","Both Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu were looking at Han Ye. Han Ye said to them, \"Uncle Qin, Aunt Qiao, this is my classmate, Liu Wenqiu.\"","Han Ye seemed reluctant to introduce her. Just by looking at his expression, Qiao Lanshu could tell that he didn't seem to be very familiar with this classmate and didn't really want to bring her here.","Liu Wenqiu smiled and greeted Qiao Lanshu and the others, \"Hello, Uncle and Aunt.\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, \"Hello.\"","Looking at the peach in Qin Qiao'an's hand, she quickly picked up an apple and handed it to Liu Wenqiu. \"It's already noon. Are you hungry? This apple is very sweet. Try it.\"","Liu Wenqiu took the apple shyly.","Seeing that she took the apple, Han Ye quickly said, \"Alright, you've seen the soft-sleeper carriage. Let me take you back, okay?\"","If it weren't for Qin Qiao'an being greedy for the peach, Han Ye wouldn't have wanted him to take it.","But since his little brother wanted to eat it, he couldn't stop him.","So when Liu Wenqiu said she wanted to visit the soft-sleeper carriage, Han Ye couldn't refuse and had to bring her here.","Holding the apple in her hand, Liu Wenqiu sized up the soft-sleeper carriage. She said to Han Ye, \"The soft-sleeper carriage is so impressive. Do you always take the soft-sleeper carriage when you go out, Han Ye?\"","Han Ye nodded with a straight face. \"Sort of, but I don't go out very often.\"","Liu Wenqiu stood at the carriage door and chatted with him. \"Didn't you say the one just now was your younger brother? I thought Uncle and Aunt were your parents.\"","Han Ye glanced at Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu.","He saw that they were both looking at him with curiosity and even a hint of gossip on their faces.","Even Xiaxia, who was reading a book on the upper bunk, had stopped reading. She was looking at him one moment and then at Liu Wenqiu the next, with a shocked expression on her face.","Han Ye: \"...\"","Being stared at like this, Han Ye felt extremely embarrassed.","He said to Liu Wenqiu, \"Let's go. I'll take you back first.\"","This was already the second time he had said this, so Liu Wenqiu followed him out somewhat awkwardly.","Along the way, she kept curiously sizing up the compartments of the soft-sleeper carriage.","Liu Wenqiu asked, \"Han Ye, were they really not your parents just now?\"","Han Ye was quite sparing with his words in front of outsiders. He just said, \"No.\"","But he didn't say who they were to him.","After all, he wasn't really familiar with Liu Wenqiu. They were just classmates and didn't talk much to each other on normal days.","It was quite a surprise to meet her on the train.","Liu Wenqiu didn't seem to feel embarrassed at all and was already used to Han Ye's coldness. She smiled and said, \"I thought the uncle just now was Director Han. It turns out he wasn't.\"","Many people in the class knew that Han Wenlin's father was a director.","So it wasn't strange for Liu Wenqiu to say this.","Liu Wenqiu was just curious about the relationship between Han Ye and the family in the soft-sleeper carriage.","After all, a whole family could take the soft-sleeper carriage, which showed that they had a high status.","Thinking about it, Liu Wenqiu took a few more glances at Han Ye.","Han Ye remained silent and didn't say anything else.","When he sent Liu Wenqiu to the hard-sleeper carriage, he said, \"Alright, then I'll go back first.\"","Liu Wenqiu looked at him, hesitating to say something, but still asked, \"Han Ye, where are you all going this time? Are you going to visit relatives?\"","Han Ye thought this Liu Wenqiu was a bit strange. Why was she so talkative and asking so many questions? He wasn't familiar with her at all.","He just gave a perfunctory answer, \"Yes, going to visit relatives.\"","Han Ye obviously didn't have the intention to have a long conversation with Liu Wenqiu on the train, so he quickly turned around and left.","Liu Wenqiu hesitated to say something behind him: \"...\"","When Han Ye came back, he saw that all four people in the carriage were staring at him in unison.","Han Ye: \"...\"","Han Ye rarely felt a bit uncomfortable. He said, \"Why are you all looking at me like that? I didn't do anything bad.\"","Xiaxia became curious. She put the book aside, sat up, and asked him, \"Brother Ye, was that girl just now your classmate?\"","Han Ye glanced at her. \"Yes, Liu Wenqiu. Qiao'an has met her before.\"","Qin Qiao'an nodded while eating the peach.","Xiaxia smiled and said, \"Oh, what a coincidence! It's rare to go on a long trip, and you actually met your classmate, and it's a female classmate.\"","Han Ye: \"...\"","Han Ye looked at her and said, \"Come on. Everyone on this train is from Wencheng. If we go by what you said, then I'd say it's a coincidence with everyone on this train.\"","Xiaxia couldn't help but burst out laughing.","Han Ye stared at her seriously and said, \"I've always told you to read fewer strange books, but you just don't listen. Look, it's addled your brains.\""]},{"number":254,"title":"Chapter 254: Breakfast Stall","paragraphs":["I had thought that Han Ye running into his classmate would just be a small episode in their long journey.","But as it turned out, over the next ten or so hours, Han Ye kept running into Liu Wenqiu from time to time.","After all, Han Ye was never one to sit still, and Qin Qiao'an was just as restless and playful. They couldn't settle down and read like Xiaxia could.","So the two brothers would, every now and then, go out together for a stroll.","And every time they went out for a stroll, they'd inevitably run into Liu Wenqiu.","Han Ye was truly fed up with this classmate of his. He had nothing to say to Liu Wenqiu, and he didn't want to make awkward small talk.","Besides, he wasn't good at dealing with female classmates anyway.","So after only a couple of strolls, Han Ye holed up in the soft sleeper compartment and refused to go out again.","When Qiao Lanshu woke from her nap, she was quite surprised to see Han Ye and Qin Qiao'an both curled up on the lower bunk reading.","She said in astonishment, \"What's wrong with you two? Since when do you read books?\"","They definitely hadn't brought any books with them. Qiao Lanshu had brought textbooks, which she read on the way.","Xiaxia, on the other hand, had brought a few random books — a collection of essays, a poetry anthology, and a martial arts novel.","What the two of them were holding now were the martial arts novels from Xiaxia's bag.","Qiao Lanshu climbed down from the upper bunk and sat beside Qin Qiao'an, saying, \"Why aren't you brothers going out for a walk?\"","Both of them reading books — Qiao Lanshu was really taken aback by these two rascals.","From above, Xiaxia said gleefully, \"Oh, Mom, you don't know — Brother Ye's been so scared by his 'fated encounter' that he doesn't dare go out anymore.\"","Han Ye put down his book and shot Xiaxia a fierce glare, telling her, \"Read your book. What nonsense are you spouting?\"","Xiaxia stuck out her tongue and went back to reading.","Qin Qiao'an also let out a sigh and said gloomily to Qiao Lanshu, \"Mom, girls outside are really scary. That Liu Wenqiu keeps coming to find Big Brother, and now Big Brother won't even go out.\"","Qin Qiao'an repeated himself over and over: \"I'm so bored I could die.\"","Qiao Lanshu looked at Han Ye. The usually unruly Han Ye was also sighing. He said, \"Mom, how many more hours until we arrive? I'm going to grow mold lying here.\"","Qiao Lanshu couldn't help asking, \"That young girl — she seemed pretty nice to me. Why are you so afraid of her?\"","At that, Han Ye couldn't hold it in anymore. He sat up, crossed his legs on the bed, and said to Qiao Lanshu in a low voice, \"She talks too much. The moment she sees me, she starts asking all sorts of questions. I'm not even that familiar with her. Besides, she keeps giving me food. It's not like I'm short on food — but if I eat it, I owe her a favor.\"","The worst part was that every time he refused, she'd put on this hurt, aggrieved look, as if he were some terrible villain.","Han Ye rarely interacted with female classmates, so he had no idea what to do.","So he just hid in the compartment and stayed put.","Hearing all this, Qiao Lanshu understood everything clearly.","That classmate Liu was most likely interested in Han Ye.","Qiao Lanshu studied Han Ye carefully.","Han Ye would be starting eighth grade soon. At fourteen, he looked like his father Han Wenlin — tall, broad-shouldered, and after years of training, sturdy and well-built.","His features were still a bit youthful, but you could already see his deep-set brows and sharp, handsome face.","Great physique, good looks, and a well-off family — even if his grades weren't the best, that was more than enough to catch the attention of female classmates.","Middle school — they weren't that young anymore.","When Qiao Lanshu was in middle school, some of her female classmates had already gotten married before finishing their studies.","So these kids had reached puberty, the age when young hearts begin to stir.","Thinking about this, Qiao Lanshu couldn't help but smile and asked Han Ye, \"From what you're saying, you've never really gotten along with any female classmates?\"","Han Ye had caught on a bit by now, so upon hearing this, he quickly said, \"Of course not. I only hang out with guys. Girls are a no-go — what if they report me for harassment?\"","Qiao Lanshu said with some relief, \"You're quite cautious.\"","In the old days, if a man and a woman so much as stood by the roadside and talked a little too long, people would accuse them of 'improper relations between the sexes.' And if the label of 'hooliganism' got slapped on you, you'd be sent off for reeducation through labor.","Though things weren't as strict now, unmarried men and women still had to keep their distance.","Qiao Lanshu felt that Han Ye was really clever. He didn't even need adults to teach him — he understood a lot on his own.","Then Han Ye said, \"Of course. That old man of mine has been pestered by all kinds of female comrades over the years. If he hadn't been careful, he'd have ended up with who knows how many wives by now. I learned from his experience too.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"About four more hours to go, so not long now. You two should eat something first.\"","The train to the capital took about ten hours or so, which wasn't really that long. Sleep a bit in bed, read a bit, eat a bit — and the time would pass soon enough.","When they reached their destination and got off the train, Han Ye, carrying two bags on his back, said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Mom, you go out first and keep an eye out for me. I'm afraid I'll run into her again.\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled and nodded: \"Alright.\"","However, Qin Yuanzheng was the first to step in front of Qiao Lanshu. He said, \"Get behind me. Han Ye, you stay in the back. Everyone hold hands. The platform is crowded — we can't afford to get separated.\"","The train station really was crowded at this time, and with the lax management, it was especially chaotic.","Qin Yuanzheng led the way in front, Han Ye followed at the back, and Qiao Lanshu walked in the middle with the two younger children. She kept turning back to check on Han Ye every now and then, afraid he might get lost.","When the family came out of the station, the guard sent to pick up Qin Yuanzheng drove over.","Qin Yuanzheng didn't let the guard drive. He borrowed the car and drove his wife and kids himself to the guesthouse, checked them in.","By then, it was already quite late. They got two rooms — Qin Yuanzheng stayed in one with the two boys, and Qiao Lanshu stayed in the other with Xiaxia.","They went to bed early that night, and when they woke up the next morning, the whole family went out for breakfast.","There were plenty of breakfast stalls by the roadside. They sat down at a stall selling soy milk and fried dough sticks, the five of them squeezed around a small square table.","Qin Qiao'an kept looking around curiously the whole way, then said, \"Mom, I think the capital isn't really that special. It's pretty much the same as our Wencheng.\"","Qiao Lanshu said with a smile, \"Well, they're both northern cities, so the difference probably isn't that big? If you ever go to Guangzhou, you'll see the obvious difference between northern and southern cities.\"","Actually, the food in the capital and Wencheng was fairly similar too. To Qiao Lanshu, a southerner, it all felt the same.","Still, the capital was busier and livelier — more buildings, more people packed together.","After the reform and opening up, most people flooded into the cities, and the capital had absorbed countless migrant workers.","Even early in the morning now, the streets were bustling and noisy — chaotic, but lively.","Just then, Han Ye suddenly said angrily, \"What do you think you're doing? Give it back!\"","With that, he abruptly stood up, glaring at a woman in her forties or fifties standing behind him.","The woman was startled by his shout. Then, she curled her lips and tossed over a little red flower, saying, \"Who cares? So grumpy.\"","With that, she stared at Xiaxia for a few good seconds, muttered curses under her breath, and walked off.","Han Ye tucked the little flower back into Xiaxia's hair, frowning. \"That woman's really messed in the head. What's wrong with her, going after Xiaxia's clip like that?\""]},{"number":255,"title":"Chapter 255: Catch the Thief","paragraphs":["The capital had a large population, so naturally all kinds of people could be found there. After the reform and opening up, far too many people had poured into the cities. There weren't enough jobs in the cities, nor enough housing, so many people just found whatever spots they could to set up shacks and live in them, making things rather chaotic.","The capital was in somewhat better shape, but in the more suburban areas, this kind of situation still existed.","Although the various departments were already working hard on urban construction, the work was just getting started, and the development of each city would still take time.","Qin Yuanzheng walked alongside Qiao Lanshu, the whole family strolling along slowly, looking around as they went. He leaned in close to Qiao Lanshu and said, \"You all need to be extra careful, don't go running off. This place is different from Wencheng—there are lots of people and it's chaotic.\"","Then he added another warning: \"The alleyways around here are pitch black, many of them have no lights at all. You three shouldn't go into any alleyways either.\"","Qin Qiao'an was almost ten now, and Qin Qiaoxia was nearly eight. Their ages were not that young, and they were fairly sensible kids.","But Qin Yuanzheng still worried, and so did Qiao Lanshu. She lowered her voice and warned them several times, telling the three of them to stay close to Mom and Dad and not to run off anywhere.","Fortunately, the woman who had earlier tried to steal Xiaxia's hair flower had already run off without a trace.","She had probably just thought the hair flower was pretty and deliberately tried to snatch it for herself.","After the family finished breakfast, Qin Yuanzheng took Qiao Lanshu and the others to the school where she would be training in the future, just to familiarize themselves with the route.","The training would last six months, and Qiao Lanshu would be staying in the dormitories with the other teachers, so this time there was no need to worry about housing.","Qin Yuanzheng deliberately took the whole family on a few loops around the school, checking out the surrounding area.","Then he said to Qiao Lanshu, \"There aren't many streetlights around here. It's probably going to be very dark at night. Don't come out alone after dark. If you need to buy anything, find someone to go with you. Don't go wandering off by yourself.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded and said, \"Don't worry. I definitely won't go out at night.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was worried out of his mind. If it weren't for the kids needing his care, he would have rented a place near the school in a heartbeat and become Qiao Lanshu's companion attending classes with her.","After thoroughly scouting out the area around the school, it was getting late, and the family had to head back to the guesthouse.","On the way back, as they neared the guesthouse, the streets became livelier and livelier.","There were convenience stores by the roadside, fruit stalls, and even more snack stands—ones selling lü dagun, braised offal buns, candied hawthorns, sugar figurine painters...","There were lots of people around. Nearby stood a big willow tree with stone tables and benches beneath it, where some elderly people sat cooling off and chatting, while kids ran around in small groups, playing and chasing each other.","If Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu hadn't been keeping a close eye on them, Han Ye and Qin Qiao'an would have already darted off to play.","Xiaxia tugged at Qiao Lanshu's hand and said, \"Mommy, I want to eat that.\"","She was pointing at a pastry stall. Qiao Lanshu walked her over, took a look, and bought half a jin of mung bean cakes.","Qin Yuanzheng then went over to the next stall, planning to let the kids try some of the local zhajiang noodles.","As luck would have it, they ran into the same woman who had tried to steal Xiaxia's hair flower that morning.","The woman was carrying a bag. As she passed by a sugar figurine stall across the street, she slowed her pace and glanced at the children gathered around watching the figurine maker.","Then, all of a sudden, she reached out toward some little girl who was hopping and skipping along and yanked at the girl's hair.","The girl let out a yelp, clutched at her disheveled hair, and glared at the woman.","But the woman had already snatched the girl's hair flower and was walking away. The little girl wanted it back, so she frantically shouted and chased after the woman.","Han Ye recognized her at first sight and said with disgust, \"That woman's got something wrong with her head. She goes around stealing girls' hair flowers everywhere. What's she trying to do? Steal them to wear herself, or what?\"","Qin Qiao'an immediately looked at Xiaxia's head and said, \"Let me check—good thing Xiaxia's hair flower didn't get lost. That one Mom just bought!\"","Then, his voice turning angry, Qin Qiao'an added, \"She's definitely stealing them to sell for money! She's so wicked.\"","The elastic bands and clips girls used to tie up their hair came in all sorts of styles. Some clips had beads strung on them—bright, colorful beads that were really pretty, though those were expensive.","The ordinary kind used velvet flowers tied onto the clips, either red or yellow, which also looked lovely in the hair.","Xiaxia had many of those. Some were bought by Qiao Lanshu, and others were made by Auntie Shi back in the old days.","But these velvet flowers weren't even expensive. Having lived in Wencheng for so many years, Qiao Lanshu had never seen anyone steal something like that.","Qiao Lanshu sighed and remarked, \"Sure enough, a big forest has all kinds of birds in it.\"","Qin Yuanzheng turned his head, gazing into the pitch-black alleyway. His expression gradually hardened, his brows furrowed deeply, and he said, \"Something seems... off.\"","Han Ye immediately stepped closer to him and whispered in return, \"I think so too, Uncle Qin. Should we go check it out?\"","Qin Qiao'an immediately puffed out his chest and raised his hand. \"I want to go too—take me along!\"","Qin Yuanzheng stared into the distance for a moment, then said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Sweetheart, take the kids back to the guesthouse first. Han Ye and I will go take a look.\"","By now they had already reached the entrance of the guesthouse. It was dark out, and Qin Yuanzheng didn't feel comfortable letting them stay outside.","Qiao Lanshu also felt that something about this wasn't right, but she knew she couldn't be of much help out there—the most important thing was to take care of her own kids.","So she nodded, took one child by each hand, and said to Qin Yuanzheng and Han Ye, \"You two be careful. Especially you, Han Ye—don't try to be a hero. The moment you sense anything wrong, you run, got it?\"","Han Ye was raring to go. \"Don't worry, Mom. Running away is what I do best.\"","Qin Yuanzheng watched Qiao Lanshu lead the two children through the guesthouse doors before giving Han Ye a look. The two of them headed off in the direction the woman had gone.","Qin Qiao'an, still being led along by Qiao Lanshu, was struggling and protesting. \"Mom, just let me go too! I'm grown up now—I want to catch the thief too!\"","Qiao Lanshu held onto his hand and said, \"Oh, stop it. You're not even as tall as me yet. You've got a long way to go before you're grown up. Listen to your father—let's head back and wait for them.\"","Qin Qiao'an was dragged back to the guesthouse by Qiao Lanshu, unwilling and restless.","Meanwhile, outside, Qin Yuanzheng was leading Han Ye along the dark, shadowy alleyway.","Neither of them spoke, and they both did their best to keep their footsteps quiet as they moved forward. The deeper they went, the darker it became. The homes on both sides of the alley had lanterns hanging by their doors for light, but once they went further in, they found there were no more lanterns—the alley was pitch black.","Han Ye pressed close to Qin Yuanzheng and whispered, \"What about that little girl just now? Didn't she chase her in here too? Why is she nowhere in sight?\"","That little girl was probably a local resident, out playing like she always did. She looked to be about eight or nine, and parents wouldn't usually keep such a close watch on a kid that age.","So by now, with her having run so far, no one had come looking for her yet.","Han Ye looked left and right but still couldn't find that girl. He had no idea where she'd run off to.","He muttered under his breath, \"Could I have been wrong? Maybe she never came in here?\"","Qin Yuanzheng made a shushing gesture, and the two of them pressed themselves against the wall, hidden in the shadows.","The alley was completely still. No one was walking around. All they could hear was the faint sound of voices coming from the houses nearby.","But when they tried to listen more carefully, the voices vanished.","Han Ye didn't dare move. It was his first time experiencing something like this, and his heart was pounding with excitement. He pressed close to Qin Yuanzheng, scanning their surroundings.","Qin Yuanzheng crouched down to check for footprints, but the ground here was made of bluestone slabs and it hadn't rained, so there were no traces to be found.","He paced around the alley twice, then said to Han Ye, \"Come on, let's loop around to the back.\"","The alley was home to many families, and most of the houses had both front and back doors.","Qin Yuanzheng led Han Ye around to the rear alley. They circled through the narrow lanes several times but discovered nothing at all.","Finally, even Han Ye began to doubt himself. He lowered his voice and said, \"Uncle Qin, could we have been mistaken? Maybe that little girl lives right here and just went home?\"","Qin Yuanzheng stepped out of the alley and looked around. Then he pointed at a building and said, \"There's a hotel over there. I'm going to book a room. You go back to the guesthouse and let Aunt Qiao know. I'll be keeping watch from here tonight, so I won't be coming back. You all get some rest early.\"","The moment Han Ye heard that, he perked up, full of energy. \"Uncle Qin, I want to keep watch with you! Is that okay?\"","Qin Yuanzheng glanced at Han Ye. The boy was fourteen now, tall and sturdy, a young man full of passion. It wouldn't hurt to give him some real experience.","He nodded. \"Fine. Go back and tell them first, then come back. Be quick about it.\"","Han Ye immediately stood up straight and whispered, \"Got it!\"","With that, Han Ye hurried off.","He ran out of the alley and down the street until he reached the entrance of the guesthouse. It was a busy area with lots of guests and street vendors lining the road, their cries of trade filling the air with lively noise.","Before going inside, Han Ye paused to listen for a moment, but he didn't hear anyone calling for a missing child. Frowning, he dashed into the guesthouse.","Meanwhile, Qin Yuanzheng strode over to the five-story building. It was a hotel run by a private owner, seemingly built only a few years ago, so it looked quite new.","From the third floor of this hotel, one could clearly see the front and back entrances of those two alleys.","Qin Yuanzheng had already scoped out the angle, so he went straight in and booked a room on the third floor.","After getting the room key, he told the front desk clerk, \"My son will be coming to find me in a bit. Could you tell him my room number? He's about my height, fourteen or fifteen years old, wearing a black jacket.\"","The clerk nodded. \"Sure thing, comrade. I'll bring him up to you when he arrives.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded, took his key, and went upstairs. He stepped into the room, pulled open the curtains, and looked out at the two alleys under the streetlights and moonlight.","...","Han Ye rushed back to the guesthouse and dashed up to the second floor to the door of Qiao Lanshu's room. He knocked urgently.","When Qin Qiao'an opened the door, Han Ye ran inside and found Qiao Lanshu. \"Mom, Uncle Qin said he's going to keep watch from the hotel across the street tonight, so he won't be coming back. You all should get some rest.\"","Then he turned and bolted for the door.","Qiao Lanshu quickly called out, \"Wait a second.\"","Han Ye slammed on the brakes, nearly crashing into the doorframe. He turned around, breathing hard. \"What? Something else?\"","Qiao Lanshu asked quietly, \"What's going on? What are you watching?\"","Han Ye gave her the short version: \"Uncle Qin thinks something's off in those two alleys, so he booked a room at the hotel across the street to keep watch from up there. I need to go now too. He can't do it alone — I can be his backup.\"","With that, Han Ye headed for the door, but then he stopped and turned back, lowering his voice. \"Mom, you all stay in the guesthouse. Don't go anywhere, got it? It's dangerous out there!\"","Qiao Lanshu had already guessed that tonight's incident might have something to do with human traffickers.","Han Ye had nearly been snatched by traffickers when he was little. He still remembered it vividly, and he hated those people with every fiber of his being.","Qiao Lanshu only reminded him, \"You two be careful. If things get tough, don't be reckless. Go to the police station and let them handle it. When you went to the school this afternoon, did you notice the police station? It's just two streets away from here. You remember?\"","Han Ye nodded. \"I remember, of course I do. Don't worry about me. I'm off now.\"","And with that, he ran out.","Qin Qiao'an saw his big brother about to go catch bad guys without him and got anxious. He chased after him. \"Brother! Brother! Wait for me! I want to come catch the bad guys too!\"","Han Ye ran a few steps, heard his call, and turned back. He pushed Qin Qiao'an back and said sternly, \"No, you can't. You have to stay here and protect Mom and your little sister. When Uncle Qin and I aren't around, that important duty falls on you. Can you handle it?\"","Qin Qiao'an: \"...\"","Suddenly, Qin Qiao'an felt the weight of an enormous responsibility on his shoulders!","He stood up straight and declared, \"You bet I can!\"","Han Ye patted him on the shoulder. \"Good brother. I believe in you.\"","Then Han Ye turned and sprinted off.","Qin Qiao'an watched his back, wishing he could chase after him too.","But he remembered he had to protect Mom and his little sister, so he ran back inside. He closed the door and locked it, then said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Mom, you and sister get some rest. I'll guard the door.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu shook her head, a knot of worry forming in her chest.","She walked to the window and pulled the curtain aside, looking out at the street.","From her angle, she could only see the bustling street outside. The stretch of alleys in the distance was too far to make out clearly.","She felt uneasy about Qin Yuanzheng, but he was always cautious. Dealing with a few traffickers shouldn't be a problem, right?","The three of them stayed up worrying about the two men, too anxious to sleep.","Qiao Lanshu got her son and daughter washed up and fed, then had them read books while she stood by the window, glancing out from time to time.","..."]},{"number":256,"title":"Chapter 256: Catching Human Traffickers","paragraphs":["When Han Ye arrived on the third floor of the hotel, the room was pitch dark with no lights on.","He quietly closed the door behind him and walked over to Qin Yuanzheng’s side. Together, they looked out the window. “Uncle, do you see anything?” Han Ye whispered.","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head. “Not yet.”","But if his guess was right, the other party would soon make a move.","The two stood silently by the bed, watching for more than half an hour.","At that moment, Qin Yuanzheng noticed a car slowly driving to the entrance of an alley.","Han Ye whispered, “Uncle, look at that car!”","Qin Yuanzheng made a shushing gesture. The sky was dark, and the license plate was hard to make out, but there weren’t many cars around at this hour, so recognizing it wouldn’t be difficult.","A back door in the alley opened. In the pitch-black night, a woman opened the gate, and then a man carried a woman out. He placed her inside the car. Immediately after, he went back inside and carried out a girl about eight or nine years old, placing her in the back seat.","They were too far away to clearly see if the girl was the same one who had been chasing the woman earlier that evening.","From a distance, her clothes didn’t seem quite right either.","Han Ye hesitated. “Uncle, should we make a move now?”","Qin Yuanzheng’s face darkened. He gave Han Ye a meaningful look and said, “Let’s go.”","Han Ye instantly became excited.","Since childhood, he had dreamed of becoming a soldier, just like Uncle Qin and Han Wenlin—traveling everywhere on missions to uphold justice.","He especially hated human traffickers and wanted to see them all captured and executed!","Rubbing his hands together, he said, “Don’t worry, Uncle Qin. I’ll do my best when the time comes.”","Qin Yuanzheng said nothing but quickly led him out.","They hurried downstairs and ran out of the hotel.","The street was still lively at this hour. Many elderly men and women hadn’t gone home yet; they sat outside their doors, fanning themselves and chatting.","Qin Yuanzheng turned to Han Ye and asked, “Do you know where the police station is?”","Han Ye nodded. “Yes.”","He thought to himself, Uncle Qin and Aunt Qiao really are a perfect couple—their questions were exactly the same.","Then he heard Qin Yuanzheng say, “You need to go to the police station right now and report this. Tell them to block the highway and send officers here to make the arrest. Speed is crucial.”","Han Ye was stunned. “???”","He was confused. “Uncle Qin, didn’t you want me to come with you to catch the bad guys? I’m pretty good at this—I won’t hold you back.”","Qin Yuanzheng shot him a sharp glare. “No nonsense. Follow orders!”","Han Ye immediately stood up straight. “Understood!”","Then he turned and sprinted toward the police station.","Qin Yuanzheng walked briskly to the opposite side of the alley and peered inside.","The car was still parked at the alley entrance, its side facing inward. From his vantage point, he couldn’t see what was happening inside or how many people were in the vehicle.","The car hadn’t started yet, which meant they were still preparing to leave.","Qin Yuanzheng thought for two seconds, then pulled a folding knife from his pocket. He crept along the wall toward a car, crouched down, and stabbed the blade hard into one of the rear tires.","He put all his strength into it, making sure the tire was punctured before retracting the knife.","Just as he was about to stab the second tire—","He heard voices coming from the alley entrance.","A man was complaining, “I told you, I want young and pretty girls. Look at what you’ve found—either women in their thirties or forties, or little girls barely seven or eight years old. None of these meet the requirements.”","A woman’s sharp, bitter voice responded quietly, “It’s easy for you to say. Do you think young, beautiful women just fall from the sky or grow out of the ground? Girls at that age are the most cautious. They’re either working or studying, many already have boyfriends. I’m the only one who can’t take action.”","Her voice paused before she added, “Besides, these women in their thirties may be a bit older, but age has its advantages. They’ve already given birth, which proves they’re fertile. Those men who can’t find wives just want to buy women to carry on the family line, right?”","“And as for the eight or nine-year-old girls, their price isn’t low at all. Raise them for two or three years, and they can be brides—still pure young girls. Isn’t that perfect?”","Qin Yuanzheng was dressed all in black today. Calmly, he stabbed the second tire as well, then crouched in the shadows by the wall, listening to their conversation.","He still didn’t dare to act rashly. After all, aside from his folding knife, he had no other weapons.","And these days, many people carried guns.","Especially these desperate criminals trafficking women and children—they likely had plenty of weapons and manpower.","Qin Yuanzheng remained silent, leaning against a small pile of bricks by the wall to conceal himself.","Inside, the voices continued. The man spoke angrily, “I said this is a special shipment. The people over there are opening a dance hall and need young dancers. They’re paying more than ever before.”","The woman scoffed, “What dance hall? Never heard of it. Anyway, I can’t get any girls aged eighteen or nineteen—there aren’t many on this street.”","As they talked, another man spoke in a low voice, “Alright, alright, stop arguing. Hurry up before someone finds out.”","The woman said smugly, “Don’t worry. I only make my move after careful observation. These girls aren’t from around here or have families who care about them. No one will notice for a while.”","The man asked, “Are there any more? Just these three?”","Another man replied, “Just three. Damn it—two women in their thirties and forties, and one eight or nine-year-old girl. This batch won’t sell well. We’ll have to take them up into the mountains.”","The first man was clearly unhappy, “Originally, we just needed to deliver them to the dance hall. Now we have to leave the province and go into the mountains. This trip’s really not worth it.”","The woman had already disappeared down the alley, and Qin Yuanzheng couldn’t quite make out what she was saying—only faint murmurs, as if she was cursing someone under her breath.","At this point, it seemed there were only three of them here: two men and one woman. Inside the car were two other women and a girl.","These two men were probably in charge of finding buyers, while the woman here was responsible for scouting targets, then finding a way to lure the women over, capture them, and under the cover of night, drug them and send them off.","Over the years, Qin Yuanzheng had carried out countless missions and encountered all sorts of villains and monsters.","He had seen human traffickers before, but back then, with strict household registration controls, you needed a letter of introduction wherever you went. Such incidents existed but were relatively rare.","Now, several years into the reform and opening-up, with the country’s economy booming, the number of villains had increased.","Even human traffickers had become so brazen!","Listening to their conversation, Qin Yuanzheng realized they were about to leave.","His expression grew serious. Han Ye—he wondered if he had already reached the police station. Why hadn’t the officers shown up yet?","Hesitating for a moment, Qin Yuanzheng quietly rose and circled to the mouth of the opposite alley, crouching again by the wall. Both tires of their car had been slashed; they wouldn’t be going anywhere anytime soon.","Sure enough, as soon as the two men got into the car, they sensed something was wrong. One of them got out to check and then muttered in confusion, “What’s going on with the car? The tires are flat.”","The other man also stepped down and walked to the back to inspect the tires. When they saw both were completely deflated, anger flared up immediately. “Damn it! Who the hell slashed my tires? They were fine when we got here.”","They muttered as they circled the car, scanning the surroundings. Qin Yuanzheng remained motionless in the darkness, unnoticed by their sweeping gaze.","“There are a lot of kids around here. Maybe it’s some prank—needles or something.”","“That’s impossible. If it were kids playing tricks, we would have noticed earlier. Maybe we ran over some nails on the way here?”","The two men discussed quietly and inspected the area again. It was pitch dark, and no one had passed the alley entrance.","But they were clearly nervous, behaving like guilty thieves. They lowered their voices, exchanged glances, and one slowly slipped his hand into his pocket. The other opened the car door and dragged the unconscious woman out. Realizing they couldn’t leave, they feared lingering too long would attract attention, and they worried the three women might wake up.","So they decided to move the three back to a house inside the alley.","If their place had a tunnel or secret room, it would be hard to find them.","They couldn’t let them get away.","But the man assigned to keep watch obviously had a gun.","His hand was in his pocket, as if gripping something. Qin Yuanzheng didn’t hesitate. After locking eyes with him a few times, as the other man carried the woman away, Qin Yuanzheng suddenly charged at the lookout.","The man was startled and hastily pulled a gun out of his pocket. Unfortunately, he was half a step too slow. In the darkness, Qin Yuanzheng pressed down on the man’s arm with one hand and twisted his wrist hard, instantly disarming him. Then, he delivered an elbow strike to the man’s stomach, followed by a knife strike to the back of his neck.","The man clutched his stomach and collapsed to the ground in pain.","Another man was carrying a woman as he just entered the alley. Hearing the commotion, he immediately shouted, “Who’s there? What’s going on?”","Panicked, he threw the woman he was carrying onto the ground, then pulled a gun from his pocket and fired two wild shots toward the entrance of the alley.","At the alley’s mouth, a middle-aged woman heard the gunfire and rushed out shouting, “Idiot, stop shooting! Run!”","Then she hurried back inside the house and quickly slipped out the back door to escape.","The man who fired the shots was also losing his composure. After two rounds, worried that the gunfire would attract others, he turned and started running away.","Qin Yuanzheng guessed there were probably only three people here.","One had already been dealt with, so the other two couldn’t be allowed to escape.","If they got away and raised the alarm, both their superiors and subordinates would likely flee, making it much harder to catch them.","Without hesitation, Qin Yuanzheng quickly gave chase and fired a shot at the fleeing man in the darkness.","Despite the poor visibility and distance, he still managed to hit the man’s leg with a single bullet. The man screamed in agony and fell to the ground, then wildly fired his gun in all directions.","Soon, he ran out of bullets. He struggled to get up and limped off, trying to escape.","Qin Yuanzheng didn’t know if there were ambushes inside the house or if the woman might be hiding with a gun in the shadows.","Pressing his back against the wall, Qin Yuanzheng fired another shot at the man’s other leg.","Both legs were hit. The man wailed in pain, lying on the ground, unable to crawl away.","Confident that the man wouldn’t be able to run anytime soon, Qin Yuanzheng left the alley entrance and took a detour, intending to pursue the woman.","Just then, the police officers finally arrived. Qin Yuanzheng heard Han Ye’s voice, but he didn’t stop where he was. Instead, he circled around to a back alley and chased forward for a bit.","However, in the pitch-black maze of alleys, he lost track of the fleeing woman.","There were too many narrow lanes and no streetlights. If she was determined to escape, Qin Yuanzheng found it difficult to follow.","He chased for several minutes in the darkness, passing two more alleys and emerging onto a main street, but still saw no sign of her. Worried that she might be armed, he realized pursuing her recklessly in the dark would be too dangerous.","After a moment’s thought, he decided to circle back and regroup with the police officers who had just arrived.","This time, six officers were present, with Han Ye leading at the front.","Han Ye ran while urging, “Come on, hurry up! Don’t let them get away!”","The Deputy Public Security Bureau Chief was accompanied by five young and robust officers, all of whom had recently transferred from the military. They kept themselves in good physical shape and were quite fast runners.","Yet, despite this, they nearly failed to catch up with Han Ye.","Each of them was surprised, silently thinking to themselves that this young man was truly a promising talent. His speed was almost on par with the military dogs they had served with.","Han Ye sprinted toward the alley entrance, and from a distance, he saw the tall figure of Qin Yuanzheng standing beside a car, holding two guns in his hands.","Those guns had been confiscated from the two men. After thoroughly searching them and finding no other weapons, Qin Yuanzheng had come to the roadside.","Han Ye hurried over, breathless: \"Uncle Qin, how’s it going? Have they caught the traffickers?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded and said to the officers who had just arrived, \"There were two men and one woman involved in the trafficking. The woman got away—send people to chase her down. As for these two men, bring them in for overnight interrogation to see if they have any accomplices. The three abductees are all here; go check on them. Also, make sure to conduct a thorough search of that house.\"","The Deputy Chief was busy assigning tasks while approaching Qin Yuanzheng to get a briefing on the situation.","Qin Yuanzheng handed over the two confiscated guns to him.","Han Ye stomped his foot in frustration. \"That woman got away? She’s the worst one. She even targeted Xiaxia before.\"","Qin Yuanzheng recalled how Xiaxia’s hairpin had nearly been taken and felt a chill of fear.","He asked the Deputy Chief standing nearby, \"Has anyone reported missing family members tonight? Three people—no one noticed they were gone?\"","The Deputy Chief shook his head. \"No, if anyone had, we would have been out looking for them already.\""]},{"number":257,"title":"Chapter 257: Preparing to Return to the City","paragraphs":["It had to be said, these human traffickers really knew how to pick their victims. A whole night had passed, and none of the families of the victims had come to report them missing.","Qin Yuanzheng and Han Ye cooperated with the police comrades in the investigation and taking statements, so they were busy the entire night and didn't return to the guesthouse.","Fortunately, they had already informed Qiao Lanshu beforehand, telling her not to wait up and to rest first.","The next day at around six in the morning, Qin Yuanzheng brought Han Ye out of the police station.","This time, they had caught two male human traffickers, one female suspect had escaped, and three trafficked women were rescued.","The police station said they wanted to commend Qin Yuanzheng and Han Ye, father and son.","Qin Yuanzheng declined, but he still asked the police station to send a letter of commendation to Han Ye's school.","In the future, Han Ye would be joining the military, and this kind of merit would be very helpful to him.","Han Ye followed Qin Yuanzheng to a steamed bun stall and asked in a low voice, \"Uncle Qin, does this count as me performing a meritorious deed? Will it be useful for me when I join the army later?\"","Having participated in a mission to catch bad guys for the first time, Han Ye was still a bit excited. He even fantasized that this merit could get him a platoon leader position as soon as he entered the army.","Qin Yuanzheng looked at his smug expression and said seriously, \"It's not useful.\"","Han Ye: \"...\"","The smile on Han Ye's face froze a little. He asked Qin Yuanzheng, \"Why? I've made a great contribution here!\"","Qin Yuanzheng said to him, \"If you were already in the army right now, this would indeed be very useful. But since you're at least four years away from joining the military, this isn't very useful. At most, the school will hold a general assembly to praise you and give you a few yuan as a bonus.\"","Han Ye: \"...\"","Han Ye instantly deflated.","For other students, maybe a bonus of a few yuan was quite a lot.","But for him, his monthly allowance was already a few dozen yuan, so a bonus of a few yuan didn't mean much to him.","Qin Yuanzheng bought ten steamed buns, five with cabbage filling and five with meat filling, and then he and Han Ye each munched on a meat bun as they walked back to the guesthouse.","After being busy the whole night, both of them were starving, so they each finished two big buns on the way.","...","The night before, Qiao Lanshu had been worried about Qin Yuanzheng and Han Ye, so she barely slept either.","She had heard the gunfire outside last night, and her heart was so tense!","She really wanted to go out and see what was happening, but she was afraid of causing trouble for Qin Yuanzheng. She was also worried about the two children in the room, so she forced herself to stay inside.","In the middle of the night, when she heard that there was no more noise outside, she relaxed a little, but she still couldn't fall asleep.","The two children were also on edge because of her, but they were still young and couldn't stay awake. They fell asleep in the middle of the night.","Qiao Lanshu sat at the table reading a book, making it to around six-thirty in the morning until she finally heard Qin Yuanzheng knocking on the door.","Qiao Lanshu hurried over to open the door. Qin Yuanzheng and Han Ye were standing outside, holding steamed buns in their hands.","Qin Yuanzheng glanced inside the room and asked in a low voice, \"Are the children still asleep?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded.","Then, Qiao Lanshu came out of the room and went into Qin Yuanzheng's room next door.","Qin Yuanzheng and Han Ye followed her in, and Qiao Lanshu couldn't wait to ask, \"What happened last night? Were the traffickers caught?\"","Han Ye was someone who couldn't hold back his words, and he immediately started babbling to Qiao Lanshu, \"Mom, you don't know how dangerous it was last night! Uncle Qin and I were watching from the third-floor window of the hotel, and then, we saw a car...\"","Han Ye gestured wildly, describing it as extremely thrilling, leaving Qiao Lanshu stunned.","But fortunately, Qiao Lanshu could tell from what he said that he wasn't in any danger, so she said, \"You did very well. You were very brave. When we get back this time, I'll make sure Director Han gives you a proper commendation.\"","Han Ye puffed out his chest and said smugly, \"It's a pity that Uncle Qin later told me to go call the police. I didn't even get to show off my skills. Otherwise, I could have done even better!\"","Qin Yuanzheng glanced at him. \"Don't go doing anything reckless. Don't think this kind of thing is easy. Last night, those two people were carrying guns. You're just a teenager, unarmed, and you think you could have fought them?\"","Qin Yuanzheng had never planned to let Han Ye actually take part in the action. He was just bringing him along for some experience.","Han Ye also knew those people had guns. He said, \"So what if they had guns? They were still captured by Uncle Qin.\"","Hearing them talk like this, Qiao Lanshu felt very worried. She asked Qin Yuanzheng, \"Did you get hurt?\"","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head. \"Don't worry, I'm fine.\"","Looking at Qiao Lanshu's dark circles and tired complexion, he said in a low voice, \"Did you not sleep last night? Are you tired?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"How could I sleep when you two weren't back yet?\"","Qin Yuanzheng's heart ached for his wife. She had been worried about him all night and must be really exhausted.","But there was nothing he could do. Anyone who encountered a situation like that couldn't just stand by and do nothing.","He reached out and rubbed Qiao Lanshu's head, then turned to look at Han Ye and asked, \"Why are you still here?\"","Han Ye: \"???\"","Han Ye was eating a bun, his cheeks puffed out, and looked confused as he said, \"Huh? If I'm not here, where should I go?\"","Qin Yuanzheng felt that Han Ye was clearly a smart person, but sometimes he could be a bit oblivious and not read the room.","He said, \"Go sleep next door. Your Aunt Qiao and I also need to rest.\"","Han Ye: \"...\"","Han Ye hadn't finished bragging yet. He still wanted Qiao Lanshu to praise him a little more, but Qin Yuanzheng was already rushing him out.","With a bun stuffed in his mouth, Han Ye reluctantly walked out of the room and had no choice but to go back to the room next door.","Next door, Qin Qiao'an and Qin Qiaoxia were sleeping on the same bed. Both children had only fallen asleep in the middle of the night, and they were sound asleep now. Even when he opened and closed the door, it didn't wake them.","Han Ye finished the bun in his hand, then went to wash up and got into bed as well.","Today, the family was planning to visit Tiananmen, so while it was still early, they should get some sleep to recharge!","Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu also planned to take a nap.","Neither of them had slept all night. Qin Yuanzheng could handle a night without sleep, but Qiao Lanshu was already dead tired.","Qin Yuanzheng felt bad for her, so he held her in his arms as they went to bed together.","With his soft and fragrant wife in his arms, Qin Yuanzheng also felt a bit weary, so he fell asleep holding Qiao Lanshu.","They slept from seven all the way until ten in the morning.","They were awakened by the guesthouse staff knocking on the door.","Qin Yuanzheng was the first to be woken up, and then Qiao Lanshu also woke up.","As the two of them were getting up and getting dressed, they heard the sound of a door opening in the next room.","Then came the sound of Han Ye's voice.","Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng exchanged a glance, and both quickly stood up. Qin Yuanzheng opened the door and looked out, seeing three or four people standing in the hallway outside: one was the front desk woman from the guesthouse, two were male comrades in police uniforms, and one was a thin, gray-haired woman wearing glasses.","They heard the sound of the door opening, turned around, and the two police officers recognized Qin Yuanzheng. They immediately came over to greet him: \"Comrade Qin, sorry to disturb you. This is Professor Rong Ji from Capital Normal University. She came specifically to thank you.\"","As soon as Qin Yuanzheng heard this, he instinctively glanced back at Qiao Lanshu.","A professor from Capital Normal University?","Qiao Lanshu had graduated from Wencheng Normal University, so the two of them would likely have plenty in common.","Qiao Lanshu was startled by this news as well!","Professor Rong Ji—could it be the same Rong Ji she knew of?","Professor Rong, who studied modern Chinese, wasn't just a university professor; she was also a contemporary poet. Qiao Lanshu had bought several of her poetry collections, and they were still sitting on the bookshelf in her room.","Qiao Lanshu mulled this over in her mind, but didn't dare to ask anything, nor did she dare to stare at Professor Rong Ji's face directly, since that would be quite rude.","When Professor Rong Ji saw Qin Yuanzheng, she immediately walked over, extended her hand to shake his, and said to him: \"Comrade, last night you saved three young women who were nearly trafficked, and one of them was a nine-year-old girl, right?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded, roughly understanding what was going on.","Sure enough, he then heard Professor Rong Ji say: \"That little girl is my granddaughter. She was on holiday these past few days, visiting her grandmother's house. Everyone at that house was busy and no one noticed she had run out to play, and was taken by those people. If you hadn't spotted it in time, she might already have been sent away by now... I only received the news this morning, learning that she had almost been abducted. I thank my lucky stars...\"","As she said this, a trace of lingering fear mixed with relief showed on her face.","She thought to herself that her granddaughter had been fortunate, for otherwise...","When Qin Yuanzheng heard this, he quickly said: \"Professor Rong, there's no need for you to be so polite. This is just what we should do. You didn't have to come all this way to thank me.\"","A nine-year-old girl had been missing for an entire night, and no one had even filed a police report.","When the police contacted the family the next day, it wasn't the parents or the paternal grandmother's family who came, but the maternal grandmother.","This suggested there were likely some hidden family conflicts.","Still, Qin Yuanzheng wasn't interested in other people's domestic affairs.","Judging by Professor Rong Ji's attitude, she clearly cared deeply for her granddaughter.","Fortunately, this little girl had a grandmother who cherished her.","Qin Yuanzheng shook her hand and added: \"That said, there are a lot of traffickers around lately, and the city is crowded and chaotic. Since there are children in the family, you really should be extra careful and keep a close eye on them.\"","Upon hearing this, Professor Rong Ji's expression, which had been fairly calm, betrayed a faint trace of irritation.","Of course, that irritation wasn't directed at Qin Yuanzheng, but at her in-laws.","She quickly composed herself; she couldn't very well criticize her in-laws in front of outsiders. Dirty linen shouldn't be aired in public, and bringing it up would cast a bad light on both families.","Professor Rong Ji simply nodded and said: \"You're right. This was also my negligence. My daughter is abroad on academic exchange, and her daughter nearly got kidnapped. That was my fault, and it won't happen again. I'll arrange for someone to look after the child exclusively.\"","From the fact that she was telling all this to Qin Yuanzheng, it was clear that Professor Rong Ji had truly been shaken this time. She was probably still angry, anxious, and carrying no small amount of resentment.","The two chatted for a while, with Professor Rong Ji expressing her thanks many times over and even asking about Qin Yuanzheng's workplace, saying she wanted to write him a letter of commendation.","Naturally, Qin Yuanzheng couldn't casually reveal his workplace.","If he were talking to an ordinary person, Qin Yuanzheng would simply have said he had no work unit or something of that sort.","But Professor Rong Ji asked in all sincerity, and he didn't feel right brushing her off with a flimsy excuse.","So he said: \"My unit has a confidentiality agreement, so I can't disclose it freely. Professor Rong, please don't concern yourself with it. Anyone who discovered what happened would not have stood by and done nothing.\"","As soon as she heard this, Professor Rong Ji seemed to understand somewhat. She then asked: \"And what's your name? Where are you from?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"My name is Qin Yuanzheng, from Longcheng.\"","Professor Rong Ji nodded slowly: \"Qin Yuanzheng? That's a fine name. And this, is this your wife?\"","Qiao Lanshu had been standing quietly beside Qin Yuanzheng the whole time, not daring to speak carelessly.","After all, the woman before them was a professor!","Qiao Lanshu's dream was to become a university professor, so her three-year plan was to pass the postgraduate entrance exam and then stay on as faculty at her university.","Qin Yuanzheng introduced his wife to Professor Rong Ji: \"Yes, this is my wife. Her name is Qiao Lanshu. She graduated from Wencheng Normal University and currently teaches at Wencheng Middle School.\"","Sure enough, upon hearing this, Professor Rong Ji's eyes lit up slightly as she looked at Qiao Lanshu. She then took a moment to chat with Qiao Lanshu specifically, asking about her school and her work.","Then, suddenly, she said: \"You're a high school teacher, and you're here in the capital at this time—are you here for the training program?\"","Qiao Lanshu was a bit surprised: \"Yes, Professor Rong, you know about it too?\"","Professor Rong Ji smiled at her: \"Of course I know. Our school received the notice as well.\"","What she didn't mention was that she was one of the lead lecturers for this national teacher training program.","She chatted with Qiao Lanshu for a while, and found herself quite impressed with her, thinking that if Qiao Lanshu performed excellently in the assessments after the six-month training, she might take her on as her own student.","Professor Rong Ji didn't stay for long. Before leaving, she thanked Qin Yuanzheng once more, and then departed.","After she was gone, Han Ye and Qin Qiao'an, who had been standing nearby watching the whole time, finally let out a long sigh of relief.","Han Ye clutched his chest and exclaimed dramatically: \"Good heavens, middle school teachers were already scary enough — I didn't think a university professor would be even more terrifying. The way her eyes swept over us, every hair on my body stood on end.\"","Qin Qiao'an chimed in: \"Yeah, yeah, she looks so stern. Her granddaughter probably isn't much fun to be around either, right?\"","The previous night, they had only seen the girl chase after that woman after her hair clip was snatched.","They hadn't actually gotten a good look at the girl's face.","But now, seeing that she had such a stern, rigid grandmother, they figured the girl was probably a little stick-in-the-mud too.","After that episode, the family became even more careful when going out.","Qin Yuanzheng took them around the capital city to sightsee, and on the fifth day, Qiao Lanshu had to officially report in and begin her classes.","Qin Yuanzheng then took the three children aboard the train back to Wencheng.","..."]},{"number":258,"title":"Chapter 258: Chief Qin Misses His Wife","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu's time studying in the capital was extremely fulfilling. Here, she met many like-minded teacher friends and learned a lot of more profound knowledge.","At the same time, she also got to know many respected scholars and professors.","Professor Rong Ji was one of the main lecturers during their study period. Qiao Lanshu didn't know this in advance. It was only after the official start of the courses and when she received the list of tutors that she found out it was her.","Professor Rong Ji highly appreciated Qiao Lanshu and intended to give her more guidance. Therefore, during this six - month study period, Qiao Lanshu's schoolwork was much heavier than others.","Professor Rong Ji always liked to assign extra projects and tasks to her, keeping her extremely busy.","Qin Yuanzheng wrote to her every week. Yes, he wrote letters every single week, four letters a month, without fail.","Qin Yuanzheng kept a close eye on her, fearing that she might be lured away by other men during this study period.","However, Qiao Lanshu was too busy and sometimes couldn't find time to reply. When Qin Yuanzheng didn't receive her reply, he would immediately call her from the military camp to the school.","Even Professor Rong Ji knew about this. Once in the office, when Qiao Lanshu came to hand in her thesis, she said to her with a smile, \"I really didn't expect that your husband is so clingy. I thought he was a tough guy who didn't care about trivial matters.\"","Qiao Lanshu felt a bit embarrassed and said, \"Maybe the kids at home are too naughty and he's too busy with work to manage them all alone.\"","Professor Rong Ji knew that Qiao Lanshu had three children, and one of them was an adopted son.","She then said with a smile, \"Your adopted son is quite good. I think he can share some of the burden with your husband.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded and said, \"Han Ye is very sensible. He's older, and his younger brothers are very attached to him.\"","Professor Rong Ji lowered her head and flipped through Qiao Lanshu's thesis.","In this era, it was not like later times when there were computers, mobile phones, and various office software. People could write their theses on computers.","At that time, theses were all written by hand, and even the format of the thesis cover was drawn stroke by stroke. So everyone had to practice calligraphy, and the writing must be regular, neat, clean, tidy, and beautiful.","The content inside also had to be substantial, and all kinds of tables also had to be drawn by hand.","Qiao Lanshu's thesis was beautifully written, and her handwriting was delicate and elegant, pleasing to the eye.","Professor Rong Ji flipped through the pages one by one. After reading a few pages, she put down the thesis and asked Qiao Lanshu, \"There's only about a month left in our study period. Do you have any plans?\"","Hearing Professor Rong Ji's question, Qiao Lanshu felt a faint excitement in her heart.","There were nearly a hundred young teachers who came here to study this time. Among them, there were many outstanding ones, and some had been secretly selected as students by their tutors during the study.","Qiao Lanshu was also among the top ten excellent students. However, no professor had invited her all this time because Professor Rong Ji had always valued her, and others were too embarrassed to snatch students from Professor Rong Ji.","Before Qiao Lanshu could say a word, as expected, she heard Professor Rong Ji say, \"I wonder what your future plan is? Have you ever thought about furthering your studies and taking the postgraduate entrance examination? Coincidentally, I still have a quota here. If you want to study, I can reserve it for you.\"","Qiao Lanshu's heart started pounding with excitement. She quickly nodded and said, \"I've thought about it, Professor Rong! I thought before that I would teach for three years first and then prepare for the postgraduate entrance examination. It's just that I may not be able to come to the capital. I can only apply for a school in Wencheng.\"","Although it would be great to come to the capital, Qin Yuanzheng had only been transferred to the Wencheng Military Sub - district for three years, and he probably wouldn't be transferred in the next few years.","If she went to the capital to study, the whole family would have to be separated.","They had only been apart for half a year, and Qin Yuanzheng was writing four letters a day and making calls from time to time. The kids were also constantly complaining that they missed her.","If she came here to study for a few years, what would happen to her kids and husband at home?","In the past, she would never have dared to imagine that she could have Professor Rong Ji as her tutor. But now, the opportunity was right in front of her, yet she could only give it up.","Hearing this, there was a look of regret in Professor Rong Ji's eyes. She really liked Qiao Lanshu. This student seemed very smart and easy to teach.","However, Professor Rong Ji quickly said, \"Then you can consider Wencheng University. The president of Wencheng University is my classmate. I heard that he is also taking on students now. I can write a recommendation letter for you and send it to him.\"","Qiao Lanshu said excitedly, \"Thank you, Professor Rong.\"","Professor Rong Ji then said with a smile, \"He invited me to be a visiting professor at Wencheng University before, and I refused. However, next year, I can consider accepting his invitation. You should prepare well for the exam. It's actually not difficult. With your strength, you will definitely pass. Review hard this year. I'm looking forward to your good news next year.\"","Qiao Lanshu thanked her again and again.","It had to be said that getting to know Professor Rong Ji was truly a stroke of luck for her.","Professor Rong Ji was a well - known scholar across the country. If she went to be a visiting professor at Wencheng University, it would probably cause a stir among the three universities in Wencheng.","Visiting professors also participated in training and guiding students. By then, Qiao Lanshu would definitely be able to choose her as her tutor.","Thinking of this, Qiao Lanshu was immediately full of motivation. She went back and stayed up late reading books and working on projects. She didn't go to bed until midnight.","Then, she forgot to pick up the letters at the school gatekeeper's room again. Naturally, she didn't reply to Qin Yuanzheng.","...","Since Qiao Lanshu went to the capital to study, Qin Yuanzheng had been smiling less.","He always had a straight face in his office. The entire military sub - district was on tenterhooks, thinking that something bad had happened to Chief Qin's family and that was why he was so serious.","One day, Guan Wenjun came to Wencheng on business and dropped by to see Qin Yuanzheng.","He couldn't enter the military camp, so he had to call Qin Yuanzheng out. The two of them went to a restaurant for a meal.","Over the years, Guan Wenjun had become the father of two children. His personality had matured a lot, but he still looked like a pretty boy on the outside.","He was wearing a white shirt and sunglasses. Sitting across from Qin Yuanzheng, he shoveled food into his mouth frantically and said, \"Eat, eat quickly. The food is getting cold. Aren't you hungry?\"","Qin Yuanzheng was in his military uniform, sitting across from him. He only took a few simple bites and then put down his chopsticks. Looking at Guan Wenjun's wolf - like eating appearance, he frowned slightly and said, \"How many days haven't you eaten? Is it really necessary?\"","Guan Wenjun said while eating, \"You know what? I really haven't eaten for two days. I've been running around in Wencheng for business these two days. I'm almost exhausted.\"","Qin Yuanzheng ignored Guan Wenjun. He missed his wife. He hadn't seen her for months and couldn't sleep well at night. He missed his wife so much that he just couldn't fall asleep.","But his wife was so heartless. She often forgot to reply to his letters.","It had been half a month, and she had forgotten to write to him again!","After Guan Wenjun finished eating, he suddenly said, \"By the way, Lao Qin, will you go to Yangcheng at the end of this year?\"","Qin Yuanzheng was silent for a few seconds and then said, \"I have to stay at the military sub - district this year. It'll probably be another two years.\"","Even though he is the commander of the military sub - district, he doesn't have much freedom in terms of time. The main problem is that it's too far to go back to Yangcheng. It takes a lot of time. Each trip to Yangcheng takes at least half a month, so it's not easy to ask for leave.","Qin Yuanzheng looked at him and asked, \"What, are you going back for a family visit at the end of the year?\"","Qin Yuanzheng was a bit curious and said, \"I thought Zhong Mei never goes back to her natal family?\"","Guan Wenjun was holding a teacup and drinking tea. Then he said, \"For the sake of her younger sisters, she said she wants to go back quietly and take her two younger sisters away.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Hearing this, Qin Yuanzheng immediately fell silent. Since it involved the other person's family affairs, he didn't think it was appropriate to make any comments.","Guan Wenjun said with a worried face, \"I don't want to go to Yangcheng.\"","Qin Yuanzheng gave him a sidelong glance and seriously told him, \"They are your wife's younger sisters. You should help. Even if you don't have contact with her natal family, her sisters are innocent. You should give them a hand if you can.\"","Guan Wenjun put the water cup on the table and said angrily, \"I'm still in a cold war with her. If she doesn't apologize to me, I won't go to Yangcheng with her.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu have been married for so many years. Not to mention having a cold war, if Qiao Lanshu just gave him a glare, he would be anxious, afraid that his wife would ignore him.","How dare he show a bad temper to Comrade Xiao Qiao?","Even if Qiao Lanshu was wrong, Qin Yuanzheng would still go up and coax her. He really couldn't understand how a couple could quarrel with each other.","So, he curiously asked, \"What's wrong with you and Zhong Mei? Weren't you getting along well before? Why did you have a quarrel?\"","Guan Wenjun had been holding it in for a long time. Now that he finally had someone to talk to, he started to pour out his grievances. \"It's all because of her. You know she quit her job before, right? She said she wanted to do business. After researching for several months, she said she wanted to open a grocery store or something. In the past two months, she has been busy with opening the store every day.\"","Hearing this, Qin Yuanzheng nodded and said, \"There's nothing wrong with this. It's good to open a store. Why, don't you support her?\"","Anyway, he supported whatever Qiao Lanshu did.","He thought Guan Wenjun had too many problems.","Guan Wenjun immediately said, \"Does it matter whether I support her or not? It doesn't! She simply doesn't listen to my suggestions!\"","It was only after a year of marriage that Guan Wenjun gradually got to know Zhong Mei's personality.","She was really a very independent and strong - willed woman.","After marriage, she took control of the family's financial power and suppressed him completely.","Qin Yuanzheng took a sip of tea and said, \"Since that's the case, then let her do what she wants to do. Why are you angry now?\"","Guan Wenjun moved his chair next to Qin Yuanzheng and whispered, \"What I care about is that she has been focusing on her so - called great cause recently and has neglected the family and me!\"","Guan Wenjun said impatiently, \"She hasn't slept with me for three months! Lao Qin, no man can stand this, right?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Three months. Indeed, no man could endure that.","Anyway, Qin Yuanzheng couldn't even endure three days away from Qiao Lanshu.","So Qin Yuanzheng fell silent again.","Guan Wenjun asked him, \"Lao Qin, tell me honestly. What would you do if you were in this situation?\"","Qin Yuanzheng said in a puzzled way, \"How would I know? I've never been in this situation.\"","Guan Wenjun stared at him and said, \"You and Comrade Xiao Qiao have been married for ten years, right? Hasn't she ever disliked you or kicked you out of the room?\"","Qin Yuanzheng thought for a while and said, \"Really, she hasn't.\"","Qiao Lanshu had never even quarreled with him.","She had never kicked him out of the room either. Every time he wanted to be intimate, he just hugged Qiao Lanshu and rubbed against her, and she would go weak all over and let him do what he wanted.","Oh, thinking of this, Qin Yuanzheng felt restless again. He missed his wife.","It had been four months since they last saw each other.","He wondered how his wife was doing in the capital.","He mustn't let some other man seduce her.","No, he had to go back to the military camp and call Qiao Lanshu's school.","Thinking like this, Qin Yuanzheng couldn't sit still.","Guan Wenjun said with envy, jealousy and hatred, \"Is your relationship with your wife really that good? I just can't believe it. After marriage, even the gentlest woman will turn into a shrew. Why hasn't yours changed?\"","Qin Yuanzheng was too lazy to talk to him and said slowly, \"Why? Just because I have better luck than you.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun originally came to Qin Yuanzheng to complain, but he was so angry with Qin Yuanzheng's words that he was speechless.","What is the most painful thing in the world?","It is that after being disliked by his wife and sleeping in separate rooms for three months, he learned that his brother had been married for ten years and still had an affectionate relationship with his wife, sleeping together every night.","Isn't it said that a kiss between middle - aged couples can give you nightmares for several nights?","Why doesn't it apply to Qin Yuanzheng?","Guan Wenjun had been suppressed by Zhong Mei for several years. Now his rebellious psychology kicked in.","He didn't stay in Wencheng for the night. He drove back to Longcheng before it got dark.","When he got home, Zhong Mei had already put the two children to sleep and washed and dried the clothes.","They used to have a nanny. But now that the two children had grown up, they didn't have one anymore.","After all, the nanny they hired was not as good as Nanny Shi. She didn't take good care of the children and always liked to take advantage. From time to time, she would steal some things and take them back to her own home.","Zhong Mei endured it several times. Finally, she couldn't stand it anymore. She quarreled with the nanny over these trifles and finally fired her.","Zhong Mei was very capable. She could take good care of both the family and outside affairs and even had time to think about opening a grocery store.","At this time, she heard the sound of a car at the door. Then she heard footsteps entering the yard.","She knew that it was Guan Wenjun who had come back.","Guan Wenjun had gone to Wencheng on business for several days and came back so late. He must be very tired.","Zhong Mei quickly got up, opened the door and turned on the light bulb in the yard.","She looked at the tired - looking Guan Wenjun and said, \"You're back?\"","Guan Wenjun put his hands in his pockets, looked at her and said seriously, \"Yes, I'm back.\"","Zhong Mei looked at his expression and knew that he was up to something again and was about to throw a tantrum.","She turned around and went into the house.","Guan Wenjun immediately flew into a rage and shouted, \"Stop.\"","Zhong Mei turned around and looked at him. \"What?\"","Guan Wenjun strode forward, grabbed her arm and pinned her against the wall. He stared at Zhong Mei and said, \"Make love to you!\"","Zhong Mei: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun pulled Zhong Mei's hand and walked in the direction of the bathroom, saying as he walked, \"Take a bath with me. It's been three months. Don't even think about kicking me out again.\"","Zhong Mei: \"...\"","Zhong Mei wondered what had stimulated Guan Wenjun.","Previously, when they had a quarrel, she had kicked Guan Wenjun out of the room. Then Guan Wenjun had said harshly that he would sleep in a separate room and that if he ever went back to the bedroom, he would be a dog.","But now, after only three months, he couldn't hold it in anymore?","Zhong Mei had been in a good mood these days. She didn't want to quarrel with Guan Wenjun either because Guan Wenjun's job was being transferred. It seemed that he was going to be transferred to the provincial level, and then they could move to Wencheng.","Zhong Mei planned to open a grocery store in Wencheng, and she could also visit Qiao Lanshu from time to time. Thinking of this, the more she looked at Guan Wenjun, the more promising she thought he was.","She followed Guan Wenjun into the restroom and comforted him, saying, \"Okay, okay. I'll prepare hot water for you. Take off your dirty clothes first and put them in the bucket.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun asked suspiciously, \"Really? Aren't you angry?\"","Zhong Mei stared at him and said, \"It's been several months. I'm not angry anymore. It's you who are being awkward. If you want to sleep in the room every day, just say so directly. Stop being so coy. I really don't know who you take after in terms of this personality.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun: \"Anyway, it's not you.\""]},{"number":259,"title":"Chapter 259: Xia Xia Meets Her Enemy","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu had been away from home for several months, so naturally she couldn't tend to the household.","As for Qin Yuanzheng, he had to go to the military base, and the work there was very busy — leaving early and returning late was his usual routine.","As a result, there were no adults at home most of the time; often it was just the three children.","Mornings were manageable, because Qin Yuanzheng got up very early and would cook breakfast for the kids.","Of course, Qin Yuanzheng cooked as simply as possible — he would never put thought into meals the way Qiao Lanshu did, who, whenever she had time, would rack her brain to prepare something special for the children.","His breakfasts were simple: soy milk, fried dough sticks, and steamed buns, or millet porridge with steamed sweet potatoes and pickled vegetables.","Luckily, the children weren't picky eaters — mainly because they didn't dare to be picky with him. So during the months Qiao Lanshu was away, the children behaved quite well.","Lunch was even easier to sort out. Most of the time, Han Ye would simply take Qin Qiao'an and Qin Qiaoxia to the Public Security Bureau canteen to eat.","Han Wenlin's workplace wasn't far from the school, and since there was an internal canteen, it was convenient for the kids to go there for meals.","Occasionally, when they didn't go to the canteen, Han Ye would cook himself.","Of course, his cooking skills were inherited from his father, Han Wenlin — absolutely terrible. The food he made was awful.","Even Qin Qiao'an, who adored him the most, couldn't, in good conscience, force himself to praise it.","One day after lunch, the two brothers were about to head out to play as usual. Before leaving, Han Ye reminded Qin Qiaoxia, saying, \"Xia'er, don't go out while you're home alone, alright? Your brothers are going out to play for a bit, and we'll bring you a popsicle when we come back.\"","Qin Qiaoxia was sitting at the desk by the window in her room, with a thick wuxia novel placed on the desk. She nodded and said, \"Got it. And don't go picking fights out there either. Mom's not home, so no one's going to have your backs.\"","When Qin Qiao'an thought about how, after every incident, he would be punished with horse-riding stance, his legs went weak just thinking about it.","Han Ye tugged at Xiaxia's braid and teased her: \"Alright, alright, look at you sounding like such an old stick-in-the-mud.\"","With that, Han Ye took Qin Qiao'an and ran out the door.","Han Ye rode his old twenty-eight-inch bicycle, carrying Qin Qiao'an on the back, and headed to the area near the clothing market in Wencheng.","The streets there were lively and bustling — there was everything: music stores, dance halls, places where young people went roller skating, playing arcade machines, and even billiards.","These were all things that had become popular in recent years, and young people loved them.","Han Ye enjoyed playing arcade games too, but recently, he wasn't taking Qin Qiao'an out just to play.","His main goal was to do some business, to make some money.","Han Ye rode the bike to the side of a big building on the street corner, where five or six teenagers in their early teens were already waiting.","Beside them stood three or four bicycles, with large bags strapped to the rear racks and front bars.","Han Ye rode over and asked them, \"So, what goods do you have today? Still selling clothes?\"","One of the teens, around Han Ye's age, said, \"We've got clothes today too, but since you don't have much time, you should sell cassette tapes.\"","With that, he took a bag off his bicycle, untied the rope, and revealed a bag stuffed full of cassette tapes.","Each tape had a cover photo of various singers — most of them were Teresa Teng.","The boy handed the tapes to Han Ye to look at and said, \"These are cheap. One-fifty each, and you can make fifty cents profit per tape. Interested?\"","These tapes weren't originals — they were copies people had made by recording over blank tapes. Of course, plenty of people didn't care whether it was original or pirated.","As long as they could listen to the songs, and it matched the singers on the covers, that was enough.","The price was several times cheaper than the authentic ones.","Plus, this item was selling really well right now — there was no worry about finding buyers.","So, besides setting up stalls to sell clothes, these young men had recently made selling these cassette tapes their main hustle.","Han Ye, because he had school, didn't have as much time. He didn't source the goods himself, nor did he find people to help him.","What he did was cooperate with these young men — he and Qin Qiao'an would take the goods and sell them, and the other party promised to pay him a certain amount per tape sold. The more he sold, the more money he made.","That was enough for him. He had no intention of making a career out of it, nor did he dream of getting rich. He just thought doing business was interesting and that he could learn a lot from it, which was why he did this kind of thing.","He nodded, had Qin Qiao'an pick up the tapes, and said to the teenagers, \"Alright, this is good. I'll take them. We'll meet here at six this afternoon?\"","The other guy nodded: \"Don't be late, remember.\"","So Han Ye took Qin Qiao'an, lugged that big bag of tapes, and left.","They found a spot in the busy marketplace, set the goods down on the ground, and started setting up their stall and hawking their wares with practiced ease.","Qin Qiao'an had never experienced anything like this before either.","At first, Qin Qiao'an felt too embarrassed to shout out their sales pitch, and when people asked about prices, he was too shy to answer.","It was Han Ye who taught him what to say and encouraged him to shout it out boldly.","After a while, Qin Qiao'an's courage grew. Once he successfully sold his first tape, he got incredibly excited, like he'd been injected with adrenaline.","Han Ye said to him, \"Xia'er is home alone right now. These next few days, we can't stay out too late — we need to get home early.\"","Qin Qiao'an immediately said, \"Big brother, don't worry! I guarantee we'll sell out before dark!\"","Qin Qiao'an grabbed passersby and enthusiastically pitched: \"Songs by Hong Kong and Taiwan stars! We've got Teresa Teng, we've got Alan Tam! One-fifty each, five bucks for three! It's a steal for you!\"","Han Ye listened nearby and thought — something about that didn't sound right?","Before he could figure out what, the passerby started complaining: \"Do you think I'm stupid? One-fifty each, and you're giving me three for five bucks? Give me four for five and I'll buy.\"","Qin Qiao'an couldn't agree to that.","So he said, \"How about this: six bucks. Six bucks for four. Deal? Can't go any cheaper.\"","Han Ye: \"...\"","Luckily, Qin Qiao'an still managed to make a sale in the end — two bucks eighty cents, selling two tapes.","After the customer left, he muttered to Han Ye, \"That guy was so stingy. He haggled with me over twenty cents and wouldn't budge a penny.\"","But well, one-forty apiece still made a profit, so Qin Qiao'an had sold them anyway — after all, he needed to get home early today, so he had to sell out quickly.","The two brothers set up their stall in the busy market and were doing booming business.","Xiaxia was still home alone, reading her book.","Lately, she had noticed that Han Ye was taking Qin Qiao'an out every single day to do something or other — there wasn't a day they weren't rushing out.","And every time they came back, it was quite late.","Han Wenlin couldn't keep Han Ye in check, and Qin Yuanzheng was too busy to pay attention.","And the only person who could truly keep both brothers in line, Qiao Lanshu, still had over a month before she'd be back.","With that, the two brothers were like young calves that had slipped their ropes — running wild and free all day.","Every time Han Ye came back, he would bring Xiaxia some snacks, stationery, books, or little accessories and hair clips that girls liked.","Xiaxia knew he had plenty of money, so she never asked questions.","During pauses in her reading, she also felt that Han Ye was acting a bit strangely, because books were expensive, and no matter how much allowance he had, he couldn't afford to spend like that.","While turning a page, Xiaxia glanced at the fountain pen on the desk, musing for a brief moment, but soon she couldn't be bothered to think about it anymore.","Because the book was too good, and she was once again immersed in the storyline.","She had a habit: whenever she came across a well-written sentence or phrase in a book, she liked to copy it down.","She picked up her notebook and pen, and after copying a few pages, realized that the notebook was full.","She closed the notebook, opened the drawer of the desk, and rummaged inside—no new notebooks left.","So she took a one-yuan coin from her little savings jar, turned around, and headed out the door, planning to go to the stationery store near the military compound to buy a new one.","The area around her was all familiar; although she rarely went out alone, it was broad daylight now, so there was nothing much to fear.","Xiaxia came out of the military compound, crossed one street, then walked forward to the intersection, crossed another street, and there was a large stationery store.","As Xiaxia arrived at the entrance of the stationery store, she suddenly ran into someone who looked very familiar.","It was her former classmate, Li Taohua.","Li Taohua's parents had both been suspended from their jobs and were now stuck at home with no work.","With their bad moods, they naturally took out their frustrations on the children.","Especially Li Taohua.","Wang Lanying felt that if Li Taohua hadn't deliberately bullied Qin Qiaoxia in the first place, none of this chain of events would have happened.","So she scolded Li Taohua every day, and sometimes even hit her.","Li Taohua couldn't stand staying at home, so she kept running outside, and over time, she made quite a few friends on the streets.","When Xiaxia arrived at the stationery store, she happened to see Li Taohua standing at the street corner with five or six boys and girls, chatting and laughing.","The older ones among those kids looked about thirteen or fourteen, while the younger ones were around Li Taohua's age—nine or ten. They were all just a bunch of semi-grown children.","But judging by their clothes and manner, Xiaxia could tell they didn't look like students; they seemed more like the kind of kids who had started working early to make a living.","While Xiaxia was sizing them up, Li Taohua happened to turn her head and caught sight of her in one glance.","Li Taohua's expression froze for a second, then immediately darkened, her face twisting with venom as she glared viciously at Xiaxia. She pointed at Qin Qiaoxia from across the street and shouted loudly: \"Qin Qiaoxia!\"","The friends beside Li Taohua immediately asked: \"Taohua, who is she?\"","Someone said, \"Is she that bitch you were talking about?\"","\"Which bitch? Not the one who got Taohua's parents fired, is it?\"","With so many friends backing her up, Li Taohua felt smug. She wasn't afraid of Han Ye or Qin Qiao'an anymore—she had plenty of friends, and they'd all have her back.","She shouted loudly: \"That's her! Don't let her get away—today we're going to teach her a good lesson!\"","The moment Li Taohua shouted that, Xiaxia made a snap decision and turned to run.","Li Taohua hadn't expected Qin Qiaoxia to bolt without saying a word, so she immediately started chasing: \"Chase her! Don't let her get away!\"","Her friends were loyal enough and went after Qin Qiaoxia with her, yelling things like \"Stop running!\" and \"Catch her!\"","Qin Qiaoxia wanted to run back toward the military compound, but Li Taohua's group had numbers on their side and had already started to surround her. Not only was the direction to the military compound cut off, but so was the way to the police station.","Qin Qiaoxia steeled herself and ducked into the crisscrossing alleyways.","Xiaxia didn't exercise much; her only hobby was reading, so she wasn't a fast runner.","However, Li Taohua and her group were all noise and bluster, so they weren't exactly fast either. Listening to their racket, she darted randomly through the alleys.","Soon, she found herself in a run-down area of old houses.","Before the reform and opening up, this place had been a large compound with many people living there.","But after the reforms, these houses had become too old, many had collapsed, so the residents had all moved away.","She ran frantically among the broken walls and ruins until, in a weed-choked, abandoned courtyard, she spotted a disused dry well. The well was filled with sandy soil, but it still looked nearly two meters deep.","Xiaxia was panting heavily, her legs weak, and she couldn't run anymore.","But she couldn't let Li Taohua and her group catch her either—if they did, who knew what kind of bullying she'd endure. Those people were thirteen or fourteen, and a couple of boys among them. She was scared.","Without hesitation, she pushed aside the overgrown weeds and dead branches, and using the footholds carved into the well wall, she carefully climbed down into the well.","The well was dry—no water, just damp sand and stones. The walls were covered in moss, and it was pitch black inside. She was frightened, crouching at the bottom and straining to hear what was happening above.","She heard Li Taohua yelling: \"Where did she run off to? I just saw her coming this way! Did any of you see her?\"","Someone said, \"No, we were all right behind you.\"","\"She definitely seemed to run this way—could she have gone into one of those broken-down houses?\"","\"Those houses look so old. If we go in, won't they collapse on us? Look, half of them are already rubble.\"","\"Would she really hide in there? Maybe we should just go. This place is too remote and creepy.\"","Li Taohua said in fury: \"Qin Qiaoxia is my enemy. If I get my hands on her, I'll beat her up good—I'll scratch her face to pieces!\"","\"Could she have gone that way? There's a small path over there.\"","\"Come on, let's go check. Don't let her get too far.\"","The group of five or six babbled and chattered, ran through the overgrown courtyard, cut into a side alley, and with a clatter of footsteps, they were gone into the distance.","In the weed-covered corner, down at the bottom of the dry well, Xiaxia crouched, and only then did her taut nerves begin to relax.","She had just been sprinting for over half an hour, and she still hadn't caught her breath. Every inhale made her chest ache.","Her arms and legs were weak, and she slumped to sit on the ground, quietly listening to the sounds outside.","Those people were running around the ruined courtyard, their voices rising and falling, sometimes near, sometimes far.","Xiaxia knew—they realized she was hiding, or at least that she hadn't gotten far, so they were running around the area looking for her.","She couldn't go out now, and she was terrified they'd find her, her heart pounding anxiously in her chest."]},{"number":260,"title":"Chapter 260: Finding Xiaxia","paragraphs":["Han Ye and Qin Qiao'an headed home while it was still dusk.","Han Ye rode his bicycle with Qin Qiao'an sitting on the back, and in the basket in front were a popsicle, a bottle of soda, and a nice box of colored pencils.","Those were all things he'd bought for Xiaxia.","Qin Qiao'an sat on the back seat of the bike, feeling very pleased with how he'd done that day.","It was thanks to his enthusiastic selling that they'd gotten rid of their goods so quickly—it wasn't even dark yet, and the two brothers were already on their way home.","Qin Qiao'an asked proudly, \"Bro, bro! How much money did we make in total today?\"","Han Ye smiled and said, \"Didn't I just show you a moment ago? Twenty-eight yuan.\"","Qin Qiao'an then counted on his fingers, calculated, and said in surprise, \"That's a lot!\"","In this era, the average worker's salary was around one hundred fifty to two hundred yuan a month.","They'd made twenty-eight yuan in just one afternoon, and that was without even trying hard.","If they put in more effort and were more diligent, leaving at noon every day and selling all the way until the night market closed, the money they'd earn would at least double—that way, they could make close to a hundred yuan.","For the two of them, that was already a lot of money.","Qin Qiao'an sighed and said, \"No wonder people drop out of school and go set up stalls to do business. Business really does make money. We're just selling goods for them—if we went and got the stock ourselves and sold it, we'd make even more!\"","At this rate, even without studying, it seemed like they could make a decent amount of money. Life wouldn't be a problem at all.","Han Ye also did the math in his head. It was true—although they'd been making a fair bit helping sell things these past few days, when you added it all up, the profit margin wasn't actually that high.","Because the other party's profit was even higher, and they were the bosses who supplied the goods to them to sell in bulk. They must be making a good chunk of change.","Han Ye muttered under his breath, \"Looks like anyone going into business now can make big money. The country's economy is on the rise overall. Things coming over from Hong Kong and Taiwan are also selling like hotcakes. Just open a shop and sell some imported goods, and you can make money. This is actually an opportunity.\"","Qin Qiao'an suddenly felt that the popsicle in his mouth didn't taste that great anymore. He grabbed hold of Han Ye's shoulders, stood up, and shouted, \"Bro, how about we go get our own stock and sell it too? How about that? Let's go make big money!\"","Han Ye: \"...\"","Han Ye made a \"tsk\" sound and said to him, \"How old are you, and you're already thinking about doing business? Didn't you say you wanted to join the army later?\"","Qin Qiao'an said, \"I can make money first, then join the army! Bro, I really think we can do it! Why should we work for other people to make a living?\"","Han Ye was silent for a moment, then said, \"There's no rush on this. We'll talk about it later.\"","The two brothers rode their bicycle through the streets and alleys, heading back to the military compound the whole way.","On the way, Qin Qiao'an didn't stay quiet for even a few minutes. As he ate his popsicle, he said, \"Bro, what are we having for dinner tonight? I'm starving. I want to eat meat.\"","Qin Yuanzheng had been swamped these past few days, stuck in meetings at the headquarters building every day, and he didn't come home until after seven in the evening. Counting on him to come back and cook for them? That was out of the question.","Qin Qiao'an sighed, \"I miss my mom. A kid without a mom is like a blade of grass! When is my mom coming back!\"","Han Ye missed Qiao Lanshu too. Without Qiao Lanshu around, the three of them—the siblings—had to fend for themselves.","Just then, Han Ye had made some money today and was feeling happy about it. He immediately said, \"In a bit, we'll take Xiaxia with us. Big bro will take you all to a restaurant. We're eating out!\"","In the 1980s, there were already quite a lot of restaurants on the streets. It was no longer like before, when only state-owned restaurants existed and you had to use ration tickets.","In Wencheng, ration tickets had basically been done away with. Except for certain specialty goods, ordinary things could be bought with just cash.","Every restaurant had all sorts of things available, with no spending limits—as long as you had money, you could buy.","When Qin Qiao'an heard they were going to a restaurant, he got so excited that he started crazily pounding Han Ye on the back, making \"bang bang bang\" sounds. He shouted, \"Awesome, bro! Restaurant! Restaurant! I want roast chicken and roast duck, braised pork knuckle, red-braised pork, meat buns, and a full set of steamed flower rolls and mantou!\"","Han Ye: \"...\"","Han Ye was speechless and said to him, \"Qin Qiao'an, are you a pig? Eating that much! You're not treating me like your big brother—you're treating me like your enemy!\"","Qin Qiao'an just laughed out loud, patting Han Ye's back all the way, urging him to pedal faster.","He couldn't wait to eat roast chicken and roast duck.","Han Ye steered the bike with one hand. After riding this long, he was thirsty too, so he pulled out a popsicle, held it in one hand, and crunched on it noisily. He still doted on his younger brother.","He said to Qin Qiao'an, \"Alright, let's do this—we'll buy one roast chicken and one roast duck. We'll eat half and save half for your dad. Forget the buns; we still have flower rolls and mantou at home, so no need to spend money on those. We've also got cucumbers at home—we'll make a cucumber salad and some millet porridge. How does that sound?\"","These were all things they loved, so of course Qin Qiao'an nodded like crazy.","He tossed the popsicle stick away and said excitedly, \"Whatever you say, bro! Pedal faster, I'm so hungry.\"","Both brothers were starving—they'd been out working for hours without eating a thing.","Young lads in their growth spurt burned through energy quickly and got hungry fast.","As Han Ye talked about eating out, he managed to make even himself crave the food.","So, he finished off his popsicle in a few quick bites, then pedaled the bicycle as fast as he could.","...","There was no helping it—the weather was hot, and the popsicle melted quickly. He needed to get the popsicle home to Xiaxia soon, otherwise, by the time they got there, the little girl would only be left with melted popsicle water.","Soon enough, the brothers arrived at the front gate of their home. Qin Qiao'an jumped off the bike first, ran up to the door, and shoved it—but it didn't budge. That was when he noticed the front door was locked.","That was strange.","Usually, the courtyard gate of their house rarely stayed shut.","Even if it was closed, they generally didn't lock it.","Because the military compound was a safe place, and the neighbors around them were all familiar faces. People frequently dropped by each other's homes.","All the kids knew each other, so there was no need to lock the door at all.","Qin Qiao'an looked at the courtyard gate, then at the lock on it. He frowned and tilted his head to ask Han Ye, \"Bro, did you lock the door when we left?\"","Han Ye pushed the bike over and said, \"No, I didn't lock it. Did Xiaxia go out?\"","Qin Qiao'an pulled out the key hanging around his neck and unlocked the front door of their home.","Then he ran inside shouting, \"Xiaxia, big brothers are back!\"","He barged into Xiaxia's room and saw it completely empty—no one was there.","Xiaxia's book was still on the desk with a bookmark tucked in it.","Qin Qiao'an ran back out and said, \"Bro, Xiaxia's not home. She seems to have gone out.\"","Han Ye parked the bike in the courtyard and ran inside too: \"Xiaxia? Xiaxia? Are you home?\"","The two brothers looked around the room, but of course they couldn't find Xiaxia anywhere.","Qin Qiao'an tossed the finished popsicle stick into the trash can before saying, \"It's almost dark by now. Where did Xiaxia go?\"","Han Ye stood in the yard for a while, then said, \"She probably went to the stationery store on the corner. She goes there pretty often to buy things.\"","With that, he said to Qin Qiao'an, \"An'an, you stay here and steam the rice. I'll ride my bike to pick up Xiaxia. It's almost dark, and there are plenty of bad people around—she's just a young girl, she shouldn't be out on her own.\"","Qin Qiao'an nodded. \"No problem, leave it to me.\"","With that, Qin Qiao'an headed to the kitchen to steam the rice.","Han Ye, meanwhile, pushed his bicycle back out the gate. As he left the compound, he stopped by the guardhouse and asked the guard, \"Hey, brother, have you seen my little sister Xiaxia?\"","Han Ye was quite well-known in the military compound—everyone recognized him.","The guard smiled and said, \"Yeah, I saw her. She left around four-thirty, headed that way.\"","He pointed in a direction, which happened to be toward the stationery store on the corner.","Han Ye smiled and thanked him, then hopped on his bike and pedaled toward the corner.","But deep down, he still felt something was off. After all, the guard said Xiaxia had left at four-thirty, and it was already five-thirty now—an hour had passed, so why hadn't she come back yet?","Could buying stationery really take that long?","As Han Ye rode his bike past the intersection, he casually glanced around, and out of the corner of his eye, he caught sight of a familiar figure.","He turned to look, and sure enough, he spotted Li Taohua and Li Jian.","Both siblings were dark-skinned and stocky, very distinctive, so Han Ye recognized them at a glance.","He couldn't be bothered with them, so he sped up and passed the intersection, riding all the way to the stationery store.","He walked in and looked around the shop. It wasn't big to begin with—you could see the whole place in one glance.","No Xiaxia.","Han Ye's expression immediately turned serious. He walked to the counter and asked the shopkeeper, \"Boss, have you seen my sister? Xiaxia? She's about this tall, with straight bangs and a round face, and she has dimples when she smiles. She comes here often to buy things, and you've even complimented her on how cute she is. Do you remember?\"","The shopkeeper definitely remembered. She said, \"Of course I remember her, but she didn't come in today.\"","Han Ye's face grew even grimmer. \"She didn't come? Around four or five this afternoon, she said she was coming here to buy something?\"","The shopkeeper waved her hand. \"She didn't come, she really didn't. I know Xiaxia, she wasn't here this afternoon.\"","Han Ye's expression turned dark.","He stepped out of the stationery store and stood at the entrance, looking around.","Next to the stationery store was a convenience store, and across the street was an old barber giving haircuts. This wasn't a main street, so it wasn't usually too busy.","And since this was the military compound, the surrounding residential areas were sparse.","Everyone around here knew each other. By all logic, Xiaxia shouldn't have gotten lost.","Han Ye came out of the stationery store and went to the convenience store next door to ask. The convenience store owner said the same thing—Xiaxia hadn't been there.","Han Ye crossed the street and went to ask the old barber.","The old man usually had a few stools set up with a handwritten sign reading \"Haircut 5 mao.\" Plenty of people came to him for haircuts, all of them neighbors.","Qin Yuanzheng had brought Qin Qiao'an and Han Ye there several times, all of them getting crew cuts.","Han Ye ran over and asked him, \"Uncle, did you see my little sister Xiaxia this afternoon? Did she come by here?\"","The barber was just sitting around with a few men in their fifties and sixties, playing chess.","Before he could answer, one of the men watching the chess game spoke up. \"Are you talking about Xiaxia? It looked to me like she was being chased by someone this afternoon.\"","The moment Han Ye heard that, his expression changed. \"Chased? By who? Which way did she run?\"","A couple of the old men started chiming in: \"Oh, right, now I remember. It was Zhuzi and his crew—they're usually idle and up to no good, hanging around and bothering young girls here. They were here this afternoon too.\"","\"That's right, that's them. They probably saw that Xiaxia was pretty, so they chased after her...\"","When Han Ye heard this, his face turned ashen. \"They were harassing Xiaxia, and you didn't help?\"","The old men shook their heads and looked at Han Ye. \"We couldn't even run if we tried.\"","Han Ye: \"...\"","Han Ye nearly cursed them out for being useless.","He didn't have time to worry about who had chased after her now. He asked urgently, \"Which way did Xiaxia run? Do you know?\"","\"Yeah, she ran that way. Over there.\"","One of the old men pointed down another street and said, \"There's a row of abandoned courtyard houses over there. She went that way. It's been over an hour and she still hasn't come back. You'd better hurry and check.\"","Han Ye was frantic. He immediately hopped on his bike and tore off in that direction.","As he rode, he shouted at the top of his lungs, \"Xiaxia! Qin Qiaoxia! Where are you? If you can hear me, answer me!\"","Han Ye kept shouting as he rode, his voice loud enough to stir up both streets full of neighbors. People came running out one after another, and someone asked, \"Who's Xiaxia? Hey, that young man looks pretty familiar, doesn't he?\"","\"Of course he looks familiar—last month your boy got his face beaten black and blue by him. Forget already?\"","\"...\"","\"Oh, it's him. I remember he has a cute little sister, isn't her name Xiaxia? Xiaxia's missing?\"","In no time, all the neighbors were out. It wasn't like they had anything better to do, so as soon as they heard there might be some excitement, everyone came out.","Li Taohua and Li Jian had been walking along the road. The moment she heard Han Ye screaming Qin Qiaoxia's name all over the street, Li Taohua's face turned pale with fright. She quickly said to Li Jian, \"Brother, it's getting dark already. Let's just hurry home.\"","With that, she turned around to leave.","Li Jian was confused. \"Didn't we just come out? We haven't even bought the soy sauce yet. Why are you in such a rush?\"","Li Taohua stamped her foot and let out an anxious \"Hal hey,\" saying, \"You go buy the soy sauce, I'm heading home first!\"","She turned and ran off.","Li Jian watched her back with a helpless look and went to buy the soy sauce himself with the bottle in hand.","Meanwhile, Han Ye rode his bike around the abandoned courtyard houses twice, all the while shouting Qin Qiaoxia's name until his voice went hoarse.","He was terrified that something might have happened to her. If he couldn't find her in another ten minutes, he'd have to go to the military base to find Qin Yuanzheng and then to the police station to find Han Wenlin."]},{"number":261,"title":"Chapter 261: Mind Your Boundaries","paragraphs":["Han Ye rode his bicycle, searching everywhere through that abandoned compound of old courtyard homes.","It wasn't easy to ride a bicycle through the compound, with its overgrown weeds and crumbling walls.","In the end, he had to get off and push the bike as he walked around, searching.","Watching the sky gradually darken, Han Ye grew anxious.","The longer the delay, the worse it would be for Xiaxia, of course.","Han Ye's father was a police officer, so he naturally understood these things.","After searching all afternoon, Han Ye's voice was hoarse from calling out, and he still hadn't found Xiaxia.","He was drenched in sweat, his face somewhat pale—whether from exhaustion or fear, it was hard to tell.","He pushed his bicycle to the entrance of a run-down courtyard and picked his way through the rubble, calling out as he went: \"Xia'er! Xiaxia! Qin Qiaoxia! Are you in here? Can you hear me?\"","He called out while studying the dilapidated gate of the compound.","The yard was thick with weeds, and as the daylight faded, it grew darker and colder inside, looking rather eerie.","Han Ye thought to himself: Xiaxia usually seemed calm and composed, but she was still a girl, and her nerve was actually pretty small.","Maybe Xiaxia wouldn't have come here.","Maybe he'd been looking in the wrong direction.","Han Ye wondered whether he should switch places to keep searching, or whether he should hop on his bicycle and race as fast as he could to the public security bureau or the military district headquarters, to find Han Wenlin and Qin Yuanzheng to help look for her.","He was just one person, and he didn't know much about investigative work, so he wasn't very good at finding people.","More importantly, Qin Yuanzheng's unit had police dogs—maybe he could get the dogs involved.","Thinking this, he hurriedly turned to leave.","But just as he swung his leg over the bicycle and was about to ride away from the broken wall of the compound, he suddenly heard Xiaxia's voice!","Han Ye froze, rooted to the spot. He tested a call: \"Xia'er? Qin Qiaoxia!\"","He listened carefully. The voice was faint, but it really did sound like Xiaxia!","She was calling for him!","Han Ye quickly got off the bike, shoved it carelessly to the ground, and charged into the ruined compound, following the sound.","His years of training in the military hadn't been wasted—Han Ye was sharp. He jumped over a crumbling wall, called out to Xiaxia again, and this time her voice was louder.","Listening carefully to the sound and tracking the footprints on the ground, he soon pushed through the weeds and found the dry well.","He scrambled to the edge of the well. It was nearly dark now, and the well was pitch black, but he could still make out Xiaxia.","Xiaxia was crouched at the bottom of the well, filthy all over, her hair a tangle.","The moment he saw her down there, the weight lifted off Han Ye's chest.","But only for a moment—because as soon as he took in poor, pitiful Qin Qiaoxia crouching in that dry well, a wave of heartache and fury surged through him!","Who dared to bully their Xiaxia like this?!","They'd even thrown the girl into some godforsaken well in a place like this!","Han Ye's chest ached with anger.","With emotions churning like that, he couldn't speak for a moment.","Xiaxia looked up and saw it was him. Her eyes instantly lit up. Her voice was hoarse too, but you could hear the joy in it: \"Brother Ye, you finally came! Get me out of here—I can't climb up.\"","She'd hidden down there earlier, listening as those people searched for her all over. She was terrified, so she crouched silently.","After they'd left, she stayed put for another twenty minutes, just to be safe.","Only when she was sure they weren't coming back did she start trying to climb out.","But the grooves in the well wall were covered in moss, and the walls were slick. She tried twice and fell back down both times.","Exhausted and unable to climb out, she watched the sky grow darker and darker, and she was scared out of her wits.","Thankfully, she'd heard Han Ye's voice.","When it came down to it, Brother Ye really was the one she could count on.","The moment Xiaxia saw Han Ye, the tears started falling.","She called up to him: \"Brother Ye, I'm scared to climb out.\"","Han Ye let out a huge sigh of relief. He leaned over the mouth of the well and said: \"Don't panic. I'm coming down to get you.\"","With that, he gauged the depth of the well and jumped in himself.","The well was too narrow, so once he was down there, he hoisted Xiaxia up onto his shoulders and pushed her out.","Then, bracing his foot on a notch in the wall and using his hands to grip the edge, he hoisted himself up and out of the well, which was over two meters deep.","As soon as he got out, he had Xiaxia stand up. He squeezed her arms, then her legs, and looked at her face: \"Are you hurt?\"","Xiaxia wiped her tears and shook her head: \"No, I'm fine. I just fell twice trying to climb, so my knees sting a little.\"","By now, Han Ye was seething inside. He wished he could beat the people who'd tormented Xiaxia to a pulp.","But he held it in. He rolled up Xiaxia's pant legs to check. Both knees were skinned.","He said: \"It's nothing. When we get back, I'll put some medicine on it.\"","With that, he hoisted Xiaxia onto his back and started walking out, his expression dark as he asked: \"Did those people throw you down there?\"","Xiaxia shook her head: \"No, I jumped in myself. Li Taohua brought her friends to chase me, saying they wanted to teach me a lesson. I was afraid they'd catch me, so I jumped into the dry well to hide.\"","Han Ye scolded her angrily: \"Why didn't you run toward the military compound?\"","Xiaxia sounded a bit aggrieved: \"There were six or seven of them, coming at me from all sides. The way home was blocked.\"","Han Ye gave a cold laugh: \"Li Taohua, right? Who else? Do you know any of the others?\"","Xiaxia named the ones she recognized, but couldn't describe the people she didn't know.","Han Ye ground his teeth and said: \"Fine. Got it.\"","He'd give those people a real beating tomorrow, or his name wasn't Han!","He set Xiaxia on the back of the bicycle and said: \"Hold on tight. Let's head home first.\"","Xiaxia sat obediently on the bike.","Han Ye swung his long leg over the old-style bicycle and glanced back at Xiaxia. She was looking at him too, and said: \"Brother Ye, let's hurry. It's dark now, and this place is creepy.\"","It was, after all, an abandoned compound—crumbling walls, wild grass rustling, the whole thing giving off a eerie vibe.","If Han Ye hadn't come to rescue her, her heart couldn't have taken staying there much longer.","But Xiaxia was the steady type—when it came to her emotions, she didn't let much show.","By now she'd stopped crying, and she wasn't making a big show of gratitude toward Han Ye.","Han Ye, though, teased her: \"What, you're not crying anymore? You only shed a couple of tears, and you've already managed to comfort yourself?\"","Xiaxia: \"...\"","Xiaxia said quietly: \"Brother Ye, let's go back. I'm starving.\"","Han Ye pushed off with his long leg and pedaled toward the military compound, saying: \"You scared me half to death just now, you know that? Mother Qiao asked me to look after the two of you. If you'd really gotten lost, would I even have the face to show myself to our mom again?\"","Xiaxia sighed at these words and said, \"I miss Mom. Why isn't she back yet?\"","Han Ye: \"Another month or so, right? She'll be back when school starts.\"","Xiaxia had always loved clinging to Qiao Lanshu since she was little. Even though she was in elementary school now, she still loved sticking close to her mom.","Since the day she was born, this was the first time she'd been apart from Qiao Lanshu for this long.","If Qiao Lanshu were here right now, Xiaxia would definitely be holding onto her mom and crying for a long time.","Han Ye brought Xiaxia back to the military compound. Qin Qiao'an had almost finished steaming the rice.","He'd been waiting anxiously in their own yard, and had already run out to sit by the compound entrance to wait.","He'd originally wanted to go out and look for Xiaxia too, but he was afraid he'd miss Han Ye bringing her back.","So he didn't dare wander off.","Now that it was dark out, he finally saw Han Ye riding back on his bicycle. He jumped up excitedly: \"Bro, Xiaxia, you're finally back!\"","The moment Han Ye got home, he said darkly, \"Qiao'an, tomorrow you're coming with me. We're getting revenge for Xiaxia. Those rotten bastards—daring to bully someone in our family. Watch me show them a thing or two.\"","Qin Qiao'an looked at him with his hair all disheveled and said angrily, \"That Li Taohua? Her parents are both suspended from duty, and she still dares to act this arrogant! Tomorrow I'm going to throw her into that dry well too and let her stay in there for a night. Then we'll see if she still dares to be so cocky!\"","Han Ye sneered: \"Not just her—her accomplices too. Throw them all in. Damn it, a bunch of bastards.\"","East, west, north, south four streets—they hadn't asked around to find out who the boss was.","If they dared to bully his little sister, they were going to pay the price.","Xiaxia was covered in dirt. Qin Qiao'an quickly said to her, \"Xiaxia, go take a bath first. I've boiled hot water—we'll eat once you're done.\"","Xiaxia nodded and obediently went off to bathe.","Han Ye then took out twenty yuan and told Qin Qiao'an to go to a nearby restaurant and buy roasted chicken and roast duck.","At the time, a roast duck cost around eight yuan and a roasted chicken around six.","For a little over ten yuan, he could bring both back.","Qin Qiao'an took the money, ran out quickly, and bought everything.","By the time Xiaxia came out of her bath, the three siblings were sitting at the dining table eating.","Qin Qiao'an gnawed on a chicken leg as he asked, \"Big brother, should we tell Dad about this?\"","It was already seven in the evening. Normally at this time, Qin Yuanzheng should have been home by now.","Han Ye shoveled rice into his mouth as he shook his head: \"No need. Big brother can handle this. No need to tell your dad. He's busy enough as it is—he doesn't have time for it.\"","Qin Qiao'an nodded: \"Yeah, I think so too. This is between us young people. No need to tell Dad. They're too old now, can't keep up. Revenge is for us.\"","Han Ye tore off a roast duck leg and put it in Xiaxia's bowl, telling her, \"Eat some meat, why are you only eating greens? What's so good about those vegetable leaves?\"","Then he put half a duck head into her bowl and said, \"Eat some duck brain to nourish your head. Your brain is fried from reading all those books. You're like a little dullard.\"","Xiaxia: \"...\"","She gave Han Ye a speechless look. She wanted to snap back at him, but considering he saved her today, she decided to let it slide. Today she'd let him win.","Just then, the sound of a car reached the entrance. Qin Yuanzheng was home.","The moment Qin Yuanzheng entered the yard, he caught the aroma of roasted chicken and roast duck.","He hadn't eaten yet either, and said as soon as he got inside, \"You guys went and bought roast duck?\"","Han Ye nodded: \"Uncle Qin, we left some food for you—it's in the pot.\"","Qin Yuanzheng set down his hat, took off his coat, and came over to glance at the table. Seeing not only roast duck but also roasted chicken today, he raised an eyebrow at Han Ye: \"Where did you kids get this much money? This isn't cheap, is it?\"","Han Ye: \"Uncle Qin, I have money. Qiao'an wanted to eat, so I went and bought it.\"","Actually, he wanted to eat too, but he was afraid Qin Yuanzheng would interrogate him.","So he just said Qiao'an wanted it.","Qin Yuanzheng went to wash his hands, came back, took out the meal that had been left for him in the pot, and sat down next to Han Ye to eat.","Once Qin Yuanzheng arrived, the three younger ones didn't dare talk much. Xiaxia didn't talk much anyway.","The other two usually caused trouble and had mediocre grades, so they were afraid of saying the wrong thing and getting smacked by Qin Yuanzheng.","But then, Xiaxia, who had been quietly gnawing on her duck leg, suddenly spoke up. She said, \"Dad, I went out this afternoon to buy stationery, and Li Taohua and the others chased me. I had nowhere to run, so I hid in a dry well in the abandoned courtyard nearby. Brother Ye found me and brought me back.\"","Han Ye: \"...\"","Qin Qiao'an widened his eyes and whispered to her, \"Didn't we agree not to say anything?\"","Xiaxia looked back at him innocently—she never agreed to that.","When Qin Yuanzheng heard this, he set down his chopsticks seriously, looked at Xiaxia, and asked with concern, \"Did you get hurt?\"","Xiaxia shook her head: \"No.\"","Qin Yuanzheng let out a breath of relief: \"Good, as long as you're not hurt.\"","Otherwise, he wouldn't know how to explain to his wife.","Qin Yuanzheng was silent for a moment, then turned to Han Ye: \"You're thinking of going after those people for revenge, aren't you?\"","Han Ye: \"...\"","Han Ye said a bit indignantly, \"Why not? They dared to bully Xiaxia. What's wrong with me giving them a beating? They brought it on themselves.\"","Han Ye and Qin Qiao'an both expected Qin Yuanzheng to scold them and forbid them from going out to pick fights and cause trouble.","Instead, Qin Yuanzheng simply said, \"Watch your limits. Give them a slight lesson is enough—don't actually hurt anyone badly.\"","Han Ye: \"...\"","Qin Qiao'an: \"...\"","Xiaxia: \"...\"","All three thought they'd heard wrong and stared at Qin Yuanzheng in surprise.","But Qin Yuanzheng acted as if nothing had happened and said, \"What are you all staring at me for? Get back to eating.\"","Qin Qiao'an whispered to Xiaxia, \"See, Mom and Dad love you most. When I got bullied before, Dad made me apologize and forbade me from getting revenge. But when you get bullied, he lets us go avenge you.\"","Xiaxia looked at him and said ruthlessly, \"That's because you were the one who started it every single time. How is that the same?\"","Qin Qiao'an: \"...\"","...","Han Ye had said he would get revenge for Xiaxia. The very next morning, he took Qin Qiao'an and rode out on his bicycle.","Xiaxia was left at home. Han Ye, as her older brother, was stricter with her than Qiao Lanshu ever was.","When he left, he locked the compound gate and told Xiaxia to stay home and not go out.","After everything that happened yesterday, Xiaxia didn't plan on going out anyway.","So she stayed quietly at home.","Han Ye and Qin Qiao'an circled the area a few times outside, but didn't see Li Taohua or her brother Li Jian."]},{"number":262,"title":"Chapter 262: Qiao Lan Shu Is Back.","paragraphs":["Han Ye and Qin Qiao'an suddenly stopped going out these past few days.","What business? What making money?","They had tossed all of it aside.","None of that mattered anymore!","What mattered was taking revenge for their little sister!","Han Ye had been fearless since childhood. He was the undisputed bully of the military compound, unbeatable in a fight and such a headache that officers from every unit dreaded running into him.","Over the years, he had turned Qin Qiao'an into just as much of a menace. Qiao'an was already showing signs of inheriting Han Ye's ways.","The two of them were troublemakers no one dared provoke outside—and yet their one and only little sister had been bullied.","How could they possibly let that go?","Han Ye and Qin Qiao'an were so furious that they couldn't eat or sleep.","Even in their dreams, they were beating the hell out of those bastards who had bullied Xiaxia.","Their own sister had been bullied. Wasn't that the same as trampling all over their dignity?","If they could still put up with that, could they even call themselves men?","And so, for the past few days, the two brothers had been riding their bicycles around the streets and alleys near the military compound.","Based on Xiaxia's description, they went looking for the culprits one by one.","In less than two days, they had identified the six or seven people who had bullied Xiaxia.","It turned out that they were all from families living in the nearby neighborhoods. Two or three had stopped studying after graduating from junior high, while several others were still in school.","Though judging by the look of things, they had no intention of studying seriously. Every one of them was a street punk.","What was more, the brothers knew all of them.","Han Ye said to Qin Qiao'an, “It's just these few. We'll beat up every one of them we see. Let's see if they still dare bully Xiaxia after that!”","Qin Qiao'an nodded grimly. “We'll throw them into that dry well for a few hours too. I'd like to see whether they cry from fright.”","Han Ye nodded. Then, spotting several boys standing by the roadside, he said, “Let's go.”","The brothers rolled up their sleeves and walked toward the group.","Among them were two boys who had joined Li Taohua in bullying Xiaxia.","Han Ye knew these people. Even though he wasn't close to them, they all knew who he was.","When they saw Han Ye approaching, they grew nervous. One of them took the initiative to ask, “Han Ye, what do you want with us?”","Han Ye planted his hands on his hips, pointed at the two boys, and said, “I have a score to settle with those two. Anyone else want to join in?”","His expression was fierce, and his tone was cold. It was obvious that he had come looking for a fight.","Who in the surrounding neighborhoods didn't know how good Han Ye was in a brawl?","Who would dare take him on?","The others looked at the two boys. The boys were nervous too. They stared at Han Ye and asked, “Settle a score with us? We—we haven't offended you, have we?”","They sounded guilty as they spoke, but they were still clinging to the hope that they might get away with it.","Han Ye couldn't be bothered to waste words on them. He charged forward and kicked each of them, sending them sprawling to the ground. Then he said coldly, “You're so young, yet your memories are already this bad? Fine, I'll help you remember.”","With that, Qin Qiao'an rushed over as well, and the two brothers began pummeling the pair together.","In the end, they beat the two of them until they were crying for their parents before finally letting them go.","...","Of course, that wasn’t the end of it. There were several others besides those two.","For the next several days, the two brothers took revenge on anyone they came across.","They picked up every boy and beat him first, making sure not to hit them in the face but kicking them all over the body instead, until they wailed and begged for mercy.","Han Ye couldn’t very well beat up the girls, so he merely warned them not to bully Xiaxia again. Otherwise, he would beat them up too.","Han Ye was tall and powerfully built, and when he put on a fierce expression, he looked downright intimidating.","He scared all the girls into tears. One after another, they explained that Li Taohua had been the one who wanted to bully Xiaxia. They claimed they didn’t actually know Xiaxia and had no grudge against her.","In short, after they had all cried their hearts out, Han Ye and Qin Qiao’an couldn’t bring themselves to do anything more and let them go.","Han Ye and Qin Qiao’an had wanted to throw every one of them into the abandoned well.","But they were children from the military compound, and if they did something like that, it could easily be misconstrued. If it attracted the attention of investigators, that would be troublesome.","So, in the end, they reined themselves in somewhat.","...","But whether Li Taohua was afraid of retaliation or not, she didn’t show herself for a long time.","Xiaxia had never liked going out in the first place, and after this incident, she became even more of a homebody.","Han Ye and Qin Qiao’an wandered the streets and alleys for several days. With the start of the school term drawing near, they asked around and finally learned that Li Taohua’s family had moved away.","Both of Li Taohua’s parents had lost their jobs, so naturally, their home had been taken back by their work units.","This neighborhood consisted either of military compounds or housing complexes for various government departments. Once their home was repossessed, they could no longer live nearby and had no choice but to move away.","And so, the matter of avenging Xiaxia came to an end.","During the month Xiaxia spent at home reading, she had no idea that she had already become the local boss.","Everyone in the area paled at the mere mention of Xiaxia. They all knew that she was the one person in the neighborhood whom nobody could afford to provoke!","Anyone who dared bully her would be in for a month of retaliation!","September arrived, bringing autumn—and the start of the new school term.","Qiao Lanshu had finally completed her studies and passed the examination. She took the train back from the capital.","On the day she returned, Qin Yuanzheng took the day off and drove to the train station to pick her up.","The three children had all gone to school for the opening ceremony, and Qin Yuanzheng hadn’t told them that Qiao Lanshu was coming back.","He had planned from the beginning to go pick her up alone.","After all, if the children were there, neither he nor Qiao Lanshu would be able to do anything intimate.","Qiao Lanshu arrived in Longcheng at around three or four in the afternoon.","By the time she walked out of the train station, Qin Yuanzheng had already been waiting there for nearly half an hour.","The moment he saw Qiao Lanshu, Qin Yuanzheng stood where he was and stared at her for a while.","They had been apart for nearly half a year, and his wife seemed to have lost quite a bit of weight. Over the past few years, he had finally managed to put some healthy fullness on her, but now she looked noticeably thinner again.","Though... didn’t she seem fairer?","It was probably because she had spent those months studying, staying indoors every day and avoiding the sun, which had left her skin lighter.","His wife was still as beautiful as ever. She was especially lovely when she smiled, her eyes shining brightly and two adorable dimples appearing in her cheeks.","The more he looked at her, the prettier she seemed.","Qin Yuanzheng stood where he was, doing nothing but staring at Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu had spotted him from far away as she dragged along her luggage. She had thought Qin Yuanzheng would hurry over, give her a hug, and take her bags for her.","But what did he do? He simply stood there, staring at her with a foolish grin, without moving an inch.","Qiao Lanshu: “......”","She pushed her way out of the crowd, still carrying her luggage. The bags were quite heavy, since they were filled with gifts she had bought for the children.","She was exhausted, and seeing Qin Yuanzheng standing there like that immediately made her a little annoyed.","She dropped the luggage on the ground and stood there glaring at him, refusing to take another step.","Qin Yuanzheng, who had been staring at her the whole time, suddenly came back to his senses. Only then did he realize what was happening. He strode toward her, then pulled her tightly into his arms and quickly kissed her forehead.","“Why did you stop?” he asked in a low voice.","As he spoke, he naturally picked up Qiao Lanshu’s luggage with one hand and put his other arm around her, leading her forward.","Qiao Lanshu had still been a little angry, but seeing him like this, she could no longer bring herself to stay mad.","After all, they had been apart for several months, and she had missed her family too.","She had missed Qin Yuanzheng, and she had missed the children.","She glanced around and asked Qin Yuanzheng, “Where are the kids? Why didn’t they come to meet me?”","Without the slightest hint of guilt, Qin Yuanzheng replied, “They’ve started school. They’re all at school and didn’t have time to come.”","In fact, it wasn’t as though they couldn’t have asked the teacher for permission to take a short leave. He simply hadn’t wanted the children to come along.","Qiao Lanshu nodded in understanding. “That’s true. School has already started, and I’m getting back so late this year. I don’t even know what my work arrangements will be like. I have to report to the school first thing tomorrow morning.”","Qin Yuanzheng held her close and looked down at her. “You’re going to work tomorrow? Can’t you take a day off? Why are you in such a hurry?”","He had been planning to spend some quality time reconnecting with his wife.","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. “Of course not. After this training, the school will probably make some adjustments to my position. My responsibilities will be even heavier in the future, so I need to get there as soon as possible.”","At that moment, Qin Yuanzheng deeply understood Guan Wenjun’s previous frustration and resentment.","Because Zhong Mei wanted to open a shop and start a business, Guan Wenjun had poured out all his complaints to him. Once Zhong Mei got busy with the business, she had little time left for Guan Wenjun and often ignored him.","Now Qin Yuanzheng realized that his own wife also intended to make a name for herself in her career.","If she became busy and turned into a career-minded woman, wouldn’t she end up neglecting the family too?","What would he do then?","He couldn’t manage without his wife.","Qin Yuanzheng felt a little sour inside.","He took Qiao Lanshu to the car. Since he had driven there himself that day, Qiao Lanshu took the passenger seat.","Qin Yuanzheng sat there for a while but didn’t start the car right away.","Qiao Lanshu looked at him and asked in confusion, “What’s wrong? Why aren’t you driving?”","Although they hadn’t seen each other for several months, there was no awkwardness between them. After all, they were an old married couple. The moment they saw each other and exchanged a few words, that familiar feeling returned.","Qin Yuanzheng sat beside her, watching her. “I haven’t even settled accounts with you yet, sweetheart. I write you a letter every week, and what about you? Why do you only write once every half a month? Sometimes you go twenty days without writing. Don’t you miss me at all?”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","Qiao Lanshu was just about to explain when Qin Yuanzheng continued, “Looks like you’ve been living a pretty fulfilling, happy life over there. Have you made any friends? Men or women? How many men? How old are they?”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","She didn’t even have time to get a word in before Qin Yuanzheng went on, “They’re all educated people, intellectuals. You probably have much more in common with them, don’t you? They must be young too— in their twenties, around your age. You can probably talk to them easily. Unlike me. I’m uneducated, I’m older, and we have a generation gap, so you don’t want to write to me anymore. Is it because you’ve run out of things to say to me and can’t be bothered to pay me any attention?”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","She pinched the bridge of her nose and said, “Commander Qin, tone it down. Your jealousy is practically choking me.”","Qin Yuanzheng looked at her with an enigmatic smile. “What, am I too pungent for you? So all the men around you smelled sweet while you were studying over there?”","Qiao Lanshu couldn’t help laughing. “That’s not true at all. Stop letting your imagination run wild. I was only so busy because the coursework was overwhelming. I was afraid I wouldn’t be able to finish it and Professor Rong would be disappointed in me.”","Qin Yuanzheng raised an eyebrow as he thought of that woman. “Professor Rong values you, so she assigned you all that heavy coursework?”","He muttered, “How is that repaying kindness with cruelty? I saved her granddaughter, and yet she’s tormenting you with your studies.”","Qiao Lanshu smiled. “Professor Rong said she wants me to apply to her graduate program. Oh, right—she’ll be coming to Wencheng University next year as a visiting professor. I’ll be able to apply to her department then.”","Qin Yuanzheng: “...”","For a moment, Qin Yuanzheng didn’t know what to say.","He already thought his wife was busy enough. For the past two years, she had been so occupied with work that even the time she spent chatting and cuddling with him in the evenings had become scarce.","And once she started graduate school and became a scholar, wouldn’t she be even busier, researching this and that every day?","But Qin Yuanzheng couldn’t stop her from pursuing her dreams.","After all, Qiao Lanshu had never complained about how busy he was in the military, how often he was unable to look after the family, or how he would occasionally leave on missions and disappear for several days at a time.","So, after a moment of silence, Qin Yuanzheng said, “Keep it up, sweetheart. I believe you’ll definitely get in.”","His wife was simply that talented. Whenever she truly set her mind to something, she was sure to accomplish it.","Qiao Lanshu looked at him and asked, “Commander Qin, you don’t seem very happy.”","Qin Yuanzheng gave her a half-smile. “How would I dare be unhappy? I’m absolutely terrified.”","With that, he started the car and drove his little wife home.","Qiao Lanshu explained to him on the way, “I really was too busy with my studies. I wasn’t deliberately ignoring your letters. Once, I was writing a reply to you, but I fell asleep halfway through. When I woke up in the middle of the night, my whole face was covered in ink.”","Seeing her act so pitiful, Qin Yuanzheng’s heart immediately ached for her. “No wonder you’ve gotten so thin. Now that you’re back, you need to eat properly and put on some weight. Just look at your face—it’s lost all its fullness.”","Qiao Lanshu had indeed lost weight, but she didn’t think it was a big deal. After resting at home for a few days, she would fill out again.","After they returned home, Qiao Lanshu sighed contentedly. “Home really is the best. I haven’t been back in so long—I’ve missed it.”","Then she turned to look at him. “By the way, how have the children been behaving lately? Han Ye and An’an haven’t caused you any trouble, have they?”","Qin Yuanzheng carried Qiao Lanshu’s luggage into the bedroom. Then he came back out, wrapped his arms around her, and buried his face against her neck for a deep breath. In a low voice, he said, “Forget about that for now. The children haven’t gotten out of school yet, so let’s spend some time together first. I’ve been holding it in for months—I’m practically dying here.”","Qiao Lanshu pushed his head away. “Hey, wait. We haven’t even taken a bath yet.”","Qin Yuanzheng pressed her against the wall and murmured, “Just give me one kiss first.”","With that, he pulled her close and kissed her.","The couple had been apart for a long time, and it wasn’t only Qin Yuanzheng who had missed their intimacy—Qiao Lanshu had missed it too.","So they held each other and kissed for quite a while before Qin Yuanzheng finally let her go and went to the kitchen to heat some water for their baths."]},{"number":263,"title":"Chapter 263: Puppy Love","paragraphs":["The children knew Qiao Lanshu was coming back today, but they didn't know what time.","So the moment school let out, the three siblings forgot about everything else. Han Ye pedaled his old twenty-eight inch bicycle as fast as his long legs would carry him, with Qin Qiao'an riding on the back and Xiaxia perched on the front. The bike bell rang all the way from the street to their front door.","Before Han Ye even came to a full stop, Qin Qiao'an dashed inside, shouting excitedly: \"Mom, Mom, Mom, are you back?\"","Qiao Lanshu had already heard the commotion and came out of the house with a smile: \"I'm back. Did you all get out of school?\"","Qin Qiao'an's eyes lit up the moment he saw his mother. He tossed his schoolbag into the yard without a second thought, and it landed right in the vegetable patch.","Qin Yuanzheng, standing behind Qiao Lanshu, raised an eyebrow and shot Qin Qiao'an a look that said trouble was brewing.","But Qin Qiao'an was far too excited at that moment to spare even a glance at his father.","He dashed over and threw his arms around Qiao Lanshu: \"Mom, you're finally back! We missed you so much!\"","Qiao Lanshu nearly toppled over from the impact.","She quickly steadied herself and hugged Qin Qiao'an back, patting his sweaty forehead as she said: \"An'an, you've grown so tall in the six months I've been away.\"","Qin Qiao'an had just started the fourth grade, and he was already a big kid now. At nearly five-foot-two, he was the tallest in his class, sitting in the very last row. Standing next to Qiao Lanshu, he was almost as tall as she was.","Qiao Lanshu said with pride: \"And you've gotten even more handsome.\"","As Qin Qiao'an grew older, he looked more and more like Qin Yuanzheng. His complexion took after Qiao Lanshu — fair and light — but his face and features were all Qin Yuanzheng's. Even his hands and feet were big like his father's. At only ten years old, he was already tall and sturdy, and he was bound to grow into a real handsome young man someday.","Xiaxia lagged behind a step, then ran up to Qiao Lanshu breathless and sweaty, looking up at her with sparkling eyes: \"Mom, I missed you so much.\"","With that, Xiaxia nudged Qin Qiao'an aside a little and wrapped her arms around Qiao Lanshu herself.","Qin Qiao'an quietly moved to Qiao Lanshu's left side, giving up the right side to his sister.","Both siblings clung to Qiao Lanshu, refusing to let go.","Han Ye picked up Qin Qiao'an's schoolbag, dusted it off, and walked over happily: \"Mom, I missed you too.\"","Before Qiao Lanshu could say anything, Qin Yuanzheng spoke in a low voice: \"You're practically a grown man now. Don't you go joining in and hugging your Auntie Qiao.\"","Han Ye was nearly fifteen and already over six feet tall, looking almost like a full-grown adult. If he tried to come over and hug Qiao Lanshu, Qin Yuanzheng would kick him.","Han Ye rubbed his nose and muttered: \"I never said I was going to hug her.\"","He couldn't help but feel nostalgic for the old days.","Back when he was little, Qiao Lanshu had held him plenty of times.","But when he was small, he could get away with acting cute and shameless. Not anymore — he'd get a beating now.","Qiao Lanshu put an arm around each of the two kids and said: \"You're all home at just the right time. I brought gifts for all of you. Come take a look.\"","As soon as the children heard about gifts, they all cheered and followed Qiao Lanshu into the house.","Qiao Lanshu unzipped her duffel bag and pulled out a complete set of Jin Yong's martial arts novels — all ten volumes, brand new and beautifully packaged.","Xiaxia's eyes lit up instantly, and she pounced over: \"Mom, did you get these for me?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded with a smile: \"I was going to get you the San Yan Er Pai collection, but I thought about it, and you're still a bit young for those. They might be too much of a challenge. Why not try some martial arts novels instead? You love those, don't you?\"","Xiaxia nodded eagerly: \"I do! I absolutely love them!\"","She didn't have much pocket money these days, and she had too many books she wanted to read, so she'd gotten a library card and went borrowing books every single week.","But Jin Yong's martial arts novels were way too popular everyone wanted them and they were always in short supply.","Half the time she could find the first volume but not the second, or sometimes she couldn't find the first at all but the second one would show up. Either way, she could never get through a full series smoothly.","And now her mother had gone and bought her all ten volumes at once. Xiaxia said from the bottom of her heart: \"Mom, you're so good to me.\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at Xiaxia and shook his head. This girl took after her mother — when she was truly moved, all she could say was 'you're so good to me,' nothing else.","Han Ye crouched beside them, watching Xiaxia clutch her books with a look of deep gratitude, and said to Qiao Lanshu: \"Mom, why did you get her so many books? You don't know, she's been reading herself silly lately. All day she walks around like a bookworm, totally spacey...\"","Xiaxia shot him a glare: \"You're the spacey one. You're the silly one.\"","Han Ye pointed at her: \"See? That right there is you acting silly.\"","Xiaxia turned her head away and ignored him.","She couldn't beat Han Ye in a verbal fight, so she decided to just stop talking and focus on tearing open her gift.","Qiao Lanshu smiled as she watched them bicker. Qin Qiao'an tugged on her arm, all worked up: \"Mom, Mom, what did you get me? Let me see!\"","Qiao Lanshu pulled out a box set of illustrated picture books based on the Four Great Classical Novels and handed them to Qin Qiao'an: \"Here. You don't like reading proper books, but you love picture books, so I got you a complete set.\"","Qin Qiao'an grabbed them excitedly: \"Mom, how did you know I love these?\"","Then he glanced at Qin Yuanzheng, hugged the comic books close to his chest, and said: \"Dad, Mom bought these for me, so you can't scold me for wasting time.\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at Qiao Lanshu with a hint of helplessness.","Qin Qiao'an's grades had always been so-so scattered somewhere in the middle of the pack. Qin Yuanzheng wanted to push him to do better in school, which was why he had banned comic books like these.","But Qiao Lanshu spoiled them. She believed that besides studying, there were plenty of other pastimes worth exploring — like reading novels, comic books, poetry, or essays.","Being a teacher, Qiao Lanshu was well-educated, and when it came to the children's schooling, Qin Yuanzheng always deferred to her.","He teased: \"No wonder the bag felt so heavy. Turns out it was packed full of books.\"","Qiao Lanshu laughed: \"It's not just books. There's a radio in there too.\"","She took out a small, compact radio and handed it to Han Ye: \"Here, Han Ye. I got this for you. You can keep it in your room to listen to the news and radio programs. Oh, and you can even use it to practice English. There are English channels and military channels. You can listen to those.\"","Qin Qiao'an jumped up immediately, shouting: \"Bro, bro! We can also listen to Teresa Teng! We can buy cassette tapes tomorrow!\"","Han Ye hadn't expected Qiao Lanshu to buy him something so expensive, and he felt genuinely happy.","It was clear that auntie Qiao loved him a lot — his gift was the most expensive one of all. Han Ye was secretly delighted.","He said to Qin Qiao'an: \"Alright, tomorrow we'll head to the record store and pick up a bunch of tapes.\"","The two brothers excitedly went off to fiddle with the radio.","Meanwhile, Xiaxia clutched her books like precious treasures and headed to her room.","Qin Yuanzheng crouched down next to Qiao Lanshu and said with a helpless smile: \"Why did you buy them a radio? They'll probably stay up all night listening to music instead of sleeping.\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said: \"Don't worry. Han Ye knows where to draw the line.\"","Qin Yuanzheng lowered his voice and asked: \"That must have cost you a pretty penny. Do you still have any money left on you?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"Yes, I got second place in my class, with a two hundred yuan prize.\"","As she spoke, she took out a men's watch with a Shanghai-brand movement, took Qin Yuanzheng's hand, and slipped the watch onto his wrist, saying softly, \"Didn't your watch break? You've had it fixed so many times. Why not just replace it? I bought you a new one—see if it fits?\"","Qin Yuanzheng hadn't expected to get a gift himself, and a smile broke out on his face before he could stop it.","He didn't scold Qiao Lanshu for spending money.","Because he also loved it when Qiao Lanshu bought him gifts.","He stretched out his arm to look at it, grinning. \"It fits. Of course it fits—my wife picked it out.\"","Qiao Lanshu said, \"Glad you like it. I was worried you wouldn't. This one was bought all the way from the capital, so there's no returning it.\"","Qin Yuanzheng pulled Qiao Lanshu into his arms and kissed her on the cheek, saying, \"My wife is the best. You spoil me the most, don't you?\"","Before Qiao Lanshu could say anything, she looked up and saw Xiaxia standing at the bedroom door, watching them with a completely expressionless face.","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Xiaxia said very seriously, \"Go on, you two. I didn't see anything.\"","Then Xiaxia turned and went back to her room, gently closing the door behind her.","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu jabbed him with her elbow. \"See? I told you to be more careful.\"","The kids were still little!","Qin Yuanzheng coughed and stood up, saying, \"It's fine. We're affectionate all the time—they've grown up watching us. They're used to it by now.\"","Qiao Lanshu tidied up her luggage, then went with Qin Yuanzheng to cook dinner.","The whole family had a lively meal together.","After dinner, Han Ye didn't go back to the Han family. He actually hadn't been back in months. From the time Qiao Lanshu left for the capital for training until now, he hadn't returned to the Han residence, so now that Qiao Lanshu was back, he really should go home for a visit.","But Qiao Lanshu had bought him a radio, so he heartlessly forgot all about Han Wenlin and stayed at Qiao Lanshu's place to keep playing with his radio.","...","The new school year began, and all the kids moved up a grade. Qin Qiao'an entered fourth grade, while Xiaxia, having skipped a grade, went into third grade.","Unfortunately, she couldn't skip two grades, or she'd have been in the same class as Qin Qiao'an.","Still, being in third grade was good, because there was no Teacher Qian in third grade—all the teachers were new, and they were very kind to her. Knowing she was a grade-skipper, they doted on her.","And so the kids started school without a hitch.","As for Qiao Lanshu, her position had been adjusted—she'd been promoted to head of the teaching research group. As the new semester began, she had new work to do.","She was so busy from the start that she barely had time to cook for the kids. Qin Yuanzheng came home early every day to make their meals.","Sometimes he couldn't make it back, so he'd have the kids eat at the police station cafeteria. Han Wenlin was the bureau chief, after all, so he'd cover their meal costs.","The peaceful, busy days lasted only a few days before Qiao Lanshu was once again summoned as a parent—something she hadn't experienced in a long time.","When Qiao Lanshu heard that a teacher wanted to see her, she felt a flicker of nervousness out of habit.","She asked the messenger at the gate, \"Which grade's teacher is looking for me?\"","It couldn't be Xiaxia again, could it?","Xiaxia was such a good kid, and her new homeroom teacher really liked her.","The gatekeeper smiled. \"Oh, it's from the middle school next door. They said your son has some issues at school and needs a parent to come in and help sort things out.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu let out a sigh of relief. It wasn't Xiaxia.","Then her worry kicked back in. Not Xiaxia—it was Han Ye, who was in middle school?","Wouldn't that mean the problem was even more serious?","If it was Xiaxia, she'd have some idea of what was going on, because she knew Xiaxia was very well-behaved and would never cause trouble.","But if it was Han Ye, there was no telling what the situation was.","Qiao Lanshu hurriedly asked her department head for leave and rushed over to the middle school next door.","The school teachers had thought to come find her, probably because Han Wenlin wasn't at his office—he'd gone out on business.","Being a police bureau chief kept him pretty busy. Han Wenlin still wasn't married, and he didn't pay much attention to Han Ye, precisely because he was so busy he often couldn't find the time.","Qiao Lanshu wore a light blue shirt and black pants, with her hair pinned up at the back of her head—a crisp, efficient look.","The teachers at the middle school campus didn't interact much with those at the high school, but most of them knew each other.","So when Qiao Lanshu walked into the teachers' office, Han Ye's homeroom teacher, Zhao Yanfang, stood up and called out, \"Teacher Qiao, over here.\"","Qiao Lanshu came over but didn't see Han Ye.","She walked to Zhao Yanfang's desk, her face full of concern, and asked, \"Teacher Zhao, did Han Ye get into trouble again? He didn't get into another fight at school, did he?\"","Back when Han Ye was in elementary school in Longcheng, according to Han Wenlin, he'd made the whole school a mess—arguing and fighting every day, becoming a notorious problem student.","The teachers would go out of their way to avoid him.","After all, he was a little demon—and his father was the police bureau chief—so no one dared to mess with him.","Han Wenlin had even come to Qiao Lanshu to complain and asked her to talk some sense into the boy, because apart from Qiao Lanshu, Han Ye wouldn't listen to anyone.","Teacher Zhao shook her head and sighed. \"If it were just a fight, I wouldn't have called you in.\"","After all, Han Ye was fifteen now and knew his limits. He'd hit people hard enough to make them cry, but he wouldn't actually injure them to the point where parents had to get involved.","Teacher Zhao would just make him stand in the corner, scold him, or have him do extra chores, and that usually did the trick.","But today's problem, Teacher Zhao couldn't handle—it required notifying the parents.","She lowered her voice and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Teacher Qiao, here's what happened. Han Ye—well, he was romantically involved with a girl in his class. And the love letter she wrote him—he posted it on the blackboard. The whole class saw it. The girl ran home crying, and afterward, her best friend testified that Han Ye was the one who put the letter up, and also said that Han Ye was behaving improperly toward the girl.\"","Having a relationship with her, acting improperly, and then treating her like this—it made the girl so angry she went home crying and didn't come to school today.","Qiao Lanshu frowned. \"When did this happen?\"","Zhao Yanfang sighed. \"Yesterday afternoon. There was a stir in class, but since it was almost time to leave, it didn't blow up. This morning, that girl didn't show up and didn't ask for leave, so I asked around and found out what had happened. That's when I called you in right away.\"","Qiao Lanshu was silent for a moment, then asked, \"Where's Han Ye? Get him over here and ask him.\"","Zhao Yanfang lowered her voice. \"I already asked. Han Ye says he wasn't in a relationship, but several girls in the class testified that they'd seen him with that girl multiple times—sometimes going to the hill behind the school together, sometimes on the sports field. It looked like their relationship was anything but ordinary.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\""]},{"number":264,"title":"Chapter 264: Educating Children","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu really hadn’t expected that, before she even turned thirty, she’d be worrying about her son’s early romance issues.","Even though this son wasn’t her biological child.","But she still counted as Han Ye’s guardian.","After all, all the teachers here knew that Han Ye had acknowledged her as his mother.","So whenever anything came up about Han Ye, as long as they couldn’t reach Han Wenlin, they’d come to Qiao Lanshu about it.","Before, they’d only talked to her about schoolwork, and those were minor matters.","But now, out of nowhere, it was straight to a puppy love situation.","Qiao Lanshu reached up and pressed a hand to her forehead, saying with a headache: “I’ll go ask him about it in a bit, see what’s really going on.”","Zhao Yanfang nodded and said in a low voice: “Han Ye’s personality, well, he’s a bit hard to discipline, but he’s very popular at school. He gets love notes passed to him from girls all the time during class. When it comes to early romance, it’s not exactly impossible.”","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu said: “Even though he won’t be controlled, he’s still sensible and steady. There might be more to this. That girl didn’t come today, did she? Why don’t we wait until she comes and ask her then?”","Zhao Yanfang stood up, gathering her things as she spoke: “Teacher Qiao, since we’re already so familiar with each other, I won’t entertain you as a guest. During the next break, go find Han Ye and ask him. I need to go to that girl’s home for a visit and see what her situation is.”","Zhao Yanfang slung her bag over her shoulder, put on her hat, and added: “Kids at this age care the most about saving face, especially girls. Having her love letter pasted up in public like that, and being mocked by the whole class—that’s really a heavy blow. I won’t feel at ease unless I go check on her.”","Qiao Lanshu said: “Alright, Teacher Zhao, you go ahead then. I’ll go find Han Ye and ask him about it now.”","Actually, Teacher Zhao had already questioned Han Ye earlier.","Han Ye firmly insisted that he wasn’t in a relationship, but when asked about anything else, he refused to say more.","For example—had he written back to the girl?","Had he gone to the hills behind the school with her?","And again—what was that business about the girls saying he’d acted like a hooligan? Had he touched one of them?","Han Ye wouldn’t say a word about any of it. Zhao Yanfang could do nothing with him, so she could only call Qiao Lanshu over.","After Zhao Yanfang left for her home visit, Qiao Lanshu waited until the class bell rang, then went to the door of Han Ye’s classroom.","Han Ye was tall. Walking beside his classmates, he stood out like a crane among chickens.","He was walking out of the classroom with a few male classmates, arms slung over each other’s shoulders, when he notices Qiao Lanshu standing in the hallway in one glance.","Han Ye’s footsteps faltered. Smart as he was, he knew exactly why Qiao Lanshu was here.","The smile on his face instantly vanished. He scratched his head and walked over to Qiao Lanshu with a guilty look: “Qiao, Qiao Teacher, you’re looking for me?”","Qiao Lanshu was almost irritated into laughter.","This kid knew he’d done something wrong, which was why he was suddenly calling her “Teacher Qiao.”","Qiao Lanshu straightened up and looked at him with a stern expression: “Student Han Ye, come with me for a moment.”","Han Ye: “...”","A few of the boys beside him looked at him with puzzled expressions, raising their eyebrows at him.","One of them said: “Han Ye, she’s not even our teacher. Why’re you going with her?”","Han Ye kicked him and muttered a curse: “Scram. She’s my mom!”","The boys: “...”","They were all absolutely stunned.","They all stared at Qiao Lanshu from a distance.","This was Han Ye’s mother?","She didn’t look like it. Saying she was his older sister would have been far more convincing.","Han Ye followed behind Qiao Lanshu until they reached the corner of the staircase.","Qiao Lanshu looked at Han Ye, who was a head taller than she was. She studied him in silence for a few seconds.","His features were striking. He’d inherited some of Han Wenlin’s ruggedness, but his eyes, brows, and mouth didn’t resemble Han Wenlin’s at all—probably they took after his mother.","He was tall, broad-shouldered, long-legged, skilled in a fight, and unbeaten across the entire school.","It was pretty normal for girls to like him.","Qiao Lanshu thought about that, then asked him: “Han Ye, are you in a relationship?”","Han Ye: “...”","His face instantly flushed crimson. He argued loudly: “Of course not! Mom, how could I possibly be in a relationship? All the girls in my class are ugly.”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","She shot Han Ye a glare and scolded him: “You can’t say things like that about girls. That’s very rude.”","Han Ye looked downcast after being criticized by Qiao Lanshu. He said: “Anyway, I’m not dating anyone. In the future I’m going to join the army anyway. Why would I date anyone now? Wouldn’t that be wasting time?”","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu felt relieved at once.","So she said: “Then explain to me what happened with that love letter, and what’s going on with that girl.”","Han Ye said with a disgusted look: “Anyway—anyway, it’s not that big a deal. That love letter wasn’t posted by me. Who knows which jerk did it? And besides, she didn’t hide her own love letter properly, leaving it on the desk where people could see it. She’s got some blame in this too, right? Mom, this really isn’t my fault. I’m the victim here.”","Qiao Lanshu: “Then with that being the case, had you received her love letter before?”","Han Ye: “...”","Han Ye rubbed his nose guiltily: “Maybe... probably? I don’t remember clearly.”","Qiao Lanshu stared at him: “Say that again?”","Han Ye quickly explained: “It’s too many. I have way too many love letters in my desk. I threw them all out. How am I supposed to know if it was hers or not?”","Even Qiao Lanshu, who had such a good temper, was getting worked up by him.","She asked: “You just threw them away like that so carelessly? What if someone else picked them up and read them?”","Han Ye scratched his head nervously: “I didn’t think that far ahead at the time. I treated them as trash.”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","She finally understood why that girl’s love letter had ended up pasted onto the blackboard.","Even if he hadn’t done it himself, he was definitely not unconnected to it.","Qiao Lanshu also felt a bit guilty herself.","Han Ye wasn’t her biological son, nor did he live at her house permanently. He bounced back and forth between the two households.","Because of that, Qiao Lanshu often didn’t discipline him much.","Which naturally meant she’d neglected teaching him about these adolescent issues.","Han Ye had no biological mother. Han Wenlin was busy with work. And Han Ye was far too independent—whenever he hit a problem, he handled it alone.","More often than not, his personality was unruly and arrogant. He came from a well-off family, Han Wenlin spoiled him and would cover things up for him no matter what.","That was what had cultivated this fearlessness in him, this tendency to look down on everyone else.","Qiao Lanshu was silent for a long moment.","Inwardly, Han Ye felt anxious. He asked in a low voice: “Mom, is this really that serious? This isn’t a big deal, right? It’s just that the letter got seen by people. I’m not afraid of being laughed at. Why should she be? Just take it in stride, right?”","Qiao Lanshu shook her head: “You think it’s no big deal, because you’ve got thick skin.”","Han Ye: “...”","Qiao Lanshu went on: “That girl has thin skin, so of course she’s going to feel upset.”","Han Ye muttered, unconvinced: “I think if it were Xiaxia, she wouldn’t care. Xiaxia’s got a heart that’s pretty strong.”","Qiao Lanshu was noncommittal. She said, “You need to understand that people are all different. You have to learn to put yourself in others’ shoes and to respect them. When you receive love letters from others and you don’t want them, you can take them home and put them away, burn them, or tear them up — any of those is fine. But you can’t toss them into the school trash can. Understand? Everyone at school is your peer, and most of them know each other. If someone sees that, it’s really not good.”","Qiao Lanshu sighed and added, “Also, they’re saying you went up to the back hill alone with that girl. Is that true?”","Hearing Qiao Lanshu ask that, Han Ye felt even more dejected.","He nodded and answered honestly, “Yeah, it happened, but only once. She asked me to go — said she had something to tell me. I had nothing better to do at the time, so I went.”","What had actually happened was pretty simple: Han Ye went to the back hill with the girl, they exchanged a few words, all about schoolwork. Han Ye couldn’t even clearly remember what was said — it was all completely trivial.","On the way back down to the classroom, the girl tripped on a rock. Han Ye’s reflexes were faster than his brain. He reached out and pulled her up.","And in other people’s eyes, it looked like they were hugging.","A few classmates who were close to that girl started teasing them about dating and told Han Ye to keep his hands to himself, saying it looked bad.","Han Ye found the whole thing utterly ridiculous.","When Qiao Lanshu heard him explain, she was even more speechless.","She asked in a low voice, “Why didn’t you tell me about this earlier?”","At the time, there was a strict crackdown going on, and they were very strict about male-female relationships. Even students couldn’t mess around. If things got blown out of proportion, it wouldn’t be good for anyone.","Han Ye said with an innocent look, “It’s just a small thing. What was there to say?”","He didn’t think being teased about puppy love was any big deal at all.","What he cared about far more was the fighting with other kids getting back to his family.","So he was constantly on guard against those rivals. He had no time at all for the girls’ romantic little dramas.","Han Ye frowned, a little impatiently, and said, “Women are just trouble! Oh no — not you, and not Xiaxia. Every other woman is a bundle of trouble.”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","Han Ye felt like he was developing a fear of women. From now on, if he saw any girls, he’d stay far away from them.","Otherwise, this kind of thing would happen again, and it would just be a total headache.","With all the questions asked and answered, Qiao Lanshu felt relieved.","As long as Han Ye hadn’t actually been in a relationship and broken some girl’s heart, everything was fine.","She trusted Han Ye quite a bit. He had no reason to lie to her.","That had always been his personality since he was little. If he couldn’t do something or didn’t want to admit something, he’d just keep his mouth shut and refuse to speak.","But the moment he did speak, then what he said was definitely the truth.","Just then, the bell for class rang, so Qiao Lanshu said to him, “Alright, go back to class. I’ll come by this afternoon and talk to Teacher Zhao about this. This isn’t entirely your fault. I’ll explain things to her.”","Hearing that, Han Ye immediately cheered up. “Thanks, Mom. I’m off.”","With that, he ran back to his classroom.","Qiao Lanshu also left the middle school section and returned to the high school next door to work.","After she became a department head, her teaching load had lightened. She only had a few classes a week now, spending most of her time in the office. When she got back to work, her colleagues in the office asked where she’d been, and she mentioned Han Ye’s situation to them.","She said helplessly, “The kid’s growing up. I’m going to have to give him some education about adolescence soon.”","A female colleague sitting in front of her said, “Oh dear, you’d better be careful about this kind of thing. What if that girl took an interest in your son’s family background and deliberately tried to get close to him?”","Qiao Lanshu paused. She set down her fountain pen and said hesitantly, “That shouldn’t be the case, right? Around here, these are all dormitories for various work units. There are plenty of cadre kids...”","The colleague held her water cup, shook her head, and said gossipily, “You know it’s plenty, not all of them! Over the last few years, there have been a lot of migrants. In our school, there are still some kids from really poor families — they rent rooms, or live in makeshift sheds they built themselves.”","Students like that were still quite rare.","Because in this era, if a family couldn’t even afford a proper house and couldn’t put food on the table, the parents wouldn’t even consider their children’s education.","That’s why everyone wanted to be a college professor or a high school teacher — because starting from high school, the students’ overall quality was already quite high. Most of them came from decent families, and they were polite and sensible.","But the children of poor families mostly finished middle school and then went off to work.","Or, some couldn’t even finish middle school — a few dropped out after elementary school and went to earn money.","Still, starting in ’86, after the country introduced nine-year compulsory education, more and more kids were able to attend middle school.","Qiao Lanshu fell into thought and said, “Han Ye comes from a single-parent family, and his temper isn’t great either. If things really were like that, then that girl would have picked the wrong person.”","Qiao Lanshu’s colleague lowered her voice and said to her:","“Last year, a relative’s kid was dating someone in middle school. He started in eighth grade, and in ninth grade, he kissed the girl, and someone saw them. Then guess what happened? The girl said his family had to arrange a job for her, or she’d report him for hooliganism and make sure he couldn’t get into high school. The boy’s family was afraid the whole thing would blow up and ruin his future, so in the end, they arranged a job for the girl! Every year during the New Year, the old folks in my family bring this story up again, teaching the kids to find partners of equal family standing — not to go after girls from the countryside, or else the whole family would be dragged into trouble.”","When Qiao Lanshu heard that, she was somewhat shocked.","She had spent half a year training in the capital, her head full of work and study, rarely gossiping with colleagues.","When Han Ye’s issue came up, she hadn’t thought about it from that angle.","But her female colleague was right. Han Ye came from a single-parent family and had a bad temper, but his father was the director of the provincial public security bureau, and he was the only child.","If some girl got tangled up with him and then came to cause a scene, then knowing Han Wenlin’s personality, he’d probably find it annoying and also worry about Han Ye’s reputation being affected.","After all, Han Ye was going to join the military in the future — he was set on that path.","His reputation mattered a great deal.","But in the end, Han Wenlin would probably also end up finding that girl a job.","For someone like Han Wenlin, that really was a small matter.","Qiao Lanshu thought it over and said with a serious expression, “Sister Lan, you make a good point. I’ll keep an eye out over the next couple of days. If that really is the situation, I’ll make plans early to deal with it.”","Sister Lan reassured her, saying, “Don’t worry. As long as they didn’t actually hug or kiss, then it’s not a big deal.”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","The thing was, it did sound like they had hugged?"]},{"number":265,"title":"Chapter 265: Parents Making a Scene","paragraphs":["Regarding Han Ye being suspected of having a crush on a classmate, Han Ye himself didn't take it seriously at all.","Qiao Lanshu, at first, also didn't think it was a big deal.","After all, it really wasn't anything major—teenage boys and girls developing feelings for each other, having crushes, passing notes, writing love letters—that was all perfectly normal.","But if the other party had some other intentions, well, that was a different story.","Qiao Lanshu worked for a while, and two hours later, she left the school and walked over to the teacher's office of the neighboring middle school.","Zhao Yanfang had just returned from her home visit as well.","The two met in the corridor outside the office, and Zhao Yanfang's expression wasn't looking too good.","Qiao Lanshu studied her face, walked over, and asked, \"Teacher Zhao, you're back from the home visit?\"","Teacher Zhao nodded, looking a bit weary. She walked closer and said in a low voice, \"Teacher Qiao, let’s talk in the office.\"","The two entered the office and found chairs to sit on.","Teacher Zhao picked up her cup, took a sip of water, then let out a sigh and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Teacher Qiao, have you talked to Han Ye yet?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded and relayed what she had discussed with Han Ye, saying, \"He said that girl is just a regular classmate to him. Going to the hillside together was just having some casual conversation—it wasn’t the kind of relationship everyone is imagining.\"","She didn’t mention that Han Ye had said the girls in the class were ugly and that he would never get involved with any of them.","Han Ye was already a handful; Qiao Lanshu figured she ought to cover for him a bit, otherwise he’d end up offending too many people.","Qiao Lanshu added, \"Also, he only helped the girl up because she had fallen—he didn’t do anything improper to her. Teacher Zhao, I trust Han Ye’s character, and you know him as his homeroom teacher as well. He’s not the kind of person who lies, nor is he someone who would do something and then be all wishy-washy about admitting it. If he really had something going on with a girl, he would have owned up to it right away.\"","Aside from Han Ye’s personality, no one at home kept tabs on him anyway—he had plenty of freedom.","If he was having a little romance, so what? Han Wenlin couldn’t discipline him anyway, or rather, he couldn’t control him. What difference would it make if he admitted it?","Since he denied it, then there must be nothing going on.","Teacher Zhao listened to Qiao Lanshu’s explanation, sighed again, and said, \"I went to visit Liu Wenqiu’s family today. She stayed locked in her room, refusing to come out, crying the whole time. Her parents both work on construction sites—they’re not educated and can barely speak Mandarin. I tried to communicate with them, but we just couldn’t make any headway.\"","Saying this, Teacher Zhao looked a bit embarrassed.","She was a young teacher who had just been assigned here from out of town, and she hadn’t yet gotten used to the climate, nor could she fully understand the regional dialect.","But she only said, \"People in her family aren’t easy to reason with. I gave Liu Wenqiu three days off, and she’ll come back to school on Monday. I’ll also tell the other students in class that they’re not allowed to tease her about this anymore. Teacher Qiao, don’t worry—it’s not a big deal. However, when Liu Wenqiu comes back to school on Monday, I hope Han Ye can apologize to her.\"","Whether or not Han Ye was at fault, this matter involved him.","Having him apologize would also help protect the girl’s fragile self-esteem.","And besides, Han Ye was the leader of the troublemakers in the class—if he took a stand, it would do more than ten lectures from Teacher Zhao ever could.","Qiao Lanshu nodded at once. \"No problem. I’ll go tell that brat when I get back.\"","After they finished talking, both of them assumed this matter was pretty much settled.","Qiao Lanshu went back to work, and after clocking out, she headed to the supply and marketing cooperative to buy groceries.","Han Ye, after school, went to the elementary school as usual to pick up Qin Qiao'an and Qin Qiaoxia, and the three of them walked home together.","On the way, Xiaxia suddenly said, \"I saw Li Taohua at school today.\"","Li Taohua was in second grade now, while Xiaxia had skipped a grade and was in third.","Qin Qiao'an immediately asked, \"You saw her? Did she bully you again?\"","Xiaxia shook her head, looking rather smug. \"Of course not! But last time she had people chase me, and I had to hide in a dry well. So this time, I put a caterpillar on her shoulder.\"","Qin Qiao'an was speechless. \"Xiaxia, are you still a three-year-old? Even two-year-olds don't pull pranks like that, do they?\"","Xiaxia: \"...\"","Han Ye cracked his knuckles and asked, \"She didn’t mess with you today, did she? Didn’t say anything bad about you?\"","Xiaxia shrugged and said, \"No. When she saw me, she was scared out of her wits. I guess you guys scared them all last summer, so now they’re too afraid to do anything.\"","Xiaxia then turned to Qin Qiao'an and said, \"I used one of those fuzzy white caterpillars. She got a rash all over her neck and face. She couldn’t even finish class—she got taken to the office to apply medicine. I even saw her when school let out.\"","Xiaxia looked very pleased with herself.","She had already disliked Li Taohua when Li Taohua had used a desk to shove her before.","She had pretty much let it go since Mom and her brother had already avenged her.","But then Li Taohua went and had people chase her again.","Even though Xiaxia had always been a good-natured girl and wasn’t one to hold grudges, that experience in the dry well hadn’t been pleasant, so Xiaxia bore a grudge against Li Taohua now.","As she spoke, she pulled out a clear bag from her pocket with three or four caterpillars still squirming inside. \"Look, it’s this kind.\"","The moment the two boys saw those bugs, they let out a yelp and jumped several feet back.","Han Ye said sternly, \"Qin Qiaoxia, throw those bugs away right now!\"","Qin Qiao'an looked terrified. \"Xiaxia, why don’t you just go back and read a book or something? Don’t touch these kinds of bugs.\"","These caterpillars were poisonous. Wherever they stung, it would itch like crazy—similar to mosquito bites in the mountains, swelling up into big welts that spread in patches and were unbearably itchy.","It was horrifying.","Back when Han Ye was at his most mischievous, he had once placed one of these caterpillars on the teacher’s podium. That day, he was punished by having to stand through an entire class, and his parents were called in.","Xiaxia watched the horror-stricken faces of the two boys and quietly tossed the bugs into the bushes by the roadside.","Qin Qiao'an was still grossed out, rubbing his arms and grimacing. \"I’m telling Mom when we get back that you were playing with caterpillars.\"","Xiaxia: \"...\"","Xiaxia let out a sigh and said, \"They’re just bugs. Look at you two—so scared it’s laughable.\"","Han Ye gave Xiaxia an odd look from head to toe, then tugged on her pigtail and said, \"Regardless, you are never touching bugs again, got that?\"","The sight of such a sweet, soft-looking little girl suddenly pulling bugs out of her pocket had genuinely startled Han Ye.","Right then and there, he discovered the beauty of studying.","As long as Xiaxia focused on her books, she wouldn’t be messing around with bugs—that was way too frightening.","The three siblings got home, and Qiao Lanshu was already cooking in the kitchen.","Qin Qiao'an, the worrywart of an older brother, immediately herded Xiaxia off to wash her hands. \"Scrub those guilty paws of yours properly, and use soap! They might be poisonous!\"","Xiaxia was shooed over to the sink, where, under the stern gazes of her two brothers, she quietly washed her hands with soap.","Qiao Lanshu heard their voices and called out from the window, \"Han Ye, come in here for a moment.\"","Han Ye acknowledged with a quick reply and jogged into the kitchen, eagerly helping Qiao Lanshu wash the vegetables. \"Mom, what did you need me for?\"","Qiao Lanshu continued chopping vegetables as she spoke. \"I talked with your Teacher Zhao today. She said that girl will be back at school on Monday. When she returns, you should apologize to her, and then this whole thing will be settled.\"","Han Ye was clearly reluctant. He rolled his eyes inwardly and said with some displeasure, \"Mom, if I apologize, doesn't that mean it becomes my fault?\"","Qiao Lanshu said patiently, \"No, it won't. Teacher Zhao will explain things clearly in class and will also talk to the girl. Your apology is just to show the other students a certain attitude, so they'll stop mocking her.\"","Hearing this, Han Ye didn't argue further. He just nodded. \"Fine.\"","Then he started complaining again. \"Honestly, girls are such a pain. From now on, I'll take a detour whenever I see them.\"","Qiao Lanshu laughed. \"You just haven't grown up yet. When you're older, you'll gradually discover and appreciate the beauty of girls. When that day comes, you'll want to get close to them, but they might not even give you the time of day.\"","Han Ye thought about it and figured such a thing would never happen to him.","He was sure he'd never fall for any girl, because he found them all quite annoying.","As far as Qiao Lanshu was concerned, this matter was settled. After talking with Han Ye, she moved on.","When Qin Yuanzheng came home, she mentioned it to him. Qin Yuanzheng was sitting at his desk looking over blueprints. When he heard this, he asked, \"What does that girl look like? Have you seen her?\"","Qiao Lanshu was holding a book at the bedside. She shook her head. \"No, I haven't seen her. But Han Ye said they're all pretty ugly and that he can't stand any of them.\"","Qin Yuanzheng chuckled. \"That little rascal sure has high standards. If he thinks all twenty-odd girls in his class are ugly, then he's destined to never find a wife.\"","After all, not everyone was as lucky as he had been.","Qin Yuanzheng continued with a smile, \"But that's Han Wenlin's problem to worry about. We don't need to get involved.\"","Luckily Qin Qiao'an was still young and a little boy, so the couple could enjoy a few more peaceful years.","After finishing with the blueprints, Qin Yuanzheng took apart a damaged pistol he had brought back.","Qiao Lanshu came over to look and was a bit shocked. \"That's a real gun?\"","She had thought it was a model when he brought it in.","She lowered her voice. \"How did you bring a real gun home? Isn't that allowed?\"","Qin Yuanzheng continued disassembling it and said, \"This one was decommissioned. I've already repaired it. I'm keeping it at home, but I'm worried those two boys might get their hands on it, so I'm taking it apart to be safe.\"","Then he lowered his voice further and added, \"Society has been a bit unstable lately. Theft and robbery cases happen from time to time, and human trafficking of women and children is on the rise. Be careful when you go out, and if necessary, this can serve as protection.\"","He went on, \"It's been about two years since our dog Dahuang passed away. Tomorrow I'll bring a puppy back from the military base and raise it in the yard as a guard dog.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. Although they lived in the military compound with a guard at the gate, having a little dog didn't require much effort, and the kids would enjoy it.","So that weekend, Qin Yuanzheng took the three children to the military base to pick out a little black puppy.","Xiaxia was the one who chose it. She said the puppy's eyes seemed to speak.","Han Ye teased her. \"Now you see human feelings in a dog?\"","Still, he accepted the puppy.","The three siblings happily made a doghouse and cooked bones for the pup, keeping themselves busy.","After a pleasant weekend, Monday brought trouble.","Teacher Zhao rushed into the high school teachers' office and found Qiao Lanshu, looking worried. \"Teacher Qiao, something terrible has happened. That student, Liu Wenqiu, tried to kill herself.\"","Qiao Lanshu was stunned.","This was the first time she had encountered something like this.","She stood up quickly, her expression tense with shock. \"Is she dead?\"","Teacher Zhao quickly clarified, \"No, no. She tried to hang herself, but her family found her in time and rescued her. Her father has gathered some workers and come to the school carrying sticks. They're making a scene, asking everyone where Han Ye is, and they said they're going to beat him to death.\"","Teacher Zhao lowered her voice. \"I've already sent Han Ye out through the back gate. I told him to run home and hide. This is no small matter — those people will actually use force.\"","Qiao Lanshu was silent for a moment.","Her expression turned cold. \"What are they trying to do? Just because they shout the loudest, they think they're in the right? They come to the school without even knowing the facts? Where's security? Have them handle it — keep them outside the school gate and confiscate their weapons. If they fly into a rage and attack the school, grabbing any random student to beat up, what then?\"","Zhao Yanfang was also shaken by this incident.","She said, \"Security is already out. The men haven't gotten into the school. They've been kept at the gate, but they're making a racket, shouting insults, and they've attracted a crowd of onlookers. It's having a bad influence.\"","Qiao Lanshu was worried about Han Ye. \"Did Han Ye really go home?\"","Zhao Yanfang nodded. \"I told him in no uncertain terms to go straight home, and he said he understood.\"","Zhao Yanfang sighed and added, \"The dean said it wouldn't be appropriate for Chief Han to show up publicly in this situation. If he did, those people would say the Public Security Bureau is abusing its power, which would reflect badly on them. So they sent me to come talk to you about how to handle this.\"","Of course, Han Wenlin could still come, but he'd have to take off his uniform first.","But with time being short, coming to find Qiao Lanshu was the fastest option.","Qiao Lanshu was silent for a long moment before speaking. \"Teacher Zhao, I think your dean is wrong. This isn't something we should try to handle ourselves. We should call the police. If it were just one person coming to talk, then we could sit down calmly as the parents of the children involved. But when someone shows up with a group of people and weapons, ready to start trouble, that clearly means this isn't up for discussion. In that case, I'm afraid to go out there myself, because I don't want to get beaten up. Better to call the police. The officers have legal authority and weapons. Them showing up will be far more effective than two women going out to face those men, don't you think?\"","Zhao Yanfang was quiet.","She was persuaded and nodded hesitantly. \"Teacher Qiao, you make a good point.\""]},{"number":266,"title":"Chapter 266: Caught by the Public Security Bureau","paragraphs":["Since the other side had gone so far as to cause trouble at the school, the nature of the matter had changed completely.","It was no longer merely an issue between two children, and Qiao Lanshu had no intention of showing herself again.","But at this point, having only the school security department handle it still wouldn’t be enough.","The police would have to step in and mediate.","The other side was clearly causing trouble deliberately and had even threatened to beat someone to death. Who could take responsibility if something happened?","The school might not be able to handle the situation properly.","Besides, Qiao Lanshu couldn’t let Han Ye actually become a target for those people.","After parting ways with Teacher Zhao, Teacher Zhao returned to the junior high division to discuss the matter with the security officers.","Qiao Lanshu, meanwhile, left the school and hurried toward the police station.","At first, she had thought the matter would be easy to resolve. Once the girl returned to school, Han Ye could simply apologize.","After all, it was because Han Ye had lost the love letter the girl gave him that this whole situation had arisen. No matter how one looked at it, Han Ye couldn’t completely escape responsibility.","But now, judging by how far the other side had taken things, they might truly be targeting Han Ye.","In that case, Han Ye absolutely couldn’t apologize.","Once he apologized, it would be tantamount to admitting that he was at fault. That would only give the other side something to use against him and make it even harder for him to get out of trouble.","As Qiao Lanshu thought this through, a plan gradually took shape in her mind. She immediately felt less flustered and quickened her pace toward the police station.","The police station wasn’t far from the school. After all, there were several schools nearby and a great many children in the area, so the station had been built close to them.","It was only a few minutes’ walk away.","However, halfway there, as Qiao Lanshu passed a street corner, she suddenly spotted Han Ye.","That troublesome boy was carrying a stick and running toward the school. Several street thugs followed behind him, each of them carrying a stick as well. Qiao Lanshu had no idea where Han Ye had even met these people!","Her heart nearly stopped.","What on earth was that brat trying to do?","Qiao Lanshu hurried down the street toward him and shouted loudly, “Han Ye! Han Ye, stop right there!”","Han Ye was leading his brothers forward with great enthusiasm. At first, he didn’t hear Qiao Lanshu calling him at all.","He waved his stick as he spoke to the men beside him. “Once we get to the school entrance, we don’t need to say a word. Just start swinging! Beat the hell out of those punks who came to cause trouble.”","The brothers accompanying him were several young men who sold goods and ran small businesses with him at the market.","They had turned out to be remarkably loyal. When they heard Han Ye was in trouble, they had come to help him without a second thought.","But the sight of this group terrified Qiao Lanshu, and on top of being frightened, she was furious!","She quickened her pace in exasperation, crossed the street, and ran toward Han Ye while shouting again, “Han Ye! Han Ye! Han Ye, you little brat, stop right there! Did you hear me?”","After shouting several times, she finally managed to get Han Ye’s attention just as she was about to catch up with him.","Han Ye was talking with his brothers when he suddenly heard someone calling his name.","He stopped and turned around. The moment he saw Qiao Lanshu, his eyes widened in shock!","Without thinking, he threw away the stick in his hand and looked at her in panic.","The stick landed on one of the men’s feet. He immediately jumped up and cursed, “Damn it, Han Ye! What the hell are you doing? You hit my foot!”","Another person called out, “Han Ye, why did you stop? Weren’t we going to fight? Come on, what are you standing there for?”","The people Han Ye had brought with him were all very young, around sixteen or seventeen years old. However, they had dropped out of school and no longer studied.","In those days, it was common for people that age to quit school. Most stopped after junior high, and many had only attended elementary school.","Han Ye had always been a student. He usually had to attend class and didn’t have much free time, so Qiao Lanshu couldn’t understand for the moment how he had gotten to know these people.","Apparently, Han Ye had been spending too much time outside and had gone off fooling around with them.","But that was not important for now, because there was something far more urgent.","Qiao Lanshu walked up to him with a stern expression and asked seriously, “Han Ye, where exactly are you going? Why are all of you carrying sticks? What are you planning to do?”","Han Ye: “......”","At that moment, Han Ye was as nervous as a frightened little lion. Standing there, he stammered and didn’t even dare call her “Mom.”","“Teacher Qiao? What are you doing here?”","Then, looking extremely guilty, he quickly added, “Teacher Qiao, aren’t you supposed to be at work right now?”","Qiao Lanshu glared at him angrily, reached out, and grabbed his ear. With a cold expression, she scolded him, “You still have the nerve to ask me? Han Ye, look at you—you’ve really grown bold. You actually dare to lead people around with sticks and go looking for a fight! Now tell me, where were you planning to go? What kind of trouble were you trying to get me into this time?”","Han Ye bent halfway over as she twisted his ear, grimacing in pain. “Ow, ow, ow! That hurts, Teacher Qiao! Please go easy on me. Don’t pull my ear off!”","Qiao Lanshu was truly furious this time and showed no mercy. She pinched his ear and twisted it several times, making Han Ye howl in pain.","Han Ye lowered his voice and pleaded, “Teacher Qiao, this matter is complicated. But believe me, I’ll handle it properly, and I absolutely won’t cause trouble for you or Uncle Qin! Really, all you need to know is that I’m on the side of justice! I would never do anything illegal.”","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu was so angry she nearly laughed. “You’re on the side of justice? Who said so—the police or the school? You’re leading people from the streets to a fight while carrying sticks, and you still have the nerve to claim you represent justice? Don’t make me laugh! Go ahead and hang a sign around your own neck that says ‘justice’ and see if anyone agrees with you.”","After a pause, she continued, “Han Ye, your father is a police officer. You ought to understand the law better than anyone! Violence can’t solve any problem. When you run into something like this, you should ask the authorities for help—not try to enforce the law yourself when you’re still a minor. What you’re doing is a crime. Do you understand?”","Han Ye lowered his head, feeling unbearably guilty. In a small voice, he said, “Teacher Qiao, it hurts. My ear really hurts.”","When Qiao Lanshu saw that his ear had turned red, she finally let go. She glanced at the few young men standing beside Han Ye.","The boys were still holding their sticks. They looked at Han Ye, then at Qiao Lanshu, and none of them dared to say a word.","Although they had not received much education, they instinctively feared teachers.","Now, as they watched Qiao Lanshu reprimand Han Ye, they didn’t dare speak. After all, judging by Han Ye’s attitude, he seemed to listen to this teacher quite obediently.","Qiao Lanshu glanced at the boys and said, “Thank you for coming to help Han Ye, but we adults can handle this. There’s no need for you kids to get involved. Throw away the sticks and go home.”","The boys scratched their heads and looked hesitantly at Han Ye.","These young boys had been brainwashed by martial arts novels. They believed in risking everything for their brothers and becoming heroes of loyalty and righteousness.","Naturally, they weren’t willing to leave so easily.","Qiao Lanshu fixed Han Ye with a cold stare. “What, my word doesn’t count anymore? You’re not going to listen to me either?”","Han Ye was most afraid that Qiao Lanshu would stop caring about him.","He had no one to look after him in the first place. If even Qiao Lanshu stopped caring about him, he really would become a wild, undisciplined child with no family.","Han Ye quickly said, “Of course I’ll listen. I’ll always listen to you!”","Then he turned to his friends and said, “You guys go home first. I’ll tell you about this another day.”","The boys nodded. “If you ever need help, just say the word. Come find us anytime.”","Han Ye nodded and said goodbye to them before following behind Qiao Lanshu with his head hanging low.","Qiao Lanshu walked a few steps down the street, feeling both furious and shaken.","If Han Ye had taken that group of boys to confront the workers outside the elementary school and they had gotten into a fight, the matter would have become impossible to resolve peacefully.","Originally, this was only a case involving students dating too young. If handled properly, it wouldn’t have had any impact on Han Ye.","But if he joined forces with young men from outside and got into a brawl that disrupted public order, the consequences would be much more serious.","If he accidentally injured someone severely, he might even end up with a criminal record.","To settle the matter through negotiation, they would have to go and plead with the other side. And if the other side made any demands, Han Ye would have no choice but to agree.","The thought made Qiao Lanshu shudder with fear.","She glared fiercely at Han Ye again.","Han Ye shrank his neck and explained, “Mom, I wasn’t actually planning to fight them. I was just going to scare them a little and drive them away from the school entrance. Or I could have lured them somewhere else. The point is, I couldn’t let them keep gathering at the school gate, or they’d only make the whole situation worse.”","Qiao Lanshu’s face remained stern as she sneered. “Yes, you weren’t planning to fight them. You were only carrying a stick and bringing a whole group of friends with you. Do you think anyone would believe you if you said you weren’t going to hit anybody? Besides, if they’re determined to blow this matter up, they’ll force you into a fight even if you don’t want one. Did you think about what you’d do then?”","Han Ye lowered his head and said nothing.","Qiao Lanshu criticized him. “Your biggest problem is that you’re too impulsive and too arrogant. You think you can do anything and do it well, but that’s only because you’ve always been protected by Director Han and your Uncle Qin. The moment the two of them can’t protect you anymore, just wait and see what happens to you.”","As she said this, Qiao Lanshu suddenly remembered what Qin Yuanzheng had told her before.","Qin Yuanzheng had always been eager to send Han Ye into the military.","He said that with Han Ye’s temperament, if he wasn’t sent to the army to be tempered for a few years, he would sooner or later get himself into serious trouble.","Han Wenlin didn’t have many connections in the military. The designation of his unit had been canceled, and his entire regiment had been demobilized. His former superior was also nearing retirement.","So after Han Ye joined the army, Han Wenlin wouldn’t be able to offer him many connections.","Qin Yuanzheng, on the other hand, had plenty.","Or rather, with Qin Yuanzheng around, Han Wenlin could rely on him and continue living comfortably.","However, Qin Yuanzheng had privately told Qiao Lanshu that during Han Ye’s first three years in the army, he had no intention of giving the boy any special treatment.","Han Ye needed to experience the hardship of being treated like everyone else.","Qiao Lanshu walked all the way to the entrance of the public security bureau in silence, her face dark.","When Han Ye saw where they were, he immediately lost his nerve again.","In a low voice, he said, “Mom, I know I was wrong, all right? Why are you still bringing me to the police station? You’re not really going to have them lock me up, are you?”","Qiao Lanshu sneered. “You guessed right. What you did this time was pretty serious. You deserve to be detained for a few days.”","Han Ye: “!!!”","Han Ye instantly felt as if the sky were falling.","He shamelessly grabbed Qiao Lanshu’s arm. “Mom, you’re my real mother, aren’t you? Don’t take me to the police station. Everyone in there is Dad’s subordinate. If I get arrested for doing something wrong, won’t that make Dad look bad?”","Qiao Lanshu sneered again. “I’m impressed that you know it would bring shame to your father. Too bad it’s too late!”","She grabbed Han Ye by the arm and dragged him into the police station.","Although Han Ye begged her nonstop, he didn’t actually try to break free.","He simply pulled a long face and secretly covered half of his face with one hand. Looking both miserable and embarrassed, he was dragged by Qiao Lanshu into the lobby of the police station.","Even with his hand covering the side of his face where he had been slapped, the officers recognized Han Ye at a glance.","After all, he was the only son of the provincial bureau director and had grown up in the military compound. He had caused no shortage of trouble over the years, so it was difficult not to know him.","A young officer hurried over. He glanced curiously at Han Ye and politely asked Qiao Lanshu, “Comrade, what brings you here?”","He cautiously added, “Are you looking for Director Han?”","Han Wenlin normally didn’t work here. This was a district police station.","Qiao Lanshu asked, “Is Director Han here today?”","The officer shook his head. “No, but if you need to see him, we can drive you there.”","Qiao Lanshu hesitated for a few seconds. Considering the seriousness of what had happened, she decided that Han Wenlin needed to be informed.","She nodded and said, “Then I’m sorry to trouble you, young comrade.”","When Han Ye heard that they were going to see his father instead of having him locked up, he immediately breathed a sigh of relief.","The officer drove them to the gates of the provincial public security bureau, where Han Wenlin’s office was located. Qiao Lanshu took Han Ye inside.","As soon as they entered the lobby, several officers who worked with Han Wenlin spotted them.","One of them immediately put down what he was doing and walked over to Qiao Lanshu. “Teacher Qiao, Han Ye, what brings you here today?”","Han Ye stood dejectedly behind Qiao Lanshu and glanced at her expression.","Qiao Lanshu said, “Comrade, is Director Han in his office? Please inform him that this concerns Han Ye and is quite serious. Tell him to come see me as soon as possible.”","The officer replied, “Since it’s something serious, there’s no need to inform him first. Let’s go directly to Director Han’s office.”","The three of them arrived at Han Wenlin’s office. Han Wenlin was working at his desk, and he was extremely surprised to see Qiao Lanshu and Han Ye.","Of course, after the initial surprise, he quickly understood what had happened.","He immediately asked, “Han Ye, you little brat, did you cause trouble for Aunt Qiao again?”","Han Ye: “......”"]},{"number":267,"title":"Chapter 267: Reading Is Harmful","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu explained the situation to Director Han, including the fact that Han Ye had grabbed a stick and gone looking for a fight.","When Han Wenlin heard this, his face turned livid. He glared at Han Ye. “Who gave you the nerve, huh? In a situation like this, you should have listened to your teacher and simply gone home. You’re just a kid, and you thought you could fight them? Do you have any idea how serious this is?”","Han Ye was unconvinced by what his father had said. “I wasn’t actually planning to fight them. I just wanted to drive them away. They were all gathered outside the school, chattering nonstop. It was driving me crazy.”","At his age, Han Ye was especially concerned about his pride and reputation.","He felt that those people had come to cause trouble because of him.","On top of that, they had been shouting outside the school that he was a pervert who toyed with female students’ feelings. He had never done anything of the sort, and he was furious.","So, acting on impulse, he had grabbed a stick and gone looking for them.","Han Wenlin sighed helplessly. “You clearly never considered your future. This matter isn’t nearly as simple as you think.”","After saying that, Han Wenlin fell silent for a moment before turning to Qiao Lanshu. “Comrade Xiao Qiao, how about I meet with the female student’s parents? Maybe we can sit down and talk.”","Of course, anyone capable of becoming a provincial bureau director was bound to have considerable means.","But when it came to Han Ye, Han Wenlin was still rather cautious.","If the matter could be resolved without making it bigger, that was what he preferred.","By “sitting down and talking,” he meant seeing whether the other side was willing to mediate and settle the matter through negotiation.","Qiao Lanshu thought for a while, then said to Han Wenlin, “Director Han, how about this? I’ll go over first and see what they want. If things really can’t be resolved, then you can step in. The reason they’re targeting Han Ye may well be because of you.”","Han Wenlin understood exactly what she meant without her having to say more.","Han Ye was smart too, and he understood.","So he muttered, “Women are terrifying.”","Since Qiao Lanshu had put it that way, Han Wenlin naturally had no objections.","Qiao Lanshu added, “By the way, Director Han, lock him up first.”","She looked at Han Ye sternly. “That brat is capable of doing anything. I don’t think he even realizes what he did wrong. Lock him up for a day and make him reflect properly. Let him out after this matter has been dealt with.”","Han Ye was stunned. “Mom, I’m your actual son! You can’t be this heartless.”","Han Wenlin’s brows twitched as well.","But after looking at Qiao Lanshu’s expression, then at Han Ye, who was wailing and clinging to Qiao Lanshu’s arm as he begged for mercy, he wisely kept his mouth shut.","Han Ye was practically at a loss for words. “I swear, I really won’t do anything reckless again. I’ll go home and stay there right now, okay?”","Qiao Lanshu looked at him and said sternly, “Teacher Zhao told you to go home and hide. You agreed, but then you turned around and went looking for a fight. You even deceived your teacher. How am I supposed to believe you now?”","Han Ye was frantic. “But—but I never lied to you, Mom! I promise I’ll keep my word. I’ll never lie again, okay?”","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. Usually, she was very lenient with the children, but Han Ye had infuriated her this time. She rejected him coldly.","“You can reflect properly at the Public Security Bureau. You can come home after this matter is resolved.”","Han Ye: “...”","Han Wenlin was standing right beside them. He wanted to plead for his son, but when he saw how stern Qiao Lanshu looked, he didn’t dare say a word.","After all, Han Ye had practically been raised by Qiao Lanshu. When Han Ye called her Mom, she was his mother, and a mother had every right to discipline her son. He had better keep quiet.","Because of this son, he was always a step lower than Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng, in a manner of speaking.","He coughed, nodded, and said, “All right. I’ll lock him in the interrogation room. Should I assign two people to go with you?”","Qiao Lanshu nodded. “Yes. Arrange for two public security officers to accompany me. I’ll go with the other teachers to visit their home.”","Han Wenlin assigned two young men who had recently transferred from the military to accompany Qiao Lanshu.","Han Ye, meanwhile, was pitifully locked up in the interrogation room.","Qiao Lanshu arrived at the entrance of the middle school with the two public security officers.","The people who had been causing trouble had already been mediated with and dispersed by the school’s security department. The only one left was the female student’s father—Liu Wenqiu’s father—who had been invited into the school office for a discussion.","Clearly, the discussion had not gone well or pleasantly.","The school director and Teacher Zhao looked extremely grim as they followed the man out of the school. The three of them had just stepped through the entrance when Qiao Lanshu arrived with the two officers.","“Teacher Qiao!” Zhao Yanfang called out hurriedly.","The female student’s father had been acting quite aggressively, but when he saw Qiao Lanshu arrive with two public security officers, he stopped at once. He turned around and glared at Zhao Yanfang.","“You actually called the police? We’re the victims! We didn’t even call the police, and you have the nerve to accuse us first?”","His booming voice gave Zhao Yanfang a headache. She looked at Qiao Lanshu for help.","Qiao Lanshu sized him up. He appeared to be in his forties, with dark, weathered skin. His clothes were covered in patches, and the cloth shoes on his feet were caked with mud.","He did indeed look like someone from an impoverished family who worked as a laborer on construction sites, just as Teacher Zhao had described.","But his temper was clearly poor, while his courage was not particularly great. The moment he saw the public security officers, he became nervous.","It was hard to imagine that someone like him would think of coming to the school to cause trouble.","Qiao Lanshu said to him, “The school didn’t call the police. I did.”","The man stared her up and down several times before asking suspiciously, “You called the police? Aren’t you a teacher at this school?”","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. “I’m not a teacher at this middle school. I’m Han Ye’s mother. I came here to see your daughter and discuss how we should deal with this matter.”","The moment the man heard that she was Han Ye’s mother, his expression darkened, and he was about to start berating her.","Then Qiao Lanshu continued, “But don’t get angry yet. That good-for-nothing Han Ye did something wrong and refuses to admit it. I’m not going to indulge him, so I called the police and had him taken to the Public Security Bureau. He’s already been locked up.”","The man: “...”","The school director and Zhao Yanfang exchanged a glance, both of them seeing the shock in the other’s eyes.","Zhao Yanfang carefully ventured, “Xiao Qiao... Han Ye really was taken to the Public Security Bureau?”","Qiao Lanshu nodded solemnly. “That’s right. Didn’t student Liu Wenqiu say she was going to kill herself? This matter appears to be very serious. One wrong step, and it could become a case involving someone’s death. We had to call the police. Otherwise, the school wouldn’t be able to bear the responsibility.”","Zhao Yanfang nodded. “You’re right. I didn’t think it through.”","The middle school director rubbed his bald head and sighed. “Ah, Xiao Qiao, you really have thought this through. I never would have considered that.”","Zhao Yanfang had mentioned calling the police before, but Liu Wenqiu’s father had objected. He refused to let them report it, insisting that they resolve the matter through negotiation because involving the police would be bad for his daughter.","As it turned out, the two sides had actually reached an agreement.","But Han Ye’s mother had nevertheless brought two police officers with her.","Liu’s father suddenly snapped, “Who do you think you’re fooling? You’re not Han Ye’s mother at all. Han Ye comes from a single-parent family, and his father is the director of the provincial Public Security Bureau. You expect me to believe that you had him arrested? You might as well just say you sent him home.”","Everyone fell silent.","Qiao Lanshu asked in surprise, “How did you know his father is a bureau director? Teacher Zhao, did you tell him?”","Teacher Zhao was stunned. “I didn’t... I don’t actually know what Han Ye’s father does for a living. How could I have told him?”","At that time, there was still a certain distance between teachers and their students’ parents.","Teachers generally didn’t ask what the parents did for work, what kind of homes they lived in, or what their family circumstances were.","Teacher Zhao only knew that Han Ye came from a fairly well-off family. His father seemed to be an official in the Public Security Bureau, but she had never imagined that he was the director of the provincial bureau.","The director of the provincial bureau was no minor figure.","Liu’s father was momentarily at a loss after Qiao Lanshu’s question, then angrily said, “What’s so hard to know about that? That boy told my daughter himself. He was dating her—of course he told her everything!”","As he spoke, he began cursing again. “That little bastard! Fine, he wanted to date my daughter, but things were going perfectly well, and then he went and plastered the love letter she wrote all over the place. Do you know that’s as good as murder? My daughter tried to kill herself because of him!”","Teacher Zhao couldn’t help speaking up. “Sir, we already explained this to you. Han Ye didn’t post that letter. Liu Wenqiu put it in his desk, and Han Ye mistook it for trash and threw it into the garbage can. Someone else found it afterward...”","Liu’s father said furiously, “I don’t care! This whole thing is Han Ye’s fault! If anything happens to my daughter, Han Ye won’t get away with it either!”","This was the first time Teacher Zhao had ever encountered a parent like him. She couldn’t help feeling irritated, and the man’s entire sense of right and wrong had left her deeply shaken.","Qiao Lanshu said, “Don’t get worked up. I’m here to resolve the problem. We’ll go home with you and see how your daughter is doing.”","Liu’s father glanced at the two tall, broad-shouldered police officers standing behind Qiao Lanshu and hesitated.","But the situation had already escalated this far. He couldn’t very well give up halfway.","So he led Zhao Yanfang, Qiao Lanshu, and the two police officers home.","Seeing that the police were going with them, the school director didn’t follow. He turned around and went back to school to write a report.","A report was mandatory after something like this happened. All he could hope for was that Qiao Lanshu would handle the matter properly and keep it from affecting the school.","They walked for three blocks, winding through one turn after another, before finally arriving at a dilapidated compound housing several families.","All the buildings in the compound were old. In a few more years, they would probably be declared unsafe.","The local residents had already moved away, and the people living there now were mostly migrant workers who had come to the city to find jobs.","The area was rather chaotic, and the ground was dirty.","But there was nothing anyone could do about it. Several years had passed since the beginning of the reform and opening-up, yet urban construction and city management had still fallen far behind the pace at which people were pouring into the cities.","Although the various municipal administrative and law-enforcement departments were increasing their staff, improving maintenance and management regulations, and expanding their enforcement teams, there were still times when they simply couldn’t keep up.","Qiao Lanshu had visited places like this during previous home visits. Her students had all been high schoolers, however, and families who could afford to send their children to high school despite living in such conditions tended to be more forward-thinking. They were not so difficult to reason with.","But the Liu family did not look like people who would be easy to deal with.","Liu’s father led them into the compound. Several families lived there, and everyone’s doors stood open. A few children ran around the courtyard while the elderly sat together chatting and knitting sweaters. The moment the group entered, several pairs of eyes turned toward them.","When those gossip-hungry eyes spotted the two police officers, they began to burn with excitement.","Zhao Yanfang leaned toward Qiao Lanshu and lowered her voice. “These are the legendary intelligence network of the communal courtyard. Whatever they ask you later, don’t say a word.”","Qiao Lanshu smiled and nodded.","But the two of them had overestimated the neighbors. As soon as the women saw the two big, muscular police officers accompanying them, they quickly suppressed their curiosity and turned their attention to the officers instead.","Qiao Lanshu almost expected them to grab the officers by the arm and start introducing them to suitable women.","Zhao Yanfang had visited Liu Wenqiu’s home before, so she knew the way.","Liu’s father glanced at the neighbors watching them, and his expression darkened further.","He was a proud man and had never intended to call the police.","Once police officers showed up, the neighbors were bound to notice.","If they learned that his daughter had fallen in love too young at school, dated a boy, and then attempted suicide—so much so that the police had come to investigate—how would he ever be able to face the neighbors again?","With a grim expression, Liu’s father reached his front door.","The door stood open. Three children were sitting on the ground outside. Two of them were girls, one around eight or nine years old and the other five or six. The youngest was a boy of about four or five.","All three children were playing outside their home. Their clothes were filthy and disheveled, and their hair was just as messy.","The moment Qiao Lanshu saw them, she instinctively thought of her good friend Zhong Mei.","Zhong Mei’s family circumstances were almost exactly the same.","Her family had been poor, and her parents had favored boys over girls. After having three daughters, they finally had a son, whom they treasured dearly.","From a young age, Zhong Mei had looked after her younger siblings. She had barely attended school before taking odd jobs wherever she could to earn money and help support the family.","In the end, her family had even planned to sell her off to pay their debts.","Standing at the doorway and looking at the three innocent, bewildered children, Qiao Lanshu felt a growing irritation. At the same time, she began to understand.","She understood why Liu Wenqiu, one of her students, had set her sights on Han Ye. She understood why the girl had used suicide as a means of forcing Han Ye’s hand.","Looking at her family, it was already astonishing that she had managed to continue her education through the eighth grade.","Qiao Lanshu guessed that Liu Wenqiu would probably be dropping out of school soon.","Sure enough, as Liu’s father walked into the house, she heard him grumbling and cursing:","“I told you not to go to school. What good does studying do? The more a girl studies, the more trouble she causes. A perfectly good girl should stay home, help take care of the children, feed the pigs, and get married once she’s old enough. Wouldn’t that be just fine?","“But you insisted on going to junior high. What use is that? If you hadn’t gone to school, you might not have tried to kill yourself. And now you’ve gone and threatened to die just because you’re studying. What a curse.”","As he spoke, he kicked open the door to the inner room and shouted inside, “Qiu’er, your teacher is here to see you, and so are the police. Tell them clearly how exactly Han Ye harassed you!”"]},{"number":268,"title":"Chapter 268: Have You Ever Heard of the Crime of Defamation","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu, Teacher Zhao, and the two police officers had already reached the doorway.","Both officers were men. They stood at the entrance and asked Liu’s father, “Can we go inside? Would that be convenient?”","After all, the person inside was a female student, and they were unsure whether they should avoid any possible impropriety. Although such considerations were not usually necessary during an investigation, it never hurt to ask.","Liu’s father had already entered the room himself. When he heard the officers ask that, he immediately said, “No, it wouldn’t be convenient. This is my daughter’s room. What are two grown men doing going in there? You two should stay outside. Let the two female teachers go in.”","The two officers exchanged a glance, then looked at Liu’s father, who was standing inside the room. One of them said, “Comrade, you should come out too. It’s not appropriate for you to stay in there.”","After all, there were two young and attractive female teachers inside. How could a short-tempered man who had just caused a scene at the school possibly be left alone with them?","Director Han had told the two officers to accompany Qiao Lanshu primarily to protect her. As for how the case would be handled, that would depend mainly on whether the two families could communicate and resolve the matter.","If they truly could not reach an understanding and a conflict broke out, the officers would step in.","Hearing this, Liu’s father immediately became displeased. He shouted, “This is my daughter’s room! I can go in whenever I want. What’s inappropriate about that? You... Hey, hey, don’t pull me! What do you think you’re doing?”","The two officers each grabbed one of his arms and dragged him outside. The three of them stood in the courtyard. One of the officers took a pen and notebook from his bag and looked at Liu’s father with a stern expression.","“We need your cooperation in investigating your daughter’s suicide attempt...”","Liu’s father: “...”","Zhao Yanfang and Qiao Lanshu entered the room. It was very cramped, with only a tiny window. Piles of miscellaneous items had been shoved against one wall, making the place look dirty and disorderly.","Against the other wall, near the window, stood a wooden plank bed. It was small, and Liu Wenqiu lay on it.","She was curled up at the very edge. Her younger brother and sisters probably slept in the space beside her.","Zhao Yanfang and Qiao Lanshu exchanged a glance. Neither of them looked particularly pleased.","Zhao Yanfang walked in first and called softly, “Wenqiu? Your teachers have come to see you. How are you feeling?”","Liu Wenqiu lay on the bed with pale lips. She glanced at Zhao Yanfang but said nothing, instead fixing her gaze on Qiao Lanshu.","She stared at Qiao Lanshu for several seconds before looking past her. When she saw that there was no one else behind Qiao Lanshu, she looked away again, her expression turning quiet and subdued.","Qiao Lanshu noticed her gaze but said nothing. She simply followed Zhao Yanfang to the bedside.","It had to be said that seeing such living conditions, such a father, and the haggard-looking girl lying on the bed would arouse pity in most people.","Qiao Lanshu did feel sorry for her, but she felt nothing beyond that.","Perhaps it was because the girl’s methods were so clumsy that Qiao Lanshu had seen through her intentions at a glance. And since the girl’s target was still her own child, Qiao Lanshu found it impossible to feel much affection for her.","Zhao Yanfang pulled over a chair and sat beside the bed. Looking down at Liu Wenqiu, she said, “Wenqiu, why didn’t you go to school? Why did you... why did you try to kill yourself?”","The last time Zhao Yanfang had visited Liu Wenqiu, the girl had seemed to be in fairly good spirits.","She said softly, “When I came to see you last time, didn’t I promise that I’d have Han Ye apologize to you? Besides, no one in our class was going to laugh at you. Lots of people write love letters. It’s really not a big deal, so you mustn’t do anything foolish.”","Liu Wenqiu’s eyes reddened, and tears began to fall.","Zhao Yanfang sighed. “Don’t cry. Do you know that your father took some people and went to the school with clubs, threatening to kill Han Ye?”","When Liu Wenqiu heard this, hesitation flickered across her face. “Teacher Zhao, I didn’t know about that. My father never tells us anything he’s going to do.”","Zhao Yanfang shook her head. “I knew it. No offense, but your father is far too impulsive. Making such a huge commotion won’t do you any good, will it?”","As she spoke, Zhao Yanfang pointed at Qiao Lanshu and said to Liu Wenqiu, “Oh, right, Wenqiu. This is Han Ye’s mother, Teacher Qiao. When she heard what happened to you, she came here with me to visit you.”","Qiao Lanshu gave her a polite nod.","Liu Wenqiu said somewhat awkwardly, “Teacher Qiao.”","Standing beside Zhao Yanfang, Qiao Lanshu asked her, “Wenqiu, can you tell me what happened? I’d like to know the whole story.”","Liu Wenqiu pressed her lips together and said quietly, “There’s... there’s nothing to talk about, is there?”","After a pause, she added, “I don’t want to talk about it.”","Qiao Lanshu remained fairly polite as she asked, “How can you say there’s nothing to talk about? You nearly took your own life. That’s a serious matter—an extremely serious one.”","At that, Liu Wenqiu looked up at Qiao Lanshu, seeming torn about what to say.","Qiao Lanshu continued immediately, “Someone nearly lost their life. This isn’t a minor issue, so I’ve already called the police. Han Ye has been taken to the police station for questioning. Since you’re ill, you don’t need to go to the station. Two police officers are waiting outside. You can tell them what happened in a moment.”","When Zhao Yanfang heard this, she felt that Qiao Lanshu’s words were a little too harsh. Wasn’t it rather cruel to say such things to a girl who had just attempted suicide?","Liu Wenqiu was visibly shocked as well, even panicked. She looked at Qiao Lanshu, her face turning even paler.","“Teacher Qiao... why did you call the police?”","Her expression grew frantic. “This... this is only a minor matter. We could have discussed it and worked it out between ourselves. Why call the police?”","No matter what the circumstances, people were always afraid of the police.","After all, they were the law enforcement authorities.","Liu Wenqiu was only a middle school student, so naturally she was even more frightened.","She had never expected Qiao Lanshu to call the police.","She had thought that by making the matter this serious, Han Ye’s father would bring him to their home to apologize. Then both families would sit down and negotiate a solution.","Han Ye certainly would not agree to marry her. He usually kept his distance from girls and had barely interacted with her a few times.","So, what she had originally hoped for was to negotiate with Director Han and see whether he could arrange a job for her. She was about to drop out of school, while her younger sisters still needed an education. Her family was already poor, and her father refused to pay school fees for his daughters.","If the younger children were going to study, the eldest had to drop out.","Over the past two years, because Liu Wenqiu had been allowed to remain in school for two extra years, her younger sister—who was already nine—still had not started school. Her youngest sister was seven and would need to begin school as well.","But if Liu Wenqiu stopped studying, she would have to enter society and, like her parents, take temporary laboring jobs. She would work herself half to death from morning until night and still earn only a few dollars a day—so little that she would not even dare spend money on meat.","She had heard that some girls managed to find well-off partners at school, after which their partners’ families arranged jobs for them.","And the jobs were said to be excellent: sitting in an office, eating in the canteen, going home early every afternoon, getting holidays during the New Year and other festivals, and even receiving generous subsidies.","She was envious.","That was why she had set her sights on Han Ye.","But Han Ye’s family had actually called the police, leaving Liu Wenqiu at a complete loss.","Qiao Lanshu looked at her and said calmly, “Your father caused a disturbance at the school, claiming that Han Ye had behaved indecently toward you. But Han Ye denied it, and you were threatening to kill yourself, so we had no choice but to turn the matter over to the police.”","Zhao Yanfang’s expression grew serious as well. She said to Liu Wenqiu, “Wenqiu, did Han Ye behave indecently toward you? You didn’t mention anything about this when I came to see you last week.”","Liu Wenqiu’s face turned an ugly mixture of pale and red. She lay there without saying a word.","Every now and then, she glanced toward the door. She probably had no idea what to do and was waiting for her father to come and speak on her behalf.","Qiao Lanshu stepped directly into her line of sight and said sternly, “Student Liu, do you know that falsely accusing someone is a crime?”","Liu Wenqiu jumped in fright. She looked up at Qiao Lanshu and hurriedly said, “I—I didn’t falsely accuse him...”","Qiao Lanshu kept a stern expression.","“How did you not? Your father repeatedly claimed that Han Ye had behaved indecently toward you and even demanded that Han Ye take responsibility for you. But Han Ye said that he barely knew you. The only time the two of you had any physical contact was when you fell and he kindly helped you up. Yet somehow, word got out that he had behaved indecently toward you. Your father even went to the school and made a scene, making sure everyone knew about it. He has ruined Han Ye’s reputation. How is that not a false accusation?”","Zhao Yanfang was about to speak, but Qiao Lanshu pressed a hand against her shoulder to stop her.","Qiao Lanshu continued, “In the past, a conviction for slander could get someone sent to a labor camp for three years. How many years is it now? Don’t worry too much. You’re a minor, so they definitely won’t arrest you. At most, they’ll arrest your father. After all, he was the one who caused a disturbance at the school without bothering to find out the truth.”","Liu Wenqiu was frightened by her words.","Crying, she said, “Teacher Qiao, Teacher Zhao, I—I didn’t...”","Zhao Yanfang asked her sternly, “Wenqiu, just answer one question. Did Han Ye behave indecently toward you? Is that why you tried to kill yourself?”","Liu Wenqiu had avoided the subject all along. But now, under Zhao Yanfang’s serious gaze, combined with Qiao Lanshu’s earlier warning, she began to feel afraid.","After hesitating for a while, she shook her head and said, “No. Han Ye... he didn’t behave indecently toward me.”","Qiao Lanshu’s expression darkened. “If he didn’t, then why did your father say he did? Why did he spread false rumors about a middle school student?”","Liu Wenqiu began crying again after being questioned. This time, however, she refused to say another word.","Zhao Yanfang asked her several more questions, but she still remained silent, doing nothing but cry.","Zhao Yanfang was softhearted. She looked helplessly at Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu, however, remained cold and stern. “Teacher Zhao, she just admitted that Han Ye did nothing to her. From beginning to end, this was all a misunderstanding. But since I’ve already called the police, we should still have the officers come in and record her statement. That way, we won’t have to worry about something else happening after we leave.”","She was mainly worried that once they left, Liu Wenqiu’s family would deny everything they had said and go back to the school to cause trouble.","Zhao Yanfang looked at Liu Wenqiu with some disappointment now.","She had never imagined that one of her students could do something like this.","Perhaps Liu Wenqiu’s family background was at fault. Or perhaps Liu Wenqiu herself was simply too calculating.","Regardless, hurting others was wrong.","As soon as Qiao Lanshu finished speaking, she walked to the door and called for the two police officers in the courtyard.","The officers had been questioning Liu’s father and recording his statement.","When they heard Qiao Lanshu call out, they immediately came over and asked, “Teacher Qiao, what is it?”","Qiao Lanshu told them, “Please come in and record a statement. Student Liu just admitted that Han Ye did not behave indecently toward her and that this suicide attempt had nothing to do with Han Ye.”","The two officers exchanged a glance, then immediately took out their notebooks and pens and entered the room.","After being questioned by the officers for quite some time, Liu’s father was drenched in sweat.","He was beginning to regret his actions. Why had he acted on impulse and taken people to the school to cause trouble?","The officers had told him that he had disrupted public order and harmed public security. If the allegations about Han Ye’s supposed misconduct were proven false, he could also be charged with spreading rumors, defamation, personal attacks, and damaging someone’s reputation.","In short, the situation was extremely complicated, and the consequences were serious.","He might even be sent to a labor camp.","Liu’s father lowered his head and paced around the courtyard twice. Noticing that the neighbors had come out to watch the spectacle, he turned away with a gloomy expression and went back inside.","The two tall police officers entered the room and, with Qiao Lanshu and Zhao Yanfang present, asked Liu Wenqiu several questions.","Liu Wenqiu was so frightened that her face had gone pale, and even her voice trembled as she spoke.","Zhao Yanfang felt sorry for her. After all, she had taught the girl for two years.","But since the officers were handling the matter, she could not interrupt.","Qiao Lanshu stood to the side, feeling no sympathy for Liu Wenqiu at all.","Liu Wenqiu needed to learn a lesson and stop thinking about harming others.","Han Ye had done nothing wrong. Why should he have to pay for her poverty and ignorance?","Everyone had to make their own way in life. If she wanted a better life, then while the market economy was just beginning to develop, she should work hard in society and gain experience.","No matter how difficult the situation Zhong Mei had found herself in, she had always managed to claw her way back out. As long as Liu Wenqiu had that kind of determination, she could do the same.","That was what Qiao Lanshu thought, though she did not say it aloud.","After all, Liu Wenqiu’s family would probably only accuse her of saying something like, “If you’re so compassionate, why don’t you give up your own food?”","The police officers finished recording the statement quickly. Liu Wenqiu no longer dared to lie, nor did she dare refuse to answer. She told them everything they asked.","What she said this time was essentially the same as what Han Ye had previously told Qiao Lanshu.","She had secretly fallen in love with Han Ye, so she had written him a love letter.","But Han Ye had thrown the letter away, and someone else had found it and posted it on the blackboard...","In short, Han Ye had not behaved indecently toward her. She had attempted suicide because she felt humiliated after being mocked by her classmates and had acted impulsively.","After finishing the statement, the officers left the Liu residence with Qiao Lanshu and Zhao Yanfang.","They were worried that Liu’s father might cause trouble again later.","So the two officers walked up to him and said sternly, “This matter hasn’t been settled yet. We need to return and speak with Han Ye himself and his family to find out whether they are willing to accept mediation or intend to pursue legal responsibility. For the time being, stay at home and wait for further notice.”","When Liu’s father heard this, he immediately panicked.","“Officers, everything has already been made clear. Why are you still talking about legal responsibility? What legal responsibility could we possibly have? This was nothing more than the children fooling around!”","The two officers reprimanded him harshly. “You used a suicide attempt to threaten someone, and you still call it fooling around? Wait for further notice. We’ll decide how to handle the matter after we’ve spoken with Han Ye’s family.”","Zhao Yanfang stood beside Qiao Lanshu, looking somewhat worried. She lowered her voice and said, “Teacher Qiao, do you think Liu Wenqiu might try to kill herself again?”","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. “No. She doesn’t look like someone who intends to take her own life.”","A girl who was constantly thinking about how to advance her prospects and secure a job could hardly be called simple-minded. She merely wanted a better life—she didn’t look like someone bent on dying."]},{"number":269,"title":"Chapter 269: Giving Children a Dose of Motivation","paragraphs":["Liu Wenqiu and her father had probably both been frightened by the police.","At first, they had likely only intended to intimidate Han Ye and see if they could get some kind of benefit out of him. They never expected Qiao Lanshu to report them directly—or even bring the police to their door to investigate.","No matter how brazen they usually were, they were still afraid when faced with police officers in uniform. So, for the next three days, the whole family made no further move.","Naturally, Liu Wenqiu did not return to school either.","Later, when Zhao Yanfang mentioned the matter to Qiao Lanshu, she told her that Liu Wenqiu had dropped out. Her family had demanded that she find work and earn money to support her younger sister and brother’s schooling. Otherwise, her father refused to pay for the two girls’ education.","There were four children in the family, but her father was only willing to support two of them. Her son was still young and had not yet reached school age, while both of her daughters were old enough to be in school. So Liu Wenqiu had no choice but to quit.","Qiao Lanshu asked Teacher Zhao to keep an eye on things for a few days and inform her immediately if the Liu family made any further moves. That way, she could respond in time if anything happened.","As for Han Ye, Qiao Lanshu had also gotten him a weeklong leave of absence, just to be safe.","That afternoon, once everything had been dealt with, Qiao Lanshu asked the two police officers to escort Han Ye home.","She waited until school let out, picked up the two younger children, and stopped by the market to buy some groceries before heading home.","As soon as she arrived, she saw Han Ye and Han Wenlin sitting in the courtyard of her house. Judging by the look of things, they had been there for quite a while.","Seeing them, Qiao Lanshu asked in surprise, “Director Han? What brings you here today? Aren’t you usually very busy?”","Han Wenlin was a busy man too. When Qin Yuanzheng was busy, he could still make it home for the night. But when Han Wenlin got busy, he was constantly out and about and often slept in his office at the Public Security Bureau. Sometimes he had to travel out of town for work, and each trip lasted ten days to half a month. During those periods, he would practically disappear.","After all these years, he was still single and had never remarried. To some extent, his demanding work had something to do with that.","Han Wenlin had already been there for quite some time. When he saw Qiao Lanshu return, he stood up with a smile and said, “Today’s matter with Han Ye really was all thanks to you, Xiao Qiao. We’re practically family, so I won’t bother with formalities. I came here today to invite your whole family out for a meal, as a way of thanking you.”","Whenever he had time during the holidays, Han Wenlin would often take Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng’s family out to eat.","The two families had long treated each other like relatives.","There was nothing unusual about getting together during the holidays, and Qiao Lanshu had never been shy about accepting his invitations.","But this time, it was neither a holiday nor a festival. Han Wenlin had come to invite the entire family to dinner solely because of Han Ye.","Han Wenlin had no wife, and Han Ye had no mother. Whenever something happened at home, Han Wenlin sometimes had no idea what to do.","The matter between Han Ye and Liu Wenqiu was a perfect example.","If Qiao Lanshu had not stepped in to help, no one knew how things would have turned out.","Naturally, Qiao Lanshu did not stand on ceremony with him. She smiled and nodded. “Then, Director Han, we’ll have to let you treat us today. I’ll bathe the children first. Once Brother Zheng gets home, we’ll head out.”","Han Wenlin nodded. “All right. Lao Qin has been busy with work lately, and I haven’t seen him in quite a while either. This is a good chance for us to get together.”","Qiao Lanshu said, “Then, Director Han, sit here for a while. I’m going to get things ready.”","With that, she carried the groceries into the kitchen.","After watching her go inside, Han Wenlin did not follow. Instead, he found a chair in the courtyard and sat down, chatting with the children from time to time.","Han Ye, however, paid no attention to his father. Since arriving, he had not even poured the man a glass of water.","Instead, he followed Qiao Lanshu into the kitchen, sticking close to her. He looked as though he wanted to say something, yet kept hesitating.","Qiao Lanshu finished putting away the groceries she had just bought and turned to look at him. “Enough. If you have something to say, just say it. Why are you dragging your feet and hemming and hawing?”","Han Ye: “...”","Her words made him feel a little embarrassed. He scratched his head and said guiltily, “Mom, I’m sorry. I really know I was wrong this time. So please... please don’t be mad at me anymore, okay?”","Qiao Lanshu glanced at him, then continued sorting things without saying anything or even looking at him.","When Han Ye saw this, he immediately grew anxious. “Mom, can’t you forgive me just this once? Kids make mistakes, right? No child can go through life without making any.”","At that moment, Xiaxia, who no one knew had entered when, suddenly spoke up. “Kids do make mistakes, but not every kid falls in love at such a young age.”","Han Ye glared at her and reached out to tug on her braid. In a stern voice, he said, “Qin Qiaoxia, how old are you? And you already know about young love? This is an adult topic. Go read your book, you little brat.”","Xiaxia rolled her eyes at him and turned to leave.","Qiao Lanshu sighed. “Sigh. I’m not even your real mother. How could I possibly have the nerve to discipline you?”","Han Ye immediately dropped to his knees and hugged her legs. “Mom, you raised me all these years. That makes you my real mother!”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","She was completely at a loss for words. “Get up.”","Han Ye got to his feet with a foolish grin. “Mom, does that mean you’re not mad at me anymore?”","Qiao Lanshu stood beside him and looked at him. “All right, tell me. What was going on with those kids? Why were they willing to fight alongside you? How did you meet them?”","Han Ye: “...”","He scratched his head, hesitating to speak.","Qiao Lanshu’s expression darkened. “No lying. Tell me the truth, and I’ll go easy on you!”","Han Ye finally understood why Qiao Lanshu had sarcastically said that she was not his real mother.","So that was what she had been waiting for.","He hesitated before saying, “If I tell you, you won’t yell at me, will you?”","Qiao Lanshu folded her arms and looked at him. “Tell me first. Then I’ll decide whether you deserve to be forgiven.”","Han Ye sighed several times before finally saying, “Actually, I had nothing to do on the weekends, so I went to take a look around the night market. Lots of people were bringing goods back from the south and selling them here. They could make several times what they paid. So I decided to give it a try too. After doing it for a while, I got to know them. They sell things as well, though they usually travel out of town to buy their goods and bring them back. Sometimes I get merchandise from them.”","Qiao Lanshu was visibly shocked when she heard this.","She had only gone to Beijing to study for half a year, yet after coming back, she already felt as if she barely knew this child anymore.","She repeated what she had heard. “You’ve been setting up a stall at the night market, and you’ve been getting your merchandise from them? You sell things together?”","Han Ye nodded. “That’s right. Mom, you have no idea how much money you can make selling at a stall!”","He sounded especially excited as he continued, “Lately, I’ve been selling cassette tapes and novels. They’re really profitable—the returns can be double what I paid.”","Cassette tapes in particular were incredibly lucrative.","Qiao Lanshu fell silent when she heard this.","She knew that as the country’s economy took off, doing business could bring in a great deal of money.","She had never objected to her children doing business. Whatever they wanted to do, she had always supported them, hoping they would pursue the things they loved.","That was why she remained silent for quite a while.","Worried that she was angry, Han Ye asked in a quiet voice, “Mom, are you mad?”","Qiao Lanshu shook her head and sighed. “I’m not angry. I just want to know— is your dream still to become a soldier in the People’s Liberation Army?”","“Of course it is!” Han Ye replied at once. “My dream has never changed!”","Han Wenlin had come from the military, and Qin Yuanzheng was still serving in the army.","Having grown up surrounded by their influence, Han Ye had always dreamed of joining the military and becoming a soldier who defended the country and its people.","That dream had never changed.","Qiao Lanshu looked at him and said earnestly, “Then why aren’t you studying properly? Why are you thinking about setting up a night stall instead? Han Ye, you’re not short of money.”","Han Ye was about to speak, but Qiao Lanshu continued.","“The friends you know are doing this because their families are poor. On top of that, they’ve dropped out of school and have no way to pursue a future through education, so they’ve had to find other ways to make a living.","“But you’re different. You have a dream, and your family can support you. So in my opinion, your main focus right now should be your studies. You’re already in your second year of middle school, and you’ll be entering your third year this September. If you don’t study hard and fail to get into high school, how are you ever going to become an officer?”","Qiao Lanshu continued, “Starting this year, the army is recruiting conscripts into special high-school classes. Didn’t your Uncle Qin tell you? If you want to stay in the military, you have to be a high-school graduate. You serve for two years, then take the military academy entrance exam. Once you graduate, you’ll become an officer. Don’t you want to take that path?”","Han Ye truly hadn’t thought that far ahead.","He simply wanted to become a soldier, and he was utterly determined about that dream.","At the same time, however, his grades weren’t very good. He didn’t particularly enjoy sitting in a classroom listening to lessons. He preferred riding his bicycle around, hanging out with his friends.","Whenever he made money reselling goods, he became excited. It made him feel like he had grown up and was capable of earning money himself.","Qiao Lanshu looked at him and said, “Go back and think about it carefully. Really think about the path you want to take in the military. How far do you want to go?","“If you only want to serve for a few years and then come out to do business, you can enlist right now. Just tell your Uncle Qin, and he can help you become a three-year conscript.","“But if you want to be like your Uncle Qin and stay in the military, if you want to accomplish something there, then you need to settle down and study hard for me. I can ask Teacher Zhao to tutor you in math. I’ll tutor you in Chinese, and I’ll find you a foreign-language teacher as well. You’re so smart—you’ll definitely be able to get into high school.”","Han Ye: “...”","The moment he heard the word “tutoring,” his entire face crumpled.","But he had taken his mother’s words to heart.","Who wouldn’t want to become an officer?","It was so impressive. So cool.","But if he wanted to become an officer, he had to study and acquire the knowledge of the new era. They couldn’t very well have an illiterate man leading troops into battle.","Han Ye’s expression gradually grew serious.","Seeing that he was listening, Qiao Lanshu added one last thing.","“How about this? I already got you a week off, didn’t I? Don’t go out for the next few days, and especially don’t go to the night market. Go back and research those military academies. Learn more about them and see if there’s one you’d like to attend. For example, the Army Armored Forces Academy is very well-known. Find out what scores and qualifications are needed to get in, then choose one school as your goal. From now on, we’ll work toward it together. How does that sound?”","Qiao Lanshu patted him on the shoulder and tricked him—no, encouraged him, saying, “Han Ye, you’re the eldest brother. You have to work hard! Your younger brothers and sisters all look up to you. If you get into a military academy and become an officer in the future, you can be An’an’s protector too. An’an is going to join the military someday as well, isn’t he?","“When An’an joins the army and someone bullies him, you can come charging out as a company commander and say, ‘That’s my brother. Let’s see who dares lay a hand on him!’ Wouldn’t that be impressive?”","Han Ye: “...”","Han Ye rubbed his chin. After thinking it over, he nodded. “That would be pretty impressive.”","Qiao Lanshu continued, “And when I go to work and tell my colleagues that my eldest son is a company commander in the army, the youngest company commander in the entire military, do you think they’ll be envious? Won’t I have plenty to be proud of?”","Han Ye nodded seriously. “That’s right, Mom. I won’t just become a company commander. I can become a regimental commander, a division commander—”","He grew more and more carried away. “Maybe I’ll even become a commander-in-chief someday!”","Qiao Lanshu couldn’t bear to crush his enthusiasm.","Keeping a straight face, she nodded solemnly. “That’s right. It’s entirely possible that you’ll become even more impressive than your Uncle Qin. Your Uncle Qin might end up serving under you.”","Han Ye was absolutely fired up by then.","“Mom, I’m going back to do some research right now. I heard there’s also something called the Ordnance Engineering College. It sounds pretty good too...”","As he spoke, he dashed out like a gust of wind.","Qiao Lanshu chased after him and called, “Hey, don’t rush! Eat first!”","Han Ye shouted back, “I’m not eating! I’m not hungry!”","Then he raced back to his room and slammed the door behind him.","Qiao Lanshu stared at his tightly closed door and thought to herself, Oh no. Did I give him too much of a motivational speech?","Hearing the commotion in the courtyard, Han Wenlin walked to the doorway and looked inside.","“What happened? What’s wrong with Han Ye now?”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","All she could say was, “He went back to his room to study. Such a good boy.”","Han Wenlin: “...”","He gave her a baffled look that seemed to say, What are you talking about?","The word “good” appearing alongside Han Ye was downright terrifying, you know.","Half an hour later, Qiao Lanshu heated some water and had An’an and Xiaxia take turns bathing.","She then went to call Han Ye. Only then did he reluctantly come out, hurriedly take a shower, and run back to his room.","When Han Wenlin took everyone to eat, Han Ye still refused to come.","Inside his room, he tuned the radio to the military channel.","Then he took every book off the shelf and began flipping through them. He even pulled out several pamphlets introducing military academies and started reading those as well.","Qin Yuanzheng changed his clothes, washed his hands and face, and stood at the doorway of Han Ye’s room for a few moments. He then walked out into the courtyard and asked Han Wenlin, “What’s happened to Han Ye? Why is he suddenly studying so seriously? He’s not even coming out to eat.”","Could he have been possessed?","Han Wenlin looked just as bewildered. “I have no idea. Maybe Liu Wenqiu’s behavior gave him such a shock that he decided to turn over a new leaf, study hard, and strive to become a pillar of the nation?”","Qin Yuanzheng: “...”"]},{"number":270,"title":"Chapter 270: Makeup Class","paragraphs":["Although Han Ye kept saying he wasn’t going, young people were still growing, and they burned through a lot of energy. No matter how unwilling he was mentally, his body simply couldn’t hold out.","Just thinking about the roast chicken, roast duck, braised pork knuckle, meat buns, chive rolls, and boiled mutton at the restaurant was enough to make it impossible for him to resist.","So in the end, he still went to the restaurant to eat with the family.","Qiao Lanshu had handled everything concerning Liu Wenqiu’s family. Han Wenlin hadn’t gotten involved at all, so he was extremely grateful to Qiao Lanshu.","Qin Yuanzheng didn’t find out about the matter until after work, when he was already sitting in the restaurant eating with them.","At the table, Han Wenlin barely ate anything. He just kept thanking Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu became embarrassed by his gratitude and said with a smile, “Director Han, you really don’t need to be so polite. Han Ye is my child too. He’s called me Mom since he was little, so anything concerning him concerns me as well.”","Then she added, “Besides, over the years, An’an and Xiaxia have often eaten at the cafeteria of your Public Security Bureau. You were the one who paid for their meals, and I never stood on ceremony with you about that. So you don’t need to be so polite with me either.”","Han Wenlin glanced at the three children sitting nearby and said emotionally, “Ah, it was only a meal. It cost a little money, that’s all. We’ve both been working for so many years—we understand that anything money can solve is a minor matter. As parents, what children need most is companionship. I’ve been so busy with work these past ten-odd years that I failed to spend enough time with Han Ye or guide him properly. That was my dereliction of duty.”","Han Ye fell silent and looked uncomfortable when he suddenly heard his father say something so sentimental. He rubbed his arm and said to Han Wenlin, “Enough, Director Han. Say a little less of that sentimental stuff. You’re making me lose my appetite.”","Han Wenlin glared at him. “I wasn’t saying it for you to hear. Why do you have so much to say?”","Han Ye: “...”","Han Ye covered his ears with both hands. Great—he had just felt moved for nothing. What a waste of emotion.","Han Wenlin turned back to Qiao Lanshu and said, “All these years, I’m so glad you were able to help take care of Han Ye. He never had a mother growing up, so he’s always been very dependent on you. You raised him well, too. You know that our whole family has always been deeply grateful to you.”","Qiao Lanshu was made even more embarrassed by his words.","After all, despite the many years their two families had spent in close contact, they rarely said anything so sentimental to each other.","Han Wenlin’s outpouring of emotion seemed to indicate that what had happened between Han Ye and Liu Wenqiu had affected him deeply.","Qin Yuanzheng had been sitting beside Qiao Lanshu, listening to them talk. At this point, he couldn’t help joining in. “Old Han, there’s no need to say all that. We’ve known each other for so long. We’ve simply helped and supported each other through all these years. As long as we understand that in our hearts, it’s enough.”","Over the years, Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu had also often relied on Han Wenlin for help.","Qin Yuanzheng and Han Wenlin were not brothers, but they were closer than brothers.","Neither of them was from the area, yet they had worked, lived, and settled here for many years, with few relatives nearby.","That was why finding each other as friends—completely trustworthy friends—was so rare and precious.","Han Wenlin let out a long sigh and said with deep feeling, “I didn’t want to say all this either. It’s just that today, I suddenly realized that the child has grown up.”","He had always thought of Han Ye as a little boy.","In his memories, Han Ye had always looked very young.","So when he heard that Han Ye was dating a girl from his class, he was startled.","How old was the boy? How had he suddenly started dating someone?","At the time, Han Wenlin had been completely stunned. But now, taking a closer look at Han Ye, he realized that the boy was almost as tall as he was. He looked every bit like a teenager. How could he still be considered a little child?","Ah, he had been neglectful. Fortunately, there had been Qiao Lanshu.","It really was impossible to run a household without a woman.","...","Han Wenlin sighed and lamented for a while before picking up his chopsticks and standing to put some food in Qiao Lanshu’s bowl. “The beef here is quite good. Try it and see how you like it.”","Qiao Lanshu smiled and thanked him as she looked at the meat in her bowl, preparing to eat.","Qin Yuanzheng had been sitting beside Qiao Lanshu and listening for quite some time. He had finally figured out what was going on.","Expressionless, he picked up his chopsticks and reached over. With one swift, decisive movement, he took the beef Han Wenlin had placed in Qiao Lanshu’s bowl and transferred it into his own.","Qiao Lanshu and Han Wenlin both stared at him, utterly bewildered.","Qin Yuanzheng ate the beef. Only then did he look expressionlessly at Han Ye and say, “Han Ye, if you don’t want to study anymore, then go out and find a job as soon as possible. You seem to have plenty of energy every day. Why not go work at a construction site and carry bricks? The sites around here are short-handed lately. You’re strong enough to do the work of two people, so you can earn two wages and easily support yourself.”","Han Ye: “...”","Today, Han Ye had only done one outrageous thing, and he hadn’t even succeeded. Qiao Lanshu had caught him halfway and dragged him to the Public Security Bureau.","He had spent the entire day at the station, squirming with anxiety and enduring Han Wenlin’s criticism.","Now Qin Yuanzheng was making sarcastic remarks at his expense.","For this single incident, Han Ye had been lectured by his own father, then by Qiao Lanshu, and now by Qin Yuanzheng.","Three adults were taking turns scolding him, while his younger siblings were mocking him from the sidelines.","And yet he couldn’t talk back. He could only lower his head and shovel rice into his mouth, letting them say whatever they wanted.","What choice did he have? He was the one who had done something wrong.","He deserved it.","Han Ye lowered his head dejectedly. “I want to study! I never said I didn’t want to study! I really know I was wrong, so please stop talking about it.”","Qin Yuanzheng gave a cold snort and finally let the matter drop.","...","After dinner, Han Ye took Han Wenlin home.","Qin Yuanzheng, meanwhile, took Qiao Lanshu and the two children back to their own home.","The restaurant was very close to their house, so the family of four walked back.","Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu held hands as they walked, while Qin Qiao’an and Qin Qiaoxia followed behind them, playing around and chattering away.","Qiao Lanshu said quietly, “Why did you eat the food Director Han put in my bowl just now?”","When Han Wenlin had seen Qin Yuanzheng place the food in Qiao Lanshu’s bowl, his expression had become rather peculiar. In short, the atmosphere had been quite awkward.","Qin Yuanzheng said solemnly, “He’s a widower. Why is he making such a show of attentiveness for no reason?”","Qiao Lanshu stared at him, astonished.","Qin Yuanzheng continued expressionlessly, “It’s bad enough that Han Ye calls you Mom every day. Now his father wants to join in too. Do you really think he doesn’t have ulterior motives toward you?”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","She was speechless. In a low voice, she said, “Chief Qin, you really need to rein yourself in. I’m not a banknote—do you think everyone is going to like me? Director Han is such an upright and proper man. How could he possibly... Honestly, stop imagining things. Don’t think about nonsense like that in the future.”","She felt that over the past two years, Qin Yuanzheng had become more and more prone to jealousy.","He got jealous whenever she went home from work with a male colleague.","When she had gone to Beijing for training for six months and replied to his letters a few days late, he had also grown suspicious and suspiciously anxious.","And now, he had even started suspecting Han Wenlin.","The two families had been close for so many years that they practically treated each other like relatives.","If Qin Yuanzheng put it that way, then she would never be able to get along normally with Han Wenlin again.","Qin Yuanzheng’s expression was rather unpleasant.","He was dissatisfied with everyone, anyway.","Any single man who lingered around Qiao Lanshu made him suspect that the man had taken a fancy to her.","There was nothing he could do about it. Who could blame him when his wife was so outstanding?","She was beautiful, adorable, gentle, cultured, capable, excellent at her work, and accomplished.","Anyone who saw her would fall in love with her, wouldn’t they?","Thinking this, Qin Yuanzheng reached out and put an arm around Qiao Lanshu’s shoulders, pulling her close as he said, “You know I get jealous easily, so from now on, keep a little distance from other men. Don’t chat and laugh with them all the time. Don’t you know that some men aren’t good people? If you look at one, he’ll think you’re interested in him. If you smile at him, he’ll think you’ve fallen in love with him. Then he’ll start pestering you. When you reject him, he might even turn around and accuse you of flirting with him first. By then, you won’t be able to explain yourself even if you have a hundred mouths.”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","Her expression was extremely complicated as she looked at Qin Yuanzheng, wondering whether he had been possessed by something.","The stern and serious Chief Qin was actually capable of saying things like that. If the soldiers under his command heard him, it would probably make the military’s internal news.","Qin Yuanzheng continued, “But our Xiaxia has a pretty good personality. She doesn’t pay attention to anyone, which is excellent. It saves us a lot of trouble.”","At that, Qiao Lanshu turned around.","She saw Qin Qiao'an darting around like an excitable puppy. He couldn’t even walk properly, jumping up to pluck leaves one moment, running laps along the roadside the next, and then rolling around on the ground.","A moment later, he was circling Xiaxia again. His mouth never stopped, chattering and muttering nonstop.","Xiaxia, meanwhile, quietly followed behind her parents the entire time, both hands in her pockets. She listened to her brother talk, nodding from time to time and responding with an “Mm,” hardly saying anything herself.","Qiao Lanshu turned back and said quietly to Qin Yuanzheng, “It’s really strange. Both of us have pretty normal personalities, so how did we end up with two children who are complete opposites—one so quiet and the other so energetic?”","Compared with them, Han Ye’s personality seemed pretty normal after all.","Qin Yuanzheng was puzzled too. “I think Xiaxia takes after you. She’s obedient and quiet, and she likes reading. It’s true that she doesn’t talk much, but you’re not exactly talkative either.”","Qiao Lanshu was a very quiet girl herself. She had been an obedient child from the time she was little, though she wasn’t quite as withdrawn as Xiaxia.","Qin Qiao'an, on the other hand, was far too energetic and far too fond of talking. In the past, he had always pestered Han Ye, who was willing to play with him and had saved Qiao Lanshu quite a bit of trouble.","Now that Han Ye was no longer around, Qin Qiao'an could only play with Xiaxia. What a handful he was.","Qin Yuanzheng added, “An'an definitely doesn’t take after me. I’m not nearly as talkative as he is.”","The couple chatted as they made their way home.","It was already getting late, so once they returned, they prepared for bed.","The next day, on her way to work, Qiao Lanshu stopped by to see Ms. Zhao.","When Zhao Yanfang saw her approaching, she got up and walked with her into the corridor outside the office. She asked, “Teacher Qiao, what brings you here? Are you here to ask about Liu Wenqiu? Nothing has happened on the Liu family’s side, so don’t worry.”","Qiao Lanshu smiled and shook her head. “No. I wanted to ask whether you’re free on Saturdays and Sundays. I’d like to ask you to tutor Han Ye.”","Zhao Yanfang taught mathematics, while Qiao Lanshu taught Chinese, so the two of them were perfectly suited to tutor Han Ye.","It was the first time Zhao Yanfang had ever heard of parents arranging tutoring for their child.","Teachers in those days were all very responsible, but even if a teacher was willing to give a particular student extra lessons, the student might not necessarily be willing to stay.","After all, once the children finished school, they still had to go home to do housework and farm work, help take care of their younger siblings, or cook for themselves.","Who had time to stay behind for extra lessons?","Zhao Yanfang was still young, passionate, and full of enthusiasm for teaching. Although she and Qiao Lanshu were about the same age—twenty-six or twenty-seven—she had previously been a sent-down youth and had spent several years living in the countryside.","After the college entrance examination was reinstated, she had managed to return to the city by passing the exam and getting into university.","Originally, she had been assigned to teach at a high school, but someone else had taken the position. Since she was from out of town, she was assigned to a middle school instead, where her salary was several dozen yuan lower.","Zhao Yanfang didn’t mind. As long as she could remain at a school and work as a teacher, she considered herself extremely fortunate.","No matter what, her life now was far better than it had been when she was a sent-down youth.","She smiled and said, “Of course I’m free. You know I’m from out of town. I have no relatives here, and I’m not married. I just stay in the staff dormitory on weekends, with nothing much to do. But is Han Ye willing to take extra lessons? He won’t cause a scene, will he?”","With Han Ye’s personality—he was so lazy that he could barely be bothered to attend class—she almost suspected that the sun had risen in the west.","Qiao Lanshu said, “He won’t make trouble. The lessons will be held at my house, and I’ll keep an eye on him myself. If he dares not to study properly, he’ll find out exactly what I’ll do to him.”","Zhao Yanfang looked at Qiao Lanshu with some envy. “Teacher Qiao, sometimes I really envy you. All your children are so good-looking, and they’re all so well-behaved.”","Qiao Lanshu smiled at her. “Once you get married, you can have a few of your own.”","Zhao Yanfang laughed and shook her head. “That’s still a long way off for me. I haven’t thought about those things yet.”","The two women discussed the matter and finalized the tutoring arrangements.","Based on what Zhao Yanfang knew, Han Ye was actually quite intelligent. Although he didn’t put much effort into mathematics, his grades weren’t particularly poor. He was somewhere in the middle of the class.","But getting into high school was difficult. There were only a limited number of places, and many students chose to apply to technical secondary schools to be on the safe side.","If Han Ye wanted to get into high school, he would have to study hard and improve his grades.","That meant he had to start reviewing mathematics from the first year of middle school.","When Qiao Lanshu left, she said to Zhao Yanfang, “Then it’s settled. From now on, come to my house every Saturday morning and give him two lessons. I’ll pay you at the end of each month.”","Zhao Yanfang didn’t stand on ceremony. She smiled and nodded. “All right. I’ll come over at nine every Saturday.”","They arranged for mathematics tutoring on Saturday mornings, Chinese and English in the afternoon, and Sunday as Han Ye’s free day.","The only problem was finding an English teacher.","After thinking it over, Qiao Lanshu decided to ask several of her university classmates whether they knew any English teachers.","And so Han Ye was arranged from head to toe by Qiao Lanshu.","From that day onward, he began two long years of grueling extra lessons."]},{"number":271,"title":"Chapter 271: Investment Bell Plum","paragraphs":["That weekend, Qiao Lanshu went to Wencheng Normal University early in the morning—the alma mater where she had once studied.","She had come to find one of her former teachers and ask whether she could recommend an English tutor.","The country was beginning to place greater emphasis on English education. Since 1983, English scores had been included in the total for the national college entrance examination, making the subject impossible to avoid.","Unfortunately, Qiao Lanshu’s own English foundation was weak. When she had taken the college entrance examination in 1977, foreign languages had not yet been tested.","Neither she nor Qin Yuanzheng could help the children with English, so they would have to leave it to a professional.","Her teacher immediately introduced her to a young university professor of foreign languages.","The professor was not yet thirty. He was biracial and had gone abroad with his family during the chaotic years. After the country opened up and called on talented people to return and help build the nation, he had come back with his family. Since his field was philosophy, becoming a professor was practically the only suitable job he could find in those days.","Qiao Lanshu met him at the university. The two of them chatted in the library, and he asked with a smile, “Comrade Qiao, how many children in your family need tutoring?”","“Just one,” Qiao Lanshu replied. “He’s in the eighth grade. I want him to get into high school, but his English is terrible.”","Lang Yangqiu nodded and sighed. “There are still a great many illiterate people in our country. Foreign languages only officially became part of the college entrance examination in 1983, so it’s only been three or four years. And according to our textbooks, children don’t even begin learning the alphabet until the first year of junior middle school. It’s perfectly normal for their English foundation to be weak. Since your child needs tutoring, I assume he’ll have to start with the first-year textbook?”","Qiao Lanshu nodded. “Yes, we’ll start with the basics.”","Professor Lang continued, “Since that’s the case, I heard you have three children. Why not let the two younger ones attend the lessons as well? They’re still in primary school, right? The earlier children are exposed to a language, the faster they learn.”","Professor Lang had grown up abroad, after all, and his foreign-language skills were excellent. It really would be a wonderful opportunity for Qin Qiao'an and Xiaxia to study with him.","After considering the suggestion, Qiao Lanshu said gratefully, “If you don’t mind, Professor Lang, that would be wonderful.”","Lang Yangqiu waved his hand with a smile. “It’s no trouble. Since you were Professor Rong’s student, that makes me your senior schoolmate. I was Professor Rong’s student too.”","Lang Yangqiu was not short of money and had never actually considered tutoring children.","But Professor Rong had not asked whether he was willing. She had merely mentioned that one of her students was looking for a tutor for her children, and then recommended him.","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu smiled. “In that case, I’ll have to give Professor Rong a generous gift to thank her for the recommendation.”","Lang Yangqiu teased her, “You can include my share too. I’ve been so busy tutoring the children lately that I won’t have time to visit our teacher.”","...","After agreeing on the tutoring schedule with Lang Yangqiu, Qiao Lanshu had finally taken care of one major matter and was in high spirits.","She rode her bicycle to the market to buy groceries. Thinking that all three children were growing and needed to nourish their minds as well, she bought some walnuts and a pig’s trotter. She planned to stew the walnuts and pig’s trotter for them when she got home.","When she returned, all three children were there. Xiaxia was sitting in a recliner in the courtyard with a book in her hands.","An'an was bored, playing with the dog by himself.","The puppy had only recently joined the family. After all, Dahuang, Han Ye’s favorite dog when he was little, had already died of old age.","This new puppy was only a few months old.","As soon as An'an saw Qiao Lanshu come home, he hurried over with the dog in his arms. “Mom, Mom, you’re finally back!”","He put the dog down and ran over to help her carry the groceries. “Mom, what are we having for dinner?”","Qiao Lanshu gave him a disdainful look. “You don’t need to carry anything. Go wash those filthy black paws of yours. I bought bread today. You can have some in a little while.”","The moment they heard there was bread, even Xiaxia stopped reading. The siblings washed their hands and ran over to get some.","As Qiao Lanshu sorted the groceries in the kitchen, she asked in confusion, “Your big brother isn’t home?”","“He came back,” An'an said around a mouthful of bread. “He got home at noon, but the moment he came back, he holed up in his room. He won’t even take me out to play.”","Qin Qiao'an had friends among the neighbors, but after spending so much time with Han Ye, he found playing with children his own age boring. He always felt that they were rather slow and knew nothing and could do nothing.","When Qiao Lanshu heard this, she put down what she was holding and went to Han Ye’s door. She knocked.","“Han Ye? Are you in there?”","Han Ye called back from inside, “I’m here.”","He opened the door and looked at Qiao Lanshu. “Mom, did you need something?”","Qiao Lanshu looked him up and down several times before asking, “What have you been doing in your room? An'an says you’ve been in there all day.”","Han Ye scratched his head, looking a little embarrassed. “I’m still looking up information about the military academies. I talked to Dad yesterday, and he suggested that I apply to the Military Armored Academy. So I looked into the school’s admissions requirements. The competition is fierce every year. Last year, they only recruited three students from Wencheng, and the requirements were extremely strict...”","Han Ye had always been carefree and had only thought about joining the military someday. He had never considered the possibility that he might fail to get into a military academy.","But after researching the requirements over the past two days, he finally realized that something was wrong.","Military academies had such strict standards. It was entirely possible that he might not get in!","What would he do if he failed?","He had never thought about it.","Now he was a little panicked—and a little regretful. He should have taken his studies seriously from the beginning.","What if he served his two years in the military and passed all the physical and training requirements, only to be rejected because of his academic scores? Wouldn’t he regret it for the rest of his life?","Seeing him like this, Qiao Lanshu felt relieved.","“The fact that you’ve realized this now means it’s not too late. Fortunately, you’re only in the eighth grade, not your second year of high school. All right, don’t be nervous. I’ll help you with your studies. As for matters concerning the military, don’t you still have two fathers? Relax. Focus on your schoolwork first, and we’ll deal with everything else later.”","Qiao Lanshu had great confidence in Han Ye.","He was strong and physically fit, having trained with Qin Yuanzheng since childhood. His fighting skills were excellent as well.","If he joined the military, he would definitely make a fine soldier.","As long as he could keep up academically, getting into a military academy would certainly be no problem.","After Qiao Lanshu encouraged him, a smile appeared on Han Ye’s face too.","He came out of the room and draped an arm over her shoulder. “Mom, I knew you wouldn’t abandon me! I’ll definitely study hard from now on!”","Qiao Lanshu nodded. “Then study hard with your tutor. I’ve already found you one, so you’d better take your studies seriously.”","Han Ye didn’t think tutoring would be a big deal. He asked, “How long will I need lessons? A month? Or a whole semester?”","A whole semester sounded rather long to him. By his way of thinking, a month or two should be enough. He was so smart, after all—surely he could learn everything by then.","Qiao Lanshu glanced at him. “What are you thinking? How could it be only one month?”","Han Ye sensed that something was wrong and asked cautiously, “Then how long will I have to take extra lessons?”","Qiao Lanshu said, “Two years. Until you get into high school.”","Han Ye: “!!!”","He was only in his second year of middle school. If he had to take extra lessons for another two years, wouldn’t he go crazy?","Seeing his face change dramatically, Qiao Lanshu showed no mercy. She added, “And after you get into high school, if you still don’t listen in class or study properly, you’ll have to take extra lessons in high school too. Understood?”","Han Ye: “...”","Han Ye felt as if the sky were falling.","He was actually going to have to take extra lessons for two years.","His days of freedom were gone forever!","Still, Han Ye did not complain. When he thought of the military academy’s stringent admissions requirements, he realized that without such capable parents supporting him, he might not be able to compete with the other applicants.","There were too many outstanding people in the world. He was merely an ordinary one among them.","If he did not work harder than everyone else, how could he stand out and be chosen from among thousands?","And so, Han Ye began taking extra lessons that week.","On Saturday mornings, Teacher Zhao and Teacher Qiao took turns tutoring him in mathematics and English.","In the afternoons, Professor Lang would bring English textbooks and magazines over and teach English to the three children.","Han Ye, An'an, and Xiaxia sat in the courtyard while Professor Lang gave them their first introduction to the language.","During their breaks, Professor Lang would read English books to them—literary works by foreign authors. Hearing him read them aloud in English made the whole experience feel wonderfully romantic.","This was Xiaxia’s favorite part. At Professor Lang’s recommendation, she had begun reading Shakespeare.","Sometimes, Professor Lang would even take the three children to the cinema and pay for the tickets himself.","Han Ye had initially been very resistant to foreign-language lessons. His foundation in English was poor, and learning a foreign language was no easy task for a second-year middle school student.","Unlike Qin Qiao'an and Xiaxia, who were still young and could learn much more easily.","But Professor Lang was simply too kind to them. Every time he came, he brought them snacks and soda, and he took them to the movies as well. Han Ye liked Professor Lang, and gradually, he came to enjoy listening to his lessons.","Once Han Ye and An'an stayed home obediently to study and stopped going out to cause trouble, peaceful days passed in the blink of an eye.","A year later, Guan Wenjun was transferred to the provincial government and came to work in Wencheng.","He brought his wife and children with him and moved into a newly built residential compound for government employees.","His two sons, one in kindergarten and the other in elementary school, attended schools near their new home. Since those schools were some distance away, they did not attend the same school as Qiao Lanshu.","Of course, the happiest person about their move to Wencheng was Zhong Mei.","On the day they moved in, Qiao Lanshu had to work, so she did not go over during the day.","After work, she drove there with Qin Yuanzheng and the children.","Although both families lived in Wencheng, one was in the east and the other in the west. They were quite far apart, and even by car, the journey took nearly half an hour.","The two families were already very close. As soon as Qiao Lanshu arrived at the entrance to the residential compound, Guan Wenjun was there waiting for her.","Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng carried a live chicken and some dried noodles they had bought and walked over to him.","With a smile, Qiao Lanshu said, “Section Chief Guan, congratulations on your promotion!”","Guan Wenjun had been transferred to the Organization Department, a position he had been working toward for some time. He said that the department would be relatively less busy.","Guan Wenjun beamed. “Thank you, Teacher Qiao. I heard that you’ve been promoted too. Congratulations to both of us!”","Qiao Lanshu had been promoted to team leader, but the position had only made her workload heavier. She had recently been working until midnight every day and was exhausted.","She shook her head helplessly. “Congratulations to both of us. By the way, where’s Zhong Mei?”","As he spoke, Guan Wenjun took a handful of White Rabbit candies from his pocket and handed them to An'an and Xiaxia. Then he said, “She’s at home unpacking and tidying things up. Come on, I’ll show you around.”","At that time, housing consisted of work-unit dormitories. If you had a job, you had a place to live; if you left the job, the housing would be taken back. Private individuals were not allowed to buy or sell homes.","Guan Wenjun’s apartment was on the third floor of the dormitory building. It was quite spacious, with a balcony and three bedrooms. The building had been constructed within the past two years, so the apartment was completely new.","Zhong Mei loved the place. She had been thrilled ever since they moved in.","She spent the entire day organizing the rooms with the children and had finally gotten most of everything put away.","Once Qiao Lanshu arrived, the four children went off to play together, while Qiao Lanshu and Zhong Mei stayed in the kitchen, chatting as they prepared dinner.","Qiao Lanshu asked Zhong Mei, “The last time we saw each other was seven or eight months ago. You said then that you were preparing to open a shop. How’s that going?”","Zhong Mei had actually mentioned opening a shop a long time ago.","But nothing had ever come of it. It had remained nothing more than an idea in her head.","As she trimmed the green beans, she said, “Oh, the children were too little before, and I could never find the time. Last year, I actually saw a storefront in Longcheng, but Guan Wenjun wouldn’t let me open a shop.”","Qiao Lanshu asked curiously, “Why not?”","As she sorted through the beans, she glanced at Zhong Mei and teased her, “You listen to him now? That doesn’t sound like you at all.”","After marrying Guan Wenjun, Zhong Mei had him completely wrapped around her finger.","Guan Wenjun had a rather sharp tongue, but he was not a bad person. Whenever Zhong Mei coaxed him a little, he became completely dazed and compliant.","Later, Zhong Mei became pregnant and gave birth to two sons in succession. After that, Guan Wenjun lost all control over the household finances.","Every month, as soon as his salary arrived—before he had even had time to warm it in his hands—Zhong Mei took it away.","If he wanted to buy even a steamed bun, he had to ask Zhong Mei for money. In short, Zhong Mei was the one who called all the shots at home.","Qiao Lanshu’s teasing made Zhong Mei a little embarrassed.","She lowered her voice. “He said he was trying to find the right connections to see whether he could be transferred to the provincial government. If that happened, we’d have to move to Wencheng, so I didn’t open a shop in Longcheng.”","Zhong Mei continued, “Now that our whole family has moved to Wencheng, I’m definitely going to open one. I want to run a general store and sell all kinds of things. Those stores can make a lot of money—the profit on many items is two or three times the cost.”","Zhong Mei had worked odd jobs since she was young, always thinking of ways to make money. She had a keen sense of the market.","In the past, circumstances had been restrictive, and no one had had much opportunity to develop a business. But now it was the 1980s, and private enterprise was springing up everywhere. Even Han Ye knew that he could make money by buying and reselling goods, let alone Zhong Mei.","She was nearly thirty now, with plenty of life experience, some savings, and a husband who could support her if necessary.","She wanted to learn how to do business.","She wanted to make a fortune.","Qiao Lanshu thought it was a good idea. She asked Zhong Mei, “Opening a shop will require quite a bit of money, won’t it? Do you have enough?”","Zhong Mei paused before answering, “Not quite. I’ll save up a little more.”","Qiao Lanshu smiled and shot her an exasperated look. “You really are something. If you don’t have enough money, why didn’t you come to me? Stop saving. Go open the shop right now. I’ll invest and become your partner. How does that sound?”","In any case, Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng did not have the time to run a business themselves.","They both had careers of their own, and neither of them planned to change professions.","Qiao Lanshu had managed to save up some money over the years. Since it was just sitting there, she figured she might as well invest it in Zhong Mei.","She trusted Zhong Mei’s abilities and judgment and was sure she would succeed.","When Zhong Mei heard her say that, however, she hesitated. “Lanshu, maybe you should think it over a little more? I’m worried that...”","Qiao Lanshu cut her off. “Worried about what? You’re sure to succeed.”","If Zhong Mei lost the money, Qiao Lanshu would simply consider it support for her friend.","But if Zhong Mei made it big, then it could be money set aside for her children’s future.","Qiao Lanshu took things in stride. She told Zhong Mei, “It’s fine. Just go ahead and do it without holding back. Even if you lose it all, it won’t matter. We both have jobs—we won’t starve.”"]},{"number":272,"title":"Chapter 272: Doing Business","paragraphs":["With Qiao Lanshu’s support, Zhong Mei was brimming with confidence in her business!","Although this was only her first day in Wencheng and she had yet to finish settling in at home, she already had grand plans for the future.","The dining table was small, so the four adults ate at one table while the four children ate at another.","Zhong Mei rather missed Han Ye, so she asked Qiao Lanshu, “Where’s Niuwa? Why didn’t he come see me?”","Qiao Lanshu laughed. “Him? He went back to his own home. He didn’t come over today, so he doesn’t know that you moved.”","Only then did Zhong Mei say, “I thought he’d forgotten about me.”","Niuwa had been such a mischievous child when he was little, and Zhong Mei had spent no small amount of time looking after him. During the New Year celebrations, she had also given Han Ye plenty of lucky money.","As they talked, Qiao Lanshu brought up the incident involving Han Ye and Liu Wenqiu’s love letters. Zhong Mei was so furious that she spent quite a while cursing.","She even said that if anyone dared to slander her son like that in the future, she would take a kitchen knife straight to the school and deal with them herself.","Her words made Qiao Lanshu burst out laughing, but Guan Wenjun, who was sitting beside them, wore a complicated expression.","He reminded her, “Don’t forget that I’m your husband, will you? You can’t just pick up a kitchen knife whenever you feel like it. If something goes wrong, I could lose my job, so take it easy.”","Zhong Mei: “......”","Zhong Mei then said, “Don’t worry. Once I grow the business and become a big boss, it’ll be perfect if you lose your job. You can come home and look after the children and do the cooking.”","Guan Wenjun: “???”","Guan Wenjun closed his eyes and said to Qiao Lanshu, “Comrade Xiao Qiao, look at her. Talk some sense into her!”","Qin Yuanzheng continued eating as he said, “It’s your wife we’re talking about. Say a little less. Your children are already this old—why are you still nitpicking over everything?”","Qin Yuanzheng really couldn’t stand watching anymore. He had never seen a man who loved arguing with his wife so much.","He couldn’t win an argument, and he couldn’t beat her either.","What else could he do—divorce her?","Guan Wenjun let out a long, weary sigh and said quietly, “I used to think Zhong Mei had the same personality as your wife—gentle, virtuous, and easygoing. But after I married her, I discovered that their personalities are completely opposite.”","He had practically married a shrew.","Qin Yuanzheng reproached him. “Zhong Mei is a good woman too. She’s already given you two children. What else is there that you can’t let her have her way over?”","Guan Wenjun rolled his eyes at Qin Yuanzheng. “Fine. I can’t be bothered to argue with you anymore.”","No matter what he said to Qin Yuanzheng, Qin Yuanzheng always told him the same things: he should give in to his wife, coax his wife, remember that his wife was always right, and never go against her.","Guan Wenjun pointed at Qin Yuanzheng and said, “Lao Qin, I really didn’t expect you to be this kind of person—a henpecked husband.”","Qin Yuanzheng smiled and shook his head without saying anything else.","The two men ate in silence while listening to Zhong Mei and Qiao Lanshu discuss her grand plan for getting rich.","Zhong Mei asked Qiao Lanshu, “Are you free this weekend? Come with me to look at some shops. I want to open a general store somewhere with lots of residential areas. There has to be enough people around for the business to thrive.”","Qiao Lanshu nodded. “I have to tutor Han Ye on Saturday morning, but I’m free Sunday afternoon.”","When Zhong Mei heard that the children were taking extra lessons, she asked a few more questions. Then she said in shock, “You’re even teaching the children a foreign language?”","Guan Wenjun frowned. “What’s the point of learning that foreign stuff? Isn’t Chinese good enough?”","Zhong Mei immediately snapped at him, “You’re just too old-fashioned. Foreign languages are absolutely worth learning, I’m telling you. In the future, as our country continues to develop, I’ll have to do business with foreigners too. How am I supposed to make money from them if I can’t speak their language?”","Guan Wenjun muttered, “If they want to do business here, can’t they learn Chinese?”","Zhong Mei ignored him. She asked Qiao Lanshu about the foreign-language teacher, and after Qiao Lanshu’s family left, she cornered Guan Wenjun.","“You’re always going on about how you’re a section chief with connections everywhere, aren’t you? Then go find the children a foreign-language teacher too!”","Guan Wenjun squeezed his eyes shut in misery. “Comrade Zhong Mei, where am I supposed to find a foreign-language teacher? The foreign-language teachers at the schools only know their ABCs. They might not even be able to say hello in English. You want to hire them to teach the children? You might as well stop wasting your money now.”","Zhong Mei sighed as well. Somewhat disappointed, she said, “But the foreign-language teacher on Lanshu’s side is a professor at Wencheng Normal University. He’s only teaching her children because of a personal favor. I can’t shamelessly send our children over there too.”","Guan Wenjun came over and put an arm around her. “Oh, it’s getting late. We should go to bed. We can talk about this foreign-language business another time. The children are still young, so there’s no rush.”","Zhong Mei had no solution for the moment, but she was already in a bad mood. She shoved Guan Wenjun away and scolded him, “All you think about day in and day out is what happens in bed. Can’t you think about something else and give me a break?”","Sometimes Zhong Mei felt that Guan Wenjun was her eldest son, with two younger sons below him. Raising three sons at once was truly exhausting.","There were times when she didn’t even want to deal with Guan Wenjun.","So she went straight to the room next door and slept with the two children.","Guan Wenjun was furious.","Zhong Mei was always refusing to sleep with him. He was genuinely going to get angry!","......","Over the next six months, Qiao Lanshu worked during the day, tutored Han Ye, and accompanied Zhong Mei as she searched for a storefront.","In the end, Zhong Mei finally found a place she was satisfied with, and the landlord was willing to rent it to her.","The shop stood beside a three-way intersection. Nearby were large compounds where ordinary residents lived, dormitories for factory workers, and even a school.","Zhong Mei thought the location was excellent. She could sell general merchandise, stationery, books—in short, just about anything. She told Qiao Lanshu, “Business will definitely be good!”","Qiao Lanshu agreed. “Then let’s go with this place. By the way, where are you planning to get your merchandise?”","At that time, the source of the goods depended on what one wanted to sell. Ordinary stationery and household items could be found in any city, though the profit margins were low.","If she wanted higher profits, she would have to source goods directly from various factories.","Some people even made a special trip by train to the south to purchase merchandise. But the south was too far away, requiring a long train journey, and along the way they had to watch out for pickpockets and thieves.","Zhong Mei immediately dismissed that option.","“I’ll visit the factories one by one first and make a list of everything I can get from them. For the rest, I’ll look elsewhere. I heard Wencheng has a wholesale market, so I’ll go take a look there.”","Qiao Lanshu didn’t know much about this either. Whatever Zhong Mei said, she nodded along and occasionally offered some suggestions.","Once they had rented the shop, Zhong Mei began handling every aspect of opening it by herself.","Qiao Lanshu, meanwhile, was busy with work and didn’t have much time to stop by.","Zhong Mei was capable and hardworking. Since the shop needed to be renovated, she spent practically every day there supervising the work, leaving the two children in Guan Wenjun’s care.","After work each day, Guan Wenjun had to pick up the children and then cook for them.","But how could he know how to cook?","Even the children complained that his food tasted awful.","A month passed like this, and both Guan Wenjun and the children had lost weight.","There was no helping it. Guan Wenjun could only help Zhong Mei keep an eye on the work at the shop, allowing Zhong Mei to go home to look after the children and cook.","But the work at the shop was even more exhausting. Day after day, Guan Wenjun was worn out like a dog.","All of Guan Wenjun’s money was with Zhong Mei. Zhong Mei had invested twenty thousand yuan in the shop, while Qiao Lanshu had invested ten thousand yuan as an advance for merchandise.","Finally, by the time Zhong Mei’s shop officially opened, half a year had passed.","By then, it was summer vacation once again.","Han Ye had finished the middle school entrance examinations and successfully been admitted to Wencheng No. 1 High School, becoming a high school student.","Qin Qiao'an had also started his first year of middle school, while Xiaxia had entered sixth grade.","In the blink of an eye, the children had all grown up.","......","After Han Ye entered high school, he became even more mature and sensible. Most importantly, he never got into fights or caused trouble.","Why?","Because Qiao Lanshu worked at the school. Every day, she heard about Han Ye’s behavior, his grades, and everything he had done—even if she did not ask, the other teachers would tell her about it when they returned to the staff room.","Han Ye could not embarrass Qiao Lanshu, so he behaved exceptionally well in high school.","Just as Qiao Lanshu was beginning to relax now that her most troublesome child had suddenly become sensible, Qin Qiao'an took up his older brother’s mantle and became the latest notorious figure in middle school.","He often failed to come home on time after school, only appearing at the door on his bicycle after night had fallen.","During holidays, he disappeared altogether.","And now that he was older, Qin Qiao'an no longer liked sticking to Han Ye. Whenever Qiao Lanshu could not find him and went to ask Han Ye, she discovered that Han Ye had no idea where he was either.","Qiao Lanshu was a little worried. She said to Han Ye, “What do you think about this Qin Qiao'an? He wouldn’t go out and cause trouble for me, would he?”","Han Ye continued reading as he said, “Mom, don’t worry. With my past mistakes as an example, An'an not only takes his studies seriously, he also won’t get too close to girls for no reason. He knows his limits.”","Qiao Lanshu was rather helpless. “That’s not what I’m worried about... Forget it, forget it. I’m not going to bother with him.”","Qiao Lanshu sighed. What she was worried about was Qin Qiao'an getting into a fight outside and causing trouble that would eventually come knocking on their door.","After all, whenever the children got into fights—whether it was Han Ye or Qin Qiao'an—they rarely lost.","Most of the time, they were the ones who beat the other family’s child black and blue, after which the child’s parents would come looking for them.","That was what Qiao Lanshu feared most of all!","Once someone else’s child was injured, a mere apology would not be enough to resolve the matter.","She decided that as soon as Qin Qiao'an came home, she would have a serious talk with him.","......","With Han Ye now in high school and Qin Qiao'an nowhere to be seen every day, Xiaxia went to and from school by herself.","She had become less introverted over the past two years and had made a few friends at school.","However, none of her friends lived along her route home. After all, Xiaxia was the only child in her class who lived in the military compound.","One day after school, she suddenly saw someone she had not seen in a long time—Li Taohua.","She stood by the roadside and watched for a while.","It really had been a long time since she had seen Li Taohua.","After Li Taohua’s parents were laid off, the family had moved away. Xiaxia had no idea where they had gone.","But Li Taohua had dropped out before finishing elementary school, and her older brother, Li Jian, had dropped out as well.","Li Taohua was wearing a dress, and her hair had actually been permed into curls. She even seemed to be wearing makeup.","She was a little older than Xiaxia, perhaps thirteen or fourteen by now.","Xiaxia did not know her exact age, but her clothes and makeup looked remarkably mature.","There were two other girls beside Li Taohua, dressed much like her. They were taller and older, probably sixteen or seventeen—about the same age as Han Ye.","Xiaxia was curious. How had Li Taohua ended up like this?","What were they dressed like that for?","The three girls came out of an alley and crossed the street. They were dressed very fashionably. Li Taohua had once been dark-skinned and stout, but after losing weight and dressing up, she had actually become quite pretty.","Xiaxia was usually a bookworm and had never really seen anyone like them before. Their hair was curled into tight waves, which looked rather attractive.","Their fingernails were painted red, and their sleeveless dresses left their arms bare. They were even wearing high heels, walking with their hips swaying from side to side.","Xiaxia did not think they looked bad, though she found it difficult to describe exactly how she felt about them.","At that moment, she thought of the many books she had read before—the various women described by authors in their stories. She searched through those characters for someone resembling Li Taohua.","In an instant, she was able to think of several, from both ancient and modern times and from countries all over the world.","Without exception, none of those characters were particularly good people.","And suddenly, Xiaxia understood.","It seemed that Li Taohua had taken the wrong path.","Li Taohua saw her as well. Looking at Xiaxia with her schoolbag on her back, she glared fiercely at her several times.","When the two girls beside her saw Xiaxia, they laughed and said, “Well, well, little sister, you’re quite pretty. Taohua, who is she? Do you know her?”","Taohua shook her head in disgust. “I don’t know her. Judging by the way she’s dressed, she’s probably a student at one of the nearby schools.”","The two girls pulled Taohua over. Carrying small handbags, they smiled as they looked Xiaxia up and down several times.","Xiaxia was beautiful, with fair skin and a pair of bright, dark eyes.","The two girls exchanged a glance, then smiled and asked her, “Little girl, what’s your name?”","They continued, “Just look at what you’re wearing. Why are you dressed so plainly? Do you like wearing dresses?”"]},{"number":273,"title":"Chapter 273: You've Actually Learned to Stay Out All Night","paragraphs":["Xiaxia didn’t really feel like dealing with these people.","She sized up the two girls in front of her, as well as Li Taohua standing behind them.","She shook her head and said, “I’m not interested. Move aside—I’m going home.”","With that, she pushed past them and headed toward the military compound.","The two girls glanced at Xiaxia’s face and followed her for a few steps.","“Come on, don’t you like dressing up and looking pretty? Just look at you—your clothes are so plain, your hair is all frizzy, and your hands too. You’d look so nice with some nail polish.”","Xiaxia looked at them and asked curiously, “You two are dressed up so beautifully. What are you going to do?”","She glanced at Li Taohua and noticed that Li Taohua had been following behind the two girls the whole time without saying much.","The two girls smiled. “We’re going dancing! Lots of people come to watch, and you can make plenty of money. Do you want to earn some?”","The other girl added, “What’s the point of going to school? Once you finish junior high, you’ll still have to go out and work for money, won’t you? You might as well go dancing while you’re young. You can make three hundred yuan a month. Do you want to come?”","Xiaxia shook her head, her face expressionless. “No, thank you.”","The two girls fell silent.","By then, they had reached the entrance to the military compound, so the two girls left with Li Taohua.","Before leaving, they were still smiling at Xiaxia.","“If you ever change your mind, come find us! Bye-bye!”","Xiaxia turned around and watched them walk away. Li Taohua also looked back at her.","The look in Li Taohua’s eyes was full of disgust.","But whether it was truly disgust, jealousy, or disgust brought on by jealousy was difficult to say.","When Xiaxia returned home in the military compound, Qiao Lanshu was already cooking in the kitchen.","She had been extremely busy with work lately. Whenever she could get home early, she would cook for the children.","Han Ye had suddenly fallen in love with studying after entering high school. Every day, he holed up in his room, fiddling with various military equipment models.","The house was quiet and peaceful. Xiaxia went into the kitchen, washed her hands, and asked, “Mom, my brother still isn’t home?”","Qiao Lanshu chopped vegetables as she replied, “No. That boy has completely let himself go since starting middle school. He’s never home and who knows what he’s doing outside.”","Looking at Xiaxia, who was helping her wash vegetables and tend the stove, Qiao Lanshu said with satisfaction, “My little darling is still the most thoughtful. You know to come home early and help your mother, unlike those two little troublemakers.”","Han Ye was holed up in his room, completely absorbed in whatever he was tinkering with.","As for Qin Qiao'an, no one knew what he was doing outside. Qiao Lanshu could only hope he wasn’t getting into trouble.","She sighed.","“Don’t worry, Mom,” Xiaxia said. “My brother won’t be the one getting the short end of the stick.”","Qiao Lanshu snorted. “I’m not worried about him being taken advantage of. I’m worried he’ll take advantage of someone else, and then they’ll come knocking on our door.”","Xiaxia fell silent.","A little after six, Qin Yuanzheng came home as well.","As soon as he arrived, Qiao Lanshu got ready to serve dinner.","Qin Yuanzheng washed his hands and had just sat down when he cast a casual glance around the table. His brow immediately furrowed.","“Qin Qiao'an still isn’t home?”","Qiao Lanshu sighed. “No. Who knows what he’s doing out there?”","Men were always so careless. Unlike Qiao Lanshu, they didn’t tend to overthink things. She was forever worrying about the children, fretting herself sick.","Qin Yuanzheng said, “Eat. Don’t save him anything tonight. If he can’t make it home by mealtime, he can go hungry.”","His expression darkened slightly. He had been busy recently and hadn’t had time to discipline the boy. Now that things had eased up, he would have to make time to give Qin Qiao'an a proper scolding.","Qin Qiao'an didn’t return home until nearly eight that evening.","He rode his bicycle into the courtyard in a whirlwind.","After propping the bicycle against the wall, he ran toward the house, shouting, “Mom! Mom! I’m hungry! I’m starving!”","His voice was still echoing through the courtyard when he burst inside.","But the only person in the house was Qin Yuanzheng, sitting on the living room sofa and reading the newspaper. Everyone else was gone.","Qin Qiao'an still had no idea how serious the situation was.","Qin Qiao'an still had no idea how serious the situation was.","Sweaty and panting, he ran to the table, grabbed the water pitcher, poured himself a glass, and gulped it down in one go. Only then did he ask, “Dad, where’s Mom?”","Qin Yuanzheng gave him several disdainful looks, turned a page of his newspaper, and replied unhurriedly, “Your mother’s in her room working. Don’t go bother her.”","“Oh,” Qin Qiao'an said before running to the kitchen to look for food. “Dad, is there anything to eat? I’m starving.”","Qiao Lanshu usually left food and dishes for him every day, and Qin Qiao'an was used to coming home no matter how late and still finding a meal waiting.","But this time, he was disappointed.","He searched the kitchen from top to bottom. Forget food—even the dishes and chopsticks had been washed spotless. He checked the pots, only to find them scrubbed until they gleamed.","Qin Qiao'an rummaged through every corner of the kitchen, circling around two or three times before finally realizing that his beloved mother had not left him any dinner.","Not even a single grain of rice!","Qin Qiao'an felt as though the sky had fallen.","He ran out of the kitchen and charged toward Qiao Lanshu’s room. Qin Yuanzheng saw him but didn’t stop him.","It wouldn’t do any good to ask Qiao Lanshu. If she hadn’t left him dinner, then she hadn’t left him dinner.","He was destined to go hungry that night.","Qin Qiao'an rushed to Qiao Lanshu’s room. The door was open, and she was sitting at her desk preparing lesson plans.","With an exaggeratedly miserable expression, Qin Qiao'an ran inside. “Mom, why didn’t you leave me any food today? Are you trying to starve me to death?”","At six feet tall, Qin Qiao'an half-crouched beside Qiao Lanshu, leaned against her shoulder, covered his face, and pretended to cry.","Qiao Lanshu shook her shoulder, thoroughly exasperated. “Stop making noise. I’m working.”","Qin Qiao'an pitifully draped himself over the desk. His stomach was growling with hunger, so loudly that even Qiao Lanshu could hear it.","She glanced at his stomach and said sarcastically, “You didn’t come home until after dark, so I assumed someone outside had treated you to dinner. What’s wrong? Hungry now?”","Qin Qiao'an nodded miserably and rubbed his stomach. “I am, Mom. I’m really hungry. Is there anything left to eat?”","Qiao Lanshu crossed her arms and looked at him. “Tell me. What have you been doing outside every night lately, coming home so late?”","As soon as she asked, Qiao Lanshu felt that the words sounded strangely familiar.","After all, she had said the same thing countless times when Han Ye was younger.","And now, years later, she had to say it all over again—only this time, she was talking to someone else.","Qin Qiao'an was nothing like Han Ye when it came to obedience.","Han Ye wasn’t her biological son. Since Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu had rescued and raised him from childhood, he sometimes held himself back and generally listened whenever Qiao Lanshu told him to do something.","But Qin Qiao'an was their biological son. He felt secure in their indulgence, and he was especially good at making a fuss and refusing to reason with anyone.","He clung to Qiao Lanshu’s arm and whined pitifully, “Oh, Mom, I’m so hungry right now. I’m really starving. Can’t you let me fill my stomach first before you start questioning me?”","Qiao Lanshu was getting dizzy from all the shaking. She said sternly, “No.”","Qin Qiao’an continued shaking her. “Come on, Mom, are you trying to starve me to death? Am I not your most beloved child? Mom, Mom, I’m hungry. I haven’t eaten a single bite since noon. I’m still growing, and if I don’t eat, I won’t grow any taller.”","Qiao Lanshu had once worried that her own height might affect Qin Qiao’an, so she had been especially particular about making sure he and his sister ate properly.","They had to eat three meals a day, and they had to eat their fill. She often bought eggs and meat for them, while Qin Yuanzheng would buy goat’s milk. Whenever money was a little less tight, Qiao Lanshu was also willing to spend on milk or powdered milk for them.","Now that Qin Qiao’an was in his first year of middle school, he had already grown to six feet tall.","Xiaxia was in sixth grade and already five foot three. She was still young and could grow quite a bit more.","Qiao Lanshu hadn’t worried about their height for a long time. If Qin Qiao’an hadn’t brought it up, she might have forgotten all about it.","Qiao Lanshu was just about to speak when Qin Yuanzheng’s cold voice suddenly came from the doorway.","“Qin Qiao’an, how old are you? And you’re still clinging to your mother like that? What kind of behavior is that? Get out here!”","Qin Qiao’an fell silent.","He wasn’t afraid of his mother, but he was still rather intimidated by his father.","Even so, he stubbornly argued, “Dad, what’s wrong with hugging my mom? She’s my own mother. I’ll hug her if I want to.”","The moment he finished speaking, Qin Yuanzheng strode into the room, grabbed him by the collar, and said icily, “You’re just asking for a beating.”","Qin Qiao’an was over six feet tall, yet his father simply grabbed him and dragged him out.","Qiao Lanshu watched the father and son bickering as they went and shook her head.","She had actually been planning to go to the kitchen and make noodles for her son.","But after remembering what Qin Yuanzheng had said that evening—that she had to give An’an a proper scolding, or he would keep acting this way and might even cause serious trouble—she held herself back.","Still, hearing the screams coming from the courtyard made her heart ache.","She knew Qin Yuanzheng would show restraint. Qin Qiao’an also knew his mother would feel sorry for him, which was why he was deliberately screaming so loudly, hoping she would come out and rescue him.","Even so, Qiao Lanshu couldn’t hold back. She left the room and hurried to Han Ye’s door, knocking on it.","Han Ye had already put away his tools and taken off his gloves. He had placed the half-disassembled model airplane in a drawer.","He opened the door, and before Qiao Lanshu could say anything, he said, “Mom, don’t worry. I’ll go take a look.”","Qiao Lanshu nodded and lowered her voice. “Uncle Qin is very angry today. Go see what’s happening. Don’t let them actually start fighting.”","Han Ye nodded. “Don’t worry, Mom. I know what to do.”","In the past, whenever Qin Yuanzheng disciplined him, Qin Qiao’an had been the one to cover for him and sneak him food.","Now the situation had turned around.","Han Ye shook his head.","When he reached the courtyard, he saw Qin Yuanzheng exchanging blows with Qin Qiao’an. Qin Qiao’an had been training for years and had inherited Qin Yuanzheng’s talent, so he was extremely skilled at fighting. But because he was still young and lacked experience, he came off worse every time he sparred with Qin Yuanzheng.","What was more, he had an empty stomach that night and was feeling weak all over.","Whenever Qin Yuanzheng hit him, he howled in agony, making it sound as though Qin Yuanzheng had used all his strength.","Qin Yuanzheng and Han Ye both knew he was doing it on purpose, waiting for Qiao Lanshu to lose heart and come out to save him.","Unfortunately for him, Qiao Lanshu didn’t come out that evening.","In the end, Qin Qiao’an truly couldn’t hold on any longer. Qin Yuanzheng swept his feet out from under him, sending him sprawling onto the ground, and this time he really started crying.","His eyes red, Qin Qiao’an wailed, “Mom! Mom, Dad’s going to beat me to death! You didn’t even come out to see me!”","Qin Yuanzheng fell silent.","Han Ye fell silent too.","Qin Yuanzheng glared at him angrily. “Get up!”","Qin Qiao’an rolled around on the ground and shouted, “I’m not getting up! You’re going to beat me to death! Chief Qin, you’re going to kill your own son!”","Qin Yuanzheng was so furious that he closed his eyes and took a deep breath.","Han Ye hurried over and said, “Uncle Qin, why don’t you let it go? An’an didn’t really do anything wrong, did he? He just went out to play with his classmates and came home a little late. Maybe you could just make him come back earlier from now on?”","As he spoke, he kept winking at Qin Qiao’an.","Qin Yuanzheng walked over and sat down on the steps. Looking at Qin Qiao’an, he said, “Tell me. You’ve been coming home so late every day lately. What have you been doing?”","Qin Qiao’an climbed to his feet and brushed the dirt off his clothes. Touching his nose, he said, “I—I haven’t been doing anything.”","Qin Yuanzheng’s face darkened. “Don’t lie!”","Qin Qiao’an fell silent.","Qin Yuanzheng stared at him sternly. He had somehow produced a length of rough rope and was fiddling with it while keeping his eyes fixed on Qin Qiao’an.","The moment Qin Qiao’an and Han Ye saw the rope, their bodies went cold and sweat broke out on their foreheads.","Han Ye had once skipped school and gotten into a fight. Since Han Wenlin had been away on a business trip, Qin Yuanzheng had been the one to deal with him.","After they got home that day, Qin Yuanzheng had tied Han Ye up with that very rope, hung him from a tree, and given him a thorough whipping.","Of course, Qin Yuanzheng had known how to control his strength, and Han Ye hadn’t been injured.","But the fear he had felt at the time had stayed with him.","That night, Qiao Lanshu had secretly come out of the house, untied Han Ye, and let him return to his room to sleep.","After that, Han Ye had never done anything reckless again.","Han Ye turned to look at Qin Qiao’an.","The brothers exchanged a glance. Qin Qiao’an silently swallowed.","Qin Yuanzheng looked at him and asked again, “Don’t lie. Give me a proper explanation. What have you been going out to do lately?”","Qin Qiao’an squatted on the ground and poked at the dirt with a stick. After agonizing over it for a long while, he finally said, “Actually, I haven’t been doing anything. I’ve just been going out with my best friend. My friend doesn’t have a bicycle, so I have to give him a ride. We go to the library, the movie theater, places like that.”","Their former English tutor often took them to see movies, so the three of them were quite familiar with the theater.","But movie tickets weren’t cheap.","Besides, Qin Yuanzheng knew exactly how much money Qin Qiao’an had. He only had a little pocket money—enough for snacks and soft drinks, but certainly not enough to go to the movies all the time.","Qin Qiao’an scratched his head and added, “Actually, we don’t go that often. Most of the time, we go play by the river. There are lots of people there, and some of them fish. It’s pretty fun...”","Qin Yuanzheng let out a cold laugh. “It’s already dark. You go to the river at night to watch people fish? Do you think I’m going to believe that?”","Even Han Ye found that strange. He looked at Qin Qiao’an and asked, “Who did you go with? I know all your friends. Which one were you with?”","Qin Qiao’an fell silent.","He stared at Han Ye in disbelief, his eyes accusing him.","Big brother, why are you interrogating me too?"]},{"number":274,"title":"Chapter 274: Keep Provoking Him","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng interrogated Qin Qiao'an for half a day, but Qin Qiao'an stubbornly insisted that he had merely gone out to have fun with his classmates.","He hadn’t done anything wrong or bad, so Qin Yuanzheng couldn’t really hang him up and beat him.","That was the experience Qin Qiao'an had gained from matching wits with Qin Yuanzheng ever since he was little—and from following Han Ye around for so long.","Qin Yuanzheng was so furious that he was speechless.","Of course, he couldn’t just let this rebellious son off so easily.","In the end, Qin Yuanzheng made Qin Qiao'an stand in a horse stance in the courtyard on an empty stomach for an hour. He also warned him, “Starting tomorrow, if you’re not home before seven in the evening, I’m locking the door. You can sleep on the street. Understand?”","Qin Qiao'an nodded, then silently glanced at the wall surrounding the courtyard.","Qin Yuanzheng sneered. “There are spikes on top of the wall. Go ahead and climb it if you can.”","Qin Qiao'an: “...”","He stared at Qin Yuanzheng in shock, almost beginning to wonder whether he was really his biological son.","Otherwise, how could his father be so ruthless?","At that moment, Qin Qiao'an’s stomach was growling with hunger. Standing in a horse stance was usually easy enough, but now that he was hungry, his legs felt weak.","He was simply too hungry and had no strength.","So he could only nod pitifully. “I understand, dear Father. Don’t worry. I’ll definitely be home at six fifty-nine tomorrow. I won’t give you the chance to kick me out to sleep on the street.”","Qin Yuanzheng: “...”","Damn it. His fists were itching to hit him again.","This little rascal was constantly provoking him!","He really had no idea where this personality had come from.","More than once, Qin Yuanzheng had reflected on himself. Had he been this irritating when he was young?","Even a dog would go around Qin Qiao'an to avoid him.","Just then, Qiao Lanshu came out of the house as well. She had heard the argument between father and son.","Qin Qiao'an was far too rebellious, while Qin Yuanzheng was furious. Qiao Lanshu felt sorry for both of them.","So she took Qin Yuanzheng’s hand and said softly, “All right, all right. Don’t be angry with him. You get angry every time—be careful you don’t ruin your health. It’s very late. Come inside and rest.”","As she spoke, Qiao Lanshu pulled Qin Yuanzheng toward the house.","Qin Yuanzheng had still wanted to lecture Qin Qiao'an a little more, but since his wife had come to take him inside, he followed her back into the house.","Still, he remained irritated. “Tell me, what will it take for that brat to grow up and act sensibly?”","He wanted to discipline him physically, but he was afraid of hurting the child. Qin Yuanzheng knew exactly how strong he was.","But if he went easy on him, the little brat wasn’t afraid of being beaten at all. Even after getting thrashed, he would remain just as unruly.","He had even considered sending Qin Qiao'an to the military to undergo some training and suffer a little. In the end, the boy actually liked the idea. Qin Qiao'an had even clamored to go himself.","Qin Yuanzheng was completely at a loss.","When it came to raising children, he realized that he truly had no idea what to do.","If only every child were as obedient and sensible as Xiaxia.","She was practically an angel.","Qiao Lanshu said softly, “Take it slowly. Don’t be angry. Han Ye was even more mischievous when he was younger, but he always knew where to draw the line and never did anything outrageous.”","Qin Yuanzheng let out a cold snort. “If they ever do anything outrageous, I’ll tie them up, hang them from a tree, and use them as punching bags.”","Qiao Lanshu laughed again. Qin Yuanzheng was all bark and no bite. Deep down, he couldn’t bear to hit the children.","Otherwise, Qin Qiao'an wouldn’t be provoking him every day.","Qin Qiao'an knew perfectly well that Qin Yuanzheng didn’t dare to beat him seriously, which was why he behaved so recklessly.","...","Han Ye had watched the married couple return to the house from the courtyard. As soon as they were gone, he hurried over to An'an’s side and lowered his voice.","“Qin Qiao'an! Seriously, you knew your dad would really hit you, so why did you deliberately provoke him? Would it kill you to say a few less words?”","Han Ye had been sweating bullets for Qin Qiao'an just now.","This troublesome little brother was getting bolder and bolder. Han Ye himself didn’t even dare to provoke Qin Yuanzheng.","As soon as Qin Yuanzheng left, Qin Qiao'an immediately plopped down on the ground. There was no way he was going to keep holding the horse stance. Every minute of slacking off was a minute earned.","Sitting on the ground, he said dejectedly, “Bro, I’m really innocent. How did I provoke Dad? He’s the one who’s narrow-minded and always likes to lecture me. I didn’t even hold it against him. I’m already being very filial.”","Han Ye: “...”","Han Ye was completely speechless. “How did you not provoke him? What did you say just now?”","Qin Qiao'an replied righteously, “He told me to be home before seven, and I said I’d be home at six fifty-nine. Isn’t that perfectly reasonable? I didn’t say I’d come home at seven-oh-one. I was already giving him plenty of consideration.”","Han Ye lightly kicked him. “Just wait until Uncle Qin hangs you up and beats you. If I’m not home then, no one will be there to save you.”","Qin Qiao'an grabbed Han Ye’s arm and pulled himself to his feet, completely unconcerned. “I’m not afraid. My mom loves me. She’ll definitely save me.”","Han Ye: “...”","All right. Han Ye was utterly speechless now.","The two brothers went to the kitchen in perfect unspoken agreement.","Qin Qiao'an sat down in a chair and sighed repeatedly. “Bro, I’m so hungry. I’m seriously about to starve to death.”","Han Ye lowered his voice. “Keep your voice down. I’ll make you some noodles.”","With that, Han Ye began rummaging through the cupboards for dried noodles.","Qin Qiao'an couldn’t cook, but Han Ye could at least boil food until it was done. As for the taste...","Qin Qiao'an thought it over. Never mind, never mind. As long as it didn’t make him sick, it would be fine.","He was too hungry to be picky about flavor.","While the brothers were rummaging through the kitchen, Xiaxia walked in.","She looked at the two of them with deep disapproval. “What are you doing?”","Han Ye immediately put a finger to his lips and said, “We’re making your brother some noodles.”","Xiaxia glanced at Qin Qiao'an. He was filthy, his clothes soaked through with sweat, and there was dirt all over him.","She said with obvious distaste, “You should take a shower first.”","Qin Qiao'an sat there without moving and said weakly, “I’m almost starving to death, and you want me to shower... I think Mom doesn’t love me anymore. She doesn’t care about me at all. She didn’t leave me any food, and even after I begged her, she still wouldn’t make me any noodles.”","Xiaxia shook her head and walked over. She took a packet of dried noodles from the cupboard and said, “I’ll make them for you. Go take a shower.”","Qin Qiao'an brightened immediately and jumped to his feet. “I knew my little sister was the best! Xiaxia, what would I ever do without you? I could never repay your kindness, not even in a lifetime.”","Xiaxia: “...”","Even Han Ye couldn’t stand listening to him anymore. He grabbed Qin Qiao'an and dragged him outside. “Go take your shower. You talk way too much.”","...","Qin Yuanzheng was sitting inside the house, listening to the noisy commotion outside. He said unhappily, “Weren’t we supposed to let him go hungry for the whole night so he’d learn his lesson?”","Qiao Lanshu stood beside him and said softly, “The child is still growing. He gets a lot of exercise and digests food quickly. If we don’t let him eat dinner, he probably won’t be able to sleep all night. Then he’ll get up and make a fuss in the middle of the night, and the whole family won’t get any sleep.”","Qin Yuanzheng: “...”","Qin Yuanzheng took advantage of the moment and pulled Qiao Lanshu into his arms. “You’re just too softhearted,” he told her. “You’re always indulging them. You’ll spoil them rotten.”","Qiao Lanshu sighed and said quietly, “I was thinking about how they’ll be joining the army in the future. Won’t they suffer enough once they’re there? Since they’re at home now, let them have some fun. As long as they don’t fall behind in their studies, we can afford to be a little more relaxed about everything else.”","Qin Yuanzheng lowered his voice. “I have a feeling that kid Qiao'an might be dating already.”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","These days, just hearing something like that was enough to put Qiao Lanshu on high alert.","She sat up straight and looked at Qin Yuanzheng. “Did he say that himself? How old is he? He’s only just started seventh grade. Does a boy that age even know what love is?”","Qiao Lanshu still remembered what had happened with Han Ye when he was in eighth grade!","In the past, she had been fairly open-minded about her children dating young. But after that incident, she had become extremely wary of it—in fact, she was completely opposed to it.","She wouldn’t allow the children to date in middle or high school.","At the very least, they would have to wait until they joined the army and got into a military academy before she would let them think about relationships.","Qin Yuanzheng reassured her, “No, An'an didn’t say anything. That was just my guess.”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","Qiao Lanshu slid off him, climbed onto the kang, and lay down. Her brows furrowed with worry. “Could he really have started dating while he was away these past two months?”","Qin Yuanzheng moved closer and hugged her through the quilt. “He refuses to say anything. I’ll keep an eye on him for the next couple of days...”","Qiao Lanshu reached out and pushed him away, glaring at him. “Move. You’re so hot.”","Qin Yuanzheng: “???”","He looked at her, feeling a little wronged. “You’re under the quilt too. How can you be hot?”","Qiao Lanshu shifted farther toward the inside and turned her head away, ignoring him.","Qin Yuanzheng felt as if the sky had collapsed. His wife actually wouldn’t let him hold her anymore.","What did their son’s dating have to do with him now? He didn’t want to worry about anything else. He only wanted to ask his wife why she had suddenly stopped talking to him.","Could it be that he was getting old?","He lowered his head and glanced at himself. His abs were still there, weren’t they?","Qin Yuanzheng moved closer again and braced both hands on the bed as he looked at her. “Honey, why are you angry?”","He reached out, took her chin, and turned her face toward him. His expression was serious. “Did I say something wrong again?”","Qiao Lanshu looked at him and sighed. “It’s not your fault. I’m just feeling irritated.”","Qin Yuanzheng refused to let it go. “It’s not my fault? You won’t even let me hold you anymore. Then it definitely has something to do with me.”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","Looking at him like this, Qiao Lanshu suddenly felt like teasing him.","She said, “I heard one of my coworkers say something recently. She said that when a middle-aged couple kisses, it can give you nightmares for several nights. We’ve been married for so many years, and you’re getting on in age yourself. Why are you still so clingy?”","Qin Yuanzheng: “???”","His brows drew tightly together, and he said solemnly, “Who did you hear that from? What nonsense.”","Qiao Lanshu thought for a moment. “Well, one of my coworkers at the office said it...”","Before she could finish, Qin Yuanzheng pinned her down and kissed her several times in a row.","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","Qin Yuanzheng held her face in both hands and asked, “Are you going to have nightmares? How many do you think you’ll have?”","Qiao Lanshu couldn’t help laughing. “They said it, not me. My man is so handsome—how could I possibly have nightmares?”","Qin Yuanzheng snorted. “So, are you going to let me hold you or not?”","Before Qiao Lanshu could answer, Qin Yuanzheng slipped beneath the quilt and wrapped her tightly in his arms. In a deep voice, he said, “Nothing else matters. You’re my wife. If I want to hold you, I’ll hold you.”","Qiao Lanshu shook her head with a smile and let him hold her.","After a while, Qiao Lanshu said again, “No, I’m still worried about An'an. How about I go ask him? He should tell me, shouldn’t he?”","She made as if to sit up, but Qin Yuanzheng pressed her back into his arms. “Forget it. You don’t need to ask him. He isn’t Han Ye—he’s not that honest with you. I’ll have someone keep an eye on him for the next couple of days. That little rascal had better not be up to anything bad.”","Qiao Lanshu sighed. “Children really do grow up and stop listening to their parents.”","Come to think of it, she needed to have a talk with Xiaxia, too. Xiaxia had to be kept under strict watch. She absolutely couldn’t start dating. She was so beautiful that no matter who she dated, she would be the one at a disadvantage.","And as a girl, she was even more vulnerable.","Qiao Lanshu had once thought that raising young children was the most troublesome part, and that things would get easier once she brought them up. Then she thought everything would be fine once they started elementary school. Later, she told herself it would be better once they reached middle school...","Now she had realized that whether they were in elementary or middle school, children would always find new ways to cause trouble.","Being a mother was never easy.","While Qiao Lanshu was worrying over all this, Qin Yuanzheng grew more and more dissatisfied. Before long, he had pinned Qiao Lanshu down and started pulling off her clothes.","Qiao Lanshu: “???”","She asked in surprise, “Didn’t we just... yesterday?”","Qin Yuanzheng’s expression darkened. “Don’t think that just because I’m getting older, I can’t perform anymore. I’ll show you what I’m capable of.”","She had even joked about nightmares? Hmph. He would keep her so busy that she wouldn’t have time to dream of nightmares at all. Let’s see if she dared to make fun of him again.","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","She was utterly helpless.","She had truly only been joking.","Who would have thought she had hit Qin Yuanzheng’s sore spot again?","Honestly, this man became harder and harder to placate with age.","...","Early the next morning, there were no classes, so Qiao Lanshu and the children were all at home.","Han Ye had gone back to the Han family that morning.","Only Qiao Lanshu, An'an, and Xiaxia were left at home.","Qiao Lanshu was planning to visit Zhong Mei’s department store. Over the past two years, Zhong Mei had first expanded her grocery shop. After earning some money, she invested it back into the business and opened a two-story department store. Business there was booming.","Qiao Lanshu had invested in it, and Zhong Mei gave her a share of the profits every month, almost like a salary. Qiao Lanshu saved all the money, planning to buy a few properties in a couple of years, once homes could be freely bought and sold.","After getting ready, Qiao Lanshu urged Qin Qiao'an, “An'an, hurry up. We’re about to leave.”","Qin Qiao'an came out of his room and said, “Mom, you and Xiaxia go ahead. I don’t feel like going out today.”","Qiao Lanshu exchanged a glance with Xiaxia, and the two of them looked at him. Xiaxia asked suspiciously, “You’re not going out, big brother? We’re going to Aunt Mei’s today. Aren’t you coming?”","Qin Qiao'an used to enjoy browsing around the department store.","Qin Qiao'an coughed and said with a perfectly serious expression, “Oh, I still have homework to do. You two go ahead. Mom, remember to bring me lunch. Oh, and I want egg tarts—buy me two.”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”"]},{"number":275,"title":"Chapter 275: Tracking An'an","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu had originally planned to visit Zhong Mei’s department store today, lend her a hand, and chat with her for a while.","After all, Zhong Mei had two children at home—both boys, and particularly mischievous ones. Whenever the children were on vacation, Zhong Mei was busy beyond belief.","But Qin Qiao’an didn’t want to go, and Xiaxia didn’t like playing with those two boys.","Besides, Qin Qiao’an would be home alone, and there wouldn’t even be any lunch for him.","As his mother, Qiao Lanshu worried every day about whether her child had anything to eat.","Now that Qin Qiao’an wasn’t going out, after Qiao Lanshu and Xiaxia left, she said to Xiaxia, “Why don’t we go home for lunch today? Your brother’s home alone, and he can’t cook. We can’t just let him go hungry.”","As the first child in the family, Qin Qiao’an should have been sensible and steady, and capable of handling every household chore.","Unfortunately, he was lucky enough to have Han Ye, his older brother, above him.","Han Ye had taken on the responsibilities of the eldest son and done everything for him.","As a result, Qin Qiao’an couldn’t do many things. For instance, he didn’t know how to cook.","Qiao Lanshu had never demanded that he learn.","She felt that cooking wasn’t difficult. If he wanted to learn, he could pick it up easily.","Qin Yuanzheng hadn’t known how to cook when he was young either, but after spending several years in the military, he became an all-rounder, to say nothing of cooking.","When it came to raising children, Qiao Lanshu was fairly hands-off.","The children could do whatever they wanted, as long as they didn’t let their grades slip and could make it into high school. That was her only requirement.","But now, she wondered whether she had been too lax with them.","She pushed her bicycle and walked with Xiaxia toward the entrance of the compound.","Xiaxia linked her arm through her mother’s as they walked, but after only a short distance, Qiao Lanshu suddenly stopped.","Xiaxia looked up at her. “Mom, why did you stop?”","Qiao Lanshu stood there silently for a moment before turning to look at Xiaxia.","Xiaxia gazed back at her innocently.","Everyone said Xiaxia looked a lot like her mother, but what she had inherited from Qiao Lanshu was mainly her fair skin and face shape. She had a pale complexion, an oval face, and dimples when she smiled.","Her eyes and brows, however, resembled Qin Yuanzheng more, and she had a high, straight nose, which made her features look even more refined.","Xiaxia also clearly took after him in height. Tall and slender, she was truly beautiful.","Qiao Lanshu stared at her for quite a while.","Xiaxia began to feel uncomfortable under her gaze. “Oh, Mom, why are you looking at me like that?”","Qiao Lanshu smiled. “I was just admiring how amazing I am to have given birth to such a beautiful daughter.”","Xiaxia: “...”","She had grown up being showered with compliments, so she was completely unfazed. Her expression remained unchanged, and she wore an almost expressionless face.","“Mom, what are you really trying to say?”","Qiao Lanshu lowered her voice. “Is there any boy at school you like?”","Xiaxia: “...”","She frowned and shook her head. “Of course not. They’re all so childish, just like kindergarteners. They’re terribly boring. Mom, you can stop asking me questions like that from now on.”","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","“You skipped grades, and the students in your class are all older than you, right? You still think they’re childish?”","Xiaxia nodded. “Extremely childish. I can’t even be bothered to talk to them, let alone like them. Mom, don’t ask me this kind of question again.”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","She lowered her voice again. “Then tell me—does your brother have someone he likes at school?”","This time, Xiaxia fell silent.","She thought for a moment before answering, “I don’t know either. After he started middle school, most of his classmates changed. I knew some of them before and could have asked, but I don’t know many of his current classmates, so I really have no idea.”","There had been more students in elementary school and fewer in middle school.","That was because the middle school took in students from three nearby elementary schools.","Back when Xiaxia and her brother had attended the same elementary school, Qin Qiao’an often went to look for her, so their classmates knew each other as well.","Now that Qin Qiao’an had started middle school, Xiaxia no longer knew the people in his class.","Qiao Lanshu walked a few more steps. Then she lowered her voice and said, “We’re not going to Aunt Mei’s today. We’re going to follow your brother.”","At that, Xiaxia’s eyes widened slightly. She looked at Qiao Lanshu and whispered, “Mom, secretly following someone doesn’t seem very proper.”","As a teacher, Qiao Lanshu felt a little guilty too.","She lowered her voice. “Well... it’s not really a big deal, is it? I’m following my own son. I’m only worried that he might go astray. If a child turns out badly, the mother bears some responsibility too. Don’t you agree?”","Xiaxia was silent for a moment before nodding. “Mom, I do think there’s something off about Brother too. But how are we supposed to keep an eye on him?”","Qiao Lanshu left her bicycle in the parking shed at the compound.","Then she took Xiaxia back to a spot near their home.","The two of them hid behind a shrub and peered out through the gaps between the branches.","It was the first time either of them had done anything like this, and they found it rather thrilling.","Xiaxia usually acted like a little adult, but at that moment, her eyes were shining faintly with excitement.","She lowered her voice. “Mom, I bet Brother will come out in five minutes.”","Qiao Lanshu whispered back, “Your brother is so impatient. Do you really think he can hold out that long?”","Xiaxia was usually calm and unhurried, but Qin Qiao’an was rather hotheaded and had very little patience.","Han Ye was somewhat irritable by nature, but he was fairly steady in daily life.","As for someone as impatient as Qin Qiao’an, Qiao Lanshu silently calculated.","She hadn’t even counted to sixty when Qin Qiao’an really did come out.","The mother and daughter’s expressions instantly turned solemn.","Qin Qiao’an had clearly said he didn’t want to go out. He had even asked Qiao Lanshu to bring him lunch and buy him some egg tarts.","But now, they had barely left, and he had slipped out right behind them.","What was he up to?","Qiao Lanshu and Xiaxia exchanged a glance before quietly following him.","However, it was broad daylight, so they couldn’t get too close or they would easily be noticed.","The two of them kept their distance.","After turning down two streets, they lost him.","The mother and daughter stood at a fork in the road, both completely dumbfounded.","Xiaxia scratched her head, looking a little confused. “Mom, I think we lost him.”","Qiao Lanshu stood there silently for several seconds before saying, “We’ll each take one road and see if we can find him. We’ll meet back here in an hour. Got it?”","Xiaxia nodded gravely, then parted ways with her mother.","The two of them took separate roads to search for Qin Qiao’an.","That boy could really run. Neither of them found him again, and they had no idea where he had gone.","Xiaxia had been walking along the street for a while when she ran into Zhou Dingwen, a neighbor from the compound.","Zhou Dingwen was also in high school, one grade above Han Ye. The children from families in the compound all followed roughly the same path.","First, they attended high school. After graduating, they joined the military, served for two years, and then took the military academy entrance exam.","If they were admitted, they were practically guaranteed to become officers.","If they failed to get into a military academy, they could only leave the service and return home to find work.","Competition at military academies was fierce. So although these children of influential military families enjoyed comfortable lives thanks to their privileged backgrounds, their training and studies were anything but easy.","After Zhou Dingwen started high school, he rarely showed up around the compound either. Xiaxia used to see him often, but she had seen less and less of him over the past two years.","When Zhou Dingwen spotted her, he called out at once, “Xiaxia, what brings you here?”","Xiaxia stopped by the roadside and glanced at him. “Brother Dingwen, I... I just came out for a walk.”","Zhou Dingwen looked around. There wasn’t even a bookstore on this street.","He smiled and walked over. “Where are you going now?”","Xiaxia shook her head. “Nowhere. I’m going to find my mom.”","“Where’s Aunt Qiao? I’ll take you to her.”","Xiaxia nodded and walked back with him. Along the way, she asked, “Brother Dingwen, did you see my brother just now?”","Zhou Dingwen slipped the stack of documents he was carrying into his backpack and asked casually, “Which brother?”","“Qin Qiao’an.”","Zhou Dingwen thought for a moment. “No, I didn’t. Did you come looking for him?”","Xiaxia sighed, looking troubled.","She didn’t say anything else, while Zhou Dingwen occasionally glanced back at her.","After a while, he asked again, “Xiaxia, your brothers are definitely going to join the military, right? What about you? Are you going to join the military someday?”","Many girls who grew up in military compounds went on to join performing troupes or become military doctors.","Zhou Dingwen had a cousin who had joined a performing troupe.","He thought that with Xiaxia’s beautiful looks and lovely voice, she would have no trouble getting in.","But Xiaxia shook her head and glanced at him. “No. I don’t want to be a soldier.”","She had never dreamed of joining the military.","Her dream was to become a writer. She loved writing.","Of course, if possible, she also wanted to become a teacher like her mother.","After all, teaching and writing didn’t conflict with each other. Many of her favorite writers were university professors.","Zhou Dingwen asked curiously, “Then what do you want to do in the future? Do you have a plan?”","Xiaxia: “...”","Xiaxia thought Zhou Dingwen asked far too many questions.","Even her mother had never asked her things like that.","Besides, she wouldn’t be starting middle school until September, when she turned thirteen. Those questions were still far too early for her.","So she shook her head without answering.","Seeing that she didn’t want to talk, Zhou Dingwen didn’t press her.","However, when they reached the end of the street, he suddenly said, “My dream is to become a pilot—a fighter pilot. But my dad says I don’t meet the requirements, so now I’m thinking that maybe I could become a sniper instead.”","Xiaxia thought that her Brother Han Ye seemed to want to become a sniper too. Recently, she had even seen Han Ye assembling a gun from a pile of scattered parts.","Come to think of it, where had the gun come from in the first place?","Could Director Han have given it to him?","There probably weren’t any bullets in it, right?","Zhou Dingwen was still talking to her, but Xiaxia had stopped listening.","When they reached the end of the street, Xiaxia saw Qiao Lanshu already standing there.","She immediately waved goodbye to Zhou Dingwen and ran over to Qiao Lanshu.","Zhou Dingwen shook his head helplessly, then walked over and greeted her. “Aunt Qiao.”","Qiao Lanshu looked at Zhou Dingwen. He was young and handsome, with a refined, scholarly air. She thought he seemed like a fine young man.","She smiled. “Oh, it’s Dingwen. What are you up to?”","“I went to print some materials. I’m heading home to study now.”","Qiao Lanshu said goodbye to him. Zhou Dingwen glanced at Xiaxia once more. Xiaxia waved at him, and he turned and left.","Qiao Lanshu watched until Zhou Dingwen was out of sight, then lowered her voice and asked Xiaxia, “What did Zhou Dingwen say to you just now?”","Qiao Lanshu was beginning to feel a little paranoid.","She had started to suspect everyone she saw.","Before, she would never have thought in that direction.","But now...","She whispered to Xiaxia, “Why do I feel that Zhou Dingwen’s eyes looked a little strange when he was looking at you? Does he like you?”","Xiaxia: “...”","Xiaxia stared at Qiao Lanshu in shock. She rubbed the goose bumps on her arms and glared at her. “Mom, wake up. I’m not even thirteen yet! What are you talking about?”","If Qiao Lanshu hadn’t kept bringing it up, Xiaxia would never even have considered the question of who liked whom.","Why did girls have to like boys? Or rather, why would boys like girls?","Boys and girls couldn’t even play well together.","Qiao Lanshu looked at Xiaxia. “Xiaxia, you’re a complete block of wood.”","But she quickly added, “Though the way you are now is pretty good. Being a blockhead is fine. Whatever you do, don’t start developing feelings yet. The moment you do, your father and I will have a headache.”","Xiaxia was utterly speechless.","It was the first time mother and daughter had gone out to follow someone—and they had chosen to follow Qin Qiao’an—but in the end, they had failed to keep up with him.","The two of them walked down the street arm in arm, whispering and discussing the situation for a long while. But neither of them had any experience with this sort of thing.","So Qiao Lanshu sighed and said, “Forget it. Let’s eat first. We don’t get to go shopping together very often. Mom will treat you to a proper meal.”","Qiao Lanshu took Xiaxia to a restaurant. Neither of them had much of an appetite, so Qiao Lanshu ordered only two dishes, a soup, and two bowls of rice.","They were halfway through the meal when Xiaxia’s eyes suddenly lit up. She lowered her voice and said, “Mom, I think I see my brother.”","Qiao Lanshu put down her bowl and chopsticks. “Where?”","Xiaxia pointed across the street. “Over there, at the entrance to that convenience store.”","Qiao Lanshu looked over and immediately saw him.","Her expression darkened at once. She stood up and said, “Come on. Let’s go take a look.”","Xiaxia glanced anxiously at the food. “But, Mom, we haven’t finished eating.”","Qiao Lanshu turned to the restaurant server. “Could you please pack this up for us? I’ll come back for it in a little while.”","The server agreed.","Qiao Lanshu grabbed Xiaxia and hurried out of the restaurant, heading straight for the convenience store across the street.","The convenience store was tiny. Apart from a few shelves, it had a long wooden bench along the left wall.","Qin Qiao’an was sitting on that bench now, holding a popsicle. A girl sat beside him. She was fairly pretty, with delicate features and a simple, plainly dressed appearance. She spoke in a soft voice and held a popsicle of her own.","Every so often, Qin Qiao’an leaned toward her and spoke in a low voice. They whispered together, looking quite intimate. No one knew what they were talking about, but they seemed awfully happy.","Qiao Lanshu took only one look before turning away and pulling Xiaxia against the wall.","She pressed a hand to the spot beneath her nose, looking as though she were about to faint.","Xiaxia: “...”","With a solemn expression, Xiaxia held her up and whispered, “Mom, you have to hold on!”"]},{"number":276,"title":"Chapter 276: Going to the Hotel","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu and Xiaxia were crouching by the wall outside the convenience store.","The mother and daughter had similar faces, and both wore deeply troubled expressions.","“Mom,” Xiaxia whispered, “aren’t we going inside to find my brother?”","Qiao Lanshu lowered her voice. “At your brother’s age, he’s at the stage when he cares most about his pride. He sneaked out to meet that girl. If we rush in like this, wouldn’t that embarrass him in front of her?”","Xiaxia looked a little shocked. “Mom, you’re already this angry, and you’re still worried about my brother’s dignity?”","Qiao Lanshu fell silent.","After a moment, she sighed.","After all, she was a high school teacher herself, so she understood children of this age to some extent.","They were sensitive and cared deeply about how others saw them.","What mattered to these children was different from what mattered to adults. They cared about their pride, and even the smallest things could seem enormously important to them.","The students in her class sometimes quarreled over a single remark from a classmate for ages.","Qin Yuanzheng had always said that she was too softhearted. Now, she had to admit that she really couldn’t bring herself to be tough.","She was afraid of leaving a bad memory for a child going through adolescence.","She whispered to Xiaxia, “In any case, we still don’t know what’s really going on. Let’s wait a little longer.”","About ten minutes later, Qin Qiao'an and the girl came out of the convenience store. They were eating popsicles and chatting and laughing as they walked away.","Qiao Lanshu cautiously poked her head out and took a look. When she saw that the two of them weren’t holding hands, she instantly let out a sigh of relief.","“They’re not holding hands!” she whispered to Xiaxia. “They’re not holding hands.”","If they weren’t holding hands, that proved they were just ordinary friends.","There were so many students in Qiao Lanshu’s class who had fallen in love at a young age that she had become quite experienced at spotting it.","Xiaxia also relaxed. She whispered, “I don’t think my brother would get into an early relationship. He’s older than me, but he’s even more childish than I am. Does he even understand what dating is?”","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","She thought Xiaxia made a great deal of sense.","But that didn’t make the situation any easier for her to bear!","Qiao Lanshu was silent for a few seconds before pressing the spot beneath her nose again.","The situation was supposed to be very serious, but Xiaxia nearly burst out laughing at her mother.","She slipped her arm through Qiao Lanshu’s and lowered her voice. “Mom, should we follow them a little longer? Let’s see where they’re going.”","Qiao Lanshu glanced at the sky. It was already past two in the afternoon.","The food she and Xiaxia had packed was still waiting to be picked up.","But they couldn’t worry about that now. She took Xiaxia’s hand and stood up. “Let’s go! We’ll see where they’re headed.”","The two of them followed Qin Qiao'an down another street. Then Qin Qiao'an followed the young girl into a hotel.","Qiao Lanshu: “!!”","Xiaxia: “...”","Qiao Lanshu closed her eyes and raised a hand to her forehead.","Xiaxia stood there dumbfounded, unable to say a word.","They remained under a tree across the street, repeatedly confirming that the sign really did say “hotel”—not restaurant, not some newly opened skating rink, and not an audiovisual shop popular with young people.","This time, Qiao Lanshu genuinely felt as though she was about to faint.","Xiaxia’s expression grew solemn. The mother and daughter stood there for a while. Qiao Lanshu anxiously paced back and forth several times. When she checked her watch, five minutes had already passed, yet that little bastard still hadn’t come out.","Of course, neither had the girl.","Hotels like this had only recently begun to appear. Many were private establishments run out of people’s homes, and management was not particularly strict.","There was no rule saying that minors couldn’t rent a room.","So as long as Qin Qiao'an had money, he could certainly get a room.","The question was, how many times had he done this already?","Qiao Lanshu couldn’t wait any longer. She grabbed Xiaxia and charged toward the hotel.","“Come on. We’re going inside to take a look.”","Just as the mother and daughter reached the entrance, a military vehicle suddenly pulled up outside the hotel.","They turned to look and saw Qin Yuanzheng stepping out of the vehicle in his military uniform.","The mother and daughter were both surprised to see him.","“Why are you here?” Qiao Lanshu asked.","Still, she was relieved that Qin Yuanzheng had arrived. The anxiety in her heart immediately settled somewhat.","Qin Yuanzheng was always reliable. As long as he was there, he could handle any situation, no matter how serious!","He strode over and put an arm around Qiao Lanshu’s shoulders. In a low voice, he said, “Didn’t I say last night that I’d keep an eye on him? Someone reported to me as soon as he met that girl.”","Qin Yuanzheng had also wanted to know what Qin Qiao'an had been doing lately, but he didn’t have time to watch him himself. So he had arranged for a guard to keep an eye on Qin Qiao'an and find out what he had been sneaking out to do these past few days.","And now, the surveillance had turned up something.","Of course, Qin Yuanzheng also knew that Qiao Lanshu and Xiaxia had been following Qin Qiao'an.","That was why he had hurried over.","After all, Qin Qiao'an had taken a female classmate to stay at a hotel. This was no longer something they could simply overlook.","Qiao Lanshu didn’t even know what to say.","She was a little flustered. Grabbing Qin Yuanzheng’s hand, she whispered, “Come on, let’s go inside and take a look. But stay calm, okay? Until we know exactly what happened, don’t hit him. We need to ask him first.”","Qin Yuanzheng looked at her, finding her current appearance somewhat amusing.","To be honest, he had never seen Qiao Lanshu look like this before.","If she hadn’t become a parent, she probably would never have been this flustered in her entire life.","He said quietly, “Don’t worry. I’m perfectly calm. You need to calm down too. Don’t be nervous.”","Qiao Lanshu took a deep breath!","She felt that there was no way she could keep from being nervous!","Qin Yuanzheng took her hand, and the family of three entered the hotel.","The hotel owner was a woman in her forties. She was sitting behind the front desk listening to the radio, nodding off, when she looked up and saw a soldier in a military uniform and cap walking toward her. A gun was even tucked at his waist.","The hotel owner was so startled that her drowsiness vanished instantly. She hurriedly stood up and looked past the soldier.","Outside the hotel entrance, a car was parked, with two imposing guards standing beside it.","The guards also had rifles slung over their backs.","The hotel owner was speechless.","For a moment, she wondered if she had committed some unforgivable crime.","Why else would soldiers come after her with guns?","She was so frightened that she nearly stammered. “C-Comrade, what... what’s going on?”","Qin Yuanzheng walked up to her expressionlessly and asked, “Excuse me, did two children just come in? A boy and a girl. Middle school students. The boy was wearing a black top, and he was about this tall.”","He gestured roughly to indicate Qin Qiao'an’s height.","Qin Qiao'an and his female classmate had only just entered. As soon as Qin Yuanzheng described them, the hotel owner immediately understood.","So it wasn’t her who had caused trouble. It was that child.","She instantly relaxed, and her speech became fluent again.","She quickly said, “Yes, yes, there are! Two children like that are staying here. Comrade, are you looking for them?”","After a pause, she added, “If you don’t mind me asking, what’s your relationship with these two children?”","Although Qin Yuanzheng was wearing a military uniform and had a guard with him, which was certainly intimidating, the hotel proprietress couldn’t simply take strangers to a child’s room and open the door without asking any questions, could she?","Qin Yuanzheng wasn’t angry. He explained, “That boy just now is my son. He’s been upset with the family lately and hasn’t been coming home. I had no choice but to track him down here. Could you show us the way and open the door? I’d like to talk to him and take him home.”","Of course, Qin Yuanzheng couldn’t say that he had come to catch his son dating behind their backs.","In any case, just as Qiao Lanshu had said, before they knew the whole story, they had to preserve the boy’s dignity.","When the proprietress heard this, she immediately took out a spare key and said courteously, “So that’s what’s going on. Oh, these children nowadays are all being led astray by the things outside. Video games, pop singers, and all sorts of other nonsense... Back in our day, we didn’t have any of that. The children are being ruined, and there’s really nothing we can do about it.”","Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu exchanged a glance and silently sighed to themselves.","They really were almost at their wits’ end.","Ah, until you raise a child yourself, you’ll never know how difficult it is to raise one to adulthood.","The proprietress walked ahead with the key, smiling as she said to Qin Yuanzheng, “Come along, comrade. I’ll show you upstairs. Your child’s room is on the second floor.”","Qiao Lanshu followed her upstairs. On the way, she couldn’t help asking, “Boss, how long have these two children been staying here? When did they check in?”","The proprietress replied, “Oh, if you want the exact truth, the boy isn’t actually staying here. It’s just the girl who’s been living here. She’s been here for... five or six days, I’d say. The boy comes to see her from time to time during the day and often brings her delicious food. They’re practically inseparable—the two of them are very close.”","Qin Yuanzheng’s face turned black when he heard the phrase “practically inseparable.”","Qiao Lanshu had wondered earlier how Qin Qiao’an could be so hungry after skipping just one meal at night when he clearly had pocket money.","So he had been spending all his money on someone else.","He was going hungry himself while bringing food to that girl every day. What a little gentleman he was, always eager to play the romantic hero.","Qiao Lanshu could only hope that things hadn’t reached the worst possible outcome.","The family of three followed the hotel proprietress to a room on the second floor. She was just about to take out the key when Qiao Lanshu quickly stopped her hand and said softly, “Boss, there’s no need yet. Let’s knock first.”","Opening the door with a key and walking straight in would be rather disrespectful, and Qiao Lanshu didn’t want to do that.","Qin Yuanzheng said nothing. He raised his hand and knocked several times.","Soon, Qin Qiao’an’s loud voice came from inside. “Who is it? Who’s knocking?”","As his footsteps approached, his voice grew louder. “Who’s knocking? Is something wrong?”","The hotel rooms of that era weren’t particularly soundproof. Qin Qiao’an’s voice was so loud that it sounded grating even through the door.","Qin Yuanzheng was already fuming, and hearing his son’s voice only irritated him further.","With a dark expression, he called out, “Your old man. Open the door, now!”","The room fell silent for two seconds. Then Qin Qiao’an opened the door, his face full of shock.","Along with the shock came panic, and beneath the panic was a guilty conscience.","His expression was all wrong. He stared at his father, mother, and Xiaxia standing outside, stumbling over his words. “Dad, Mom, Xiaxia... why are you all here?”","Qin Qiao’an was genuinely frightened.","He had been coming here from time to time over the past few days and had never been caught. How could he have known that his father and mother had followed him?","When Qiao Lanshu saw that he was willing to open the door and that he was fully dressed—not bare-chested or anything like that—the weight in her heart finally lifted.","Qin Yuanzheng, however, was still furious.","His face dark, he shoved the door open with force, grabbed Qin Qiao’an by the collar, and hauled him straight out of the room.","Qin Qiao’an didn’t resist. Like a drowned rat, he was dragged out by his father and dumped into the corridor. When Qin Yuanzheng let go, he crumpled to the floor like a puddle of mud, sliding down with a pathetic, limp little thud.","Qin Yuanzheng glared at him, his face dark with anger. “Qin Qiao’an! Stand up straight!”","Qin Qiao’an immediately sprang to his feet, puffed out his chest, and shouted nervously, “Yes, sir!”","Qin Yuanzheng: “...”","Qin Yuanzheng took a deep breath and closed his eyes for a moment.","If this had been one of the soldiers under his command, he would have kicked him without hesitation.","But this was his own son. His body was still developing, and his physical condition was far from adequate. If he kicked Qin Qiao’an, the boy would probably end up flat on his back.","Besides, Qiao Lanshu wouldn’t allow him to hit the child.","After holding himself back for quite some time, he finally punched Qin Qiao’an in the shoulder and said in a low voice, “Get your ass home!”","Qiao Lanshu and Xiaxia looked into the room and saw the girl standing there, tense and uneasy. When she met their eyes, she quickly looked away, standing awkwardly and at a loss.","Qin Qiao’an said to Qin Yuanzheng, “Dad, can I go home a little later? I want to say a few more words to A-Zhi.”","Qin Yuanzheng’s expression remained grim. “You have one minute.”","Qin Qiao’an knew that his father was truly angry this time.","And his mother was angry too.","That meant there was no one left in the family to save him.","So he became timid and obedient, not daring to argue. He hurried into the room and, under the watchful eyes of his family, walked over to Yuan Zhi. In a low voice, he said, “A-Zhi, just keep staying here. I paid for ten days in total, and they won’t refund the room charge if you leave early. I... I’ll go home with my parents first. I’ll come see you again tomorrow.”","Yuan Zhi looked at him, then glanced at Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng standing outside the door. She nodded and said softly, “All right. If you’re busy tomorrow, you don’t have to come.”","Qin Qiao’an whispered, “I’ll sneak over to see you. I’ll definitely find the time. Don’t worry.”","Although the two of them spoke very quietly, Qiao Lanshu, standing in the doorway, heard every word.","Her expression turned gloomy as well. Without saying anything, she studied Yuan Zhi, her thoughts impossible to read."]},{"number":277,"title":"Chapter 277: Just Good Brothers","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng drove Qiao Lanshu and the two children home.","The girl named Yuan Zhi was left alone at the hotel.","Qiao Lanshu sat in the car, her expression somewhat grave. She ignored Qin Qiao'an.","From time to time, Qin Qiao'an glanced at Qiao Lanshu’s face, leaning close to speak to her, but she still paid him no attention.","He immediately grew anxious, his expression turning a little guilty.","When his mother ignored him, he looked to Xiaxia, only to find her staring at him with an equally serious expression.","In a low voice, Qin Qiao'an asked Xiaxia, “How did you find your way there today?”","Xiaxia replied speechlessly, “Mom and I followed you the entire way. You were the one who didn’t notice. You were like an idiot.”","He had been followed all the way without realizing it, and Qiao Lanshu and Xiaxia were both ordinary people. They had simply run along behind him.","Yet even so, Qin Qiao'an had failed to notice. Xiaxia truly felt that her brother was becoming rather useless.","Normally, Qin Qiao'an would have argued with Xiaxia properly after being looked down on by his little sister.","But right now, he did not even dare to speak too loudly.","Lowering his voice, he said, “I usually conduct myself honorably. I don’t have to fear a knock on the door in the middle of the night. Of course I never imagined someone would follow me. Besides, even if I had been followed, so what? I didn’t do anything wrong. What do I have to be afraid of?”","Xiaxia glared at him and also lowered her voice. “You went to stay at a hotel with a female classmate, and you still have the nerve to say you conduct yourself honorably? What exactly is honorable about that?”","Then she added, “And if you really aren’t afraid, why are you acting so guilty now?”","Qin Qiao'an: “...”","Xiaxia shook her head and said with barely concealed delight, “Just wait. You’re in for it once we get home.”","Qin Qiao'an: “...”","Looking at the silent Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu, Qin Qiao'an suddenly sensed that a storm was about to break.","The family returned home in silence.","Han Ye had gone back to the Han family home these past few days. He had recently started high school and was growing up, with secrets of his own, so he had been staying here less often and going back to the Han home more frequently.","Since Han Wenlin was busy with work and did not pay much attention to him, Han Ye had a great deal of freedom when he was home alone.","When Qin Qiao'an got home and found that Han Ye was not there either, he thought that he was truly finished today. There was really no one left to protect him now.","The family of four entered the house.","Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu sat down on the sofa. Xiaxia pulled over a small stool and sat beside them to watch the show.","Qin Qiao'an looked from one person to the other, then walked over to the sofa beside Qiao Lanshu, intending to sit down.","But then Qin Yuanzheng gave him a look, and he immediately snapped to attention, standing rooted to the spot.","Qin Yuanzheng looked at him and said, “You have ten minutes to explain. Go on—what exactly is going on between you and that girl?”","He had only just started middle school. He was still practically a child, yet he was already thinking about dating?","Wasn’t that ridiculous?","Under his family’s stares, Qin Qiao'an hurriedly said, “First, let me make one thing clear: my relationship with Yuan Zhi is not what you think it is.”","The moment Qiao Lanshu heard that, she felt a little relieved. She quickly asked, “Then what exactly is going on? Why did you go to a hotel with her?”","Qin Qiao'an took the opportunity to dash over to Qiao Lanshu and squeeze in beside her.","Qin Yuanzheng’s face darkened, but he said nothing, merely waiting for him to explain.","Qin Qiao'an said, “Actually, it’s not that complicated. Yuan Zhi is my deskmate, and we get along pretty well. Sometimes she brings candy for me, and I bring her snacks and things too. Her grades are pretty good, and there are things I don’t understand that I can ask her about.”","Qin Qiao'an’s grades were not bad either. In a class of forty students, he ranked among the top ten.","Who would have thought that Yuan Zhi’s grades were even better than his?","Qiao Lanshu studied Qin Qiao'an’s expression and nodded. “And then? Get to the point.”","Qin Qiao'an said, “Then her father suddenly got into trouble and was arrested. Her mother was taken in for questioning too. No one knows whether her parents will be able to come back. She’s all alone—she has no relatives, no grandparents, nobody. And these past few days, lots of people have come to her house, saying they needed to investigate something involving her parents. The house was even sealed off!","“She had nowhere to go. By the time I found out, she had already been staying alone in a hotel for several days. She said she was running out of money and didn’t know where she would stay from now on. So I said I had money and would help her find a cheaper hotel. That’s how we found that place. I gave her all the money I had—fifty yuan in total.”","When Qin Yuanzheng heard this, his face darkened further. “Do you even know what her parents did before you decided to help her?”","Qin Qiao'an lowered his head. “I know whatever her parents did must have been serious. But what does that have to do with her? We’re good friends, and now she has no one to help her. I happened to be able to help, so I did. Mom, didn’t you always teach us to be kind and righteous people? Wasn’t what I did kind? Wasn’t it the right thing to do?”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","Qiao Lanshu exchanged a look with Qin Yuanzheng before asking, “Her mother was also taken in for questioning—what could her father possibly have done? Should we ask Director Han?”","Qin Qiao'an looked at Qin Yuanzheng expectantly as well.","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head. “Cases like this are confidential before they’re closed. Even if we ask, they won’t tell us.”","Qiao Lanshu looked back at Qin Qiao'an. “You really were only helping her out of simple kindness, not because of anything else?”","She was truly beginning to suspect that there was something more between Qin Qiao'an and Yuan Zhi.","It was not that she did not trust her son. She had been young once too.","A teenage boy just beginning to experience first love, seated beside a girl in class and close to her; then the girl runs into trouble, and the boy steps forward to help her.","It sounded exactly like the beginning of a romantic love story.","It was such a classic setup that Qiao Lanshu did not even know what to say.","Qin Qiao'an immediately said, “No. A-Zhi and I are just good friends. What else could there be?”","Qiao Lanshu looked at Qin Qiao'an, who still seemed a little guilty.","And Qiao Lanshu understood.","There was probably a little mutual affection between him and Yuan Zhi.","But first, they were still young. Second, Yuan Zhi’s family had suffered such a sudden upheaval that the two of them probably had not had the chance to think in that direction yet.","Qiao Lanshu fell silent for a moment, considering how this should be handled.","Then Qin Yuanzheng said, “How much money do you have to keep her in a hotel? Given her circumstances, the Women’s Federation or another department will surely step in. If nothing else, you could have asked a teacher for help.”","Qin Qiao'an scratched his head. “But Yuan Zhi said no one had come looking for her. And she might be sent to an orphanage.”","Qiao Lanshu’s heart skipped a beat. “Is it really that serious? What exactly did her parents do?”","Qin Qiao'an shook his head. “I don’t know. She doesn’t know either. She wanted to ask, but she said she went to the police station, and they told her they hadn’t arrested her parents. It seems her parents were taken away by people from some other department.”","As he spoke, Qin Qiao'an looked at Qin Yuanzheng and asked, “Dad, don’t tell me they were taken away by people from your unit?”","Qin Yuanzheng fell silent for a moment. Then he suddenly said, “Come to think of it, Si Zhemao came to Wencheng last month.”","The children had never heard of this man, but Qiao Lanshu knew who he was.","When she had still been pregnant with Qin Qiao'an, Qin Yuanzheng had worked with Si Zhemao on a mission to capture spies in the mountains.","Si Zhemao was an investigator from the capital, dispatched to carry out an assignment. He worked for the Investigation Department and had apprehended quite a few spies over the years.","After all these years, why had he suddenly come to Wencheng again?","Qin Yuanzheng knew Si Zhemao had come to Wencheng, but he had never had the time to meet with him.","After a brief silence, he said, “I’ll go see him and ask what’s going on.”","Qiao Lanshu’s expression darkened as well. “If that really is the case, then what will happen to Yuan Zhi?”","Qin Yuanzheng said, “Usually, children aren’t implicated in situations like this. If their parents are dealt with, the children are sent to an orphanage or placed with relatives.”","Although times had changed since the old days, spies and covert agents hiding in all kinds of places were still far from rare.","They blended into the crowd, living ordinary lives, working, studying, and waiting quietly for their chance.","The fact that Si Zhemao was still carrying out missions like this after all these years showed that this war without smoke had never truly disappeared.","Both Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng looked grave.","They turned to look at Qin Qiao'an.","Qin Qiao'an more or less understood that the situation was serious.","Troubled, he asked, “Will Yuan Zhi really be sent to an orphanage? Will she still be able to go to school? What will happen to her in the future?”","Qin Yuanzheng got to his feet. “In any case, this isn’t something you should be worrying about. And don’t go looking for her at the hotel anymore. It wouldn’t be appropriate. When the time comes, the relevant department will contact her.”","The Women’s Federation would send her to an orphanage, and she would still be able to continue her education.","But once she turned eighteen, she would have to make her own way in the world.","Qiao Lanshu had not expected things to turn out this way. Looking at Qin Qiao'an, she said, “You’re just ordinary classmates, right? Then don’t concern yourself with her anymore. Listen to your father.”","Qin Qiao'an looked conflicted, but he did not agree.","Instead, he returned to his room in low spirits.","In a quiet voice, Xiaxia said, “Mom, I don’t think my brother is going to listen.”","Of course Qiao Lanshu knew that. Still, if Yuan Zhi truly was innocent, then her parents’ crimes really had little to do with her.","It was just that, as a young girl, life and school would both be very difficult for her from now on.","Qin Qiao'an would surely help her in secret—saving up his pocket money to give her some, or something like that.","After thinking it over, Qiao Lanshu decided to have a talk with her son.","Qin Qiao'an was in his room, sitting at his desk and rummaging through a drawer for something.","Qiao Lanshu saw that his door was open, so she walked straight in and asked, “How much money do you have left?”","Qin Qiao'an whipped around, startled. Then, looking a little embarrassed, he said, “Mom, how come you don’t make any noise when you walk? You scared me half to death.”","Leaning against the desk, Qiao Lanshu wore an unusually serious expression. “An'an, I’ll be direct. I don’t mind if you want to help your desk mate. Giving her some money to improve her living situation, speaking up for her at school if she runs into trouble—that’s all fine. But I don’t want you getting too close to her. You’re only in your first year of middle school, and you still have to get into high school. I want you to focus on your studies...”","Before she could finish, Qin Qiao'an suddenly interrupted her. “Mom, are you worried that I’ll start dating too early?”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","She glared at him. “You know what I’m worried about? That’s right, I’m worried you’ll start dating too early. You are not allowed to date before you go to university.”","In truth, Qiao Lanshu did not want him to end up with Yuan Zhi either, but she could not say that to him now.","After all, most youthful crushes did not last.","Perhaps they were drawn to each other now because they were desk mates and got along well. That kind of attraction might fade away after a few days or a few months.","But if she forcefully stopped him from seeing Yuan Zhi or from helping her, it might trigger his rebellious streak and backfire.","The two children might end up thinking that the whole world had abandoned them, then cling to each other for comfort and grow even closer. Feelings that had not existed in the first place might emerge by then.","Qiao Lanshu would probably be angry enough to make herself sick.","Qin Qiao'an laughed. “Mom, what are you thinking? Yuan Zhi and I are just good friends—good buddies! If any one of my friends ran into trouble, I’d lend them a hand!”","Then he added, “Just like Aunt Zhong Mei. When she was having a hard time, didn’t you help her too, Mom? When she needed money to keep her business going, you lent her some. My situation with Yuan Zhi is exactly like yours with Aunt Zhong Mei.”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","Qiao Lanshu studied his expression and asked hesitantly, “So that’s really how you see it?”","Qin Qiao'an replied as if it were only natural, “Of course. What else would I think? Mom, Yuan Zhi and I are good buddies, so stop imagining things, okay?”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","Qiao Lanshu left Qin Qiao'an’s room with a complicated expression. As she closed the door, she looked back at him, still searching through his piggy bank.","Shaking her head, she shut the door.","Xiaxia had been keeping a close watch. The moment Qiao Lanshu came out, she hurriedly asked, “Mom, how did it go? What did my brother say?”","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. “Your brother? He’s just like you.”","At Xiaxia’s bewildered look, Qiao Lanshu added, “You’re both blocks of wood.”","Xiaxia: “...”","From the way that little girl Yuan Zhi looked at Qin Qiao'an, Qiao Lanshu could tell there was nothing ordinary about her feelings for him.","Qin Qiao'an saw her as one of the guys, but she was a girl, and girls were naturally more sensitive.","She certainly did not see him as one of the girls.","Forget it. There was no use overthinking things. It was better to let nature take its course.","...","Two days later, Qin Yuanzheng finally got the information from Si Zhemao.","He had indeed arrested several people recently. One of them had the surname Yuan. His wife was innocent, but she had been deceived by her husband into doing something that was not entirely aboveboard, so she had effectively been dragged down with him.","The husband would not survive, while the wife would be imprisoned for many years.","Their daughter would naturally be placed in the care of the Women’s Federation and an orphanage.","The details could not be disclosed, but Qin Yuanzheng had learned everything he wanted to know.","No wonder the Public Security Bureau had been unaware of it.","The case was being handled by Si Zhemao of the Investigation Department."]},{"number":278,"title":"Chapter 278: Puppy Love, Huh","paragraphs":["Since Qin Yuanzheng had already gotten to the bottom of the matter, there was now a definite conclusion.","Qiao Lanshu told Qin Qiao'an about it.","When Qin Qiao'an heard, he was rather surprised. He remained silent for a long while before asking, “Yuan Zhi’s parents were spies?”","Qiao Lanshu lowered her voice. “Apparently, she has Japanese ancestry. Her father may be descended from Japanese people who remained in China. I’m not sure about the details, but she definitely has some connection to Japan.”","Although Si Zhemao had given Qin Yuanzheng some information, the case was confidential, so even Qin Yuanzheng wasn’t allowed to know everything.","He only knew the general outline, but that was enough.","After clarifying the matter, Qiao Lanshu came to tell Qin Qiao'an. She said to him, “As I’ve said before, I have no objection if you want to help her financially. But I still hope you’ll keep your focus on your studies.”","Qin Qiao'an’s expression was complicated. He nodded and said, “I understand, Mom. Don’t worry.”","Seeing that he understood, Qiao Lanshu said no more about it.","Qin Qiao'an went to the hotel again the next day, but this time he returned before dark. He acted perfectly normally afterward, and he didn’t go out for the next few days.","Little by little, Qiao Lanshu relaxed.","As long as he wasn’t getting involved in some puppy love, everything else could be discussed.","Time passed slowly. Qiao Lanshu kept an eye on Qin Qiao'an for a while. He continued to go to school and come home as usual. When he didn’t have classes, he followed Qin Yuanzheng to the army base to play, train, and practice boxing. He also enjoyed hiking, swimming, and riding motorcycles.","Unfortunately, there was no motorcycle at home. Qin Qiao'an could only stare enviously at other people’s bikes, yet he was too embarrassed to ask Qiao Lanshu to buy him one.","After all, he was spending all his money on Yuan Zhi.","Yuan Zhi had indeed been sent to an orphanage.","There were many children in the orphanage, most of them girls. Some were around Yuan Zhi’s age as well. Under national regulations, these children were entitled to a compulsory education, with the government covering their tuition. But if they wanted to attend high school or a vocational secondary school, they had to earn the money themselves.","Yuan Zhi’s parents were never coming back.","The Women’s Federation had contacted her parents’ distant relatives. Only a rural great-uncle on her mother’s side was willing to take her in.","Yuan Zhi refused to go.","She wanted to stay in the city and continue her education. She didn’t want to go to the countryside.","She didn’t have much money, so Qin Qiao'an gave her his allowance. As a result, he didn’t have a single cent left in his own pockets.","Qin Qiao'an also began tinkering with little things to sell for money. Back when Han Ye was in junior high, he had made money by reselling cassette tapes with some young people from the neighborhood. Qin Qiao'an had accompanied Han Ye several times and knew a few of the channels.","So, in order to earn Yuan Zhi’s tuition, he started working too. He resold DVDs and all kinds of novels—pirated copies, naturally.","But in those days, no one paid much attention to whether something was original or pirated, and even fewer people cared. As long as the content was good, that was all that mattered.","Many of the discs sold in audio and video shops were copies the owners had burned themselves.","Those discs and videotapes were profitable, and plenty of people were willing to buy them.","Every day after school, Qin Qiao'an went out with those people to sell things, returning home after dark.","Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng both knew about it.","One night, while the couple lay in bed, they had a serious discussion about the matter.","Qiao Lanshu said anxiously, “What should we do? Should we stop him?”","The reason Qiao Lanshu had previously forbidden Han Ye from doing this kind of work was that his grades had been terrible—so terrible that she had needed to find him a tutor.","But Qin Qiao'an probably knew that, which was why he studied so diligently. At the very least, his grades had remained excellent, and he would have no problem getting into high school.","Besides, selling these things wasn’t illegal. Many people did it, and many made money from it.","If she forcefully stopped Qin Qiao'an, it didn’t feel entirely appropriate either.","Lying on the bed and staring at the ceiling, Qin Yuanzheng said, “Leave him be. There’s nothing wrong with selling things to make money. Recently, I’ve seen plenty of young people going to dance halls, skating rinks, and arcades. Compared with them, he’s actually quite worry-free.”","Qiao Lanshu fell silent.","She sighed. The couple lay side by side for a long while without speaking.","After some time, Qin Yuanzheng suddenly said, “That rascal. He’s figured things out early, hasn’t he? He’s actually thinking of earning money to support her education. Has he already decided that she’s the one?”","Qiao Lanshu said nothing, but she felt much the same way.","Although Qin Qiao'an kept saying that he and Yuan Zhi were good friends, brothers even, and that he couldn’t stand by while his good brother was in trouble, in his parents’ eyes, it was obvious that he had feelings for Yuan Zhi.","If two people went this far for each other, claiming there was nothing between them would simply be a lie.","Qin Yuanzheng continued, “That girl must be very touched, right? She’ll probably be devoted to him for life.”","Qiao Lanshu glared at him. “How old are they? They’re just teenagers.”","“Teenagers aren’t that young,” Qin Yuanzheng replied. “My grandmother married my grandfather when she was thirteen. And you married me when you were eighteen, didn’t you? Kids of fourteen or fifteen already understand plenty of things.”","On this matter, Qin Yuanzheng was much more open-minded than Qiao Lanshu.","He said, “I’ve been paying close attention to An'an these past few months. Ever since he started earning money, he seems to have become much more mature. As expected, love makes people great.”","Qiao Lanshu angrily smacked him. “You’re still joking at a time like this!”","She couldn’t laugh at all, could she?","Qin Yuanzheng grinned and pinned her down, saying in a low voice, “That girl’s grades are pretty good too, aren’t they? I heard she’s in the top three in her class. The teachers all like her and say she has a bright future. Looking at it that way, our An'an isn’t losing out either.”","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","She thought about it. Teenagers were at the age when their feelings first began to awaken.","Who hadn’t liked someone at that age?","So Qin Qiao'an and Yuan Zhi...","Qiao Lanshu tossed and turned, unable to sleep for most of the night.","In the end, she decided to continue observing them. As long as they didn’t do anything inappropriate, she would endure it for now.","...","Qin Qiao'an was extremely busy these days. Every day, he rode the old twenty-eight-inch bicycle Han Ye had left behind, weaving through the streets and alleys to resell small goods.","Yuan Zhi’s house had already been returned to her. She lived there alone, and after school, she went out selling things with Qin Qiao'an.","When night fell, Qin Qiao'an would ride his bicycle and take her home, each of them with a popsicle in their mouth—sometimes a piece of bread instead.","Then he would ride back to his own home.","As long as he got home before seven every evening, Qin Yuanzheng wouldn’t say anything, so Qin Qiao'an made sure to arrive right on time every day.","Still, Qin Qiao'an did have a conscience. Whenever he made money, he remembered to buy books and stationery for Xiaxia, as well as food and useful things for Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng.","When Han Ye went to serve in the army, Qin Qiao'an even bought him a bag to carry his belongings.","Qiao Lanshu felt that this son of hers still had some conscience. At least he hadn’t given every last penny to Yuan Zhi.","...","As time went on, Qiao Lanshu gradually stopped bothering with Qin Qiao'an’s affairs.","Now that she was on vacation, she rode her bicycle to visit Zhong Mei all by herself.","Ever since Zhong Mei had moved to Wencheng, Qiao Lanshu had often come to see her.","Zhong Mei’s general store had two floors. The first floor sold food, while the second sold household goods.","The store was quite large, with more than a dozen employees, and business was booming.","Zhong Mei had made a great deal of money running the store. She had even brought her two younger sisters over to help, putting them in charge of management and purchasing.","Zhong Mei wore her hair in a perm, along with a dress, makeup, and a pair of sunglasses perched on her head. She was dressed in the height of fashion.","When Zhong Mei saw Qiao Lanshu approaching, she walked to the entrance of the store and looked behind her.","“Oh, my godson and goddaughter didn’t come again today?”","“They’re both busy,” Qiao Lanshu replied grumpily. “One is busy dating, and the other is busy writing novels. Neither of them was willing to come with me.”","Zhong Mei was astonished. “Oh, Xiaxia has started writing novels? What a capable girl!”","Then she added, “But you know, Xiaxia might become a great writer someday—someone like Lu Xun, perhaps?”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","Zhong Mei’s teasing made Qiao Lanshu laugh. She said, “Stop joking around. Lu Xun? I can’t believe you actually said that.”","Then she continued, “Xiaxia is writing fiction. She submitted her work to several newspapers last time, but every one of them rejected it. She even received three rejection letters yesterday and hid in her room crying.”","Xiaxia had previously submitted some pieces to magazines and had several accepted, earning a few dozen yuan in royalties.","That had encouraged her to start writing a novel. Unfortunately, the first one she completed was rejected.","Zhong Mei pretended to be angry. “Those newspaper editors clearly have no taste! Their aesthetic sense is terrible! Our Xiaxia writes so well, and they still failed to recognize her talent. Once she becomes famous, they’ll come begging her, but it’ll be too late.”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","Qiao Lanshu sighed. “She’s still too young. She ought to spend a few more years studying and gaining experience—at least until she’s in high school. I think her writing will be much better by then.”","Zhong Mei and Qiao Lanshu went into the office at the back of the store.","As the owner, and having made quite a bit of money over the years, Zhong Mei had developed an imposing presence. These days, Guan Wenjun didn’t even dare raise his voice at home.","Whenever he spoke a little too loudly, Zhong Mei would raise her voice even higher and suppress him completely.","To make matters worse, their two sons also took their mother’s side. Guan Wenjun felt deeply aggrieved and would go to Qin Yuanzheng to complain whenever he had the chance.","Qiao Lanshu and Zhong Mei went out for a meal together. Afterwards, they spotted Qin Qiao'an on the street.","Qin Qiao'an was riding a bicycle with Yuan Zhi sitting on the back. The backpacks they carried were stuffed full. Anyone could tell they had gone out to set up their stall again.","Standing outside the restaurant, Zhong Mei folded her arms and offered her verdict.","“What a pair of lovey-dovey little waifs.”","Then she added, “Would you call them childhood sweethearts?”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","By now, Qiao Lanshu was completely calm and thoroughly accustomed to Zhong Mei’s remarks.","She said, “They’re enjoying themselves. How are they pitiable?”","Zhong Mei smiled. “Yuan Zhi really is lucky. At the lowest point in her life, she happened to have a male classmate willing to lend her a hand—someone who would even earn money to pay her tuition and support her education. The two of them have gone through hardship together since childhood. I imagine their relationship will be very strong in the future.”","She sounded a little envious. “Too bad no one helped me when I was young. Well, I suppose everyone has their own fate.”","The two sisters sighed over the young couple for a while, then continued strolling and chatting happily.","Sitting behind Qin Qiao'an, Yuan Zhi suddenly said, “Qiao'an, I think I just saw your mother.”","Qin Qiao'an grew tense and glanced around. “My mother? Where is she? Where?”","Yuan Zhi pointed toward a street corner in the distance. “Over there. We’ve already passed it.”","Qin Qiao'an let out a breath of relief. “It’s fine. My mother’s easygoing. She’s known about us for a long time.”","Yuan Zhi lowered her head shyly, her face flushing. “Known about what? There’s nothing going on between us.”","“How could there be nothing?” Qin Qiao'an said casually. “What’s going on between us is a very big deal!”","Yuan Zhi lowered her head even further, embarrassed. “Don’t say things like that. What big deal could there possibly be between us?”","Qin Qiao'an clicked his tongue and lowered his voice. “The fact that we’re working together to make money—doesn’t that count as a big deal? All our classmates say we’re business partners, bound together and sharing the risks. Doesn’t that count as a big deal?”","Yuan Zhi: “...”","Qin Qiao'an gave nearly all the profits to Yuan Zhi. In truth, he kept very little for himself, because Yuan Zhi needed the money for school and daily living expenses.","Yuan Zhi had initially harbored a faint hope, but after hearing him describe their relationship that way, she was left speechless.","So she said nothing.","Qin Qiao'an continued talking to her. “Yuan Zhi, have you thought about what you want to do in the future?”","Yuan Zhi shook her head. “I don’t know. For now, I’ll just focus on my studies. I’ll think about the future when it comes.”","Then Yuan Zhi suddenly asked, “Are you planning to join the army?”","Qin Qiao'an nodded as he pedaled, sweating heavily from the exertion. “Of course. My eldest brother is waiting for me in the army. He said he’d look out for me once I got there.”","Yuan Zhi’s mood darkened at those words.","If Qin Qiao'an joined the army, wouldn’t that mean she would hardly ever see him again?","Would they still have any chance to meet in the future?","She probed cautiously, “Couldn’t you not join the army? I’ve heard military service is very hard. Why not go to college instead, then become a teacher after you graduate?”","“No way,” Qin Qiao'an said seriously. “I like being a soldier.”","Yuan Zhi grew angry.","She felt that Qin Qiao'an was as dense as a block of wood. No matter how clearly she hinted at things, he seemed incapable of understanding what she meant.","And yet he treated her so well. At school, he barely spoke to any other girls, but he was always talking to her. They ate together, attended classes together, studied together, and he even helped her earn money for tuition and living expenses.","He was so good to her. Could it be that he truly saw her only as a brother?","Yuan Zhi didn’t want Qin Qiao'an to join the army. She felt that once he left, she might lose her chance to hold on to him.","Fortunately, he still had two or three years before he enlisted. She could afford to wait.","Once their relationship changed, she would try to persuade him."]},{"number":279,"title":"Chapter 279: Dreamscape","paragraphs":["When Han Ye enlisted, he was assigned to guard the border.","The area was at a high altitude, with a bitterly cold climate. Temperatures could drop to thirty degrees below zero at night, and life there was extremely hard.","Qiao Lanshu often bought warm gloves, thermal underwear, and other necessities to mail to Han Ye.","Han Wenlin’s second wife also sent him socks, and every time, she sent them together with Qiao Lanshu’s parcel.","It was worth mentioning that Han Wenlin’s second wife was none other than Han Ye’s former teacher, Zhao Yanfang.","Zhao Yanfang had always taught at a middle school. Qiao Lanshu had once asked her to tutor Han Ye in mathematics. Originally, she had only planned to tutor him for two years; once he entered high school, there would be no need for extra lessons.","But before Han Ye even started high school, Zhao Yanfang gradually became acquainted with Han Wenlin. Somehow, the two of them ended up together.","Before Han Ye entered high school, Han Wenlin married his teacher.","After Han Ye started high school, Zhao Yanfang was transferred to the high school division, where she continued tutoring him...","Today, Qiao Lanshu and Zhong Mei once again went shopping for things to send Han Ye. They bought some dried beef, thick gloves, thick socks, and specially insulated thermal underwear. After wrapping everything in two layers of waterproof bags, they took the package to Han Wenlin’s home to find Zhao Yanfang.","Zhao Yanfang had been married to Han Wenlin for only two years, and she still had no children. She had always treated Han Ye well, too.","When Qiao Lanshu went to Han Ye’s home, she had no idea that Qin Yuanzheng was there as well.","Qin Yuanzheng had come that morning to see Han Wenlin.","The two men were sitting in Han Wenlin’s study. Looking at Qin Yuanzheng’s grim expression, Han Wenlin asked in surprise, “Lao Qin, what brings you here? Is something wrong?”","Qin Yuanzheng almost never came to Han Wenlin’s house.","One of them was in the military, while the other worked for the police. They belonged to two different systems and usually had little reason to interact in the course of their work.","They generally only saw each other when their families gathered for a meal during the holidays.","Seeing that Qin Yuanzheng looked troubled, Han Wenlin couldn’t help growing concerned. “What happened? Did something happen to Han Ye in the army?”","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head. “I’m not here because of Han Ye.”","Han Wenlin simply looked at him without saying anything.","They had known each other for so many years, yet this was the first time Han Wenlin had seen Qin Yuanzheng look so grave—and so helpless.","Qin Yuanzheng remained silent for a long while before finally saying, “I might...”","He stopped again. The corners of his eyes had actually reddened slightly.","Han Wenlin: “...”","Han Wenlin was truly frightened by his expression. He hurriedly stood up and asked, “Lao Qin, what exactly is going on?”","Qin Yuanzheng himself didn’t know what was happening to him. He had joined the army in his teens, dedicating himself to defending his country. He had taken part in more than a dozen battles of all sizes and had never once deserted.","He had earned plenty of military honors and saved countless lives.","Now, at long last, he had a beloved wife to keep him company, children, and a successful career. He had even been planning to take some time off during the summer to travel around the country with Qiao Lanshu.","But then, after going for a medical examination a few days ago, the doctor told him that he might have an incurable illness.","When Han Wenlin heard this, he was stunned. “That’s impossible. Are the results back? Are you sure there’s something wrong with your liver?”","Qin Yuanzheng sat there and said, “I need to undergo more tests. They want me to go to the capital.”","He really hadn’t been feeling well lately. From time to time, he felt pain in his liver—sometimes mild, sometimes excruciating.","The problem had continued for some time, but he hadn’t taken it seriously before.","On top of that, ever since last month, he had been having nightmares almost every night.","He didn’t feel able to tell anyone what the nightmares were about.","But they terrified him.","In the dreams, he died of an illness that very year.","His emaciated body lay in a hospital bed, connected to a ventilator and so weak that he looked as though he had been completely drained of life. Qiao Lanshu was thin as well.","She sat beside the bed, haggard and skeletal, her face worn with exhaustion.","In the dream, after he died, he entrusted Qiao Lanshu to one of his comrades.","But in that dream, they had no children.","There was no Qin Qiao'an, no Qin Qiaoxia, and Han Ye never appeared either.","Dreams were only dreams, and he had never paid much attention to them.","But he had been having the same kind of nightmare for an entire month. Every time he woke from one, he felt a dull ache in his liver, heart, spleen, lungs, and kidneys. He had even lost his appetite.","He had grown noticeably thinner during this period.","Han Wenlin looked at Qin Yuanzheng. He really had lost weight, and his complexion was terrible.","Could he truly be ill?","Han Wenlin said, “Then go to a major hospital in the capital for an examination as soon as possible. Until the results are out, don’t panic.”","Qin Yuanzheng said in a low voice, “I’m not exactly panicking. I’m just worried about the three of them.”","“Lao Qin, you can put your mind at ease,” Han Wenlin said immediately. “After all these years, don’t you know what kind of person I am? Comrade Xiao Qiao, An'an, and Xiaxia—you can rest assured about them. If you really...”","He paused before continuing, “Don’t worry. I’ll take good care of them for you.”","After leaving Han Wenlin’s home, Qin Yuanzheng went to see Guan Wenjun as well.","These matters had to be kept confidential. He had no intention of telling Qiao Lanshu; he was afraid she would worry.","Whether the diagnosis was true or not, he had to make arrangements first.","Han Wenlin and Guan Wenjun were both trustworthy.","He also wanted to see Si Zhemao from the Investigation Department. He and Si Zhemao had known each other for many years. Although they were not often in contact, Qin Yuanzheng trusted his character.","There were also some of his former subordinates and comrades-in-arms. They were all dependable men.","But he had hesitated for a long time, thinking about it for several nights. Si Zhemao was about the same age as him, yet after all these years, he still hadn’t married. Could he introduce Qiao Lanshu to Si Zhemao?","Si Zhemao was sure to rise to a position of power in the central government in the future. If Qiao Lanshu followed him, she would have nothing to worry about for the rest of her life.","But every night, when Qin Yuanzheng woke and looked at Qiao Lanshu lying in his arms, he still couldn’t bear it.","He couldn’t bear to part with his little wife. He couldn’t bear to introduce her to someone else.","In the end, he decided to wait until the day he was truly dying before saying anything.","By the time Qin Yuanzheng left Guan Wenjun’s office, it was already afternoon. The pain in his abdomen had begun to return, faint but persistent.","He went home early, only to find the house empty. He sat alone on the living-room sofa, staring at the quiet home.","He thought of the dream, in which he had only met Qiao Lanshu at the age of forty.","Before meeting her, he had come home to this kind of silence every day. He had already grown accustomed to it.","But then panic rose within him once more.","He was afraid that everything in the dream was real, and that what lay before his eyes was nothing but an illusion.","Perhaps he didn’t have any children at all, and perhaps he had never married Qiao Lanshu.","Perhaps he had married Qiao Lanshu, but his health had already failed him. Perhaps he had dragged her down with him, and before long, he would die.","The more Qin Yuanzheng thought about it, the less he could sit still. He hurried out of the house once again.","He had to find Qiao Lanshu.","...","At that moment, Qiao Lanshu was at Han Wenlin’s home, sorting through things with his second wife, Zhao Yanfang.","Everything they were organizing was meant to be packed up and sent to Han Ye. There was food and daily necessities, most of it nonperishable items such as dried meat and steamed-bun crisps, as well as warm clothes to protect him from the cold.","The two women chatted as they worked. Han Wenlin came out of the study and walked to the doorway, where he glanced at Qiao Lanshu.","When Qiao Lanshu saw him, she was slightly surprised. “Director Han? You’re home today? Isn’t work keeping you busy?”","Han Wenlin: “...”","He was silent for a moment. Before he could speak, Zhao Yanfang said, “Old Han hasn’t been very busy lately, has he? I haven’t seen you work overtime recently. You’ve been coming home on time every day.”","Han Wenlin nodded. “Yes, things haven’t been very busy lately...”","But his expression remained grave, and his gaze toward Qiao Lanshu was filled with complicated emotions.","Qiao Lanshu felt that something was strange about Han Wenlin today. She wanted to chat with him a little longer, but Han Wenlin merely sighed and walked away with a solemn expression.","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","In a low voice, she asked Zhao Yanfang, “Don’t you think Old Han is acting strange today? Did something happen at work?”","As she packed the supplies, Zhao Yanfang replied, “Maybe. He’s been fairly idle lately. I think it has something to do with his superior. You know how chaotic things have been recently. His superior was caught up in it and is currently suspended at home while under investigation. No one knows when he’ll be able to resume his post. Old Han has to avoid suspicion, so a lot of his work has been put on hold.”","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu nodded in sudden understanding. Then she sighed and said, “Listening to you, I’m guessing my Brother Zheng is probably in the same situation. He’s been coming home very early every day lately, and he looks awful. He barely eats, and every night he tosses and turns in bed instead of sleeping.”","What she didn’t mention was that Qin Yuanzheng always got up in the middle of the night to stare at her.","She had been wondering what was wrong with him.","So it was because of work?","Zhao Yanfang said, “Lao Qin is a division commander now, right? At his rank, he’ll definitely be fine. You can rest easy.”","They had made it through the war years. Now that the People’s Republic of China had been under construction for so many years, surely they could get through this as well.","The two women continued chatting. Before long, they saw Han Wenlin standing in the doorway again, his expression heavy as he looked at Qiao Lanshu.","His face made it look as though Qiao Lanshu’s husband had died.","Unable to bear it any longer, Qiao Lanshu asked, “Director Han, is there something you want to say to me?”","Zhao Yanfang couldn’t stand it either. She asked him, “Old Han, why are you standing there staring at Xiao Qiao? Did you do something to wrong her?”","“How could I?” Han Wenlin sighed. “I just wanted to thank you both on Han Ye’s behalf for preparing all these things for him. Without you, that child would have no idea how much hardship he’d have to endure at the border.”","When Han Wenlin had been young, he had served in the army, and his life had been truly difficult.","Back then, times had been hard. His mother had been living in the countryside, where she barely had enough to eat, let alone spare anything to send him.","That was why he was genuinely moved to see Qiao Lanshu and Zhao Yanfang caring so much about his son.","Qiao Lanshu smiled. “You’re being too formal. Han Ye is my son too.”","Han Wenlin nodded awkwardly, then walked away again with a grave expression.","Qiao Lanshu and Zhao Yanfang exchanged a look before shaking their heads.","“I really don’t know what’s gotten into Old Han,” Zhao Yanfang muttered.","As it was getting late, Qiao Lanshu left Han Wenlin’s house and rode her bicycle home.","On the way, she stopped at the market to buy some vegetables.","As she was heading home, she saw Qin Yuanzheng in the distance. He was still wearing his military uniform, walking briskly down the street alone without his car.","The moment he saw her, Qin Yuanzheng quickened his pace and ran toward her.","Qiao Lanshu pressed one foot against the ground and stopped her bicycle. Looking at him, she asked, “Brother Zheng, where are you going?”","When Qin Yuanzheng saw her, he slowed down and gradually steadied his breathing. His face was a little pale, but he concealed his emotions well.","He came over, glanced at the things in her bicycle basket, then looked her up and down before asking, “Where did you go today? Why are you only getting home now?”","Qiao Lanshu said in surprise, “It isn’t even dark yet. It’s only six o’clock—how is that late? Besides, what about you? Are you off work already?”","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. He took hold of the handlebars and said, “I’ll give you a ride home.”","The dream he’d had before had felt far too real, leaving him somewhat dazed.","He hadn’t been in good shape these past few days. Fortunately, there hadn’t been any assignments recently, so work was relatively easy.","As he rode the bicycle, he said, “Don’t come home so late next time. I was worried when I got back and didn’t see you.”","As he spoke, a faint pain began spreading through his chest again.","Qiao Lanshu wrapped her arms around his waist and felt that he had lost a noticeable amount of weight. She asked, “Brother Zheng, has something happened to you lately?”","He wasn’t eating or sleeping well, and his whole condition seemed off.","She had noticed it long ago, but when she asked Qin Yuanzheng about it before, he hadn’t said anything. And since she had been busy with work herself, she hadn’t paid much attention.","Only now did she realize that something was truly wrong with him.","Qin Yuanzheng merely said, “It’s nothing. Nothing’s happened.”","Then he added, “By the way, Si Zhemao will be returning to the capital in a little while. How about we invite him over for dinner in the next few days?”","Qiao Lanshu nodded. “Sure. You can decide. I’ll buy some meat and vegetables in advance and give him a proper welcome.”","The husband and wife returned home together.","Xiaxia was already back and was watering the vegetables in the courtyard.","The moment Qin Yuanzheng entered the courtyard and saw Xiaxia, he felt dazed again.","Xiaxia glanced at them and continued watering the plants. “Mom, Dad, you’re back.”","Qiao Lanshu got off the bicycle, picked up the vegetables from the basket, and carried them into the house. As she walked, she asked, “Where’s your brother? He hasn’t come home yet?”","“No,” Xiaxia replied. “He always comes back at seven. You know that.”","Qiao Lanshu nodded and said nothing more, carrying the vegetables straight into the kitchen.","Qin Yuanzheng leaned the bicycle against the wall, then stood silently in the courtyard, looking at Xiaxia before turning his gaze toward Qiao Lanshu’s retreating figure.","He believed this was real, not something he had imagined.","He only hoped he wouldn’t have that terrifying dream again tonight.","It had been nearly a month. He kept dreaming about those things over and over, and it was taking a toll on his mental state.","He wasn’t afraid of dying.","What he feared was that Qiao Lanshu and the children would be left without anyone to rely on.","Without his protection, what would become of them?"]},{"number":280,"title":"Chapter 280: A Promising Future","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng quietly walked into the courtyard and stared at Xiaxia for a while.","As Xiaxia watered the vegetables, she noticed his gaze and looked at him curiously. “Dad, what are you looking at?”","Qin Yuanzheng watched her for a moment longer before saying, “Nothing.”","Then he turned and went inside.","Qiao Lanshu was cooking in the kitchen. When Qin Yuanzheng came in, he helped her wash and chop the vegetables.","Seeing him enter, Qiao Lanshu walked over and looked up at his face.","Qin Yuanzheng met her eyes, then quickly looked away. “What is it?”","Qiao Lanshu asked softly, “Is something going on lately? You haven’t looked well, and you’ve lost weight.”","Qin Yuanzheng was silent for several seconds before saying, “Nothing’s wrong. But I’ll have to go to Beijing in a few days. When I do... well, if you need anything, you can ask Han Wenlin for help.”","Qiao Lanshu didn’t think much of it. She simply asked, “Another assignment? How many days will you be gone? Oh, right—there’s going to be a military parade next year, isn’t there? You’ll be participating, won’t you? I wonder if Han Ye will get the chance to go.”","Being selected for the grand military parade was an incredible honor.","Han Ye would probably love to participate. It was just a question of whether he would be chosen.","Qin Yuanzheng would certainly be going too. He would be leading the soldiers under his command.","Although the parade was still a year away, preparations would probably have to begin now.","When Qin Yuanzheng heard her, he nodded. “That’s right. There’ll be a parade next year. This trip to Beijing will probably take... about three days. Three days should be enough.”","Qiao Lanshu nodded. “When are you leaving? I’ll pack your things.”","Qin Yuanzheng fell silent for a moment before saying, “No need. It’s only three days. I don’t need to bring much.”","Qiao Lanshu thought about it. Beijing wasn’t all that far away, and for just three days, he really didn’t need much preparation.","She asked again, “Are you worried about something?”","They had been husband and wife for so many years that they could still tell when something was troubling the other.","But Qin Yuanzheng had no intention of telling her. “It’s nothing. Work has just been busy lately, and I haven’t been sleeping well. I’m a little worn out.”","Qiao Lanshu knew that he hadn’t been sleeping well recently. He had been going to bed very late, and sometimes he would wake up in the middle of the night after finally falling asleep.","As she continued cooking, she said, “When I went out to buy groceries just now, I stopped by the pharmacy and got some traditional Chinese medicine. I’ll brew it for you after dinner. Remember to drink it before you go to bed. The doctor said it helps calm the nerves and improve sleep. Try taking it for a few days and see if it works.”","The doctor had been recommended to her by Zhong Mei. Zhong Mei was running her own business now, and the pressure and workload were both considerable, so she often had trouble sleeping. She had bought some traditional medicine to help regulate her health and said it worked very well.","Qin Yuanzheng reached out and rubbed Qiao Lanshu’s head, then nodded. “All right.”","His wife really was wonderful. Even though they had been married for so many years and their children were already in their teens, he still thought she was the best—and he still couldn’t bear to be parted from her.","...","Two days later, Qin Yuanzheng left for Beijing. Qiao Lanshu assumed he had gone on a mission.","But this time, he went alone. He didn’t bring anyone with him and drove there himself.","Qiao Lanshu carried on with her work and daily life at home as usual.","Han Wenlin did come by once with some things. He asked about the two children’s studies, then left soon afterward.","Qiao Lanshu didn’t think much of it. The two families were close, so it was perfectly normal for Han Wenlin to stop by for a visit.","But Guan Wenjun also came over—without Zhong Mei.","Whenever he visited, Zhong Mei and Guan Wenjun usually came together.","If Guan Wenjun wanted to see Qin Yuanzheng, he would normally go straight to Qin Yuanzheng’s workplace.","Now that Qin Yuanzheng wasn’t home, Guan Wenjun came by himself with a few gifts. He hadn’t even brought Zhong Mei along.","At the time, Qiao Lanshu was sweeping the courtyard. She had something to do at the school that afternoon, and there was no one else at home.","When she saw Guan Wenjun approaching, she was a little surprised. She put the broom aside and went to greet him.","“Section Chief Guan, what brings you here by yourself? Zhong Mei didn’t come with you today?”","As she spoke, she even glanced up at the sky, as though she suspected the sun had risen in the west.","Guan Wenjun set down the fruit and milk he was carrying, then walked around the courtyard. After that, he let out a long sigh.","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","She thought something must have happened and asked, “What’s wrong? Did you get into another argument with Zhong Mei? Coming to me won’t help. You know I’m definitely going to take Zhong Mei’s side.”","Guan Wenjun: “...”","He looked at her with a complicated expression and shook his head with another sigh. “Teacher Qiao, I came to check on you. And I didn’t argue with Zhong Mei. Do you really think I’d dare argue with her?”","Argue with Zhong Mei? Every time he said even a few extra words, she could shut him up completely.","Zhong Mei was so fierce and domineering. It was hard to believe she hadn’t been like this before they got married.","But after they married, she had completely changed into another person, leaving Guan Wenjun utterly speechless.","Qiao Lanshu certainly had no intention of sympathizing with him. She was obviously going to defend Zhong Mei.","So when she heard this, she rolled her eyes at him. “That’s what you get for being so long-winded all the time. If you talked less, Zhong Mei wouldn’t argue with you.”","Then she asked, “All right, no one comes here without a reason. Tell me, what is it? I have somewhere to be soon, so if you need something, get to the point.”","Guan Wenjun sighed. He paced around the courtyard a few times before asking Qiao Lanshu, “By the way, how old are your two children now? They’re still young, aren’t they?”","Qiao Lanshu couldn’t figure out what he was getting at. “Why are you asking about the children all of a sudden? Section Chief Guan, what exactly brings you here?”","Guan Wenjun scratched his head, wondering what he could possibly say.","It was just that after Qin Yuanzheng had spoken with him, he couldn’t stop thinking about what would happen if Qin Yuanzheng were gone one day. Qiao Lanshu would become a widow.","How would a widow raising two children manage on her own?","He would certainly have to help her when that happened. He couldn’t just stand by and watch Qiao Lanshu struggle.","Qiao Lanshu watched Guan Wenjun linger there for ages without saying what he had come for. He paced around the courtyard, looking at this and that, then glancing at her, all while sighing countless times a minute.","He looked as though he were having some kind of fit.","Qiao Lanshu asked him several times, but he refused to explain. All he would say was, “Comrade Xiao Qiao, if you ever run into any difficulties, remember to come to me. I’ll definitely help you and the children, so don’t worry.”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","Qiao Lanshu began to suspect that Guan Wenjun had gotten into a fight with Zhong Mei and been hit so hard that it had damaged his brain.","She tidied up the courtyard and then stopped paying attention to him. Pushing her bicycle, she prepared to leave.","She was busy. She still had to go to the school for a meeting.","When Guan Wenjun saw that she was about to leave, he was stunned. He grabbed the handlebars of her bicycle and asked, “Wait, Teacher Qiao! I’m still here, and you’re already leaving?”","Qiao Lanshu said inexplicably, “What else? If you want to stay here sighing, then take your time. Just close the door for me when you leave.”","After all, no one stole anything in the military compound, so they usually left their doors unlocked.","Guan Wenjun watched Qiao Lanshu wheel her bicycle away. She really had left.","He let out a heavy sigh and walked out of the house, muttering inwardly, If Lao Qin is really gone, then I can’t just sit by and do nothing about things here either.","Poor Comrade Xiao Qiao. Sigh.","......","After Qin Yuanzheng arrived in the capital, he went straight to the hospital for an examination.","At that time, only a few major hospitals had CT scanners, and blood tests were expensive as well. Many people were reluctant to pay for them.","The doctors in Wencheng had told Qin Yuanzheng to come to the capital for his examination precisely because the hospitals there had CT scanners that could show the condition of his internal organs.","Qin Yuanzheng went through the examination without hesitation. He didn’t care how expensive it was.","Afterward, the doctor told him that the results would not be ready for another two days.","He would have to stay there for three days, collect the results, see the doctor, and then return to Wencheng.","Of course, if the results were particularly bad, he might have to be admitted to the hospital immediately.","But he hoped he wouldn’t have to stay in the hospital. He didn’t want to be hospitalized.","In his dreams these past few days, he had constantly seen himself lying in a hospital bed, surrounded by all kinds of medical equipment.","He didn’t want to live the kind of life he saw in those dreams. Even if he really had to die, he wanted to return home and die there.","After leaving the hospital, Qin Yuanzheng found a random guesthouse nearby and checked in. He was only staying for two days, so he could make do.","......","As it happened, he had come at just the right time, because he ran into Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen at the hospital.","He had been standing in the lobby on the first floor when he happened to look up and saw Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen supporting each other as they slowly made their way into a ward on the second floor.","Qin Yuanzheng: “...?”","His eyes widened slightly, and he wondered if he had seen wrong.","Why had those two boys suddenly appeared here?","At this time, they should have been stationed at the border. Had they actually returned?","When had they come back?","Why hadn’t he received any notice?","Qin Yuanzheng didn’t remain puzzled for long. He immediately put his own concerns aside, strode up the stairs to the second floor, and checked one ward after another along the corridor Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen had just passed through.","He soon found the two boys.","Back when Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen had lived in the military compound, they had been sworn enemies since childhood. Whenever they met, they had to trade a few insults, and they had gotten into more than a few fights.","Their brawling had begun when they were still children in Longcheng and continued until everyone moved to Wencheng and settled in the military compound.","It wasn’t until they reached high school, grew older, and became more sensible that they began to rein themselves in. Even so, the two of them truly couldn’t stand one another.","Everyone in the military compound knew about it.","With their relationship having reached that point, it seemed almost impossible that they could ever become friends.","But fate was fate. Who would have thought that after joining the army, they would be assigned to the same place?","They came from the same area, were assigned to the same regiment and the same company, and in the end were stationed at the same post.","Even during recruit training, they had competed against each other for the title of top recruit.","Qin Yuanzheng stood at the doorway for a while, but he didn’t hear any arguing or fighting.","Only then did he walk in suspiciously. He said nothing and simply stared at the two of them.","The two young men were sitting on separate beds. A radio in the ward was broadcasting news and stories about the military.","Qin Yuanzheng studied them and noticed that both had grown thinner and darker. The fair-skinned, handsome young men they had once been were now tanned and rugged, and they looked taller too.","In terms of appearance, the two had grown into steady, mature men.","Han Ye had one arm in a sling, while one of Zhou Dingwen’s legs was encased in a cast. One had an unusable hand, and the other an unusable foot.","They both looked rather comical.","Qin Yuanzheng thought to himself, No wonder they can’t fight. Their arms and legs are both out of commission.","For a moment, he didn’t know what to say.","When they saw Qin Yuanzheng enter, both boys’ eyes widened in shock.","Han Ye stared at him in astonishment. “U-Uncle Qin? You got the news and rushed here so quickly?”","Then he asked excitedly, “What about my mom? My little brother? My little sister? Did they come to see me too? Did they bring me anything good to eat?”","Zhou Dingwen also kept looking past him, barely able to conceal his excitement. “Chief Qin, what about my father? Did he come?”","Qin Yuanzheng: “...”","Qin Yuanzheng looked the two of them over and said, “I’m here on business. I didn’t receive any news. What exactly happened to you two?”","Han Ye: “...”","Disappointment appeared on Zhou Dingwen’s face. “Oh, all right. I thought my father had come to see me too.”","They had been soldiers for more than two years and would soon be returning home to take the college entrance examination. After two years without going home, they both missed their families terribly.","Qin Yuanzheng sat down on a stool and asked them, “What exactly happened to you two?”","Han Ye explained, “There was a clash at the border. Zhou Dingwen and I happened to be on guard that night. We got into a fight, and then we ended up like this.”","There had been quite a few people involved, and the fighting had been fierce.","Four soldiers had been injured. Two had suffered minor injuries and remained with their unit.","Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen had been more seriously hurt. They were awarded third-class merit, and their superiors approved a week of leave for them to return and receive treatment, as well as visit their families.","This was their first time going home on leave, and they were so excited that they hadn’t even had time to write to their families before boarding the military helicopter and setting off.","Qin Yuanzheng calculated the timing. The news that Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen had been awarded merit should have reached his unit by now.","He simply hadn’t known because he happened to be away.","A smile appeared in his eyes. He patted them both on the shoulder and said with a laugh, “Third-class merit. Not bad.”","Opportunities to earn military merit didn’t come to everyone.","Besides, in Qin Yuanzheng’s opinion, their injuries weren’t particularly serious. That in itself was a good thing.","If this had happened earlier—ten or twenty years ago, when the country still occasionally fought wars abroad—many soldiers would have returned from the battlefield with severe injuries and permanent disabilities.","That was what truly counted as tragic.","The present era was already the best time in Qin Yuanzheng’s eyes.","He said to Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen, “It just so happens that I drove here. The two of you can come home with me in two days.”","At the same time, he thought to himself that since the two boys had earned third-class merit, getting into a military academy in the future probably wouldn’t be so difficult.","Their futures were bright. He wouldn’t have to worry about them too much."]},{"number":281,"title":"Chapter 281: Bring the Children Home","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng stayed in Beijing for three days. During that time, he called both Han Ye’s father and Zhou Dingwen’s father, telling them not to make the trip since he would take care of the two boys and bring them back to Wencheng.","And so, Qin Yuanzheng became just like an ordinary old father. Every day, he brought them food, watched them have their dressings changed, and asked how things were going in the army.","The army really was the best place to temper a person’s character.","Just look at how even that ox had been trained into good behavior.","Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen were now on excellent terms. The two of them often squeezed together and chatted.","Once, when Qin Yuanzheng brought them food, he found them huddled together listening to the radio.","“Are you two usually on duty together?” he asked.","“Of course not,” Han Ye replied. “But we’re in the same company, so we see each other often.”","Zhou Dingwen sighed. “Our comrades there come from all over the country. The only ones from Wencheng are Han Ye and me. When we first arrived, neither of us could adapt. It was far too cold over there. Later, Han Ye gave me a pair of thick socks, and that was how I managed to tough it out.”","Although Han Ye’s biological mother had passed away when he was very young, he now had two mothers—Qiao Lanshu and Zhao Lanfang—and both of them were extremely thoughtful.","Every year, they sent Han Ye plenty of warm clothing. They especially made sure to pack lots of gloves and socks.","Han Ye also wore through clothes quickly in the army, but if he used them sparingly, he had enough.","Zhou Dingwen’s mother, however, probably hadn’t thought of everything so carefully. She had prepared those things for him too, but they weren’t thick enough.","Neither of them had realized just how low the temperatures could drop at the border.","On winter nights, they stood at their posts on mountaintops for most of the night, often until their hands and feet went numb with cold.","The chilblains were painful and itchy, making them especially miserable.","These two boys had grown up without ever suffering hardship.","They might have been formidable at home, but after spending two days standing guard there, they would hide beneath their blankets at night and cry silently.","It was under those circumstances that Han Ye saw the chilblains covering Zhou Dingwen’s feet. At last, the two of them let go of their grudge.","Han Ye gave Zhou Dingwen two pairs of the thick cotton socks his mother had sent him.","From then on, they became sworn brothers.","Han Ye sighed. “We were young and foolish back then. Brother Zhou, don’t hold it against me.”","With his injured leg suspended, Zhou Dingwen reached out and hooked an arm around Han Ye’s shoulders. Moved, he said, “Good brother, I’ll never forget how you helped me when I was in need. From now on, we’re real brothers.”","Qin Yuanzheng: “...”","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless. The two boys were only nineteen, if one counted carefully, yet the way they spoke made them sound as though they were already sixty-nine.","Qin Yuanzheng sat there and sighed, choosing not to say anything else.","Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen continued chatting more and more enthusiastically.","Zhou Dingwen asked Han Ye, “By the way, which home will you be staying at when you go back?”","Han Ye thought about it. “I guess I’ll be staying at the hospital.”","Zhou Dingwen: “...”","Zhou Dingwen said, somewhat annoyed, “Oh, right. I almost forgot.”","His leg was still hanging there, after all, and he had actually managed to forget about it.","Han Ye was utterly exasperated.","Zhou Dingwen continued, “Then when we get to Wencheng Military Hospital, how about we stay in the same room again?”","Han Ye nodded. “Of course. Who else would we stay with? Naturally, we have to share a room!”","A smile spread across Zhou Dingwen’s face. He tightened his arm around Han Ye’s shoulders and lowered his voice. “By the way, now that you’re coming back wounded, your younger sister and brother will come visit you too, right?”","Han Ye didn’t think much of the question at first. He replied casually, “Of course. I’m their big brother.”","Zhou Dingwen nudged him with his elbow again. “Right, how old is your sister? Is she in junior high now?”","Qin Yuanzheng, who had been sitting nearby, looked up and studied Zhou Dingwen.","Zhou Dingwen had grown up in a military compound, so Qin Yuanzheng could practically say he had watched the boy grow up.","He knew him far too well.","Qin Yuanzheng was also familiar with Zhou Dingwen’s parents.","Zhou Dingwen’s father was even Qin Yuanzheng’s subordinate and currently worked at the military district in Wencheng.","Zhou Dingwen’s future prospects would certainly be much the same as Han Ye’s. Their family backgrounds and starting points were similar.","As for how high they could rise in the future, that would depend entirely on their abilities—and their luck.","So why had Zhou Dingwen been asking Han Ye about Xiaxia?","As a father, Qin Yuanzheng was extremely picky.","Even though Zhou Dingwen had good conditions, Qin Yuanzheng still didn’t approve of him.","His expression darkened as he shot Zhou Dingwen a stern look.","Zhou Dingwen immediately felt a chill down his back. He instinctively hunched his neck and turned to look at Qin Yuanzheng.","He found Qin Yuanzheng staring at him with a grim expression.","Zhou Dingwen: “...”","Zhou Dingwen instantly lost his nerve. He gave Qin Yuanzheng an awkward smile and scratched his head, not daring to say anything else.","Han Ye continued listening to the radio and casually said, “You mean Xiaxia? She should be in her second year of junior high, right?”","As he spoke, Han Ye began reminiscing too. “Come to think of it, I really miss my little brother and sister. I wonder if they miss me.”","Zhou Dingwen glanced at Qin Yuanzheng again and saw that he was already lying on the bed beside them with his eyes closed, resting.","Only then did Zhou Dingwen breathe a sigh of relief. He wiped the cold sweat from his forehead and lowered his voice. “They probably do. They’ve been attached to you since they were little, after all.”","Han Ye failed to notice that anything was amiss.","He continued, “Not at all. Xiaxia isn’t attached to me in the slightest, okay? I’m starting to wonder if she’s forgotten me after more than two years without seeing me.”","Han Ye had always been closer to Qin Qiao’an.","After all, Qin Qiao’an had grown up alongside Han Ye, so the two had a bond.","But by the time Xiaxia was born, Qiao Lanshu’s family had already moved to Wencheng, while Han Ye remained in Longcheng with Han Wenlin. He didn’t move to Wencheng until after he finished elementary school.","By then, Xiaxia was already six years old and rather distant toward him.","Han Ye said jealously, “To be honest, my sister is probably more familiar with you than with me.”","Zhou Dingwen smiled again. “That’s true. We grew up in the same compound and lived close to each other.”","The two of them whispered together for a while.","Then Han Ye asked Qin Yuanzheng, “Uncle Qin, you came to Beijing this time without wearing your uniform or bringing an escort. Did you come here to take care of some personal business?”","Qin Yuanzheng nodded with his eyes closed. “More or less.”","Then he added, “It’s an adult matter. Children shouldn’t ask so many questions.”","Han Ye: “...”","Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen exchanged a glance, and neither dared to ask anything else.","They had been afraid of Qin Yuanzheng since they were young, while also admiring him greatly.","Now that they had joined the army, their admiration for Qin Yuanzheng, a senior commander, had only grown stronger. The two huddled together and spoke in low voices, afraid of disturbing Qin Yuanzheng’s sleep.","By afternoon, Qin Yuanzheng decided that enough time had passed and went to ask the doctor about the results.","He didn’t fully understand his own condition. He was still having nightmares these past two days, but the pain in his body seemed to have eased.","In addition, he felt that there was nothing wrong with his body.","Could he really have a terminal illness?","Qin Yuanzheng's face was solemn. He went to the doctor's office and found the doctor who had examined him.","The doctor took out his examination results, looked at them, and said, \"At present, no problems have been found.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng was a bit skeptical. Of course, he was excited deep inside, but he was afraid of getting too happy too soon, so there was no change in his facial expression.","He looked at the examination form in the doctor's hand and asked, \"Is there really no problem?\"","This time when he came to this hospital, he had his blood drawn and also had a CT scan.","The examination result was hand - written by the doctor. The doctor looked at his report and asked, \"Do you still feel very uncomfortable these days?\"","Qin Yuanzheng thought for a while and said, \"Not really. It's just that I occasionally have some abdominal pain, but it's not frequent, and the situation has improved a lot compared to before.\"","He remembered very clearly that the abdominal pain started last month. That's when he began to have nightmares.","Every time he had a nightmare, he would die once in the dream.","That feeling was very strange, and he didn't know how to tell the doctor about it.","He just said, \"I have pain, and I often have nightmares at night. But the situation has improved a bit in the past two days. I didn't have a nightmare last night, and my abdomen doesn't hurt today.\"","The doctor looked at the report and asked him, \"Have you seen a traditional Chinese medicine doctor?\"","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head. \"No.\"","When he was seeing a doctor at the hospital in Wencheng, the doctor there gave him a simple examination. Of course, they didn't do a CT scan because that hospital didn't have the equipment.","But the doctor there said that his condition was not optimistic, and it was very likely a serious liver disease.","And now this doctor said he had no problems?","Qin Yuanzheng wasn't sure for a moment, but he was more willing to believe that there was no problem.","He took his examination report and looked at it, then asked the doctor, \"Is this CT scan accurate? Can it really show the internal situation of the body?\"","Doctor: \"Of course it can. But this thing is too expensive, so not many people get it done. Actually, we've only been using this thing for a few years. It's normal for you to doubt its accuracy.\"","Qin Yuanzheng then asked, \"Since there's nothing wrong with my body, why does my abdomen hurt? It's been a continuous month, not just one or two days.\"","Qin Yuanzheng just wanted to know why it hurt. If he didn't know the reason, he would always be worried.","The doctor also couldn't figure it out. He thought for a while and said, \"Otherwise, you can go and get some traditional Chinese medicine for conditioning?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","The doctor thought for a while and said again, \"By the way, you said you've had the same nightmare continuously for a month. Then maybe...\"","He said vaguely, \"You can go and ask a fortune - teller?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at the doctor suspiciously, then leaned over to look at the name tag on his chest.","Doctor: \"...\"","The doctor was a bit annoyed. \"I'm a real doctor. What are you looking at?\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at him with a complicated expression and said, \"I thought doctors were all materialists. I didn't expect...\"","The doctor was a bit embarrassed by what he said. He lowered his voice and said, \"Well, it's really hard to say. I've never encountered a situation like yours where you have the same nightmare continuously for a month. The last time I heard about such a thing was when my grandma told me bedtime stories when I was a kid.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","The doctor also said, \"Comrade, if you're not lying, then I really advise you to go to a temple and pay your respects. What if it works? Right?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng took his examination report and walked out of the hospital gate.","When he reached the gate, he even walked up to look at the hospital plaque.","It was indeed the largest military - region hospital in Jing City. Those two kids were still staying in the hospital.","So why were the doctors here so funny, talking to him about metaphysics?","Qin Yuanzheng stood at the hospital gate, looking at the people coming in and going out. He was silent for a long time.","Between going to another hospital for another check - up and going to a temple to burn incense, he finally decided to go to the most famous temple and burn some incense.","What if it worked?","Qin Yuanzheng drove to the temple. He knelt down properly in the bustling temple and offered a stick of incense to the Buddha.","He didn't make any wishes or ask for any fortune - telling sticks. After offering the incense, he walked out of the temple.","He drove back to the hospital and told Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen to pack up their things and go back to Wencheng that night.","Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen didn't have much stuff.","Each of them had a backpack, and the backpacks were filled to the brim, very solid. One backpack weighed dozens of catties.","Qin Yuanzheng picked up one backpack in each hand and asked Han Ye, \"Can you support him?\"","Han Ye's arm was still in a sling around his neck. He said, \"Sure! I'll carry him on my back.\"","It so happened that although Zhou Dingwen's leg was injured, his two arms were fine. Han Ye bent down to carry him on his back, and Zhou Dingwen wrapped his hands around Han Ye. The two of them cooperated quite well.","Qin Yuanzheng went through all the discharge procedures for them and then took them out of the hospital.","He threw the two backpacks into the trunk, let Han Ye sit in the front passenger seat, and then Zhou Dingwen lay diagonally on the back seat.","Originally, Zhou Dingwen and Han Ye could have recovered from their injuries in Jing City before returning to the army.","But they both missed home so much that even though it was a bit of a hassle, they still wanted to go back and have a look.","Han Ye didn't have much of a problem. The main issue was Zhou Dingwen. His leg was in a cast, and it was very inconvenient for him to move around.","Qin Yuanzheng glanced at the two of them and said, \"Sit tight. Let's go home.\"","Han Ye was so excited. \"Uncle Qin, how is my mom? How is she doing?\"","Qin Yuanzheng had always had an issue with him calling Qiao Lanshu \"mom\"!","Because Han Ye called Qiao Lanshu mom, Han Wenlin dad, and him Uncle Qin.","Just listen! Just listen!","People who didn't know would think that Qiao Lanshu was Han Wenlin's wife!","But fortunately, Han Wenlin had remarried, so Qin Yuanzheng didn't have as many negative feelings now.","He said calmly, \"Without you causing trouble for her at home and getting into mischief every day, she's doing great.\"","Han Ye: \"...\"","Han Ye scratched his head a bit embarrassedly. He had a crew cut, and his skin was dark. After two years of tough training in the army, he had grown a bit taller and was even bigger and stronger.","He was now 1.9 meters tall and looked even bigger than Qin Yuanzheng. He was really as strong as an ox.","Qin Yuanzheng sized him up a few times and thought to himself that the younger generation was really impressive.","It was precisely because of outstanding young people like them from generation to generation that the country would become stronger and stronger.","Han Ye said with a silly smile, \"My mom doesn't mind me. When she sees me later, she'll definitely be very happy!\""]},{"number":282,"title":"Chapter 282: Let’s Talk Again About the Child About to Cry.","paragraphs":["It wasn’t just Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen who were homesick. Even Qin Yuanzheng was longing for home.","He had spent a month away on missions before. But never had he felt such an overwhelming urge to return home as he did this time.","He folded up his medical report and placed it in the small compartment of his car. He had also followed the doctor’s advice and gone to a temple to burn incense. He felt he had done everything he could.","From now on, he decided, he would stop worrying about it.","There was certainly an element of avoidance in that decision, but he believed there was nothing wrong with his health.","After driving for several hours, Qin Yuanzheng finally brought Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen back to Wencheng.","He didn’t go home. Instead, he took the two of them straight to the First Military District Hospital and arranged for them to be admitted.","While completing the admission procedures, Qin Yuanzheng asked Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen, “Do you two want separate rooms?”","“No need, Uncle Qin,” Han Ye replied at once. “I can stay in the same room as Zhou Dingwen.”","Zhou Dingwen naturally had no objections. “Yeah, let’s stay together. It’d be so boring by myself, with no one to talk to.”","In truth, Zhou Dingwen had a little ulterior motive. Only by staying in the same room as Han Ye could he see Han Ye’s younger siblings.","If they were put in separate rooms, there was no way the Qin family’s younger siblings would come visit him on their own, right?","No one knew about Zhou Dingwen’s little scheme.","Han Ye’s reasoning was much more straightforward. He said to Qin Yuanzheng, “Uncle Qin, just look at his leg. It’s in such bad shape that he can barely walk. If I don’t stay with him, there’ll be no one to help him get to the bathroom. That would be awful, wouldn’t it?”","Zhou Dingwen: “...”","Qin Yuanzheng glanced at the two of them and shook his head. “All right, then.”","So he arranged a shared room for them.","Once all the paperwork had been taken care of, Qin Yuanzheng left the hospital and prepared to go home.","As it happened, Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen’s fathers had already received the news and arrived at the hospital to see their sons.","Qin Yuanzheng checked the time. It wasn’t time for Qiao Lanshu to get off work yet, and the two children were still at school.","He drove straight to the school where Qiao Lanshu worked and waited by the roadside for her to finish.","Qiao Lanshu had been busy with work these past few days. As the head of her teaching group, she was also responsible for a senior class. On top of that, Qin Yuanzheng had seemed somewhat off lately, so she had planned to make time to accompany him to the hospital once he returned from his mission.","Fortunately, their son, Qin Qiao'an, was already in high school, so she didn’t need to worry about his studies.","Yuan Zhi, who had a close relationship with Qin Qiao'an, had chosen to attend a vocational secondary school. The tuition was lower there, and she would be able to graduate and receive a job placement after three years.","Although the two of them had always been quite close, Qiao Lanshu had been paying attention over the past two years and hadn’t noticed any signs that Qin Qiao'an was dating early. He was cheerful and loyal, and had plenty of friends.","At first, Qiao Lanshu had worried that he and Yuan Zhi might fall in love, but later she discovered that among Qin Qiao'an’s close friends, Yuan Zhi wasn’t even the only girl.","After thinking it over, Qiao Lanshu decided not to interfere.","Now that Qin Qiao'an was in high school, he had started looking into military academies after being admitted. He spent every day thinking about joining the army.","If he knew Han Ye had returned, he would surely be overjoyed.","By the time Qiao Lanshu got off work, the students were also leaving school.","Qin Qiao'an was waiting for Qiao Lanshu at the school gate. Once she came out, the mother and son would go together to the junior high school next door to pick up Qiaoxia.","As it happened, Qin Yuanzheng had also come to pick them up. The moment Qiao Lanshu saw him, she immediately hurried over, leaving the two children behind.","Qin Qiao'an and his sister had long since grown used to it.","Qin Qiao'an muttered, “The moment Mom sees Dad, she forgets all about us.”","Xiaxia watched as Qiao Lanshu ran up to Qin Yuanzheng and tilted her head back to speak to him. Qin Yuanzheng affectionately slipped an arm around Qiao Lanshu’s shoulders, his gaze filled with tenderness.","Xiaxia couldn’t help envying her parents.","They had been married for so many years and their children were already grown, yet they were still so loving. How many couples in the world could achieve that?","If she could also find a love that lasted a lifetime, with one person by her side forever, how wonderful would that be?","Qin Yuanzheng really wanted to hold Qiao Lanshu and talk with her properly for a while.","But this wasn’t the right place or time.","So he merely draped an arm over her shoulders and drew her into his embrace for a moment before asking softly, “Why did you get off work so late today?”","She was ten minutes later than usual.","“The principal called an impromptu meeting,” Qiao Lanshu explained. “It ran a little long.”","Then she studied Qin Yuanzheng’s face. “You look better. Does that mean the problem at work has been resolved?”","Qin Yuanzheng was silent for two seconds before replying, “You could say that.”","If necessary, he could always find another temple and burn some more incense.","Qiao Lanshu immediately relaxed. She had been worried about Qin Yuanzheng these past few days as well.","Qin Yuanzheng opened the car door. “Get in first. We need to make a trip to the military hospital later.”","At those words, Qiao Lanshu’s heart tightened again. “What happened? Were you injured?”","As she spoke, she anxiously looked Qin Yuanzheng up and down. Qin Qiao'an, who had just reached them, heard this and hurriedly asked, “What? Dad, you were injured? This mission only lasted three days. Was it really that dangerous?”","Qin Yuanzheng: “...”","Qin Yuanzheng said, “It wasn’t me. Han Ye was injured. He earned a Third-Class Merit, and I just brought him back today. He’s staying at the military hospital.”","The most excited of them all was Qin Qiao'an.","He practically leaped three feet into the air, his face lighting up as he exclaimed, “What? My big brother is back? And he earned a commendation? That’s my big brother for you! He really is amazing!”","Qin Qiao'an’s face flushed with excitement. He immediately scrambled into the car and urged Qin Yuanzheng, “Dad, then let’s hurry to the hospital!”","Before Qiao Lanshu could say anything, Qin Qiao'an urged her into the car as well.","Once the whole family was seated and Qin Yuanzheng had started driving, she finally had a chance to ask, “How serious are Han Ye’s injuries? He’s come all the way back to be hospitalized, so he must be badly hurt, right?”","Most military districts had their own hospitals. Injured soldiers could be transferred directly to the military hospital at their base.","Why had Han Ye been sent all the way back to Wencheng? Could it be that his injuries were so severe that they wanted him to return and see his family?","Qiao Lanshu’s heart was in her throat. She was terribly worried.","Qin Qiao'an and Xiaxia stayed quiet as well, both watching Qin Yuanzheng.","Seeing the concern in their eyes, Qin Yuanzheng smiled and said, “Don’t worry. He’s fine. He earned a Third-Class Merit this time, and he hadn’t been home on leave for two years, so they granted him leave to visit his family. Once his injuries have mostly healed, he’ll return to his unit.”","Only then did Qiao Lanshu relax. “So that’s how it is.”","After a pause, she added happily, “Han Ye really is impressive. He’s already earned a Third-Class Merit? Does that mean he’ll have priority when applying to a military academy later?”","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. “It will improve his chances.”","It could be said that Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen no longer needed their parents to worry about them.","As long as they didn’t mess up on the college entrance exam and got scores high enough, they were certain to be admitted.","Now that Qiao Lanshu knew Han Ye’s injuries weren’t serious, she wasn’t in much of a hurry anymore.","She said to Qin Yuanzheng, “Why don’t we go to the market and buy some groceries first? Director Han and Teacher Zhao should be at the hospital by now. Let their family spend some time together first, and we’ll go over later. We can buy some meat and fish. I’ll go home and cook Han Ye a meal—his favorite braised pork, steamed fish, and some meat-filled steamed buns.”","Han Ye’s favorite foods were steamed buns and mantou.","He especially loved meat-filled steamed buns and could eat five or six in one sitting.","Back when Auntie Shi was still working for their family, she made Han Ye steamed buns every day.","Later, Qiao Lanshu learned how to make them from Auntie Shi, and she often made them for the children too.","But Han Ye had now been stationed at the border for more than two years. He probably hadn’t had any homemade steamed buns in all that time. After all, something like that couldn’t exactly be mailed.","Qin Yuanzheng thought about it and agreed.","At this hour, Han Wenlin had surely taken Zhao Yanfang to see Han Ye. After all, Han Wenlin was Han Ye’s biological father. Since their family was spending time together, they shouldn’t hurry over and disturb them.","Besides, Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen were staying in the same hospital room.","Zhou Dingwen’s family had probably gone over as well. Wouldn’t the room be terribly crowded?","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. “All right. Let’s go to the market first.”","Qin Qiao'an was beside himself with impatience. He hurriedly called out, “Aw, Mom, I want to see my big brother first! Can’t we go to the hospital now?”","Before Qiao Lanshu could answer, Qin Yuanzheng glared at him and said sternly, “Listen to your mother!”","Qin Qiao'an: “...”","Qin Qiao'an hunched his shoulders and went back to sit beside Xiaxia. Still extremely dissatisfied, he muttered under his breath, “You’re so gentle with Mom, but so fierce with me!”","It wasn’t fair at all.","Qin Yuanzheng didn’t pay him any attention. Since Qiao Lanshu had said they were going to the market for groceries, he simply took them all there.","After they bought the groceries and returned home, the whole family pitched in to prepare the meal. They made braised pork, steamed sea bass, tossed shredded vegetables, and two baskets of large steamed buns stuffed with pork and scallions.","By the time they finished cooking, it was completely dark. After eating dinner, the family arrived at the hospital before seven-thirty.","Most of Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen’s family members had already gone home.","Only Han Wenlin and Zhou Anping remained in the hospital room.","The two middle-aged men sat chatting as they kept their sons company and listened to them talk about life in the army.","After all, it had been more than two years since they had seen their sons. Both fathers had missed them terribly.","Zhou Anping asked Zhou Dingwen, “I heard your regimental commander is named Wang Wenjia. He used to be the Recruit Champion and is quite famous in the army. Have you met him?”","Once the conversation turned to the army, the two young men had endless things to talk about.","Zhou Dingwen nodded. “That’s him. Regimental Commander Wang really is impressive. We didn’t get many chances to see him. The last time I saw him was during recruit training.”","Hearing this, Han Ye immediately joined in. “Regimental Commander Wang was the Recruit Champion? I was a Recruit Champion too! Uncle Zhou, didn’t you know? I was last year’s Recruit Champion!”","Zhou Dingwen nodded and gave him a thumbs-up. “Han Ye really was amazing. Regimental Commander Wang presented him with his medal himself.”","The army frequently held various training exercises. People were injured in them all the time, but the outstanding soldiers also had a chance to distinguish themselves.","New recruits joined the army every year, and recruit training was arranged for them. Han Ye had been the standout soldier who emerged from last year’s recruit training.","At the time, people from other units had even approached him, wanting to transfer him to their unit.","Han Ye had refused.","He had already made his own plans. He had decided long ago to spend three years guarding the border before returning to take the military academy entrance exam.","If he were selected for another unit while he was still a new recruit and took part in their selection trials, what would happen if he failed to make the cut?","Would they send him back to his original unit?","And if he did make the cut and entered the special forces, what if he couldn’t return to take the military academy entrance exam?","His dream was to attend the Army Armored Forces Academy.","When Han Wenlin heard this, he was startled. Frowning, he asked, “Why didn’t you tell me about this?”","Han Ye said indifferently, “What was there to tell? I can make my own decisions.”","Han Wenlin asked again, “Which unit wanted you?”","“I forgot. I didn’t ask for the details at the time,” Han Ye replied. “But that regimental commander said he wanted me to become a sniper.”","Zhou Anping was surprised as well. “Being a sniper sounds pretty good. You didn’t want to be one?”","Han Ye glanced at Zhou Dingwen.","Zhou Dingwen let out a sigh and said mournfully, “Unfortunately, they didn’t choose me. Becoming a sniper was what I wanted most.”","What boy who had joined the army wouldn’t like guns?","Being a sniper was Zhou Dingwen’s goal.","But the selection and training process in the army was extremely grueling. Even the best soldiers in their respective units couldn’t easily get chosen.","Han Ye was silent for a while before saying, “Anyway, I wanted to stay at the border. I think guarding the border is really cool. I wanted to temper myself there.”","Zhou Anping smiled. “You’ve always been strong-minded, even as a child. Being this determined is a good thing. In the army, the worst thing is to hesitate and waver.”","What they needed was decisiveness, courage, and the will to keep moving forward.","Han Wenlin looked at Han Ye with undisguised admiration as well.","How could a father not be moved by having such an outstanding son?","The four of them chatted for a long time. As for the rest of the family, they had all gone home after night fell.","There were other matters to attend to at home, after all. The whole family couldn’t spend the night at the hospital.","As time passed, both Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen began to grow distracted.","Zhou Dingwen kept glancing toward the door. It was already seven in the evening, and the sky outside was completely dark, yet no one had come in all this time.","Unable to hold back any longer, Zhou Dingwen asked Han Ye in a low voice, “Han Ye, didn’t you say your younger siblings missed you terribly and would come to see you at the first opportunity? Why haven’t they come yet? Are they not coming after all?”","Han Ye: “...”","Han Ye let out a long sigh.","He, too, kept staring out the window, his heart growing cold.","They hadn’t seen each other for more than two years, and his younger siblings really were heartless. They hadn’t even come to see him.","And Mother Qiao hadn’t come either...","Sigh. When the sky cries, the fish know. But when he cried, who would know?","He was so heartbroken that he sighed and said mournfully, “Don’t ask me. I feel like crying.”","Zhou Dingwen: “...”"]},{"number":283,"title":"Chapter 283: My Archenemy Turns Out to Be in the Same Hospital Room","paragraphs":["Han Ye was actually getting rather annoyed with Han Wenlin.","His father was becoming more and more long-winded. He had been in the hospital room with Regiment Commander Zhou, droning on and on without end.","The two elders took turns asking about their life in the army—whether they were eating and sleeping well, how their comrades were doing, and how things were in their company.","In short, they had a great deal to say.","Every so often, Han Ye glanced toward the door. Zhou Dingwen did the same. Both of them seemed distracted, their minds clearly elsewhere.","Finally, Han Ye couldn’t take it anymore. He asked Han Wenlin, “Dad, why hasn’t Mom come? Neither have my younger brother and sister. Don’t tell me you offended Mom while I was away?”","Han Wenlin immediately glared at him. “What kind of nonsense are you talking about? How could I possibly offend Teacher Qiao?”","Han Ye looked at him doubtfully. “Then why hasn’t Mom come to see me even though I’ve been back for so long? If you hadn’t offended her, she should’ve come by ages ago, right?”","Han Wenlin was so irritated that he didn’t know what to say.","Zhou Anping, sitting beside him, began laughing as well.","Zhou Anping had known both their families for more than a decade and had watched all the children grow up. Naturally, he knew that the “Mom” Han Ye was referring to was Qiao Lanshu, not Zhao Yanfang.","Han Ye called Qiao Lanshu “Mom” with remarkable affection. Now that she hadn’t come, he was even starting to find his own father irritating.","Han Ye continued, “Then it must be that you didn’t tell Mom I was back—and that I was injured, right? Otherwise, there’s no reason she wouldn’t have come to see me.”","Han Wenlin was speechless. He glared at Han Ye and said, “I only found out you were hospitalized after receiving word from your Uncle Qin. I came over in such a hurry that I didn’t even have time to see Teacher Qiao. How could I have told her? Uncle Qin should have told her. Just wait a little longer.”","The moment Qin Yuanzheng was mentioned, Han Wenlin felt troubled again.","A few days earlier, Qin Yuanzheng had gone to see him specifically to entrust his wife and children to him. He had said that he was worried he had terminal cancer and wouldn’t be able to look after Qiao Lanshu and the others if he died.","Han Wenlin had been deeply shaken at the time and desperately wanted to know how Qin Yuanzheng’s examination had gone.","Several days had passed now. Qin Yuanzheng had returned from the capital, but Han Wenlin still didn’t know whether his test results were out.","Ever since learning about the matter, Han Wenlin had been constantly worried. He had barely slept these past few days.","He had hardly had any appetite, either.","He didn’t dare tell his wife, Zhao Yanfang. After all, Zhao Yanfang and Qiao Lanshu were close friends and colleagues.","If he told Zhao Yanfang, Qiao Lanshu would know about it within half a day.","There was nothing he could do but keep it bottled up inside.","That was also why he had been so talkative today. He had something weighing on his mind, and he had suddenly realized that he and Qin Yuanzheng were about the same age. Even someone as physically fit as Qin Yuanzheng could come down with such a serious illness.","He didn’t even dare imagine what would happen if he became ill. What would Han Ye do? And what would happen to Zhao Yanfang, his wife of only a few years?","The more he thought about it, the more worried he became.","Seeing that Han Wenlin’s expression was off, Han Ye nudged his leg with his own. Sitting at the edge of the bed, he looked at him and asked, “Dad, what are you spacing out for? Don’t tell me you’re really hiding something from me?”","Han Wenlin: “...”","Han Wenlin helplessly brushed at his trousers and glared at him. “I told you there’s nothing going on. Why are you so talkative?”","Honestly, Han Ye had nearly managed to extinguish all the fatherly affection Han Wenlin had finally worked up.","Han Wenlin had initially felt so sorry for him. Han Ye had spent two years being toughened up in the army, stationed along the bitterly cold and difficult border, and had come back injured at only nineteen.","The moment Han Wenlin heard the news, he had hurriedly abandoned his work and rushed over. He had fussed over Han Ye, asking about his work and daily life, and worrying about his injuries.","Yet after two whole hours, Han Ye had barely paid him any attention. He had even seemed impatient, bringing up Qiao Lanshu again and again.","Han Wenlin’s heart had gone cold.","This unfilial son had been away from home for more than two years—long enough for him to nearly forget how rebellious the boy had been ever since childhood.","Han Wenlin sighed. “I thought two years in the army would teach you to rein in that rebellious temper of yours. But apparently, you haven’t changed at all.”","Han Ye: “...”","Han Ye said helplessly, “I went to defend the country, not to undergo reform through labor.”","Han Wenlin: “...”","Hearing the father and son bicker, Zhou Anping and Zhou Dingwen couldn’t help bursting into laughter.","Zhou Anping pointed at Han Ye. “You brat. You were the terror of the military compound when you were little, beating all the neighborhood kids until they cried for mercy. I bet you took quite a few hard knocks in the army, didn’t you?”","Han Ye said smugly, “Uncle Zhou, I’m afraid I’m going to disappoint you. Even in the army, no one could make me take a beating.”","Zhou Anping glanced at Zhou Dingwen.","Zhou Dingwen coughed and said, “Han Ye really is impressive. He’s incredibly strong and very perceptive. In a one-on-one fight, no one is his match.”","Of course, when it came to teamwork, having Han Ye on the squad was like holding the trump card.","Sometimes, one had to admit that certain people were simply born with particular gifts.","Everyone might put in the same amount of effort, yet some people would still stand out far more than others.","By now, Han Ye could no longer sit still in bed. He glanced at the wall clock. It was already past seven in the evening, and eight o’clock would be here soon. It was getting so late, yet Qiao Lanshu, Qin Qiao'an, Xiaxia, and the others still hadn’t come to see him.","How was he supposed to accept that?","Fine. If they weren’t coming to see him, then he would go find them himself.","His arm was injured, but it wasn’t as if he were Zhou Dingwen, who had one leg crippled. If he could walk, he could make it home on his own!","With that thought, Han Ye stood up and said to Han Wenlin, “Dad, it’s getting late. You’ve been here all evening too. Why don’t you go home first? It’s not right to leave Teacher Zhao by herself at home, is it?”","Han Wenlin: “...”","How could Han Wenlin not know what his son was thinking?","He looked at Han Ye with a stern expression. “Han Ye, don’t even think about doing anything reckless. The doctor already said that the two of you need to stay in the hospital for observation and can’t be discharged yet. So don’t even think about wandering off!”","Han Ye immediately bristled. “What are you thinking? Of course I know I can’t leave the hospital. Don’t worry, I’m not going to break the rules. I just want to go outside for a stroll, breathe in the air of my hometown, and take a look at the night sky here. That’s all.”","Han Wenlin snorted coldly. “Cut the nonsense. Do you think I’ll believe you? Lie down and stay there!”","Han Ye: “...”","If Han Ye actually listened to Han Wenlin, he wouldn’t be Han Ye.","He looked out the window. Night had completely fallen, and the lights at the hospital entrance illuminated the view outside.","He began calculating how long it would take to walk home from here.","He was about to say something else when a knock suddenly came from outside.","Before anyone in the room could react, his eyes lit up. He sprang to his feet, hurried to the door, and opened it.","Sure enough, Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu were standing outside, with Qin Qiao'an and Qin Qiaoxia peeking into the room from behind them.","The moment Qin Qiao'an saw Han Ye open the door, he shouted, “Big Brother! You really came back!”","Han Ye was just as excited.","The instant he saw Qiao Lanshu, he rushed over to her. “Mom! My real mom! You finally came to see me! I thought you’d forgotten all about me!”","Qiao Lanshu looked at him in surprise, carefully examining him from head to toe. They hadn’t seen each other in more than two years, and Han Ye had changed so much.","Her eyes grew slightly moist.","With a smile, she said, “I raised you from the time you were little. How could I forget you? What a silly boy.”","Han Ye genuinely felt like crying now.","His nose grew stuffy, and he sidled up to Qiao Lanshu, hugging her arm with his uninjured one. In a pitiful voice, he said, “I’ve been back for hours already. Why did you only come to see me now? I thought none of you were coming. I was so anxious just now... Ow, Mom, look at my arm. My arm hurts so much! It’s practically broken. It’s terribly injured! Ow, I’m so pitiful.”","As he spoke, Han Ye’s eyes reddened.","It looked as though he might burst into tears at any moment.","Han Wenlin watched him with a speechless expression, wishing he could pretend not to know this son of his.","He had been visiting Han Ye for most of the evening, and Han Ye hadn’t once complained that his arm hurt, let alone cried.","But the moment he saw Qiao Lanshu, Han Ye became so ridiculously affected and melodramatic that it was almost unbearable to watch.","As expected, Qiao Lanshu immediately grew worried. “Is your arm really broken? The bone? That sounds terribly serious!”","Qin Yuanzheng added, “It’s only a fracture. It’s not as serious as he makes it sound.”","Han Ye continued putting on an act. “But it hurts so much! The doctor said it’ll take a long time to heal. Mom, you have no idea how dangerous that confrontation was. I almost didn’t make it back.”","Everyone fell silent.","Qin Yuanzheng, Zhou Anping, and Han Wenlin were all men who had fought their way up through the military.","In their eyes, what Han Ye had gone through was really nothing major. Compared with actual combat, this kind of confrontation had practically been a walk in the park.","Yet seeing Han Ye wailing like this made all three men hesitate despite themselves.","Could the border clash really have been that dangerous and serious?","Qiao Lanshu reached out and patted Han Ye’s arm before stroking his head. Her heart ached as she said, “You’ve lost so much weight in the past two years. And you’ve gotten so tanned. You’re practically a big black bull now.”","Han Ye had been fair and chubby since childhood.","After spending time in the military, he had slimmed down considerably. The lines of his face had become sharper, and he now looked every inch the mature, capable man.","Qin Qiao'an’s eyes practically sparkled as he looked at Han Ye.","He was carrying two insulated food containers, and he squeezed right between Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu, forcing Qin Yuanzheng out into the hallway.","Qin Yuanzheng closed his eyes and endured it.","Qin Qiao'an went over to Han Ye, set the food containers on the table, and then threw his arms around him. “Bro! Bro, you’re so handsome! Wow, is your hand in a cast? That’s so cool! And you’ve got a scar on your face too. Did you get it during this mission? A man’s medal of honor! Bro, you’re amazing!”","Qin Qiao'an was incredibly loud, shouting so enthusiastically that he nearly shook the entire hospital room.","Qin Yuanzheng quickly brought Xiaxia inside and closed the door.","Han Ye naturally wanted to show off a little in front of his younger brother. He pointed to his arm and said, “Do you know how I injured this arm?”","Qin Qiao'an obediently shook his head. “Nope. Tell me about it, Bro.”","Han Ye immediately began to embellish the story. “The other guy swung an iron rod at us, and it was about to smash into my squad leader’s head. Could I just stand by and let that happen? Of course not! So I sprinted forward in one bound and threw out my arm to take the blow for my squad leader!”","Qin Qiao'an gazed at him with admiration. “Big Brother, you’d really go through fire and water for your comrades. You’re the very soul of honor!”","Qiao Lanshu felt her own arm begin to ache just listening to him.","Han Ye hooked an arm around Qin Qiao'an’s neck and compared their heights. Then he said, “Not bad, An'an. You’re almost as tall as your big brother now. Impressive.”","Qin Qiao'an had inherited Qin Yuanzheng’s build. Tall and broad-shouldered, he was already over six feet tall at sixteen or seventeen.","His features and fair skin, however, resembled Qiao Lanshu’s, making him a handsome, light-skinned boy.","Qin Qiao'an said proudly, “I exercise every day. I’ll definitely end up taller than you.”","Han Ye snorted. “Keep dreaming. I’m already six foot two. It won’t be that easy for you to catch up.”","The brothers slung their arms around each other’s necks and went over to one of the beds to chat.","They hadn’t seen each other in more than two years, so once they started talking, they had an endless amount to say.","After Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu came in, they exchanged a few words with Han Wenlin and Zhou Anping.","Xiaxia had always been quiet by nature, and she said little now as well. However, she kept glancing at Han Ye from time to time. She felt that he had changed so much.","After more than two years apart, she almost didn’t recognize him.","Han Ye had become more masculine and even more handsome—and, of course, more mature.","Xiaxia watched him for a while before hearing someone call her.","“Xiaxia? Xiaxia?”","She came back to herself and turned around. Only then did she realize that Zhou Dingwen was lying in the hospital bed right beside Han Ye’s.","Even Xiaxia, who had always been exceptionally composed, nearly lost her composure.","Her eyes widened slightly as she studied Zhou Dingwen carefully.","Yes, he had gotten tanner, shaved his head in a buzz cut, and become rougher around the edges, but he was definitely Zhou Dingwen.","Xiaxia then turned to look at Han Ye. He was still chatting animatedly with Qin Qiao'an and hadn’t noticed her at all.","After a moment of hesitation, Xiaxia walked over to Zhou Dingwen. “Brother Dingwen? It really is you?”","Zhou Dingwen straightened his clothes and smiled. “It’s me. Han Ye and I are in the same unit, and we usually patrol together. Didn’t you know that?”","Xiaxia nodded. “I knew that. I just didn’t realize you were injured too.”","What she hadn’t expected even more was that these two sworn enemies would end up sharing a hospital room.","It was such a surreal scene."]},{"number":284,"title":"Chapter 284: Why Do You Keep Talking to Xiaxia","paragraphs":["Zhou Dingwen and Han Ye’s relationship had long since improved. They were no longer merely comrades-in-arms—they were brothers now.","As Zhou Dingwen looked at Xiaxia, he wondered if this might be a chance to grow even closer to Han Ye.","Xiaxia was in her second year of middle school. She was naturally pretty and quiet, and because she loved reading, she had a refined, scholarly air about her—the kind of girl every elder would adore.","As Zhou Dingwen looked at her, he found himself growing inexplicably nervous. He cleared his throat before asking, “Xiaxia, what year of middle school are you in?”","“I’m in my second year, Brother Dingwen. Is your leg badly hurt? Are you all right?”","Most of his leg was encased in plaster and propped up at the foot of the bed. It looked rather serious.","Han Ye had just been complaining bitterly to Qiao Lanshu that his arm was practically broken. Even a tough guy like him had cried so pitifully.","Zhou Dingwen’s leg injury must hurt a lot too, right?","Thinking this, Xiaxia kept looking at his plastered leg.","Zhou Dingwen glanced at Han Ye. Although he had been rolling his eyes at Han Ye’s melodramatic performance moments ago, he now lowered his head, sighed, and put on a pained expression.","“Actually, it’s nothing serious. It almost broke back then, but luckily the doctors managed to save it. It did hurt, but the worst of it has already passed. I can bear the pain I’m feeling now.”","Xiaxia’s expression softened with sympathy. “You’ve both had it so hard. Once you’ve recovered, will it affect your mobility?”","“The doctor said that as long as I take good care of it, it won’t affect me in the future. I’ll still be able to return to the unit and train normally.”","Xiaxia relaxed when she heard that. “That’s good. You and Brother Ye both love being in the military so much. You mustn’t let your injuries affect that.”","If Han Ye were unable to remain in the military because of his injury, he would probably be devastated.","Zhou Dingwen was just about to say something else when Han Ye suddenly shouted from the bed beside them, “Mom, Mom! What did you bring? It smells so good! I think I smell meat buns! No, wait—there’s braised pork too, isn’t there? It smells amazing!”","Han Wenlin shot him a glare. “Why are you acting like a dog? How can your nose be so sensitive? Didn’t you already eat your fill?”","Han Ye ignored him. After all, when Han Wenlin had brought him food earlier, he hadn’t brought any meat buns!","Only his arm was injured, and his legs were fine, so he promptly hopped out of bed and went over to Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu smiled. “I brought them, I brought them. They’re all your favorites.”","Qin Qiao’an quickly added, “Brother, I was just about to tell you. The reason Mom and I came so late was because she wanted to make meat buns and braised pork for you. Look—everything’s meat!”","As she spoke, Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng carried over the two insulated food containers and set them on the table beside the bed.","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, “As soon as I found out this afternoon that you were coming back, I went out and bought meat and fish. I made your favorite meat buns, braised fish, steamed sea bass, and cold tossed shredded vegetables. You like that too, don’t you? But the food containers couldn’t hold anything else, so I didn’t make soup.”","As Han Ye watched Qiao Lanshu arrange the dishes one by one, his eyes lit up. He practically drooled.","He reached out, grabbed a meat bun, and stuffed it into his mouth. His cheeks bulged as he continued speaking through the mouthful.","“As expected of my mom! You’re the one who loves me most!”","Then he glared at Han Wenlin, accusing him, “Look at you. You didn’t even buy me meat buns.”","Han Wenlin was speechless.","His expression grew complicated as he said to Qiao Lanshu, “I already brought him food earlier. He ate two bowls.”","The moment Qiao Lanshu heard that, she hurriedly told Han Ye, “Then don’t eat too much. You might make yourself sick.”","Han Ye ate another bite of his bun and said, “That was two hours ago! I’m hungry again now. Mom, you have no idea—Dad only brought vegetables. I couldn’t possibly get full on that.”","Han Wenlin was furious. “You just ate half a chicken. Was that a vegetarian chicken?”","Han Wenlin had brought roast chicken, while Zhou Anping had brought braised pork knuckle. Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen had devoured every last bit of it.","And now he was claiming Han Wenlin had brought him vegetables.","Han Wenlin felt that sooner or later, this unfilial son of his was going to anger him to death.","While eating, Han Ye picked up a meat bun and handed it to his good comrade Zhou Dingwen. “Here, here, try one of my mom’s meat buns. They’re amazing! Ah, when I was stationed with the unit, I thought about this flavor every single day. They’re so good!”","It was obvious how much Han Ye had missed the buns. He was practically wolfing them down, one after another.","Zhou Dingwen reached out to take the bun. Before eating it, he asked Xiaxia, who was standing nearby, “Xiaxia, did you help make the buns too?”","Xiaxia didn’t answer.","Han Ye was being so noisy that she hadn’t heard Zhou Dingwen at all.","She walked over to Han Ye and tilted her head back to watch him shove bun after bun into his mouth. She looked exasperated.","“Brother Ye, slow down. No one’s going to steal them from you. Be careful not to choke!”","With his mouth stuffed full of bun, Han Ye grinned foolishly at Xiaxia and said indistinctly, “Xia’er, you’ve grown taller. And you’re even prettier than before.”","Xiaxia sighed helplessly. “Don’t talk while you’re eating.”","Han Ye reached out and flicked her forehead. “What’s this? Are you lecturing your big brother now?”","As he spoke, he stuffed another bun into his mouth.","Xiaxia sighed again. “Why can’t I lecture you? Even my brother listens to me.”","Han Ye turned to look at Qin Qiao’an.","Qin Qiao’an was examining Han Ye’s medals. Hearing that, he immediately said, “That’s right. Other than Mom, Xiaxia is the boss of our family. Even Dad has to listen to her.”","Xiaxia was simply too sensible. She was smart, did well in school, was pretty, and always spoke with sound reasoning.","Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu doted on her.","Whenever Qin Qiao’an argued with Xiaxia, there was no need to guess who would be blamed. Qin Qiao’an was always the one who got scolded.","So he had no choice but to compromise and listen to Xiaxia. At least that way, he could avoid getting yelled at quite so often.","Qin Yuanzheng neither agreed nor disagreed. He simply doted on his daughter. Besides, Qin Qiao’an was always causing trouble.","More than once, he had congratulated himself that their second child had been a girl instead of another boy.","One son was already enough to drive him crazy.","With so many people in the hospital room, it had become rather crowded.","After chatting with Qin Yuanzheng for a while, Zhou Anping took his leave. After all, he needed to give Qin Yuanzheng’s family some time together.","Zhou Dingwen and Han Ye were both doing quite well, so there was no need to arrange for anyone to stay overnight with them.","After Zhou Anping left, Han Wenlin stayed a while longer.","He called Qin Yuanzheng out into the hallway, closed the door to the hospital room, and walked with him to the end of the corridor.","As they walked, Han Wenlin asked Qin Yuanzheng in a low voice, “Lao Qin, how did it go? What did the doctors in Beijing say this time? Are the test results back?”","Han Wenlin had genuinely been worried about Qin Yuanzheng. Now that he saw Qin Yuanzheng had returned looking perfectly fine, he finally let out a sigh of relief.","Qin Yuanzheng nodded slowly. He sighed and lowered his voice as well. “The results are back. They even did a CT scan and took blood samples. Anyway, they ran every test they could.”","Han Wenlin quickly asked, “And? What did the doctor say? Is it serious?”","Qin Yuanzheng walked over to the window and leaned against it. In a low voice, he said, “The doctor looked at the results and said everything was fine. There’s nothing wrong.”","Hearing this, Han Wenlin’s anxious heart finally relaxed. He breathed a sigh of relief and said, “That’s good news. Are you sure there’s nothing wrong? You don’t need to get checked again?”","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head. He gazed at the lush trees outside the window and said solemnly, “If the doctor says there’s nothing wrong, then there’s nothing wrong. I don’t think I need another examination.”","He didn’t want to go through another examination, either.","Leaning against the window, Han Wenlin was silent for a while before saying worriedly, “You said your abdomen and chest have been aching faintly from time to time lately. If there’s nothing wrong, then why do they hurt? How about seeing a traditional Chinese medicine doctor? Find an old physician to take your pulse.”","Qin Yuanzheng remained silent for a long while before saying, “We’ll talk about it later.”","Then he added, “It’s my own body, and I know it best. You don’t need to worry so much about me. If necessary, I’ll see a doctor.”","Han Wenlin nodded. The two men stood silently by the window for a while. Finally, Han Wenlin let out a long sigh and said, “Ah, we’re getting old. Our bodies just aren’t what they used to be.”","Back when Han Wenlin had been in the army, his physical fitness had been among the best in his company.","If he hadn’t been outstanding, he never would have risen to the rank of regiment commander.","But as the years passed, he was now well into his forties, and his child was almost twenty.","Time waited for no one. He felt old.","His work at the Public Security Bureau had been demanding all these years. Sometimes he had to stay up all night for meetings, and he had begun to realize that his body couldn’t keep up anymore. He was finding it harder and harder to endure the strain.","Qin Yuanzheng remained silent.","How could he not feel troubled, too?","He was in his forties, but his wife was only in her thirties, still young and beautiful.","Teacher Qiao, successful in her career, was very popular at school.","Qin Yuanzheng often felt melancholy as well. Now that he was getting old, would his wife come to dislike him?","He hadn’t been sleeping well this past month, with something weighing on his mind. Whenever he looked in the mirror, he noticed that his temples had already begun to turn gray.","It was frightening.","Qin Yuanzheng stared out the window. After a long while, he sighed, patted Han Wenlin on the shoulder, and said, “Come on. Let’s go back and see the kids.”","Han Wenlin followed him for a few steps, then thought it over and said, “Forget it. I’ll go home first. I’ll come see that brat tomorrow. You all should spend more time with him.”","With that, Han Wenlin sighed. “From the time he was little, you’ve spent more time with him than we have. You know he likes Teacher Qiao, and he likes the two children in your family, too. Spend more time with him. It’ll make him happy.”","Hearing this, Qin Yuanzheng said nothing more. After saying goodbye to Han Wenlin, he returned to the hospital room.","Inside, Han Ye, Zhou Dingwen, and Qin Qiao'an had already finished all the meat buns they had brought.","Qiao Lanshu had packed more than twenty meat buns in two insulated food containers this time.","The three young men had polished off every last one. It was true what they said: raising half-grown boys could eat a family out of house and home.","If there were two more boys in the family, Qiao Lanshu would have started wondering whether she could afford to feed them all.","After finishing the meat buns, Han Ye picked up his chopsticks and went for the braised pork. Like a good buddy, he placed a piece in Zhou Dingwen’s bowl and said, “Come on, try my mom’s braised pork. I’m telling you, my mom’s braised pork is absolutely incredible! Even the restaurants can’t make it as well as she does!”","Life at the border had been tough. Sometimes, when Han Ye missed home in the middle of the night, all he could think about were the meat buns and braised pork Qiao Lanshu made.","He hadn’t eaten them in more than two years, and he had truly been craving them.","Even now that his stomach was full, he felt as though he could keep eating!","Zhou Dingwen tried a piece of braised pork and immediately nodded in praise. “Aunt Qiao’s cooking really is excellent. The pork is so tender and flavorful. It’s just a shame we don’t have any rice.”","Han Ye nodded in agreement. “Exactly! Braised pork is meant to be eaten with rice. But it’s still delicious without rice.”","Qiao Lanshu watched them devour the food and said with a smile, “Then next time I’ll bring rice to go with the braised pork. I didn’t cook any today because I made the buns.”","After all, Han Ye’s favorite foods were buns, steamed rolls, and flower-shaped steamed breads. The only people in the family who preferred rice were Qiao Lanshu and Xiaxia.","Even Qin Qiao'an had northern tastes and preferred noodles and other wheat-based foods.","With his mouth stuffed full, Han Ye still managed to say, “You absolutely have to make braised pork with rice next time! It’s my favorite!”","Qin Qiao'an said to him, “Brother, is there anything you don’t like? You like everything.”","...","Before long, a few more mouthfuls were all it took to finish the braised pork. Then they moved on to the fish.","Young people really did have healthy appetites. They could eat so much and still digest it quickly. None of them ever seemed to complain about being too full.","Qiao Lanshu and Xiaxia sat to one side, watching the three young men fight over the food, their eyes filled with warm affection.","Zhou Dingwen didn’t eat as much as Han Ye. In fact, his thoughts weren’t entirely focused on the food.","He liked talking to Xiaxia. “Xiaxia, Xiaxia.”","Xiaxia turned to look at him, and Zhou Dingwen asked, “What have you been reading lately?”","Xiaxia thought for a moment before answering, “A little bit of everything, though mostly foreign literature.”","She had already read much of the well-known domestic works, as well as many ancient texts. Now that she was in middle school, her teachers often recommended foreign literature, so she had read quite a lot of it—and a wide variety at that.","Zhou Dingwen asked her again, “Have you thought about which university you want to attend in the future?”","Xiaxia was silent for a moment before saying, “Not yet.”","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, “Try to choose one close to home. Mom would still like you to stay nearby.”","If Xiaxia went to a school too far away, Qiao Lanshu would worry.","Han Ye finished an entire plate of shredded vegetables in sauce. Hearing their conversation, he raised his head and asked Zhou Dingwen, “Wait, why do you keep asking Xiaxia all these questions? She’s still young. How could she possibly have planned that far ahead?”","He paused, then added, “And why do you keep talking to Xiaxia? You two are pretty familiar, aren’t you?”"]},{"number":285,"title":"Chapter 285: Stay away from all those older brothers.","paragraphs":["The reason Han Ye asked that was because something felt off to him.","After all, the Zhou and Qin families both lived in the same military compound. How could Han Ye not know whether the two families were close?","When Han Ye was in school, he and Zhou Dingwen had been sworn enemies, getting into fights practically every day.","They could have fought one day, then run into each other the next, and Zhou Dingwen would still greet Xiaxia and An'an with a smile.","The Zhou and Qin families exchanged gifts and paid visits during every holiday. After all, Zhou Anping was Qin Yuanzheng's subordinate. They served in the same military district and lived in the same compound, so the families were quite close.","Han Ye knew perfectly well that they were close, which was why he had deliberately asked the question.","Ever since he was little, he had felt that his younger brother and sister belonged to him—only him.","Yet Zhou Dingwen kept coming around to win them over. Was he trying to steal them away?","That was why Han Ye had always minded Zhou Dingwen talking to Xiaxia and the others.","But then he reconsidered.","Before, he had objected because he and Zhou Dingwen had been sworn enemies. Of course he didn’t want his younger siblings associating with his archrival.","But what about now?","He and Zhou Dingwen were no longer enemies. They were good friends now. And yet Han Ye still felt uncomfortable whenever Zhou Dingwen spoke to Xiaxia.","As for why, he hadn’t really thought about it. His younger siblings were his, and Zhou Dingwen trying to get closer to them was simply unacceptable.","With that thought, he continued eating in big mouthfuls.","Holding his bowl, he plopped himself down beside Zhou Dingwen’s bed, blocking Zhou Dingwen from view and facing Xiaxia himself.","He looked Xiaxia up and down a few times, then said, “Xia'er, you’ve been in the room this whole time. How come you haven’t asked about me?”","Xiaxia glanced at his face, then at his arm.","She thought Han Ye was almost as big as Qin Yuanzheng.","Qin Yuanzheng was a big, powerfully built man, which was why Qin Qiao'an had grown tall and sturdy as well. Han Ye had spent more than two years in the army, and he had become just as broad. Clearly, he hadn’t been lacking food.","So Xiaxia asked, “Brother Ye, does your arm hurt?”","Han Ye had eaten his fill this time. How could he still remember the act of suffering he had put on earlier?","He answered casually, “No, it stopped hurting ages ago. Look, I can’t feel a thing.”","As he spoke, he tapped his suspended arm with his chopsticks.","Then he noticed everyone around him staring.","Qiao Lanshu in particular was looking at him with an utterly helpless expression.","Han Ye: “...”","Han Ye pointed at Xiaxia, thinking, Xiaxia, you’re getting pretty mischievous. Two years apart, and my sweet, quiet little sister has suddenly become devious.","He set down his chopsticks, furrowed his brows, and put on a pained expression. “Ow, it’s starting to hurt again. Ah, why does it keep coming and going? Wait, it doesn’t hurt anymore. See? It’s intermittent pain.”","Everyone: “...”","Zhou Dingwen couldn’t hold back any longer. He leaned out from behind Han Ye and said to Xiaxia, “Xiaxia, don’t listen to your brother. He’s faking it.”","Han Ye jabbed him with his elbow. “Get lost! Whether my wound hurts or not, don’t I know that myself?”","Zhou Dingwen refused to back down. “Of course you know. Did you install a switch in your wound so you could turn the pain on and off whenever you wanted?”","Han Ye: “...”","Everyone burst out laughing.","Xiaxia couldn’t help laughing either. “All right, then eat as much as you can while it doesn’t hurt. The food will get cold soon.”","Han Ye went back to eating. After a while, he said to Xiaxia, “You’re a grown woman now. You can’t go around chatting with all kinds of older brothers like you used to. You need to keep your distance, understand?”","Xiaxia: “...”","She looked at him suspiciously, wondering whether Han Ye had somehow forgotten to include himself in that warning.","Zhou Dingwen immediately grew dissatisfied when he heard this. He reached over and nudged Han Ye. “Han Ye, that’s not fair. We all grew up together. We’re not bad people. Is there really any need to keep our distance?”","Han Ye continued eating his braised pork as he replied, “So what if we grew up together? Men and women are different. Don’t you know that?”","Zhou Dingwen felt stifled, but he still couldn’t help glancing at Xiaxia.","Xiaxia, however, didn’t look at him again.","She gave Han Ye a glance, then turned and walked toward the door.","Qiao Lanshu had been sitting to the side, listening to the youngsters’ conversation. When she heard that, she gave Zhou Dingwen a meaningful look.","They were all young and innocent, at an age when they couldn’t hide their feelings.","Naturally, Qiao Lanshu could see at a glance what Zhou Dingwen was thinking.","She said nothing. After all, when a family had a daughter, it was only natural for plenty of families to come courting. Her daughter was beautiful and outstanding. It would have been strange if no one liked her.","With his mouth stuffed full of food, Han Ye saw Xiaxia heading toward the door and called out, “Hey, Xia'er, where are you going this late at night? Stay right here in the room.”","He instinctively wanted to tug on Xiaxia’s braid, but she was a grown woman now. Besides, one of his arms was injured, and his uninjured arm was busy eating braised pork, so he didn’t do it.","Xiaxia leaned against the wall and said, “Wasn’t it you who told me to stay away from all kinds of older brothers? I’m just keeping my distance from you two.”","As she spoke, she gestured toward Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen.","Zhou Dingwen immediately laughed when he heard that.","Han Ye, however, was displeased. He knitted his brows, and even the meat in his mouth no longer tasted good.","“What are you talking about? I’m your big brother. Why are you being so formal with me? Other than me and Qin Qiao'an, it’s the other older brothers you need to watch out for. Got it?”","Even though he was already very familiar with Han Ye, Zhou Dingwen was still stunned by his shamelessness.","He nudged Han Ye with his elbow and cursed, “Han Ye, you might as well just say my name outright.”","Then, still feeling indignant, he added, “Not that I’m saying anything, but Xiaxia’s grown up now. She’s much smarter than you. With a brain like yours, you’ve got some nerve trying to teach her. Just don’t lead her astray.”","Han Ye rolled his eyes, furious. “Bullshit! What’s wrong with my brain? Even if my brain isn’t much, it’s still better than yours. Have you forgotten how, back when the heavy snow blocked the mountain roads, half your body got buried in the snow and I had to pull you out? If your brain were better than mine, how come there were ten people on our team and everyone else was fine, while you were the only one who ended up buried in a snowdrift? You’ve got some nerve talking.”","Zhou Dingwen: “...”","Zhou Dingwen angrily closed his eyes.","He really had no way to explain that one.","It had happened when they had just joined the army.","Although they were both from the north, neither of them had ever experienced such harsh conditions, and Zhou Dingwen hadn’t been paying enough attention. He had simply fallen into a snow pit.","That was also one of the reasons Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen had become such close brothers.","It wasn’t only because of the socks Han Ye had given him. Han Ye had also helped him more than once.","Zhou Dingwen reached up and rubbed his forehead, then stopped talking.","If he said anything else, Han Ye would only find another way to tear into him.","Just then, Qin Yuanzheng came in from outside. He stepped into the room, took a look around, and asked Han Ye, “Finished eating?”","Han Ye nodded. “Finished.”","Han Ye had eaten the most of all the steamed buns and dishes Qiao Lanshu had brought.","Even Zhou Dingwen hadn’t had as much of an appetite as he did. Han Ye had polished off all the food and buns, leaving not even a drop of soup.","Han Ye even asked Qiao Lanshu, “Mom, are you coming to see me tomorrow? Will you bring me pork buns again? If you don’t make pork buns, scallion rolls are fine. Pancakes are fine too, or chive dumplings, or big steamed buns.”","As he listed everything with a frown, Qin Yuanzheng was rendered speechless. “Are you reciting a menu? Doesn’t the hospital have a cafeteria? Use your card and buy something yourself.”","He wanted this and that, but Qiao Lanshu was already busy with work. Normally, he took Qin Qiao'an and Xiaxia to eat at the military cafeteria, all so Qiao Lanshu would have less housework to do and could get home earlier to rest.","Han Ye scratched his head and looked pitifully at Qiao Lanshu. “All right, then. Mom, I’ll just eat at the cafeteria. You don’t have to cook for me anymore.”","Seeing that pitiful look on his face, how could Qiao Lanshu bear to refuse him?","So she said, “You only come home once in a while, and before long you’ll have to return to your unit. Just tell me what you want to eat, and I’ll make it for you.”","After all, she could manage to cook one meal a day.","Three meals a day would be a little difficult. She simply didn’t have that much time.","Han Ye immediately brightened. Sitting close beside Qiao Lanshu, he said, “Thank you, Mom. But you don’t have to make anything else. Just make me some chive-and-egg dumplings. That’s my favorite.”","In reality, Han Ye had far too many favorite foods.","There was practically nothing he wouldn’t eat.","Qiao Lanshu’s cooking was only average, but Han Ye loved everything she made.","Qiao Lanshu ruffled his hair. “All right. I’ll bring you dumplings tomorrow.”","Zhou Dingwen was rather envious of Han Ye. Qiao Lanshu was genuinely good to him—better to him than Zhou Dingwen’s own mother was.","Even after learning that he had returned, Zhou Dingwen’s mother had merely come to see him and bought him a meal from the cafeteria. She hadn’t cooked anything herself.","Zhou Dingwen sat silently to one side for a while. Then he heard Qiao Lanshu ask him, “Dingwen, what kind of dumplings do you like? I’ll make some for you too.”","Zhou Dingwen froze. Looking at Qiao Lanshu, he asked hesitantly, “Me?”","Qiao Lanshu nodded. “I’m making dumplings anyway, so I might as well make a few different fillings. What kind do you like?”","Zhou Dingwen was silent for a moment before answering, “Lotus-root, I suppose.”","Qiao Lanshu nodded. “All right. I’ll make extra and bring them tomorrow.”","They chatted in the hospital room for nearly two hours. By the time they finished, it was already getting late.","Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu prepared to leave.","Qin Qiao'an loudly protested, “Brother, can I sleep here with you tonight?”","Han Ye glanced at the narrow single bed and said with deep disdain, “Forget it. Go home and come see me tomorrow. This bed is so narrow I can barely stretch out by myself. If you squeeze in too, where are you going to sleep?”","Qin Qiao'an didn’t want to leave. He still wanted to hear Han Ye tell stories about life in the military.","So he hurriedly said, “I can sleep on the floor! Actually, I don’t have to sleep at all. I can just sit in the chair.”","“Enough, enough, enough. Hurry up and go home. You have school tomorrow. Come see me after class, and if you dare skip school, I’ll beat you up.”","Qin Qiao'an: “...”","He muttered, “How did you know I was going to skip school?”","He had never skipped class, all right? After all, Qiao Lanshu and Zhao Yanfang both taught at his high school.","If he so much as glanced at a girl for a little too long during class, his mother could come to his room that very evening for a serious talk.","What could he possibly dare to do?","Nothing. He didn’t dare do anything.","Even during his most rebellious years, he hadn’t managed to do a single rebellious thing.","However, before leaving, Han Ye grabbed Qin Qiao'an again and asked in a lowered voice, “I heard you were dating Yuan Zhi before. It had been two years, right? Are you two still together?”","Qin Qiao'an looked shocked. “Who told you that?”","“Mom. She mentioned it in her letters, saying you went out with her every day and that you two were very close.”","But that had all been two years ago.","Han Ye had been stationed far away in the military and had never known the details, so he took the initiative to ask now.","“There’s nothing to it,” Qin Qiao'an said. “Yuan Zhi and I are just good friends. Dating? How could that be? I’m not going to date until I’ve become a battalion commander.”","Han Ye was puzzled. “Why? Why wait until you’re a battalion commander?”","Qin Qiao'an replied with absolute seriousness, “Because once I’m a battalion commander, I can have my family join me. Isn’t the point of marrying a wife so she can stay by my side? If she can’t come with me and we have to live apart, what’s the point of finding a partner? Just to have someone as a decoration? No thanks.”","After a pause, Qin Qiao'an added, “Brother, weren’t you the one who taught me that? You said the same thing when I was little.”","Han Ye: “...”","Had he really said that?","Han Ye had long since forgotten.","Even so, he still said, “As for Yuan Zhi, I don’t think the two of you are very compatible. If she ever confesses her feelings to you, you’d better turn her down.”","Han Ye was very good at judging people. He had always felt that Qin Qiao'an and Yuan Zhi were fundamentally different and would never work as a couple.","Of course, he was worrying unnecessarily, because Qin Qiao'an hadn’t realized his own feelings yet.","Qin Qiao'an lowered his voice. “Mom has said the same thing, but don’t worry. Yuan Zhi might not even like me. She’s attending a vocational secondary school now, and once she graduates, she’ll become a teacher. She has a bright future ahead of her.”","Yuan Zhi had chosen vocational school because she wanted to start working sooner.","Graduates were assigned jobs, so it was indeed a pretty good option.","Since Qin Qiao'an had put it that way, Han Ye didn’t say anything more.","He turned to Xiaxia and asked, “Xia'er, what about you? Have you been keeping your distance from the boys at school?”","Xiaxia: “...”","Xiaxia said helplessly, “Brother Ye, why is dating all you ever think about? Do you want to fall in love?”","Han Ye: “...”","His expression turned solemn, and he said awkwardly, “Don’t talk nonsense. When did I ever say I... I’m only worried about you, understand? You’re so pretty. What if some scumbag takes an interest in you?”","Lying on the bed, Zhou Dingwen felt as if he had been struck by an arrow.","Why did Han Ye seem to be taking shots at him from every possible angle?","After Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu left with the two children, the lively hospital room instantly fell quiet.","Zhou Dingwen kicked Han Ye with his uninjured leg and said, “Han Ye, try not to say so much about me in front of your family from now on. At least leave me a little dignity.”","Han Ye remained unmoved. “What dignity do you need in front of my family? We’re all so familiar with each other. Who doesn’t know what you’re like?”","Zhou Dingwen: “...”"]},{"number":286,"title":"Chapter 286: About the Future of Children","paragraphs":["Han Ye watched Zhou Dingwen’s expression, feeling that something about it was odd.","He narrowed his eyes at Zhou Dingwen and asked, “Comrade Zhou, you were acting kind of strange tonight.”","Zhou Dingwen coughed and avoided looking at him. Instead, he busied himself straightening his bedsheets and said, “What do you mean? How was I acting strange? You’re the strange one, aren’t you? Han Ye, from now on, talk less about me in front of your family. We’re both adults, and we have our pride, okay?”","Han Ye shook his head, still eyeing him suspiciously. “See? This is where you’re wrong. Why do you need to worry about your pride in front of my family?”","Zhou Dingwen: “...”","For a moment, Zhou Dingwen was rendered speechless by the question. He turned to look at Han Ye. “It’s not that I only care about my pride in front of your family. Whether I’m with your family, my family, or anyone else, I care about my pride. Do you understand?”","Han Ye shook his head and continued staring at him. “No.”","Zhou Dingwen: “...”","Zhou Dingwen rolled his eyes angrily. “Forget it. Why am I even trying to explain this to a blockhead like you?”","Han Ye pointed at him. “Don’t think I didn’t hear that. You just insulted me.”","Zhou Dingwen said, “I called you a blockhead because it’s the truth. How does that count as insulting you?”","Han Ye said, “Zhou Dingwen, don’t think that just because my arm is injured, I can’t deal with you. I still have my legs.”","As he spoke, he swung one leg toward him.","Zhou Dingwen hurriedly raised an arm to block it and punched Han Ye in the leg.","The two of them then broke into a chaotic scuffle on the bed, one using his leg and the other using his arm.","In the end, they startled a passing nurse. She opened the door, walked in, and was instantly stunned. She shouted at them, “What are you two comrades doing?”","Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen were tangled up together on the bed. Han Ye quickly explained, “It’s nothing. We’re exchanging feelings... I mean, exchanging information about our injuries.”","Zhou Dingwen also said, “We’re just playing around. It’s nothing.”","The nurse was speechless. She walked over to their beds and said to Han Ye, “Comrade, please go back and lie down on your own bed.”","Han Ye coughed and exchanged a glance with Zhou Dingwen. Then one released his leg, and the other withdrew his arm.","Han Ye returned to his own bed next to Zhou Dingwen’s and lay down.","The nurse examined Zhou Dingwen’s leg, then checked Han Ye’s arm as well.","She found that neither of them was injured.","She gave them a complicated look and said, “It’s getting late. No loud disturbances are allowed in the hospital. Get some proper rest. If you really don’t want to stay in the same room, you can always apply for a room change.”","Han Ye quickly said, “There’s no need to change rooms. His leg is injured, and he still needs me to help him to the bathroom.”","The nurse glanced at Zhou Dingwen.","Zhou Dingwen: “...”","Feeling awkward, Zhou Dingwen turned his head away.","He suspected that Han Ye had done it on purpose!","They had just been arguing over his pride, and now Han Ye had deliberately announced in front of the nurse that he needed someone to help him use the bathroom.","Zhou Dingwen was so furious that his head began to throb.","Sure enough, even after sworn enemies became good friends, they still couldn’t avoid getting into fights!","The nurse looked at the two of them. Knowing that they were soldiers recovering from injuries sustained while earning merit, she didn’t say anything else and turned to leave.","As soon as she was gone, Han Ye called out again, “Zhou Dingwen? Zhou Dingwen?”","Zhou Dingwen was already furious enough to burst and had no intention of answering him.","Han Ye began muttering to himself, “Oh, don’t be angry. I only did that because the nurse was so pretty, and I wanted to help you get her attention. Didn’t you see the sympathetic look on her face when she heard that your leg was injured and you needed someone to support you to the bathroom? Put in a little effort tomorrow, and you might just have a beautiful encounter...”","Zhou Dingwen finally couldn’t take it anymore and shouted, “Han Ye, shut up! Say one more word and I’m going to lose my temper.”","Han Ye turned on the radio and sighed. “Fine, fine. I was only thinking of you. That nurse was really cute... Forget it, forget it. I won’t say anything more. Let’s listen to the broadcast. Listen to the broadcast.”","Zhou Dingwen: “...”","...","By the time Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng left the hospital, it was already past eight in the evening, nearly nine.","Qin Qiao'an and Xiaxia had school the next day, so they couldn’t stay up too late.","As soon as they got home, the couple sent the two children to wash up and get ready for bed.","Qin Qiao'an was so excited that he had no desire to sleep. Qin Yuanzheng knew his son all too well, so he went to Qin Qiao'an’s room and warned him, “Don’t even think about sneaking out to see Han Ye in the middle of the night. Otherwise, I’ll tie you to a tree and use you as a punching bag tomorrow.”","Qin Qiao'an: “...”","He stared at his father in shock. “Dad, you really don’t trust me at all. How could I possibly sneak off to the hospital in the middle of the night? Am I that kind of person?”","Qin Yuanzheng gave a cold snort. “Good. You’d better not be.”","With that, Qin Yuanzheng left with ruthless efficiency.","Qin Qiao'an: “...”","Qin Qiao'an let out a long sigh, then closed the window he had quietly opened.","Forget it. His father seemed to be in a particularly bad mood tonight. He’d better not walk straight into the line of fire. Being tied to a tree as a punching bag sounded absolutely terrifying.","When Xiaxia finished bathing and returned to her room, she sat at her desk and stared into space for a while.","She hadn’t seen Han Ye for more than two years, and she did miss her big-brother figure somewhat.","But Han Ye had changed so much. The change made him seem unfamiliar, and he looked less and less like the older brother she remembered.","Zhou Dingwen had changed quite a bit too, though his personality remained the same. As always, he liked talking to her and asking her all sorts of questions.","Xiaxia actually hated being questioned.","After staring blankly for a while, she stopped thinking about it. She picked up her textbook again, worked on her homework, and played some music on the radio at the same time.","When Qin Yuanzheng returned to his room, he saw that Qiao Lanshu had already washed up. She was sitting on the bed, using a towel to dry her hair.","Qin Yuanzheng immediately walked over, took the towel from her, and said softly, “Let me dry it for you.”","Qiao Lanshu’s hair was thick, glossy, and black. As Qin Yuanzheng dried it for her, he thought that his wife was still so young and beautiful, yet he already had gray hair.","Time passed far too quickly. For the first time, he felt a sudden urge to make it slow down.","As he continued drying Qiao Lanshu’s hair, he asked, “What are you thinking about? Why are you so quiet?”","Qiao Lanshu placed her hand over his and pulled him down to sit beside her. Then she said, “Brother Zheng, don’t you think there’s something strange about the way Zhou Dingwen looks at Xiaxia?”","Qiao Lanshu had mentioned this before.","At the time, however, the children had still been young, so neither of them had paid much attention to it.","But now, the children had grown up.","Zhou Dingwen was a year older than Han Ye and was already twenty.","Xiaxia had also reached the age of budding youth. Her features had matured, and she was becoming more beautiful by the day.","Qiao Lanshu kept a fairly close eye on Xiaxia. It wasn’t that she was worried Xiaxia might fall in love too young; what she was mainly concerned about was other boys pestering her.","After all, pretty girls attracted attention in every era.","Qin Yuanzheng sat beside Qiao Lanshu and pulled her into his arms. In a low voice, he said, “Actually, after giving it some serious thought, I think Zhou Dingwen is a pretty good kid.”","Then he continued, “Look, they’ve grown up together, and Xiaxia has always had a good relationship with him. As for Zhou Anping, he’s been my subordinate for more than ten years. I know their family situation better than anyone. Our Xiaxia will grow up sooner or later, and eventually she’ll have to find someone and get married. Rather than have her meet some boy whose background we know nothing about, it would be better for her to find someone from the compound—someone we know well. What do you think?”","Qin Yuanzheng had never been particularly pleased with any of the boys around them.","The thought of his beautiful, adorable Xiaxia dating one of those boys was enough to make his heart ache.","Still, he was reasonably sensible. He was already in his forties; he couldn’t protect his wife and children for the rest of their lives.","Once the children grew up, they would have lives of their own.","There was no need to worry too much about Qin Qiao'an. All he had to do was send the boy into the army, then let him stay there. That way, there was no need to fear that he would stray.","With Han Ye looking out for him as well, the two brothers shouldn’t run into any problems in the future.","It was Xiaxia who occupied most of his thoughts.","To put it nicely, Xiaxia was obedient and quiet. To put it less nicely, she was too reserved and somewhat introverted.","People with that kind of personality often ended up at a disadvantage. Qin Yuanzheng would almost rather Xiaxia were petty and calculating, or even a spoiled, willful girl.","As she was now—so quiet, and so beautiful—he was afraid she would be bullied in the future if he didn’t find her a husband whose background they knew well.","Qin Yuanzheng was silent for a moment before saying, “Zhou Dingwen did well in school. He’s intelligent and mature beyond his years, and he’s performed very well in the army too. He even earned a third-class merit this time. He’s Zhou Anping’s eldest son, and Zhou Anping will certainly pave the way for him. That boy has a very promising future.”","Qiao Lanshu nodded. She felt that Qin Yuanzheng made a lot of sense.","But after nodding in agreement, she said to him, “Everything you said is true, and I do think Dingwen is a good kid. But isn’t it a little too early to be talking about this? Xiaxia won’t even turn fourteen for another six months. We could wait ten years before discussing her marriage. Why are you thinking about this already? Are you in such a hurry to marry her off?”","She continued, “Look, Xiaxia has just started middle school. She still has high school ahead of her, and then she’ll have to take the college entrance exam. Whether she’ll get married or look for someone in the future is still uncertain. I haven’t even thought that far ahead. How did you manage to plan so far into the future?”","Qin Yuanzheng actually thought Zhou Dingwen was suitable enough that Qiao Lanshu began to wonder whether he had secretly planned to approach Zhou Anping about an engagement.","He was being far too hasty.","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless.","He rubbed his face and said helplessly, “Weren’t you the one who brought up Zhou Dingwen? You’ve mentioned him several times. I only gave you an answer after considering it seriously. Why are you unhappy about it now?”","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, “I’m only worried that Xiaxia might fall in love too young. An'an’s situation is still unclear, and if Xiaxia starts dating too, I’m afraid I really won’t be able to stop myself from beating the two of them.”","Qin Yuanzheng muttered, “That brat is so disobedient. You should have beaten him ages ago.”","Even Qin Yuanzheng himself had lost count of how many times he had beaten Qin Qiao'an. He always restrained his strength, afraid of actually injuring the boy.","But whenever he went too easy on him, Qin Qiao'an would dare to do it again the next time.","Every time, Qin Yuanzheng was furious.","Then Qin Yuanzheng heard Qiao Lanshu say, “Zhou Dingwen may have excellent qualifications, but there’s one problem: isn’t he too much older than Xiaxia? He’s a full seven years older. By the time Xiaxia graduates from college, he’ll be nearly thirty. He certainly can’t wait that long.”","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless.","He lowered his head and looked at Qiao Lanshu, his expression extremely complicated.","Noticing his gaze, Qiao Lanshu finally realized what she had said. She couldn’t help laughing. “Oh, that’s not what I meant... I wasn’t talking about you.”","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless.","He felt that her explanation had only made things worse.","With a complicated expression, he said, “You think seven years is too much, yet there are eleven years between us. Were you particularly put off by that when we got together?”","Qiao Lanshu hurriedly said, “I wasn’t. I really wasn’t. Don’t let your imagination run wild.”","She added, “If I’d really disliked you, I wouldn’t have gotten together with you in the first place. Back then, I was only eighteen. I was young, and I had plenty of choices.”","As she spoke, she suddenly remembered how Qin Yuanzheng had once tried to introduce her to several army officers, and she began reminiscing about the past.","“Oh, speaking of that, I suddenly remembered those officers you introduced me to. They were all quite impressive. Is Xiao Yang a regimental commander now? And Staff Officer Lin—wasn’t he transferred to another military region? Who else was there?”","Qin Yuanzheng’s face darkened. He listened to her chatter on about those former subordinates without saying a word, simply lying there and quietly watching her.","After she finished, he gave a meaningful snort and said, “What a shame. Would you like me to summon all of them here so you can reminisce together?”","Qiao Lanshu didn’t even try to placate him. Instead, she nodded and said, “Sure. It’s been so many years since we’ve seen each other; getting together would be nice. What do you think, Chief Qin?”","Qin Yuanzheng’s face turned black with displeasure. It was obvious that he was unhappy.","Seeing him like that, Qiao Lanshu was utterly exasperated.","They had been married for so many years, yet Qin Yuanzheng could still brood over something that had happened more than a decade ago.","There was nothing for it but to coax him. In a low voice, she said, “Things were different back then. In our day, we didn’t have to study for so many years. Girls were expected to marry at eighteen, and if they didn’t, they had to go to the countryside. But Xiaxia has to attend college now. Seven years really is a long time. What man could wait until he was thirty? Don’t you agree?”","Qin Yuanzheng snorted. “Our Xiaxia is wonderful. If someone truly loves her, would waiting until she’s thirty really be so difficult? If he can’t even wait that long, then there’s nothing more to say.”","Qiao Lanshu thought for a moment before saying, “Forget it. Maybe we’re just imagining things. Zhou Dingwen is a very sensible child. Even if he really does like Xiaxia, he may not say anything. She’s still so young and hasn’t realized anything yet. He probably wouldn’t dare to confess.”","There were already male students in Xiaxia’s class who had crushes on her. As long as they didn’t say anything, it didn’t really count as a problem.","Qin Yuanzheng hadn’t had a proper rest all month, and he was feeling rather tired now. Seeing the pallor of his face, Qiao Lanshu said, “All right, it’s getting late. Let’s get some sleep first.”","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. As he lay down, he was still wondering whether he would have another nightmare that night.","His body wasn’t hurting much today. If he didn’t have any more nightmares, perhaps this ordeal would finally be over?"]},{"number":287,"title":"Chapter 287: Night Talk","paragraphs":["After Qin Yuanzheng returned this time, he still had a nightmare in the middle of the night.","It was the same dream as before. In it, he lay sick in bed, his illness terminal, while Qiao Lanshu sat beside him, looking haggard and painfully thin.","Why did he keep having a dream like that?","Everything in the dream felt so real, as though it had actually happened.","Qin Yuanzheng woke from the nightmare once again.","He lay in bed and glanced toward the window. The curtains were drawn, and it was still dark outside. Not a sliver of light seeped through.","He picked up the little clock on the bedside table. It showed three o’clock in the morning.","Qin Yuanzheng quietly put the clock back.","Then he turned to look at Qiao Lanshu beside him, only to realize that she had woken at some point.","Qin Yuanzheng froze, slightly surprised. “Why are you awake? Did I wake you?”","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. In the darkness, she sat up and turned on the light.","As soon as the room lit up, Qin Yuanzheng sat up as well. He looked at Qiao Lanshu with concern, wrapped an arm around her, and asked softly, “What’s wrong? Did you have a nightmare?”","Qiao Lanshu looked at him and wiped the sweat from his forehead with her sleeve. “Nothing’s wrong with me. I woke up to see what was wrong with you.”","Qin Yuanzheng fell silent.","He lowered his head and said quietly, “I’m fine too. I just had a nightmare. Go back to sleep.”","As he spoke, he reached for the light.","Qiao Lanshu pressed down on his hand and looked at him seriously. “What kind of nightmare was it? Tell me.”","Qin Yuanzheng stared at her in silence. After a long moment, he still said nothing.","If it had been an ordinary nightmare, he could have told her without a second thought.","But this nightmare was far too frightening. In it, he had died, and Qiao Lanshu had died afterward. The two of them had never had any children.","There was no Qin Qiao’an, no Qin Qiaoxia, and no Han Ye.","Even he could barely bear a dream like that. If he told Qiao Lanshu, wouldn’t she be even more frightened?","That was why Qin Yuanzheng remained silent, unsure how to begin.","Qiao Lanshu noticed that something was wrong with his expression. She shifted around until she was sitting directly across from him. Facing him, she asked softly, “Brother Zheng, you haven’t been sleeping well this whole past month, have you? Have you been having nightmares often? I thought it was something going on at work, but now it seems that isn’t the case?”","Qin Yuanzheng looked at her silently. He reached out and smoothed the bangs away from her forehead.","“It has nothing to do with work,” he said quietly. “I just haven’t been sleeping well.”","Qiao Lanshu had previously assumed that something had happened in the army. After all, every time she asked Qin Yuanzheng about it, he refused to say anything.","Matters in the army often required confidentiality, so since he wouldn’t tell her, she hadn’t dared ask further.","But more than a month had passed, and Qin Yuanzheng still wasn’t sleeping well. He had been taking the traditional herbal medicine she prepared for him every day, yet it clearly wasn’t helping.","He had only just returned from the capital, and now he had woken from another nightmare in the middle of the night.","This time, Qiao Lanshu had no choice but to get to the bottom of it.","She moved closer and sat directly on Qin Yuanzheng’s thigh. He looked at her in surprise, then instinctively wrapped his arms around her.","Qiao Lanshu leaned into his embrace, draped her arms around his shoulders, and asked softly, “Brother Zheng, how long have we been married?”","Qin Yuanzheng thought for a moment. “A long time. An’an is already in high school.”","They had been married for more than a decade, yet they still got along wonderfully and had never argued.","They always kept each other in their thoughts and had never once felt that the other was lacking.","Qiao Lanshu had known from the beginning that Qin Yuanzheng was a good man, and that life with him would be comfortable and happy.","As it turned out, she had been right.","Qiao Lanshu said gently, “We’ve been married for so long. There are no secrets between us. Whenever something happens to me, I always tell you directly. But now that something is clearly bothering you, you still want to hide it from me.”","Holding Qiao Lanshu in his arms, Qin Yuanzheng silently sighed when he heard that.","He knew she was worried about him and wanted to know what had happened.","He was still hesitating when Qiao Lanshu continued, “Brother Zheng, be honest with me. Is there someone else?”","Qin Yuanzheng: “???”","Her words startled him. He hurriedly explained, “No! Of course not. How could you possibly think that?”","How could he have someone else outside?","He spent every day worrying that someone might steal his wife away. Where would he find the time or inclination to look at anyone else?","Besides, in his eyes, there were very few women out there who could compare with his wife. He already had such a young and beautiful wife—why would he be interested in anyone else?","Qin Yuanzheng had still been feeling exhausted a moment ago, but Qiao Lanshu’s words had jolted him fully awake.","He pinched her cheek, somewhat annoyed, and scolded her, “Someone else? Why would you suddenly say that? Is there someone else in your life? Do you think I’m too old and don’t want to stay with me anymore?”","Qiao Lanshu fell silent.","It seemed Qin Yuanzheng really was hung up on his age.","There was nothing he could do about it. He had married a woman much younger than himself.","He was already in his forties, while his wife was only in her thirties—the prime of her beauty and maturity.","Qin Yuanzheng stared at her and pressed, “Teacher Qiao, you tell me. Have you started thinking I’m too old?”","Qiao Lanshu pushed his hand away, climbed off him, and sat down on the other side of the bed. With complete seriousness, she said, “Well, that’s hard to say. If you refuse to tell me anything and insist on hiding everything from me, I might just discover the virtues of other men. Don’t you agree?”","Qin Yuanzheng fell silent.","His face darkened with anger.","He lunged at Qiao Lanshu and pinned her beneath him. In a low voice, he threatened, “You’d better not. Go ahead and try getting involved with another man.”","Qiao Lanshu wasn’t frightened in the slightest. She merely said, “Whether the men outside are any good depends on you, doesn’t it? What do you think, Chief Qin?”","Qin Yuanzheng fell silent again.","He truly had no way of dealing with Qiao Lanshu.","For the first time, he felt that his position at home was rather low.","His son didn’t listen to him, his daughter didn’t listen to him, and even his wife refused to listen.","What a life.","Having run out of options, Qin Yuanzheng pulled Qiao Lanshu into his arms and looked down at her. “You really want to know?”","Qiao Lanshu nodded. “What has been happening to you all this time? Did something happen?”","Qiao Lanshu didn’t believe that he was merely having nightmares.","She suspected that Qin Yuanzheng was hiding something else from her, refusing to tell her because he was afraid she would worry.","Qin Yuanzheng remained silent for a long while before finally sighing and saying quietly, “Actually, I’ve been having nightmares almost every night for more than a month now. It’s always the same nightmare.”","The elders often said that if someone had the same nightmare for several days in a row, it might be a prophecy—or perhaps something else—and that they should consult a fortune-teller or spiritual master to have it dealt with.","Qin Yuanzheng had never believed in such things before. Naturally, he had never considered anything supernatural either.","But the doctors in the capital had suggested that he go to a temple to burn incense.","So he went.","They had already paid their respects and burned incense, so why was he still having nightmares?","Qin Yuanzheng was feeling troubled.","“Nightmares? Have you really been having the same nightmare over and over for this long?” Qiao Lanshu asked worriedly.","Her expression gradually grew solemn. She sat up again and looked at Qin Yuanzheng. “What kind of nightmare is it? Tell me about it.”","Qiao Lanshu couldn’t help thinking of the period just after she had been reborn.","At that time, although she was already together with Qin Yuanzheng, she often had nightmares about her past life.","She dreamed of being locked in a cave dwelling, of Qin Yuanzheng dying from the aftereffects of his blast injuries.","In short, she had dreamed of many terrible things. But after the man who had kidnapped her died and everything came to an end, the nightmares stopped.","She had never had another one since.","The events of her past life had gradually faded from her life like smoke drifting away.","So much time had passed that she had almost forgotten those memories.","Sometimes, she even wondered whether everything that had happened in her previous life had really been nothing more than a dream.","It had been a long time since she had thought about those events.","That was why she couldn’t help growing tense when she heard Qin Yuanzheng say that he had been having the same nightmare for more than a month.","She looked at him, waiting for his answer.","Qin Yuanzheng was silent for a while before saying, “It’s nothing good, anyway. In the dream, I—I’m seriously ill, and there’s no cure. You’re heartbroken, crying every day...”","He paused, then pulled Qiao Lanshu tightly into his arms before continuing. “In the dream, I die from my illness. Not long after I die, you also...”","He couldn’t bring himself to finish.","He didn’t want to say that Qiao Lanshu died too.","It was an inauspicious thing to say, and he didn’t want to put it into words.","Qiao Lanshu’s heart trembled when she heard this.","In a low voice, she asked, “In the dream, are you the same age as you are now? Is the me in the dream in her thirties and in poor health? When you’re lying in the hospital bed, do all your internal organs hurt terribly, yet you still force yourself to endure the pain and introduce other men to me?”","Qin Yuanzheng fell silent.","He stared at her in shock. “How—how did you know?”","In the dream, his internal organs hurt terribly.","And every time he woke up, he could still feel the pain inside him. He didn’t know whether it was his liver or some other organ; all he knew was that it hurt terribly.","But he had forced himself to bear it without showing anything. He was afraid Qiao Lanshu would worry.","Yet Qiao Lanshu had just described everything that happened in his dream.","Qin Yuanzheng stared at her, too stunned to speak for a long while.","By then, tears were streaming down Qiao Lanshu’s face.","In her previous life, she had married Qin Yuanzheng when she was around thirty.","They had been married for five years and had spent those five years in happiness together.","When she was thirty-five, Qin Yuanzheng had been hospitalized after his old injuries resurfaced. He had suffered severe internal damage from the explosion, and some of his organs had been left with lasting complications.","Old injuries were prone to flaring up. Five years later, he had failed to recover.","Qin Yuanzheng had left her forever when Qiao Lanshu was thirty-five.","Only now did Qiao Lanshu remember that, in her previous life, this was around the time when she and Qin Yuanzheng should already have been dead.","She was exactly thirty-five now, and Qin Yuanzheng was already forty-six.","They were no longer young.","But in this life, they were destined to live happier and longer together than they had in the past.","Qiao Lanshu suddenly threw her arms around Qin Yuanzheng and began to cry silently. She cried so hard that she couldn’t speak for a long time.","Qin Yuanzheng was deeply shaken as well. He didn’t know what had happened to Qiao Lanshu, but he knew there had to be more to this than met the eye.","A strange sadness also welled up inside him. He held her tightly and told her what he had been going through these past few weeks.","“Every time I woke up from the nightmare, all my internal organs would cramp with pain. It was awful, but I was afraid you’d worry, so I didn’t dare tell you. More than half a month ago, I secretly went to see a doctor. After hearing me describe my symptoms, the doctor said I might have a serious illness.”","The moment Qiao Lanshu heard this, she jerked her head up and stared at him. Her tears flowed even faster.","Qin Yuanzheng quickly took his clothes and wiped her tears as he said, “See? This is exactly why I didn’t want to tell you. I was afraid you’d cry once you found out. Don’t worry. It’s all over now. I went to Beijing this time to get examined at a hospital there. The results are already out. I’m fine—the doctor said I’m in excellent health.”","Qiao Lanshu had been so frightened that she could barely think. Hearing this, she finally let out a sigh of relief.","After calming herself down, she choked out, “Where—where’s your medical report? Let me see it.”","Although she wasn’t a doctor and might not understand the reports, she was afraid Qin Yuanzheng was merely saying this to comfort her. She had to see the results herself before she could truly relax.","Qin Yuanzheng reassured her, “I left the reports in the car and haven’t brought them inside yet. If you want to see them, should I go get them now?”","Qin Yuanzheng usually parked his car just outside the courtyard gate. It wouldn’t take long to go out and get them.","Qiao Lanshu looked at him hopefully.","Under her gaze, Qin Yuanzheng could only give in. “All right, all right. Stop crying. I’ll go get them now.”","Qiao Lanshu wiped her tears and immediately climbed out of bed with him. “I’m coming with you.”","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless.","He said helplessly, “The night wind is cold, and the car’s right outside. I’ll bring them back for you. Stay here and wait for me, all right?”","Qiao Lanshu ignored him. She had already put on her shoes and gone outside.","Qin Yuanzheng had no choice but to hurry after her.","When they stepped out of the room, Qiao Lanshu sniffed and reminded him in a hushed voice, “Keep your voice down. Don’t wake the children.”","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. He picked up a flashlight and quietly crossed the courtyard. After opening the gate, the couple walked over to the car outside.","Qin Yuanzheng had tossed the medical reports into the car earlier without giving them much thought.","He hadn’t brought them into the house because he had originally intended to keep them from Qiao Lanshu and the children.","But since Qiao Lanshu wanted to see them, he might as well let her. He was perfectly healthy, after all, and seeing the reports would help put her mind at ease.","In those days, medical reports were still handwritten by doctors. The handwriting on them wasn’t particularly difficult to read.","As soon as Qiao Lanshu got the reports, she hurried back inside and bent over them beneath the lamp.","There were two pages in total, one of them a CT report.","Qiao Lanshu examined them carefully for more than ten minutes before finally setting them down. Her expression had relaxed somewhat.","Qin Yuanzheng said quietly, “See? I told you I’m fine. You really don’t need to worry.”"]},{"number":288,"title":"Chapter 288: Vows","paragraphs":["The results on Qin Yuanzheng’s medical report showed that there was indeed nothing wrong with him.","And yet, he was still having nightmares about his past life, which Qiao Lanshu found difficult to understand.","Qiao Lanshu set down the report, which she had read carefully several times, and sat by the bed, lost in thought.","Looking at her, Qin Yuanzheng asked in a low voice, “You still haven’t told me how you knew what I dreamed about. Could it be that you’ve been having the same nightmares too?”","At the thought, Qin Yuanzheng immediately broke out in a cold sweat.","It was one thing for him to have nightmares continuously for over a month, but if Qiao Lanshu was having the same nightmares, then...","Qin Yuanzheng grew nervous, even feeling the hairs on his body stand on end.","It really was frightening.","He leaned closer and looked at Qiao Lanshu’s face. In a low voice, he asked, “When did you start having these nightmares?”","Qiao Lanshu was silent for a while as she organized her thoughts. Only then did she say, “This dream is actually very long, and incredibly real. In it, there’s another life that belongs to the two of us. It’s a long story. Do you want to hear it?”","Qin Yuanzheng nodded and held her as they lay down on the bed. Neither of them was in the mood to sleep anymore, so Qiao Lanshu carefully began telling him about her past life.","In a low voice, Qiao Lanshu said, “If this really is a dream, then I had it much, much earlier than you. I was eighteen, on a train from Yangcheng to Longcheng...”","If only it really was a dream.","That was what Qiao Lanshu was thinking.","If everything from her past life had merely been an unusually realistic dream, then none of it had actually happened. Just thinking about that made her feel incredibly happy.","She told Qin Yuanzheng about the events of her past life as if they had been nothing more than a dream.","Naturally, she had much more to tell him than he did.","Qin Yuanzheng had only dreamed about the moment of his death.","Qiao Lanshu, however, had experienced everything from the moment she arrived in Longcheng—being abandoned by her fiancé, being kidnapped, eventually staying in Longcheng to work, and later meeting Qin Yuanzheng through an introduction.","In their previous lives, they had ultimately met and fallen in love, but by the time they met, both of them were already covered in wounds.","After listening to everything, Qin Yuanzheng’s eyes reddened, and he silently held Qiao Lanshu tighter.","Only then did Qin Yuanzheng remember that during the early days of their marriage, Qiao Lanshu would often tell him that she had been having nightmares.","At the time, he had felt sorry for her. But after hearing what she had just told him, he could not help beginning to believe in past and present lives.","The two of them held each other in silence for a long time. They did not sleep all night. Only when the morning light illuminated the windows did Qin Yuanzheng realize that dawn had already broken.","Qiao Lanshu, however, had fallen asleep at some point.","She had never stayed up all night before, and was completely exhausted.","Qin Yuanzheng did not wake her. He slept for a short while, then got up to pack.","He planned to take Qiao Lanshu to Mount Wutai to burn incense and pray.","Mount Wutai was not close, and they might have to stay there for one night, so they would need to request leave.","As for whether they should bring the children, the answer was obviously no. The children still had school to attend.","Han Ye had only just returned and was still recovering in the hospital. Ordinarily, Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu should not have left home at a time like this.","But Qin Yuanzheng felt that this matter could not wait.","Although he did not know what had caused him and Qiao Lanshu to share such a past life, it had to be because of some extraordinary bond that Heaven had given them the chance to live their lives over again.","So he wanted to take Qiao Lanshu to a temple to burn incense and fulfill their vow.","Since Qiao Lanshu had not slept the night before, she woke up later than usual. By then, both children had already gone to school, and she was almost late herself.","She hurriedly got out of bed, changed clothes, washed up, and rushed out of the room.","Just as she came out, she saw Qin Yuanzheng organizing a backpack. She froze for a moment and asked, “Why are you packing? Do you have a sudden assignment?”","The two of them had just discussed their past lives the night before, and Qiao Lanshu was feeling complicated emotions. She had actually wanted to spend more time with Qin Yuanzheng and talk with him.","She had not expected him to be leaving again so soon.","Qin Yuanzheng did not have much to pack for himself. Most of what he put in the bag was for Qiao Lanshu.","Although they only planned to spend one night away, Qiao Lanshu liked to keep clean, so he packed her a change of clothes and socks, along with toiletries, dry food, water, and other necessities.","As he packed, Qin Yuanzheng said, “I want to take you to Mount Wutai. Are you busy with work lately? Can you take some time off?”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","She was taken aback. “Huh? So suddenly?”","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. “Go to the school this morning and ask for leave. I’ll wait for you at home.”","Qin Yuanzheng still had many days of annual leave unused, and work had not been particularly busy lately, so it would be easy for him to take time off.","He was only worried that Qiao Lanshu’s work at the school might be too demanding for her to get leave easily.","After all, Qiao Lanshu was now a team leader, and she had quite a heavy workload.","Qiao Lanshu thought it over, then nodded without much hesitation. “All right. I’ll go to the school now and ask for leave. We’ll set out after lunch.”","The only children they had were Qin Qiao’an and Qin Qiaoxia. They were no longer little kids—one was in high school and the other in middle school—and they could get to and from school on their own and even cook for themselves.","Qiao Lanshu was quite confident in their ability to take care of themselves.","So, after the couple arranged matters at work and settled things with the children, they drove off toward Mount Wutai.","It took Qin Yuanzheng about six hours to drive there. They stopped along the way for half an hour to rest.","By the time they reached the area around Mount Wutai, it was already dark. They found a nearby hotel and spent the night there. Early the next morning, the couple climbed the mountain to offer incense at the temple.","They burned incense, worshiped Buddha, donated money for incense, and ate vegetarian meals. The couple spent the entire day at Mount Wutai.","Before leaving, Qiao Lanshu even went to request a protective talisman for Qin Yuanzheng.","Everything went smoothly and peacefully.","As they came down from the mountain, Qiao Lanshu looked back at the magnificent peaks and asked Qin Yuanzheng, “Is that all? Are we just going home now?”","Qin Yuanzheng was not entirely sure either. “If not, should we visit some other temples and burn more incense?”","Qiao Lanshu thought for a moment, then placed the protective talisman they had obtained into Qin Yuanzheng’s pocket. “That should be enough. Let’s go home.”","Qin Yuanzheng held Qiao Lanshu’s hand, and the two of them slowly made their way out of the mountains. Then they began the six-hour drive home.","Qin Yuanzheng had always believed that he and Qiao Lanshu were destined to be together.","If not for fate, how could a woman from Yangcheng and a man more than two thousand kilometers away ever have ended up together?","But he did not know that in their previous life, the bond between him and Qiao Lanshu had already run its course.","He had originally been destined to have no children.","Yet it was precisely because he had repeatedly risked his life, carried out countless missions, and saved countless people from danger that he accumulated immense blessings. Those blessings had given him the happy and complete life he had now.","On the way back, Qin Yuanzheng slipped the protective talisman Qiao Lanshu had obtained for him back into her pocket.","He said to Qiao Lanshu, “It’s enough for the Buddha to protect you. As long as you’re safe, I’ll be fine too.”","Qiao Lanshu was his entire world. As long as she was well, nothing else mattered.","—End of Main Story—","Next will be several extra chapters about the children, focusing on their romantic futures. I may write another twenty or thirty thousand words. Thank you, dears, for making it this far. I’m truly grateful."]},{"number":289,"title":"Chapter 289: Extra Story 1: Han Ye & Xia Xia","paragraphs":["Qin Qiaoxia had been accepted to a university in the capital. At seventeen or eighteen, she was about to leave her hometown to pursue her studies, and both Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng were deeply worried.","Qiao Lanshu had originally wanted Qin Qiaoxia to attend her alma mater and simply go to university in Wencheng.","But Qin Qiaoxia said she wanted to see the world beyond her hometown. She had spent more than a decade in Wencheng, from childhood to the present, and didn’t want her entire future—university, work, and even marriage—to take place there.","Because of this, Qiao Lanshu sighed to Qin Yuanzheng, “I suppose the more obedient children are when they’re little, the more rebellious they become when they grow up. Look at her—these days, Xiaxia doesn’t listen to a word we say.”","Qin Yuanzheng felt somewhat melancholy as well. Qin Qiao’an was already serving in the military, and after joining the army, he rarely had the chance to return home. It was perfectly normal for them not to see him for two or three years.","And now even Xiaxia was leaving home to attend university. After all these years of marriage, the two of them had worked so hard to raise their children. In the past, they had often found the kids troublesome.","But now that neither child was by their side, they couldn’t help feeling a little sad.","Qin Yuanzheng comforted Qiao Lanshu in a low voice. “Children have to leave home once they grow up. We can’t keep her by our side forever.”","Qiao Lanshu was simply overwhelmed with emotion.","In the blink of an eye, even Xiaxia was off to university.","Qin Yuanzheng consoled her again. “Isn’t Han Ye in the capital? He can go check on Xiaxia from time to time. There won’t be any problem.”","Han Ye had served for more than two years before returning to take the national college entrance examination. He was successfully admitted to the Army Armored Forces Academy. That year, the school had only two admission slots in Wencheng.","The competition had been fierce, but Han Ye had made it.","Zhou Dingwen hadn’t been admitted. He had gotten into the Army Engineering University in the south, which meant he, too, had been away from home for a long time.","After graduating, Han Ye was assigned to an army unit in the capital. Since Xiaxia was going to university there as well, the siblings would be able to look after each other.","Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu personally escorted Xiaxia to the university and took a look around her dormitory.","Before leaving, Qiao Lanshu held Xiaxia’s hand and gave her a long list of instructions. “Other than attending class and studying, try not to go out at night, all right? Society is chaotic these days. There are so many human traffickers and scammers. A young, pretty girl like you is the easiest kind of person for them to target.”","Xiaxia was already eighteen. Qiao Lanshu had married Qin Yuanzheng when she herself was eighteen.","So, looking at Xiaxia now, Qiao Lanshu was filled with emotion.","She never would have imagined that her daughter with Qin Yuanzheng would already be eighteen—and a student at one of the country’s top universities at that.","Xiaxia was half a head taller than Qiao Lanshu, but she looked very much like her mother had in her youth. She had fair skin, large eyes, a cherry-red mouth, and an oval face with dimples that appeared whenever she smiled.","With such a beautiful daughter studying so far from home, Qiao Lanshu was practically worried sick.","She even felt that she was becoming more and more long-winded. “Your father and I aren’t here with you, so you have to get along well with your classmates. If anything happens, call home or find your big brother. Have you memorized all the phone numbers?”","Xiaxia nodded obediently. “I’ve memorized them all. They’re written in my address book, and I remember them too. I even know Brother Ye’s unit number by heart.”","Han Ye was stationed with an army unit in the capital, and although he was still young, he had already become a company commander.","However, the unit was quite far from Qin Qiaoxia’s university. It would probably take more than an hour to drive there, and Han Ye was busy with his work in the army. He couldn’t just leave whenever he wanted.","He hadn’t come today because the unit was holding a training exercise and he couldn’t get away.","Qiao Lanshu nodded. “When you’re away from home, don’t believe everything people tell you. Don’t casually go anywhere with strangers, and never accept things from them. Do you understand?”","Qin Qiaoxia was at a loss for words. She took Qiao Lanshu’s arm and said, “Mom, I know all that. You don’t have to keep repeating yourself.”","Qiao Lanshu had indeed been unusually talkative that day, going over the same warnings again and again until Xiaxia was almost helpless.","After Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng left, Qin Qiaoxia went to familiarize herself with the campus.","Being able to leave home and attend university in another city felt quite novel to her. This was the first time since growing up that she had truly left home and traveled somewhere far away. She was both excited and full of anticipation.","Han Ye had known for a long time that Xiaxia would be attending university there, and he was eager to see his little sister. After all, he was now the one his younger siblings could rely on.","When Qin Qiao’an had been serving in the army, Han Ye had even gone through all sorts of channels to call Qin Qiao’an’s company commander, asking him to take extra care of his little brother.","Qiao Lanshu probably never imagined that the words she had once used to encourage Han Ye would be taken so seriously.","Every few days, he called Qin Qiao’an’s company commander to ask about him. In the end, because he kept pulling strings, Han Ye was given a stern reprimand by his battalion commander.","At the same time, Qin Qiao’an’s battalion commander, unable to bear it any longer, gave Han Ye a thorough tongue-lashing over the phone.","But Han Ye had thick skin and didn’t take any of it to heart.","He continued asking about his little brother from time to time. Eventually, Qin Qiao’an’s battalion commander even called Qin Yuanzheng to complain.","Qin Yuanzheng still got a headache whenever he thought about it. Later, he had Qin Qiao’an transferred to another military district without telling Han Ye.","There were army units all over the country. Han Ye couldn’t call every single one of them to ask where Qin Qiao’an was, and the military had its own rules and discipline. Because of that, Han Ye finally quieted down somewhat over the past year.","But the fact that Qin Qiao’an had not only a general for a father but also a brother-protective maniac for an elder brother had already spread throughout the army.","Qin Qiao’an was under a great deal of pressure as well. If he failed to get into a military academy—or if he backed down when faced with difficulties or performed poorly—wouldn’t that bring shame upon his father and elder brother?","In any case, it had indirectly pushed him to work even harder.","But those were matters for another time.","As for Han Ye, after spending more than half a month in a training exercise with his unit, he was finally able to leave.","The first thing he did was drive to Xiaxia’s university to see her.","Han Ye was six years older than Xiaxia and was already in his mid-twenties. Aside from being more mature and steady, his domineering personality hadn’t changed much.","Xiaxia had already received a call from him, so as soon as class ended at noon, she went to wait for him at the university’s east gate.","Han Ye was wearing a dark green T-shirt. His hair had been shaved down to a short layer of stubble, and his skin was deeply tanned. He was tall and broad-shouldered, with an imposing presence that increasingly resembled Qin Yuanzheng’s.","Both men carried the same intimidating air that came from spending years training and leading soldiers in the army.","Xiaxia came out with her two roommates. When the girls saw Han Ye from a distance, they both silently took two steps back.","Confused, Xiaxia looked at them. “What’s wrong? Are you leaving already?”","One of her roommates lowered her voice. “Qiao Xia, is that really your brother?”","Xiaxia nodded. “Yes.”","The other roommate said, “Then why doesn’t he look anything like you? You’re so pretty, but he looks so fierce.”","Qin Qiaoxia glanced at Han Ye. She didn’t think he looked fierce at all.","Perhaps it had something to do with the fact that she had grown up in a military compound. All the adults around her had been officers, and they carried themselves much like Han Ye.","Han Ye strode over to Xiaxia and, looking down, gave her a once-over. As usual, he reached out to tug on her braids and said with a grin, “Why are you just standing there like an idiot? Aren’t you going to say hello?”","Xiaxia pulled her braids back and greeted him. “Brother Ye.”","Han Ye nodded. “All right, let’s go. I’ll take you out to eat.”","Xiaxia hurriedly introduced her roommates. “Brother Ye, these are my roommates. This is Mei Xiaofang, and this is Liu Wenli.”","Han Ye stopped and finally followed Xiaxia’s gaze to the two girls behind her.","He had only noticed Xiaxia just now and hadn’t realized there were two other people standing behind her.","Since Xiaxia had introduced them, he nodded a greeting to the two girls. Both of them shyly stole glances at him.","Han Ye didn’t say much more and soon took Xiaxia out to eat.","On the way, he asked her, “You’ve been at school for a few days now. Haven’t you gone out to look around?”","Xiaxia shook her head. “No. Mom won’t let me go out. She says it’s dangerous outside.”","At that, Han Ye’s expression turned serious, and he nodded. “Our mom is right. You’re a young girl, so you’d better not wander around for no reason. Especially at night—there really are quite a few human traffickers around.”","“You know me. I’m usually too lazy to leave the house anyway.”","She was a homebody. Normally, she preferred to curl up at home, and now she mostly stayed in her dorm room as well. She didn’t particularly like going out.","Han Ye took her around the streets near the school, helping her familiarize herself with the area. He even deliberately took her to the nearby police station and told her, “See that? That’s the police station. If anything happens, come straight here.”","Qin Qiaoxia: “...”","After that, Han Ye took her to a restaurant.","While they were eating, Han Ye asked about the two girls he had seen earlier. “They’re both your roommates? You get along pretty well?”","Xiaxia nodded. “We get along all right. We’ve only known each other for a few days.”","As she spoke, Xiaxia suddenly gave Han Ye a meaningful look. “Brother Ye, why are you suddenly asking about them?”","After a pause, she tentatively asked, “Do you think they’re pretty?”","Han Ye was eating a meat bun. “What does pretty or not pretty have to do with anything? They...”","With the bun still in his mouth, he thought for a moment, then asked, “What did they look like again?”","Qin Qiaoxia: “...”","Qin Qiaoxia was speechless. After a few seconds, she placed a bun in Han Ye’s bowl and said, “Never mind. Just eat your buns. Eat plenty.”","Han Ye put a chicken leg in her bowl. “You eat too. Come on.”","Qin Qiaoxia picked up the chicken leg and took a bite, sighing silently to herself.","She had little appetite, so she stopped eating after only a little.","Once Han Ye saw that she was finished, he began devouring the rest of the food like a whirlwind.","When he was nearly done, he noticed that the chicken leg in Xiaxia’s bowl was still there, so he very naturally picked it up and started eating it too.","His movement startled Qin Qiaoxia, and she quickly said, “I—I already ate from that.”","Han Ye bit into it. Hearing what she said, he held the chicken leg back out toward her and asked, “Do you still want it? I thought you were done.”","Qin Qiaoxia: “...”","She silently shook her head. “I don’t want it anymore.”","Han Ye nodded. “Good. Don’t waste food.”","Then he took a few bites and finished the chicken leg Xiaxia had left behind.","Xiaxia really wanted to point out that it was her leftovers, and that her saliva was still on it. Han Ye truly didn’t seem to mind at all.","After dinner, Han Ye walked her back to school. He only had one day off and still had to return to his unit.","He told Xiaxia, “I’ll come see you again next week. Zhou Dingwen is coming next week too, so I’ll bring him along and make him treat the two of us to dinner.”","It had also been a long time since she had seen Zhou Dingwen.","He was coming this way on a mission and planned to visit Han Ye while he was here. Since Xiaxia happened to be studying nearby, the three of them could get together.","Before leaving, Han Ye took two hundred yuan from his pocket and handed it to Qin Qiaoxia. “If you don’t have enough living expenses, come to me. Don’t ask our mom. Your brother has plenty of money.”","Then he added, “I’ll support you from now on.”","He meant that he would cover Xiaxia’s living expenses and tuition in the future, but his words sounded entirely different to Xiaxia.","She really didn’t know what to say about Han Ye.","Forget it. Why should she argue with this clueless blockhead?","...","By the time Han Ye returned to the barracks dormitory, everyone there already knew he had gone to visit his younger sister that day.","The moment he came back, they all crowded around him and began teasing him. “Company Commander, where’s your sister? Why didn’t you bring her back for us to see?”","Han Ye took off his clothes as he replied, “Get lost. Why would I bring my sister here for you to look at?”","Someone else said, “Company Commander, isn’t your sister our sister too? What’s wrong with letting us see her?”","Han Ye kicked him. “My sister is mine. What business is it of yours?”","Another person asked, “Company Commander, is our sister pretty? Do you have any photos?”","Han Ye was finally at the end of his patience. He glared angrily at the teammates surrounding him. “Are you all so idle that you have nothing better to do? I’m warning you—stop asking about my sister. No matter how pretty she is, she has nothing to do with any of you.”","Someone muttered, “Why are you being so fierce, Company Commander? Anyone who didn’t know better would think she was your wife, not your sister. Last time, I even showed you my family photo. I’ve got two younger sisters, and I don’t act like this.”","Han Ye: “...”"]},{"number":290,"title":"Chapter 290: Bonus Episode 2: Han Ye & Xia Xia","paragraphs":["After parting ways with Han Ye, Qin Qiaoxia returned to her dormitory.","The dorm was a four-person room, shared by her and three other girls. Two of her roommates were the same classmates who had seen Han Ye with her at the school gate.","When Liu Wenli saw her come back, she immediately went over and asked, “Qiao Xia, you’re back so early?”","Qin Qiaoxia nodded. “It’s already getting dark. He told me to come back early.”","Han Ye had probably been taking care of Qin Qiao’an, his little brother, since childhood. Then, after moving to Wencheng for middle school, he not only had Qin Qiao’an to look after, but also gained a little Xiaxia.","So although Han Ye had been an only child, he had worried like a mother hen ever since he was young.","That had made him more steady and mature. Whenever he dealt with his younger siblings, he sometimes seemed to channel Qiao Lanshu, declaring that this was not allowed and that was not allowed.","He had been quite happy to see Xiaxia today, but before the sun had even set, he had hurriedly insisted on taking her back to school, saying that it was getting dark and girls shouldn’t stay outside. He told her to hurry back to the dormitory and stay there.","Thinking of that, Xiaxia found it rather amusing.","When Liu Wenli heard this, she said enviously, “That’s so nice, Xiaxia. I’m really jealous that you have such a wonderful big brother.”","Xiaxia thought to herself that she actually had two such wonderful brothers. Qin Qiao’an was very good to her too.","But she didn’t say that. Although she and Liu Wenli had gotten along fairly well over the past few days, they weren’t close enough yet to exchange their entire family histories.","Liu Wenli was also a northern girl, with a straightforward personality. She didn’t bother beating around the bush. Instead, she hugged Xiaxia’s arm and asked with a grin, “Qiao Xia, does your brother have a girlfriend?”","Xiaxia: “...”","Xiaxia stared at her in surprise. “Wenli, you...”","Liu Wenli smiled shyly and leaned close to her ear. “I think your brother is great. He’s exactly my type. I heard he’s serving in the military—is that true? He’s so attractive. I really like men like him.”","Then Liu Wenli continued, “What do you think of me? If he’s single, do you think he’d like someone like me?”","Liu Wenli was tall and slender, with delicate features and a frank, outspoken personality. She was the kind of person most people found easy to like.","Qin Qiaoxia, on the other hand, was more reserved and quiet, so she particularly liked Liu Wenli’s outgoing, straightforward nature.","Now, hearing what Liu Wenli had said, she fell silent for a moment.","To be honest, Han Ye treated her very well—but it was the kind of affection an older brother had for his younger sister. She could feel that clearly.","Han Ye was six years older than her and was twenty-four this year. Yet she had never heard of him having a girlfriend.","He hadn’t dated anyone while attending military college.","Now that he spent every day at his unit, there was even less chance of hearing about him dating anyone.","Still, he was a company commander, and apparently some of his superiors had tried to introduce him to women. As far as she knew, none of those arrangements had worked out.","Liu Wenli grabbed Xiaxia by the shoulders and shook her. “Oh, Qin Qiaoxia, say something! I’m dying of curiosity over here!”","Qin Qiaoxia scratched her head and hesitated before saying, “I think he’s probably single right now.”","Liu Wenli asked doubtfully, “Probably? Doesn’t he tell his family anything?”","Qin Qiaoxia explained, “He isn’t my biological brother. Um... how should I put this? You can think of him as my mother’s godson. I don’t actually know all that much about his situation, but judging from the way he acts, I think he’s single.”","Han Ye was such a clueless, utterly straight-laced man that even if a girl liked him, he probably wouldn’t notice.","After hearing Qin Qiaoxia’s explanation, Liu Wenli suddenly understood. “I knew it! You two don’t look alike at all. You definitely don’t look like real siblings.”","But Liu Wenli remained determined. She really liked Han Ye, and there weren’t many men with his bearing and presence.","She said, “Could you ask him for me? He saw me today, didn’t he? Ask him whether he likes my type. If he doesn’t, that’s fine. I just want to know. Maybe he does like someone like me, right?”","Liu Wenli had only seen Han Ye once, but she had immediately felt that not only was he handsome, his imposing presence was also incredibly attractive.","So she wanted to give it a shot.","After all, she was a university student from a prestigious school, and her own qualifications weren’t bad either.","She added, “It’s okay if it doesn’t work out. I just want to ask. If I don’t, I’ll never be satisfied.”","Hearing this, Qin Qiaoxia smiled and nodded. “All right. I’ll ask him the next time my brother comes.”","After thinking for a moment, she added, “Actually, forget that. Next time, I can take you to meet him yourself.”","Liu Wenli immediately brightened. “Then it’s a promise! To thank you, I’ll treat you to lunch tomorrow.”","Their relationship grew much closer in an instant. Liu Wenli was open and carefree, and she pulled Qin Qiaoxia along as they chatted. Most of the conversation, naturally, was about Han Ye.","Han Ye had no idea that after meeting her only once, one of Xiaxia’s classmates had already taken a liking to him.","But his fellow soldiers had been clamoring to see a picture of his little sister, which had left him annoyed for quite some time.","He had originally planned to take Qin Qiaoxia around his military base.","Now, that was out of the question. He decided Xiaxia couldn’t come to the base after all. There were too many men there—and men, after all, were no good.","...","About ten days after Qin Qiaoxia began university, someone came to see her again.","This time, the visitor didn’t have her phone number. Instead, he registered at the guard station by the university gate and asked someone to locate Xiaxia for him.","When Xiaxia arrived at the guard station, she saw Zhou Dingwen waiting there. He was dressed in civilian clothes and wearing glasses.","Qin Qiaoxia had heard Han Ye mention that Zhou Dingwen intended to visit her.","She hadn’t expected him to come so soon.","Several years had passed since they’d last seen each other, and Zhou Dingwen had changed considerably. He was studying engineering, and his entire demeanor was different from before.","He looked more refined and scholarly now.","Zhou Dingwen pushed his glasses up the bridge of his nose and looked Xiaxia up and down a few times before smiling. “Xiaxia, it’s been several years. You’re a university student now.”","Qin Qiaoxia felt a little embarrassed. “Brother Dingwen, when did you arrive?”","Carrying a bag, Zhou Dingwen followed Qin Qiaoxia out of the guard station. “I just got here. I heard you were studying here, so I thought I’d come see you first.”","All Qin Qiaoxia could say was, “Thank you for coming to see me, Brother Dingwen.”","After that came an awkward silence.","Qin Qiaoxia didn’t know what to say to Zhou Dingwen.","She more or less understood what he meant, but she didn’t know how to respond.","After all, she and Zhou Dingwen had grown up together. She had always thought of him as the older boy next door and had never felt anything more.","Zhou Dingwen, however, was very considerate and maintained a proper distance from her. He had even brought her a gift.","Over the past few years, Zhou Dingwen had been living in the south and rarely returned to Wencheng, so they hadn’t even seen each other during the New Year holidays.","This time, he had come to the capital and visited her at the first opportunity.","She had to admit that Xiaxia was touched.","Zhou Dingwen took a box of pastries from his bag and handed it to Xiaxia. “I heard these pastries are pretty good. There are several flavors in the box, and women seem to like them, so I bought one for you. Take it home and try them.”","Xiaxia had loved sweets ever since she was little, so she was quite happy to see the box of pastries.","She didn’t stand on ceremony with Zhou Dingwen. Taking the box from him, she said, “Thank you, Brother Dingwen.”","After a brief pause, she asked, “By the way, Brother Dingwen, did you pass through Wencheng on your way back this time?”","Zhou Dingwen shook his head. “No. But once I finish this assignment, I’ll have one day off. I’ll go home for a visit then.”","This mission had not originally been assigned to him. He had not been home in several years, and since the route would take him through Wencheng, he had requested the assignment from his superiors.","He really had been missing home. Of course, he also wanted to come and see Qin Qiaoxia.","After all, he had heard that Xiaxia was now in college and had already turned eighteen. Many people started dating once they went to college. What if Xiaxia had already found someone? Wouldn’t he miss his chance then?","Qin Qiaoxia asked him again, “Brother Ye told me before that you would go see him this time. Are you heading to the military base now?”","After arriving, Zhou Dingwen had gone straight to see Xiaxia. He had not yet visited Han Ye.","So he hesitated for a moment before saying, “Xiaxia, we haven’t seen each other in so many years. I came all this way especially to see you, and you’re not even going to treat me to a meal?”","Qin Qiaoxia felt a little embarrassed and hurriedly said, “Oh, right! Brother Dingwen, let’s go eat first.”","Fortunately, Han Ye had taken her around the area before, so she knew her way around now.","She led Zhou Dingwen to the restaurant they had visited last time, and the two of them had a meal together.","Zhou Dingwen kept looking as though he wanted to say something, but in the end, he still couldn’t bring himself to say it.","After they finished eating, Zhou Dingwen felt too embarrassed to stay any longer, so he went to find Han Ye first.","They agreed that a few days later, he would come back with Han Ye to see Xiaxia.","......","On the day they had arranged to meet, Qin Qiaoxia remembered what her roommate Liu Wenli had said before and brought her along.","That day, the four young people met beside the lake.","Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen came together, while Qin Qiaoxia brought Liu Wenli.","Han Ye had met Liu Wenli once before and knew she was Qin Qiaoxia’s classmate, so he greeted her warmly. “Hello. We meet again.”","Liu Wenli nodded somewhat shyly, then took the initiative to strike up a conversation with him. “Big Brother Han, are you usually busy at the military base?”","Han Ye nodded. “Of course I am.”","As he spoke, he asked Qin Qiaoxia, “Xia’er, do you want to go boating? There are boats over there.”","The lake in the park was very large, and since it was the weekend, many young people were out rowing on it.","Zhou Dingwen glanced at the lake and suddenly said, “They’re all small boats meant for two people. Xiaxia, do you know how to row? Would you like me to take you?”","As he spoke, Zhou Dingwen glanced at Liu Wenli, who was standing beside Han Ye.","Qin Qiaoxia also looked at Liu Wenli and Han Ye. Liu Wenli had been winking at her repeatedly.","Qin Qiaoxia knew that Liu Wenli wanted to spend some time alone with Han Ye. She must have something she wanted to say to him.","So, before Han Ye could say anything, Qin Qiaoxia nodded and said, “Then let’s go boating, Brother Dingwen.”","The moment he heard her agree, Zhou Dingwen’s eyes lit up, and he immediately brightened.","He had finished his assignment over the past few days and was preparing to leave by train.","Before leaving, he really wanted to say a few things to Qin Qiaoxia. No matter what happened, he had to tell Xiaxia how he felt. Otherwise, wouldn’t this trip have been for nothing?","So Zhou Dingwen quickly said, “All right, let’s go. I’ll take you rowing. Let me tell you, I’m a real expert. I practiced rowing in the army.”","Watching the two of them leave, Han Ye quickly called out, “Hey, you two—wait, Zhou Dingwen, be careful! Don’t row toward the middle of the lake. The water’s deep there. It’s dangerous!”"]},{"number":291,"title":"Chapter 291: Extra Story 3: Han Ye & Xia Xia","paragraphs":["Han Ye had practically turned into a nag. Walking beside Xiaxia, he kept reminding her, “Just row around near the shore. The water in the middle of the lake is over two meters deep, and you can’t swim. How dangerous would that be?”","Qin Qiaoxia turned to glance at Liu Wenli, who was looking at Han Ye with a somewhat surprised expression.","She probably hadn’t expected that a soldier who looked so cool and tough could be this long-winded—almost as nagging as her own mother.","Qin Qiaoxia nodded and said perfunctorily, “I know, I know. You be careful too.”","Standing on the shore, Han Ye muttered, “What do I have to be careful about? I’m not the one rowing. Besides, I can swim.”","As soon as he said that, he suddenly realized something. He called out to Zhou Dingwen, “Hey, Zhou Dingwen, get off the boat. Get off.”","Zhou Dingwen was already seated in the boat. He had finally gotten the chance to be alone with Xiaxia and row her around, and he was thrilled about it.","Naturally, he didn’t want to get off.","He looked up at Han Ye and asked, “What now? Is there something else?”","Then Zhou Dingwen added, “Don’t worry. I’ll be careful. Don’t you trust me?”","Han Ye frowned. “No, get off. I’ll row Xiaxia around.”","Zhou Dingwen: “...”","Zhou Dingwen was completely speechless. He waved his hand, picked up the oars, and began rowing.","From the shore, Han Ye continued shouting, “No, I mean, I should be the one rowing Xiaxia around. What are you trying to pull?”","Qin Qiaoxia said to Han Ye, “All right, Brother Ye. Keep Liu Wenli company for a while. We’ll be back soon.”","Han Ye: “...”","Qin Qiaoxia added, “If you want to row, you can row with Wenli.”","Han Ye: “...”","Speechless, Han Ye said, “You’re my sister. Of course I...”","Forget it.","Han Ye was at a loss for words.","He stood on the shore, watching Zhou Dingwen row with a broad smile while chatting with Qin Qiaoxia. Something about it rubbed him the wrong way.","For some reason, at that moment, he found Zhou Dingwen’s smile rather irritating.","How strange. It had been many years since he’d found Zhou Dingwen annoying.","But now, looking at him, that childhood aversion had resurfaced.","Seeing Han Ye standing on the shore and staring intently at Zhou Dingwen and Qin Qiaoxia’s boat, Liu Wenli smiled and said, “You don’t have to worry so much. They’re only rowing. They probably won’t fall into the water.”","Only then did Han Ye turn to look at her. “My sister can’t swim, so they still need to be careful.”","As he spoke, he quickly turned his attention back to Zhou Dingwen and Qin Qiaoxia.","Whether he was truly worried that they might fall into the water, or worried about something else, he couldn’t quite figure it out himself.","Liu Wenli stood beside him on the shore. There were many willow trees planted along the bank, their branches swaying in the breeze. With the beautiful lake stretching out before them, the scenery was truly lovely.","Although Liu Wenli was straightforward by nature, she was still somewhat nervous at the moment. Han Ye was focused entirely on Zhou Dingwen’s boat and didn’t seem inclined to speak with her.","So Liu Wenli had no choice but to find a topic herself.","She asked, “Big Brother Han, do you usually get much time off?”","“Not much. We’re usually pretty busy.”","Han Ye had only taken time off recently because Qin Qiaoxia had come to town for school.","Normally, if there was nothing special going on, he stayed at the base practically every day.","Liu Wenli asked again, “Are there many female soldiers in your unit?”","Han Ye turned to look at her, curious about why she would ask such a question.","“Not many.”","And that was it.","He was practically a man of few words.","Just moments ago, he had been quite talkative while speaking with Zhou Dingwen and Qin Qiaoxia.","But now, he barely said anything.","After trying several times to start a conversation, Liu Wenli understood.","Han Ye simply didn’t want to talk to her.","In other words, he wasn’t interested in her.","Liu Wenli was a clever girl, and she understood that immediately.","She felt a little disappointed. What a pity. It was so rare to meet such an outstanding man.","But Han Ye seemed as though he wasn’t interested in women at all.","After observing the two of them for a while, Liu Wenli discovered that Han Ye was actually quite concerned about Zhou Dingwen...","She decided not to make a nuisance of herself. Finding a stone, she sat down and waited for Qin Qiaoxia to return.","Meanwhile, Qin Qiaoxia was sitting in the boat and occasionally glancing toward Liu Wenli and Han Ye as well.","She had assumed that someone as talkative as Han Ye would have plenty to say to Liu Wenli. Instead, she discovered that the two of them had barely spoken.","Qin Qiaoxia was puzzled. Big Brother Han didn’t usually seem so aloof.","Zhou Dingwen rowed slowly. Looking at Qin Qiaoxia, he said with a smile, “Xiaxia, where do you want to go? How about we row all the way around the lake?”","Qin Qiaoxia nodded. “Sure.”","Zhou Dingwen rowed the boat to the center of the lake, then slowed down. He wanted to spend more time talking with Qin Qiaoxia.","When he noticed her glancing toward Han Ye from time to time, he smiled and said, “What is it? Are you worried that Brother Ye will get angry?”","“I thought he looked upset just now.”","Zhou Dingwen said, “That’s just how he is. Hasn’t he always been like that, ever since we were kids? You’ll get used to it.”","Qin Qiaoxia said nothing.","Zhou Dingwen quietly watched her for a while.","Under the sunlight, Qin Qiaoxia looked even fairer and more beautiful. Her face was small, and her features were delicate. Her glossy black hair was tied high, while the wispy strands over her forehead were tousled by the breeze.","Zhou Dingwen stared at her for some time. When Qin Qiaoxia noticed his gaze, she looked back at him.","Suddenly, Zhou Dingwen reached out to take her hand. In a low voice, he said, “Xiaxia, we grew up together too. We’ve been childhood friends since we were little. Do you... do you think of me as...”","He didn’t finish.","Qin Qiaoxia moved her hand away, avoiding his outstretched fingers.","Zhou Dingwen: “...”","Qin Qiaoxia didn’t look at him. She lowered her head and gazed at the water beside the boat. “Brother Dingwen, let’s go back. Rowing isn’t very interesting.”","Zhou Dingwen: “...”","In that instant, his heart slowly went from burning with nervous anticipation to cold, silent resignation.","Unwilling to give up, he looked at Qin Qiaoxia again. “Xiaxia, do you know that I...”","“Brother Dingwen,” Qin Qiaoxia interrupted, looking at him. “You’ve always been like an older brother to me. Thank you for taking care of me all these years. As a brother, I do like you very much.”","Zhou Dingwen didn’t speak for a long while.","Eventually, he gave a bitter smile and said, “Since I’m your brother, isn’t taking care of my little sister only natural? What are you thanking me for? You’re making things sound so formal between us.”","After saying that, Zhou Dingwen didn’t know what else to say. He fell silent and rowed toward the shore.","The two of them remained quiet. Qin Qiaoxia mainly felt awkward, while Zhou Dingwen was filled with disappointment and helplessness, along with a sense of embarrassment.","He had been secretly in love with Qin Qiaoxia for quite some time. Ever since she started middle school, he had thought this little sister of his was adorable, and he had liked her very much.","But they had both been young then. They still had school and exams to worry about, and he had also needed to go serve in the military.","So he had never planned to confess his feelings.","That was the year he learned Qin Qiaoxia had started college. He felt the time was right, so he took the opportunity to come over and see her.","But in the end...","Zhou Dingwen sighed. It was his first time pursuing a girl, and after being rejected, he had no idea what to say or do.","His mind was a complete mess. All he could do was row the boat back to shore.","Han Ye had been waiting there the whole time. As soon as the boat reached the bank, he stepped forward and offered, “Xia'er, come on. I’ll help you down.”","Zhou Dingwen glanced at Xiaxia. Feeling too embarrassed to reach out and help her himself, he could only watch as Han Ye took her hand and led her away.","Noticing that both Zhou Dingwen and Xiaxia looked a little off, Han Ye frowned and asked, “Xia'er, what’s wrong? Are you seasick?”","Qin Qiaoxia gave him a helpless look. “How could I get seasick in a boat ride this mild?”","Han Ye said, “Your face looked strange to me, so I thought something was wrong. As long as you’re fine.”","Qin Qiaoxia shook her head, not knowing what else to say.","Han Ye really was unbelievably slow on the uptake.","The four of them wandered around by the river for a while and walked through the park. For some reason, Han Ye noticed that Zhou Dingwen and Liu Wenli were both unusually quiet. The two of them barely spoke at all.","Qin Qiaoxia had never been much of a talker to begin with, and Han Ye started to feel the pressure.","After hesitating for a moment, he said, “It’s getting late. How about we go grab something to eat?”","Everyone: “...”","Qin Qiaoxia raised her wrist and checked her watch. It wasn’t even five yet, and the sun hadn’t gone down. Wasn’t it a little early to be having dinner?","She hesitantly said, “Isn’t it a bit too early?”","Zhou Dingwen suddenly said, “I’ll skip dinner with you all. I still have to go back to Wencheng to see my family, and I need to catch a train, so I’ll be going now.”","Han Ye asked, “Didn’t you say you were going back tomorrow?”","Zhou Dingwen glanced at Xiaxia and gave a bitter smile. In a low voice, he said, “It’s been too long since I went home. I should go back earlier... the sooner, the better.”","Han Ye thought about it and decided that made sense. It wasn’t often that Zhou Dingwen got to go home, so the earlier he left, the more time he could spend with his family.","He immediately said, “All right, then. We’ll see you off.”","Zhou Dingwen refused. “No need. I can go by myself. You stay and have dinner with them.”","With that, Zhou Dingwen left.","Han Ye still wanted to say something, but he didn’t get the chance.","Zhou Dingwen left in such a hurry, striding away so quickly that by the time Han Ye finished hesitating, he was already a long way off.","Han Ye scratched his head and said to Qin Qiaoxia, “Why do I feel like Zhou Dingwen was acting strange? Do you think he was upset?”","Qin Qiaoxia shook her head. “How would I know? You’re asking the wrong person.”","Liu Wenli, who was standing beside them, looked thoughtfully at Qin Qiaoxia, then at Zhou Dingwen’s retreating figure. She smiled and said, “Qiao Xia, does that Zhou Dingwen like you?”","Han Ye: “???”","Han Ye abruptly turned to look at Xiaxia. “What? Zhou Dingwen likes you?”","A moment later, he added somewhat blankly, “But isn’t it perfectly normal for him to like Xiaxia? I like Xiaxia too. Everyone in our compound likes Xiaxia.”","Qin Qiaoxia: “...”","Liu Wenli: “...”"]},{"number":292,"title":"Chapter 292: Extra Story 4: Han Ye & Xia Xia","paragraphs":["Liu Wenli took Qin Qiaoxia by the hand and lowered her voice. “Your big brother really is hopelessly dense.”","Before, Liu Wenli had thought Han Ye simply wasn’t interested in her. But now it seemed he was just a block of wood.","Liu Wenli continued, “Are all the men in the army like this? This clueless?”","Qin Qiaoxia thought of Zhou Dingwen just now. “Not necessarily, right?”","Brother Dingwen had figured things out pretty early.","Her own older brother, Qin Qiao'an, was pretty sharp too. He didn’t seem like the type to mature late in matters of love.","When Qin Qiao'an had called home before, he’d learned that she was going to college and immediately warned her not to start dating casually, afraid she might be deceived or something.","Perhaps Han Ye wasn’t slow to catch on. Maybe he had simply never considered the matter of men and women.","After all, he had spent all these years in the army and was always saying that his sniper rifle was his wife, and that he planned to spend his whole life with his gun.","For someone like that, it was truly hard to say when he might develop feelings for a woman.","The two girls walked close together, chatting in low voices.","Han Ye followed behind them, and the more he thought about it, the more something seemed off.","He wasn’t actually stupid. When he first heard Liu Wenli say that Zhou Dingwen liked Xiaxia, he simply hadn’t thought of it in romantic terms, which was why he hadn’t reacted.","But now he had caught on. He might have been a little late, but it wasn’t too late.","Frowning, he walked over to Xiaxia, grabbed her by the arm, and asked, “Xia'er, when you went boating with Zhou Dingwen just now, did he say something to you?”","Xiaxia exchanged a glance with Liu Wenli. Liu Wenli coughed and quietly moved aside, leaving Xiaxia and Han Ye to talk.","Xiaxia hesitated before saying, “Actually, Brother Dingwen didn’t really say much.”","Han Ye snorted. “Just tell me the truth. Don’t hide anything.”","Since he was asking so directly, Xiaxia decided to tell him. “Brother Dingwen said that he and I were childhood sweethearts. Then he tried to hold my hand.”","The moment Han Ye heard this, he blew up. “What childhood sweethearts? What does he have to do with being your childhood sweetheart? I’m your childhood sweetheart, aren’t I?”","When he reached that point, Han Ye paused, then quickly added, “No, that’s not what I meant. I mean, he wasn’t close to you when you were little, so you two don’t count as childhood sweethearts. You’re young, and he’s trying to deceive you...”","As he spoke, he suddenly thought of something else and continued, “No, wait. You said he tried to hold your hand? Why would he do that for no reason? Can a girl’s hand just be held whenever he wants? What’s wrong with him?”","Even as Han Ye ranted, he couldn’t help thinking that he hadn’t even held Xiaxia’s hand before.","Xiaxia had already been living in Wencheng when she was born.","Han Ye had been attending school in Longcheng, so he had barely seen Xiaxia at all.","By the time Han Ye went to Wencheng, Xiaxia was already in elementary school. At that age, he couldn’t exactly hold a little girl’s hand.","Besides, during those years, he had been too busy taking Qin Qiao'an everywhere to run wild and hadn’t spent much time with Xiaxia.","Although he and Xiaxia had known each other since childhood, they had never really been that close.","Holding hands...","He lowered his head and glanced at Xiaxia’s hand. “He really held your hand?”","After listening to him rant in a frenzy for so long, Qin Qiaoxia shook her head. “No. I refused him, and then I rowed the boat back.”","Zhou Dingwen was probably in a terrible mood by now.","Qin Qiaoxia figured that when he came home in the future, he probably wouldn’t visit the Qin family anymore. Otherwise, wouldn’t it be awkward for the two of them to see each other?","Hearing this, Han Ye let out a sigh of relief. “You should have rejected him! That Zhou Dingwen has wanted to steal my little sister from me since we were kids. Luckily, he ran off quickly this time. Otherwise, I would have beaten him up.”","Looking at Han Ye’s expression, Xiaxia sighed inwardly.","Han Ye was still cursing Zhou Dingwen. “That bastard keeps saying he wants to be my best friend for life, then turns around and tries to pursue my sister. Has he even looked in a mirror? What makes him think he’s good enough for you?”","Xiaxia said nothing, simply listening as he continued to grumble and curse.","Han Ye really did seem angry.","Liu Wenli had been watching from the side for quite some time. She quietly pulled Qin Qiaoxia aside and whispered, “Qiaoxia, why is your brother so angry? Is it just because Zhou Dingwen likes you?”","Qin Qiaoxia shook her head. “My brother has always been like this. He gets angry whenever any boy gets a little too close to me.”","Come to think of it, Qin Qiao'an never acted this way, and he was her actual brother.","Liu Wenli said, “This godbrother of yours isn’t even your real brother. Could it be that he likes you?”","Qin Qiaoxia turned to look at her. “Huh?”","Her heart began to pound. Lowering her voice, she asked, “Why would you say that?”","Liu Wenli whispered, “The way he looks at you is strange. It doesn’t look like the way a brother looks at his sister.”","Liu Wenli had cousins and various older brothers of her own. To be honest, she felt that some older brothers did care about their younger sisters, but they didn’t have this kind of possessiveness.","Han Ye was possessive of Xiaxia. Earlier, he hadn’t even been happy about Zhou Dingwen going boating with her.","The more Liu Wenli thought about it, the more convinced she became. “It has to be that. Your wonderful big brother definitely has feelings for you, but he’s embarrassed to say anything. After all, you two are brother and sister.”","Qin Qiaoxia: “...”","Qin Qiaoxia lowered her voice. “What brother and sister? He isn’t actually my brother.”","They weren’t even formally god-siblings. Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu had never acknowledged him as their godson.","After all, according to local customs, becoming godparents or godchildren required certain ceremonies, such as burning incense before the ancestors.","People took such things quite seriously.","But neither family had ever brought it up.","At this thought, Qin Qiaoxia realized that she was clever enough to see the possibility. Could it be that both families had never mentioned the matter because they had long intended for the two of them to become in-laws?","Qin Qiaoxia had guessed only half the truth.","Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng truly regarded Han Ye as their own son. They had never considered making him their son-in-law.","Han Wenlin, however, had thought differently.","Ever since Xiaxia was born, Han Wenlin had secretly hoped that she would become his daughter-in-law.","It was just that Qiao Lanshu’s family had been too good to them and had helped them far too much, so he had never dared bring up the idea.","Han Wenlin knew how much Qin Yuanzheng cherished his daughter. He also knew perfectly well how troublesome Han Ye had been from childhood onward.","If he dared suggest a marriage alliance, Qin Yuanzheng would probably beat him black and blue.","Still, he couldn’t help wondering: what if?","What if his rotten son suddenly came to his senses and fell in love with Xiaxia?","So, even though Qiao Lanshu had once suggested formally taking Han Ye as their godson, Han Wenlin always brushed it off by saying that Han Ye was already her real son, and that making him a godson would only make them less close.","And yet, so many years had passed. Xiaxia was already in college, and Han Ye still showed no signs of waking up to his feelings. It seemed there was no hope.","Behind his son’s back, Han Wenlin had often complained to his wife about Han Ye, saying that the boy was useless and whatnot.","Of course, none of the children knew about any of this.","Qin Qiaoxia was lost in her thoughts. Then she glanced at Han Ye.","Han Ye still looked awful. Standing beside Xiaxia, he said, “Qin Qiaoxia, I’m giving you a serious reminder: You’re still young and still in school. There’s no rush to date. You can wait until you’re older and more mature, then take your time thinking about it! A great man once put it very well: Love without marriage as its goal is just hooliganism! Don’t be a hooligan, and don’t let anyone else be one with you either. Understand?”","Qin Qiaoxia: “...”","Liu Wenli: “...”","Liu Wenli was practically dumbstruck.","What on earth was he talking about? She wanted to laugh so badly, but she didn’t dare, because Han Ye looked completely serious.","He meant every word.","Liu Wenli lowered her head and covered her mouth with one hand, struggling desperately to hold back her laughter.","Qin Qiaoxia stared at Han Ye’s solemn expression for several seconds. Then, without warning, she reached out and took his hand.","Han Ye: “???”","Han Ye froze. He didn’t pull away. Instead, after his initial shock, he tightened his grip around Xiaxia’s hand.","His rough palm clasped hers tightly, and he asked nervously, “W-what’s wrong? Why did you suddenly take my hand?”","Xiaxia looked at him for a few seconds before pulling her hand away. She shook her head with a smile and said, “Nothing. Let’s go.”","With that, she pulled Liu Wenli away.","Han Ye: “...”","Han Ye looked at his hand, then at Xiaxia, and hurried after them. “What exactly was that about? Why did you suddenly take my hand?”","Liu Wenli glanced at Han Ye and noticed that his eyes were fixed intently on Xiaxia. There wasn’t room in them for anyone else.","After thinking it over, she said to Xiaxia, “Qiaoxia, I just remembered that I have something to do. I’d better go first.”","Xiaxia paused for a second, then nodded. “All right. Do you want me to walk you back to school?”","How could Liu Wenli possibly let them escort her?","Just look at the two of them. How awkward would it be for her to stay?","She quickly said, “No, no, that’s fine. It’s still broad daylight, and it’s only a short walk. I’ll go first. You stay and have some fun with your brother.”","Xiaxia nodded and said goodbye to her.","Zhou Dingwen had left, and Liu Wenli had left too. Now only Xiaxia and Han Ye remained.","The key point was that when Liu Wenli said goodbye to Han Ye, he hadn’t heard her at all. He hadn’t even glanced at her.","Liu Wenli left feeling speechless.","Xiaxia watched her walk away, then turned to Han Ye. “Brother Ye, Wenli spoke to you when she left just now. Why didn’t you answer her?”","Han Ye folded his arms and frowned at Xiaxia, his mind automatically filtering out the things he didn’t want to hear.","He asked again, “Xia’er, what was that all about just now? Why did you suddenly take my hand?”","Xiaxia: “...”","From childhood to adulthood, they had never held hands.","Han Ye had never held another girl’s hand, either.","This was his first time holding a girl’s hand, and it had turned out to be Xiaxia’s.","Still, he felt relieved that it was Xiaxia. If he had held Liu Wenli’s hand instead, he would definitely have felt uncomfortable.","Just imagining it made him uneasy.","Actually, ever since he had been pestered by a female classmate in middle school, he had disliked being around girls. From middle school all the way through college, he had never been comfortable interacting with them. Whenever he got too close, he felt as if they would start clinging to him and accusing him of fooling around with them.","It was simply too troublesome. It was better to keep his distance and avoid any problems.","Xiaxia looked at Han Ye without saying a word. Then she reached out again and took his hand.","Han Ye: “...”","He lowered his head to look at her, his expression filled with surprise and bewilderment. For a long moment, he said nothing.","Xiaxia held his hand and looked at him. “Han Ye, you know I’ve never thought of you as my brother.”","When she was little, she hadn’t been familiar with Han Ye. Somehow, everyone had decided he was her brother, but she had always been the slow-to-warm-up type. She had lumped Han Ye and Zhou Dingwen together as the neighborhood older brothers.","Later, after Han Ye began staying at her house often, they gradually became closer, and she started thinking of him as a brother. But this brother was different from Qin Qiao’an.","As for when her feelings toward Han Ye had changed, she couldn’t say.","Perhaps it was because she had grown up in a military compound, and she had always been drawn to the rough, roguish air of soldiers like them.","Besides, Xiaxia herself didn’t talk much and was introverted and slow to warm up. She particularly liked Han Ye’s outgoing, carefree personality.","Whenever she was with Han Ye, he always had plenty to say, making everything lively. He had lots of friends, and no matter what he did, he seemed to take it all in stride.","All in all, he was quite attractive.","With Xiaxia holding his hand, Han Ye frowned when he heard this and said unhappily, “Qin Qiaoxia, do you have any conscience? How good have I been to you all these years? When you fell into that dried-up well as a child, I was the one who pulled you out. I rode around on my bicycle looking for you for over an hour, and I was so exhausted I could barely breathe!","“When people bullied you, I was the one who went and got revenge for you. I bought most of your books and notebooks too. And now you’re telling me you’ve never thought of me as your brother? Tell me, do you have any conscience at all?”","Qin Qiaoxia: “...”","She looked up at Han Ye and said expressionlessly, “Han Ye, if a pig were standing in front of me right now, even it would understand what I’m saying.”","Han Ye grew even angrier. “Qin Qiaoxia, don’t push it! How can you call me a pig?”","Qin Qiaoxia: “Brother Ye, you’re giving yourself far too much credit. I mean that you’re worse than a pig.”","Han Ye: “...”","Han Ye suspected that Xiaxia was insulting him.","But he couldn’t understand why.","And all the while, their hands were still clasped together.","Han Ye couldn’t bring himself to be harsh with Xiaxia. He had never snapped at her since they were children.","But now he could tell that something was wrong. His thoughts were a complete mess. One moment he was thinking about how Zhou Dingwen liked Xiaxia and wanted to hold her hand; the next, he was staring at Xiaxia holding his.","He scratched his head and said, “Xiaxia, you can’t do this in the future. Who insults her own brother by calling him a pig? It’s terribly rude.”","Xiaxia expressionlessly pulled her hand back, said, “Oh,” and then added, “I’m going back to school. What about you, Brother Ye?”","Han Ye: “...”","Han Ye glanced at his hand, then stuffed it into his pocket. “It’s still early. I’ll take you out for something to eat first, then walk you back.”","Xiaxia said expressionlessly, “No.”","Han Ye: “No what?”","Xiaxia: “I don’t want to eat with a pig.”","Han Ye: “???”"]},{"number":293,"title":"Chapter 293: Extra Story 5: Han Ye & Xia Xia","paragraphs":["Han Ye had no idea why Xiaxia had suddenly gotten angry.","That afternoon, Xiaxia really did refuse to eat with him and returned to school early.","Han Ye had finally managed to get a day off and come out, only for his good friend Zhou Dingwen to leave early, while Xiaxia refused to go shopping or eat with him either.","This left Han Ye feeling rather depressed.","He couldn’t figure out why Xiaxia was angry, and wondered if Zhou Dingwen had somehow offended her.","Even after returning to the military base, he was still complaining about Zhou Dingwen to his roommates, saying that Zhou Dingwen was no good at all. He had treated him like a brother, yet Zhou Dingwen had actually dared to have designs on his sister.","Han Ye wanted to call and give Zhou Dingwen a piece of his mind, but Zhou Dingwen wasn’t at the unit, so he had no choice but to wait a few more days.","Fortunately, after more than half a month passed, Han Ye gradually began to figure things out.","After all, he was a man in his twenties, not an ignorant little boy who understood nothing.","He carefully replayed what had happened that day and felt that Xiaxia’s reaction had been strange.","Zhou Dingwen had wanted to hold Xiaxia’s hand because he liked her.","Then if Xiaxia had held his hand, that must have been because she liked him too, right?","But hadn’t Xiaxia always found him annoying since they were children?","Han Ye couldn’t make sense of it.","Just because he and Xiaxia had held hands twice, Han Ye had been sleeping badly for days. Even his dreams were filled with Xiaxia holding his hand.","In his dreams, he kept asking Xiaxia, “Why did you hold my hand? Didn’t you always find me annoying?”","But the Xiaxia in his dreams still ignored him.","Lying in bed in the middle of the night, he could even feel that his right hand was slippery, as if he could still sense the touch of Xiaxia’s hand.","The whole thing was just strange.","Maybe he had been thinking about it too much, which was why he kept dreaming about it at night.","Even more terrifyingly, one night Han Ye dreamed that Xiaxia kissed him. Not only had he not resisted in the dream, he had actually enjoyed it. And then...","In the middle of the night, he got up to wash his sheets and pants.","Han Ye felt as though the sky had collapsed.","How was he supposed to face Xiaxia—or Qiao Lanshu and the others—after this?","Because of that, Han Ye didn’t go to see Xiaxia again for several months.","...","After Qin Qiaoxia returned home, she reflected on things as well. She felt that Han Ye had always treated her as a younger sister.","Although she didn’t have the kind of sibling affection for Han Ye that one would normally have between brother and sister, any other kind of relationship between them would be inappropriate.","She had to take Han Ye’s feelings into consideration.","If Han Ye really regarded her only as a younger sister and had no other feelings for her, then if she made her feelings clear, wouldn’t they lose even their brother-and-sister relationship?","Qin Qiaoxia thought about it. If she and Han Ye were to become complete strangers who no longer had anything to do with each other, she didn’t think she would be willing to accept that.","So she decided to let it go.","She was still young, after all, and there was no need to rush into matters of the heart.","Maybe she would meet a man more charming than Han Ye in the future.","After all, her father was a military district commander, and there were so many young men in the army. Surely she could find someone with a good bearing.","After Xiaxia thought things through, she stopped looking for Han Ye as well.","Although they were both in the same city, they didn’t see each other again for several months.","When her holiday arrived, Qin Qiaoxia pulled her suitcase to the train station. That was when she saw Han Ye again.","Han Ye knew that she was going home for the holiday, so he had come to pick her up.","He had driven over and was waiting outside the school gate, just about to go inside to look for her.","As luck would have it, he saw her come out.","He scratched his head and walked over awkwardly. “Xia'er, you’re going home today. Why didn’t you tell me? I almost missed you.”","It was Qiao Lanshu who had called Han Ye to tell him that Xiaxia would be taking the train home that day. The train station was chaotic and crowded, and Xiaxia was a young girl traveling there alone for the first time. Qiao Lanshu was simply too worried to let her go by herself.","After all, there were far too many children abducted at train stations.","Xiaxia was so beautiful—what if someone kidnapped her?","Since Qiao Lanshu had called him, Han Ye had no choice but to make time, no matter how busy he was.","So he had hurried over that day.","Xiaxia was a little surprised to see him.","But after thinking about it, she realized that this really was something her mother would do.","Her mother was always worrying about her, constantly afraid that she would be abducted by human traffickers and sold to some remote mountain village.","Xiaxia looked Han Ye up and down before saying, “Aren’t you very busy at the military base? I was afraid I’d disturb you. Besides, I’m only going to the train station. I’ll be fine on my own.”","Han Ye didn’t dare look at Xiaxia’s face, much less meet her eyes.","This tall, strapping young man was usually arrogant and overbearing when reprimanding people at the military base. Yet in front of Xiaxia, he kept his head lowered and seemed completely at a loss.","He came over, took Xiaxia’s suitcase, and placed it in the car. Only then did he say, “Oh, stop that. How could a little girl like you know how dangerous society can be? Get in. I’ll drive you home.”","Xiaxia was startled. “You’re driving me home? All the way to Wencheng?”","Han Ye nodded, still refusing to look at her. “I took a few days off. I’ll drive you home and visit Mom while I’m there.”","Han Ye hadn’t gone home during the New Year holiday the previous year, and he had been busy ever since. This time, he had finally taken some annual leave.","When Xiaxia heard that he was taking her back to Wencheng, she felt a little happy.","After getting into the car, she asked, “How many days are you staying at home this time?”","Han Ye kept his eyes on the road and answered expressionlessly, “Seven days.”","Xiaxia asked again, “So you’re going home to visit your family? Did you call Uncle Han to tell him?”","Han Ye said, “What’s there to tell him? Won’t he know once I get home?”","Xiaxia fell silent.","Han Ye added, “But I did tell Mom. I said I’d taken leave to drive you home and visit the family while I was there. I also told her that I might not be able to come home for the New Year this year.”","Returning home for the New Year required drawing lots. Not everyone could get permission to go home.","As a company commander, Han Ye had heavy responsibilities and often had to remain at the military base.","Still, he could usually take leave to visit his family, so whether he could return home during the New Year didn’t matter much to him.","After all, during a time when the entire country was celebrating reunion, there had to be people standing guard in silence.","After talking with Han Ye for a while, Xiaxia realized that he seemed not to have looked at her even once.","It wasn’t her imagination. From the moment they had met, Han Ye hadn’t looked at her at all!","Why wouldn’t he look at her?","Was he afraid to, or simply unwilling?","What was Han Ye feeling guilty about?","Xiaxia really wanted to ask him, but since he was driving and still had several hours of highway ahead of him, she decided not to.","Along the way, Han Ye stopped to rest for a while and brought Xiaxia a large amount of snacks: dried beef, biscuits, apples, bananas, sunflower seeds, red dates, and all sorts of other things.","He had prepared an entire pile of food.","Even Xiaxia was a little stunned.","She picked up an apple and took a bite, then looked at Han Ye. “Brother Ye, where did you get all this food?”","Sitting in the driver’s seat, Han Ye took snacks out of the bag one by one as he said, “I bought them especially for you. It’ll take several hours to get there. Wouldn’t you be bored if you had nothing to eat along the way?”","Han Ye paused, glanced at Xiaxia, then quickly lowered his head. He took out a can of peaches and handed it to her. “Besides, there’s no town or village anywhere along this road. If you get hungry and want something to eat, there won’t be anywhere to buy it.”","Xiaxia nibbled on her apple while eyeing Han Ye suspiciously.","She thought he was acting strange.","Han Ye had always treated her and Qin Qiao'an well since they were little, often buying them stationery and snacks.","But Han Ye was actually a careless person.","Their family went out together fairly often, yet he had never prepared food for her before.","Why was he suddenly being so thoughtful this time? He was worried she would get bored, and worried she wouldn’t have enough to eat.","Xiaxia was finding it a little difficult to get used to.","She looked at Han Ye and asked quietly, “Brother Ye, did you do something guilty?”","Han Ye jolted in alarm and nearly jumped out of his seat.","He immediately looked up at Xiaxia, swallowed, and said somewhat nervously, “What are you talking about? I’ve always conducted myself properly. What could I possibly have done?”","Xiaxia studied his expression. “If you didn’t do anything guilty, why are you so nervous?”","Han Ye clicked his tongue, reached over, and flicked her on the forehead. In a deep voice, he said, “When was I nervous? All this food still can’t keep you from talking. Honestly, aren’t you usually pretty quiet?”","With that, he settled back into his seat, fastened his seat belt, and said, “Let’s go. We’re heading home.”","He started the car and continued down the road.","Sitting in the passenger seat, Xiaxia ate while watching the scenery outside. Every now and then, she turned to look at Han Ye.","His expression was definitely strange. He was obviously feeling guilty.","And he even had the nerve to turn it around on her.","Xiaxia grumbled inwardly, unaware that Han Ye was already in a complete panic.","After driving for more than half an hour, he finally couldn’t take it anymore and said, “Stop looking at me all the time. You’re distracting me. Just eat your food.”","Xiaxia: “...”","Driving while distracted really was dangerous.","So Xiaxia stopped looking at him, and the two of them didn’t speak again. They returned to Wencheng in silence.","Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng knew they were coming back today, so they had both left work early. They went to the market, bought a chicken, some pig’s feet, and pork, then returned home and immediately began making steamed buns, simmering chicken soup, and preparing braised pig’s feet.","After Xiaxia came home, she put her suitcase in her room and went to help Qiao Lanshu make the buns.","Qiao Lanshu pulled Xiaxia close and asked about school.","In those days, making phone calls wasn’t cheap, but Qiao Lanshu had never been one to scrimp on that. She often called Xiaxia, so naturally she already knew what had been going on at school.","But now that her daughter was home, she still couldn’t help asking a few more questions.","After earning her master’s degree two years earlier, Qiao Lanshu had returned to her alma mater, Wencheng University, to teach. She often went away for training and research, and even knew some of the teachers at Xiaxia’s school.","Once mother and daughter started talking, they showed no sign of stopping.","Qin Yuanzheng kneaded dough nearby while listening to them chat.","Han Ye was crouched beside him, listening as well.","Seeing him standing there in a daze, Qin Yuanzheng found it strange. Han Ye hadn’t been home in two years, yet he was unusually quiet.","Whenever Han Ye came back, he always had plenty to say. Either he would tell Qin Yuanzheng about life in the army, or he would boast to Qiao Lanshu about his achievements there.","This was the first time he had ever been so silent.","But Qiao Lanshu was busy talking with Xiaxia and preparing dinner, so she hadn’t had a chance to ask Han Ye what was wrong.","Qin Yuanzheng called Han Ye over and asked him, “Has anything happened in your unit?”","Han Ye stood beside Qin Yuanzheng and watched him knead the dough.","There were already strands of white in Qin Yuanzheng’s hair, and wrinkles had appeared on his face, but Han Ye didn’t dare underestimate him.","No one should think that just because Qin Yuanzheng was getting older, he was no longer formidable. If he found out that Han Ye had feelings for Xiaxia, he would probably break Han Ye’s legs on the spot.","Because he felt guilty, Han Ye was especially respectful in front of Qin Yuanzheng. “N-No, nothing happened. Everything’s been fine lately.”","Qin Yuanzheng rolled up his sleeves, revealing arms with strikingly well-defined muscles.","Han Ye glanced at them and silently took half a step back.","Qin Yuanzheng noticed and looked at him in confusion. Frowning, he asked, “What’s wrong with you? Is something going on that you can’t tell me?”","Han Ye swallowed and scratched his head. “Really, nothing’s wrong...”","Under Qin Yuanzheng’s stare, Han Ye took another two steps back and hurriedly came up with an excuse to escape. “Well, Uncle Qin, I’m going back to my place to take a look. I haven’t been home in two years. My dad must be missing me.”","With that, he ran to the kitchen doorway and called out to Qiao Lanshu, “Mom, I’m going home for a bit.”","Qiao Lanshu quickly asked, “Remember to come back for the steamed buns, okay? Oh, and bring your father and Aunt Zhao over for dinner. Tell them they don’t need to cook tonight.”","Han Ye glanced at Xiaxia. She was sitting beside Qiao Lanshu and had just looked up at him.","His heart gave a sudden leap, and he immediately turned around and ran.","Qiao Lanshu froze for a moment, then chased him to the kitchen doorway and shouted outside, “Hey, you little rascal! Did you hear me? Remember to come back for dinner!”","Han Ye didn’t answer. In the blink of an eye, he had run out the door.","As expected of someone who had trained in the army for so many years—he was incredibly fast.","Qiao Lanshu stood at the kitchen doorway for several seconds before turning to Qin Yuanzheng, who was kneading dough beside the table. “That boy’s pretty impressive. He runs so fast. If he entered the Olympics, he’d definitely win a gold medal, wouldn’t he? He’d bring glory to the country.”","Qin Yuanzheng: “...”","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head helplessly. “I don’t know what’s gotten into Han Ye. He seems preoccupied this time. When I talked to him just now, he was distracted too. I have no idea what he’s thinking.”","Qiao Lanshu returned to the kitchen and continued making buns with Xiaxia. As she worked, she said, “Han Ye’s already in his twenties. Could he be seeing someone?”","Qin Yuanzheng’s hands paused. Only then did he say, “If he can actually find someone, that would be a good thing. Just look at him—he’s built like a bull, wild and unruly, talks too much, and has a stubborn temper. He charges ahead without thinking. I’m worried he’ll never find a wife.”","Han Ye had improved a lot over the past few years. After all, he was already a company commander, with a whole group of soldiers under him. He couldn’t afford to keep acting recklessly.","In the past, he had been rather impulsive and had gotten into plenty of fights in the army. Fortunately, he had won every time, so he hadn’t embarrassed Qin Yuanzheng.","Hearing this, Xiaxia suddenly chimed in, “Dad, don’t say that about Brother Ye. I think he’s a good person. And life in the army hasn’t been easy for him these past few years.”","Qin Yuanzheng snorted. “Not easy? If it hasn’t been easy, that’s because he brought it on himself. He was always getting into fights in the army—of course it wouldn’t be easy. If only he were a little more steady, his commanding officer wouldn’t have had to complain to me time and time again.”","Qiao Lanshu smiled. “If Han Ye really is in love, that would be wonderful news. I wonder which girl he’s taken a fancy to. When he comes back tonight, I’ll have to question him properly.”","As she spoke, she turned to Xiaxia and asked, “Xiaxia, do you know about this? Did he tell you?”","Xiaxia: “......”"]},{"number":294,"title":"Chapter 294: Extra Story 6: Han Ye & Xia Xia","paragraphs":["How would Xiaxia know whether Qin Qiao'an was dating anyone?","When her roommate had asked her before, she had firmly insisted that Han Ye was single. But now, she wasn't so sure.","After all, Han Ye hadn't gone to see her at school for several months, and she had no idea what he had been busy with. Unless he was on a special mission or in training, he should still have had some free time, even if he was stationed with his unit.","Yet an entire semester had passed. Aside from seeing each other twice at the beginning of the school year, Han Ye hadn't gone to see her even once.","And this time, as Han Ye drove her home, he had looked strangely uneasy the entire way. It was obvious he was hiding something, but when Xiaxia asked him about it, he refused to say.","In the past, Han Ye and Qin Qiao'an had seemed to Xiaxia like a calf and a husky—impatient, reckless, and a little adorably foolish.","She could tell what they were thinking from a single look or gesture.","This was the first time Xiaxia had been unable to figure Han Ye out.","Could it be that he really had a girlfriend?","At the thought, Xiaxia's expression grew troubled.","Qin Yuanzheng was still discussing Han Ye's love life with Qiao Lanshu. After all, Han Ye was already in his mid-twenties and had become a company commander in the army. A young man who was handsome, promising, and had risen to become an officer at such a young age was highly sought after in the military.","\"Several comrades-in-arms have already asked me about Han Ye's marriage,\" Qin Yuanzheng said. \"I told them I needed to ask Han Ye what he thought, so I've kept putting off arranging any blind dates for him.\"","Han Ye was much like Qin Yuanzheng had been when he was young.","He had grown into a tall, handsome man of outstanding ability, becoming an officer while still very young. Although he could be somewhat hotheaded, he knew how to distinguish priorities when it came to work. He didn't act recklessly and had a fair amount of strategic sense.","A young man like that was highly desirable. The senior officers in the military all wanted to introduce their daughters to him.","Back then, Qin Yuanzheng had been alone. Aside from his former commanding officer, he had no relatives in the military, so when his superiors introduced women to him, it had been difficult for him to refuse.","If he hadn't suffered from infertility at the time, his wife now would not have been Qiao Lanshu, but the daughter of one of his superiors.","Han Ye, however, was luckier. He had Qin Yuanzheng and Han Wenlin behind him.","If Han Ye's superiors wanted to arrange a match for him, they had to ask Qin Yuanzheng's opinion first.","And Qin Yuanzheng's thinking was much the same as that of Han Ye's superiors. He, too, was currently keeping an eye out for promising young officers in the military, hoping to find a suitable husband for his daughter, Xiaxia.","After all, there were plenty of advantages to marrying his daughter to one of his subordinates.","For one thing, the man would not dare look down on Xiaxia, and she would hold the dominant position in the household.","Even after Qin Yuanzheng eventually retired, he would still be Xiaxia's husband's former commanding officer. The man would hardly dare treat him disrespectfully.","Qin Yuanzheng simply hadn't found a suitable candidate yet. Since Xiaxia was still in college, there was no need to rush.","As she busied herself making dumplings, Qiao Lanshu said, \"Actually, I think you could ask Director Han to look into it. Director Han has plenty of old friends and former colleagues. Perhaps he has someone in mind as well.\"","After all, Han Wenlin had only one son. He probably wanted to form a marriage alliance with the children of some of his old comrades too.","\"I already mentioned it to him,\" Qin Yuanzheng replied. \"He said everything should be based on Han Ye's wishes. We can arrange a blind date, but Han Ye has to like her.\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled. \"That blockhead Han Ye has no idea when he'll finally figure things out. He's almost twenty-five. If he dates someone for two years, he'll be twenty-seven by the time he gets married. It's time we started introducing people to him.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. \"All right. I'll talk to him tonight.\"","Xiaxia listened to their conversation from the side and let out a silent sigh.","In her heart, she thought, Forget it. I'll just treat Han Ye like an older brother.","Although she was reluctant to give up, there was nothing she could do about it.","Once she had come to terms with that, Xiaxia shook her head and focused on making the dumplings.","Han Ye loved pork-and-scallion dumplings.","Or rather, as long as the filling contained meat, he loved it. Pork with scallions, pork with mushrooms and corn, lamb dumplings, beef dumplings—he liked them all.","He simply loved meat.","Xiaxia stuffed generous amounts of filling into the wrappers, making the dumplings round and plump. They looked adorable.","When Qiao Lanshu saw them, she praised her. \"Oh, our Xiaxia is getting more and more skillful! Look how cute these dumplings are—thin wrappers and plenty of filling. They'll be so juicy once they're steamed. Your two brothers love them.\"","Then Qiao Lanshu sighed. \"An'an hasn't come home in more than two years. He must be craving dumplings too.\"","An'an wouldn't be able to return until after the New Year, though. Like Han Ye, he had enlisted first and then taken the college entrance examination. He had specifically applied to a military academy, where he would study a military-related major before returning to serve in the army.","That would give him better prospects in the future. After all, even the military was beginning to place more importance on academic qualifications.","Qin Yuanzheng snorted. \"Don't worry. The army canteen has all kinds of food. His meals might even be better than ours at home.\"","Over the years, the food in the military had steadily improved, as the country continued to place great importance on its soldiers.","Whatever else one could say, there was certainly no shortage of meat.","They were all young men, after all, and trained intensely every day. How could they manage without meat?","The family chatted as they cooked. By the time it grew dark, the steaming meat dumplings were ready.","The chicken soup that had simmered all afternoon was done as well.","Qin Yuanzheng went to check the braised pig's feet. He poked one with his chopsticks. The meat had been stewed until tender; the skin split at the touch, releasing a sizzling sheen of fat and an irresistible aroma.","Qin Yuanzheng lifted the pig's feet from the pot. Qiao Lanshu made blanched lettuce and stir-fried napa cabbage with vinegar, while Xiaxia prepared smashed cucumber salad. That was just about enough to start dinner.","Around six in the evening, Han Ye, Han Wenlin, and Zhao Yanfang arrived together.","The six members of the two families gathered around the large table and enjoyed a lively dinner.","Usually, Han Ye was extremely talkative and animated whenever he came home on leave. This time, however, he was unusually listless.","He sat there without saying a word, listening as the adults chatted. If someone asked him something, he would answer in a few words; otherwise, he simply remained silent and ate dumplings.","Although he seemed completely dispirited, he showed no restraint when it came to eating. He popped two dumplings into his mouth at a time, and within minutes, he had already eaten seven or eight.","Xiaxia was quiet by nature and didn't say much either. But every now and then, she would glance at Han Ye, wondering to herself whether he really had someone he liked.","Unbeknownst to her, those seemingly casual glances made Han Ye so nervous that he could hardly sit still.","He wanted to look at Xiaxia, but didn't dare. All he could do was endure her gaze while sweat beaded on his forehead.","Seeing that Han Ye had eaten nearly enough, Qin Yuanzheng took the initiative and asked, \"Han Ye, how are things going in the army? Is there anyone you like?\"","Han Ye nearly spat out the chicken soup he was drinking. He stared at Qin Yuanzheng in shock and said, “Uncle, it’s not like you don’t know that the army is all men. Women are as rare as giant pandas there. The only way to see one is to go to the hospital. Where am I supposed to find a girl to fall for?”","As he spoke, he instinctively glanced at Xiaxia.","Xiaxia was drinking chicken soup too, listening intently to the adults’ conversation.","Han Ye silently sighed to himself. He was interested in his own little sister—what was he supposed to do?","If the four adults sitting here found out, wouldn’t they beat his legs until they were broken?","Han Wenlin said, “I’ve heard about it. Isn’t there a commander in your military district who wants to introduce you to his daughter?”","Han Ye was stunned. “What? Who? Which commander?”","Qin Yuanzheng said, “Commander Qian from your military district. Haven’t you met him? You made quite an impression on him.”","At that, Han Ye immediately knew who he meant. He was puzzled. “What does he see in me? No, wait—how old is his daughter? I’ve never met her. We don’t even know each other. How are we supposed to date? Uncle, just help me turn him down. I’m not ready to get married.”","Han Wenlin grew anxious—not because he was eager to have grandchildren, but because Han Ye was already in his mid-to-late twenties, the perfect age to find a partner.","If he waited several more years, he would be older, and finding someone would become much harder.","He put on a stern face. “Don’t you know what kind of person you are? How dare you start being picky? That girl is willing to go on a blind date with you, so you should be secretly celebrating. The commander only agreed because he respects your Uncle Qin. If you had to rely on yourself, you’d be single for the rest of your life!”","Han Ye: “...”","Han Wenlin’s words made Han Ye’s face burn. For some reason, he suddenly felt the need to save face in front of Xiaxia.","He said unhappily, “Dad, can you stop putting me down like that? Can’t you show me a little respect?”","Han Wenlin said coldly, “You’re with family. What do you need face for?”","Han Ye: “...”","Han Ye knew he had no leg to stand on, so even his anger lacked conviction. “I can’t get through to you, you old man.”","Han Wenlin was only in his forties, but Han Ye had been calling him an old man for several years. He was used to it and didn’t get angry.","Beside him, Zhao Yanfang, Han Wenlin’s current wife, said with a smile, “Actually, if Han Ye doesn’t want to look for someone in the army, he could always find someone at a school. Lanshu and I know plenty of young female teachers. They all graduated from normal universities—young, beautiful, and well-educated. We could introduce you to one of them.”","Qiao Lanshu now taught at Wencheng University, while Zhao Yanfang taught at a high school. Both had been teachers for many years, and everyone around them was an educated professional. It would be easy enough for them to find Han Ye a good girl.","After all, Han Ye himself had plenty going for him.","But Han Ye said again, “No need, Teacher Zhao. Really, there’s no need. I don’t want to get married.”","Han Wenlin’s face turned cold. “You don’t want to get married? Then what do you want to do? When I was your age, you were almost born already.”","Han Ye was exhausted. He really didn’t want to say anything more.","The main problem was that he felt guilty and didn’t dare argue with all the adults present.","Qiao Lanshu also noticed that something was off with Han Ye. She smiled and said, “Usually, you get very angry whenever this topic comes up. But why are you being so obedient this time? You haven’t even talked back. This isn’t like you at all.”","The adults suddenly understood and all turned their eyes on Han Ye.","Han Ye: “...”","Han Ye instinctively looked at Xiaxia again. He happened to see her looking at him too. Her large, dark eyes made his heart race, and the tips of his ears turned bright red.","The moment he realized it, Han Ye suddenly raised his hand and slapped himself hard across the face.","The sharp crack of the slap stunned everyone.","Even Xiaxia froze for a moment, her large dark eyes filled with shock and disbelief.","The warm, cheerful atmosphere suddenly fell silent.","Everyone stared at Han Ye, then at the clear handprint on one side of his face.","Qiao Lanshu was startled by him. After a few seconds of silence, she hurriedly said, “Um... Han Ye, it’s a good thing that you’re behaving better. You don’t have to hit yourself over it. Didn’t that hurt?”","At that moment, even Han Wenlin felt embarrassed to keep pressuring him about marriage.","He coughed and asked in an unusually gentle tone, “You little brat, what exactly happened to you? Tell us. Don’t hit yourself. You look like a complete idiot...”","Han Ye stood up and said, “I’m full. I’m heading home.”","Qiao Lanshu asked, “You’re going home? You’re not staying here tonight?”","“No, I’m leaving.”","With that, he didn’t even wait for Han Wenlin and Zhao Yanfang. He hurried away.","Han Wenlin had driven there, but Han Ye didn’t wait for him. Instead, Han Ye ran all the way home that night.","After Han Ye left, the four adults sat in silence for a while, looking at one another.","Xiaxia also sat there quietly. She couldn’t shake the feeling that there was something strange about the way Han Ye looked at her.","After a long while, Zhao Yanfang finally said, “What happened to that boy? Did something happen to him in the army?”","Han Wenlin looked up at the sky and said nervously, “As long as he isn’t into men...”","Everyone else: “...”","Han Wenlin and Qin Yuanzheng had both spent many years serving in the army.","There were, in fact, some men in the military who were attracted to other men, though it was quite rare.","But Han Ye had said he didn’t want to get married or go on blind dates. He was acting strangely and had even slapped himself...","He must have done something terribly wrong.","Han Wenlin couldn’t imagine what kind of guilty act could make someone like Han Ye slap himself.","The only explanation he could think of was that Han Ye might be attracted to men.","Qiao Lanshu exchanged a glance with Zhao Yanfang and hurriedly reassured him, “How could that be? You’re overthinking it. Han Ye definitely likes girls. He probably just has something on his mind, and that’s why...”","As she spoke, she realized she didn’t know how to finish the sentence either.","Qin Yuanzheng said, “Let’s talk to him tomorrow and see what’s really going on.”","Han Wenlin glanced at Xiaxia. She had remained quiet the whole time and rarely said anything.","Han Wenlin said to her, “Xiaxia, you and Han Ye grew up together, and you two have always had a pretty good relationship. Why don’t you help us out and go talk to him? Find out what’s on his mind. Maybe he’s run into some trouble—or maybe he’s fallen for someone?”","Zhao Yanfang nodded. “If we ask him, he definitely won’t tell us. But if Xiaxia asks, he might be willing to talk.”","Qiao Lanshu sighed. “It’s a shame Zhou Dingwen wasn’t here when he came back last time. Otherwise, Zhou Dingwen would have been the best person to ask. Aren’t the two of them close friends?”","The adults sat around the dining table, but the food had long since gone cold. They made tea and continued talking in the courtyard, one person adding to another, for a long time.","Xiaxia listened to them and finally agreed to go talk to Han Ye.","She was curious too.","She just didn’t know whether Han Ye would be willing to tell her."]},{"number":295,"title":"Chapter 295: Extra Story 7: Han Ye & Xia Xia","paragraphs":["On the second day after Han Ye came home, he headed over to Qiao Lanshu’s house early in the morning.","As luck would have it, Qiao Lanshu wasn’t working that day. She was already on vacation, so she had gone shopping with Xiaxia.","When Han Ye arrived, he found the house empty.","He couldn’t help feeling disappointed.","After thinking it over, he rode his bicycle out and made two rounds of the Cloth Street. Sure enough, he spotted Qiao Lanshu shopping for clothes with Xiaxia.","Han Ye hesitated, then slowly pedaled toward them.","Xiaxia spotted him first and said to Qiao Lanshu, “Mom, Brother Ye is here.”","Qiao Lanshu looked up and saw Han Ye. She immediately lowered her voice and said to Xiaxia, “Didn’t Director Han say last night that you should ask him about it? Go ask him now, and keep him company while you’re at it. He hasn’t been home in a long time, after all. I’ll go to the market to buy groceries first. You two come home for lunch.”","Xiaxia hesitated for two seconds before nodding. “All right. I’ll go ask him.”","By the time Han Ye reached them, Qiao Lanshu had already placed the clothes she and Xiaxia had bought into his bicycle basket. She said, “Han Ye, I have to go buy groceries. Take Xiaxia around Cloth Street and get some clothes, shoes, socks, and whatever else she needs. Remember to come home for lunch.”","Han Ye: “...”","He quickly glanced at Xiaxia and said awkwardly, “Huh? Mom, aren’t you coming with us? It’s still early. You can go buy groceries later.”","Qiao Lanshu patted him on the shoulder, her eyes filled with tenderness. “Better to go early. I’m making your favorite meat dragon for lunch, but I’m not very good at it, so I’ll have to ask Teacher Zhao to come over and help. All right, enough talking. You two go look around. You’ve both just gotten back, so take a walk and see more of the town. I’m off to buy groceries.”","Han Ye was about to say something else.","But Xiaxia had already walked behind him and naturally climbed onto the back seat of his bicycle.","Han Ye: “...”","Without thinking, he fell silent.","After Qiao Lanshu left, he remained sitting on the bicycle without moving.","Xiaxia reached out and tugged at the hem of his shirt. “Brother Ye, let’s go.”","Han Ye: “...”","Han Ye stiffly began pedaling, riding slowly along Wencheng’s Cloth Street.","Cloth Street was quite large, with three main streets and several alleys. Besides clothes and fabrics, there were all kinds of general stores, audiovisual shops, arcades, and more. It was bustling with people.","When Xiaxia was little, she often came here to buy things at the stationery and bookstores.","As they passed a bakery, Xiaxia said, “Brother Ye, stop for a moment. I want to buy some bread.”","Han Ye stopped the bicycle with a tap of his foot, moving like a robot.","Xiaxia got off the back seat and walked toward the bakery. After taking two steps, she turned around and looked at him. “Brother Ye, aren’t you coming in?”","Han Ye lowered his head. “I’ll wait here. I need to watch the bicycle and the clothes. What if someone takes them?”","Qiao Lanshu had just bought Xiaxia two new outfits, both warm thermal sets for autumn. They were currently sitting in the bicycle basket.","Xiaxia glanced at them and said nothing more. She went into the bakery by herself.","Han Ye watched her retreating figure and silently sighed.","Xiaxia bought a box of egg tarts. The three siblings had loved eating them since they were children, and they weren’t easy to find anywhere else.","When she came out with the egg tarts, Han Ye looked up at the sky.","Xiaxia had noticed long ago that Han Ye was acting strangely. He would look at the sky or the ground—anything but her.","She put the egg tarts into the bicycle basket and said, “Brother Ye, shall we take a walk?”","Han Ye immediately grew nervous. “A walk? Where are we going?”","Xiaxia walked beside him as they headed forward. “After dinner last night, once you left, Mom and Dad started wondering whether something was bothering you. So they asked me to find out.”","Han Ye: “...”","He did have something on his mind, but could he really say it?","He was just about to speak when Xiaxia asked again, “Brother Ye, be honest. Do you have a girlfriend?”","Han Ye jumped and blurted out loudly, “Of course not! Why would you ask that?”","Xiaxia said, “It’s not me who wants to know. It’s the four elders.”","Han Ye: “...”","Looking at Xiaxia’s delicate little face, Han Ye said awkwardly, “There’s nothing like that. Don’t make wild guesses.”","Seeing the panic in his expression, Xiaxia understood. “I see. Then you must have someone you like?”","Han Ye: “...”","Xiaxia leaned closer and asked in a low voice, “Who is it? Tell me.”","As Xiaxia moved closer, Han Ye’s face and ears immediately turned bright red. His eyes darted nervously from side to side, refusing to meet hers. He stammered, “You’re just a kid. Why are you asking about this?”","Xiaxia was astonished. Judging from his reaction, he really did have someone he liked.","But weren’t there only men in the military?","He had said himself that the only women he got to see were at the military hospital.","So how had he suddenly found someone he liked?","Xiaxia leaned in even closer. She was a head shorter than Han Ye, so she tilted her head to study his expression.","Han Ye shifted to the side, but she followed him and continued looking.","Han Ye: “...”","His ears burning red, he glared at her. “Qin Qiaoxia, you’d better stop while you’re ahead.”","Xiaxia suddenly asked, “Han Ye, why won’t you look at me?”","Han Ye retreated half a step. “What do you mean, I won’t look at you? I am looking at you.”","Xiaxia said with certainty, “See? You’re not looking at me right now.”","Han Ye took another half-step back and pretended to be angry. “Qin Qiaoxia, you’re getting more and more disrespectful...”","He didn’t finish.","Xiaxia had placed her hand on the back of his.","His hands were gripping the handlebars, and Xiaxia had set her hand over his right hand, giving it a gentle squeeze.","Her expression remained calm as she did it. She simply stared intently at Han Ye’s face, watching for any change in his expression.","Han Ye was completely flustered. He stood rigidly still, glancing at Xiaxia’s hand before looking back at her.","His heart was racing. His face was full of panic, while his eyes held both surprise and delight. His emotions were incredibly complicated.","He swallowed and met Xiaxia’s gaze, but for a long while, he couldn’t say a word.","Xiaxia studied him for quite some time before suddenly smiling.","Xiaxia had always been emotionally steady. She rarely showed her feelings openly, and most of the time, her expressions were rather restrained.","But now she grinned, revealing eight neat little teeth. Two dimples appeared at the corners of her mouth, just like Qiao Lanshu’s, making her unbearably adorable.","Han Ye was completely mesmerized.","It had been so long since he had seen Xiaxia this happy. Somewhat puzzled and more than a little nervous, he asked, “Xia’er, why did you suddenly start smiling?”","Xiaxia’s hand was still resting on his. It was cool and soft, and it made his entire arm feel as though it were burning.","She looked at him for a long moment before finally smiling and saying, “It’s nothing. Come on, let’s keep looking around.”","With that, she climbed back onto the bicycle’s rear seat and urged him, “Han Ye, hurry up.”","Han Ye: “...”","Han Ye was like a puppet manipulated by Xiaxia. He climbed onto the bicycle and continued pedaling her around Bu Street.","But before long, he felt Xiaxia, sitting on the back seat, suddenly reach both arms around and hug him by the waist!","Han Ye: “!!!”","Han Ye’s entire body jolted, and the bicycle wobbled with him. They nearly fell over and almost collided with someone else.","Fortunately, his legs were long enough. He hurriedly planted both feet on the ground and managed to steady the bicycle.","A passerby glared at him. But when he saw Han Ye’s dark skin, crew cut, and towering build, he immediately withdrew his hostile stare and hurried away, deciding it was safer not to get involved.","Han Ye remained there with both feet braced against the ground and fell silent for a long while.","He waited and waited, but Xiaxia still didn’t let go.","Han Ye’s entire body was taut, every muscle drawn tight. As Xiaxia hugged him, she could feel how hard and rigid he was. Curious, she reached out and patted the side of his waist.","It really was hard. How strange.","Han Ye nearly jumped out of his skin. At last, unable to take it anymore, he turned around and glared at Xiaxia. “Qin Qiaoxia, what exactly are you doing?”","Xiaxia smiled at him. “What do you think?”","Han Ye: “...”"]},{"number":296,"title":"Chapter 296: Extra Story 8: Han Ye & Xia Xia","paragraphs":["On the fourth day after Han Ye returned, he suddenly left the Han family home and moved back in with Qiao Lanshu’s family.","He had often stayed there before, so Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng were already used to it. Neither of them thought much of it.","Qin Yuanzheng usually had to go to work, and Qiao Lanshu had plenty to keep her busy as well. That meant Xiaxia was generally home alone.","Xiaxia had plenty of childhood friends and classmates in Wencheng, but after going out to meet them for two days, she stopped leaving the house much.","Whenever she did go out, Han Ye would take her on the back of his bicycle. No one knew what the siblings did all day, but they always came home after dark.","Qiao Lanshu was quite at ease about the two children. Han Ye had grown mature and steady, and Xiaxia went without saying. Even if the two of them stayed out all night, Qiao Lanshu trusted them not to get into trouble.","But Han Ye had come home this time on annual leave, which meant his vacation was limited. In just a few days, he would have to return to his unit.","So Qin Yuanzheng thought he ought to leave work early these days, so he could come home and have a heart-to-heart talk with Han Ye.","Yet on the rare day he actually got off work early, Han Ye was nowhere to be seen when he got home!","With no other choice, he accompanied Qiao Lanshu to buy groceries.","Then, at a street corner, they saw Han Ye riding his bicycle with Xiaxia on the back.","Qin Yuanzheng glanced at them and frowned. “Han Ye has been taking Xiaxia out every day lately. What exactly are they doing? Was Xiaxia ever this attached to him before?”","Qiao Lanshu was curious too. The two of them followed them for a look and saw Xiaxia sitting on the back of Han Ye’s bicycle. One arm was wrapped around his waist, while she held a popsicle in the other hand. She took a bite herself, then held it out to him. Han Ye turned his head and took a bite from the spot she had just eaten.","When he finished, Xiaxia laughed and continued eating.","Her smile was so radiant. Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng rarely saw Xiaxia this happy.","Before long, Han Ye’s bicycle disappeared into the distance.","Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu stood at the street corner. He was holding the groceries, while she had her arm linked through his.","The two of them fell into an awkward silence.","Nearly two full minutes passed before Qiao Lanshu finally spoke hesitantly. “When did Han Ye and Xiaxia become so close?”","Qin Yuanzheng looked solemn. “Don’t you think something’s off about them?”","Of course, Qiao Lanshu had noticed it too.","But she still said, “They grew up together. Sharing a popsicle isn’t necessarily a big deal.”","When Qin Qiao'an and Xiaxia were little, they often drank from the same cup and ate from the same bowl. Sometimes Qin Qiao'an even ate Xiaxia’s leftovers. After they started middle school, that happened much less often.","But it wasn’t as if it had never happened. So sharing a popsicle...","Qiao Lanshu rubbed her forehead. “Forget it. The more I think about it, the less normal it seems. How much does a popsicle cost? Ten cents? If they wanted one, they could have bought two. Why did they have to share?”","“Xiaxia has always disliked the two of them,” Qin Yuanzheng said. “She’s never eaten anything they’ve already had. She won’t even eat food you’ve taken a bite of.”","Xiaxia disliked eating anything other people had eaten, even if that person was Qiao Lanshu.","The only person in the family who didn’t mind was Qin Yuanzheng. He ate whatever his wife left behind, and whatever the children left behind too.","Now Xiaxia didn’t mind eating a popsicle Han Ye had bitten into. That was highly unusual—unless the two of them...","The husband and wife exchanged a look.","Qiao Lanshu wasn’t angry. She was simply astonished—extremely astonished.","Qin Yuanzheng, however, was somewhat angry. His face darkened. “Let’s go home.”","By the time they returned, it wasn’t dark yet.","It was only after night had fallen that the sound of a bicycle bell rang out at the gate.","A moment later, Han Ye pushed his bicycle into the courtyard with Xiaxia beside him, the two of them chatting as they walked.","They were both smiling and laughing, clearly in high spirits.","Xiaxia especially was so obviously happy that Qiao Lanshu couldn’t help taking several more looks at her.","The moment they saw Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu in the courtyard, they stopped short.","Still smiling, Xiaxia said, “Dad, Mom, I’m back! I bought some apples and pears. Oh, and I bought sunflower seeds too. Mom, do you want some?”","Qiao Lanshu looked at her and said flatly, “No. Your mother doesn’t feel like eating anything right now.”","Qin Yuanzheng stood there with a stern, expressionless face, staring intently at the two of them.","He had been watching them ever since Han Ye and Xiaxia entered the courtyard.","They had been walking quite close together, side by side at first. And the way Han Ye looked at Xiaxia...","Qin Yuanzheng had been around long enough to understand exactly what that look meant.","Besides, the moment they saw the two adults at home, Han Ye and Xiaxia immediately put some distance between themselves. It was practically a confession in itself!","Qin Yuanzheng’s face darkened. “Han Ye, you...”","He had barely begun when Qiao Lanshu grabbed his arm.","She gave him a meaningful look.","Frowning, Qin Yuanzheng forced himself to hold back.","Han Ye sensed that the atmosphere was strange, but he didn’t dare ask. After all, he felt guilty.","He carried the things inside and asked, “Uncle, did you want to talk to me about something?”","“It’s nothing,” Qiao Lanshu said. “You two rest for a while. Dinner will be ready soon.”","With that, she pulled Qin Yuanzheng into the kitchen.","The moment they entered, Qin Yuanzheng couldn’t hold it in any longer. He lowered his voice and said, “Why didn’t you let me ask him just now?”","Qiao Lanshu lowered her voice as well. “Of course I couldn’t let you ask like that. Think about it. If there’s nothing going on between them, wouldn’t asking embarrass them? Wouldn’t it hurt their feelings? But if there really is something between them...”","She fell silent for several seconds before continuing. “Actually, when you think about it carefully, this is a good thing too. We know exactly what kind of person he is, and Xiaxia wouldn’t have to marry someone from outside the family. She could stay here with us. Wouldn’t that be wonderful?”","Qiao Lanshu had only stopped being angry after thinking it through this way.","Qin Yuanzheng had previously favored Zhou Dingwen, believing that he was a good man.","But now that he looked at it, Han Ye was actually much more suitable than Zhou Dingwen.","A child they had watched grow up from infancy—there was no one more dependable than him.","Besides, Han Ye had always taken good care of his younger siblings.","That was all true, but Qin Yuanzheng was still displeased.","He said darkly, “That brat actually set his sights on Xiaxia. When do you think he started? Don’t tell me he had these intentions back when Xiaxia was still little.”","If that was really the case, he would break Han Ye’s legs himself."]},{"number":297,"title":"Chapter 297: Side Story 9: Han Ye & Xia Xia","paragraphs":["Han Ye still had no idea that his relationship with Xiaxia had already been discovered.","The two of them were still whispering secretly in her room. Standing beside Xiaxia’s desk, he held her hand and said in a furtive voice, “Xia’er, don’t you think there was something strange about the way our dad was looking at me just now?”","Han Ye had always had his principles.","He had eaten countless meals at Qin Yuanzheng’s house growing up, but he had never once called Qin Yuanzheng “Dad.”","Yet now, less than three days into his relationship with Xiaxia, he was already calling him “our dad” at every opportunity.","The two of them had grown up together as childhood sweethearts and knew each other inside and out.","Even so, now that they were dating, there was still that thrilling, heart-fluttering excitement between them.","Han Ye lowered his voice. “The way he looked at me just now was exactly the same as when he wanted to beat me for doing something wrong as a kid.”","Xiaxia sat in her chair with one hand propping up her cheek as she looked at him. “So what did you do wrong this time?”","Han Ye said, “What could I have done? I’ve been with you every day since I got back. Don’t you know whether I’ve done anything wrong?”","As he spoke, he reached out and pinched Xiaxia’s cheek.","She did not dodge, simply letting him pinch her. Then she said, “Then you must have gotten into trouble in the army. Your commanding officer complained to my dad.”","Han Ye frowned and fell silent for several seconds before saying, “Impossible. I haven’t caused trouble in a whole month. When I asked for leave to come back, my commanding officer even said I’d been performing well, so he approved two extra days off.”","Xiaxia looked at him, her expression gradually turning serious. “Ah. Then there’s only one possibility...”","Before she could finish, there was a knock on the door. Qiao Lanshu called from outside, “Xiaxia, are you in there? I’m coming in, okay?”","Han Ye immediately let go of Xiaxia’s hand and straightened up, standing ramrod-straight. He exchanged a nervous glance with her.","Xiaxia, on the other hand, remained perfectly calm. She gave him an exasperated look. “Honestly, what are you so nervous about?”","Of course they would have to tell their parents eventually. And this was hardly a big deal, was it?","They weren’t biological siblings, after all.","Cold sweat broke out on Han Ye’s forehead. He wiped it away and said in a low voice, “I don’t know. I’m just nervous.”","Being scolded or beaten up by Qin Yuanzheng was no big deal.","He was tough as nails. Surely he wasn’t afraid of getting hit?","He didn’t even know what he was afraid of. All he knew was that he was incredibly nervous.","Xiaxia stood up and went to open the door. “Mom, what’s up? Did you need something?”","She opened the door and saw Qiao Lanshu standing outside.","Qiao Lanshu glanced at her, then walked straight into the room. A moment later, she spotted Han Ye standing beside the desk by the window.","Han Ye scratched his head awkwardly. “Mom, I—I just came in to see Xiaxia.”","Han Ye rarely went into Xiaxia’s room. In fact, he almost never went there alone.","She was a girl, after all, and Han Ye had always understood the importance of keeping a proper distance.","But now they were both adults, and he had come into her room anyway. How could that not make people suspicious?","Qiao Lanshu looked at him helplessly. “You go outside first. I have something to discuss with Xiaxia.”","Han Ye wiped the cold sweat from his forehead, glanced at Xiaxia, and silently left the room.","The moment he stepped outside, he saw Qin Yuanzheng standing in the courtyard, rolling up his sleeves.","When Qin Yuanzheng saw him, he beckoned. “Come here. Let’s spar a few rounds.”","Han Ye: “...”","...","Inside the room, Qiao Lanshu chatted with Xiaxia for a while. Xiaxia did not hide anything and directly told her about her relationship with Han Ye.","Qiao Lanshu was not surprised in the slightest. She asked, “How long have you two been together?”","Xiaxia held up three fingers. “Today is the third day.”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","Qiao Lanshu let out a sigh of relief. “I thought you’d been together for a long time.”","Xiaxia shrugged. “How could that be? Just look at Han Ye. He’s completely clueless. If I hadn’t made things clear first, he probably still wouldn’t have realized how I felt.”","Qiao Lanshu: “...”","Qiao Lanshu was so startled by Xiaxia’s words that she froze for several seconds. Then she poked Xiaxia on the forehead. “You were the one who made the first move? You child, how could you...”","She did not even know what to say.","Xiaxia smiled and hugged her arm, pleading sweetly, “Oh, Mom, don’t be mad. Haven’t you always worried that I’d marry far away? Well, this is perfect. I won’t have to move far away like you did. I can stay here with Han Ye, and after we get married, I can still live nearby. Wouldn’t that be great?”","Those words struck a chord deep inside Qiao Lanshu.","She had married far from home herself. Although she had lived a happy life, returning to her family home had always been difficult.","After marrying here, she had only managed to visit her family in Yangcheng five or six times over the years.","When the children were young, she could not get away and had no way to make the trip.","Once they were older, she could finally take the whole family back to visit—but the train ride alone took two days and one night, making the journey exhausting.","She rubbed Xiaxia’s head and said, “Feelings between lovers are different from feelings between siblings. You need to think carefully. When two people get together, it’s for a lifetime. A person’s life is very long, so you need to consider this carefully and not act on impulse.”","Xiaxia was only eighteen, still very young. She still had four years of university ahead of her, and there was no need to rush into thinking about marriage until after graduation.","What Qiao Lanshu feared was that Xiaxia and Han Ye might break up by then. Wouldn’t that mean they could not even remain siblings afterward?","Xiaxia said, “Don’t worry, Mom. I’ve thought it through. I think Han Ye is a great guy.”","Finding a man who suited her better than Han Ye would probably be difficult.","After Qiao Lanshu finished talking with Xiaxia, their relationship had officially been acknowledged by the adults.","When Qiao Lanshu and Xiaxia came out of the room, they saw Qin Yuanzheng and Han Ye sparring shirtless in the courtyard.","Han Ye spent most of the time being beaten up. It was not that he could not defeat Qin Yuanzheng; he simply did not dare use his full strength.","Qin Yuanzheng, meanwhile, showed no mercy. He claimed they were only sparring, but he gave Han Ye quite a beating.","After a full round of training, both men were drenched in sweat. Han Ye sat on the ground, groaning and complaining, “Chief Qin, you’re hitting way too hard! Are you trying to beat me to death?”","Qin Yuanzheng snorted. “You’re tough as an ox. Are you really afraid of taking a few hits?”","Did he think Qin Yuanzheng did not know him?","Han Ye was clearly putting on an act because Qiao Lanshu and Xiaxia had come outside, pretending to be pitiful.","It seemed he had gone too easy on him just now.","Xiaxia did feel sorry for Han Ye. She said, “Oh, Dad, stop hitting the brothers all the time. They’re grown up now. They need to save face.”","Qin Yuanzheng: “...”","Qin Yuanzheng was furious. His daughter was not even married yet, and already she was taking someone else’s side.","Still, he could not bring himself to scold Xiaxia. He turned to Han Ye instead. “A grown man should act like one. What’s with all the whining and groaning?”","Han Ye: “...”","Han Ye hurriedly scrambled to his feet.","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, “All right, all right. Go take a shower. Dinner will be ready soon.”","And so, Han Ye and Xiaxia’s relationship won the approval of both families.","Unfortunately, Han Ye was about to return to his military unit.","He couldn’t bear to leave her!","They had only held hands for a few days, and already he had to go back to the unit. To make matters worse, Qin Yuanzheng refused to let him stay at home during the days before his departure.","He sent Han Ye back to the Han family home instead. Han Ye could only come visit Xiaxia during the day and had to take her home before dark. Otherwise, he would have to face a beating.","On the afternoon before he returned to his unit, Han Ye took a walk with Xiaxia by the river. His face was full of worry as he said, “After I go back this time, we probably won’t see each other again until you start school.”","Xiaxia was reluctant to part with him too. She asked, “You’re not coming home for the New Year either?”","Han Ye shook his head. “Not this year.”","He looked at Xiaxia and hesitated for a long while before asking quietly, “Xia’er, can I hug you?”","Xiaxia: “......”","The tips of Han Ye’s ears turned red, and he looked a little embarrassed.","Although he was older than Xiaxia, he was rather innocent when it came to relationships.","The two of them had gone out together every day over the past few weeks, but all he had dared to do was hold her hand.","Xiaxia took the initiative and hugged him. She said, “You have to keep yourself in check while you’re in the military. Call and write to me regularly. And when I start school, remember to meet me at the train station. Do you hear me?”","Han Ye’s heart was pounding. He hugged her tightly and hurriedly said, “I hear you, I hear you. I’ll do everything you say.”","Ever since he was little, he had thought Xiaxia was sensible and clever.","Now that Xiaxia was his girlfriend, he naturally saw her through rose-colored glasses. Whatever she said was right.","The next day, Qiao Lanshu loaded plenty of food into Han Ye’s car, and Han Ye drove back to his unit himself.","Xiaxia secretly handed him a bracelet and whispered, “Remember to think about me, okay?”","Han Ye looked at the silver bracelet. It was one Xiaxia had been wearing herself—a delicate women’s bracelet.","It looked somewhat out of place on his wrist, since the women’s bracelet was so thin.","But he was thrilled. This was their token of love!","He gazed at Xiaxia reluctantly and said, “You remember to think about me too. Don’t talk to other men, understand?”","Qin Yuanzheng had been standing nearby, watching the two of them act all lovey-dovey, and found it rather irritating.","He walked over to Han Ye and said sternly, “All right, enough. Hurry up and go.”","They were dragging things out too much. What kind of behavior was this?","Han Ye had wanted to give Xiaxia one more hug, but with Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu there, he didn’t dare. He didn’t even dare hold her hand.","In the end, the two of them merely exchanged one deeply affectionate look before Han Ye drove away.","Han Wenlin had been watching from the side as well, and he was quite pleased.","After Han Ye left, he walked over to Qin Yuanzheng and said, “Yuanzheng, should we find a matchmaker and choose a date for the two of them to get engaged? They can get engaged first, and then get married after Xiaxia graduates.”","Qin Yuanzheng was already feeling irritated, so he said, “Xiaxia just turned eighteen. It’s too early for an engagement. We’ll talk about it later.”","Han Wenlin was a little disappointed, but he soon became happy again.","His son was truly impressive. He had actually managed to win Xiaxia over.","From now on, Xiaxia would be his daughter-in-law! Their family and Qin Yuanzheng’s family would become related by marriage—truly one family.","That was a good thing.","......","......","After Qin Qiaoxia graduated from university, she stayed in the capital to work.","By then, she and Han Ye were preparing to get married.","Han Ye had waited four years for Xiaxia. From the moment they had confirmed their relationship, he had already wanted to marry her.","But their families had refused to agree, insisting that they wait until Xiaxia finished university before registering their marriage.","In the year Xiaxia graduated, Han Ye was already twenty-seven or twenty-eight. If he waited any longer to marry, he would become a confirmed bachelor.","Both Han Ye and Xiaxia owned homes in the capital. Qiao Lanshu had bought them years ago—one shop and one house for each of her three children.","After they got married, Han Ye was assigned housing through the military. For convenience, they moved into the home provided by his unit.","Han Ye had already decorated the place. He had even prepared a study especially for Xiaxia.","The young couple wandered around the house, and Han Ye asked proudly, “Well? Do you like it? I decorated everything according to your preferences. Look, even the curtains are the blue you like.”","Xiaxia nodded. “I like it.”","Han Ye wrapped his arms around her. “From now on, this is our home.”","They were married now—husband and wife. They had created a little family of their own and had a warm, cozy home.","Han Ye had looked forward to this day for three or four years. Now that he could finally carry Xiaxia home in his arms, he was indescribably excited.","Xiaxia had her arms around his neck as he carried her in his arms, and she was happy too.","She and Han Ye had been together for nearly four years, and they had hardly ever argued.","However, because Han Ye was in the military, they could usually only see each other about once a week. When he was busy, it was perfectly normal for them to go ten days or even half a month without meeting.","Fortunately, Xiaxia wasn’t the clingy type, so she felt it was all right. Han Ye, on the other hand, was very attached to her. Every time they met, he couldn’t wait to see her, and he was constantly worried that her classmates might steal her away.","Xiaxia was so beautiful and striking that many people at her university liked her.","Han Ye had spent the past few years constantly on edge. The key problem was that they weren’t married, so they couldn’t be intimate, and it had been very difficult for him to endure.","Holding Xiaxia against the wall, he sighed, “We’re finally married. From now on, you’re my wife. You’re not allowed to get close to other men anymore.”","Xiaxia said, “Even before we registered our marriage, I never got close to other men.”","Han Ye said unhappily, “But other men were getting close to you. Don’t think I didn’t know...”","As he spoke, he suddenly scooped Xiaxia up and carried her into the room. “Shouldn’t we consummate our marriage? You’re my woman now.”","These past few years had nearly driven Han Ye crazy with frustration.","When he had still been clueless, he hadn’t thought much about the kind of things that happened between men and women.","But after he and Xiaxia began dating, he started having dreams all the time.","He was always dreaming about Xiaxia, and then they would do this and that...","The men in his unit would also chat about such topics in their spare time...","Once he understood those things, it became difficult to restrain himself. Now that they were married, he no longer had to hold back.","Xiaxia said to him, “Are you really in such a hurry? We haven’t even gone home to hold the wedding banquet yet.”","Han Ye: “......”","He pressed her onto the bed and said in a low voice, “I don’t care. We’re legally married now.”","They had been dating for so long, but when it came to intimacy, the two of them were still rather shy.","Fortunately, they were both adults, so they didn’t fumble too badly.","Han Ye simply had an excessive amount of energy, and Xiaxia could barely keep up with him.","Luckily, he had taken a long marriage leave this time, so he had plenty of time to take Xiaxia with him to explore this new world every day.","Originally, they should have chosen a date to return to Wencheng and hold their wedding banquet.","But during his marriage leave, Han Ye became so absorbed in their married life that he spent every day holding Xiaxia at home. Sometimes, they didn’t even leave the house all day.","He had completely forgotten that they were supposed to go home and hold a wedding banquet."]},{"number":298,"title":"Chapter 298: Extra Story 10: Qin Qiao'an","paragraphs":["After graduating from university, Qin Qiao'an was transferred to a military district in the south.","It was more than a thousand kilometers from home, so going back was never easy. Fortunately, the area was fairly close to Yangcheng, and he would sometimes return to visit his maternal grandfather.","His middle-school classmate, Yuan Zhi, often wrote to him. Although neither of them had ever broken through that final barrier, their relationship had long since gone beyond that of ordinary friends.","But Qin Qiao'an had never taken the initiative to say anything, because Yuan Zhi had once opposed his decision to apply to a military academy. The issue had even led to a heated argument between them. They had parted on bad terms, and for roughly half a year afterward, neither of them contacted the other.","Now he had graduated from university and been assigned a job, while Yuan Zhi had become a teacher at a school and had a stable career. After he returned home and reunited with their old classmates, he and Yuan Zhi gradually began speaking again.","Still, their relationship was destined to remain unstable.","The last time Yuan Zhi wrote to him, she had told him that she planned to study in Japan. Qin Qiao'an had asked whether she could stay, whether she had truly made up her mind to go, and told her that if she insisted on leaving, there would be no need for them to keep in touch afterward.","From then on, they lost contact once again.","Of course, it was Qin Qiao'an who had unilaterally cut things off. He never wrote back.","And so, during the Mid-Autumn Festival that year, Yuan Zhi found his unit and came to see him in person.","His comrades nudged one another and gave Qin Qiao'an knowing looks.","“Company Commander, your girlfriend is here to see you.”","Qin Qiao'an had just finished training and was about to return to the dormitory. Hearing that, he froze for a moment.","“What girlfriend? I don’t have one.”","Another soldier hurriedly added, “She says she’s your girlfriend. She came all the way from Wencheng to see you, and she’s pretty attractive, too.”","Qin Qiao'an: “...”","Then it dawned on him, and his expression turned complicated.","He had never expected Yuan Zhi to actually come.","He had made himself perfectly clear in his letter. He had assumed that, like before, she would stop contacting him after their argument.","They had been classmates in middle school. From high school onward, they had attended different schools, but during the years they were both in Wencheng, they still saw each other often.","Back then, Yuan Zhi had been struggling financially. Qin Qiao'an had even brought his friends to set up a stall at the night market, taking Yuan Zhi along with them. They had given most of what they earned to her.","They might have become the best of friends—or perhaps childhood sweethearts.","But their values were ultimately too different.","Yuan Zhi had not wanted him to apply to a military academy. She had not wanted him to leave home and become a soldier elsewhere. All she wanted was for him to stay in Wencheng, find a job, and live a stable life with her.","Then she had found an opportunity to study in Japan.","She knew perfectly well that he was a soldier in the People’s Liberation Army. She knew that Japan was the country he despised most of all.","And yet she still wanted to study there.","Qin Qiao'an was not particularly angry.","He was simply disappointed—disappointed in the friend he had valued most during his youth and adolescence, and in the girl he had liked most.","Of course, he was even more disappointed in himself.","But all of that was in the past. Qin Qiao'an had grown up and become more mature. He understood that everyone had their own ambitions, and that people who followed different paths could not walk together.","He took a shower, changed his clothes, and went to see Yuan Zhi.","Yuan Zhi had a delicate, wholesome sort of beauty. She was not strikingly beautiful, but after working as an elementary school teacher for several years, she had acquired a gentle, scholarly air.","She was waiting for Qin Qiao'an in a café. The moment she saw him enter, her eyes lit up, and she waved him over.","Qin Qiao'an was looking more and more like Qin Yuanzheng, especially after being tanned by the sun over the past few years.","Yuan Zhi had not seen him in a long time. Every time they met, she still found it difficult to let him go.","She looked at him. “Qiao'an, you finally came. I thought you weren’t going to see me.”","Qin Qiao'an sat down across from her and looked at her. “Why did you come?”","Yuan Zhi’s expression was complicated as well. She remained silent for a long while before asking, “Why didn’t you write back to me?”","Qin Qiao'an said, “I thought you knew why.”","Yuan Zhi grew displeased. “What era are we living in, Qin Qiao'an? You’re actually going to cut me off just because I’m going to study in Japan? Do you know how many people from our country study in Japan every year? And how many Japanese scholars come to our country to conduct research?”","Qin Qiao'an’s face darkened. He had always been bad at hiding his emotions, and his displeasure was plain to see.","“So what? How many people go there to study has nothing to do with me. I don’t care.”","He paused, then stared at Yuan Zhi and added, “What I care about is my...”","He did not finish the words my girlfriend. Instead, he only said, “Since you’ve already made your decision, why did you come all this way to see me? Train tickets aren’t cheap.”","With that, he stood up. “I still have training to get back to. From now on, we shouldn’t see each other anymore. You don’t need to write to me either. I won’t reply.”","Seeing him stand up after barely saying a few words, Yuan Zhi hurriedly rose to her feet and called after him.","“Qin Qiao'an! Back when I didn’t want you to apply to a military academy, you insisted on doing it. Didn’t I forgive you in the end? Now I’m only going abroad to study. I’ll be back in a few years. This is an extremely rare opportunity, and it will help my future tremendously. So I hope you can understand me, too.”","Qin Qiao'an paused. His lips parted, as though he wanted to say something.","But he knew that nothing he said would make a difference.","Just as he had stubbornly insisted on applying to the military academy back then, even though it had caused them to quarrel, Yuan Zhi had clearly made up her mind to study abroad.","So Qin Qiao'an said nothing and strode out of the café.","The two of them had met and parted in less than ten minutes.","Yuan Zhi continued saying something behind him, but Qin Qiao'an did not stop to listen.","...","After returning to his unit, Qin Qiao'an thought about it for a long time.","He had once imagined being with Yuan Zhi. But after they had argued during the year he applied to university, whatever feelings they shared could no longer return to the way they had been before.","Over the years, Yuan Zhi had written to him from time to time. This time, she had even come all the way to see him.","He felt that things could not continue like this.","Dragging things out and hesitating was not his style. He needed to make a clean break.","Then he thought of Han Ye and Xiaxia. The two of them had actually gotten married.","They had even carried on a secret relationship for several years behind his back.","The three of them had been as close as siblings since childhood. But now those two had become a family of their own and were leaving him out.","Qin Qiao'an realized that he was already in his twenties. Perhaps it was time to start thinking about marriage.","Maybe he should take advantage of his youth and find a partner whose values were compatible with his own."]},{"number":299,"title":"Chapter 299: Extra Story 11: Qin Qiao'an","paragraphs":["Qin Qiao'an had thought about finding himself a girlfriend, but he hadn’t been in any particular hurry.","When he was twenty-seven, he took a train back to Wencheng and met a young woman at the station.","She had permed hair, a stylish polka-dot dress, and high heels. A suitcase sat beside her.","Amid the surging crowd, she struggled to keep hold of her suitcase, swaying as people jostled her from all sides.","“Hey! Don’t push! Stop pushing!” she said nervously.","Her accent was almost exactly the same as his mother Qiao Lanshu’s.","She was probably visiting relatives in Wencheng from Yangcheng. Even her clothes were clearly in the style of those imported from Hong Kong.","Qin Qiao'an hadn’t been home to visit his family in two or three years. Hearing a girl with the same accent as Qiao Lanshu’s suddenly made him feel an inexplicable sense of closeness.","He immediately strode over, pushed the crowd aside, and steadied the girl. He even picked up her suitcase for her.","“Come with me,” he said.","When the girl first saw him, she was frightened. But then she noticed his military-green T-shirt and camouflage trousers, the army-style bag slung over his shoulder, and his tall, broad build and close-cropped black hair. Without thinking, she followed him forward.","The train station was packed with people at the end of the year. And Wencheng’s station was a major stop, so the crowds were especially heavy.","Public safety was poor in those days, with pickpockets and kidnappers everywhere.","Qin Qiao'an couldn’t understand what this girl had been thinking, dressing so beautifully and traveling alone to a place so far away.","After they left the station, Qin Qiao'an found a corner and set down her suitcase. Then he lowered his head to look at her.","“Are you alone?” he asked.","The girl nodded somewhat sheepishly.","“Did you come here from the south to visit relatives?”","The girl looked a little embarrassed. “Sort of. My father runs a business here. I just graduated this year, so I came to help out at his factory.”","Qin Qiao'an frowned at her. “You don’t even know who I am, and you’re already telling me all about your family? Don’t you know how easy it would be for someone to kidnap you?”","The girl’s eyes widened slightly, and she asked nervously, “Huh? Then... are you a bad person?”","Her large eyes revealed a certain innocent cluelessness.","Qin Qiao'an looked at her speechlessly for a couple of seconds before asking, “Where is your father? I’m not in a hurry. I’ll take you there.”","The girl immediately brightened. “Really? Thank you so much! Here’s the address.”","She pulled a telephone directory from her handbag and flipped to a page with her father’s phone number and the factory’s address written on it.","Qin Qiao'an had grown up in Wencheng and knew the city like the back of his hand. He recognized the place at a glance.","“It’s a bit far to walk,” he said. “Let’s take a motorcycle taxi.”","Motorcycle taxis were common in those days, though the drivers were notorious for overcharging passengers.","Qin Qiao'an paid two yuan to have the girl taken to the entrance of a food factory. After watching her reunite with her family, he turned around and left.","The girl hurried after him.","“Hey, wait! What’s your name? Could you give me your phone number?”","Her voice was soft and sweet, and her accent really did sound just like Qiao Lanshu’s.","Qin Qiao'an liked hearing it. Without hesitation, he wrote his name and his family’s telephone number in her directory.","“I’m from Wencheng. I’m going home for the New Year. If you need anything, you can call me.”","The girl smiled and nodded. “My name is Chen Yafeng. I’ll give you my number too.”","With that, she took the pen and wrote down a number, then tore off the page and handed it to Qin Qiao'an.","He accepted it casually and walked away without looking back.","Chen Yafeng watched his departing figure. She wanted to call out to him, but felt too embarrassed.","A middle-aged woman said to her, “Yafeng, who was that man just now?”","Chen Yafeng answered shyly, “Sister Wang, he’s a good person. He brought me here.”","Sister Wang tugged her back toward the factory, lecturing her as they walked. “Oh, please. You think far too many people are good just because you say so. Your boss already told you not to talk to strangers. You should have waited for us to pick you up at the station. You shouldn’t have gone off by yourself...”","Sister Wang went on and on, but Chen Yafeng didn’t take any of it in.","Her face flushed as she lowered her head, apparently lost in thought. At last, she said, “He’s different from the others. He’s really handsome—tall and good-looking—and his voice is wonderful too.”","Sister Wang: “...”","Sister Wang was truly at a loss. “Child, do you only care about someone’s looks? You’re going to get yourself tricked sooner or later.”","Chen Yafeng ignored her completely. “Qin Qiao'an would never trick me. Besides, even his name sounds nice!”","Sister Wang: “...”","...","The following afternoon, Qiao Lanshu was at home when she received a call from a young woman. The girl’s voice was soft and sweet, with the accent of someone from Yangcheng. She asked somewhat nervously, “Hello, is this Qin Qiao'an’s home?”","Qiao Lanshu was sitting on the sofa with her eyes still fixed on the television, but her expression had already turned to utter astonishment.","She turned to look at Qin Yuanzheng. He lowered his newspaper and asked, “What is it?”","Qiao Lanshu ignored him and smiled as she answered, “Yes, it is. And you are?”","The girl on the phone sounded a little embarrassed. “I’m Chen Yafeng. I need to speak to him about something. Could you ask him to come to the phone?”","“Of course. Just a moment,” Qiao Lanshu replied.","She set down the receiver and hurried over to knock on Qin Qiao'an’s door.","When Qin Qiao'an came out, he immediately noticed the strange look on Qiao Lanshu’s face.","Qin Qiao'an: “...”","He picked up the phone, spoke for less than a minute, and quickly hung up.","Qiao Lanshu hurriedly asked, “Who was that? Who called you? What did you talk about?”","Qin Qiao'an walked to the entrance and put on his shoes as he said, “A friend. She just arrived in Wencheng and doesn’t know her way around, so she asked me to show her the city.”","Before Qiao Lanshu could ask anything else, Qin Qiao'an had already hurried out.","Standing in the doorway, she muttered, “That rascal. He sure ran fast...”","At first, Qin Qiao'an didn’t think there was anything strange about Chen Yafeng getting lost.","But on the third day, and then the fourth, Chen Yafeng called him every day to ask him out. Each time, she claimed that she didn’t know where she was, didn’t know where to find good food, or didn’t know what there was to do for fun...","After they went out, the two of them would eat together and stroll around the city. Sometimes, when she was in the mood, she would even drag him to the cinema.","Over the course of his more than ten days of holiday, their relationship progressed by leaps and bounds. They went from strangers who had met by chance to close friends who got along extremely well.","After the New Year, Qin Qiao'an went to the train station to return to his military unit.","To his surprise, he ran into Chen Yafeng there again.","Qin Qiao'an was startled. “I thought you said you were going to help out at your father’s factory?”","Chen Yafeng said with a smile, “My dad says I’m all thumbs, so he won’t let me help.”","Qin Qiao’an sat beside her. After a moment of silence, he looked at her and asked, “Are you going back to Yangcheng this time?”","Chen Yafeng looked at him. “No. I’m going to the same place as you.”","As she spoke, she handed him the train ticket.","Qin Qiao’an: “...”","Chen Yafeng was from Yangcheng, where all her grandparents and other relatives lived.","Her parents ran a factory and a business in Wencheng.","She wasn’t going to either place. Instead, she was following him to the city where his unit was stationed.","What else could he possibly misunderstand?","He was silent for a long while before finally saying, “My—my father is with the Wencheng Military Region, and my mother is a university professor. My older brother is with the Capital Military Region, and my younger sister works at the Capital Commerce Bureau. I—I’m a lieutenant now. As for my salary, I’ll need to send two or three tenths of it home every month. Would... would that bother you?”","His family didn’t actually need his money. Qiao Lanshu and her husband both earned good salaries, and she also owned shares in Zhong Mei’s department store. Han Ye and Xiaxia often sent money home as well.","But Qin Qiao’an still wanted to send money to his family. He felt that supporting his parents was part of his duty, and that he ought to contribute to the household.","Still, he stammered a little and seemed somewhat embarrassed.","The moment Chen Yafeng heard this, she brightened. “My family is in business. I have two older brothers. My eldest brother runs the factory with our parents, while my second brother studied traditional Chinese painting and now teaches at a school. As for me, well...”","She looked a little embarrassed. “I just graduated from university. I used to work at the Forestry Bureau, but it was too exhausting, so I quit. I don’t have a job at the moment. You—you don’t look down on me, do you?”","Chen Yafeng had grown up in comfortable circumstances, doted on by both her parents and her brothers.","She had lived a carefree life and had never had to worry about making ends meet.","So when she disliked her job, she simply quit.","Now, she was wholeheartedly chasing after Qin Qiao’an, without ever considering that he might look down on her.","Looking into her innocent eyes, Qin Qiao’an smiled. “Of course not. I can afford to support you.”","Chen Yafeng happily hopped in place. The two of them were remarkably sincere with each other. They hadn’t even started dating, yet they were already discussing such practical matters.","Chen Yafeng said earnestly, “Once we get there, I’ll study hard and take the civil service exam. Don’t worry—I’ll work hard for sure! We’ll use your salary to support the family, and I’ll save mine. Then we can use it to raise our children in the future.”","Qin Qiao’an: “...”","This girl really could think far ahead—very far ahead indeed.","He took Chen Yafeng’s hand and said, “Come on. The train’s here.”","—The End—"]}]);
